(29223,'chemistry',67,1076,2569,'Match Column I with Column II and choose the correct combination from the options given.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - Q,\\tB - S,\\tC - P,\\t\\tD - R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Q, \\tB - P,\\tC - S, \\t\\tD - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S,\\tB - Q,\\tC - R, \\tD - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P,\\tB - R,\\tC - S,\\t\\tD - Q", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{2}(\\mathrm{OH})-\\mathrm{CH}(\\mathrm{OH})-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}(\\mathrm{OH})}}$ has highest boiling point because of presence of 3 - OH groups which form intermolecular H -bonding.<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{C}-\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{2}\\right)_{4}-\\mathrm{OH}}}$ and<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)(\\mathrm{OH})-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CH}_{3}}}$ have same molecular masses but as the branching increases boiling point decreases.<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29223_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_29223_question_1.png'),
(29224,'chemistry',70,1250,3045,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> $\\mathrm{\\beta}$-glycosidic linkage is present in maltose,  https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764955154/preptracker/questions/q_29224_col1_1764955153627.png<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Maltose is composed of two glucose units in which C-1 of one glucose unit is linked to C-4 of another glucose unit.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Maltose is composed of two $\\mathrm{\\alpha}$-D-glucose units in which $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C} 1}$ of one glucose unit (I) is linked to $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C} 4}$ of another glucose unit (II).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
