(29244,'chemistry',69,1176,2821,'<br>Select the percentage in which these amine derivatives are formed in the reaction mixture along with the reason.','[{"text": "I $\\\\rightarrow 2 \\\\%$ II $\\\\rightarrow 47 \\\\%$ III $\\\\rightarrow 51 \\\\%$<br>In the acidic medium, aniline is protonated to form the anilinium ion which is ortho directing.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I $\\\\rightarrow 51 \\\\%$ II $\\\\rightarrow 2 \\\\%$ III $\\\\rightarrow 47 \\\\%$<br>In the acidic medium, aniline is protonated to form the anilinium ion which is para directing.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I $\\\\rightarrow 51 \\\\%$ II $\\\\rightarrow 47 \\\\%$ III $\\\\rightarrow 2 \\\\%$<br>In the acidic medium, aniline is protonated to form the anilinium ion which is meta directing.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I $\\\\rightarrow 50 \\\\%$ II $\\\\rightarrow 20 \\\\%$ III $\\\\rightarrow 20 \\\\%$<br>In acidic medium aniline is protonated to form the anilinium ion which is ortho directing.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Anilinium is formed due to acid base reaction of aniline and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HNO}_{3}}}$, which is a meta director.<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29244_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/69_29244_question_1.png'),
