(29250,'chemistry',67,1077,2576,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Ethers are not obtained during the dehydration of secondary and tertiary alcohols.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In the secondary and tertiary alcohols, elimination competes over substitution during dehydration.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but reason is true.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ethers are formed as a result of acid dehydration by ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{S}_{\\mathrm{N}} 2}}$ mechanism (from primary alcohols). If secondary or tertiary alcohols are used, due to steric hindrance alkene is formed because of elimination reaction.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29251,'chemistry',69,1176,2821,'<br>Which of the following reagent systems will be most suitable for this conversion?','[{"text": "$\\\\xrightarrow[\\\\begin{subarray}{l} \\n  {\\\\text{2}}{\\\\text{.}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{A}}{{\\\\text{c}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{O}} \\\\\\\\ \\n  3.\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{dil}}{\\\\text{.}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{S}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{4}}}/\\\\Delta  \\\\\\\\ \\n  {\\\\text{4}}{\\\\text{.}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B}}{{\\\\text{r}}_{\\\\text{2}}} \\n\\\\end{subarray} ]{{{\\\\text{1}}{\\\\text{.}}\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{S}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{4}}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\xrightarrow[\\\\begin{subarray}{l} \\n  2.\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B}}{{\\\\text{r}}_{\\\\text{2}}}/{\\\\text{FeB}}{{\\\\text{r}}_{\\\\text{3}}} \\\\\\\\ \\n  3.\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{dil}}.\\\\,{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{S}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{4}}}/\\\\Delta  \\n\\\\end{subarray} ]{{{\\\\text{1}}{\\\\text{.}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{A}}{{\\\\text{c}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{O}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\xrightarrow[\\\\substack{\\\\text { 2.dil } \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{4} \\\\text { 3. } \\\\mathrm{HBr}}]{\\\\text { 1. } \\\\mathrm{Ac}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\xrightarrow{\\\\mathrm{Br}_{2} / \\\\mathrm{FeBr}_{3}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Frist – ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{2}}}$ group should be blocked so that only one \'Br\' comes (at Para Position).<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29251_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/69_29251_question_1.png'),
(29253,'chemistry',70,1258,3072,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The two strands of DNA are complementary to each other.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Adenine forms hydrogen bonds with guanine and thymine forms hydrogen bonds with cytosine.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but Reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Two strands of DNA are complementary to each other because the hydrogen bonds are formed between specific pairs of bases. Adenine forms hydrogen bonds with thymine whereas cytosine forms hydrogen bonds with guanine.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
