(29261,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'What is suitable reagent \' X \' is?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mid \\\\mathrm{Pt}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}\\\\left|\\\\mathrm{THF}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}\\\\right| \\\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Br}_{2} \\\\mid \\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HBr} \\\\mid \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The suitable reagent X for the conversion is $\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6} \\mid$ THF, $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}_{2} \\mid \\mathrm{OH}$. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29261_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Alkenes react with diborane $\\left(\\mathrm{B}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}\\right)$ in presence of THF or diglyme to form alkyl borane (by hydroboration) which on oxidation gives alcohol. The reaction is known as hydroboration-oxidation reaction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_29261_question_1.png'),
