(29265,'chemistry',67,1077,2577,'What reagent(s) can be used to convert 2-methyl pentan-1-ol into 2-methyl pentanal?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{7}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{3}$-pyridine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Reagents used to convert alcohol to aldehyde is $\\mathrm{CrO}_{3}$-pyridine <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29265_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29266,'chemistry',69,1176,2821,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> p-fluoroanilinium ion is more acidic than anilinium ion.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Electron density in the N-H bond of p-fluoroanilinium ion decreases and release of a proton from p-fluoroanilinium ion is much easier than from anilinium ion.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but reason is true.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Due to – I effect of F – atom it withdraws electrons from ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}^{+} \\mathrm{H}_{3}}}$ group. As a result, electron density in the ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}-\\mathrm{H}}}$ bond of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{p}-}}$ fluoroanilinium ion decreases and hence release of a proton from p - fluoroanilinium ion is much more easier than from anilinium ion.<br>So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29267,'chemistry',68,1118,2677,'The descending order of acidity for the following carboxylic acids is<br>A. $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}$<br>B. $\\mathrm{F}_{3} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{COOH}$<br>C. $\\mathrm{ClCH}_{2}-\\mathrm{COOH}$<br>D. $\\mathrm{FCH}_{2}-\\mathrm{COOH}$<br>E. $\\mathrm{BrCH}_{2}-\\mathrm{COOH}$<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "D $>$ B $>$ A $>$ E $>$ C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B $>$ C $>$ D $>$ E $>$ A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B $>$ D $>$ C $>$ E $>$ A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "E $>$ D $>$ B $>$ A $>$ C", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Acidic strength $\\alpha-\\mathrm{I}$ effect . and  $ - \\,{\\rm{I}}$ effect order : $-\\mathrm{F}>-\\mathrm{Cl}>-\\mathrm{Br}>-\\mathrm{I}$<br>So, the correct order is<br>$\\mathrm{B}>\\mathrm{D}>\\mathrm{C}>\\mathrm{E}>\\mathrm{A}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29268,'chemistry',67,1077,2577,'Conversion of ethyl alcohol into acetaldehyde is an example of','[{"text": "hydrolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "oxidation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "molecular rearrangement", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ethyl alcohol is oxidised to produce acetaldehyde <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29268_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Thus, the conversion of ethyl alcohol into acetaldehyde is an example of oxidation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29269,'chemistry',69,1176,2817,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In acylation reaction of amines, equilibrium shifts to the right hand side in the presence of pyridine.</div><div class="column-right">In the presence of strong base, HCl is removed and the reaction shifts towards the right hand side.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In acylation reaction of amines, equilibrium shifts to the right side in presence of pyridine because it is a stronger base than amine which removes, HCl so formed in the reaction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29270,'chemistry',68,1118,2684,'The major product \'  P  \'  formed in the given reaction is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}$ oxidises benzylic carbon containing at least one $\\alpha$-hydrogen atom to -COOH .  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29270_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29270_question_1.png'),
(29272,'chemistry',67,1077,2577,'The most suitable reagent for the conversion of ${\\rm{RC}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{OH}} \\to {\\rm{RCHO}}$ is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{K}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{7}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{PCC}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pyridinium chlorochromate (PCC) prevents further oxidation of aldehydes to carboxylic acid and steps the reaction at aldehydic stage. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29272_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29273,'chemistry',69,1177,2826,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Benzene diazonium salts are soluble in water.</div><div class="column-right">Benzenediazonium fluoroborate is covalent in nature, so it is soluble in water.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Benzene diazonium salts are soluble in water because diazonium salts are polar in nature and water is a polar solvent. Thus, polar diazonium salt gets dissolved in water. Benzene diazonium fluoro borate is insoluble in water.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29274,'chemistry',68,1113,2660,'A \' and \' B \' in the below reactions are','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29274_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29274_question_1.png'),
(29275,'chemistry',70,1251,3048,'The difference between amylose and amylopectin is','[{"text": "Amylopectin have $\\\\mathrm{1 \\\\rightarrow 4 \\\\alpha}$ - linkage and $\\\\mathrm{1 \\\\rightarrow 6 \\\\beta}$ - linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amylose is made up of glucose and galactose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amylose have $\\\\mathrm{1 \\\\rightarrow 4 \\\\alpha}$ - linkage and $\\\\mathrm{1 \\\\rightarrow 6 \\\\beta}$ - linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amylopectin have $\\\\mathrm{1 \\\\rightarrow 4 \\\\alpha}$ - linkage and $\\\\mathrm{1 \\\\rightarrow 6 \\\\alpha}$ - linkage.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29275_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29276,'chemistry',67,1077,2574,'Decreasing order of reactivity of hydrogen halide acid in the conversion of ${\\rm{ROH}} \\to {\\rm{RX}}$  is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HCl}>\\\\mathrm{HBr}>\\\\mathrm{HI}>\\\\mathrm{HF}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HI}>\\\\mathrm{HBr}>\\\\mathrm{HCl}>\\\\mathrm{HF}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HF}>\\\\mathrm{HCl}>\\\\mathrm{HBr}>\\\\mathrm{HI}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HF}>\\\\mathrm{HBr}>\\\\mathrm{HI}>\\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{HI}>\\mathrm{HBr}>\\mathrm{HCl}>\\mathrm{HF}$.This is due to the fact that, nucleophilicity of a halide ion increases with increase in size. As the size of halide ion increases from $\\mathrm{F}^{\\ominus}$ to $\\mathrm{I}^{\\ominus}$, thus, $\\mathrm{I}^{-}$ion will be a better nucleophile followed by $\\mathrm{Br}^{-}, \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}$and $\\mathrm{F}^{-}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29277,'chemistry',69,1176,2821,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Anilinium hydrogen sulphate, on heating forms a mixture of ortho-and paraaminosulphonic acids.</div><div class="column-right">The sulphonic acid group is electron withdrawing.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Anilinium hydrogen sulphate on heating decomposes to aniline and ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}}}$. Sulphonation of aniline with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}}}$ takes place at o- and p – positions, since ${\\mathrm{-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}}}$ group is o - and p – directing.<br>${\\mathrm{-\\mathrm{SO}_{3} \\mathrm{H}}}$ group is meta directing group.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29279,'chemistry',67,1076,2569,'Boiling point of alcohol is comparatively higher than that of corresponding alkane due to','[{"text": "intermolecular hydrogen bonding", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "intramolecular hydrogen bonding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "volatile nature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "none of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Because of intermolecular hydrogen bonding in alcohols, they exist as associated molecules. Consequently, a large amount of energy is required to break these bonds and therefore, their boiling points are higher than that of the corresponding hydrocarbons (hydrogen bonding is absent in hydrocarbons).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29280,'chemistry',70,1253,3054,'Which of the following compounds can form a zwitter ion?','[{"text": "Benzoic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acetanilide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aniline", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29280_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29281,'chemistry',68,1113,2659,'The major product formed in the following reaction is','[{"text": "D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It is clemmensen reduction. The reaction involves elimination of  $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ (due to - OH group) and reduction of  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29281_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29281_question_1.png'),
(29282,'chemistry',69,1176,2823,'Match the column I and choose the correct combination from the options given.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - R,\\tB - S,\\tC - Q,\\tD - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, \\tB - R,\\tC - Q, \\tD - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q,\\tB - S,\\tC - R, \\tD - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S,\\tB - R,\\tC - Q,\\tD - P", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hinsberg reagent is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}}}$.<br>In Hoffmann\'s bromamide reaction,<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{RCONH}_{2}}}$ changes into ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}}}$.<br>In Carbyl amine reaction, ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}}}$ changes into RNC. <br>${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{NH}}}$ is a secondary amine.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/69_29282_question_1.png'),
(29283,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'In the following reaction, A is','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{CHO}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{OH}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{OH}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}{\\\\rm{COH}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29283_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_29283_question_1.png'),
(29284,'chemistry',69,1174,2812,'Match the column I and choose the correct combination from the options given.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - R,\\tB - S,\\tC - Q,\\tD - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, \\tB - P,\\tC - S, \\t\\tD - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Q,\\tB - S,\\tC - R, \\tD - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S,\\tB - R,\\tC - Q,\\tD - P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(A) Tetraethyl ammonium iodide is a quaternary ammonium salt.<br>(B) Tertiary butyl amine is a primary amine<br>(C) Schmidt reaction is<br>R- ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{COOH}+\\mathrm{N}_{3} \\mathrm{H}+}}$ Conc. ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{RNH}_{2}}}$<br>(D) Trialkyl amine is a tertiary amine.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/69_29284_question_1.png'),
(29285,'chemistry',68,1113,2659,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully and mark the correct option.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29285_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   can be subjected to Wolff-Kishner reduction to give  https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764949401/preptracker/questions/q_29285_col1_1764949401000.png<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Wolff-Kishner reduction is used to convert   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29285_qtext_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />','[{"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The base sensitive group is affected during Wolff-Kishner reduction. The halogen group undergoes dehydrohalogenation under strongly basic conditions. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29285_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29286,'chemistry',70,1253,3053,'The non-essential amino acid among the following is:','[{"text": "Valine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leucine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alanine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lysine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Alanine is an example of non-essential amino acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29287,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'The product of following reaction is ${{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{MgBr}} + {\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O/}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}}}}$','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_3}{\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_2}{\\\\text{OH}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29287_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29288,'chemistry',69,1176,2823,'Match the column I and choose the correct combination from the options given.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A}} - {\\\\text{R}},\\\\,{\\\\text{B}} - {\\\\text{S}},\\\\,{\\\\text{C}} - {\\\\text{Q}},\\\\,{\\\\text{D}} - {\\\\text{P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-S; ${\\mathrm{1^{\\circ}}}$ aliphatic amine with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}}}$ gives ${\\mathrm{1^{\\circ}}}$ alcohol ${\\text{i}}{\\text{.e}}{\\text{. R\'OH}}\\,{\\text{ + }}\\,{{\\text{N}}_{\\text{2}}}$.<br>B-Q;   ${\\mathrm{1^{\\circ}}}$ aromatic amine with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}}}$ gives diazonium salt ${\\text{i}}{\\text{.e}}{\\text{. ph}} - \\mathop {\\text{N}}\\limits^ +   \\equiv {\\text{NC}}{{\\text{l}}^ - }$.<br>D-P; ${\\mathrm{2^{\\circ}}}$ aliphatic amine with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}}}$ gives ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}-}}$ nitroso compound ${\\text{i}}{\\text{.e}}{\\text{. RR\'}}\\,{\\text{N}} - {\\text{N}} = {\\text{O}}$.<br>C-R; ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{N}, \\mathrm{N}}}$-Dimethyl aniline with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}}}$ gives Paranitroso – N,N – dimethyl aniline i.e. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29288_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/69_29288_question_1.png'),
(29289,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'In the following reaction,','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29289_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29289_question_1.png'),
(29290,'chemistry',70,1253,3053,'Which of the following is a basic amino acid?','[{"text": "Alanine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tyrosine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Serine", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29290_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Since it contains more number of $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{2}}$ groups as compared to - $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{COOH}}$ groups hence it is basic amino acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29291,'chemistry',67,1080,2586,'Starch is converted to ethanol by fermentation. The sequence of enzymes used are','[{"text": "amylase, maltase, zymase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "diastase, maltase, zymase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "amylase, invertase, zymase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "amylase, zymase, maltase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The manufacture of ethyl alcohol from starch consists of the following steps :<br>(i) Hydrolysis of starch  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29291_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  This step is called saccharification.<br>(ii) Fermentation <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29291_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29294,'chemistry',67,1077,2574,'When alcohol reacts with conc. $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}$, intermediate compound formed is','[{"text": "carbonium ion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "alkoxy ion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "alkyl hydrogen sulphate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Conc. $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}$ is an excellent dehydrating agent. Upon reaction with an alcohol, it forms an alkene and water molecule is given out. First step involves protonation of alcohol. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29294_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29295,'chemistry',69,1177,2828,'When aniline is treated with benzene diazonium chloride at low temperature in weakly acidic medium, the final product obtained is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Diazonium cation reacts with aniline in weakly acidic medium resulting in N,C – coupling at para position to ${\\mathrm{-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}}}$ group and <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29295_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29296,'chemistry',70,1250,3044,'Sucrose on hydrolysis gives','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\alpha}$-D-Glucose $\\\\mathrm{+\\\\beta}$-D-Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\alpha}$-D-Glucose $\\\\mathrm{+\\\\beta}$-D-Fructose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\alpha}$-D-Fructose $\\\\mathrm{+\\\\beta}$-D-Fructose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\beta}$-D-Glucose $\\\\mathrm{+\\\\alpha}$-D-Fructose", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\text{Sucrose }}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{Hydrolysis }}}]{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}^{\\text{ + }}}}}\\alpha \\,\\,{\\text{ -  D -   Glucose  + }}\\beta \\,\\,{\\text{ - }}\\,{\\text{D}}\\,{\\text{ - }}\\,\\,{\\text{Fructose}}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29297,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'Correct statements for the given reaction are : <br> <br>A. Compound \' B \' is aromatic.<br>B. The completion of above reaction is very low.<br>C. \'A\' shows tautomerism<br>D. The bond lengths of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ in compound B are found to be same.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "A, B and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, C and D only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A, B and C only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29297_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>\' B \' is aromatic as it obeys Huckel\'s rule. Due to resonance, it has all $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{C}$ bonds equal. \' A \' can show tautomerism too.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29297_question_1.png'),
(29298,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'The only alcohol that cannot be prepared by the indirect hydration of alkene is','[{"text": "ethyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "propyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iso-butyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "methyl alcohol", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Methyl alcohol cannot be prepared by hydration of alkene as simplest alkene has two carbon atoms so alcohol of atleast two carbon atoms can be formed by this method. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29298_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
