(29299,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'The increasing order of basicity of $\\mathrm{RCN}, \\mathrm{RCH}=\\mathrm{NR}$ and $\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}$ is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RCN} < \\\\mathrm{RCH}=\\\\mathrm{NR} < \\\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RNH}_{2} < \\\\mathrm{RCN} < \\\\mathrm{RCH}=\\\\mathrm{NR}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RCH}=\\\\mathrm{NR} < \\\\mathrm{RNH}_{2} < \\\\mathrm{RCN}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{RNH}_{2} < \\\\mathrm{RCH}=\\\\mathrm{NR} < \\\\mathrm{RCN}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{RCN}, \\mathrm{N}}}$ – atom is sp hybridized. In ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{RCH}=\\mathrm{NR}, \\mathrm{N}}}$-atom is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{2}}}$ hybridized In ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{RNH}_{2} \\mathrm{~N}}}$-atom is ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{sp}^{3}}}$ hybridized. As \' ${\\mathrm{s}}$ \' character increases in hybridization, electro-negativity increases and basicity decreases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29300,'chemistry',68,1118,2684,'The major product \' P \' formed in the following sequence of reactions is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29300_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29300_question_1.png'),
