(29302,'chemistry',69,1174,2811,'Isopropylamine can be obtained by','[{"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHCHO}+\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{OH} \\\\longrightarrow \\\\xrightarrow{\\\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}{\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}{\\\\text{CHO}} + {\\\\text{N}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}\\\\xrightarrow[\\\\Delta ]{{}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\xrightarrow{{{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}}/{\\\\text{Ni}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Isopropyl alcohol on heating with ammonia, isopropyl amine is formed.  ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{CHOH}+\\mathrm{NH}_{3} \\rightarrow\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{CHNH}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29304,'chemistry',67,1077,2572,'Which of the following compounds is most acidic?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{6}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH} \\\\equiv \\\\mathrm{CH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Among given choices, $\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{OH}$ can give proton $\\left(\\mathrm{H}^{+}\\right)$most easily.<br>$\\therefore \\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{OH}$ is most acidic among $\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{6}, \\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ and $\\mathrm{CH} \\equiv \\mathrm{CH}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29305,'chemistry',70,1256,3067,'The incorrect statement regarding enzymes is:','[{"text": "Like chemical catalysts enzymes reduce the activation energy of bio processes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enzymes are polysaccharides.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Enzymes are very specific for a particular reaction and substrate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enzymes are biocatalysts.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Enzymes are polysaccharides $\\mathrm{\\Rightarrow}$ This is incorrect statement because enzymes are protein in nature',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29306,'chemistry',69,1176,2819,'$\\mathrm{RNH}_{2}$ reacts with $\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\mathrm{Cl}$ in aqueous KOH to give a clear solution. On acidification, a precipitate is obtained which is due to the formation of','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{R}-\\\\mathrm{N}^{-} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{~K}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{SO}_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{R}-\\\\mathrm{NHSO}_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}$<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{Cl}}}\\limits_{{\\text{Benzene}}\\,\\,{\\text{sulphynoyl}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{chloride}}}  + {\\text{RN}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow{{ - {\\text{HCl}}}}$<br>$\\mathop {{\\text{RNHS}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{N}} - \\,{\\text{alkyl}}\\,\\,{\\text{benzene}}\\,\\,{\\text{sulphonamide}}} \\xrightarrow{{{\\text{KOH}}}}$<br>${\\text{R}} - \\mathop {\\text{N}}\\limits^ -  \\mathop {{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}\\,{{\\text{K}}^ + }}\\limits_{{\\text{soluble}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{in}}{\\kern 1pt} {\\kern 1pt} {\\text{KOH}}} \\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}^{{\\text{ }} + {\\text{ }}}}}}{\\text{RNHS}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29307,'chemistry',68,1118,2684,'<br>The correct sequence of reagents for the preparation of Q and R is','[{"text": "(i) $\\\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{3}, 770 \\\\mathrm{~K}, 20 \\\\mathrm{~atm}$;<br>(ii) $\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{O}^{+}$; (iii) NaOH ;<br>(iv) $\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{O}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(i) $\\\\mathrm{Mo}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{3}, \\\\Delta$; (ii) $\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{O}^{+}$;<br>(iii) NaOH ; (iv) $\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{O}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) $\\\\mathrm{CrO}_{2} \\\\mathrm{Cl}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{O}^{+}$;<br>(ii) $\\\\mathrm{Cr}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{3}, 770 \\\\mathrm{~K}, 20 \\\\mathrm{~atm}$;<br>(iii) NaOH ; (iv) $\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{O}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) $\\\\mathrm{KMnO}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$; (ii) $\\\\mathrm{Mo}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}_{3}, \\\\Delta$;<br>(iii) NaOH ; (iv) $\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{O}^{+}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29307_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29307_question_1.png'),
(29308,'chemistry',67,1077,2577,'When vapours of iso-propyl alcohol are passed over heated copper, the major product obtained is','[{"text": "propane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "propylene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "acetaldehyde", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "acetone", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29308_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29309,'chemistry',69,1177,2827,'I. Diazonium salts are very good intermediates for the introduction of $\\mathrm{F}, \\mathrm{Cl}, \\mathrm{Br}, \\mathrm{I}, \\mathrm{CN}, \\mathrm{OH}, \\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ groups into the aromatic ring.<br>II. Aryl fluorides and iodides can be prepared by direct halogenation.<br>III. Cyano group can be introduced by nucleophilic substitution of chlorine in chlorobenzene easily.<br>IV. The replacement of the diazo group by other groups is helpful in preparing those substituted aromatic compounds which cannot be prepared by direct substitution in benzene or substituted benzene.<br>Select the incorrect statements.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Aryl fluorides and iodides can not be prepared by direct halogenation. Due to double bond nature between \' C \' and \' Cl \' in chlorobenzene, it is not easy to replace \' Cl \' group by \' CN \' group',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29310,'chemistry',70,1247,3032,'Glucose on oxidation with bromine water yields gluconic acid. This reaction confirms the presence of','[{"text": "six carbon atoms linked in straight chain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "secondary alcoholic group in glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "aldehyde group in glucose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "primary alcoholic group in glucose", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glucose on oxidation with bromine water yields gluconic acid. This reaction confirms the presence of aldehyde group in glucose.   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29310_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   Here, $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Br}_{2}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}}$ act as an oxidising agent and led to the oxidation of glucose into gluconic acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2016,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29311,'chemistry',68,1113,2662,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully and mark correct option.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Acetal / ketal is stable in basic medium.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The high leaving tendency of alkoxide ion gives the stability to acetal/ketal in basic medium.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion .", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Acetal and ketal are stable in basic medium as there is no suitable leaving group for $S_{N} 2$ reaction in basic medium.<br>Acetal or ketal readily hydrolyse to the corresponding carbonyl compounds and alcohol under acidic conditions.',NULL,'Hard','Assertion and Reason',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29312,'chemistry',67,1077,2574,'In the reaction given below, X is neo-pentyl alcohol $\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}}{\\text{X}}$','[{"text": "2-methylpentane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-methylpent-2-ene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-methylbut-2-ene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "neo-pentane", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29312_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29482,'chemistry',70,1257,3069,'The vitamin that helps in clotting of blood is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{A}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{C}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{B}_{2}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{K}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{A}}$ - Night blindness<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}}$- Scurvy<br>$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{B}_{2}}$ - Antichelosis',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29313,'chemistry',69,1176,2821,'Which of the following reactions belong to aromatic electrophilic substitution?<br>I. Bromination of acetanilide<br>II. Coupling reaction of aryl diazonium salts<br>III. Diazotization of aniline<br>IV. Acylation of aniline<br>Choose the correct option.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29313_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  both these reactions are not EAS reactions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
