(29432,'chemistry',68,1117,2676,'Read Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct option given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> p-Hydroxybenzoic acid has a lower boiling point than o-hydroxybenzoic acid.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> o-Hydroxybenzoic acid has intermolecular hydrogen bonding.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but reason is true.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\mathrm{p}}$-Hydroxybenzoic acid has higher boiling point than o-hydroxybenzoic acid as it has intermolecular hydrogen bonding.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29433,'chemistry',67,1077,2578,'${\\text{Glycerol}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{KHS}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}}{\\text{A}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{HClO}}}}{\\text{B}}$ <br>A and B  respectively are','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29433_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29434,'chemistry',69,1176,2818,'Reaction of chloroform with $\\mathrm{KOH}$ in the presence of a primary aromatic amine is called','[{"text": "carbylamine reaction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hydrolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wurtz reaction", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Aliphatic as well as aromatic amines when<br> treated with chloroform in an alkaline medium, gives an offensive melting compound, called carbylamine. <br>Hence, the reaction is known as carbylamine reaction.<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{3KOH}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ + }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{CHC}}{{\\rm{l}}_{\\rm{3}}} \\to \\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{6}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{NC}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ + }}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{3KCl}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ + 3}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}}\n\\end{array}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29435,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'Match Column I with Column II.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{P,B}} - {\\\\rm{Q,C}} - {\\\\rm{R,D}} - {\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{S,B}} - {\\\\rm{P,C}} - {\\\\rm{R,D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{P,B}} - {\\\\rm{S,C}} - {\\\\rm{Q,D}} - {\\\\rm{R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{Q,B}} - {\\\\rm{S,C}} - {\\\\rm{R,D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29435_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  A -S, B - P, C - R, D - Q.<br>So,  the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29435_question_1.png'),
(29436,'chemistry',70,1251,3048,'The glycosidic linkage involved in linking the glucose units in amylose part of starch is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{C}_{1}-\\\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\\\beta}$ - linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{C}_{1}-\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\alpha}$ - linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{C}_{1}-\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\beta}$ - linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{C}_{1}-\\\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\\\alpha}$ - linkage.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In amylose $\\mathrm{\\alpha-D}$ glucose units are linked to one another through $\\mathrm{\\alpha}$-glycosidic linkage involving $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{1}}$ of one glucose unit with $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{4}}$ of the other glucose unit.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29437,'chemistry',67,1078,2583,'An organic compound \'B\' is formed by the reaction of ethyl magnesium iodide with a substance A followed by treatment with dilute aqueous acid. Compound B does not react with PCC or PDC in dichloromethane. Which of the following is a possible compound for A ?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_2}{\\\\rm{C}} = {\\\\rm{O}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{ \' B \' }}$  is a tertiary alcohol based on given properties. Tertiary alcohols are formed by the reaction of ketones with Grignard reagent. <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29437_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br> Tertiary alcohols do not have oxidisable hydrogen linked to carbon atom bearing hydroxyl group, thus, are stable to oxidation under ordinary conditions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29438,'chemistry',69,1176,2822,'When ethylamine react with sodium metal, the<br> gas evolved is','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{N}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When ethylamine is heated with sodium metal, then hydrogen gas is evolved.<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + 2Na}} \\to \\\\\n\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{5}}}\\overline {\\rm{N}} {\\rm{HN}}{{\\rm{a}}^{\\rm{ + }}}{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}} \\uparrow \n\\end{array}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
