(29446,'chemistry',70,1253,3054,'Which of the following molecules form a Zwitter ion?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COOCH}_{3}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{NCH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COOH}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COC}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{COOH}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Zwitter ion is a molecule containing a positively charged ion at one end and a negatively charged ion at the other. Among the given compounds amino acid.$\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{NCH}_{2} \\mathrm{COOH}}$ forms a Zwitter ion which is shown below   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29446_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29447,'chemistry',68,1113,2656,'Give the decreasing order of the following in the extent by hydration or towards nucleophilic addition reaction.','[{"text": "IV ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ III ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ II ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ II ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ III ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ II ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ III ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ III ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ II ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Aldehyde is more electrophilic than ketone and Br acts as – I group.<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Order of rate of hydration ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{Nu}^{\\oplus}\\right.}}$ attack ${\\mathrm{)}}$ is<br> IV ${\\mathrm{>}}$ III ${\\mathrm{>}}$ II ${\\mathrm{>}}$ I.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29447_question_1.png'),
