(29450,'chemistry',68,1118,2678,'Among the given three acids:<br> <br> <br>The correct order of ease acid catalyzed esterification is','[{"text": "${\\\\mathrm{X>Z>Y}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Y ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ X ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ Z", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{Z>X>Y}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{Y}>\\\\mathrm{Z}>\\\\mathrm{X}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'More sterically hindered acid is least reactive towards esterification.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29450_question_1.png'),
(29451,'chemistry',70,1253,3054,'At $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pH}=4}$, glycine exists as','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\stackrel{+}{\\\\mathrm{N}}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{COO}^{-}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\stackrel{+}{\\\\mathrm{N}}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{COOH}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\stackrel{+}{\\\\mathrm{N}}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{COOH}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\stackrel{+}{\\\\mathrm{N}}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{COO}^{-}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\text{At pH = 4}}$  (i.e. acidic medium), an amphoteric Zwitter ion structure changes into cation when an acid is added to it.  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29451_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29452,'chemistry',67,1078,2579,'The alcohol having molecular formula $\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\mathrm{H}_{9} \\mathrm{OH}$, when shaken with a mixture of anhydrous $\\mathrm{ZnCl}_{2}$ and conc. $\\mathrm{HCl}$ gives an oily layer product after five minutes. The alcohol is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{C}\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{3} \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{CH}(\\\\mathrm{OH}) \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Secondary alcohol, on reaction with anhydrous $\\mathrm{ZnCl}_{2}$ and conc. $\\mathrm{HCl}$ (Lucas reagent) gives an oily layer product after five minutes. <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29452_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br> Oily layer (turbidity) formed after 5 min.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29453,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'The correct order of the increasing basicity of<br> methyl amine, ammonia and aniline is','[{"text": "methyl amine $ < $ aniline $ < $ ammonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "aniline $ < $ ammonia $ < $ methyl amine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "aniline $ < $ methyl amine $ < $ ammonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ammonia $ < $ aniline $ < $ methyl amine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In aniline the lone pair on N is involved in delocalization with benzene ring and is not available for protonation. Methyl amine is a stronger base than ammonia because + I effect of methyl group increases electron density on N making it more basic than ${\\rm{N}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}$. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29453_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Cannot be protonated. least basic <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29453_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29454,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'In the given reaction','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Intramolecular Cannizzaro\'s reaction.<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29454_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29454_question_1.png'),
