(29456,'chemistry',70,1254,3059,'There are 20 naturally occurring amino acids. The maximum number of tripeptides that can be obtained is','[{"text": "6470", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7465", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5360", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8000", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Since there are 20 naturally occurring amino acids.<br>$\\mathrm{\\therefore}$ Maximum no.of tripeptides that can be obtained are $\\mathrm{=(20)^{3}=8000}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29457,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'Which of the following is the correct increasing order of basicity of amines in gaseous phase?','[{"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}>\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}>\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}>\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}>\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}>\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}>\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}>\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}>\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Alkyl amines $\\left(1^{\\circ}, 2^{\\circ}\\right.$ and $\\left.3^{\\circ}\\right)$ are stronger bases than ammonia. This can be explained in terms of electron releasing inductive effect of alkyl group. As a result, the electron density on the nitrogen atom increases and thus, they can donate the lone pair of electrons more easily than ammonia.<br>The electron releasing effect is maximum in tertiary amines and minimum in primary amines (in gas phase).<br>$3^{\\circ}$ amine $>2^{\\circ}$ amine $>1^{\\circ}$ amine $>\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$<br>So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29458,'chemistry',68,1113,2659,'Suitable reagent for conversion of following reaction','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Ni} / \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Zn} / \\\\mathrm{Hg} / \\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red $\\\\mathrm{P}+\\\\mathrm{HI}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The suitable reagent for the conversion<br>$\\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CHO} \\xrightarrow{?} \\mathrm{CH}_{2}=\\mathrm{CH}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{OH}$ is $\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}$. It is a selective reagent that reduces $>\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{O}$ group to $-\\mathrm{OH}$ and does not reduce carbon-carbon double bond. Thus, unsaturated alcohols can be prepared.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29458_question_1.png'),
(29459,'chemistry',67,1084,2608,'Sometimes explosion occurs while distilling ethers. It is due to the presence of','[{"text": "peroxides", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "oxides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ketones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "aldehydes.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the presence of air and light, ethers form peroxides which cause explosion during distillation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29461,'chemistry',70,1253,3054,'The amino acids which is not optical active is','[{"text": "lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "serine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "alanine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "glycine.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29461_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   Except glycine, all $\\mathrm{\\alpha}$-amino acids are optically active and have an asymmetric carbon atom. Hence each of these aminoacid can exist in two optical isomeric forms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2007,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29462,'chemistry',68,1108,2639,'Write IUPAC name of the following','[{"text": "2-bromo-2-ethyl hexanal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3-bromo-2-methyl hexanal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2-methyl-3-bromo hexanal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3-bromo-2-formyl hexane", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The priority order of functional group is $-\\mathrm{CHO}>\\mathrm{Br}$ Therefore, IUPAC name of the given compound is as follows <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29462_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29462_question_1.png'),
(29463,'chemistry',67,1070,2551,'The formula of ethyl carbinol is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{COH}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In carbinol system of nomenclature, methyl alcohol is called carbinol and other alcohols are named as alkyl or aryl derivatives of carbinol. Thus, the formula of ethyl carbinol is <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29463_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29464,'chemistry',69,1176,2823,'${{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{N}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow[{0^\\circ {\\text{C}}}]{{{\\text{NaN}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{/HCl}}}}{\\text{X}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{CuCN}}}}{\\text{Y}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O/}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ + }}}}}{\\text{Z}}$ <br>${\\text{Z}}$ is identified as','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}-\\\\mathrm{NH}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}-\\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29464_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29465,'chemistry',68,1113,2663,'Which of the following is the correct sequence of step involved in the mechanism of Cannizzaro reaction?','[{"text": "Nucleophilic attack, transfer of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{-}$and transfer of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transfer of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{-}$, transfer of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$and nucleophilic attack", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transfer of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$, nucleophilic attack and transfer of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electrophilic attack by $\\\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$, transfer of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{+}$and transfer of $\\\\mathrm{H}^{-}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Consider the following Cannizzaro reaction, <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29465_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> The mechanism of Cannizzaro reaction is as<br>Step I Attack of nucleophile $\\left(\\mathrm{OH}^{-}\\right)$to the carbonyl carbon. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29465_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Step II The transfer of hydride ion from anion (I) to second molecule of aldehyde and finally rapid transfer of proton takes place.  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29465_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29466,'chemistry',67,1078,2581,'Which of the following gives red colour in Victor Meyer\'s test?','[{"text": "n-Propyl alcohol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iso-Propyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "tert-Butyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "sec-Butyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In Victor Meyer\'s test, primary alcohols give red colour. The structures of the given compounds are <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29466_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29466_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29466_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29466_explanation_4.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br> Thus, ${\\rm{n}} - $ propyl alcohol being $1^{\\circ}$ alcohol gives red colour in Victor Meyer\'s test.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29467,'chemistry',70,1254,3062,'Which of the following proteins is globular?','[{"text": "Collagen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Albumin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Myosin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fibroin", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Albumin is a globular protein.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2015,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29469,'chemistry',68,1113,2665,'In the reaction, The major product formed is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{CHO}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}-\\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}-\\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}-\\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{CH}-\\\\mathrm{COCH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given reaction is an example of Perkin condensation. In this reaction, aromatic aldehydes react with acid anhydride of an aliphatic acid in presence of sodium salt of same acid to form $\\alpha, \\beta$-unsaturated acid. The steps involved in the process are as follows : <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29469_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Thus, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29469_question_1.png'),
(29471,'chemistry',69,1177,2829,'Benzenediazonium chloride on treatment with hypophosphorous acid and water yields benzene. Which of the following is used as a catalyst in this reaction?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{Red}}\\\\,{\\\\text{P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Zn}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Cu}^{+}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29471_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29472,'chemistry',70,1256,3067,'Which one of the following does not correctly match with each other?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Silk-polyamide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipase-enzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Butter-fat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxytocin-enzyme.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Oxytocin is a polypeptide hormone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29473,'chemistry',68,1113,2659,'Clemmensen reaction of ketone is carried out in the presence of','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Zn}-\\\\mathrm{Hg}$ with $\\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "glycol with $\\\\mathrm{KOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$ with Pt as catalyst", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{Zn}-\\mathrm{Hg}$ with $\\mathrm{HCl}$ reduces ketone to respective alkane, i.e.$\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{O}$ of ketone reduce to $>\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$ group. The reaction is called Clemmensen reduction.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29474,'chemistry',67,1084,2606,'When p-nitrobromobenzene reacts with sodium ethoxide, the product obtained is','[{"text": "p-nitroanisole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ethyl phenyl ether", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p-nitrophenetole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "no reaction occurs.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In general aryl halides are highly stable and do not take part in Williamson\'s synthesis, but presence of strong electron withdrawing group like $-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ makes the $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{X}$ bond weaker and facilitates the substitution of $-\\mathrm{Br}$ by $-\\mathrm{OR}$. <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29474_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29475,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'Which of the following compound is the most basic?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Benzylamine is most basic due to localised lone pair of electrons on nitrogen atom while in other compounds, as a result of resonance, the lone pair of electrons on nitrogen atom gets delocalised over benzene ring and thus, is less easily available for donation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29476,'chemistry',68,1113,2663,'Cannizzaro reaction is not shown by','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{CHO}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{HCHO}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The aldehyde/ketone, which do not contain $\\alpha-\\mathrm{H}$ atom shows Cannizzaro reaction.<br>In $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHO}$, carbonyl group is attached to $\\mathrm{C}$-atom having $\\alpha-\\mathrm{H}$; Hence, $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CHO}$ does not show Cannizzaro reaction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29477,'chemistry',70,1257,3069,'The vitamin that belongs to aromatic series is','[{"text": "${\\\\text{B complex}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{K}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{C}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{A}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The vitamin that belongs to aromatic series is vitamin $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}}$. It has an aromatic structure. The structure of vitamin $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{K}}$ is given below.   <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29477_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29478,'chemistry',67,1078,2583,'Consider the following compounds, <br>$({\\text{I}}){\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} ({\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{OH}})$<br>$({\\text{II}}){\\mkern 1mu} ({\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{\\text{COC}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}})$<br>(III) $(IV)\\,({\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{H}}_3}{\\rm{OH}})$ <br> which of the above compounds on being warmed with iodine solution and $\\mathrm{NaOH}$, will give iodoform?','[{"text": "(I), (III) and (IV)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only (II)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(I), (II) and (III)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only (I) and (II)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Compounds having either <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29478_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  group or $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CH}(\\mathrm{OH})$ - group, give iodoform when warmed with $\\mathrm{I}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{NaOH}$. <br> Thus, <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29478_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_29478_question_1.png'),
(29479,'chemistry',69,1174,2810,'The product formed when phthalimide is treated with a mixture of $\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ and strong $\\mathrm{NaOH}$ solution is','[{"text": "aniline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "phthalamide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "phthalic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "anthranilic acid.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29479_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29480,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'Which of the following compounds undergoes both Cannizzaro and aldol reaction?','[{"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH} \\\\cdot \\\\mathrm{CHO}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HCHO}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{CHO}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CHO}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'2-methylpropanal contains one $\\alpha$-H-atom. Hence, it undergoes aldol condensation. It also undergoes Cannizzaro\'s reaction. Aldol reaction proceeds via formation of carbanion. In 2-methylpropanal, due to +I - effect of the two alkyl groups attached to alpha-carbon, the carbanion of 2-methylpropanal is not stable. Thus, it prefers to undergo nucleophilic attack by $\\mathrm{OH}^{-}$ ion at the aldehyde leading to the formation of Cannizzaro products. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29480_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29481,'chemistry',67,1089,2613,'The decrease in stability of cyclohexanol is due to','[{"text": "skew interaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "flag-pole interaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Baeyer\'s strain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1,3-diaxial interaction.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Any substituent prefers to occupy the less sterically hindered equitorial position. Thus, the decrease in stability of cyclohexanol is due to 1,3-diaxial interaction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29483,'chemistry',69,1176,2819,'p-Toluidine and benzyl amine can be distinguished by','[{"text": "Sandmeyer\'s reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dye test", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Molisch\'s test", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gattermann reaction.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\text{p}} - $ Toluidine undergoes diazotisation reaction and gives red dye while benzyl amine does not undergo diazotisation reaction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29484,'chemistry',68,1113,2662,'The product formed when acetone reacts with nitro methane in the presence of a base is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COCH}=\\\\mathrm{CHNO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29484_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Hence, the product formed when acetone reacts with nitromethane in the presence of a base is <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29484_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29485,'chemistry',67,1072,2558,'Equatorial alcohol is more stable than axial alcohol to an extent of','[{"text": "11 kcal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.7 kcal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "11.7 kcal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10.3 kcal", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Equitorial alcohol is more stable than axial alcohol to an extent of 0.7 kcal .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29486,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'Which one of the following will be most basic?','[{"text": "Aniline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p-Methoxyaniline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p-Methylaniline", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Benzylamine", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In aniline, ${\\text{p}} - $ methoxyaniline and ${\\text{p}} - $ methylaniline, the lone pair of electrons on the <br>$\\mathrm{N}$-atom is delocalised in the benzene ring while in benzylamine it is localised and more available for donation. Hence, benzylamine is most basic among the given compounds.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29487,'chemistry',70,1257,3069,'Hypothyroidism is caused by the deficiency of','[{"text": "adrenalin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "thyroxine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "glucocorticoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "vitamin B-12", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Increased level of thyroxine cause hyperthyroidism and low level of thyroxine cause hypothyroidism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29488,'chemistry',68,1113,2668,'In Tollen\'s test, aldehyde','[{"text": "are oxidised", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "are reduced to alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "neither reduced nor oxidised", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "precipitate $\\\\mathrm{Ag}^{+}$as $\\\\mathrm{AgCl}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When aldehydes are treated with Tollen\'s reagent (ammoniacal solution of silver nitrate), <br>these are oxidised to carboxylate ion while <br>Tollen\'s reagent reduces to metallic silver which gives a shiny appearence of silver mirror. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29488_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29489,'chemistry',67,1078,2583,'A compound that gives positive iodoform test is','[{"text": "1-pentanol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-pentanol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3-pentanol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "pentanal.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Alcohols having  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29489_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  group and aldehydes and ketones having  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29489_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> group give positive iodoform test.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29491,'chemistry',68,1113,2659,'In the conversion of X is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{H}_{2} / \\\\mathrm{Pt}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Zn}-\\\\mathrm{Hg} / \\\\mathrm{HCl}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Li} / \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}$ does not reduce olefin (alkene) double bond, it only reduces $\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{O}$ group. Thus, the reagent $(\\mathrm{X})$ is $\\mathrm{NaBH}_{4}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29491_question_1.png'),
(29492,'chemistry',70,1257,3069,'Pick the wrong statement from the following.','[{"text": "Consumption of citrus fruits and green leafy vegetables in food prevents scurvy.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deficiency of vitamin $\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{B}_{6}}$ (pyridoxine) results in convulsions.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sources of vitamin $\\\\mathrm{B_{1}}$ are yeast, milk, green vegetables and cereals.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deficiency of vitamin D causes xerophthalmia.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Deficiency of vitamin A causes xerophthalmia and deficiency of vitamin $\\mathrm{\\mathrm{D}}$ causes rickets.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29493,'chemistry',67,1072,2558,'Which one of the following is optically active?','[{"text": "n-Butyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Isobutyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2-Butanol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tertiary-Butyl alcohol", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29493_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29494,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'The one which is least basic is','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}\\\\right)_{3} \\\\mathrm{~N}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{NH}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Presence of electron withdrawing group like phenyl group decreases the electron density of nitrogen and hence, the lone pair of nitrogen is not available for donation.<br>Thus, $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5}\\right)_{3} \\mathrm{~N}$ is least basic because of the presence of three electron withdrawing phenyl groups.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
