(29540,'chemistry',68,1113,2662,'In the given compound, which of the following hydrogen is most acidic?','[{"text": "Only A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both B and C", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29540_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> This compound undergoes enolisation by the following mechanism. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29540_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Thus, hydrogen B is most acidic as it is attached with the active methylene group.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29540_question_1.png'),
