(29551,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'A compound $A\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{5} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{Cl}_{2}\\right)$ on hydrolysis gives $\\mathrm{C}_{5} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{O}$ which reacts with $\\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\mathrm{OH}$, forms iodoform, but does not give Fehling test. $A$ is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29551_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  $\\mathrm{C}_{5} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{O}$ must be aldehyde or ketone because it reacts with $\\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\mathrm{OH}$.<br>(ii) It must be a ketone as it does not give<br> Fehling test.<br>(iii) It must have $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}$ group because it gives iodoform test. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29551_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
