(29556,'chemistry',67,1074,2562,'${\\text{Isopropyl}}\\,{\\text{benzene}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{423}}\\,{\\text{K/(alkaline}}\\,{\\text{medium)}}}]{{{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{,}}\\,{\\text{Cobalt}}\\,{\\text{naphthenate}}}}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{X}}\\xrightarrow[\\Delta ]{{{\\text{dil}}{\\text{.}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}}{\\text{Y + Z}}$<br>${\\text{Y}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{conc}}{\\text{.}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}}{\\text{P}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{conc}}{\\text{.HN}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{3}}}}}{\\text{Q}}$<br>How many electron withdrawing groups is/are present in the final product \'Q\'?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The final product picric acid (Q) contains 3 electron withdrawing groups $ - {\\text{N}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}}$ groups. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29556_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29556_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29557,'chemistry',69,1176,2816,'How many of the following amines are stronger bases than ammonia?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Aliphatic amines are stronger bases than ammonia due to +I effect of alkyl groups.<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Compounds II, IV, V and VI are stronger bases than ammonia.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/69_29557_question_1.png'),
(29558,'chemistry',68,1120,2687,'The product of acid hydrolysis of $(P)$ and $(Q)$ can be distinguished by','[{"text": "Lucas reagent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2,4-DNP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fehling\'s solution", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{NaHS}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The product of (P) and (Q) are  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29558_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  $\\because$ Fehling solution cannot be reduced with acetone.Thus it can be used to differentiate ketone (acetone) and aldehyde.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29558_question_1.png'),
(29562,'chemistry',68,1118,2684,'In the above reaction A and B respectively are','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COOC}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}, \\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CHO}, \\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{OH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{OH}, \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CHO}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{OH}, \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{COOC}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29562_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29562_question_1.png'),
