(30389,'chemistry',70,1254,3059,'Functionality of protein depends on','[{"text": "its shape and structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{pH}$ of medium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Functionality of protein depends on the shape and structure, $\\mathrm{pH}$ of medium and temperature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29599,'chemistry',70,1247,3035,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Glucose gives reddish brown precipitate with Fehling solution.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Reaction of glucose with Fehling solution gives $\\mathrm{CuO}$ and gluconic acid.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both  Assertion and  Reason are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Glucose gives reddish brown precipitate with Fehling solution consists of $\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$ which gets reduced to $\\mathrm{Cu}^{+}\\left(\\mathrm{Cu}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$, not to $\\mathrm{CuO}$.<br>$\\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{12}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{6}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Glu cose }}} {\\text{ +  2CuO}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{O}}{{\\text{H}}^{\\text{ - }}}}}{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{5}}}\\mathop {{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{11}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{5}}}{\\text{COOH}}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Gluconic acid }}} {\\text{  +  C}}{{\\text{u}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}$',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2017,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29600,'chemistry',67,1089,2613,'Glycerine has one ${\\mathrm{2^{\\circ}}}$ and ____ ${\\mathrm{1^{\\circ}}}$ alcoholic groups.','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29600_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29601,'chemistry',68,1120,2687,'The end product $C$ in the following sequence of chemical reactions is','[{"text": "acetaldehyde oxime", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "formaldehyde oxime", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "methyl nitrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "acetoxime", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29601_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29601_question_1.png'),
(29602,'chemistry',69,1177,2829,'${\\text{PhN}}_{\\text{2}}^{{\\text{  +  }}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{l}}^{{\\text{ }} - {\\text{ }}}}{\\text{  +  p }} - {\\text{ Cresol}}\\xrightarrow[{({\\text{pH}} \\approx {\\text{9  -  10}})}]{{{\\text{O}}{{\\text{H}}^{{\\text{ }} - }}({\\text{273 - 278}}\\,{\\text{K}})}}{\\text{X}}$<br>The total number of sigma bonds in product \' X \' is ____ .','[{"text": "29", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "30", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "28", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "31", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29602_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Product (X) contains 29 sigma bonds.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29603,'chemistry',70,1250,3044,'Hydrolysis of sucrose with dilute aqueous sulphuric acid yields','[{"text": "${\\\\text{1:2D  -  ( + )  -  glucose; D  -  ( - )  -  fructose}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{1:2 D  -  ( - )  -  glucose ; D  -  ( + )  -  fructose}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{1:1D  -  ( - )  -  glucose ; D  -  ( + ) fructose}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{1:1D  -  ( + )  -  glucose ; D  -  ( - )  -  fructose}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'On hydrolysis with dilute aqueous sulphuric acid, sucrose forms an equimolar mixture of D - (+) - glucose and D -(-)- fructose.<br>$\\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_{{\\text{12}}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{22}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{11}}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{ Sucrose }}} {\\text{  +  }}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{O}}\\xrightarrow{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{\\text{S}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{4}}}}}$<br>$\\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{12}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{6}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{ D  -  (  +  )  -  glucose }}} {\\text{  +  }}\\mathop {{{\\text{C}}_{\\text{6}}}{{\\text{H}}_{{\\text{12}}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{6}}}}\\limits_{{\\text{ D  -  (  -  )  -  fructose }}} $',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2018,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29605,'chemistry',68,1118,2677,'Carboxylic acids readily dissolve in aqueous sodium bicarbonate, liberating carbon dioxide. Which one of the following is correct?','[{"text": "The free carboxylic acid and its conjugate base are of comparable stability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The free carboxylic acid is more stable than its conjugate base", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The conjugate base of the carboxylic acid is more stable than the free carboxylic acid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29605_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   Conjugate base,${\\rm{RCO}}{{\\rm{O}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ is more stable than the free carboxylic acid due to resonance.That is why equilibrium shifts in the forward directions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29610,'chemistry',70,1247,3036,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Glucose does not give 2, 4 - DNP test<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Glucose exists in cyclic hemiacetal form','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both  Assertion and  Reason are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In nature, glucose exists in cyclic hemiacetal form and has no free - $\\mathrm{CHO}$ group, thus it does not give 2,4-DNP test. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29610_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Therefore, Assertion and Reason both are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the given Assertion.<br>Hence, option (1) is the correct.<br>',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2019,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29611,'chemistry',67,1083,2597,'The electrophile involved in above reaction has ____ lone pair of electrons on central carbon atom.','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'This is Reimer-Tiemann reaction. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29611_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> The electrophile dichlorocarbene (${\\mathrm{: \\mathrm{CCl}_{2}}}$ ) possesses one lone pair of electrons.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_29611_question_1.png'),
(29625,'chemistry',70,1253,3056,'Lysine is least soluble in water in the $\\mathrm{pH}$ range','[{"text": "$3-4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5-6$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$6-7$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$8-9$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lysine is $\\alpha, \\in$ - diaminocaproic acid.<br>$\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~N}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$<br>$\\mathrm{CH}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{2}\\right) \\cdot \\mathrm{COOH}$<br>It is least soluble in water in the $\\mathrm{pH}$ range $6-7$.<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29612,'chemistry',68,1118,2680,'The reagents used in the conversion are','[{"text": "(i) $\\\\mathrm{PBr}_{3} /\\\\left(\\\\right.$ ii) $\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i) red $\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ /<br>(ii) alc. $\\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ (excess)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(i) $\\\\mathrm{PBr}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{NaCN} /$ (ii) $\\\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given hexanoic acid can be converted <br>into 2-amino hexanoic acid in two steps:<br>(i) Hexanoic acid is converted into $\\alpha$-bromo <br>hexanoic acid through Hell-Volhard Zelinsky<br> reaction (HVZ)  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29612_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   (ii) This $\\alpha$-bromo hexanoic acid is converted into<br> 2-aminohexanoic acid by heating it with an<br>alcoholic solution of ammonia, and this process is called ammonolysis (cleavage of C-X  bond by ammonia).  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29612_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29612_question_1.png'),
(29613,'chemistry',69,1177,2826,'${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{PhN}_{2}^{+} \\mathrm{Cl}^{-}+\\mathrm{Ph}-\\mathrm{OH} \\xrightarrow[273-278 \\mathrm{~K}]{\\mathrm{OH}^{-}}}}$Orange dye<br>Total number of sigma and pi bonds present in orange dye is ____ .','[{"text": "31", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "33", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "32", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "34", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29613_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Orange dye i.e., p-hydroxyazobenzene contains ${\\mathrm{26 \\sigma}}$ and ${\\mathrm{7 \\pi}}$ bonds.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29614,'chemistry',70,1250,3044,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Two sugar units are joined by 1,2- glycosidic bond in sucrose<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It contains $\\mathrm{C}_{1}-$ glucose and $\\mathrm{C}_{2}-$ fructose glycosidic bond.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both  Assertion and  Reason are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sucrose on hydrolysis gives equimolar mixture of D - $(+)$ - glucose and D - (-)-fructose. These two monosaccharides are held together by a glycosidic linkage between $\\mathrm{C}-1$ of $\\alpha-$ glucose and $\\mathrm{C}-2$ of $\\beta$ - fructose.<br>Therefore, both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of the given Assertion.  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29614_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2019,'AIIMS','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29616,'chemistry',68,1118,2682,'Dichlorobenzoic acid $\\xrightarrow{\\text { Mononitration }}$ Product (only one). The structure of reactant can be','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Carboxyl group of benzoic acid is meta activating group. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29616_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> As the position is ortho and para with respect to chlorine atoms, hence, the nitro occupies meta position near to p-chloro position to avoid steric hinderance.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
