(29710,'chemistry',68,1113,2668,'An organic compound of molecular formula $\\mathrm{C}_{3} \\mathrm{H}_{6} \\mathrm{O}$ did not give a silver mirror with Tollens\' reagent, but gave an oxime with hydroxylamine, it may be','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\\\mathrm{CO}-\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\\\mathrm{H}_{5} \\\\mathrm{CHO}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$({\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_2} = {\\\\rm{CH}} - {\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_2} - {\\\\rm{OH}})$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\\\mathrm{O}-\\\\mathrm{CH}=\\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'(1) Organic compound gave an oxime with hydroxylamine, therefore, it must be an aldehyde or ketone.<br>(2) Organic compound did not give silver mirror with Tollens\' reagent, therefore, it cannot be an aldehyde.<br>Therefore, compound is ketone and its molecular formula will be $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCH}_{3}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29712,'chemistry',69,1176,2817,'A compound with molecular mass 180 is acylated with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COCl}}}$ to get a compound with molecular mass 390 . One half of number of amino groups present per molecule of the former compound is ____ .','[{"text": "0.4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29712_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Each <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29712_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  group increases the molecular mass by 42.<br>Total increase in molecular mass ${\\mathrm{=390-180=210}}$<br>Number of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{NH}_{2}}}$ groups ${\\mathrm{=\\dfrac{210}{45}=5}}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$$\\dfrac{5}{2}=2.50$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29713,'chemistry',68,1113,2656,'Which of the following statement(s) is/are true about the above given reaction ?','[{"text": "Nucleophiles, such as ${\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_3}$ and its derivatives<br>${{\\\\rm{H}}_2}{\\\\rm{N}} - {\\\\rm{Z}}$ add to the carbonyl group of aldehydes<br>and ketones.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The reaction is reversible and catalysed by acid.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The equilibrium favours the product fomation due<br> to rapid dehydration of the intermediate to form", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nucleophiles, such as ammonia and its derivatives $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{~N}-\\mathrm{Z}$ add to the carbonyl group of aldehydes and ketones. The reaction is reversible and catalysed by acid. The equilibrium favours the product formation due to rapid dehydration of the intermediate to form <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29713_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_29713_question_1.png'),
(29714,'chemistry',67,1077,2572,'0.218 g of acetyl derivative of polyhydric alcohol with molecular mass ${\\mathrm{=92}}$, requires 0.168 g of KOH for hydrolysis. The number of ${\\mathrm{(-\\mathrm{OH})}}$ groups in the alcohol being halved is ____ .','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2.5", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Let formula of Alcohol ${\\mathrm{=\\mathrm{R}(\\mathrm{OH})_{n} \\&}}$ acyl derivative ${\\mathrm{=\\mathrm{R}\\left[\\mathrm{OCOCH}_{3}\\right]_{n}}}$  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29714_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Molecular mass of $\\left. {{\\rm{R[}} - {\\rm{O}} - {\\rm{COC}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{3}}}} \\right]\\,\\,({\\rm{m}}\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,{\\rm{42n}})$  Molecular mass of Alcohol ${\\mathrm{=\\mathrm{M}}}$<br>Molecular mass of ${\\mathrm{\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{3}-\\mathrm{CO}-\\right)}}$ group ${\\mathrm{=43}}$<br>${\\mathrm{1-\\mathrm{OH}}}$ group of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}}}$ replaces 1-H atom.<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ Mol. mass of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{R}\\left(\\mathrm{OCOCH}_{3}\\right)=[m+(43-1) n]}}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ = [m}}\\,{\\rm{ + }}\\,{\\rm{42n]}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{R}\\left(\\mathrm{OCOCH}_{3}\\right) \\xrightarrow{n \\mathrm{KOH}} \\mathrm{R}(\\mathrm{OH})_{n}+n \\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{COOH}}}$<br>Mol. mass of ${\\mathrm{n \\mathrm{KOH}=65 n}}$<br>0.218 g of acetyl derivative requires 0.168 g KOH ${\\mathrm{(m+42 n) \\mathrm{g}}}$ acetyl derivative requires<br>$=\\dfrac{0.168(m+42 n)}{0.218}=56 n$<br>${\\rm{30}}{\\rm{.67}}\\,{\\rm{n = 92}}\\,$<br>${\\rm{n = 2}}{\\rm{.9 = 3}}$<br>${\\rm{No}}{\\rm{.of}} - {\\rm{OH}}\\,{\\rm{groups = 3}}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\frac{3}{2} = 1.50$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
