(29726,'chemistry',67,1072,2555,'How many isomeric alcohols (including stereo isomers if any) are possible for the compound with molecular formula ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{5} \\mathrm{H}_{12} \\mathrm{O}}}$','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'i.Write the five C atoms straight chain and put ($-$OH) group at different positions  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29726_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />   ii.Write the four atoms in straight chain and put Me and ($-$OH) group at different positions. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29726_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  iii.Write the three C atoms in straight chain and put two Me and ($-$OH) group at different position. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29726_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Hence ,total isomers including stereoisomers of ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{5}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{12}}}}{\\rm{O}}$ are 8.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29727,'chemistry',69,1176,2819,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">All of the following compounds react with p -toluenesulfonyl chloride.\n${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{NH}_{2} ;\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{NH} ;\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{6} \\mathrm{H}_{5}\\right)_{3} \\mathrm{~N}}}$.</div><div class="column-right">Their products in the above reaction are soluble in aqueous ${\\text{NaOH}} \\cdot $</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hinsberg\'s reagent or p-toluenesulfonyl chloride reacts with ${\\mathrm{1^{\\circ}}}$ and ${\\mathrm{2^{\\circ}}}$ amines. The product formed of ${\\mathrm{1^{\\circ}}}$ amine with Hinsberg\'s reagent is soluble in aqueous NaOH due to acidic hydrogen bonded to nitrogen. Thus, both the statements are false. So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
