(29750,'chemistry',69,1176,2821,'The arenium ion which is not involved in the bromination of aniline is ____.','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bromination occurs at ${\\mathrm{o / p}}$ positions and it never occurs at the meta position of aniline because ${\\mathrm{-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}}}$ group is a ortho/ para directing group and the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29751,'chemistry',67,1073,2559,'Identify the product ${\\mathrm{A}}$ and product ${\\mathrm{B}}$ in the following set of reactions.','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{OH}}}$;<br>B: ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2}-\\\\mathrm{OH}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} ; \\\\mathrm{B}: \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{2} \\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Formation of \' ${\\mathrm{A}}$ \' is according to Markovnikov\'s addition. <br>Formation of \' B \' is HBO (antimarkovnikov\'s addition of water). <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29751_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29751_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, correct option is (1).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_29751_question_1.png'),
(29752,'chemistry',68,1113,2662,'On treatment of propanone with dilute $\\mathrm{Ba}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}$, the product formed is','[{"text": "aldol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "phorone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "propionaldehyde", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4-hydroxy-4-methyl-2-pentanone.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In the presence of $\\mathrm{Ba}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2^{\\prime}}$ propanone (acetone) undergoes aldol condensation as : <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29752_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29753,'chemistry',69,1176,2823,'Which of the following reaction is correct?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}{\\\\rm{CON}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ + B}}{{\\\\rm{r}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ + NaOH}} \\\\to \\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{N}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{ + N}}{{\\\\rm{a}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{C}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}{\\\\rm{ + NaBr + }}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}{\\\\rm{O}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'It follows Markovnikov\'s addition<br>(1)  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29753_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  (2) ${\\mathrm{1^{\\circ}}}$ aliphatic amine with ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{HNO}_{2}}}$ at ${\\mathrm{0-5^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}}}$ gives alcohols (rearrangement is possible) <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29753_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  (3) This reaction is known as Hoffmann bromamide degradation reaction.<br>$\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{CONH}_{2}+ & \\mathrm{Br}_{2}+4 \\mathrm{NaOH} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{5} \\mathrm{NH}_{2} \\\\& +\\mathrm{Na}_{2} \\mathrm{CO}_{3}+2 \\mathrm{NaBr}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\end{aligned}$<br>(4) In presence of heat and light, allylic bromination occurs to form 3-bromocyclohex1 -ene <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29753_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (1)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29754,'chemistry',67,1077,2578,'The final product ${\\mathrm{A}}$, formed in the following reaction sequence is<br>${\\text{ph}} - {\\text{CH = C}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}\\xrightarrow[\\begin{subarray}{l} \n  {\\text{(iii)HBr}} \\\\ \n  {\\text{(iv)Mg,ether,then}} \\\\ \n  {\\text{HCHO/}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{{\\text{O}}^{\\text{ + }}} \n\\end{subarray} ]{\\begin{subarray}{l} \n  {\\text{(i)B}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}} \\\\ \n  {\\text{(ii)}}{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{2}}}{{\\text{O}}_{\\text{2}}},\\mathop {\\text{O}}\\limits^ -  {\\text{H}} \n\\end{subarray} }$','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{ph}} - {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}} - {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}} - {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{ph}} - {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}} - {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_{\\\\text{2}}} - {\\\\text{C}}{{\\\\text{H}}_2} - {\\\\text{OH}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29754_explanation_1.jpg\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, correct option is (4).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
