(29756,'chemistry',68,1113,2656,'Formation of cyanohydrin from a ketone is an example of','[{"text": "electrophilic addition", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "nucleophilic addition", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "nucleophilic substitution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "electrophilic substitution.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29756_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br> Thus, it is an example of nucleophilic addition because the attacking species is a nucleophile.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
