(29758,'chemistry',67,1077,2572,'Read the Assertion  and  Reason carefully to mark the correct option out of the options given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Alcohols react both as nucleophiles and electrophiles.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Alcohols react with active metals such sodium,potassium and aluminium to yeild corresponding alkoxides and liberate hydrogen.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Alcohols are versatile compounds. They react both as nucleophiles and electrophiles.Alcohols and phenols react with active metals such as sodium, potassium and aluminium to yield corresponding alkoxides/phenoxides and liberate hydrogen,<br>$\\text { e.g., } 2 \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{OH}+2 \\mathrm{Na} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{ONa}+\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\uparrow$<br>But it\'s not the correct explanation. So, correct option is (2).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29759,'chemistry',68,1117,2676,'Benzoic acid has higher molecular weight in benzene and less in water because','[{"text": "water has lower freezing point and higher boiling point than benzene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "it dissociates to a greater extent in benzene than in water.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "it associates in water and dissociates in benzene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "it dissociates in water and associates in benzene.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In water : <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29759_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br> In benzene solution :<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29759_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29760,'chemistry',70,1253,3053,'Identify basic $\\alpha $ -amino acid from the following','[{"text": "Alanine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Asparagine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lysine is basic $\\propto-$ amino acid. It has extra $-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group, so basic',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29761,'chemistry',69,1176,2821,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Aniline reacts with conc. ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{SO}_{4}}}$, followed by heating at ${\\mathrm{453-473 \\mathrm{~K}}}$ gives p-aminobenzene sulphonic acid, which gives blood red colour in the \'Lassaigne\'s test\'.</div><div class="column-right">In Friedel-Craft\'s alkylation and acylation reactions, aniline forms salt with the ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}}}$ catalyst. Due to this, nitrogen of aniline aquires a positive charge and acts as deactivating group.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/69_29761_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  In case, nitrogen and sulphur both are present in an organic compound, sodium thiocyanate (from Lassaigne\'s extract) is formed. It gives blood red colour in the Lassaigne test.Aniline does not undergo Friedel-Crafts reaction (alkylation and acetylation) due to salt-formation with aluminium chloride, the Lewis acid, which is used as a catalyst. Due to this, nitrogen of aniline acquires positive charge and hence acts as à strong deactivating group for further reaction. So, the correct option is (3)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29762,'chemistry',67,1070,2552,'Common name of Benzene-1,2-diol is','[{"text": "catechol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "quinol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "o-cresol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "resorcinol", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Catechol is the common name of Benzene-1,2-diol.  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29762_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, correct option is (1).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29763,'chemistry',68,1113,2670,'${\\left( {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{H}}_3}} \\right)_2}{\\text{CO}}\\xrightarrow[{{\\text{HCl}}}]{{{\\text{NaCN}}}}{\\text{A}}\\xrightarrow[{}]{{{{\\text{H}}_{\\text{3}}}{{\\text{O}}^{\\text{ + }}}}}{\\text{B}}$ <br> In the above sequence of reactions (A) and (B) are','[{"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}(\\\\mathrm{OH}) \\\\mathrm{CN},\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}(\\\\mathrm{OH}) \\\\mathrm{COOH}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}(\\\\mathrm{OH}) \\\\mathrm{CN},\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}(\\\\mathrm{OH})_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}(\\\\mathrm{OH}) \\\\mathrm{CN},\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{CHCOOH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}(\\\\mathrm{OH}) \\\\mathrm{CN},\\\\left(\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}\\\\right)_{2} \\\\mathrm{C}=\\\\mathrm{O}$<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29763_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(29764,'chemistry',70,1247,3032,'Which of the following reagents is used to identify straight chain of glucose?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HI}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{dil}}{\\\\text{.}}\\\\,{\\\\text{HN}}{{\\\\text{O}}_{\\\\text{3}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{HCN}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{Acetic anhydride}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'On prolonged heating with $\\mathrm{HI}$, it forms n-hexane, suggesting that all the six carbon atoms are linked in a straight chain  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_29764_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2021,'MHTCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
