(29769,'chemistry',67,1083,2596,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Bromination of phenol in solvent with low polarity such as ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CHCl}_{3}}}$ or ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{CS}_{2}}}$ requires Lewis acid catalyst.</div><div class="column-right">The Lewis acid catalyst polarises the bromine to generate ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Br}^{+}}}$.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29769_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  This reaction does not require any catalyst. Presence of Lewis acid promotes generation of ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Br}^{+}}}$in some reactions, e.g., monohalogenation of benzene and in some other arenes, reaction is carried out at low temperature in the absence of sunlight and in presence of Lewis acid catalyst. So, correct option is (2).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
