(29771,'chemistry',68,1118,2679,'An optically active compound $\'{\\text{X}}\'$ has molecular formula $\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\mathrm{H}_{8} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$. It evolves $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ with aqueous $\\mathrm{NaHCO}_{3}$. \' $\\mathrm{X}$ \' reacts with $\\mathrm{LiAlH}_{4}$ to give an achiral compound. $\'{\\text{X}}\'$ is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'As $({\\text{X}}\\xrightarrow{{{\\text{NaHC}}{{\\text{O}}_{{\\text{3(aq}}{\\text{.)}}}}}}{\\text{C}}{{\\text{O}}_2})$<br> $\\therefore$ It must contains $-\\mathrm{COOH}$ group. <br> <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_29771_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
