(29792,'chemistry',67,1083,2591,'For the given compounds, the correct order of increasing ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}}}$ value: Choose the correct answer from the options given below','[{"text": "(II) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (V)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(V) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (III)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(IV) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (V) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(V) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I)", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'acidic nature ${\\mathrm{\\propto-\\mathrm{M}}}$ effect &  $-$I effect$\\propto \\dfrac{1}{+\\mathrm{M\\,effect}} \\& \\dfrac{1}{+\\mathrm{I} \\text { effect }}$$-$<br>M effect is more dominated at ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{o} / \\mathrm{p}}}$ positions. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29792_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29792_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Hence the order of pKa values is (II) ${\\mathrm{ < }}$ (IV) ${\\mathrm{ < }}$ (III) ${\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I) ${\\mathrm{ < }}$ (V).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/67_29792_question_1.png'),
