(29824,'chemistry',67,1083,2591,'Read the Assertion  and  Reason carefully to mark the correct option out of the options given below.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{pK}_{\\mathrm{a}}}}$ value of phenol is 10.0 while that of ethanol is 15.9 .<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Ethanol is stronger acid than phenol.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is incorrect but reason is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phenol are stronger acids than alcohols.The ionisation of an alcohol and a phenol takes place as follows <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29824_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/67_29824_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  The declocalisation of negative charge makes phenoxide ion more stable and favours the ionisation of phenols.Higher Ka,lower pKa-strong acid.Given pKa values are correct values.So,correct option is (3)',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
