(29827,'chemistry',68,1120,2687,'A compound with molecular formula $\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$ is converted by the action of acetyl chloride to a compound of molecular mass 190. The original compound $\\left(\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{O}_{3}\\right)$ has','[{"text": "two OH groups", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "four OH groups", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "one OH group", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "three OH groups.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Molecular mass of  $\\mathrm{C}_{4} \\mathrm{H}_{10} \\mathrm{O}_{3}$<br>${ = 4 \\times 12 + 10 \\times 1 + 3 \\times 16 = 106\\,{\\rm{u}}}$<br>Acetylation introduces $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}$ - group by replacing H of  $ - \\,{\\rm{OH}}$ group.<br>Molecular mass of $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}=16+12 \\times 2+3 \\times 1$<br>$=43 \\mathrm{u}$<br>No. of ${ - {\\rm{OH}}}$ groups in  the compounds <br>$=$ Molecular mass of  ${{{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{4}}}{{\\rm{H}}_{{\\rm{10}}}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{3}}}}$ + <br>2 $ \\times $ Molecular mass of $\\mathrm{CH}_{3} \\mathrm{CO}-190$<br>$=106+43 \\times 2-190=2$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
