(30090,'chemistry',70,1247,3036,'${\\text{D}} - ( + ) - {\\text{Glyceraldehyde}}\\xrightarrow[\\begin{subarray}{l} \n  ({\\text{ii}})\\,\\,{{\\text{H}}_2}{\\text{O}}/{{\\text{H}}^ + } \\\\ \n  ({\\text{iii}})\\,\\,\\,{\\text{HN}}{{\\text{O}}_3} \n\\end{subarray} ]{{({\\text{i}})\\,\\,{\\text{HCN}}}}$<br>The products formed in the above reaction are','[{"text": "two optically active products", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "two optically inactive products", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "one optically active and one meso product", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "one optically inactive and one meso product.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_30090_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  Meso compounds are optically inactive due to plane of symmetry.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(30093,'chemistry',68,1111,2649,'This reduction reaction is known as','[{"text": "Wolff-Kishner reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Etard reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rosenmund reduction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stephen reduction.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Conversion of acid chlorides to aldehydes using $\\mathrm{H}_{2}-\\mathrm{Pd} / \\mathrm{BaSO}_{4}$ is known as Rosenmund reduction. So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_30093_question_1.png'),
