(30099,'chemistry',70,1253,3056,'Which is not true for arginine?','[{"text": "It has a fairly high melting point.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It has high solubility in benzene.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is associated with more than one   $\\\\mathrm{pK}_{\\\\mathrm{a}}$ values.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a crystalline solid.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Arginine is a polar compound and it has high solubility in polar solvents like water. It is not soluble in non-polar solvents like benzene.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(30100,'chemistry',68,1111,2649,'Identify the name of the following reaction.','[{"text": "Stephen reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Etard reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rosenmund reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gatterman - Koch reaction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Benzene on reaction with $\\mathrm{CO}+\\mathrm{HCl}$ in the presence of anhyd. $\\mathrm{AlCl}_{3}$ to form benzaldehyde is known as Gatterman-Koch reaction. So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/68_30100_question_1.png'),
(30102,'chemistry',68,1113,2662,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Acidity of $\\alpha$-hydrogens of aldehydes and ketones is responsible for Aldol reaction.</div><div class="column-right">Reaction between benzaldehyde and ethanal will not give cross-Aldol product.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Aldehydes and ketones with $\\alpha$-hydrogen give aldol condensation reaction. Benzaldehyde and ethanal can give cross-Aldol condensation reaction. <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_30102_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_30102_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_30102_explanation_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> So, the correct option is (1).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
