(30114,'chemistry',70,1254,3059,'Following tetrapeptide can be represented as<br> <br>(F, L, D, Y, I, Q, P are one letter codes for amino acids.)','[{"text": "FIQY", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "YQLF", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PLDY", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "FLDY", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/70_30114_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br>Arranging these four peptides we will get the given tetrapeptide, thus the tetrapeptide is FLDY.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/70_30114_question_1.png'),
(30115,'chemistry',68,1113,2656,'Which among the following aldehydes is most reactive towards nucleophilic addition reactions?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Less steric carbonyl compound is more reactive towards nucleophilic addition.  <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/68_30115_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  ${\\rm{ }}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{(formaldehyde)}}$  <br>is least  sterically hindered, so it is most reactive towards nucleophilic addition reactions. So, the correct option is (2).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
