(30120,'chemistry',70,1250,3047,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully and mark the correct option.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Ketoses give Seliwanoff\'s test faster than aldoses.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Ketoses undergo $\\beta$-elimination followed by formation of furfural.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The reagent of Seliwanoff\'s test consists of resorcinol and concentrated HCl . Ketoses are more rapidly dehydrated than aldoses.Ketoses undergo dehydration in the presence of concentrated acid to yield 5-hydroxymethyl furfural. The dehydrated ketose reacts with two equivalents of resorcinol in a series of condensation reactions to produce a complex (not a precipitate), termed xanthenoid, with deep cherry red colour. Aldoses may react slightly to produce a faint pink to cherry red colour if the test is prolonged. Thus , both assertion and reason are correct and reason is the correct explanation of the assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
