(36735,'physics',23,860,1970,'A circular plate of uniform thickness has a diameter of $112\\,cm.$ A circular portion of diameter $84\\,cm$ is removed from one edge as shown in the figure. The distance of centre of mass of the remaining portion from the centre of plate will be','[{"text": "$12\\\\,cm$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$18\\\\,cm$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$21\\\\,cm$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$29\\\\,cm$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Let $m$ be mass of disc removed,<br>$\\therefore \\quad m = \\frac{M}{{\\pi {{(56)}^2}}} \\times \\pi {(42)^2}$<br>$ = \\frac{{9M}}{{16}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{ (Surface}}\\,{\\text{density}}\\,{\\text{is constant)}}$<br>$\\therefore $  Remaining mass $ = M - \\frac{{9M}}{{16}} = \\frac{{7M}}{{16}}$<br>$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{{7M}}{{16}} \\times O{O_2} = \\frac{{9M}}{{16}} \\times O{O_1}$$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,(1)$<br>$\\therefore \\quad O{O_1} = (56 - 42)cm = 14\\,cm$<br>Substituting in equation (1) we get,<br>$O{O_2} = \\frac{9}{7} \\times 14\\,cm = 18\\,cm$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','physics/23_36735_question_1.png'),
