(36740,'physics',27,1380,3311,'A Sealed glass jar is full of water. When it is kept in a freezing mixture, it is broken because','[{"text": "Water expands from$4^\\\\circ C$ to $0^\\\\circ C$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ice expands while melting", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water expands due to freezing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ice expands since its temperature falls below $0^\\\\circ C$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Water density is maximum at $4^\\circ C$. If we heat or cool water present at $4^\\circ C$  expands. Option (1) is correct',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(36741,'physics',25,896,2059,'A thick rope of density $\\rho$ and length $L$ is hung from a rigid support. The Young\'s modulus of the material of rope is $Y$. The increase in length of the rope due to its own weight is','[{"text": "$(1/4)\\\\rho g\\\\,{L^2}{\\\\rm{/}}Y$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$(1/2)\\\\rho g\\\\,{L^2}{\\\\rm{/}}Y$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\rho g\\\\,{L^2}{\\\\rm{/}}Y$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\rho g\\\\,L{\\\\rm{/}}Y$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\Delta \\ell  = \\frac{{F(L/2)}}{{AY}} = \\frac{{(AL\\rho g)(L/2)}}{{AY}}$<br>$ = \\left( {\\frac{1}{2}} \\right)\\rho g\\,{L^2}/Y$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(36744,'physics',27,1380,3311,'Match the following<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Rate of variation of density $\\left( \\rho  \\right)$ is zero for water<br>B. Least volume of water<br>C. Triple point</div><div class="column-right">P. Less than $4^\\circ C$<br>Q. Coexistence of three phases of a substance<br>R. Equal to $4^\\circ C$</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\kern 1pt} {\\\\rm{C - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B - Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B  -  R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{B  -  P,}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{C  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The density of water increases from $0 \\rightarrow 4^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and reaches maximum at $4^\\circ \\,C$. After crossing $4^\\circ \\,C$ it decreases. So rate of variation of density is zero at $4^\\circ C$',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(36745,'physics',25,896,2059,'If the ratio of radii of two wires of same material is $2: 1$ and ratio of their lengths is $4: 1$, then the ratio of the normal forces that will produce the same extension in the length of two wires is','[{"text": "$2: 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4: 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1: 4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1: 1$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$Y = \\frac{{F\\ell }}{{A\\Delta \\ell }}; \\Rightarrow F = \\frac{{YA\\ell }}{\\ell }$<br>$\\frac{{{F_1}}}{{\\,{F_2}}} = \\frac{{{A_1}}}{{\\,{A_2}}} \\times \\frac{{{l_2}}}{{{l_1}}} = \\frac{{r_1^2}}{{r_2^2}} \\times \\frac{{{l_2}}}{{{l_1}}} = \\frac{4}{1} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = 1:1$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(36746,'physics',26,1133,2710,'Two pieces of metal when immersed in a liquid have equal upthrust on them; then','[{"text": "Both pieces must have equal densities", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both pieces must have equal weights", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both pieces must have equal volumes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both are floating to the same depth", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Since, up thrust $$(F)=V \\sigma g$$ i.e., $$F \\propto V$$ where $$V$$ is the volume of the solid and $$\\sigma$$ is the density of liquid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
