(39506,'physics',32,482,988,'A spherical capacitor is made of two conducting  spherical shells of radii $a$ and  $b$.The space  between the shells is filled with a dielectric of dielectric constant $K$ upto a radius $b$ as shown  in figure. Calculate the capacitance.','[{"text": "$\\\\frac{{K4\\\\pi {\\\\varepsilon _0}abc}}{{Ka\\\\left( {c - b} \\\\right) + c\\\\left( {b - a} \\\\right)}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{K4\\\\pi {\\\\varepsilon _0}abc}}{{Kab + bc}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{K4\\\\pi {\\\\varepsilon _0}abc}}{{{a^2} + {b^2} + {c^2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The capacitance system can be redrawn as shown in the figure.<br>${C_1} = \\frac{{K4\\pi {\\varepsilon _o}(ab)}}{{b - a}}{C_2} = \\frac{{4\\pi {\\varepsilon _o}(bc)}}{{c - b}}$<br>${C_{13}} = \\frac{{{C_1}{C_2}}}{{{C_1} + {C_2}}} = \\frac{{K4\\pi {\\varepsilon _o}abc}}{{Ka(c - b) + c(b - a)}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','physics/32_39506_question_1.png'),
