(44203,'physics',36,908,2098,'Two conducting circular loops $A$ and $B$ are placed in the same plane with their centres coinciding as shown in figure. The mutual inductance between them is','[{"text": "$\\\\dfrac{\\\\mu_{0} \\\\pi a^{2}}{2 b}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{\\\\mu_{0}}{2 \\\\pi} \\\\cdot \\\\dfrac{b^{2}}{a}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{\\\\mu_{0} \\\\pi b^{2}}{2 a}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{\\\\mu_{0}}{2 \\\\pi} \\\\cdot \\\\dfrac{a^{2}}{b}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Let current in the outer loop $B$ be $i$.<br><img src=\'/img/data/physics/36_44203_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  <br>Magnetic field at centre of loop $O$ is given as,<br>$B=\\dfrac{\\mu_{0} i}{2 b}$<br>Now, magnetic flux through inner coil $A$,<br>$\\phi=\\vec{B} \\cdot \\vec{A}$<br>$\\therefore \\phi=B \\times \\pi a^{2}$<br>$\\Rightarrow \\phi=\\dfrac{\\mu_{0} i}{2 b} \\times \\pi a^{2}$<br>As per definition of magnetic flux, $\\phi=M i$<br>$\\Rightarrow M=\\dfrac{\\phi}{i}$<br>$\\Rightarrow M=\\dfrac{\\mu_{0}}{2 b} \\times \\pi a^{2}$<br>So, option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','physics/36_44203_question_1.png'),
(44204,'physics',39,1102,2626,'If the work function of a metal is \' $$\\phi$$ \' and the frequency of the incident light is \' $$v$$ \', there is no emission of photoelectron if','[{"text": "$$v=\\\\dfrac{\\\\phi}{h}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$v < \\\\dfrac{\\\\phi}{h}$$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$v \\\\geq \\\\dfrac{\\\\phi}{h}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$$v>\\\\dfrac{\\\\phi}{h}$$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'For no emission of photoelectron, energy of incident light $$ < $$ Work function<br>$$\\Rightarrow h v < \\phi \\Rightarrow v < \\dfrac{\\phi}{h}$$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
