(45922,'physics',37,973,2268,'A resistor $R$, an inductor $L$ and capacitor $C$ are connected in series to an oscillator of frequency $n$. If the resonant frequency is $n_{r}$, then the current lags behind voltage, when','[{"text": "$n=0$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$n < n_{r}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$n=n_{r}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$n>n_{r}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In a series $L C R$ circuit, the current lags behind voltage if, $X_{L}>X_{C}$<br>$i.e.,$ $\\omega L>\\dfrac{1}{\\omega C} ; \\omega>\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{L C}}$ or $n>\\dfrac{1}{2 \\pi \\sqrt{L C}}$<br>As $n_{r}=\\dfrac{1}{2 \\pi \\sqrt{L C}}$<br>$\\therefore \\quad n>n_{r}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(45923,'physics',41,408,814,'Among the following true option is','[{"text": "Energy released per nucleon is same in both fission  and fusion reactions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy released per nucleon is more in fission than  in fusion reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Energy released per nucleon is less in fission than  in fusion  reaction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "No energy is released in fusion reaction", "isCorrect": false}]',2,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(45924,'physics',40,239,478,'In Bohr model of hydrogen atom, the force on the electron depends on the principal quantum number ${n}$ as','[{"text": "${F \\\\propto 1 / n^{3}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${F \\\\propto 1 / n^{4}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${F \\\\propto 1 / n^{5}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "does not depend on ${n}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Force ${\\propto r^{\\frac{1}{2}}}$,<br>Radius ${\\propto n^{2}}$<br>${\\Rightarrow}$ force ${\\propto \\dfrac{1}{n^{4}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(45926,'physics',37,973,2265,'An inductive circuit contains a resistance of $10 \\Omega$ and an inductance of $2.0H$. If an AC voltage of $120\\,V$ and frequency of $60\\,Hz$ is applied to this circuit, the current in circuit would be nearly','[{"text": "$0.32\\\\,A$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.16\\\\,A$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$0.43\\\\,A$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.80\\\\,A$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Impedence, $Z=\\sqrt{R^{2}+X_{L}^{2}}$<br>Current, $I=\\dfrac{V}{Z}=\\dfrac{V}{\\sqrt{R^{2}+X_{L}^{2}}}$<br>Here, $R = 10\\,\\Omega ,L = 2.0H,V = 120\\,V$<br>$v = 60\\,H\\,z,\\omega  = 2\\,\\pi v = 120\\,\\pi \\,rad{s^{ - 1}}$<br>${X_L} = \\omega L = 240\\,\\pi  \\simeq 754\\,\\Omega $<br>$\\therefore \\quad I = \\frac{{120}}{{\\sqrt {{{10}^2} + {{754}^2}} }} = 0.16\\,A$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
