(46019,'physics',42,323,593,'A zener diode','[{"text": "Is a lightly doped junction diode", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heavily doped junction diode", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Is either $p$-type or $n$-type", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Has no $P$-$N$ junction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(46023,'physics',42,323,592,'The reverse bias in a junction diode is changed from 5$V$ to 15$V$ then the value of current changes from $38\\,\\mu A$ to $88\\,\\mu A$. The resistance of junction diode will be','[{"text": "$4 \\\\times {10^5}\\\\Omega $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3 \\\\times {10^5}\\\\Omega $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\times {10^5}\\\\Omega $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${10^6}\\\\Omega $", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$R = \\frac{{\\Delta V}}{{\\Delta I}} = \\frac{{15 - 5}}{{\\left( {88 - 38} \\right) \\times {{10}^{ - 6}}}} = \\frac{{10}}{{50 \\times {{10}^{ - 6}}}}$<br>$ = \\frac{{{{10}^6}}}{5} = \\frac{{10}}{5} \\times {10^5} = 2 \\times {10^5}\\Omega $',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(46024,'physics',40,241,480,'One of the lines in the emission spectrum of $L{i^{2 + }}$ has the same wavelength as that of the ${2^{nd{\\rm{ }}}}$ line of Balmer series in hydrogen spectrum. The electronic transition corresponding to this line is $n = 12 \\to n = x$. Find the value of $x$.','[{"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'For $2^{\\text {nd }}$ line of Balmer series in hydrogen spectrum<br>$\\frac{1}{\\lambda } = R{\\rm{ }}(1){\\rm{ }}\\left( {\\frac{1}{{{2^2}}} - \\frac{1}{{{4^2}}}} \\right) = \\frac{3}{{16}}R$<br>For $L{i^{2 + }}\\left[ {\\frac{1}{\\lambda } = R \\times 9\\left( {\\frac{1}{{{x^2}}} - \\frac{1}{{{{12}^2}}}} \\right) = \\frac{{3R}}{{16}}} \\right]$<br>which is satisfied by $n = 12 \\to n = 6$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(46025,'physics',41,406,809,'In the nuclear reaction  ${}_6{C^{11}} \\to {}_5{B^{11}} + {\\beta ^ + } + X,$ what does  $X$ stand for?','[{"text": "A proton", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A neutrino", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A neutron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "An electron", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${}_6{C^{11}} \\to {}_5{B^{11}} + {\\beta ^ + } + v$ because ${\\beta ^ + } = {}_1{e^0}$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(46027,'physics',42,323,592,'In the following reverse biased diode is','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'For reverse biasing of an ideal diode, the potential of $n$-side should be higher than potential of $p$-side. Only option (4) is satisfying the 	criterion for reverse biasing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(46028,'physics',41,406,809,'In the following reaction the value of  $\'X\'$ is ${}_7{N^{14}} + {}_2H{e^4} \\to X + {}_1{H^1}$','[{"text": "${}_8{{\\\\rm{O}}^{17}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${}_7{{\\\\rm{O}}^{16}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${}_7{{\\\\rm{N}}^{16}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$_8{{\\\\rm{N}}^{17}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${}_7^{14}N + {}_2^4He \\to {}_8^{17}O + {}_1^1H$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(46029,'physics',40,240,479,'The third line of Balmer series of an ion equivalent to hydrogen atom has wavelength of $108.5\\,nm$. The ground state energy of an electron of this ion will be','[{"text": "$3.4\\\\,eV$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$13.6\\\\,eV$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$54.4\\\\,eV$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$122.4\\\\,eV$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For third line of Balmer series ${n_1} = 2,{n_2} = 5$<br>${\\therefore \\frac{1}{\\lambda } = R{Z^2}\\left[ {\\frac{1}{{n_1^2}} - \\frac{1}{{n_2^2}}} \\right]{\\rm{ }}}$ given ${{Z^2} = \\frac{{n_1^2n_2^2}}{{\\left( {n_2^2 - n_1^2} \\right)\\lambda R}}}$<br>${E =  - \\frac{{13.6{Z^2}}}{{{n^2}}} = \\frac{{ - 13.6{{(2)}^2}}}{{{{(1)}^2}}} =  - 54.4\\,eV}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(46030,'physics',37,977,2770,'In the circuit shown the transformer is ideal with turn ratio ${\\dfrac{N_{1}}{N_{2}}=\\dfrac{5}{1}}$. The voltage of the source is ${V_{{s}}=300 {~V}}$. The voltage measured across the load resistance ${R_{l}}$ is 50 $V$ . Find the value of resistance ${R(}$ in ${\\Omega}$ ) in the primary circuit.','[{"text": "$250\\\\,\\\\Omega $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$500\\\\,\\\\Omega $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$700\\\\,\\\\Omega $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$300\\\\,\\\\Omega $", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$V_{1}=\\left(\\dfrac{N_{1}}{N_{2}}\\right) V_{2}\\left[V_{2}=V_{L}=50 {~V}\\right]$<br>and $\\quad V_{s}=I_{2} R+\\left(\\dfrac{N_{1}}{N_{2}}\\right) V_{2}$<br>Current in secondary circuit is $I_{2}=\\dfrac{V_{2}}{R_{L}}$<br>and $\\quad I_{1}=\\left(\\dfrac{N_{2}}{N_{1}}\\right) I_{2}=\\dfrac{N_{2}}{N_{1}} \\dfrac{V_{2}}{R_{L}}$<br>$\\therefore \\quad V_{s}\\left(\\dfrac{N_{2}}{N_{1}}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{V_{2}}{R_{1}}\\right) R+\\left(\\dfrac{N_{2}}{N_{1}}\\right) V_{2}$<br>$ \\Rightarrow \\,\\,R = \\frac{{{N_1}{R_L}}}{{{N_2}{V_2}}}\\left[ {{V_s} - {V_2}\\left( {\\frac{{{N_1}}}{{{N_2}}}} \\right)} \\right]$<br>$ = 5 \\times \\frac{{100}}{{50}}\\left[ {300 - 50 \\times 5} \\right]$<br>$ = 100 \\times 50 = 500\\,\\,\\Omega $',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','physics/37_46030_question_1.png'),
(46031,'physics',42,323,592,'The value of current in the following diagrams is (diode assumed to be ideal one)','[{"text": "$0.1\\\\,amp$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.01\\\\,amp$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1\\\\,amp$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{Zero}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In reverse bias current through ideal diode is zero',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','physics/42_46031_question_1.png');
