(46182,'physics',40,240,479,'The radiation emitted when an electron jumps from ${n}=3$ to ${n}=2$ orbit in a hydrogen atom falls on a metal to produce photoelectrons. Find the work function  of the metal, when maximum kinetic energy of ejected electron is $1.376 \\times 10^{-19} {~J}$.','[{"text": "$1.04\\\\,eV$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$3.64\\\\,eV$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$7.16\\\\,eV$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5.09\\\\,eV$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Energy of the photon emitted when the electron makes a transition from ${n}=3$ to ${n}=2$ energy level,<br>$h \\nu=E_{3}-E_{2}=-13.6\\left[\\dfrac{1}{3^{2}}-\\dfrac{1}{2^{2}}\\right] {eV}=1.88\\, {eV}$<br>From Einstien\'s photoelectric effect equation,<br>${h} v=\\phi+{KE}_{\\max }$<br>So, $\\phi=(1.9-0.86) 7\\,{eV}$<br>$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\left( {\\because 1.376 \\times {{10}^{ - 19}}\\,J = 0.86\\,eV} \\right)$<br>$=1.04\\, {eV}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(46183,'physics',41,403,801,'Assume that the nuclear mass is of the order of ${10^{ - 27}}\\,kg$ and the nuclear radius is of the order of ${10^{ - 15}}\\,m$. The nuclear density is of the order of','[{"text": "${10^2}\\\\,kg{\\\\rm{/}}{m^3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${10^{10}}\\\\,kg{\\\\rm{/}}{m^3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${10^{17}}\\\\,kg{\\\\rm{/}}{m^3}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${10^{31}}\\\\,kg{\\\\rm{/}}{m^3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Density $d=\\dfrac{M}{V}=\\dfrac{M}{\\dfrac{4}{3} \\pi R^{3}}$<br>$d=\\dfrac{3 M}{4 \\pi R^{3}}=\\dfrac{3}{4 \\pi}\\left(\\dfrac{A m}{A R_{0}^{3}}\\right)=\\dfrac{3 m}{4 \\pi R_{0}^{3}}$<br>$=\\dfrac{3}{4 \\pi} \\dfrac{10^{-27}}{10^{-45}}$<br>$\\Rightarrow d$ is of the order of ${10^{17}}\\,kg{\\rm{/}}{m^3}$.<br>Correct option is (3).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
