(47141,'biology',102,772,1677,'Name the gases released from molten mass that covered the earth\'s surface?','[{"text": "Methane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water vapour, methane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water vapour, methane, carbon dioxide and ammonia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carbon dioxide and ammonia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Water vapour, methane, carbon dioxide and Ammonia were released from molten mass which covered the earth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47142,'biology',102,772,1677,'In primordial atmosphere when the living organism evolved the respiration process was','[{"text": "Aerobic as it was more complex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaerobic because early atmosphere contained little or no oxygen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Aerobic as it released more energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaerobic as it released more energy", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In primordial atmosphere, there was no oxygen or less oxygen. Hence the organisms were anaerobes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47143,'biology',102,772,1677,'According to one of the most widely accepted theories, earths atmosphere before origin of life was','[{"text": "Oxidizing along with $\\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reducing with $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ in small amount", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reducing with oxygen absent in $\\\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ form", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oxidizing", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Before the origin of life, atmosphere of earth was strongly reducing (without free oxygen). At high temperature, free atoms combined to form molecules and simple inorganic compounds. Oxygen, Hydrogen, Nitrogen, Carbon could not exist in free state and hence they combine among themselves and form $\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\mathrm{H}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$ vapour.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47144,'biology',102,772,1677,'Identify the wrong statement regarding the formation of earth','[{"text": "Earth, along with the other planets, is believed to have been born 4.5 billion years ago", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "From solidified cloud of dust and gases left over from the creation of the Sun", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "For perhaps 500 million years, the interior of earth stayed solid and relatively cool.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primitive earth had nitrogen, hydrogen and oxygen abundantly", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Early the primitive earth contained oxygendeficient but carbon dioxide rich atmosphere throughout the archaen. Evidence for this early atmosphere can be found in the rocks. Archaen deposits lack minerals such as hematite and instead contain abundant pyrite $\\left(\\mathrm{FeS}_{2}\\right)$ Due to lower reactivity of sulphur, pyrite can only form in oxygen deficient environments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47145,'biology',102,772,1677,'Water vapour, $\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ were released from','[{"text": "Atmosphere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Molten mass covering the surface", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "From the explosion caused", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Earth was supposed to be formed around 4.5 billion years ago. There was no atmosphere in the early earth. Water vapour, methane, carbon dioxide and ammonia released from molten mass covered the surface.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47146,'biology',102,772,1677,'Possible early source of energy was','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "UV radiation and lightning", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyll", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Available evidences and demonstrated experiments states that ultra violet radiation and lightning were possibly early source of energy',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47147,'biology',102,772,1677,'Select the most appropriate sentence.<br>i. Water vapour, ethane, carbondioxide and ammonia released from molten mass covered the surface.<br>ii. The UV rays from the sun brokeup water into Hydrogen and Oxygen and the heavier $\\mathrm{H}_{2}$ escaped. <br>iii. Oxygen combined with ammonia and methane to form water, $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and others. The ozone layer was formed.<br>iv. As it cooled, the water vapor fell as rain, to fill all the depressions and form oceans.','[{"text": "Only i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i and ii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii and iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only iii and iv are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'4-oxygen combined with ammonia and methane to form water, $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and others. The ozone layer was formed. As it cooled, the water vapor fell as rain, to fill all the depressions and form oceans.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47148,'biology',102,772,1677,'Early Greek thinkers thought units of life called spores were transferred to different planets including earth. What is this theory referred to as?','[{"text": "Cosmic panspermia theory", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Special creation theory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Theory of abiogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Theory of biogenesis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Panspermia - According to early Greek thinkers, units of life were called panspermia. They assumed that these panspermia were transferred to different planets including earth, which resulted in life.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47149,'biology',102,772,1677,'According to theory of spontaneous generation:','[{"text": "Life was created by special creation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Life came from pre-existing non-living organic molecules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Life came from dead and decaying matter", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Life came from another planet", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The idea of spontaneous generation is an obsolete theory that states that living organisms can originate from inanimate objects. Other common examples of spontaneous generation were that dust creates fleas, maggots arise from rotting meat, and bread or wheat left in a dark corner produces mice.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47150,'biology',102,772,1677,'According to the theory of abiogenesis, life originates from','[{"text": "Chemicals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Other planets", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-living", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Spontaneously", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Theory of Abiogenesis states that life or living organisms evolved from inorganic or inanimate substances.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47151,'biology',102,772,1677,'Who experimentally discarded the theory of spontaneous generation?','[{"text": "Louis Pasteur", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oparian & Haldane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Darwin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alfred Wallace", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Louis Pasteur\'s 1859 experiment is widely seen as having settled the question of spontaneous generation. He boiled a meat broth in a swan neck flask; the bend in the neck of the flask prevented falling particles from reaching the broth, while still allowing the free flow of air.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47152,'biology',102,772,1677,'Pasteur\'s experiments and similar ones that followed convinced most people that spontaneous generation of life did not happen because','[{"text": "Pasteur was extremely meticulous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pasteur used very fine mesh screens to cover his flasks", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pasteur did not boil his flask for a long time", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pasteur\'s swan necked flasks ruled out the objection that spoiled air could have contaminated his experiments", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Many argued that Pasteur used very fine mesh screens to cover his flasks and said that it was reason why the spontaneous generation could not happen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47153,'biology',102,772,1677,'Which one of the following experiments suggests that simplest living organisms could not have originated spontaneously from nonliving matter?','[{"text": "Microbes did not appear in stored meat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Larvae could appear in decaying organic matter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meat was not spoiled, when heated and kept sealed in a vessel", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Microbes appeared from unsterilized organic matter", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When meat was kept in vessel, microbes developed but when it was heated and kept no micro organisms grew. Louis Pasteur explained the same with swan neck flask experiment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47154,'biology',102,772,1677,'A well cooked piece of meat kept in an air tight sealed jar does not spoil by bacteria or other microorganisms. This experiment was done by:','[{"text": "Darwin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pasteur", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Miller", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haldane", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Louis Pasteur\'s pasteurization experiment illustrates the fact that the spoilage of liquid was caused by particles in the air rather than the air itself. These experiments were important pieces of evidence supporting the idea of germ theory of disease.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47155,'biology',102,772,1677,'Swan necked flask experiment was performed by','[{"text": "Robert Koch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Louis Pasteur", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Francisco Redi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aristotle", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Louis Pasteur conducted a swan necked flask experiment and disproved the abiogenesis theory.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47156,'biology',102,772,1677,'Select the most appropriate answer<br>A. Pasteur showed that in pre-sterilised flasks, life did not come from killed yeast<br>B. Darwin showed that in another flask open to air, new living organisms arose from \'killed yeast\'.','[{"text": "Only A is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Comes only from pre-existing life. He observed that in presterilised flasks, life did not come from killed yeast while in another flask open to air, new living organisms arose from killed yeast\'. He showed that the Source of the new appearing micro-organisms was the air and the organisms did not arise from the nutrient media.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47157,'biology',102,772,1677,'Who was not able to answer how the first life form came on earth?','[{"text": "Louis Pasteur", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Charles Pasteur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Charles Darwin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Louis Darwin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Louis Pasteur first demonstrated that life comes only from pre-existing life. He showed that in pre-sterilized flasks, life did not come from killed yeast while in another flask open to air, new living organisms arose from \'killed yeast\'.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47158,'biology',102,772,1677,'Who proposed the theory of chemical evolution for the first time?','[{"text": "Oparin and Haldane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Miller", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Louis Pasteur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Darwin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Alexander Voinovich Oparin and J.B.S Haldane proposed the theory of chemical evolution. They are also known for their works in physiology, genetics and evolutionary biology.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47159,'biology',102,772,1677,'Oparin of______ and Haldane of________ proposed that the first form of life could have come from pre-existing non-living organic molecules.','[{"text": "Russia, Russia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Russia, England", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "England, England", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "England, Russia", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the $1920 \\mathrm{~s}$ British scientist J.B.S.Haldane and Russian biochemist Alexander Oparin independently set forth similar ideas concerning the conditions required for the origin of life on Earth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47160,'biology',102,772,1677,'Who proved the theory of chemical evolution through his experiment?','[{"text": "L.S. Miller, 1953", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S.L. Miller, 1952", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S.L. Miller, 1953", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "L.S. Miller, 1952", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The Miller Urey experiment was a chemical experiment that simulated the conditions thought at the time to be present on the early Earth, and tested the chemical origin of life. Specifically, the experiment tested Alexander Operon and J. B. S. Haldane\'s hypothesis that conditions on the primitive Earth favoured chemical reactions that synthesize more complex organic compounds from simpler inorganic precursors. Considered to be the classic experiment investigating abiogenesis, it was conducted in 1952 by Stanley Miller, under the supervision of Harold Urey, at the University of Chicago and later the University of California, San Diego and published the following year.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47161,'biology',102,772,1677,'S.L. Miller created electric discharge in a closed flask containing.','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ and water vapour at $80^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ and water vapour at $800^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ and water vapour at $8000^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ and water vapour at $800^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The experiment used water $\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$, methane $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{4}\\right)$, ammonia $\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)$, and hydrogen $\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\right)$. So, the theory of chemical evolution was based on the experiment of Miller and Urey at 800 degree Celsius)The experiment used water $\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}\\right)$, methane $\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_{4}\\right)$, ammonia $\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_{3}\\right)$, and hydrogen $\\left(\\mathrm{H}_{2}\\right)$. So, the theory of chemical evolution was based on the experiment of Miller and Urey at 800 degree Celsius. 35) They observed the formation of amino acids and ultimately proteins. This proved that life originated from non-living components.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47162,'biology',102,772,1677,'Miller through his experiments observed formation of','[{"text": "Lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amino acids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleic acids", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Amino acids',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47273,'biology',102,775,1680,'Which of the following is not an examples of adaptive radiation?','[{"text": "Wombat, numbat, kangaroo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Different mammals in Australia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Darwin\'s finches", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flying squirrel and flying phalanger", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The flying phalanger is strikingly similar to the flying squirrel from North America. As they have some common traits, these animals are an example of \'convergent evolution\'.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47163,'biology',102,772,1677,'The following diagram represents experiment done by','[{"text": "Pasteur - Biotic evolution of life", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Darwin - Natural selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Miller - Chemical evolution of life", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Haldane - Chemical evolution of life", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The Miller\'s experiment is chemical evolution of life used water (H20), methane (CH4), ammonia (NH3), and hydrogen (H2). So, the theory of chemical evolution was based on the experiment of Miller and Urey at 800 degree Celsius',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/102_47163_question_1.png'),
(47164,'biology',102,772,1677,'Mark the incorrect statement','[{"text": "In the Miller experiment, control apparatus contained every arrangement except it was devoid of inorganic molecules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coacervates did not have lipid outer membrane and failed to fulfill requirement as a precursor of life", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Once cells evolved, DNA probably replaced RNA as the genetic material for most organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Earth was formed around 4.5 billion years ago while oldest rocks are dated about 3.8 billion years ago.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In Miller\'s experiment, control apparatus contained every arrangement even it is devoid of inorganic molecules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47165,'biology',102,772,1677,'Millers experiment provided evidence for theory of','[{"text": "Biogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abiogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Special creation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organic evolution", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Miller\'s experiment provided evidence for theory of organic evolution.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47166,'biology',102,772,1677,'The diagram is an experimental setup performed by____ and it was based on the concepts put forth by____','[{"text": "U. Miller, Oparin and Haldane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oparin and Haldane, U. Miller", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "U. Miller, Oparin alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "U. Miller, Haldane alone", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In 1992, JBS Haldane and Alexander Operin independently proposed a theory about origin of life which said that organic molecules could be formed from a biogenic material in the presence of an external energy source.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/102_47166_question_1.png'),
(47167,'biology',102,772,1677,'Which of the following has been basic to origin of life?','[{"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleoproteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleic acids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nucleic acids Proteins form the structural and functional unit of life. They cannot replicate and this function is performed by nucleic acids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47168,'biology',102,772,1677,'The understanding of chemical evolution is based on','[{"text": "Mystic entity about the chemicals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interaction of water and chemical under intense heat alone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Effect of UV radiation on chemicals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Possible origin of life by various different combinations of chemicals under suitable environmental conditions", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Concept of chemical evolution refers to origin of life from non living matter. First inorganic compounds and then organic compounds were formed in accordance with ever changing environmental conditions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47169,'biology',102,772,1677,'The first non-cellular form of life could have originated ____ billion years back.','[{"text": "4.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'First non cellular form of life originated about 3 billion years back. Photosynthetic bacteria appeared in 3.3-3.5 billion years ago.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47170,'biology',102,772,1677,'Select the correct statement<br>I. The first cellular form of life did not possibly originate till about 2000 million years ago. These were probably singlecells.<br>II. All life forms were in water environment only.','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cellular form of life originated about 4 billion years ago. 3 billion years ago, 2000 million years ago and 50,000 years ago is after the origination of life on earth. So, before 4 billion years ago, cellular form of life did not possibly originated or present All living things, from tiny cyanobacteria to giant blue whales need water to survive. Without water, life as we know it would not exist.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47171,'biology',102,772,1677,'Select the correct statement:','[{"text": "Life originated on earth after 4 billion years of origin of earth", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prokaryotic cells are formed after the formation of eukaryotic cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water and oxygen are two essential components for the origin of life through chemosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First non-cellular forms of life would have been gaint molecules like RNA, Protein, Polysaccharides etc.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'These macromolecules aggregated and the first noncellular forms of life could have originated 3 billion years ago as giant molecules consisting of RNA, protein and polysaccharides, etc. The noncellular life form eventually evolved into the first cellular form of life, about 2000 million years ago.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47172,'biology',102,772,1677,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Oparin<br>B. J.B.S. Haldane<br>C. Miller</div><div class="column-right">P. America<br>Q. Russia<br>R. England</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Operin-Russia, Haldane-England, Miller-America',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47173,'biology',102,772,1677,'The first living organisms on earth were:','[{"text": "Chemoautotrophs, Anaerobic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemoautotrophs, Aerobic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photoautotrophs, Aerobic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemoheterotrophs, Anaerobic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The first living beings were prokaryotes like bacteria. They were single-celled. The nucleic acid core consisted of naked DNA. These living beings were present in the environment of the soupy sea having abundant organic molecules. Nutritionally they were chemo heterotrophs. They absorbed the organic materials from outside both for body building and liberation of energy. Respiration was anaerobic since free oxygen was absent in the environment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47174,'biology',102,772,1677,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Pasteur<br>B. Oparin<br>C. S.L. Miller</div><div class="column-right">P. Life only comes from life<br>Q. Experimental verification of chemical evolution<br>R. Theory of chemical evolution</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pasteur-Life only comes from life, Operon-Theory of chemical evolution, Miller-Experimental verification of chemical evolution',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47175,'biology',102,772,1677,'Identify the correct match from column-I and column-II:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Origin of universe<br>B. Origin of Earth<br>C. Origin of first cellular form of life<br>D. Origin of first noncellular form of life</div><div class="column-right">P. 3 bya<br>Q. 20 bya<br>R. 4.5 bya<br>S. 2 bya</div></div>','[{"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - R, C - S, D - P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Q, B - S, C - R, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - R, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Origin of universe -20 bya, Origin of earth - 4.5 bya, origin of first cellular form of life - 2 bya, origin of first non-cellular form of life - 3 bya.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47176,'biology',102,772,1677,'Which one of the following gases was not present in free form at the time life originated on the earth?','[{"text": "Hydrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Methane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ammonia", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'According to Urey-millers experiment, the gases present in atmosphere were methane, ammonia and hydrogen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47177,'biology',102,772,1677,'From the point of view of early chemical evolution that preceded the origin of life on earth, the most important simple organic molecules formed were','[{"text": "Purines and pyrimidines", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugars and amino acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycerol and fatty acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Early inorganic molecules interacted and formed organic molecules like simple sugars, nitrogen bases, fatty acids, amino acids, glycerol etc.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47178,'biology',102,772,1677,'Life cannot originate today because','[{"text": "Todays atmosphere is oxidizing", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Todays atmosphere is reducing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Life has already originated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Raw materials are not available", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Present day atmosphere is oxidising with abundant of oxygen.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47179,'biology',102,773,1678,'According to theory of special creation:','[{"text": "All living organisms that we see today were created as such", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The diversity was always the same since creation and will be the same in future", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The earth is about 4000 years old", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All living organisms were created as such. Diversity was same since the creation. The Earth is about 4000 years ago.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
