(47514,'biology',102,777,1682,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Karl Ernst von Baer noted that embryo never pass through adult stages of other animals and thus discarded Ernst Haeckel\'s embryological support for evolution.<br></div><div class="column-right">Theory of aquired character was given by de Vries.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The theory of acquired character was given by French biologist Jean-Baptiste Lamarck.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47515,'biology',102,780,1685,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The skull of adult chimpanzee is more like adult human skull than baby chimpanzee skull.<br></div><div class="column-right">The skull of baby chimpanzee is more like adult human than adult chimpanzee skull.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The skull of baby chimpanzee is more like adult human than adult chimpanzee skull.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47516,'biology',102,776,1681,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Microbes are able to grow on new nutrient media due to natural selection.<br></div><div class="column-right">Adaptive ability is inherited and has genetic basis.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47517,'biology',102,779,1684,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Giant ferns fell to form coal deposits slowly.<br></div><div class="column-right">About 65 million years ago dinosaurs died out.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'About 65 mya, the dinosaurs suddenly disappeared from the earth. We don\'t know the true reason.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47540,'biology',102,772,1677,'The concept of chemical evolution is based on','[{"text": "Interaction of water, air, and clay under intense heat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Effect of solar radiation on chemicals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Possible origin of life by combination of chemicals under suitable environmental conditions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Crystalization", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The concept of chemical evolution refers to the origin of life from non-living or inorganic matter. The first organic compound was said to have been formed due to the ever-changing environmental conditions of the primitive earth and a combination of inorganic compounds.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47518,'biology',102,778,1683,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Genetic drift refers to changes in the allele frequency occurring by chance<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Sampling error often lead to the elimination of certain alleles and fixation of other reducing genetic variability','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Genetic drift refers to elimination of genes of certain traits when a section of population migrates or dies, it will alter gene frequency of remaining population.       Hence genetic drift is a mechanism of evolution that acts in concert with natural selection to change species characteristics over time.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47519,'biology',102,774,1679,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Evolution is not a directed process in sense of determination<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Evolution is a stochastic process based on chance events in nature and chance mutation in organisms','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Evolution by anthropogenic action will lead to appearance of resistant organisms in a span of time. This shows that evolution is not a directed process but based on chance event and mutations occurring in nature',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47520,'biology',102,778,1683,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Disruptive selection changes the population towards one particular direction<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This type of selection favours average sized individuals','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Disruptive type of selection favours both small sized and large sized individuals .It eliminates most of the members with mean expression,so produces two peaks in the distribution of the trait that may lead to development of two different population. This kind of selection is very rare in nature. But it is important in bringing about evolutionary change.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47521,'biology',102,772,1677,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Primitive atmosphere was of reducing type<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> First hydrogen atoms combined with all oxygen','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The interstellar dust from which earth originated was especially rich in hydrogen, it readily combined with nitrogen to form ammonia, with carbon to form methane and combined with oxygen forming water. The earths early atmosphere was strongly reducing as it contained hydrogen, methane, ammonia and water vapours.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47522,'biology',102,774,1679,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Moths living in the industrial area became dark to match body colour to the tree trunks<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Smoke from industries covers the moths, making them appear dark','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Industrial Melanism is the increase of melanic (black) forms of animals in areas darkened by industrial pollution. Common examples is peppered moth which existed in 2 strains (Black and white)',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47523,'biology',102,772,1677,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> First cells used RNA as their hereditary molecule<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> DNA evolved from RNA','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The RNA world is proposed as the first stage in the evolution of life in which RNA catalyzed all molecules necessary for survival and replication If the first cells used RNA as their hereditary molecule, DNA evolved from a RNA template. DNA probably did not evolve as an hereditary material until RNA based life became enclosed in membrane. Once cells evolved DNA probably placed RNA as genetic material for most organisms.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47524,'biology',102,778,1683,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Founder effect may lead to formation of new species<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Founders carry all the parental gene pool to a new location','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When a few individuals from some large population invades a new or an isolated geographical region, these become the founder members. These founders carryon a limited portion of parental gene pool. Some times they form a new species.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47552,'biology',102,774,1679,'Forelimbs of cat, lizard used in walking; forelimbs of whale used in swimming and forelimbs of bats used in flying are an example of:','[{"text": "Analogous organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptive radiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homologous organs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Organs which have a common fundamental anatomical plan and similar embryonic origin but functions vary. They may perform as homologous organs. For examples the flippers of a whale, a bats wing, fore-limb of a horse, a bird\'s wing and forelimbs of human are structurally as well as functionally different.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47525,'biology',102,772,1677,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> According to Big bang hypothesis about 20 billion years ago universe was a big ball of only neutrons<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Movement of these particles is known to generate tremendous heat which caused explosion due to temperature and pressure changes','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Big bang theory explains the origin of universe, according to this hypothesis about 20 billion years ago the universe was the big ball made up of neutrons. Its huge explosion due to its high temperature change in pressure, the universe was formed.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47526,'biology',102,775,1680,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The establishment of reproductive isolation is an event of biological significance<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In the absence of reproductive isolation species can merge back to a single population','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Reproductive isolation is the absence of interbreeding between members of different species. Reproductive isolation is mandatory to maintain distinct species and its absence can lead to merge of different species into one.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47527,'biology',102,780,1685,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Southern ape is called connecting link between ape and man<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> This is Australopithecus who had combined features of ape and man','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Australopithecus was found in South Africa giving it the name Southern Ape. They are considered to be the connecting links between apes and humans hence having both the characteristics of humans and apes. They had heavy hair growth like apes and bipedal locomotion like a man.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47528,'biology',102,775,1680,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Darwins finches of Galapagos islands have different types of modified beaks according to their food habits<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Adaptive Radiation leads to development of different functional structure from a common ancestral form','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Development of different functional structures froma common ancestral form is called adaptive radiation. Homologous organs show adaptive radiation.<br>Darwins finches of Galapagos island had common ancestors but now have different types of modified beaks according to their food habits',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47529,'biology',102,780,1685,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Chimpanzee is the closest relative of the present day humans<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The banding pattern in some autosomes of man and chimpanzee is remarkably similar','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'It has been observed that banding pattern of some human chromosomes is very similar to the banding pattern of corresponding chromosomes in apes. It shows common origin of man and chimpanzee.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47530,'biology',102,772,1677,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Louis Pasteur showed that in flask open to air new living organisms appeared in the heat killed yeast culture<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Life arises from pre-existing life','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Louis Pasteur demonstrated that life comes from pre-existing forms. He showed that the source of the newly appearing microorganisms was air and organisms did not arise from the nutrient media.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47531,'biology',102,774,1679,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Thorns and tendrils of bougainvillea and cucurbita respectively  homology<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Homologous organs have similar function but are different in their structure and origin','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The organs which have same fundamental structure but are different in functions are called as Homologous organs.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47541,'biology',102,774,1679,'Which one of the following pairs of items correctly belongs to the category of organs mentioned against it?','[{"text": "Wings of honey bee and wings of crow - Homologous organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thorn of bougainvillea and tendrils of cucurbita - Analogous organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nictitating membrane and blind spot in human eye - Vestigial organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nephridia of earthworm and malpighian tubules of cockroach - Excretory organs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Wings of honey bee and wings of crow Analogous organs<br>Thorn of Bougainvillea and tendrils of cucurbita - Homologous organs<br>Nictitating membrane and blind spot in human eye - Both are not vestigial organs',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47532,'biology',102,774,1679,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Embryos of fish, salamander, tortoise, chick and man of same age resemble one another closely<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Ontogeny recapitulates phylogeny','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biogenetic law given by Haeckel explains the Ontogeny recapitulates phylogeny.<br>Ontogeny is the life history of an individual starting from ovum and Phylogeny is series of adult ancestors of the individual which must have incurred evolution of groups of this individual. It means that an individual during its development briefs about its ancestral history.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47533,'biology',102,776,1681,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Evolutionary trend is continuous changes of character in a lineage<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Lineage is an evolutionary sequence arranged in a linear order','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The continuous change of characters within an evolving lineage is called as Evolutionary trend. A lineage is an evolutionary sequence arranged in a linear order from ancestral group to descendent group. A trend may be progressive or retrogressive.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47534,'biology',102,780,1685,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Neanderthal man is an intermediate between Ramapithecus and Homo erectus<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Neanderthal man with brain size $800 \\mathrm{cc}$, used hides to protect their body','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Neanderthal man had brain size of $1400 \\mathrm{cc}$. It lived in East and central Asia, 1,00,000 to $4,00,000$ years ago. They used hides to protect their body and buried their dead. Neanderthal man appeared later after Ramapithecus and <i>Homo erectus</i>.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47535,'biology',102,778,1683,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Hardy Weinberg principle explains the variation occurring in population and species over a number of generations<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Hardy Weinberg principle is applicable only when genetic drift occurs','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The relative frequencies of various kinds of genes in a large and randomly mating, sexual panmictic population tend to remain constant from generation to generation in absence of mutation, selection and gene flow. This is Hardy-Weinberg principle. It is random in gene frequency and occurs only by chance. It is nondirectional. Genetic drift can cause elimination of certain alleles or fixation of other in the population, leading to change in population of alleles in gene pool. So genetic drift must not occur to maintain equilibrium.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47536,'biology',102,778,1683,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cheetah is an example for bottleneck effect<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Bottleneck effect is when population is subjected to near extinction by a disaster or slaughter by humans','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A population bottleneck is a sharp reduction in the size of a population due to environmental events (such as earthquakes, floods, fires, or droughts) or human activities (such as genocide). Such events can reduce the variation in the gene pool of a population. According to the May 2007 study, female cheetahs seem to be at least as promiscuous as their male counterparts. Females frequently mate with several different males while they are fertile and are then likely to bear a single litter of cubs fathered by multiple males making many of the cubs within a single litter only half-siblings. This discovery has important implications for the conservation of these endangered animals. So, Cheetah is an example of bottle neck effect.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47537,'biology',102,775,1680,'The finches of Galapagos islands provide an evidence','[{"text": "Special creation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Evolution due to mutation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Retrogressive evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biogeographical evolution", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Darwins finches in Galapagos island providenevidence for Biogeographical evidence. Biogeography is the study of the geographical distribution of biological organisms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47538,'biology',102,774,1679,'Which one of the following in birds indicates their reptilian ancestry?','[{"text": "Four chambered heart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Scales on their hind limbs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Egg with a calcareous shell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two special chambers crop and gizzards in their digestive tract.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Body is scaly in reptiles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47539,'biology',102,774,1679,'When two species of different genealogy come to resemble each other as a result of adaptation the phenomenon is termed as','[{"text": "Divergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co- evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Micro evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Convergent evolution is the process whereby organisms not closely related, independently evolve similar traits as a result of having to similar environmental or ecological niches. Convergent evolution creates analogous structures that have similar form or function but were not present in the last common ancestors of those groups.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47542,'biology',102,772,1677,'Which one of the following is incorrect about the characteristics of protobionts (coacervates and microspheres) as envisaged in the abiogenic origin of life?','[{"text": "They were able to reproduce", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They could separate combinations of molecules from the surroundings", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They were partially separated from the surroundings", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They could maintain an internal environment", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The protobiont shares its weak catabolic capabilities with the liposome. They were partially isolated from environment, but, they could not separate combinations of molecules from the surroundings.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47543,'biology',102,777,1682,'Which of the scientists name is correctly matched with the theory put forth by him?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Mendel - Theory of Pangenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Weismann - Theory of continuity of Germplasm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pasteur-Inheritance of acquired characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "de Vries - Natural selection", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Theory of continuity of germplasm was given by August Weismann, who discovered Pangenesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47544,'biology',102,774,1679,'In case of peppered moth (<i>Biston betularia</i>) the black coloured form became dominant over the light coloured form in England during industrial revolution. This is a example of','[{"text": "Appearance of the darker coloured individuals due to very poor sunlight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protective mimicry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inheritance of dark colour character acquired due to dark environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Natural selection whereby the darker forms were selected", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In the case of the peppered moth (Biston betularia) the black-coloured form became dominant over the light-coloured form in England during the industrial revolution. This is an example of natural selection whereby the darker forms were selected.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47545,'biology',102,780,1685,'The most apparent change during the evolutionary history of Homo sapiens is traced in','[{"text": "Walking upright", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shortening of jaws", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Remarkable increase in the brain size (Cranial capacity)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Loss of body hair", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Brain size or cranial capacity shows gradual increases in history of <i>Homo sapiens</i>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47546,'biology',102,780,1685,'What was the most significant trend in the evolution of modern man (<i>Homo sapiens</i>) from his ancestors?','[{"text": "Binocular vision", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Upright posture", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shortening of jaws", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increasing cranial capacity", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cranial capacity of the modern man is more than the ancestors. Cranial capacity of modern man is $1400-1600 \\mathrm{cc}$ whereas the cranial capacity of java man was $900 \\mathrm{cc}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47547,'biology',102,774,1679,'Which one of the following options gives one correct example each of convergent evolution and divergent evolution?<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{Convergent}}}\n\\end{array}\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{Evolution}}}\n\\end{array}}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{Divergent}}}\n\\end{array}\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{Evolution}}}\n\\end{array}}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Bones}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{forelimbs}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Wings}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{butterfly}}\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{vertebrates}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mammals}}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Eyes}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{octopus}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Thorns}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{bougainvillea}}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{mammals}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{tendrils}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{cucurbita}}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Bones}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{forelimbs}}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\,{\\\\rm{Eyes}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{octopus}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{vertebrates}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{mammals}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{Wings}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{butterfly}}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\,{\\\\rm{Tendrils}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{Bouginvillea}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{birds}}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}&{\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n{\\\\,{\\\\rm{tendrils}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{cucurbita}}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}}\\n\\\\end{array}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Eyes of octopus & mammals have different internal structure, but they serve the common function of vision. While thorns of bougainvillea and tendrils of cucurbita have common origin but different functions like protection and climbing respectively.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47548,'biology',102,780,1685,'The extinct human who lived $1,00,000$ to 40,000 years ago in Europe, Asia and parts of Africa with short stature, heavy eye browridges, retreating for heads, large jaws with heavy teeth, stocky bodies, a lumbering gait and stooped posture (humpy)','[{"text": "Ramapithecus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Homo habilis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neanderthal human (Homosapiens neanderthalensis)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cro-magnan humans", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Neanderthal man had brain size of (13001600) avg of $1400 \\mathrm{cc}$. It lived in East and central Asia, Europe and Africa. 1,00,000 to 4,00,000 years ago. They used hides to protect their body and buried their dead, they are cannibals $\\&$ cave dwellers.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47549,'biology',102,778,1683,'The tendency of population to remain in genetic equilibrium may be disturbed by :','[{"text": "Random mating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lack of migration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lack of mutations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lack of random mating", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium can be disturbed by a number of forces, including mutations, natural selection, nonrandom mating, genetic drift, and gene flow (immigration, emigration, or migration). Lack of random mating will lead to disturbance in genetic equilibrium.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47550,'biology',102,778,1683,'Variation in gene frequencies within populations can occur by chance rather than by natural selection. This is referred to as :','[{"text": "Genetic flow", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic drift", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Random mating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic load", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'New genes/alleles are added to the new population and these are lost from the old population. There would be a gene flow if this gene migration, happens multiple times. If the same change occurs by chance, it is called genetic drift.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47551,'biology',102,775,1680,'The process by which organisms with different evolutionary history evolve similar phenotypic adaptations in response to a common environmental challenge is called :','[{"text": "Natural selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-random evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptive radiation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Analogous structures are the result of convergent evolution.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47554,'biology',102,778,1683,'In a population of 1000 individuals 360 belong to genotype AA, 480 to $\\mathrm{Aa}$ and the remaining 160 to aa. Based on this data, the frequency of allele $\\mathrm{A}$ in the population is:','[{"text": "0.4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.7", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'According to Hardy Weinberg principle.$\\mathrm{p}^{2}+2 \\mathrm{pq}+\\mathrm{q}^{2}=1 ;(\\mathrm{p}+\\mathrm{q})^{2}=1$<br>(AA)  $\\mathrm{p}^{2}=360$ out of 1000 individual or<br>$\\mathrm{p}^{2}=36$ out of 100 .<br>${{\\rm{q}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 160}}$ out of 1000 or ${{\\rm{q}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 16}}$ out of 100<br>Therefore $\\mathrm{q}=0.4$. As $\\mathrm{p}+\\mathrm{q}=1 \\quad$ so $\\mathrm{p}$ is 0.6',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47555,'biology',102,780,1685,'Which of the following had the smallest brain capacity?','[{"text": "<i>Homo sapiens</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Homo neanderthalensis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Homo habilis</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Homo erectus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Brain capacity in decreasing order:-<br><i>Homo sapiens</i> (1300 - 1600 c.c)<br><i>Homo neander thalensis</i> (approx. 1400 c.c.)<br><i>Homo eractus</i> ( 900 c.c.)<br><i>Homo habilis</i> (650 - 800 c.c.)<br>Thus the lowest brain capacity is of <i>Homo habilis</i> as shown above. <i>Homo habilis</i> lived in early Pleistocene period and used tools of chipped stones.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47556,'biology',102,778,1683,'A population will not exist in Hardy - Weinberg equilibrium if :','[{"text": "There are no mutations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is no migration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The population is large", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Individuals mate selectively", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Hardy- Weinberg equilibrium states that in the absence of disturbance on the level of genetic structure, a population\'s existence will not continue. Thus mating should be in a random way',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47557,'biology',102,778,1683,'In Hardy-Weinberg equation, the frequency of heterozygous individual is represented by :-','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{pq}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{pq}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{p}^{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$q^{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'According to Hardy Weinberg principle.$\\mathrm{p}^{2}+2 \\mathrm{pq}+\\mathrm{q}^{2}=1$. Therefore $\\mathrm{p}^{2}$ - frequency of homozygous individual (dominant) ${{\\rm{q}}^{\\rm{2}}}$ - frequency of homozygous individual (recessive) ${\\rm{2pq}}$ - frequency of heterozygous individual',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47558,'biology',102,780,1685,'The chronological order of human evolution from early to the recent is :-','[{"text": "Ramapithecus $\\\\rightarrow$ Homo habilis $\\\\rightarrow$ Australopithecus $\\\\rightarrow$ Homo erectus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Australopithecus $\\\\rightarrow$ Homo habilis $\\\\rightarrow$ Ramapithecus $\\\\rightarrow$ Homo erectus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Australopithecus $\\\\rightarrow$ Ramapithecus $\\\\rightarrow$ Homo habilis $\\\\rightarrow$ Homo erectus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ramapithecus $\\\\rightarrow$ Australopithecus $\\\\rightarrow$ Homo habilis $\\\\rightarrow$ Homo erectus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ramapithecus $\\rightarrow$ Australopithecus $\\rightarrow$ A. africanus $\\rightarrow$ Homohabilis $\\rightarrow$ Homo erectus Pekingman $\\rightarrow$ Cromagnon man $\\rightarrow$ Modern man (chronological order from early to recent)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47559,'biology',102,774,1679,'Analogous structures are a result of','[{"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Shared ancestry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stabilizing selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Divergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Analogous structures are those which are functionally same but they vary anatomically. Those are because of convergent evolution.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47560,'biology',102,772,1677,'Following are the two statements regarding the origin of life :<br>i. The earliest organisms that appeared on the earth were non-green and presumably anaerobes.<br>ii. The first autotrophic organisms were the chemoautotroph\'s has never released oxygen. Of the above statements which one of the following options is correct?','[{"text": "ii is correct but $\\\\mathrm{i}$ is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both i and ii are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both i and ii are false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i is correct but ii is false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Anaerobes were the first organism that appeared on earth and first autotrophic organisms were the chemo autotrophs. They never release oxygen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47561,'biology',102,777,1682,'According to Hugo de Vries, the mechanism of evolution is','[{"text": "Phenotypic variations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saltation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multiple step mutations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Minor mutations", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'According to Hugo de Vries Mutational theory, mechanism of evolution is saltation. Saltation is single step large mutation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47562,'biology',102,774,1679,'Among the following sets of examples for divergent evolution, select the incorrect option:','[{"text": "Brain of bat, man and cheetah", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heart of bat, man and cheetah", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Forelimbs of man, bat and cheetah", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eye of octopus, bat and man", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Divergent evolution is development of same structure along different directions due to adaptations to different needs. Divergent evolution occurs in homologous organs.Examples of Brain, Heart and Forelimbs of vertebrates are homologous organs and they have developed along different directions due to adaptations to different needs whereas eye of octopus, bat and man are examples of analogous organs showing convergent evolution.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47563,'biology',102,774,1679,'The similarity of bone structure in the forelimbs of many vertebrates is an example of','[{"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Analogy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homology", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adaptive radiation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bone structure in the forelimbs of many vertebrates are similar but they have adapted itself to different adaptation to perform different functions. These type of organs are called as Homologous organs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47614,'biology',102,775,1680,'Tasmanian Wolf is a marsupial while Wolf is a placental mammal. This is an example of','[{"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Divergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inheritance of acquired characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptive radiation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Marsupials in Australia and placental mammals in North America show convergent evolution. These two subclasses of mammals have adapted in similar ways to a particular food supply, locomotor skill or climate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47564,'biology',102,778,1683,'A gene locus has two alleles $A$, a. If the frequency of dominant allele $\\mathrm{A}$ is 0.4 , then what will be the frequency of homozygous dominant, heterozygous and homozygous recessive individuals in the population?','[{"text": "$0.36(\\\\mathrm{AA}) ; 0.48(\\\\mathrm{Aa}) ; 0.16(\\\\mathrm{aa})$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.16(\\\\mathrm{AA}) ; 0.24(\\\\mathrm{Aa}) ; 0.36(\\\\mathrm{aa})$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.16(\\\\mathrm{AA}) ; 0.48(\\\\mathrm{Aa}) ; 0.36(\\\\mathrm{aa})$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$0.16(\\\\mathrm{AA}) ; 0.36(\\\\mathrm{Aa}) ; 0.48(\\\\mathrm{aa})$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Frequency of dominant allele (say p) $=0.4$<br>Frequency of recessive allele (say q)$=1-0.4=0.6$<br>Frequency of homozygous dominant individuals (AA)<br>$=\\mathrm{p}^{2}=(0.4)^{2}=0.16$<br>Frequency of heterozygous individuals (Aa)<br>$=2 \\mathrm{pq}=2(0.4)(0.6)=0.48$<br>Frequency of homozygous recessive individuals (aa)<br>$=\\mathrm{q}^{2}=(0.6)^{2}=0.36$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47565,'biology',102,778,1683,'In a species, the weight of newborn ranges from 2 to $5 \\mathrm{~kg}$. $97 \\%$ of the newborn with an average weight between 3 to $3.3 \\mathrm{~kg}$ survive whereas $99 \\%$ of the infants born with weight from 2 to $2.5 \\mathrm{~kg}$ or 4.5 to $5 \\mathrm{~kg}$ die. Which type of selection process is taking place?','[{"text": "Directional Selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stabilizing Selection", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Disruptive Selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyclical Selection", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given data shows stabilising selection as most of the newborn having average weight between 3 to $3.3 \\mathrm{~kg}$ survive and babies with less and more weight have low survival rate.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47566,'biology',102,772,1677,'From his experimints, S.L. Miller produced amino acids by mixing the following in a closed flask:','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{4}$ and water vapor at $800^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ and water vapor at $600^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ and water vapor at $600^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ and water vapor at $800^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\mathrm{H}_{2}, \\mathrm{NH}_{3}$ and water vapor at $800^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47567,'biology',102,774,1679,'Embryological support for evolution was disapproved by:','[{"text": "Alfred Wallace", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Charles Darwin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oparin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Karl Ernst von Baer", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Karl Ernst von Baer',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47568,'biology',102,774,1679,'Flippers of Penguins and Dolphins are examples of :','[{"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Industrial melanism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Natural selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptive radiation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Convergent evolution',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47569,'biology',102,775,1680,'Which of the following refer to correct example(s) of organisms which have evolved due to changes in environment brought about by anthropogenic action?<br>(a) Darwin\'s Finches of Galapagos islands<br>(b) Herbicide resistant weeds<br>(c) Drug resistant eukaryotes<br>(d) Man-created breeds of domesticated animals like dogs','[{"text": "(a) and (c)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(b), (c) and (d)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "only (d)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "only (a)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(b), (c) and (d)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47570,'biology',102,778,1683,'The factor that leads ot Founder effect in a population is:','[{"text": "Natural selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic recombination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic drift", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The factor that leads to founder effect and bottle neck effect in a population is Genetic drift.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47571,'biology',102,775,1680,'Match Column - I with Column - II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Adaptive radiation<br>B. Convergent evolution<br>C. Divergent evolution<br>D. Evolution by anthropogenic action</div><div class="column-right">P. Selection of resonance varities due to excessive use of herbicides and pesticides<br>Q. Bones offorelimbs in man and whale<br>R. Wings of butterfly and bird<br>S. Darwin finches</div></div>','[{"text": "A - S; B - R; C - Q; D - P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - R; B - Q; C - P; D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q; B - P; C - S; D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P; B - S; C - R; D - Q", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Adaptive radiation - Darwin\'s finches<br>Convergent evolution - Wings of butterfly and bird<br>Divergent evolution - Bones of forelimbs in man and whale<br>Evolution by anthropogenic action - Selection of resistant varieties due to excessive use of herbicides and pesticides.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47572,'biology',102,774,1679,'Which of the following statements is not true?','[{"text": "Sweet potato and potato is an example of analogy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homology indicates common ancestry", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flippers of penguins and dolphins are a pair of homologous organs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Analogous structures are a result of convergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Flippers of penguins and dolphins are a pair of analogous organs that evolved due to convergent evolution.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47573,'biology',102,778,1683,'Natural selection where more individuals acquire specific character value other than the mean character value, leads to:','[{"text": "Directional change", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Disruptive change", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Random change", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stabilising change", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In directional natural selection, more individuals acquire value other than the mean character value. It involves elimination of individuals at one extreme of the phenotypic distribution and the mean value gradually shifts in the othr direction. For example the evolution of long - necked giraffes from short - necked ancestors involved directional selection.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47574,'biology',102,775,1680,'Which of these is NOT an example for Adaptive radiation?','[{"text": "Australian Marsupials", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Placental mammals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Long – necked Giraffe", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Darwin’s finches", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Long – necked Giraffe.<br>This is an example of Lamarckism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47575,'biology',102,778,1683,'In a population of 800 rabbits showing Hardy– Weinberg equilibrium, the frequency of recessive individuals was 0.16. What is the frequency of heterozygous individuals?','[{"text": "0.48", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.84", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.36", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.4", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'0.48<br>\nTotal population = 800 rabbits in H.W equilibrium\n<br>[ p2 + 2pq + q2 = 800]\n<br>Given q2 = 0.16\n<br>Then q = 0.16\n<br>q = 0.4\n<br>[p + q = 1]\n<br>If q = 0.4\n<br>p = 1-q\n<br>p = 1- 0.4\n<br>p = 0.6\n<br>Frequency of heterozygous individuals\n(2pq) = ?\n<br>2pq = 2 × 0.6 × 0.4\n<br>= 0.48.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47576,'biology',102,775,1680,'Select the correct group/set of Australian Marsupials exhibiting adaptive radiation.','[{"text": "Tasmanian wolf, Bobcat, Marsupial mole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Numbat, Spotted cuscus, Flying phalanger", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mole, Flying squirrel, Tasmanian tiger cat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lemur, Anteater, Wolf", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Numbat, spotted cuscus and flying phalanger are Australian marsupials exhibiting adaptive radiation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47577,'biology',102,774,1679,'Higher frequency of melanin British moths and DDT resistance in mosquitoes are cited as examples for:','[{"text": "Arrival of the fittest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic drift", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Natural selection", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Point mutation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'These are examples of natural selection. During industrialization, the tree trunks had become dark due to the soot and the smoke coming out of the chimneys. Thus, the survival of dark-wing moths (Biston carbonaria) enhanced as the predators could not spot them on the dark tree trunks.<br>As a result, the dark-winged moths were naturally selected over the white-winged moths and have almost replaced white winged moths. This is called industrial melanism.<br>After a few years of extensive use, DDT lost its effectiveness on insects. This is because resistance to DDT is a genetic trait, and presence of DDT in the environment changed it into a favoured trait. Hence, only those insects resistant to DDT survived, leading to populations largely resistant to DDT',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47578,'biology',102,776,1681,'Darwinism explains all the following except:','[{"text": "Organisms tend to produce more number of offspring than can survive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Offspring with better traits that overcome competition are best suited for the environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Variations are inherited from parents to offspring through genes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Within each species, there are variations", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'• The major draw back of Darwin\'s Theory of evolution was that he was not able to explain how variation among individuals originated and how they were transferred from parents to offspring.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47579,'biology',102,776,1681,'By the statement \'survival of the fittest\', Darwin meant that:','[{"text": "The strongest of all species survives", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The most intelligent of the species survives", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cleverest of the species survives", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The most adaptable of the species to changes survives", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Fitness refers to the reproductive fitness of an organism. This implies that the organism is able to survive up to the reproductive stage and is able to bear offspring and hence is able to pass on the genes to the next generation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47580,'biology',102,772,1677,'Which one of the following theories on the origin of life is mostly accepted?','[{"text": "Special creation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Steady state", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Panspermia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chemical origin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The chemical origin of life refers to the conditions that might have existed and therefore promoted the first replicating life forms. It considers the physical and chemical reactions that could have led to early replicator molecules. It is the most accepted theory.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47581,'biology',102,778,1683,'The Hardy - Weinberg principle cannot operate if:','[{"text": "The population is very large", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Frequent mutations occur in the population", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The population has no chance of interaction with other populations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Free interbreeding occurs among all members of the population", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hardy-Weinberg principle explains population genetics. It is an expression of Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium, which states that the amount of genetic variation in a population will remain constant from one generation to the next if the disturbing factors are absent. It can maintained only in hypothetical populations.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47582,'biology',102,772,1677,'The prebiotic atmosphere of the earth was of a reducing nature. It was transformed into an oxidizing atmosphere of present day due to the emergence of:','[{"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Angiosperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthetic bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eukaryotic algae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cyanobacteria or blue-green algae are photosynthetic prokaryotes. These are the organisms that evolved 3 million years back.<br>They perform oxygenic photosynthesis where they used water to get hydrogen and released oxygen in this process.<br>Hence, they added oxygen to the atmosphere and paved the path of the evolution of aerobic forms including aerobic bacteria.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47583,'biology',102,774,1679,'The formation of two species from one ancestral species is known as:','[{"text": "Phyletic evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Divergent evolution", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Allopatry", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Divergent evolution is evolution of different species from one species due to adaptations to different needs. It indicates common ancestory.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47584,'biology',102,779,1684,'The ancestors of modern day frogs and Salamanders are','[{"text": "Jawless fish", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coelocanth", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Icthyophis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amphioxus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In 1938, fish caught in south Africa happened to be a Coelacanth which was thought to be extinct. These animals evolved into the first amphibians that lived on land and water. These were ancestors of modern - day frogs and salamandes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47585,'biology',102,778,1683,'Find the mis-match from the following pairs.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Divergent evolution -Thorn of Bougainvillia and tendril of Cucurbita", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptive radiation - Australian marsupials", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Natural selection - Industrial melanism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic drift - Constant gene frequency", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Divergent evolutions are derived from the same embryological tissues or homologous organs, but they are designed to do different jobs and hence they have adapted to different needs. The thorns of Bougainvillea and the tendrils of Cucurbita exhibit homology.<br>• Adaptive radiation is a phenomenon by which a given population of a species changes when it gets distributed in different habitats in a particular region. The marsupials in Australia separated from their common ancestors and continued to evolve independently.<br>• The dark-winged moths were naturally selected over the white-winged moths and have almost replaced white-winged moths. This is called industrial melanism because of its association with industrialization.<br>• Genetic drift refers to the alteration in the frequencies of alleles in the gene pool of a finite population due to chance events. It takes place in one or over a few generations. If the change in the allele frequencies is very drastic, then new species are formed.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47586,'biology',102,779,1684,'Identify the plants that are dominant during Jurassic period.','[{"text": "Angiosperms and Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sphenopsida and Ginkgo\'s", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ferns, Conifers and Cycads", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monocotyledons and Arborescent lycopods", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Conifers dominated the Triassic period and Jurassic period had a luxuriant population of conifers, ferns, seed ferns, lycopods, horse tails and cycads. This period was dominated by the Gymnosperms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47587,'biology',102,772,1677,'The primary gases that were used by Miller in his experiment are:','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\\\mathrm{O}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{CO}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{~N}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{SO}$,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{~N}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{~N}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Stanley Miller and Harold Urey supported the chemical origin of life proposed by Haldane and Oparin. The famous Miller Urey experimented in 1953 in which primordial atmosphere was simulated, suggested that lighting might have helped to create the important building blocks of life on Earth. Methane, ammonia, hydrogen in the ratio of 2:1:2 and water, the major components of the early Earth\'s atmosphere, were taken in a spark chamber which was a closed system.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47588,'biology',102,778,1683,'The allele frequency of \' A \' and \' a \' in a population are 0.6 and 0.4 respectively. The expected frequency of heterozygous individuals is:','[{"text": "$48 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$36 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$16 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$24 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In a population, autosomal dominant recessive inheritance can be expressed by Hardy-Weinberg. The simple algebraic expression is:<br>$\\mathrm{p}^{2}+2 \\mathrm{pq}+\\mathrm{q}^{2}=1$<br>where, $\\mathrm{p}$ is the frequency of $\\mathrm{A}=0.6$<br>$\\mathrm{q}$ is the frequency of $\\mathrm{a}=0.4$<br>$2 \\mathrm{pq}$ is the frequency of $\\mathrm{Aa}$ (heterozygous individuals)<br>$=2 \\times 0.6 \\times 0.4=0.48$<br>Thus, the expected frequency of heterozygous individuals $=48 \\%$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47589,'biology',102,780,1685,'The brain capacity of Homo habilis is:','[{"text": "$1800 \\\\mathrm{cc}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Between $650 \\\\mathrm{cc}-800 \\\\mathrm{cc}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$900 \\\\mathrm{cc}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1400 \\\\mathrm{cc}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Homo habilis (Skillful humans) was the first human-like organism among all the hominid fossils discovered so far and its fossils were found in Africa about 1.5-2 mya. Their brain was large and was about $650-800 \\mathrm{cc}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(47590,'biology',102,779,1684,'Which among the following was the biggest land dinosaur?','[{"text": "<i>Stegosaurus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Brachiosaurus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Tyrannosaurus rex</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Triceratops</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Tyrannosaurus rex was the biggest land dinosaur.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47591,'biology',102,778,1683,'In a population of plants, some water extremely tall and the remaining were extremely dwarf. No plants of the population showed intermediate height. The type of operation of natural selection in the above case is','[{"text": "Balancing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Directional", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stabilizing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Disruptive", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Disruptive type of natural selection operates when characters are present in extremes and intermediates are less.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47592,'biology',102,774,1679,'Darwin\'s finches are a good example of','[{"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Industrial melanism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Connecting link", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Adaptive radiation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Darwin finches area good example of adaptive radiation. Adaptive radiation is a process of evolution of different species in a given geographical area starting from a point and radiating to other areas of geography.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47593,'biology',102,779,1684,'Select the correct order of geological time scale of earth.','[{"text": "Palaeozoic $\\\\longrightarrow$ Archaeozoic $\\\\longrightarrow$ Cenozoic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archaeozoic $\\\\longrightarrow$ Palaeozoic $\\\\longrightarrow$ Proterozoic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Palaeozoic $\\\\longrightarrow$ Mesozoic $\\\\longrightarrow$ Cenozoic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mesozoic $\\\\longrightarrow$ Archaeozoic $\\\\longrightarrow$ Proterozoic", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct geological time scale of earth is<br>Precambrian (Era/Age of early life)<br>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;$\\downarrow$<br>Palaeozoic (Age of fishes)<br>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;$\\downarrow$<br>Mesozoic (Age of reptiles dinosaurs and cycads)<br>&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;&emsp;$\\downarrow$<br>Cenozoic (Age of mammals)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47624,'biology',102,772,1677,'Stanley Miller simulated the conditions of pre-biotic earth using spark - discharge apparatus. Which organic compounds were observed by him on analysing the end product of his experiment?','[{"text": "Pigments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fats", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogen bases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amino acids<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Stanely Miller\'s experiment supports chemical evolution of life. The organic compounds observed by him on analysing the end product of his experiment were aminoacids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47594,'biology',102,772,1677,'According to Oparin, which one of the following was not present in the primitive atmosphere of the earth?','[{"text": "Methane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxygen", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hydrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water vapour", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The first scientific explanation of origin of life was put forward by A.I. Oparin in 1923. J.B.S. Haldane (1928), also made similar observation regarding the origin of life. According to them primitive atmosphere was reducing atmosphere because hydrogen atoms (most numerous and most reactive) combined with all available oxygen atoms to form water and leaving no free oxygen. Therefore oxygen was not present in the primitive atmosphere of the earth.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47595,'biology',102,772,1677,'The origin of life on earth has been because of chemical evolution. It can be justified by the<br>Statement.','[{"text": "Every organism is a special creation of god, hence there is no scope for evolution of one form of life from another", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Meteorites falling on earth have been found to contain a number of laevorotatory amino acids as are found in living beings", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Torrential rains falling on earth for years brought $\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\\\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\\\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\\\mathrm{H}_{2}$ etc. into sea water where they reacted in presence of UV rays to form sugars, purines, amino acids, pyrimidines etc", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Frothing appeared in nutrient broth kept in open after some days of sterilization, while no frothing appeared in closed jar", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Torrential rains falling on earth for years brought $\\mathrm{N}_{2}, \\mathrm{CH}_{4}, \\mathrm{NH}_{3}, \\mathrm{CO}_{2}, \\mathrm{H}_{2}$ etc. into sea water where they reacted in presence of UV rays to form Sugars, Purines, Amino acids, Pyrimidines etc, this is the most correct statement.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47596,'biology',102,777,1682,'Hugo de Vries gave his mutation theory on organic evolution while working on','[{"text": "<i>Pisum sativum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Drosophila melanogaster</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Oenothera lamarckiana</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Althea rosea</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hugo de Vries, a Dutch botanist, one of the independent rediscoverers of Mendelism, put forward his views regarding the formation of new species in 1901. According to him, new species are not formed by continuous variations but by sudden appearance of variations, which he named as mutations. Hugo de Vries stated that mutations are heritable and persist in successive generations. He conducted his experiments on Oenothera lamarckiana (evening primrose).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47597,'biology',102,774,1679,'Analogous organs are','[{"text": "Different in origin but perform similar functions.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Common in origin and perform common functions.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Common in origin but perform different functions.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Different in origin and perform different functions.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The analogous organs are different in origin or basic plan, but have similar functions or adaptations. Wings of butterfly and wings of bird and fins of fishes and flippers of whale are some of the examples of analogous organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47598,'biology',102,774,1679,'The eye of octopus and eye of cat show different patterns of structure, yet they perform similar function. This is an example of','[{"text": "Homologous organs that have evolved due to divergent evolution.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Analogous organs that have evolved due to convergent evolution.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Analogous organs that have evolved due to divergent evolution.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homologous organs that have evolved due to convergent evolution.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The eye of octopus and eye of cat show different patterns of structure, yet they perform similar functions. This is an example of analogous organs. Analogous organs have evolved due to convergent evolution. Analogous organs have developed in the evolutionary process through adaptation of quite different organisms to similar mode of life.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47599,'biology',102,780,1685,'The extinct human ancestor who ate only fruits and hunted with stone weapons was','[{"text": "<i>Ramapithecus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Australopithecus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Dryopithecus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Homo habilis</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Evidences shows australopithecines hunted with stone weapons but essentially ate fruits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47600,'biology',102,780,1685,'Which of the following not true about Neanderthal man?','[{"text": "They had a brain size of around 900 c.c.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They lived in near east and central Asia between $1,00,000-40,000$ years back", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They used hides to protect their body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They buried their dead", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Neanderthals had a brain size of $1400 \\mathrm{cc}$ and lived in near east and central Asia between $1,00,000-40,000$ years back. They used hides to protect their body and buried their dead.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47601,'biology',102,780,1685,'Select the incorrect match from the given option.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<i>Homo habilis</i> – Their brain capacities were between 650-800cc", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Homo erectus</i> – Its fossil was discovered in Java in 1891 about 1.5 mya", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Neanderthal man</i> – They used hides to protect their body and buried their dead.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ramapithecus</i> – Arose in Africa and moved across continents and developed into distinct races", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Homo sapiens arose in Africa and moved across continents and developed into distinct races.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47602,'biology',102,780,1685,'The first human-like hominid was','[{"text": "Australopithecus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homo habilis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neanderthal man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cro-Magnon man", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The first human-like hominid was Homo habilis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47603,'biology',102,780,1685,'Fossils of Homo erectus were discovered in','[{"text": "Africa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "France", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "India", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Java", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Fossils of Homo erectus were discovered in Java in the year 1891.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47625,'biology',102,780,1685,'Most ape - like ancestral primate was','[{"text": "<i>Dryopithecus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Ramapithecus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Australopithecus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Neanderthal man<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'About 15 mya, primates called <i>Dryopithecus</i> and <i>Ramapithecus</i> were existing. They were hairy and walked like gorillas and chimpanzees. <i>Ramapithecus</i> was more man-like while <i>Dryopithecus</i> was more ape-like.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47604,'biology',102,780,1685,'Select the correct statements from the following.<br>I. <i>Dryopithecus</i> and <i>Ramapithecus</i> were existing about 15 mya.<br>II. They were hairy and walked like gorillas and chimpanzees.<br>III.<i>Ramapithecus</i> was more ape-like.<br>IV.Dryopithecus was more man-like.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'About 15 mya, primates called Dryopithecus and Ramapithecus were existing. They were hairy and walked like gorillas and chimpanzees. Ramapithecus was more manlike while Dryopithecus was more ape-like.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47605,'biology',102,780,1685,'Match the following<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. First to use fire<br>B. Ape like primate<br>C. Ancestor of\nmodern apes<br>D. Connecting link\nbetween ape and\nman</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Homo erectus</i><br>Q. <i>Dryopithecus</i><br>R. <i>Australopithecus</i><br>S. <i>Propliopethecus</i></div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A - P, B - S, C - Q, D - R}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q, B - R, C - P, D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - Q, B - S, C - R, D - P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A - R, B - P, C - S, D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A - P, B - S, C -  Q, D -  R}}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47606,'biology',102,778,1683,'Choose the wrong statement regarding Hardy Weinberg principle.','[{"text": "Allele frequencies in a population are stable and constant from generation to generation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sum total of all the allelic frequencies in a population is 1 .", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Variation due to genetic drift results in changed frequency of genes and alleles in future generations.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic recombination helps in maintaining Hardy- Weinberg equilibrium.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Genetic recombination leads to variation and results in changed frequency of genes and alleles in future generation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47607,'biology',102,774,1679,'The given figure shows an example of','[{"text": "Homologous organs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Analogous organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vestigial organs", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The given figure of Bougainvillea and Cucurbita shows an example of homologous organs or divergent evolution. Homologous organ are those organs which are dissimilar in shape, size and function but their origin, basic plan and development are similar.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/102_47607_question_1.png'),
(47608,'biology',102,775,1680,'The given diagram of marsupials of Australia provides an example of','[{"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parallel evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Recapitulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Divergent evolution", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The given diagram of marsupials of Australia provides an example of divergent evolution. Divergent evolution is the accumulation of differences between groups which can lead to the formation of new species.<br>It is usually due to diffusion of the same species to different and isolated environments which blocks the gene flow among the distinct populations allowing differentiated fixation of characteristics through genetic drift and natural selection.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/102_47608_question_1.png'),
(47609,'biology',102,774,1679,'Industrial Melanism is a example for','[{"text": "Defensive adaptation of skin against ultraviolet radiations", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Drug resistance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Darkening of skin due to smoke from industries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protective resemblance with the surroundings", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Industrial melanism is a example for protective resemblance with the surroundings',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47610,'biology',102,776,1681,'Darwin\'s finches are best example of adaptive radiation which of the following best describe this adaptive radiation?','[{"text": "The evolutionary process that allows for the change that occur within the same lineage.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The genetic variability that can be found among individuals of same species.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A sudden diversification of a group of organism from closely related species.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The evolutionary process by which different forms, adapted to different niches, arose from a common ancestors.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The Darwins finches are an example of one ancestral species when moved to an isolated geographical location, undergo adaptation to meet their basic demands and evolve in different niches.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47611,'biology',102,772,1677,'The experiment that simulated conditions thought to be present on the early earth','[{"text": "Hershey-Chase experiment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Darwins experiment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hardy-Weinbergs experiment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Miller-Urey experiment", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The experiment that simulated conditions thought to be present on the early earth is known as Miller-Urey experiment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47612,'biology',102,776,1681,'According to Lamarck, a giraffe has a long neck because','[{"text": "A creator designed it that way.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Catastrophes eliminated short-necked forms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Its ancestors stretched their necks to get food.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ancestral giraffes with slightly longer necks than others got more food and left more surviving offspring.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'According to Lamarckism an organism can pass on the characteristics that it acquired during its lifetime. According to Lamarck, a giraffe has a long neck because its ancestors stretched their necks to get the food.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47613,'biology',102,774,1679,'What is true regarding industrialization in England?','[{"text": "The white-winged moths were completely wiped out after industrialization.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Since lichens grow abundantly in polluted area, the number of melanized moths got reduced.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Moths that were able to camouflage themselves, survived and produced more progeny.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "During post-industrialisation period, the tree trunks became dark due to which dark-winged moth did not survive.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During post-industrialisation period, the tree trunks became dark. The dark-winged moths that were able to camouflage themselves, survived and produced more progeny.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47651,'biology',10,258,512,'A complex of ribosomes attached to a single strand of RNA is known as','[{"text": "Polysome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Polymer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polypeptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Okazaki fragment", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A polyribosome is a cluster of ribosomes held together by a strand of messenger RNA in which each is translating.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47615,'biology',102,777,1682,'Identify the correct conclusion regarding the given statements.<br>I. There are biogeographic patterns in the distribution of species, for instance distinct bird species on an island tend to resemble one another, suggesting a common ancestor.<br>II. There are common stages in the early embryological development of organisms representing several distinct vertebrate groups.<br>III. Anatomical structures, such as forelimbs, in different groups appear to be modified versions of structures that might have been present in a common ancestor.','[{"text": "These are the example of spontaneous generation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are the evidences for the mechanism of origin of life.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are the evidences for the theory of organic evolution.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are the examples of artificial selection which occurs within populations, where natural selection does not occur.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The given statements are the evidences for Darwin\'s theory of common descent. A group of organisms share common descent, if they have a common ancestor. There is strong quantitative support for the theory that all living organisms on Earth are descended from a common ancestor. Charles Darwin proposed the theory of universal common descent through an evolutionary process in the Origin of Species.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47616,'biology',102,780,1685,'Which of the following is true about<br>Australopithecus?','[{"text": "The first human like hominid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Probably lived in East African grasslands about 2 mya", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Commonly known as Java Man", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Had a brain size of $1400 \\\\mathrm{cc}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Australopithecus evolved 2 mya and had a cranial capacity of $450 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and a height of $1.5 \\mathrm{~m}$. They were herbivorous, hunted with stone weapons.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47617,'biology',102,780,1685,'Which of the following features are correct for <i>Homo erectus</i>?<br>I. Had a brain size of around 900 c.c.<br>II. Probably ate meat.<br>III. Appeared about 1.5 mya.<br>IV. Evolved from H. habilis.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Homo erectus is an extinct species of hominid that lived throughout most of the Pleistocene, with the earliest first fossil evidence dating to around 1.5 million years ago. They had a large brain capacity around $900 \\mathrm{cc}$ and probably ate meat.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47618,'biology',102,780,1685,'Which of the following is true?','[{"text": "<i>Homo erectus</i> lived in east and central Asia and used hides to protect their bodies.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Agriculture came around 18,000 years back and pre-historic cave art developed about 10,000 years ago.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The skull of modern human resembles more closely to baby chimpanzee than to adult chimpanzee.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neanderthals made beautiful cave paintings.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The skull of modern human resembles more closely to baby chimpanzee than to adult chimpanzee. Neanderthal man lived in east and central Asia and used hides to protect their bodies. Agriculture came around 10,000 years back and pre-historic cave art developed about 18,000 years ago. Cro-Magnon man was known for cave paintings.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47619,'biology',102,780,1685,'What was the most significant trend in the evolution of hominids?','[{"text": "Shortening of jaws", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binocular vision", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increasing cranial capacity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Upright posture", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The most significant trend in the evolution of hominids is the increase in cranial capacity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47620,'biology',102,777,1682,'The following graph shows the range of variation among population members for a trait. If this population is subject to stabilizing selection for several generations, which of the distributions (1 - 4) is most likely to result?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Stabilizing selection eliminates individuals from both the extremes of phenotypic distribution and preserves individuals in the mean. The peak becomes taller.',NULL,'Medium','Graph/Figure',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/102_47620_question_1.png'),
(47621,'biology',102,774,1679,'The given bones in the forelimbs of three mammals figure shows. For these mammals, the number, position, and shape of the bones most likely indicates that they may have','[{"text": "Developed in a common environment.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Developed from the same earlier species.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Identical genotype", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Identical methods of obtaining food.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The given figures show the forelimbs of three mammals which indicate the homology among themselves. Homologous organs are those organs which are dissimilar in shape, size and function but their origin, basic plan and development are similar. Such differences are due to divergent evolution or adaptation for varied conditions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/102_47621_question_1.png'),
(47622,'biology',102,775,1680,'The given figure represents','[{"text": "Adaptive Radiation of marsupials of Australia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Convergent evolution of Homo erectus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Divergent evolution of Marupials of Australia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family tree of <i>Homo erectus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The diagram depicts Adaptive Radiation of marsupials of Australia',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/102_47622_question_1.png'),
(47623,'biology',102,774,1679,'Read the statements A and statement B carefully to mark the correct options given below.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">All vertebrates develop a row of vestigial gill slits during embryonic stage.<br></div><div class="column-right">Embryos always pass through the adult stages of other animals.<br></div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Embryological support for evolution was proposed by Ernst Heckel. It is based upon the observation of certain features during embryonic stage common to all vertebrates that are absent in adult. For example, the embryos of all vertebrates including human develop a row of vestigial gill slit just behind the head but it is a functional organ only in fish and not found in any other adult vertebrates. However, this proposal was disapproved on careful study performed by Karl Ernst von Baer. He noted that embryos never pass through the adult stages of other animals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47626,'biology',102,780,1685,'Given below are some stages of human evolution.<br>Arrange them in correct sequence. (Past to Recent)<br>A. <i>Homo habilis</i><br>B. <i>Homo sapiens</i><br>C. <i>Homo neanderthalensis</i><br>D. <i>Homo erectus</i><br>Choose the correct sequence of human evolution from the options given below:','[{"text": "D - A - C - B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B - A - D - C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C - B - D - A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - D - C - B", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct sequence of stages of human evolution from past to recent is<br><i>Homo habilis</i> $\\rightarrow$ <i>Homo erectus</i> $\\rightarrow$ <i>Homo neanderthalensis</i> $\\rightarrow$ <i>Homo sapiens</i>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47627,'biology',102,778,1683,'Which one of the following factors will not affect the Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium?','[{"text": "Genetic recombination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic drift", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gene migration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Constant gene pool", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The constant gene pool will not disturb the Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47628,'biology',102,774,1679,'The flippers of the Penguins and Dolphins are the example of the','[{"text": "Adaptive radiation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Natural selection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Convergent evolution", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Divergent evolution", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Flippers of the Penguins and Dolphins perform similar function but they are not anatomically similar structures. This is example of analogous structures. Therefore it is convergent evolution.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47629,'biology',102,779,1684,'Match Column I with Column II:<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mesozoic Era<br>B. Proterozoic Era<br>C. Cenozoic Era<br>D. Paleozoic Era</div><div class="column-right">P. Lower invertebrates<br>Q. Fish & Amphibias<br>R. Birds & Reptiles<br>S. Mammals</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  P, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q}}$ is correct option.<br>A. Mesozoic Era - R. Birds & Reptiles<br>B. Proterozoic Era - P. Lower invertebrates<br>C. Cenozoic - S. Era Mammals<br>D. Paleozoic Era - Q.Fish & Amphibia',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47630,'biology',10,262,516,'The organelles that are included in the emdomembrane system are:','[{"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum, Mitochondria, Ribosomes are Lysosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum, Golgi complex, Lysosomes and Vacuoles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Golgi complex, Mitochondria, Ribosomes and Lysosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi complex, Endoplasmic reticulum, Mitochondria and Lysosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mitochondria is not comes under endomembrane system where as endoplasmic reticulum, lysosomes, Golgi apparatus, vacuoles are endomembrane system.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47631,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following is an incorrect statement?','[{"text": "Mature sieve tube elements possess a conspicuous nucleus and usual cytoplas mic organelles.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Microbodies are present both in plant and animal cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The perinuclear space forms a barrier between the materials present inside the nucleus and that of the cytoplasm.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear pores act as passages for proteins and RNA molecules in both directions between nucleus and cytoplasm.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Choose the incorrect Statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47632,'biology',10,269,527,'Match column – I with column - II.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cristae<br>B. Thylakoids<br>C. Centromere<br>D. Cisternae</div><div class="column-right">P. Primary constriction in chromosome<br>Q. Disc-shaped sacs in golgi apparatus<br>R. Infoldings in mitochondria<br>S. Flattened membranous sacs in stroma of plastids</div></div>','[{"text": "A -S &emsp; B -R &emsp; C -Q &emsp;  D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A -P &emsp; B -S &emsp; C -R &emsp;  D - Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A -R &emsp; B -S &emsp; C -P &emsp;  D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A -Q &emsp; B -R &emsp; C -S &emsp;  D - P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cristae - Infoldings of mitochondria<br>Thylakoids - Flattened membranous sacs in stroma of plastids<br>Centromere - Primary constriction in the chromosome<br>Cisternae - Disc shaped sacs in Golgi apparatus',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47633,'biology',10,263,520,'Which of the following statements regarding mitochondria is incorrect?','[{"text": "Outer membrane is permeable to monomers of carbohydrates, fats and proteins.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enzymes of electron transport are embedded in outer membrane.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inner membrane is convoluted with infoldings.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondrial matrix contains single circular DNA molecule and ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In mitochondria, enzymes for electron transport are present in the inner membrane.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47634,'biology',10,269,527,'The shorter and longer arms of a submetacentric chromosome are referred to as','[{"text": "s-arm and l-arm respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "p-arm and q-arm respectively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "q-arm and p-arm respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "m-arm and n-arm respectively", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'● Sub metacentric chromosome is<br>● Heterobrachial.<br>● Short arm designated as ‘p’ arm (p = petite i.e. short)<br>● Long arm designated as ‘q’ arm',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47635,'biology',10,262,518,'Which of the following statements is not correct?','[{"text": "Lysosomes have numerous hydrolytic enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The hydrolytic enzymes of lysosomes are active under acidic pH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosomes are membrane bound structures", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosomes are formed by the process of packaging in the endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lysosomes bud off from trans face of Golgi bodies. Precursor of lysosomal enzymes are synthesised by RER and then send to Golgi bodies for further processing.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47636,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following pair of organelles does not contain DNA?','[{"text": "Mitochondria and Lysosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast and Vacuoles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosomes and Vacuoles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nuclear envelope and Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lysosomes and Vacuoles do not have DNA.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47637,'biology',10,262,516,'Which of the following events does not occur in rough endoplasmic reticulum?','[{"text": "Cleavage of signal peptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein glycosylation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein folding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phospholipid synthesis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum (RER) is not involved in the synthesis of Phospholipids. The smooth endoplasmic reticulum is the major site for synthesis of lipid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47638,'biology',10,256,507,'The concept of &ldquo;<em>Omnis cellula-e cellula</em>&rdquo; regarding cell division was first proposed by','[{"text": "Rudolf Virchow", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Theodor Schwann", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Schleiden", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aristotle", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Concept of &ldquo;<em>Omnis cellula-e cellula</em>&rdquo; regarding cell division was proposed by Rudolf Virchow.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47639,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following is true for nucleolus?','[{"text": "It takes part in spindle formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a membrane-bound structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Larger nucleoli are present in dividing cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a site for active ribosomal RNA synthesis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nucleolus is a cellular structure present in the nucleus of a eukaryotic cell . It is present in both plant cell as well as animal cell and it is a site for active ribosomal RNA synthesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47640,'biology',10,258,512,'Many ribosomes may associate with a single mRNA to form multiple copies of a polypeptide simultaneously. Such strings of ribosomes are termed as','[{"text": "Plastidome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polyhedral bodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polysome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleosome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A cluster of ribosomes that are connected by a strand of messenger RNA and is active in protein synthesis are called Polyribosomes or Polysomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47641,'biology',10,269,527,'Select the incorrect match :<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Submetacentric – L-shaped chromosomes chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Allosomes – Sex chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lampbrush – Diplotene bivalent chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polytene – Oocytes of chrosome amphibians", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Polytene chromosomes, also known as giant chromosomes are present in the salivary glands in third instar larvae, of two-winged flies of order Diptera. Ex: Fruit fly (Drosophila melonagaster) .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47642,'biology',10,262,517,'The Golgi complex participates in','[{"text": "Respiration in bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of secretory vesicles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fatty acid breakdown", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Activation of amino acid", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Golgi complex function in packaging of the cell products, formation of secretory vesicles and secretion.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47643,'biology',10,258,510,'Which of the following components provides sticky character to the bacterial cell?','[{"text": "Nuclear membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycocalyx", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sticky character of the bacterial wall is due to glyocalyx which is rich in glycoproteins.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47644,'biology',10,263,520,'Which of the following cell organelles is responsible for extracting energy from carbohydrates to form ATP?','[{"text": "Ribosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondrion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lysosome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mitochondrion are the sites of aerobic respiration. They are responsible for extracting energy from carbohydrates to form ATP. Therefore, they are called as Power house of the cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47645,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following cell organelles is enclosed by single membrane?','[{"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplasts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lysosomes are small vesicles (0.2-0.8µm) containing hydrolysing enzymes and surrounded by single membrane of up to 100nm thickness.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
