(47648,'biology',10,264,522,'Mitochondria and chloroplast are<br> a. Semiautonomous organelles<br>b. Formed by division of pre-existing 6.65 organelles and they contain DNA but lack protein synthesising machinery.','[{"text": "Both a and b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b is true but a is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a is true but b is false", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both a and b false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semiautonomous organelles.<br> Both mitochondria and chloroplast are semiautonomous organelles as they possess their own DNA, RNA and 70s ribosomes to have sufficient functional independence from cellular machinery.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
