(47654,'biology',10,262,518,'A cell organelle containing hydrolytic enzymes','[{"text": "Lysosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ribozyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesosome", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lysosomes, subcellular organelle that is found in nearly all types of eukaryotic cells, that contain array of enzymes capable of breaking down all of biological polymers. Lysosomes contain about 50 different degradative enzymes that can hydrolyse Proteins, DNA, RNA, Polysaccharides and lipids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47655,'biology',10,269,527,'Match the columns and identify the correct option<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Thylakoids<br>B. Cristae<br>C. Cisternae<br>D. Chromatin</div><div class="column-right">P. Disc-shaped \nsacs in golgi \napparatus<br>Q. Condensed \nstructure of DNA<br>R. Flat membranous \nsacs in stroma<br>S. Infolding in \nmitochondria</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Thylakoids are number of organised flattened membranous sacs in the stroma of chloroplast, Cristae are the partial partitions in a mitochondrion formed by infolding of the inner membrane, Cisternae is a flattened membrane disc that makes up the endoplasmic reticulum and Golgi apparatus, Chromatin is a complex of DNA and proteins that forms chromosomes within the nucleus of eukaryotic cells',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
