(47666,'biology',10,258,511,'Which structure perform the function of mitochondria in bacteria?','[{"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleiod", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mesosomes is a convoluted membranous structure formed in prokaryotic cell by the invagination of cell membrane. Its functions are as follows:<br>i. These extensions help in the synthesis of the cell wall and replication of DNA. They also help in equal distribution of chromosomes into the daughter cells.<br>ii. It also increases the surface area of the plasma membrane to carry out various enzymatic activities.<br>iii. It helps in secretion processes as well as in bacterial respiration.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
