(47671,'biology',10,262,517,'Which of the following organelle correctly matches with its function?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Rough endoplasmic reticulum-Formation of glycoprotein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi apparatus-Protein synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi apparatus-Formation of Glycoprotein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Smooth endoplasmic reticulum-Protein synthesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Golgi bodies are the sites for Glycolipids and Glycoproteins.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47672,'biology',10,262,517,'A major site for synthesis of lipids','[{"text": "Rough endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Smooth endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Symplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleoplasm", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Smooth endoplasmic reticulum is the site for synthesis of lipids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47673,'biology',10,262,516,'Which one of the following is not considered as a part of endomembrane system?','[{"text": "Golgi complex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peroxisomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vacuole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Perioxisomes is not a part of endomembrane system.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47674,'biology',10,260,514,'Which one of the following doesnot differ in E.coli and Chlamydomonas?','[{"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomal organisation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell membrane", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'E.coli (Bacteria) is a prokaryote while Chlamydomonas (algae) is a eukaryote. Itdiffers in cell wall. Cell wall organisation also differs as bacterial cell wall rich in muramic acid while algal cell wall is cellulosic. It is the\ncell membrane which has similar organisation in both the groups.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47675,'biology',10,265,523,'Which one of the following structure is an organelle within an organelle?','[{"text": "Mesosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Peroxisome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The ribosomes are the cell organelle that is present inside the other cell organelles like endoplas-mic reticulum, mitochondria, and chloroplast. So we can call it as an organelle within an organelle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47676,'biology',10,260,514,'Select the correct statement from the following regarding cell membrane:','[{"text": "Na+ and K+ ions move across cell membrane by passive transport.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteins make up 60 to 70% of the cell membrane.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipids are arranged in bilayer with polar head towards the innerpart", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fluid mosaic model of cell membrane was proposed by Singer and Nicolson", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'According to the fluid mosaic model, of cell membrane structure proposed by Singer and Nicolson (1972). Plasma membrane contains about 50-60% proteins and 50-40% lipids. Lipids form bilayer with hydrophilic\nheads pointing outwards. Cell membrane allows transport of some molecules by passive transport e.g., water, neutral solutes while some are transported actively e.g. Na+ and K+ pump.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47677,'biology',10,258,509,'Nuclear membrane is absent in','[{"text": "<em>Penicillium</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Agaricus</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Volvox</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Nostoc</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<em>Nostoc</em> is a cyanobacteria (prokaryote). So it lacks true nucleus, thus nuclear membrane is absent.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47678,'biology',10,268,526,'Which one of the following cellular parts is correctly described?','[{"text": "Lysosomes - Optimally active at a pH of about 8.5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thylakoids – Flattened membranous sacs forming the grana of chloroplasts", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centrioles – A site for active RNA synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosomes – Those in chloroplasts are larger 80s while those in the cytoplasm are smaller (70s).", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Thylakoids are arranged in stacks like the piles of coins called grana of the chloroplasts.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47679,'biology',10,265,523,'What is true about ribosomes?','[{"text": "The prokaryotic ribosomes are 80s, where ‘s’ stands for sedimentation co-efficient", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are composed of ribonucleic acid and proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "These are found only in eukaryotic cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are self-splicing introns of some RNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Ribosome is a small spherical body within a living cell that is the site of protein synthesis. Ribosome consists of two subunits, one large and one small, each of which comprises a type of RNA (called ribosomal RNA) and protein.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47680,'biology',10,262,517,'Important site formation of glycoproteins and glycolipids is','[{"text": "Vacuole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi apparatus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plastid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Golgi apparatus is the important site of formation of glycoproteins and glycolipids.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47681,'biology',10,261,515,'Which one of the following structures between two adjacent cells in an effective transport pathway?','[{"text": "Plasmadesmata", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plastoquinones", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoskeleton", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Plasmodesmata are fine cytoplasmic strands that connect the protoplasts of adjacent plant cells by passing through their cell walls. Plasmodesmata are cylindrical in shape (about 20-40 nm in diameter) and are lined by the plasmamembrane of the two adjacent cells. They permit the passage between cells of substances including ions, sugars, amino acids and macromolecules.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47682,'biology',10,266,524,'An elaborate network of filamentous proteinaceous structures present in the cytoplasm which helps in the maintainence of cell shape is called','[{"text": "Thylakoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasmalemma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoskeleton", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cytoskeleton is an elaborate network of filamentous proteinaceous structures present in the cytoplasm which helps in the maintanence of cell shape, motility and maintanence of the shape of the cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47683,'biology',10,266,524,'Cytoskeleton is made up of','[{"text": "Callose deposits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulosic Microfibrils", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteinaceous filaments", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{CaC}}{{\\\\rm{O}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$  granules", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The skeleton is made up of three kinds of protein filaments: Actin filaments, Intermediate filaments and Microtubules.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47684,'biology',10,261,515,'Plasmodesmata are________ .','[{"text": "Locomotary structures", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Membranes connecting the nucleus with\\nplasmalemma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Connections between adjacent cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lignified cement layers between cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plasmodesmata are the structures between two adjacent cells for an effective transport pathway.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47685,'biology',10,261,515,'Middle lamella is composed mainly of','[{"text": "Calcium pectate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Muramic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phosphoglycerides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemicellulose", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The middle lamella is a pectin layer which cements the cell walls of two adjoining cells together. The cell plate that is formed during cell division itself develops into middle lamellaor lamellum. The middle lamella is made up of calcium and magnesium pectates.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47686,'biology',10,265,523,'The two subunits of ribosome remain united at a critical ion level of','[{"text": "Magnesium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Calcium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Copper", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Manganese", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Each ribosome is made up of two subumits, a smaller subunit and another larger subunit. These two subunits are associated with the help of ${\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$ ions. If ${\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$ ions concentration is less in cytoplasm, the two units of ribosome separate but the ${\\rm{M}}{{\\rm{g}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$ ions concentration is increased ten times, the two unites and form a dimer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47687,'biology',10,264,522,'Select the wrong statement from the following:','[{"text": "Both chloroplasts and mitochondria have an internal compartment, the thylakoid space bounded by the thylakoid membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both chloroplasts and mitochondria contain DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The chloroplasts are generally much larger than mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both chloroplasts and mitochondria contain an inner and an outer membrane", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both chloroplasts and mitochondria contain DNA and are double membrane bound organelles. Chloroplast is also double membranous organelle but found in plants not in animals. The membrane bound matrix of chloroplasts is stroma and inside the stroma thylakoids are present which form grana.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47695,'biology',10,263,520,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> F0-F1 particles are present in the inner mitochondrial membrane.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> An electron gradient formed on the inner mitochondrial membrane forms ATP.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Oxysomes are  ${F_0} - {F_1}$ particles that are present on the inner mitochondrial membrane. The ${F_1}$ head piece of oxysome functions as ATP- synthetase which synthesises ATP from ADP and ip (inorganic phosphate) using energy from proton gradient or ATP synthetase becomes active in ATP formation only when there is proton gradient having high concentration of protons on F0 side (base) as compared to ${F_1}$ side (base) of  ${F_0} - {F_1}$ particles or oxysomes.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47688,'biology',10,267,525,'Which of the following statements regarding cilia is not correct?','[{"text": "The organized beating of cilia is controlled by fluxes of $C{a^{2 - }}$ across the membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cilia are hair-like cellular appendages", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microtubules of cilia are composed of tubulin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cilin contains an outer ring of nine doublet microtubules surrounding two single microtubules", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cilia are fine hair-like vibratile, cytoplasmic processes borne by certain cell types. Their 6.24 Cell -The Unit of Life movement either propel the organism or move the medium past a fixed cell. The cilia are enclosed by a unit membrane which is an extension of the plasma membrane of the cell. Within the membrane, is a fluid matrix having a supporting axial shaft, or axoneme. The axoneme is composed of eleven microtubules. Two microtubules are single and lie at the centre with a gap in-between. They are called central singlets. The remaining nine microtubules are double and lie in a ring around the central microtubules. The two microtubules forming a doublet are named A and B subtubules. The microtubules, single as well as double, are composed of the globular units of the protein tubulin. The arms of A microtubules contain protein dynein. The latter is ATPase enzyme which catalyzes the hydrolysis of ATP to ADP and transfers the free energy released directly to ciliary work. <br>So, the correct answer is ‘The organized beating of cilia is controlled by fluxes of Ca2+ across the membrane’',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47689,'biology',10,263,520,'Which of the following statements regarding mitochondrial membrane is not correct?','[{"text": "The outer membrane is permeable to all kinds of molecules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The enzymes of the electron transfer chain are embedded in the outer membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The inner membrane is highly convoluted forming a series of infoldings", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The outer membrane resembles a sieve", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Electron transport chains are used for extracting energy via redox reactions from sunlight in photosynthesis or, such as in the case of the oxidation of sugars, cellular respiration. In eukaryotes, an important electron transport chain is found in the inner mitochondrial membrane where it serves as the site of oxidative phosphorylation through the use of ATP synthase. It is also found in the thylakoid membrane of the chloroplast in photosynthetic eukaryotes. In bacteria, the electron transport chain is located in their cell membrane.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47690,'biology',10,267,525,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The arrangement of axonemal microtubules in cilia or flagella is called 9+2 array.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The axoneme usually has nine pairs or doublet and pair of centrally located microtubules','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The study of a cilium or the flagella shows that they are covered with plasma membrane. It possess a number of microtubules running parallel to the long axis. The axoneme usually has nine pairs or doublets of radially arranged peripheral microtubules and pair of centrally located microtubules such an arrangement of axonemal microtubules is referred to as the 9+2 array.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47691,'biology',10,269,527,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> DNA of nucleus is associated with proteins.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> DNA binds around histone proteins that form a pool and the entire structure is called nucleosome.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A chain of DNA has 140 base pairs which makes 1 ¾ turns and twists around a histone octamer forming nucleosome. The core of nucleosome consists of four histones ${H_2}A,{H_2}B,{H_3}\\,\\,and\\,\\,{H_4}$.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47692,'biology',10,262,516,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> ER acts as a circulatory system of cell.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> ER functions as cytoskeleton.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Endoplasmic reticulum functions as cytoskeleton or intracellular and ultrastructural skeletal framework by providing mechanical support to colloidal cytoplasmic matrix. The endoplasmic reticulum may act as a circulatory system for intracellular circulation of various substances. Membrane flow may also be an important mechanism for carrying particles, molecules and ions into and out of the cells.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47693,'biology',10,258,509,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Plasmids are small replicating extra-chromosomal circular DNA.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They are being used in Genetic engineering and Biotechnology.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plasmids are small self-replicating extra chromosomal circular DNA segments that endow some nonvital properties to bacteria. Plasmid that integrates temporally to nucleoid is called as episome.<br>Plasmids are transferable from one bacterium to another. They are being used in Genetic engineering and Biotechnology.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47694,'biology',10,258,509,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cyanobacteria are photosynthetic, blue green algae with all the prokaryotic structures.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They are green due to presence of chloroplasts.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cyanobacteria are the oldest organisms that appear in the fossil record dating back to 3.8 billion years. Chloroplasts first originated in cyanobacteria and it is green due to that pigment.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47696,'biology',10,262,516,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The endoplasmic reticulum which lacks ribosomes is called as smooth endoplasmic reticulum (SER).<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> SER is mainly involved in protein synthesis.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Smooth endoplasmic reticulum (SER) possesses smooth membranes which donot bear ribosomes. It is, therefore also called agranular endoplasmic reticulum. SER is responsible for synthesis of fats inside the cells of adipose tissue, formation of sphaerosomes, synthesis of glycogen as well as glycogenolysis (hydrolysis of glycogen). In liver cells, synthesis of sterols and steroid hormones as in the interstital cells of testis and ovary and formation of visual pigments from vitamin A in retinal cells.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47697,'biology',10,264,522,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Mitochondria and chloroplasts have their own genome.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Endoplasmic reticulum and Golgi body are the cell organelles which have their own DNA.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both mitochondria and chloroplast are semi-autonomous organelles as they possess their own DNA, RNA and 70s ribosomes to have sufficient functional independence from cellular machinery. The Chloroplasts DNA is bigger than mitochondrial DNA. However, genetic information contained in these DNAs is limited.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47698,'biology',10,260,514,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> A cell membrane shows fluid behaviour.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> A membrane is a mosaic or composite of diverse proteins and lipids.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The plasma membrane is the combination of phospholipids, cholesterol and proteins. Carbohydrates attached to lipids (glycolipids) and to proteins (glycoproteins) extend from the outward facing surface of the membrane.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47699,'biology',10,265,523,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Ribosomes are non-membrane bound organelles found in the prokaryotic cells only.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> These are present only in the cytoplasm','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ribosomes are non-membrane bound organelles found in eukaryotic and prokaryotic cells, within a cell. Ribosomes are found not only in the cytoplasm but also within two organelles chloroplasts (in plants) and mitochondria and on rough endoplasmic reticulum.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47700,'biology',10,263,520,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Mitochondria are common to both plant and animal cells.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The number of mitochondria in a cell doesnot corresponds to the function of the cell.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mitochondria are common to both plant and animal cells. The number of mitochondria in a cell correspond to the function of the cell.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47701,'biology',10,264,522,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semiautonomous organelles.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They are formed by division of pre-existing organelles as well as contain DNA but lack protein synthesizing machinery.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both Mitochondria and Chloroplasts are semiautonomous organelles and they possess their own DNA, RNA and 70s ribosomes for functional independence in cellular processes.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47702,'biology',10,258,511,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The fimbriae are elongated tubular structures made of special protein.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The pili are small bristle like fibres sprouting out of the cell.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'It can be corrected as<br>Assertion: The pili are elongated tubular structures made of special protein.<br>Reason: The fimbriae are small bristle like fibres sprouting out of the cell',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47710,'biology',10,262,516,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The endomembrane system comprises Endoplasmic reticulum (ER), Golgi complex, Lysosomes and Vacuoles.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Mitochondria, Chloroplast and Perioxisomes are not the part of endomembrane system as their functions are not coordinated with the same.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Endomembrane system refers to the grouping of some membrane organelles which function in close co-ordination with one another viz., endoplasmic reticulum, golgi complex, lysosomes and vacuoles. Functions\nof other organelles are not co-ordinated, they are not a part of endomembrane system e.g. chloroplasts, mitochondria, perioxisomes and glyoxisomes etc.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47703,'biology',10,257,508,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Schleiden and Schwann together formulated the Cell theory.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cells are formed from pre-existing cells.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In 1838, German botanist Matthias Schleiden found that all plant tissues are made up of cells which have essentially similar structure. German zoologist. Theodor Schwann in 1839, working independently, observed that animal cells do not have cell wall but are otherwise similar amongst them. He put forward cell hypothesis – bodies of animals and plants are made up of cells. Schleiden and Schwann (1839) compared their findings and formulated cell theory. Cell theory was further modified in the light of Virchow’s findings that new cells develop from pre-existing cells – Omnis cellula-e-cellula.<br>The two basic tenets of cell theory are:<br>I. All living organisms are composed of cells and their components.<br>II. All cells arise from pre – existing cells.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47704,'biology',10,256,507,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cell is an open system<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cell receives number of materials including energy containing nutrients from outside.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cell is an isothermal open system as all the parts of the cell at any given time maintains the same temperature and pressure. Cell is an open system in which materials and energy are transferred between organisms and the exterior environment.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47705,'biology',10,256,507,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Organisms are made up of cells.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cells are structural unit of living organisms and keeps its chemical composition steady within its boundary.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cell is the basic structural and functional unit of organisms.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47706,'biology',10,264,521,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Plastids are semiautonomous organelles.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Leucoplasts, Chromoplasts, Chloroplasts are plastids.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plastids are semiautonomous cell organelles which are surrounded by double membrane envelope, taking part in storage and synthesis of organic compounds which occur in plants and some protistans. Leucoplasts, Chromoplasts and Chloroplasts are plastids involved in different processes.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47707,'biology',10,258,509,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Plasmids are single-stranded extracellular chromosomal DNA.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Plasmids are usually possessed by eukaryotic cells.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plasmids are found mostly in prokaryotic cells and yeasts. They do not form a part of the normal chromosomal DNA of a cell and capable of replicating independently. It constitutes a form of double - stranded circular extra chromosomal DNA.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47708,'biology',10,262,516,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Endoplasmic reticulum, Golgi complex, Lysosomes and Vacuoles together form the endomembrane system.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Functions of these organelles are coordinated so, they are considered together as a system.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Endomembrane system is a system of certain cell organelles which coordinate their functions, exchanging materials among themselves by means of vesicles. Endomembrane system consists of Endoplasmic reticulum, Golgi complex, Lysosomes and Vacuoles. The term GERL is used, Golgi complex, Endoplasmic reticulum, and Lysosome. It is also used for lysosomal producing face of Golgi apparatus.The functioning of other cell organelles is not coordinated and is thus not considered as part of endomembrane system.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47709,'biology',10,269,527,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Nucleus is the controlling centre of a cell.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Pores in the nuclear envelop regulate the flow of materials in and out of the nucleus.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Nucleus is the controlling centre of a cell as it contains chromosomes and genes. Chromosomes contain the DNA which by transcription prepares RNA and that in turn leads to the formation of proteins by translation. These proteins regulate the various metabolic processes going in cell. Besides this, nucleus contains genetic information for reproduction, development and behaviour of an organism. Nuclear membrane is double layered, semi permeable and is perforated by minute circular nuclear pores. The pore controls the passage of macromolecules like tRNAs, mRNAs. Ribosomal proteins, enzymes etc, during different process of transcription, translation etc.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47711,'biology',10,258,511,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Mesosomes are the infoldings of cell membrane, they helps in cell wall formation, DNA replication and respiration.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They increase the area of surface membrane.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A special membranous structure is the mesosome which is formed by the extension of plasma membrane into the cell. These extensions are in the form of vesicles, tubules and lamellae. They help in cell wall formation, DNA replication, respiration and distribution of daughter cell. They also help in secretion processes to increase the surface area of the plasmamembrane and enzymatic content.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47712,'biology',10,260,514,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Lipids present in the outer and inner side of the bilayer membrane are commonly different.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Oligosaccharides are attached to external surface as well as inner surface of a biomembrane.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lipids present in the outer and inner side of the bilayer are commonly different e.g. Lecithin on the outerside and cephalin on the innerside of erythrocyte membrane.Oligosaccharide are attached to external surface of lipids and proteins of a biomembrane, they are absent on the inner side.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47713,'biology',10,266,524,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Eukaryotic cells have the ability to adopt a variety of shapes and carry out directed movements.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Cytoskeleton is responsible for it.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cytoskeleton is a fibrous network made of proteins that contributes to the structure and internal organisation of eukaryotic cells within the cytoplasm. It is a dynamic structure that maintains cell shape, enables some cell motion (using structures such as flagella and cilia) and plays important roles in both intracellular transport (the movement of vesicles and organelles)The cytoskeleton has three major fibre types: Microfilaments made up of actin proteins, Intermediate filaments made of various kinds of proteins (Keratin) and Microtubules made of tubulin.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47714,'biology',10,263,520,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Power house of cells is mitochondria.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Where ATP is produced in mitochondria.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mitochondria are called as “power house of a cell” because they produce large amount of energy in the form of ATP',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47715,'biology',10,258,511,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Pili are tubular structures present in bacteria which help in conjugation.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Formation of pili is controlled by or fertility factor.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pili are long and thick tubular outgrowths, which develop in response to F+ or fertility factor in gram negative bacteria. They are made up of protein pilin. A donor bacterial cell having fertility factor develops 1-4 pili. Pili are helpful in attaching to recipient cell and forming conjugation tube.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47716,'biology',10,269,527,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chromosome with two equal arms is called submetacentric chromosome.</div><div class="column-right">Chromosome with one shorter arm and one longer arm is called metacentric chromosome.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chromosome with two equal arms is called metacentric chromosome<br>Chromosome with one shorter arm and one longer arm is called sub-metacentric chromosome',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47717,'biology',10,269,527,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">When a cell it is not dividing then its nucleus is called interphase nucleus.</div><div class="column-right">Perinuclear space is generally 10 to 50 nm.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both Statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47718,'biology',10,269,527,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chromatin contains DNA and some acidic proteins called histones.</div><div class="column-right">Primary constriction of chromosome is also called centromere.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chromatin contains DNA and some basic proteins called histones.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47784,'biology',10,269,527,'The _________ of the cell directs its overall activites as well as houses its genetic material','[{"text": "Nucleolus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centromere", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The nucleus of the cell directs its overall activite as well as houses its genetic material',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47719,'biology',10,269,527,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Material of the nucleus stained the basic dyes was given the name chromatin by Flemming.</div><div class="column-right">Nucleus as a cell organelle was first described by Robert Brown as early in 1831.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both Statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47720,'biology',10,266,524,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">An elaborate network of filamentous proteinaceous structures present in the cytoplasm is called as cytoskeleton.</div><div class="column-right">Cytoskeleton consisting of microtubules, microfilaments and intermediate filaments.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both Statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47721,'biology',10,267,525,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cilia are small structures which work like oars, causing the movement of either the cell or the surrounding fluid.</div><div class="column-right">Flagella are comparatively smaller and responsible for cell movement.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Flagella are comparatively longer and responsible for cell movement',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47722,'biology',10,265,523,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Ribosomes are composed of deoxy ribonucleic acid and proteins.</div><div class="column-right">Ribosomes are surrounded by membrane.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ribosomes are composed of ribonucleic acid and proteins.<br> Ribosomes are not surrounded by membrane.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47723,'biology',10,264,522,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chloroplast contains double circular DNA molecule and ribosomes.</div><div class="column-right">The ribosomes of the chloroplasts are larger than the cytoplasmic ribosomes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chloroplast contains small double stranded circular DNA molecules and ribosomes<br> The ribosomes of the chloroplasts are smaller than the cytoplasmic ribosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47724,'biology',10,264,522,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Thylakoids are arranged in stacks like the piles of coins called grana.</div><div class="column-right">The membrane of the thylakoids enclose a space called a lumen</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both Statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47725,'biology',10,264,521,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Plastids are found in all plant cells and animals.</div><div class="column-right">Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll and carotenoid pigments.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plastids are found in all plant cells and euglenoids. Plastids are absent in animals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47726,'biology',10,264,522,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Single chloroplast is present in Chlamydomonas.</div><div class="column-right">20-40 chloroplasts are present in single mesophyll cell.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both Statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47727,'biology',10,263,520,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The number of mitochondria per cell is variable depending on the physiological activity of the cells.</div><div class="column-right">The inner compartment is filled with a dense homogeneous substance called crista</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The inner compartment is filled with a dense homogeneous substance called matrix.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47728,'biology',10,262,519,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In plant cells the vacuoles can occupy up to 10 per cent of the volume of the cell.</div><div class="column-right">In Amoeba the contractile vacuole is important for osmoregulation and excretion.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In plant cells the vacuoles can occupy up to 90 per cent of the volume of the cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47785,'biology',10,269,527,'Nucleus contain a network of subdivisions called as','[{"text": "Microfilaments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microtubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromatin fibers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromatin network", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Nucleus contains a network of subdivisions called as chromatin network.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47729,'biology',10,262,518,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Lysosomal vesicles contain hydrolytic enzymes.</div><div class="column-right">Hydrolytic enzymes are active at the basic pH</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hydrolytic enzymes are active at the acidic pH',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47730,'biology',10,262,516,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Convex cis face also called forming face</div><div class="column-right">Concave trans face also called maturing face.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both Statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47731,'biology',10,262,517,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The golgi apparatus principally performs the function of packaging materials.</div><div class="column-right">Golgi apparatus is the important site of formation of glycoproteins and glycolipids.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both Statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47732,'biology',10,262,516,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The endoplasmic reticulum bearing ribosomes on their surface is called SER.</div><div class="column-right">The SER is the major site for synthesis of protein synthesis and secretion.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The endoplasmic reticulum bearing ribosomes on their surface is called RER (Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum). The RER is the major site for protein synthesis and secretion.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47733,'biology',10,262,516,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Endomembrane system includes endoplasmic reticulum, golgi complex, lysosomes and ribosomes.</div><div class="column-right">Mitochondria, chloroplast and peroxisomes are not included under Endomembrane system.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Endomembrane system does not include ribosome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47734,'biology',10,261,515,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cell wall forms an outer covering for the plasma membrane of fungi and animals.</div><div class="column-right">The cell wall of a young plant cell, which is capable of growth is called secondary wall.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cell wall forms an outer covering for the plasma membrane of fungi only. In animal cell wall is absent. The cell wall of a young plant cell, which is capable of growth is called primary wall.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
