(47775,'biology',10,259,513,'Which of the following is not true of a eukaryotic cell?','[{"text": "Cell wall is made up of peptidoglycans", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It has 80S type of ribosome present in the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria contain circular DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Membrane bound organelles are present", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In eukaryotic cell, cellulose makes the cell wall.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47776,'biology',10,262,517,'Which of the following statements is true for a secretory cell?','[{"text": "Golgi apparatus is absent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rough EndoplasmicReticulum (RER) is easily observed in the cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum (SER) is present", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Secretory granules are formed in nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cells actively involved in protein synthesis and secretion have extensive and continuous RER within the outer membrane of nucleus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47777,'biology',10,265,523,'Select one which is not true for ribosome','[{"text": "Made of two sub units", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Form polysome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "May attach to mRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Have no role in protein synthesis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Ribosome are responsible for protein synthesis',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47778,'biology',10,269,527,'Which ofthe following stains is not used for staining chromosomes?','[{"text": "Basic Fuchsin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Safranin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Methylene blue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carmine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Other stains in the option are used for staining chromosomes or nucleus whereas safranin is generally used as counter stain in gram staining.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47779,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following features is common to prokaryotes and eukaryotes?','[{"text": "DNA is genetic material", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell wall present", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear membrane present", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Membrane-bound sub-cellular organelles present", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nuclear membrane and membrane bound organelles are absent in prokayrotes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47780,'biology',10,257,508,'Choose the correct statements from the codes given below.<br>I. Schleiden studies were based on different  kinds of plant cells and tissues<br>II. Human cheek cells have an outer membrane as the delimiting structure<br>III. Cells of plant tissues are often connected with one another through cytoplasmic bridges called middle lamella<br>IV. Human cheek cells do not possess a cell wall.','[{"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cells of plant tissues are often connected with one another through cytoplasmic bridges called Plasmodesmata.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47781,'biology',10,270,528,'Which of the following is incorrect about the microbodies?','[{"text": "These are present in bacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Minute membranous vesicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These have various enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are present in plants and animals", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Microbodies are present only in eukaryotes as they are minute membranous vesicles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47782,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following statements is not correct?','[{"text": "An incomplete cell structure does not ensure independent living", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic material is contained in the nucleus of the eukaryotes cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cytoplasm is the main arena of cellular activities in both plant and animal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centriole is non-membranous and commonly found in plant cells", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Centriole is non-membranous and commonly found in animal cells. Centrioles are absent in almost all plant cells.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47783,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following organelles contain coding DNA?','[{"text": "Chloroplast ribosomes and nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast, mitochondrion and nucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chloroplast, mitochondrion, ribosome and nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast, mitochondrion, ribosome, RER", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chloroplast, mitochondria and nucleus contain coding DNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47790,'biology',10,269,527,'Which one is correct about the nuclear membranes?','[{"text": "Inner membrane has nucleopores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the membranes are always parallel to each other and never fuse", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the membranes are parallel to each other and fuse to form nuclear pores at a number of places", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inner membrane is attached with ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both the membranes are parallel to each other and fuse to form nuclear pores at a number of places, this is the correct statement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47791,'biology',10,269,527,'The most important function of nuclear envelope is to','[{"text": "Regulate nucleo cytoplasmic traffic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA transcription", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prevent the entry of active dictyosomes into the nucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synthesize DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The most important function of nuclear envelope is to prevent the entry of active ribosomes into the nucleus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(47792,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following statements is not correct?','[{"text": "A single human cell has 2 m long thread of DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Part of chromosomes after second constriction is called telomere", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centromere forms first site of constriction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromatin consists of DNA, RNA, histones and non-histones", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Telomeres, the repetitive DNA repeat sequences at the end of linear eukaryotic chromosomes protecting chromosome ends from degradation and illegitimate recombination, play a crucial role in cell fate and aging.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47793,'biology',10,268,526,'Which of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "Centrioles form spindle poles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrioles form the basal body of spindle fibres only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centriole is membrane less, but surrounded by amorphous pericentriolar bodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrosome usually contains two cylindrical centrioles", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Centrioles forms the basal body which forms cilia and flagella and also forms spindle fibres',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47794,'biology',10,268,526,'Which of the following statement is false?','[{"text": "Both the centrioles in a centrosome lie perpendicular to each other.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Each centriole has an organization like that of a cart wheel.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Central nucleic acid hub is present in a centriole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centrosome usually contain 2 cylindrical centrioles.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The sentence can be corrected as - Central proteinaceous hub is present in a centriole',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47795,'biology',10,267,525,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "Cilium and flagellum are covered with plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Flagella are comparatively longer and responsible for cell movement.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cilia are smaller which works like oars, causing the movement of either the cells or surrounding fluid.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47796,'biology',10,267,525,'Which of the following is true about the internal structure of axoneme?','[{"text": "The axoneme usually has nine pairs of doublets of radially arranged peripheral microtubules", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Axoneme is not covered by plasma membrane at all.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radial spokes are not found.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peripheral doublets are not connected with each other", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The axoneme usually has nine pairs of doublets of radially arranged peripheral microtubules',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47797,'biology',10,268,526,'Find out the incorrect statement:','[{"text": "Centrosome is cytoplasmic structure of animal cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centriole gives rise to spindle fibres at the time of cell division in animal cell.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrosome is an organelle usually containing two cylindrical structures called centrioles.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peripheral fibril of centriole is singlet.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Peripheral fibril of centriole is singlet.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47798,'biology',10,267,525,'Which of the following statements regarding cilia is correct?','[{"text": "Cilia contains an outer ring of nine doublet microtubules surrounded by a pair of microtubules singly in centre.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centriole contains an outer ring of nine doublet microtubules surrounded by a pair of microtubules singly in centre.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cilia are not used for motility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Microtubules of cilia are composed of tubulin.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Microtubules are basic in cilia and microtubules are not made of tubulin molecules.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47799,'biology',10,267,525,'Choose the correct statement about cilia and flagella.','[{"text": "They are hair-like outgrowths of the cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eukaryotic flagella are not structurally different from prokaryotic flagella", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They originate from basal bodies - centriole like structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3 are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'1 and 3 are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47800,'biology',10,269,527,'Match the following.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Replicates emiconservati vely<br>B. Has molecules doubled in semiconservative manner<br>C. Arises from an organelle that has ribonucleopro tein particles on its outer surface<br>D. Loses its porous membrane during prophase Metaphase transition</div><div class="column-right">1. Endoplasmic reticulum<br>2. Nucleus<br>3. Chloroplasts<br>4. Centriole<br>5. Golgi complex</div></div>','[{"text": "A-4 B-3 C-5 D-2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-4 B-5 C-2 D-3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-5 B-4 C-1 D-2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-4 B-3 C-5 D-3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During centriole duplication daughter centriole is formed on parental centriole with each daughter centrosome having one parental centriole and one daughter centriole. Chloroplast has circular DNA that replicates in semiconservative manner. Golgi complex arises from E.R. that may possess Ribosomes. Nucleus is the structure whose membrane is porous and lost at the end of prophase.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47822,'biology',10,261,515,'Which of the following is the correct statement about cellwall of eukaryotic cell?','[{"text": "Algae have cell wall, made of cellulose, galactans, mannans and minerals like calcium carbonate,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It mainly consists of Ca-pectate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cell wall and middle lamellae may be traversed by plasmodesmata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the statements are correct about cell wall.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47801,'biology',10,267,525,'Which one of the following is true about cilia/ flagella of eukaryotes <br>Peripheral Central Radical Central microtubules microtubules spokes Sheath<br> &emsp; (Doublet)&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; (Singlet)','[{"text": "9 + 0 &emsp; &emsp; 2 &emsp;  &emsp; &emsp; 8 &emsp; &emsp;  &emsp; 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9 + 2 &emsp;   9 + 0  &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;  9 &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;  1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;  6  &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;  9  &emsp; &emsp; &emsp;   1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9 &emsp; &emsp; &emsp; 2&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; 9&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; 1", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In cilia and Flagella of eukaryotic organism 9 peripheral micro tubules (Doublet), 2 central microtubules (singlet), 9 radical spokes and 1 central sheath are arranged.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47802,'biology',10,268,526,'Number of structural microtubules associated with a cell of an animal in Mitosis is','[{"text": "40", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "54", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "108", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "80", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Microtubules of Centrioles, Flagella and Cilia are structural microtubules. During mitosis number of microtubules in the 4 centrioles with each centriole having 27 microtubules is 108.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47803,'biology',10,264,522,'Which of the following statements are incorrect regarding leucoplasts?','[{"text": "Amyloplasts store protein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Elaioplasts store lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteinplasts/Aleuroplast stores proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplasts contain granum and photosynthetic pigments", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Amyloplasts store starch',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47804,'biology',10,265,523,'Identify the incorrect statement about ribosomes','[{"text": "Absent in plastids and mitochondria.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-membrane bound", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Present in the cytoplasm and RER.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Take part in protein synthesis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ribosomes are present in plastids and mitochondria',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47805,'biology',10,264,522,'A plant suspension was prepared by grinding up plant material. The component parts were then separated via centrifugation. At the end of this process, there was a layer of sediment at the bottom of the test tube covered by an aqueous solution, organelles found in the sediment took up carbon dioxide and produced oxygen when illuminated. The organelles are likely to be','[{"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclei", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A plant suspension was prepared by grinding up plant material. The component parts were then separated via centrifugation. At the end of this process, there was a layer of sediment at the bottom of the test tube covered by an aqueous solution, organelles found in the sediment took up carbon dioxide and produced oxygen when illuminated. So the cell organelle is chloroplast.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47806,'biology',10,268,526,'Choose the incorrect pair.','[{"text": "Chloroplast - traps light energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromoplast - imparts colours to the plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leucoplast - stores nutrients", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrioles- motility", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Centrioles do not play direct role in motility.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47807,'biology',10,264,521,'Identify the correct statement about plastids','[{"text": "Found in all plant cells and eulenoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are large in size", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bear some specific pigments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the statements are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47808,'biology',10,264,522,'Which of the statements are false regarding chloroplast?','[{"text": "It is double membrane bound organelle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplasts are site of dark reaction only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chloroplasts are responsible for the synthesis of carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chloroplast is double membrane bound organelle, it is site of photosynthesis and responsible for the synthesis of carbohydrates',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47809,'biology',10,263,520,'All the listed characteristics are true about mitochondria, except','[{"text": "Their inner membrane forms number of infoldings called cristae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Physiological activity of cells determines its number per cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It divide by fission", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The two membranes have same enzymes associated with the mitochondrial function.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The two membranes of mitochondria have their own specific enzymes associated with the mitochondrial function.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47810,'biology',10,269,527,'A few cells and associated entities are listed. Which of them represents the correct ascending order of the size relative to each other','[{"text": "Mitochondrion &lt; <em>Paramecium</em> &lt; Human &lt; erythorocyte &lt; E. coli", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Virus &lt; Protein &lt; <em>Paramecium</em> &lt; Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein &lt; Virus &lt; Mitochondrion &lt; Chloroplast &lt; human RBC", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus &lt; Protein &lt; <em>Paramecium</em> &lt; Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Protein &lt; Virus &lt; Mitochondrion &lt; Chloroplast &lt; human RBC',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47811,'biology',10,263,520,'All the statements are true except','[{"text": "Mitochondria are called as the power plants or power houses of the cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria also serves for anaerobic respiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mitochondria is the site of krebs cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria is the site of ETS", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mitochondria is the site of aerobic respiration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47812,'biology',10,265,523,'Cell organelle A is involved in polymerizing the biomolecules which consists of amines groups.The instructions for formation is given by B and finally it is processed and packaged in C. The cell organelle A, B, C are respectively','[{"text": "Nucleus, Ribosome, Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosomes, Nucleus, Golgi complex", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chloroplast, Ribosome, Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondrion, Endoplasmic reticulum, Golgi complex", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cell organelle A- Ribosomes is involved in polymerizing the biomolecules which consists of amines groups.The instructions for formation is given by B-Nucleus and finally it is processed and packaged in C-Golgi complex',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47813,'biology',10,264,522,'Select the wrong statements from the following:','[{"text": "Both chloroplast and mitochondria contain an inner and outer membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both chloroplast and mitochondria have an internal compartment,always called as stroma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The chloroplasts are generally much larger than mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both chloroplast and mitochondria contain DNA and 70 S ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both mitochondria and chloroplast are double membrane bound organelles. Thylakoids are absent in mitochondria it is present only in chloroplast.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47814,'biology',10,264,522,'Choose the correct statements<br>i. Chloroplast transform chemical energy into sugars<br> ii. Mitochondrion is a power-house of cell as it produces most of the cellular ATP<br>iii. Mitochondria and chloroplast are found in plant cells<br> iv. Mitochondria are the sites of anaerobic respiration<br> v. The stroma of mitochondria posses a single linear DNA, many RNA molecules, 80S ribosomes','[{"text": "iv and v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv and v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii and v", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'iv. Mitochondria are the sites of aerobic respiration. <br>v. The matrix of mitochondria possesses single circular DNA molecule, a few RNA molecules, ribosomes (70S) and the components required for the synthesis of proteins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47815,'biology',10,262,519,'Which of the following statements is correct?','[{"text": "The vacuole is bound by a single membrane called tonoplast.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In many cells as in protists, food vacuoles are formed by engulfing the food particles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vacuole is always small sized in all cells of plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both these statements are correct.<br>(1) The vacuole is bound by a single membrane called tonoplast.<br>(2) In many cells as in protists, food vacuoles are formed by engulfing the food particles',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47816,'biology',10,262,519,'Why the concentration of a number of ions and other materials is higher in vacuoles than those in cytoplasm?','[{"text": "Tonoplast has a number of active transport system that pumps ions into vacuole from cytoplasm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Diffusion allows a large amount of ions to move into vacuole from cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoplasmic ions enter the vacuole through osmotic flow of water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vacuole is unable to store , so ions move themselves along concentration gradient", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In plants, the tonoplast facilitates the active transport of a number of ions and other materials against concentration gradients into the vacuole. Hence, the ions and other materials are present in a concentration which is significantly higher in the vacuole than in the cytoplasm.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47817,'biology',10,262,519,'Fill in the blanks:<br> In plant cells the vacuoles can occupy up to ...a... of the volume of the cell. In plants, the tonoplast facilitates the transport of a number of ions and other materials ...b... concentration gradient into the vacuole, hence their concentration is significantly ...c... in the vacuoles than in the cytoplasm. In Amoeba the ...d... vacuole is important for excretion. In many cells, as in protists ...e... vacuoles are formed by engulfing the food particles.','[{"text": "c--higher, d-- contractile, e -- food", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "c--higher, d-- food, e-- contractile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-- 70%, c--higher, d-- contractile,e--food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b--against, c--lower, d-- contractile", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'a. In plant cells the vacuoles can occupy up to 90% of the volume of the cell<br>b. In plants, the tonoplast facilitates the transport of a number of ions and other materials against concentration gradient into the vacuole, hence their concentration is significantly higher in the vacuole than in the cytoplasm.<br>C. In Amoeba the contractile vacuole is important for excretion.<br>D. In many cells, as in protists food vacuoles are formed by engulfing the food particles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47818,'biology',10,262,518,'Which one of the following is the function of lysosomes?','[{"text": "Presence of hydrolytic enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autolysis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lysosomes is subcellular organelles which perform many important cellular functions. For example, lysosomes digest foreign material and engulf viruses and bacteria presenting in phagosomes during the process of\nphagocytosis. In addition, lysosomes destroy targeted organelles, such as mitochondria, and injured cells via autolysis. Autolysis plays a central role in many apoptotic cascades.<br>Lysosomal functions are dependent <br>on lysosomes fusing with target vacuoles and release of digestive enzymes. Lysosomes are also responsible for digesting protein from the cell surface presented via endocytosis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47819,'biology',10,262,517,'Golgi apparatus is absent in','[{"text": "Animal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Yeast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plants", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Golgi apparatus is absent in bacteria.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47820,'biology',10,262,517,'Which one of the following organelles is located near the nucleus and contains a collection of flattened membrane bound cisternae?','[{"text": "Golgi apparatus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleolus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Golgi apparatusis located near the nucleus and contains a collection of flattened membrane bound cisternae.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47821,'biology',10,262,516,'Which of the following best describes the function of rough endoplasmic reticulum in eukaryotic cells?','[{"text": "Processing and packaging proteins into transport vesicles for delivery", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of new membrane lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synthesis of DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The endoplasmic reticulum (ER) is involved in the synthesis and delivery of proteins to their various cellular destinations or in case of plasma proteins and digestive enzymes, to the plasma membrane for secretion. The membrane part of ER known as the rough ER is studded with ribosomes. The protein RNA complexes that synthesize proteins other sections have no ribosomes and constitute the smooth ER, which is the site of synthesis of new membrane lipids and also processes and packages proteins into vesicles for transport to the Golgi apparatus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47823,'biology',10,260,514,'Which of the following describes the fluid mosaic model of the plasma membrane structure?','[{"text": "Phospholipid monolayer with embedded proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phospholipid bilayer with embedded proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phospholipid trilayer with embedded proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Triglycerides bilayer with embedded proteins", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The fluid mosaic model of the plasma membrane structure is a Phospholipid bilayer with embedded proteins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47824,'biology',10,260,514,'Which of the following statements is incorrect about the plasma membrane?','[{"text": "Biochemical investigation clearly revealed that the cell membranes also possess protein and carbohydrate.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "40% protein and 52 % lipids are in the membrane of human RBCs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Integral proteins are partially or totally buried in the membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Head of lipid is hydrophilic", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'52% Protein and 40% lipids are in the membrane of human RBCs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47825,'biology',10,260,514,'Which molecule in animal plasma membrane reduces the permeability of the membrane to most biological molecules?','[{"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phospholipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycolipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cholesterol", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cholesterol reduces the permeability of the membranes to most biological molecules',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47826,'biology',10,258,512,'Identify the incorrect statement for prokaryotic inclusion bodies.','[{"text": "These are storage granules in the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have ribosomes attached to it .", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phosphate granules, cyanophycean granules and glycogen granules are the examples of cell inclusions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gas vacuole is found in BGA and purple and green photosynthetic bacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Inclusion bodies do not have ribosomes attached to it.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47827,'biology',10,258,512,'Several ribosomes may attach to single mRNA and form a chain called polyribosomes or polysome. The ribosomes of a polysome translate the','[{"text": "m RNA to nucleic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "m RNA to proteins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "m RNA to amino acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Several ribosomes may attach to single mRNA and form a chain called polyribosomes or polysome. The ribosomes of a polysome translate mRNA to proteins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47828,'biology',10,257,508,'Choose the incorrect statement.','[{"text": "Human red blood cells are about 7.0 µm in diameter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria are 3-5 µm in lenght", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The largest cell is the egg of an ostrich", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycoplasma is the largest cell", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mycoplasma is the smallest cell.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47829,'biology',10,258,512,'Select the correct statement about prokaryotic ribosomes.','[{"text": "50S and 20S subunits unite to form 70S ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polysome consists of one ribosomes attached to many mRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosome is the site of lipid synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polysomes indicate the synthesis of identical polypeptides in multiple copies", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'50S and 30S unite to form 70S ribosome.<br>Several ribosomes may attach to a single mRNA and form a chain called polyribosomes or polysome.<br>Ribosome is the site of protein synthesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47830,'biology',10,256,507,'Which of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "Unicellular organisms are capable of independent existence", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Any structure less than a complete structure of a cell does not ensure independent living", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Matthias Schleiden, a German zoologist discovered the nucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leeuwenhoek first saw described a live cell", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Matthias schleiden was German Botanist.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47831,'biology',10,258,509,'What is the main difference between prokaryotes and eukaryotes?','[{"text": "Prokaryotes cannot undergo cell division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prokaryotes have no internal membranes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prokaryotes have no DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prokaryotes have no cytosol", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The feature of prokaryotes that sets them apart from eukaryotes is their lack of internal membranes i.e., their interiors are not compartmentalized into organelles in the way eukaryotic cells are.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47832,'biology',10,258,511,'Select the wrong statement:','[{"text": "Bacteria exhibits 4 basic shapes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pili and fimbriae are mainly involved in motility of bacterial cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria lack flagellated cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycoplasma is a wall less microorganism", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pili and fimbriae are surface structures of the bacteria but do not play a role in motility.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47833,'biology',10,258,509,'Which of the following would be found in an animal cell but not in a bacterial cell?','[{"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bacterial cells lack mitochondria',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47834,'biology',10,258,511,'Read the following statement and find out the incorrect statement:','[{"text": "Bacterial cells may be motile or non-motile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacterial flagellum is composed of two parts – filament and basal body", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The fimbriae are small bristle like fibres sprouting out of the cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The pili are elongated tubular structures of special protein", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bacterial flagellum is composed of three parts- filament, hook and basal body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47835,'biology',10,258,512,'In prokaryotic cells, the stored reserve material in the cytoplasm is in the form of','[{"text": "Inclusion body", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Reserve food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both a and b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Inclusion bodies are non-living substances present in the vacuoles, cytoplasm or cell wall. They are a kind of storage granules lying freely in the cytoplasm. The inclusion bodies are the bacterial cellular reserve materials. They are of two types: Organic inclusion bodies: They include cyanophycean starch granules and glycogen granules. Inorganic inclusion bodies: They include polyphosphate granules and  sulphur granules.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47839,'biology',10,257,508,'i. Animal cells contain another non-membrane bound organelle called centriole which helps in cell division.<br>ii. Human RBC is about 7.0 in diameter<br>iii. Cytoplasm is the main area of cellular activities<br>iv. The shape of the cells may vary with the function they perform','[{"text": "Only i and ii are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only iv is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All are correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47840,'biology',10,258,509,'In which one of the following the amount and the type of genomic DNA generally remains the same throughout their lifecycle?','[{"text": "Prokaryotes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "BGA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In prokaryotes- Bacteria, BGA, the amount of DNA remains same throughout the life cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47841,'biology',10,256,507,'Select the right option, which relates to Rudolf Virchow regarding the following statements.<br>I. Rudolf Virchow (1855) first explained <em>Omnis cellula-e cellula</em><br>II. According to him, cells divided and new cells are formed from pre-existing cells<br>III. He modified the hypothesis of Schleiden and Schwann to give the cell theory a final shape.<br>Choose the correct option from below.','[{"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and III are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Rudolf Virchow (1855) first explained cells divided and new cells are formed from pre-existing cells (<em>Omnis cellula-e cellula</em>). He modified the hypothesis of Schleiden and Schwann to give the cell theory a final shape.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47842,'biology',10,256,507,'Identify the correct option which relates to Schwann regarding the following statement<br>i. Schwann (1839), a British Zoologist, studied different types of animal cells<br>ii. He reported that cells have a thin  outer layer which is today known as  plasma membrane<br>iii. Cell wall is a unique character of the plant  cell and the body of plants and animals are composed of cells and products of cells','[{"text": "Only iii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Schwann (1839), a British Zoologist, studied different types of animal cells Schwann reported that cells outer thin layer is called plasma membrane, and cell wall is unique character of plant cell. Body of plants and animals are composed of cells and its products.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
