(47857,'biology',10,269,527,'When the chromosome has a centromere near one end of a chromosome resulting in one shorter and one longer arm, the chromosome is called','[{"text": "Telocentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acrocentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Submetacentric", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Metacentric", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Submetacentic chromosome is a chromosome with the centromere that divides the chromosome into strikingly unequal length.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47858,'biology',10,269,527,'Centromere is required for','[{"text": "Cytoplasmic cleavage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Movement of chromosomes towards poles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Crossing over", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Translation", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The centromere is the point on a chromosome where mitotic spindle fibers attach to pull sister chromatids apart during cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47859,'biology',10,269,527,'Based on the position of centromere, the chromosomes are classified into how many types?','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Based on the position of centromere, the chromosomes are classified into four types. The metacentric chromosome has middle centromere forming two equal arms of the chromosome. The sub-metacentric chromosome has centromere slightly away from the middle of the chromosome resulting into one shorter arm and one longer arm. In case of acrocentric chromosome the centromere is situated close to its end forming one extremely short and one very long arm, whereas the telocentric chromosome has a terminal centromere.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47860,'biology',10,269,527,'A chromosome having centromere at the centre is','[{"text": "Acrocentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telocentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metacentric", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sub-metric", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chromosome with centrally placed centrosome divides the chromosome into two arms having approximately equal length.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47861,'biology',10,269,527,'L – shaped chromosomes are also called as','[{"text": "Telocentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acrocentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metacentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sub metacentric", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'If the centromere divides the chromosome into two unequal arms, the chromosome is called submetacentric chromosome or L-shaped chromosome.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47862,'biology',10,269,527,'Identify the primary constriction on the chromosome?','[{"text": "Centromere", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centrosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kinetochores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spindle fibres", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Every chromosome (visible only in dividing cells) essentially has a primary constriction or the centromere. Centromere holds two chromatids of a chromosome.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
