(47933,'biology',10,264,522,'Carefully observe the given diagram and select the correct option<br>I. It is found in all plant cells and in euglenoides.<br>II. It contains chlorophyll and carotenoid pigments.<br>III. Its number in one mesophyll cell is 20-40. <br>IV. It also contains small, double stranded  circular DNA molecule and ribosomes.<br>V. Its ribosomes are larger (80S) than the cytoplasmic ribosomes (70S).','[{"text": "II, III, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ribosomes of the chloroplasts are smaller (70S) than the cytoplasmic ribosomes (80S).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_47933_question_1.png'),
