(47974,'biology',10,263,520,'Which one of the following is called as ‘power houses’ of cell?','[{"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi apparatus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mitochondria are the sites of aerobic respiration. They produce cellular energy in the form of ATP; hence they are called “Power houses” of the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47975,'biology',10,263,520,'Mitochondria is sausage-shaped or cylindrical having a diameter of______ and length_____.','[{"text": "0.2-1.0 µm, 1.0-4.1 µm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1.0-4.1 µm, 0.2-1.0 µm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.2-1.0 µm, 0.2-1.0 µm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1.0-4.1 µm, 1.0-4.1 µm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Typically mitochondria is sausage-shaped or cylindrical having a diameter of 0.2-1.0µm (average 0.5µm) and length 1.0-4.1µm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47976,'biology',10,263,520,'The amount or number of mitochondria in a cell depends on','[{"text": "Anatomical structure of cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Physiological activity of cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is always a fixed number", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Size of the cell", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Materials to be packaged in the form of vesicles from the ER fuse with the cis face of the golgi apparatus and move towards the maturing face.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47977,'biology',10,263,520,'Both the membranes of a mitochondrion are-','[{"text": "Structurally as well as functionally similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structurally different but functionally similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structurally similar  but functionally different", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Structurally as well as functionally different", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both membranes of mitochondria are structurally and functionally different.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47978,'biology',10,262,519,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Lysosomes<br>B. Vacuole membrane<br>C. Contractile vacuole<br>D. Food vacuoles</div><div class="column-right">P. Tonoplast<br>Q. Osmoregulation and excretion<br>R. Hydrolytic enzymes<br>S. Engulfing the food particles</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lysosomes – Hydrolytic enzymes <br>Vacuole membrane – Tonoplast<br>Contractile Vacuole - Osmoregulation and excretion.<br> Food vacuoles – Engulfing the food particle.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47979,'biology',10,262,517,'Choose the right sequence/route of the secretory product?','[{"text": "RER → GB → Lysosome →Nuclear membrane → Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ER → Vesicles → Cis region of GB → Trans region of GB → Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ER → Vesicles → Trans region of GB → C is region of GB → Vesicles → Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosome → ER → GB → Vesicles→ Cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'ER → Vesicles → Cis region of GB →Trans region of GB → Plasma membrane',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47980,'biology',10,262,519,'Which of the following are formed in protists, by engulfing the food particles?','[{"text": "Sap vacuole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water vacuole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Food vacuoles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Excretory vacuole", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Food vacuoles are formed in protists, by engulfing the food particles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47981,'biology',10,262,519,'Which of the following is correct about vacoule?','[{"text": "In many cells, as in protists, food vacuoles are formed by engulfing the food particles.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In plant cell the vacuole can occupy up to 90 per cent of the volume of the cell.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The vacuole is the membrane-bound space found in the cytoplasm.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The vacuole is the membrane-bound space found in the cytoplasm. It contains water, sap, excretory product and other materials not useful for the cell. The vacuole is bound by a single membrane called tonoplast. In plant cells the vacuoles can occupy up to 90 per cent of the volume of the cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47982,'biology',10,262,519,'The contractile vacuole present in amoeba is useful for','[{"text": "Digestion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Locomotion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Excretion", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In Amoeba the contractile vacuole is important for osmoregulation and excretion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47983,'biology',10,262,519,'Tonoplast membrane is important for','[{"text": "Transporting ions along concentration gradient.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transporting ions against concentration gradient.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Providing rigidity to structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In plants, the tonoplast facilitates the transport of a number of ions and other materials against concentration gradients into the vacuole, hence their concentration is significantly higher in the vacuole than in the\ncytoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47984,'biology',10,262,519,'Identify the membrane that surrounds the vacuole?','[{"text": "Protoplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tonoplast", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The vacuole is bound by a single membrane called tonoplast.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47985,'biology',10,262,519,'Cell sap is found inside','[{"text": "Vacuoles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The vacuole is the membrane-bound space found in the cytoplasm. It contains water, sap, excretory products and other materials not useful for the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47986,'biology',10,262,519,'In plant cells the vacuoles can occupy up to ________of the volume of the cell.','[{"text": "90 per cent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "80 per cent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "70 per cent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100 per cent", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In plant cells the vacuoles can occupy up to 90 per cent of the volume of the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47987,'biology',10,262,519,'Which of the following are not the contents of vacuole?','[{"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sap", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enzymes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Excretory products", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The vacuole contains water, sap, excretory products and other materials not useful for the cell. Vacuole do not contain enzymes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47988,'biology',10,262,519,'Which one of the following is a part of the endomembrane system?','[{"text": "Crystals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vacuole", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Starch", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fat droplets", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Vacuole is a large central space in the cell and it is not a cell inclusion.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47990,'biology',10,262,518,'Which of the following cannot be digested by hydrolytic enzymes?','[{"text": "DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Hydrolytic enzymes break down Protein, lipids, nucleic acids, carbohydrates and fat molecules into their simplest units. Glucose is simplest form of carbohydrate and hence cannot be converted further into simpler\ncarbohydrate hence hydrolytic enzyme cannot digest glucose.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47991,'biology',10,262,518,'A distinctive feature of the lysosome is that it has-','[{"text": "A higher pH than the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A lower pH than the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A reduced hydrolase activity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Double membraned envelope", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A distinctive feature of the lysosome is that it has a lower pH than the cytoplasm',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47992,'biology',10,262,518,'Lysosome are generally found in','[{"text": "Animal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacterial cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lysosomes are membrane bounded organelles found in animal and plant cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47993,'biology',10,262,518,'Lysosomes contain ________','[{"text": "Lipases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acid hydrolases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Lysosomes contains 50-60 types of acid hydrolases for digestion of various materials (e.g., Nucleases, Proteases, and Lipases etc.).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47994,'biology',10,262,518,'Presence of residual bodies in a cell organelle is an indication of cell aging. The cell organelle with such bodies is','[{"text": "Golgi complex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Peroxisome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lysosomes are membrane enclosed organelles that contain array of enzyme capable of breaking down all types of biological polymers',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47995,'biology',10,262,518,'Which one of the following is called the suicidal sacs of the cell?','[{"text": "Golgi body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Macrosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lysosomes are membrane enclosed organelles that contain array of enzyme capable of breaking down all types of biological polymers. One of its main function is to digest materials taken up from outside the cell. The process is called Endocytosis, that why it is called as Suicidal sac of the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47996,'biology',10,262,518,'Which one of the following is formed by packaging in golgi apparatus?','[{"text": "Lysosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lysosomes are membrane-bound vesicular structures formed by the process of packaging in the Golgi apparatus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47997,'biology',10,262,518,'The pH of lysosome is','[{"text": "Neutral", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acidic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Basic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The size of lysosomes varies from 0.1 μm to 1.2μm. With a pH ranging from 4.5 to 5.0, the interior of the lysosomes is acidic compared to the slightly basic cytosol (pH 7.2).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47998,'biology',10,262,517,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Golgi apparatus<br>B. Densely stainedreticular structures near the nucleus<br>C. Concave side of GC<br>D. Convex side of GC</div><div class="column-right">P. Cis face<br>Q. Camillo Golgi<br>R. Function of\npackaging\nmaterials<br>S. Trans face</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-Q, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Golgi apparatus – Functions of packaging materials densely stained reticular structures<br>near the nucleus – Camilo Golgi<br>Concave side of Golgi Complex – Trans face<br>Convex side of Golgi Complex – Cis face',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(47999,'biology',10,262,517,'Find out correct statement about the given diagram. A-Structure, B- discovered Scientist, C-Year.','[{"text": "A - Endoplasmic Reticulum, B - Singer and Nicolson, C - 1987", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Nucleus, B - Robert brown, C - 1898", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Nuclear membrane, B - Robert brown, C - 1831", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Golgi apparatus, B - Camillo Golgi, C - 1898", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A - Golgi apparatus, B - Camillo Golgi, C - 1898',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_47999_question_1.png'),
(48000,'biology',10,262,517,'Golgi apparatus is an important site for the formation of','[{"text": "Glycoprotein and lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycoproteins and glycolipids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glycolipids and proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glucose and glycolipids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Golgi apparatus is an important site for the formation of glycoproteins and glycolipids',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48001,'biology',10,262,517,'Golgi apparatus - identify the incorrect statement','[{"text": "Cis and the trans faces are entirely different", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Packaging materials", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Material secreted outside the cell always", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The material to be packaged comes from ER and fuses with cis face of cisternae of golgi apparatus and moves towards trans or maturing face and delievers it either to the intra-cellular targets or secreted outside the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
