(48026,'biology',10,262,516,'Rough endoplasmic reticulum is called rough because','[{"text": "Inner surface bears ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inner and outer surface bears proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outer surface bears golgi bodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outer surface bears ribosomes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RER is an extensive organelle composed of greatly convoluted but flattish sealed sacs, which are continuous with the nuclear membrane. It is called ‘rough’ endoplasmic reticulum because it is studded on its outer\nsurface (the surface in contact with the cytosol) with ribosomes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
