(48075,'biology',10,260,514,'In cell membrane, carbohydrates are oriented','[{"text": "Minimally present and can be anywhere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Towards inside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Towards outside and inside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Towards outside", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In cell membrane, carbohydrates in glycoproteins or glycolipids are oriented towards outside.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48076,'biology',10,260,514,'Which of the following are the component of plasma membrane?','[{"text": "Sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cholesterol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48077,'biology',10,260,514,'Biochemical investigation revealed that the cell membranes also possess','[{"text": "Lipids and Carbohydrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbohydrate only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein and Carbohydrate", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Biochemical investigation revealed that the cell membranes also possess Protein & Carbohydrate along with lipids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48079,'biology',10,260,514,'Phospholipids are important cell membrane constituents because these','[{"text": "Contain polar portions only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contain both polar and non-polar portions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Contain non-polar portions only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Can form bilayer in water", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A phospholipid is an amphipathic molecule. The phosphate group is negatively charged making the head polar or “Water loving” and the lipids are uncharged nonpolar and hydrophobic “Water fearing”. This combination is the characteristic of cell membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48080,'biology',10,260,514,'In human beings, the membrane of the erythrocyte contains approximately','[{"text": "52% Proteins & 40% carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "52% Proteins & 40% Lipids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "52% Lipids & 40% Proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "50% Proteins & 50% Lipids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In human beings, the membrane of the erythrocyte has approximately 52% Proteins and 40% Lipids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48081,'biology',10,260,514,'Why tails of lipids in the membrane are towards inner part?','[{"text": "This ensures that the polar tail of saturated hydrocarbons is protected from the aqueous environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "This ensures that the nonpolar tail of unsaturated hydrocarbons is protected from the aqueous environment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "This ensures that the nonpolar tail of saturated hydrocarbons is protected from the aqueous environment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "This ensures that the nonpolar head of saturated hydrocarbons is protected from the aqueous environment", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'This ensures that the nonpolar tail of saturated hydrocarbons is protected from the aqueous environment',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48082,'biology',10,260,514,'Lipids are arranged within the membrane with','[{"text": "Polar heads towards innerside and the hydrophobic tails towards outerside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both heads and tails towards outerside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polar heads towards outerside and tails towards inside", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both heads and tails towards innerside", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Polar heads towards outerside and tails towards inside',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48083,'biology',10,260,514,'Lipid bilayer is','[{"text": "Hydrophilic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrophobic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hydrophilic and Hydrophobic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Depends on the surrounding medium", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phospholipids is amphipathic molecules. This means that they have a hydrophilic, polar phosphate head and two hydrophobic fatty acid tails. These components of the phospholipids cause them to orientate themselves, so the phosphate head can interact with water and the fatty acid tails can’t, hence forming a bilayer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48084,'biology',10,260,514,'Cell membrane is absent in living -','[{"text": "Fungal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesophyll cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cell membrane is present in all living cells, without any exception.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48085,'biology',10,260,514,'Identify the most commonly used cell for studies on cell membrane ?','[{"text": "Onion cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Human erythrocytes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Platelets", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cheek cells", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Human RBCs are best study material for studies of cell membrane, which enabled scientists to deduce the possible structure of plasma membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48086,'biology',10,260,514,'The studies on the cell membrane shows','[{"text": "It is composed of lipids that are arranged in a single layer.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is composed of proteins that are arranged in a bilayer.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is composed of lipids that are arranged in a bilayer.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is composed of proteins that are arranged in a single layer.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cell membrane is mainly composed of lipids and proteins.the major lipids are phospholipids that are arranged in bilayer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
