(48100,'biology',10,258,512,'Gas vacuoles are found in','[{"text": "Blue green photosynthetic bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Purple photosynthetic bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green photosynthetic bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gas vacuoles are aggregates of hollow cylindrical structures called gas vesicles. Gas vacuoles are found in blue green, purple and green photosynthetic bacteria',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48101,'biology',10,258,512,'Reserve material in prokaryotic cells is stored in cytoplasm in the form of ________','[{"text": "Mesosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromatophores", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inclusion bodies", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Reserve material in prokaryotic cells are stored in the cytoplasm in the the form of inclusion bodies. These are not bounded by any membrane system and lie free in the cytoplasm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48102,'biology',10,258,512,'Which of the following are inclusion bodies?','[{"text": "Phosphate granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanophycean granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycogen granules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Reserve materials in prokaryotic cells are stored in cytoplasm in the form of inclusion bodies. These are bounded by membrane system and lie free in the cytoplasm. E.g., Phosphate granules, Cyanophycean granules and Glycogen granules.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48103,'biology',10,258,512,'Identify the correct statement about inclusion bodies?','[{"text": "These are not bound by any membrane system and lie free in the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "These are bound by membrane system and lie free in the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are not bound by any membrane system and lie attached to an organelle in the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are bound by membrane system and lie attached to an organelle in the cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'These are not bound by any membrane system and lie free in the cytoplasm, correct statement with regards to inclusion bodies.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48104,'biology',10,258,512,'If all the ribosomes of a cell are removed','[{"text": "Protein will not be formed", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Photosynthesis will not occur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aminoacids will not be formed", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carbohydrates will not be formed", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ribosomes are main site for protein synthesis if they are destroyed then the protein synthesis process is stoped.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48206,'biology',10,257,508,'In an animal cell, there is a dense membrane bound structure which contains chromosome.','[{"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleolus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In eukaryotic cells like animal cells a dense membrane bound structure called nucleus contains chromosomes which in turn contains genetic material, DNA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
