(48114,'biology',10,258,512,'In prokaryotes, the ribosomes are associated with which structure of the cell?','[{"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glycocalyx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In prokaryotes, ribosomes are associated with the plasma membrane of the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48115,'biology',10,258,511,'Which among the following are small bristles like fibres sprouting out of the cell?','[{"text": "Pili", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fimbriae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flagella", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fimbriae are small bristle-like fibres sprouting out of the cell. In some bacteria, they are known to help attaching to rocks in streams and also to the host tissues.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48116,'biology',10,258,511,'Absence of fimbriae will result in which of the following?','[{"text": "The bacteria will be rendered unmotile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The bacteria would not adhere to the host tissue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transporation of molecules across the membrane would stop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The bacterial cell will collapse", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fimbriae are hair-like structures present in large number in bacteria. These help in attaching bacteria to substratum or host tissues. Thus, the bacteria would not adhere to the host tissue, if the fimbrae are removed from the bacterial cell',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
