(48207,'biology',10,256,507,'Which of the following is an exception of cell theory?','[{"text": "Virus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lichen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Viruses are not applicable to cell theory. They lack protoplasm which is an essential part of a cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48127,'biology',10,258,511,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Loose sheath<br>B. Thick and tough<br>C. Cell wall<br>D. Mesosome</div><div class="column-right">P. Shape of the \ncell<br>Q. Slime layer<br>R. Capsule<br>S. Plasma\nmembrane</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P D-S", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Loose sheath- slime layer<br>Thick and tough – capsule<br>Cell wall - Shape of cell<br>Mesosome – Plasma membrane',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48128,'biology',10,258,511,'Which one is correct about mesosome?','[{"text": "Helps in photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outward folding of cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "May be in the form of vesicles, tubules or lamellae", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mesosomes do not perform photosynthesis, mesosomes are inward foldings of cell membrane. Mesosomes may be in the form of vesicles, tubules or lamellae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48129,'biology',10,258,511,'Which of the following is a form of mesosome?','[{"text": "Vesicles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lamellae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tubules", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of these',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48130,'biology',10,258,511,'What is true about mesosomes?','[{"text": "Help in cell wall formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Help in DNA replication and its distribution to daughter cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both (1) and (2)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48131,'biology',10,258,511,'Infoldings of cell membrane in prokaryotes is called','[{"text": "Mesosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lysosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inclusion bodies", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mesosomes are infoldings of cell membrane in prokaryotes. Lysosomes are not present in prokaryotes and inclusion bodies are not bound by any membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48132,'biology',10,258,511,'Presence of the following is a characteristic of some prokaryotes?','[{"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasmids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A specialised in vagination form of cell membrane called as mesosome is the characteristic of prokaryotes. Mesosomes are the infolding in the plasma membranes. Plasmids are present in prokaryotes .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48133,'biology',10,258,510,'Which of the following is not the function of cell wall?','[{"text": "Interaction with outside world", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Provide structural support and shape", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prevent from bursting and collapsing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cell wall do not perform the function of interaction with outside world, this function is performed by plasma membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48134,'biology',10,258,510,'The following statements tells us about a particular structure, identify it<br>i. It is semi-permeable in nature and interacts with the outside world.<br>ii. It is similar structurally to that of the  eukaryotes.','[{"text": "Capsule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The statement represents Cell membrane',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48135,'biology',10,258,510,'Which of the following statement is not true?','[{"text": "Response to gram stain is due to the cell envelope.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The cell envelope act as a single protective unit.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The glycocalyx layer is similar in all the bacteria.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Glycocalyx differs in composition and thickness among different bacteria.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The glycocalyx layer is similar in all the bacteria is not true.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48136,'biology',10,258,510,'Which one of the following organelle determines the shape of the bacterial cell?','[{"text": "Capsule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Slime layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cell wall determines the shape of the cell and provides a strong structural support to prevent the bacterium from bursting or collapsing.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48137,'biology',10,258,510,'Which one of the following provides a strong structural support to prevent the bacterium from bursting or collapsing?','[{"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycocalyx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell inclusions", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cell wall maintains the shape of plant cells, supports and strengthens plants, resists turgor, controls cell growth, regulates metabolic processes for the plant, acts as a physical barrier for the plant, stores carbohydrates and helps with cell to cell signalling.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48138,'biology',10,258,510,'What is internal to cell wall layer in bacteria?','[{"text": "Glycocalyx layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesosome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plasma membrane is internal to the cell wall.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48139,'biology',10,258,510,'Which among the following structures are present in both prokaryotic and eukaryotic cell?','[{"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lysosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesosome", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cellwall is present in both Prokaryotic and eukaryotic plant cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48140,'biology',10,258,510,'What is external to plasma membrane and internal to glycocalyx layer?','[{"text": "Capsule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cellular matrix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cell envelope consists of three layers – (1) outer – glycocalyx or capsule, (2) middle – cell wall, (3) innermost- plasma membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48141,'biology',10,258,510,'What is the thick, tough, layer of glycocalyx known as?','[{"text": "Slime layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Capsule", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell envelope", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The thick, tough, layer of glycocalyx is known as capsule',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48145,'biology',10,258,510,'What is the basis of classification of bacteria’s into gram +ve or gram -ve?','[{"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glycocalyx layer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell envelope", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The basis of classification of bacteria into gram +ve and gram –ve is the differences in the cell envelopes and the manner in which they respond to the staining procedure developed by gram viz. those that take up the gram stain are gram positive and those do not take up the stain are called gram negative.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48146,'biology',10,258,510,'A bacterial cell which takes up the stain and the bacteria cell which doesnot take up the stain are called','[{"text": "Gram positive and gram negative", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gram negative and gram positive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gram stain is not used to take up the stain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The staining procedure is developed by gram which says those bacteria’s cell envelope that take up the gram stain are gram positive and those do not take up the gram stain are called gram negative.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48147,'biology',10,258,510,'Bacterial cell envelope consists of','[{"text": "A tightly bound 2 layered structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A loosely bound 3 layered structure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A tightly bound 3 layered structure", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A loosely bound 2 layered structure", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A cell wall is a layer located outside the cell membrane found in plant and prokaryotic cell (Bacteria). Bacterial cell wall is composed of peptidoglycan, disacharide, Amino acids',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48148,'biology',10,258,510,'Bacterial cell envelope is composed of','[{"text": "Outermost cell wall followed by glycocalyx and plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outermost plasma membrane followed by cell wall and glycocalyx", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Outermost glycocalyx followed by cell wall and plasma membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plasma membrane and glycocalyx only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cell envelope of bacteria consists of a tightly bound three-layered structure viz., outermost glycocalyx, followed by cell wall and plasma membrane. All these layers act as \na single protective unit.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48149,'biology',10,258,510,'Most prokaryotic cells, particularly the bacterial cell, have','[{"text": "A chemically simple cell envelope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A chemically complex cell envelope", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "No cell envelope", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A physically simple cell envelope", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Most prokaryotes, particularly the bacterial cells have chemically complex but structurally simple cell envelope.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48150,'biology',10,258,509,'Select the correct answer.<br>A. Prokaryotes have something unique in the form of inclusions<br>B. Inclusions are essentially infoldings of cell membrane','[{"text": "A is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mesosomes are essentially infoldings of cell membrane. Inclusion bodies are not bound by any membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48151,'biology',10,258,509,'Select correct option (s) for prokaryotic cells<br>i. A specialised differentiated form of cell  membrane called mesosome is the characteristic<br>ii. They multiply more rapidly than the eukaryotic cells<br>iii. They are generally smaller than eukaryotic  cells','[{"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'All are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48152,'biology',10,258,509,'In which of the following, ribosomes are only 70s type','[{"text": "Prokaryotic cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Eukaryotic cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Animal cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant cell", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ribosomes are 70s type in prokaryotic cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48153,'biology',10,258,509,'Which is the common organelles that is found in both eukaryotes and prokaryote?','[{"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ribosomes are non-membrane bound organelles which are present in both eukaryotic and prokaryotic cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48154,'biology',10,258,509,'A specialised differentiated form of cell membrane in prokaryotes is','[{"text": "Inclusion bodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flagella", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasmids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A specialized differentiated form of cell membrane called mesosome is the characteristic feature of prokaryotes. These are the infoldings of cell membrane into the cell.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48155,'biology',10,258,509,'Resistance to antibiotics is conferred by','[{"text": "Plasmid DNA only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chromosome only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesosomal DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Plasmid DNA confers unique phenotypic characters to the bacteria e.g. Resistance to antibiotics.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48156,'biology',10,258,509,'Plasmids of bacterial cell possess all the following characteristics except','[{"text": "They confer unique phenotypic characters to some bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These are used in genetic engineering", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These help in the normal metabolism of the cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "These are extrachromosomal DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plasmids do not help in normal metabolism of the cell instead it gives unique phenotypic character to the cell. Genomic DNA help in normal metabolism of the cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48157,'biology',10,258,509,'Plasmids are','[{"text": "Naked genomic DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Smaller DNA than genomic DNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Enveloped DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomal DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plasmids are smaller DNA than genomic DNA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48158,'biology',10,258,509,'Where is the genetic material located in prokaryotes?','[{"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Enveloped by nuclear membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Naked in cytoplasm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Naked in Mesosome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In prokaryotes there is no well defined nucleus and genetic material is naked in cytoplasm i.e. not enveloped by a nuclear membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48159,'biology',10,258,509,'The smaller circular DNA outside the genomic DNA in bacteria is called as....................','[{"text": "Plasmid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Plastids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phasmids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleiod", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A plasmid is a small, circular, double stranded DNA molecule that is distinct from cell’s chromosomal DNA. Plasmids naturally exist in bacterial cells and they also occur in some eukaryotes. Often the genes carried in plasmids provide bacteria with genetic advantages such as antibiotic resistance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48160,'biology',10,258,509,'What is the genomic DNA of prokarytic cell?','[{"text": "Circular DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Single chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ds DNA, linear", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In prokaryotic cell genomic DNA includes the single chromosome and circular DNA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48161,'biology',10,258,509,'Which one is absent in prokaryotic cells?','[{"text": "Compartmentalisation of organelle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "80s ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Internal compartments, Nucleus and 80 S ribosomes are absent in prokaryotes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48162,'biology',10,258,509,'Mycoplasma does not possess','[{"text": "Cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nuclear membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In prokaryotic cell an organised nucleus is absent, instead a nucleoid is found. So, prokaryotic cell does not possess nuclear membrane, mycoplasma in addition doesnot possess a cellwall.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48163,'biology',10,258,509,'Which among the following is absent in prokaryotes?','[{"text": "DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mitochondria are present in the living eukaryotic cells and absent in prokaryotic cells like bacteria and blue-green algae. This organelle is known as the powerhouse of the cell as they are the site of chemical reactions that transfer energy from organic compounds in the form of ATP.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48164,'biology',10,258,509,'The smallest living cells with cell wall are','[{"text": "Virus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lichen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycoplasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mycoplasma is smallest living cell without cell wall, Bacteria is smallest cell with cell wall. Viroids are non cellular organisms.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48165,'biology',10,258,509,'The following diagram shows different types of organisms (A-D). Identify the organism in which nuclear membrane and cell organelles is present?','[{"text": "A only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C and D", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Diagram A represents typical eukaryotic cell which has nuclear membrane and cell organelles. Diagrams B, C represents bacteria and PPLO respectively which are prokaryotes and D represents viruses.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48165_question_1.png'),
(48166,'biology',10,258,509,'Which one of the following is not a eukaryote?','[{"text": "<em>Paramecium</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Nostoc</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diatoms", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<em>Nostoc</em> is a prokaryote other than that all are eukaryotes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48167,'biology',10,258,509,'Which one of the following is smallest living structure?','[{"text": "Mycoplasma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Virus", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Viruses are smallest with 0.02-0.2µm but they are between living and non living',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48168,'biology',10,258,509,'Which one of the following is a prokaryote?','[{"text": "<em>Nostoc</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Anabaena</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycoplasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<em>Nostoc</em>, <em>Anabaena</em>, Mycoplasma are bacteria which are included under Kingdom Monera which exclusively contains prokaryotes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48169,'biology',10,258,509,'Identify the different types of organism (A-D) in the given diagram?','[{"text": "A - Typical eukaryotic cell<br>B - Typical bacteria<br>C - PPLO<br>D - Viruses", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Typical eukaryotic cell<br>B - Typical bacteria<br>C - Viruses<br>D - PPLO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - PPLO<br>B - Viruses<br>C - Typical eukaryotic cell<br>D - Typical bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Viruses<br>B - Typical bacteria<br>C - PPLO<br>D - Typical eukaryotic cell", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - Typical eukaryotic cell,<br>B - Typical bacteria,<br>C - PPLO,<br>D - Viruses',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48169_question_1.png'),
(48170,'biology',10,258,509,'The following diagram shows different types of organisms (A-D). Identify the correct option w.r.t their size?','[{"text": "A - 0.02-0.2 µm, &emsp; B - 1-2 µm,<br>C - 10-20 µm, &emsp; &emsp; D - about 0.1 µm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - 1-2 µm, &emsp; B - about 0.1 µm, <br>C - 10-20µm, &emsp; &emsp; D - 0.02-0.2 µm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - 10-20 µm, &emsp; B - 1-2 µm, <br>C - about 0.1µm, &emsp; D - 0.02-0.2 µm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - 10-20 µm, &emsp; B - 0.02-0.2 µm, <br>C - about 0.1µm, &emsp; D - 1-2 µm", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A - 10-20 µm, B - 1-2 µm,<br>C - about 0.1µm, D - 0.02-0.2 µm',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48170_question_1.png'),
(48171,'biology',10,258,509,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Coccus<br>B. Vibrio<br>C. Spirillum<br>D. Bacillus</div><div class="column-right">P. Comma<br>Q. Rod like<br>R. Spherical<br>S. Spiral</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-R, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Coccus – Spherical<br>Vibrio – Comma<br>Spirillum – Spiral<br>Bacillus – Rod like',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48172,'biology',10,258,509,'What is the size of viruses?','[{"text": "0.02-0.2 mm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.02-0.2 μm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.002-0.02 μm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.2-2 μm", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The size of viruses is 0.02-0.2 μm',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48175,'biology',10,258,509,'Identify the four basic shapes of bacteria?','[{"text": "Bacillus (spherical), coccus (rod like), vibrio (comma shaped) and spirillum (spiral)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacillus (rod like), coccus (spherical), vibrio (comma shaped) and spirillum (spiral)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacillus (comma shaped), coccus (spherical), vibrio (rod like) and spirillum (spiral)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The four basic shapes of bacteria are bacillus (rod like), coccus (spherical), vibrio (comma shaped), and spirillum (spiral).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48176,'biology',10,257,508,'Identify the round and oval plant cell and amoeboid human cell respectively?','[{"text": "Mesophyll cells, RBCs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesophyll cells, WBCs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Columnar cells, Mesophyll cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mesophyll cells, Nerve cell", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mesophyll cells have round and oval shape while WBCs are amoeboid human cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48177,'biology',10,258,509,'Which of the following comprises prokaryotic cell?<br>(i) Blue-green algae,<br>(ii) Mycoplasma<br>(iii) PPLO<br>(iv) Euglenoids<br>(v) Bacteria<br>(vi) Algae<br>(vii) Cyanobacteria','[{"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v, vi, vii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, v, vii", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The prokaryotic cells are represented by bacteria, blue-green algae, mycoplasma and PPLO. All these cells contain naked DNA and lack well-defined nucleus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48178,'biology',10,257,508,'Match the columns I and II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Mycoplasma<br>B. Bacteria<br>C. Nerve cell<br>D. Human red blood cell</div><div class="column-right">P. $0.3\\mu m$<br>Q. $3\\,\\,to\\,\\,5\\mu m$<br>R. $7.0\\mu m$<br>S. Longest cells</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-S D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mycoplasma – 0.3 micro-meter<br>Bacteria – 3 to 5 micrometer<br>Nerve cell - Longest cell<br>Human red blood cell – 7.0 micro-meter.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48179,'biology',10,257,508,'Identify the long and narrow animal cells?','[{"text": "Columnar epithelial cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "WBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RBC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tracheid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Columnar epithelial cells are the long and narrow animal cells while WBCs, RBCs and tracheids have amoeboid, round-biconcave and elongated shapes respectively.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
