(48201,'biology',10,257,508,'The genetic material is not enclosed by a membrane in','[{"text": "Prokaryotic cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Eukaryotic cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unicellular organisms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The genetic material is naked in prokaryotic cells, i.e. it is not bound by any membrane. However, the genetic material in eukaryotes is well enclosed within the nucleus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
