(48229,'biology',10,256,507,'Which one of the following is basic structural and functional unit of living organisms.','[{"text": "Cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organelle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Organ", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cell is the fundamental, structural and functional unit of organisms or Cell is a unit structure and biological activity made of protoplasm surrounded by a protective and selectively permeable covering.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48230,'biology',10,256,507,'Of the following relatively levels of organisation, which one represents the smallest or lowest level?','[{"text": "Organs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Organism", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cell is the smallest structural and functional unit of an organism, which typically is microscopic and consists of cytoplasm and a nucleus enclosed in a membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48231,'biology',10,256,507,'After the discovery of living cell, Robert Brown discovered','[{"text": "Nucleolus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'After discovery of living cell by Anton Von Leeuwenhoek, Robert Brown discovered nucleus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48232,'biology',10,256,507,'Identify the correct statement.','[{"text": "All organisms are composed of cells.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some are unicellular organisms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some are multicellular organisms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of these',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48233,'biology',10,256,507,'Which of the following organisms are not composed of cells?','[{"text": "Amoeba", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "TMV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Euglena", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'TMV is a virus and viruses are acellular.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48234,'biology',10,262,519,'Function of contractile vacuole in Amoeba is','[{"text": "Digestion and respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Osmoregulation and movements", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestion and excretion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Excretion and osmoregulation", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Function of contractile vacuole in Amoeba is Excretion and osmoregulation',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48235,'biology',10,262,517,'Which of the following are NOT considered as the part of endomembrane system?<br>A. Mitochondria<br>B. Endoplasmic reticulum<br>C. Chloroplasts<br>D. Golgi complex<br>E. Peroxisomes<br>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "B and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, C and E only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, D and E only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The endomembrane system include endoplasmic reticulum (ER), golgi complex, lysosomes and vacuoles.<br>Since the functions of the mitochondria, chloroplast and peroxisomes are not coordinated with the above components, these are not considered as part of endomembrane system.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48237,'biology',10,262,517,'The RER in the cell synthesised a protein which would be later used in building the plasma membrane. But it is observed that the protein in the membrane is slightly different from the protein made in the RER. The protein was probably modified in another cell organelle Identify that organelle in the given diagram','[{"text": "A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'D- The Golgi apparatus uses cisterns to modify proteins and lipids (fats) that have been built in the endoplasmic reticulum and prepares them for export through its trans face outside of the cell or for transport to other locations in the cell. They are involved in the packaging of the material .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2009,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48237_question_1.png'),
(48238,'biology',10,259,513,'The diagram of the ultrastructure of a plant cell is given below. Identify the functions of the organelles labelled A, B, C, D, E in the diagram.','[{"text": "A - Principal director of macromolecular traffic; B - Site of oxidative phosphorylation;<br>C - Intracellular transport;<br>D - Site of photophosphorylation;<br>E - Storage of cell sap", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intracellular transport; B - Site of oxidative phosphorylation; C - Principal director of macromolecular traffic; D - Site of photophosphorylation; E - Storage of cell sap", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Storage of cell sap; B - Site of oxidative phosphorylation; C - Principal director of macromolecular traffic;<br>D - Site of photophosphorylation;<br>E - Intracellular transport", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Site of photophosphorylation;<br>B - Strorage of cell sap; C - Intracellular transport; D - Site of oxidative phosphorylation;<br>E - Principal director of macromolecular traffic", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/10_48238_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2010,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48238_question_1.png'),
(48239,'biology',10,262,516,'An interconnecting membranous network of the cell composed of vesicles, flattened sacs and tubules is:<br>','[{"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondrion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lysosome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The rough endoplasmic reticulum (RER) is typically composed of cisternae and is continuous with the outer membrane of the nuclear envelop, which also bears ribosomes on its cytosolic surface. The membranous elements of the smooth endoplasmic reticulum (SER) are highly curved, tubular and are interconnected.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48240,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following statement is correct?','[{"text": "Elaipolasts store starch whereas aleuroplasts store proteins.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acrocentric chromosomes have only one arm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The core of cilium or flagellum is the basal body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Membranous extensions into the cytoplasm in cyanobacteria which contain pigments are called chromatophores.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cyanobacteria have structures called chromatophores that are derived from the cell membrane. These contain the pigments used for photosynthesis. In green bacteria, these chromatophores are called chlorosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48241,'biology',10,259,513,'Which of the following sentences is correct?','[{"text": "Cells of all living organisms have a nucleus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both animal and plant cells have a welldefined cell wall.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In prokaryotes there are no membrane bound cell organelles.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cells are formed de novo from abiotic materials.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Prokaryotes are single celled organisms which lack membrane bound cell organelles. They do not possess well organised nucleus as present in eukaryotic organisms, rather DNA is naked, lies freely in cytoplasm, and is known as nucleoid. According to cell theory, new cells develop by division of pre-existing cells. Cell wall is outer, rigid, protective covering present in plant cells but absent in animal cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48242,'biology',10,269,527,'Identify the part labelled as \' $\\mathrm{M}$ \' in the diagram given below:<br>','[{"text": "Chromatid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Kinetochore", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centromere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Satellite", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Satellites are small fragments of chromosomes that have non-staining secondary constrictions at a constant location.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2019,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48242_question_1.png'),
(48243,'biology',10,267,525,'In the below diagram, identify the part which connects the peripheral microtubules to the central sheath.<br>','[{"text": "Plasma membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interdoublet bridge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Central microtubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radial spoke", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Radial spokes connects the peripheral microtubules to the central sheath.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2020,'kcet','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48243_question_1.png'),
(48244,'biology',10,265,523,'Proteins are synthesized in / on','[{"text": "70S ribosomes of RER", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi complex", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "80S ribosomes of RER", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'E.R. is always associated with $80 \\mathrm{~S}$ Ribosomes in eukaryotic cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48245,'biology',10,269,527,'Cellular organelles with membranes are:','[{"text": "Chromosomes, ribosomes and endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum, ribosomes and nuclei", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosomes, Golgi apparatus and mitochondria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nuclei, ribosomes and mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ribosomes are not covered by any unit membrane as they are nucleoproteins.<br>Chromosomes are not cell organelles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48246,'biology',10,269,527,'Which of the following pair lack the unit membrane?','[{"text": "Nucleus and E.R.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria and chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosome and nucleolus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Golgi body and lysosome", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cell organelles like ribosomes and nucleolus lack the unit membrane. Ribosomes are found individually in the cytoplasm and also line the membranes of the rough endoplasmic reticulum. It is composed of RNA and ribosomal protein. Nucleolus is a part of nucleus and characterized by the absence of limiting membrane, presence of chromatin and granules and fibrils of RNA and proteins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48247,'biology',10,262,519,'Tonoplasm do not contain<br>Golgi complex','[{"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Excretory products", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell organelles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Minerals", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Fluid present in the vacuole is called tonoplasm and it does not have cell organelles. Cytoplasm possess cell organelle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48249,'biology',10,264,521,'Which of the following statements are incorrect regarding leucoplasts?','[{"text": "Leucoplasts contain thylakoids and photosynthetic pigments", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Elaioplasts store lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteinoplast/Aleuroplast stores proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amyloplasts store starch", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Leucoplasts do not contain thylakoids and it is non-photosynthetic in nature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48250,'biology',10,264,522,'Protein and carbohydrate synthesizing machinery is present in','[{"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chloroplasts synthesize carbohydrate by performing photosynthesis. They also synthesize proteins due to the presence of $70 \\mathrm{~S}$ ribosomes in them.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48251,'biology',10,262,516,'The main organelle involved in modification and routing of newly synthesized proteins to their destinations is','[{"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Endoplasmic reticulum bearing ribosomes on their surface is called rough endoplasmic reticulum (RER). RER is involved in protein synthesis and are responsible for the assembly of many proteins (in a process called translation).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48252,'biology',10,268,526,'What is the angle in between two microtubular triplet in a centriole?','[{"text": "$360^{\\\\circ}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$180^{\\\\circ}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$90^{\\\\circ}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$40^{\\\\circ}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In one circle there are 9 peripheral fibres located at equal distance and same angle $\\left(360^{\\circ} / 9\\right)$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48253,'biology',10,267,525,'Long, hair like out growth responsible for cell motility are','[{"text": "Flagella", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Microtubule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cilia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fimbriae", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cilia are short whereas flagella are long microtubular proteins helpful in motility.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48254,'biology',10,266,524,'Microtubules, motor proteins, and actin filaments are all part of the','[{"text": "Mechanism of photosynthesis that occurs in chloroplasts.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rough ER in prokaryotic cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoskeleton of eukaryotic cells.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Process that moves small molecules across cell membranes.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The cytoskeleton supports the cell and allows movement of the entire cell and microtubules, motor proteins and actin filaments are part of the cytoskeleton.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48255,'biology',10,269,527,'Choose the false statement-','[{"text": "Centrosome-Cytoplasmic structure of animal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrioles form spindle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centrosome occurs in every animal cells and most of the plant cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Centriole-Membraneless, but surrounded by amorphous pericentriolar bodies", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Centrosome occurs in every animal cells and most of the plant cells. While centrosomes are common in animal cells, they are not present in most plant cells. Instead, plant cells typically have microtubule organizing centers known as the microtubule organizing center (MTOC), which function somewhat differently from centrosomes. So, statement 3 is incorrect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48256,'biology',10,269,527,'Size, count and chromosome morphology is best studied in','[{"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S phase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chromosome karyotype is best studied during metaphase as the process of spiralisation culminate resulting in short and thick chromosomes. They are clearly visible under microscope.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48257,'biology',10,269,527,'Kinetochore is','[{"text": "Centromere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein discs at primary constriction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Protein discs at secondary constriction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA at centromere", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The two protein discs to which the spindle fibres get attached are called kinetochores.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48258,'biology',10,269,527,'Nucleolus is','[{"text": "Rounded structure found in cytoplasm near nucleus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rounded structure inside nucleus and having rRNA.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rod-shaped structure in cytoplasm near the nucleus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Nucleolus is a small rounded body within a resting nucleus that contains RNA and proteins. It is usually associated with a specific chromosomal site and involved in ribosomal RNA synthesis and the formation of ribosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48259,'biology',10,262,517,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Materials to be packed to intracellular targets (or) secreted outside move from cis face to trans face of golgi complex.<br></div><div class="column-right">Materials like proteins and lipids secreted by trans face of Golgi complex are mostly synthesized in endoplasmic reticulum.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A and Statement-B are true.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is true but Statement-B is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is false but Statement-B is true.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A and Statement-B are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Proteins and lipids synthesized in endoplasmic reticulum undergo modification in golgi complex.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48260,'biology',10,262,516,'Which one of the following organelle in the figure correctly matches with its function?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Rough endoplasmic reticulum, formation of glycoproteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi apparatus, protein synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi apparatus, formation of glycolipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Rough endoplasmic reticulum, protein synthesis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Rough ER has ribosomes on its surface and performs protein synthesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48260_question_1.png'),
(48298,'biology',101,572,1151,'In context of amniocentesis, which of the following statements is incorrect?','[{"text": "It is used for prenatal sex determination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It can be used for detection of cleft lip", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is usually done when a woman is between 14-16 weeks pregnant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It can be used for detection of Down\'s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'It can be used for detection of cleft lip in context of amniocentesis it is incorrect.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48261,'biology',10,268,526,'In the diagrammatic representation of cilia/ flagella identify the parts (A-D) from the options given below:','[{"text": "A-Inner membrane, B-Peripheral microtubules, C-Central sheath, D-Central tubule, E-Inner Bridge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Plasmalemma, B-Intrinsic microtubules, C-Central Sheet, D-middle tubule, E-Inner bridge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Plasma membrane, B-Peripheral microtubules, C-Central sheath, D-Central microtubule, E-Outer doublet bridge", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Plasmamembrane, B-Peripheral microtubules, $\\\\mathrm{C}$-Central sheath, D-Central microtubule, E-Interdoublet bridge", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In the diagrammatic representation of cilia/ flagella (A-D) indicates following parts A-Plasma membrane, B-Peripheral microtubules, C-Central sheath, D-Central microtubule, E- Interdoublet bridge',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48261_question_1.png'),
(48262,'biology',10,261,515,'Which layer of cell wall is obligatory in its presence in the loosely arranged cells of a tissue?','[{"text": "Middle lamella", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary cell wall", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Secondary cell wall", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Middle lamella is absent as cells are loosely bound. Secondary wall is present only in old and mature mechanical tissues.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48263,'biology',10,260,514,'Which component of plasma membrane increase the fluidity?','[{"text": "Phospholipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cholesterol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carbohydrates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proteins", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cholesterol extend in between the bilayer and increase the fluidity of the plasma membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48264,'biology',10,262,518,'Nucleases are present in','[{"text": "Lysosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Peroxisomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glyoxysomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Nucleases are hydrolyzing enzymes in lysosomes that digest nucleic acids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48265,'biology',10,262,518,'What would happen if lysosomes get ruptured in a cell?','[{"text": "Cell dies", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cell shrinks", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cell swell up", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nothing would happen", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lysosomes are membrane-enclosed organelles and consist of hydrolytic enzymes which capable of breaking down all types of biological polymers (like proteins, nucleic acids, carbohydrates, and lipids). If lysosomes get ruptured in a cell, the cell dies due to release of hydrolytic enzymes which destroys the cells',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48266,'biology',10,262,516,'Extra luminal space refers to','[{"text": "Space inside endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Space inside chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cytoplasm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Space inside nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Endoplasmic reticulum has highly folded membrane system the divides the cell into luminal space (in the E.R) and extra luminal space (outside the E.R).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48267,'biology',10,263,520,'What is untrue regarding mitochondria?','[{"text": "Easily visible", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Visible only after staining (Janus green)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Number is variable in different cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sausage (or) cylindrical in shape", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Staining is needed for mitochondria and golgi complex.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48268,'biology',10,263,520,'ATP synthesis coupled to breakdown of water take place in','[{"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peroxisome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Photophosphorylation coupled with photolysis of water occur in chloroplast whereas oxidative phosphorylation coupled with formation of water take place in mitochondria.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48269,'biology',10,263,520,'All the statements are true except','[{"text": "Mitochondria are called as the power plants or power houses of the cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondrial DNA is called mt DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria is the site of oxidative phosphorylation and krebs cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria is the site of calvin cycle", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mitochondria is the site of aerobic respiration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48270,'biology',10,268,526,'What is the ratio of microtubules in centrioles and flagella?','[{"text": "$27: 18$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$20: 27$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1: 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$20: 9$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Peripheral fibres are triplets in centriole $(9 \\times 3)$ and are doublets in flagella $(9 \\times 2)$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48271,'biology',10,262,519,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In <i>Amoeba</i> the contractile vacuole is important for osmoregulation and excretion.<br></div><div class="column-right">In many cells, as in protists, contractile vacuoles are formed by engulfing the food particles.<br></div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement A is correct only, In Amoeba the contractile vacuole is important for osmoregulation and excretion. In many cells, as in protists, food vacuoles are formed by engulfing the food particles.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48272,'biology',10,269,527,'All chromosomes have two arms except','[{"text": "Metacentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acrocentric", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telocentric", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Submetacentric", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In telocentric chromosome centromere is present at one end. Hence there is only one arm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48273,'biology',10,270,528,'Microbody related to photorespiration is','[{"text": "Mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Peroxisome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Peroxisomes is a place where actual oxidation of photorespiratory substrate namely glycolic acid take place. Hence it is a photorespiratory cell organelle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48274,'biology',10,269,527,'Two unequal arms are present in','[{"text": "Metacentric and submetacentric chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Submetacentric and acrocentric chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Acrocentric and metacentric chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Telocentric and metacentric chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In metacentric chromosome the two arms are equal whereas in telocentric there is one arm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48275,'biology',10,269,527,'Satellite means','[{"text": "terminal part of the chromosome beyond secondary constriction.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "terminal part of the chromosome beyond primary constriction.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "terminal part of chromosome beyond tertiary constriction.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "none of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Satellite is a small chromosomal segment separated from the main body of the chromosome by a secondary constriction. In humans it is usually associated with the short arm of an acrocentric chromosome. They play a vital role in the formation of the nucleolus after cell division. In humans, chromosomes number 13, 14, 15, 21 and 22 are examples of SAT (satellite) chromosomes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48276,'biology',10,263,520,'The below diagram represents','[{"text": "A flagellum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A centriole", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A cristae with oxysomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Virion with spikes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The infoldings called cristae increase the surface area (like intestine in human body and grana in chloroplast) to accommodate more number of oxysomes $\\left(10^{5}\\right)$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/10_48276_question_1.png'),
(48277,'biology',10,262,519,'Which of the following statement is correct with reference to vacuoles?','[{"text": "It is membrane bound and contains storage proteins and lipids.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is membrane bound and contains water and excretory substances.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It lacks membrane and contains air.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It lacks membrane and contains water and excretory substances", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The vacuole is the membrane bound space found in the cytoplasm. It contains water, sap, excretory.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48278,'biology',10,269,527,'Match Column I with Column II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Nucleolus<br>B. Centriole <br>C. Leucoplasts<br>D. Golgi apparatus</div><div class="column-right">P. Site of formation of glycolipid<br>Q. Organization like the cartwheel<br>R. Site for active ribosomal RNA synthesis<br>S. For storing nutrients</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  R, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  Q, B  -  R, C  -  P, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R, B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q, C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S, D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P}}$ is the correct option.<br>• Nucleolus is a site for active ribosomal RNA synthesis<br>• Both the centrioles in a centrosome lie perpendicular to each other in which each has an organisation like the cartwheel.<br>• Leucoplasts are the colourless plastids of varied shapes and sizes with stored nutrients.<br>• Golgi apparatus is the important site for formation of glycoproteins and glycolipids.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48279,'biology',10,264,522,'The DNA present in chloroplast is:','[{"text": "Linear, double stranded", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Circular, double stranded", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Linear, single stranded", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Circular, single stranded", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The DNA present in chloroplast is circular double stranded.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48280,'biology',10,269,527,'Match Column I with Column II :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Axoneme<br>B. Cartwheel pattern<br>C. Crista<br>D. Satellite</div><div class="column-right">P. Centriole<br>Q. Cilia and flagella<br>R. Chromosome<br>S. Mitochondria</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  S, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  Q, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{ A  -  Q, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q, B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P, C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S, D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R}}$<br>is the correct option.<br>• Axoneme is seen in cilia and flagella<br>• Centriole shows cartwheel appearance<br>• Crista is found in mitochondria<br>• Satellite is present in chromosomes',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48281,'biology',10,263,520,'Given below are two statements:<br>Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Mitochondria and chloroplasts both are double membrane bound organelles.</div><div class="column-right">Inner membrane of mitochondrian is relatively less permeable, as compared to chloroplast.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both mitochondria and chloroplasts are double membrane bound cell organelles.Transport of ions occurs across the inner membrane of mitochondria. The inner membrane of chloroplast is impermeable to ions and metabolites. Therefore, it is said that inner membrane of mitochondria is relatively more permeable to that of chloroplast.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48282,'biology',101,572,1151,'Reproductive health is related to','[{"text": "Physical fitness", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Emotional compatibility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Behavioral inter-relationships", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the above. Reproductive health corresponds to physical fitness, emotional compatibility and behavioral relationships between the partners.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48283,'biology',101,572,1151,'What are the programmes called to get total reproductive health as a social goal of national level?','[{"text": "Family care", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family organization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reproductive care", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Family planning", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Family planning is the practice of controlling the number of children in a family and the intervals between their births.<br>O Contemporary notions of family planning, however, tend to place a woman and her childbearing decisions at the center of the discussion, as notions of women\'s empowerment and reproductive autonomy have gained traction in many parts of the world.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
