(48425,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which of the following STDs are not completely curable?','[{"text": "Chlamydiasis, gonorrhoea, trichomoniasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chancroid, syphilis, genital warts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS, syphilis, hepatitis B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS, genital herpes, hepatitis B", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'AIDS, genital herpes, hepatitis B',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48426,'biology',101,576,1155,'To avoid transmission of STDs we should<br>(i) Avoid sex with multiple partners<br>(ii) Use condoms during coitus<br>(iii) Avoid sex with unknown partners<br>(iv) Avoid sharing of needles','[{"text": "(i), (ii), (iii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i), (iii),", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i), (ii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them. To avoid transmission of STDs, we should<br>(i) Avoid sex with multiple partners<br>(ii) Use condoms during coitus<br>(iii) Avoid sex with unknown partners<br>(iv) Avoid sharing of needles',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48427,'biology',101,576,1155,'To prevent STDs which of the following is not useful?','[{"text": "Avoid sex with unknown partner", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Use of condoms during coitus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Use of oral pills", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Avoid sex with multiple partners", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Use of oral pills to prevent STDs is not useful',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48428,'biology',101,576,1155,'The complication of the STDs includes.<br>a. PID.<br>b. Abortionsc.<br>c. Still birthd.<br>d. Ectopic pregnanciese.<br>e. Infertility<br>f. Cancer of reproductive tract','[{"text": "a, c and d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b, d and e", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b, c, d, e and f", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them. The complication of the STDs includes<br>a. PID<br>b. Abortions<br>c. Still birth<br>d. Ectopic pregnancies<br>e. Infertility<br>f. Cancer of reproductive tract',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48429,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which one of the following groups includes only sexually transmitted diseases?','[{"text": "Gonorrhoea, hepatitis- B chlamydiasis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hepatitis-B, haemophilia, AIDS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "HIV, malaria, trichomoniasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS, syphilis, cholera", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gonorrhoea, hepatitis- B chlamydiasis',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48430,'biology',101,576,1155,'AIDS was reported for the first time in','[{"text": "India", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nigeria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ghana", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "USA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'AIDS (acquired immune deficiency syndrome) a syndrome first identified in Los Angeles (USA) in 1981. It is caused by the human immuno deficiency virus (HIV). The virus destroys a subgroup of lymphocytes, the helper T-cells (or $C D_{4}$ lymphocytes), resulting in suppression of the body\'s immune response.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48431,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which of the following is not correctly matched<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Genital warts- Viral disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlamydiasis- Protozoan disease", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Candidiasis- fungal disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Syphilis- bacterial disease", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chlamydiasis- Protozoan disease',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48432,'biology',101,576,1155,'HIV attacks','[{"text": "RBCs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blood platelets", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helper T cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The helper T cells of immune system are attacked by HIV.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48433,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which one of these STDs does not specifically affect the sex organs?','[{"text": "AIDS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gonnorhoea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Syphilis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genital warts", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'AIDS can affect any organ of the body and not specifically the sex organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48434,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which one of the following statements is correct regarding Sexually Transmitted Diseases (STD)','[{"text": "The chances of a 5 year boy contacting a STD are very little", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A person may contact syphilis by sharing milk with one already suffering from the disease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heamophilia is one of the STD", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genital herpes and sickle - cell anaemia are both STD", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The chances of a 5 year boy contacting a STD are very little',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48435,'biology',101,576,1155,'Given is a diagram of FRS with a medical condition. Identify.','[{"text": "Ectopic pregnancy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tubal blockage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Normal pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fallopian tube anomaly", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ectopic pregnancy',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/101_48435_question_1.png'),
(48436,'biology',101,576,1155,'Match the following and choose the correct option<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Hepatitis<br>B. Ectopic pregnancy<br>C. PID<br>D. World Health day<br>E. ELISA  technique<br></div><div class="column-right">P. Infection of  reproductive system<br>Q. 7\' April, 1984<br>R. Fallopian tubes implantation<br>S. Detection of antibody/organisation antigen<br>T. Hepatitis B virus</div></div>','[{"text": "A-T, B-Q, C-P, D-R, E-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-T, B-R, C-P, D-Q, E-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-T, B-Q, C-S, D-R, E-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-T, B-R, C-S, D-Q, E-P", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-T, B-R, C-P, D-Q, E-S',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48437,'biology',101,577,1156,'Infertility is the relative state of failure to conceive after how many year/years of sexual life without contraception?','[{"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Infertility is the relative state of failure to conceive after 2 years of sexual life without contraception',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48438,'biology',101,577,1156,'What is the popular name of IVF','[{"text": "GIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tubectomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Test tube baby", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amniocentesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Test tube only - This method involves in vitro fertilization (IVF) i.e., fertilization of male gamete (Spermatozoan) and female gamete (ovum) outside the body in almost similar conditions as that in the body followed by zygote or embryo transfer (ET).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48439,'biology',101,577,1156,'The technique called GIFT is recommended for those females','[{"text": "Who may not be ovulating eggs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Who do not have proper female reproductive system", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Whose cervical canal is too small", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Who cannot provide suitable environment for fertilization.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The technique called GIFT is recommended for those females who may not be ovulating eggs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48440,'biology',101,577,1156,'What is ZIFT?','[{"text": "Embryo transfer into the uterus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote transfer into fallopian tube", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mixture of sperms and ova into fallopian tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mixture of sperms and ova into uterus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'ZIFT refers to zygote intrafallopian transfer.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48441,'biology',101,577,1156,'In-vitro fertilization is a technique that involves transfer of which one of the following into the fallopian tube','[{"text": "Embryo of 32 cell stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo only, upto 8 cell stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Either zygote or early embryo upto 8 cell stage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zygote only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The baby produced by conceiving in a culture dish and nursing in the uterus is called a test tube baby. This method involves in vitro fertilization (IVF). Fertilization of male and female gamete outside the body followed by embryo transfer (ET). Either zygote or early embryo upto 8 blastomeres is transferred into the fallopian tube to complete its future',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48444,'biology',101,577,1156,'Which one of the following cannot be considered as Assisted Reproductive Technology?','[{"text": "Zygote Intra fallopian tube transfer (ZIFT)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gamete Intra Fallopian Transfer (GIFT)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Medical Termination of Pregnancy (MTP)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intra Cytoplasmic Sperm Injection (ICSI)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Medical Termination of Pregnancy (MTP)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48445,'biology',101,577,1156,'Match the column-I with column-II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Transfer of ovum collected from a donar<br>B. Semen  introduced into vagina directly<br>C. Embryo with 8 blastomeres<br>D. Sperm is directly injected  into ovum</div><div class="column-right">P. Gametes fallopian transfer<br>Q. Intrauterine transfer<br>R. Artificial inseminatior<br>S. Intra cytoplasmic sperm iniection</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{S}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48446,'biology',101,577,1156,'Embryo with more than 16 blastomeres formed due to in vitro fertilization is transferred into','[{"text": "Cervix", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uterus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fallopian tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fimbriae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'16 blastomeres stage of Embryo formed due to in vitro fertilization is transferred into the uterus of the recipient female.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48447,'biology',101,577,1156,'Test tube baby can be described scientifically as','[{"text": "IVF followed by GIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ET followed by ZIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IVF followed by ET", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ET followed by IVF", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IVF followed by ET',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48448,'biology',101,577,1156,'In which Assisted Reproductive Technologies (ART), the gametes are to be introduced into female genital tract before fertilization.','[{"text": "IVF & ZIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GIFT & ICSI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ICSI & AI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GIFT & AI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'GIFT and AI Assisted Reproductive Technologies (ART), the gametes are to be introduced into female genital tract before fertilization.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48449,'biology',101,577,1156,'The ART method used to rectify male infertility involving invitro fertilization is','[{"text": "IUI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ICSI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The ART method used to rectify male infertility involving invitro fertilization is ICSI - intra cytoplasmic sperm insemination',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48450,'biology',101,577,1156,'In which ART technique the semen is artificially introduced into the female','[{"text": "GIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IUT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ET", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'IUI stands for intra uterine insemination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(48451,'biology',101,577,1156,'The ART method used to rectify male infertility involves invivo fertilization is','[{"text": "ICSI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IVF", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ZIFT", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The ART method used to rectify male infertility involves in vivo fertilization is AI.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48452,'biology',101,572,1151,'Primary steps that can be taken towards attaining reproductive health are<br>i. Counselling and creating awareness among people about reproductive organs, adolescence and associated changes.<br>ii. Safe and hygienic sexual practices<br>iii. Creating awareness about STDs including AIDS etc<br>iv. Ban on MTP and amniocentesis','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{i}$ and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{ii}$ and $\\\\mathrm{iii}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Primary steps taken towards attaining reproductive health are counselling and creating awareness among people about reproductive organs, adolescence and associated changes, safe and hygenic sexual practices creating awareness about STDs including AIDS etc.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48453,'biology',101,572,1151,'Choose the correct statement<br>I. According to the $\\mathrm{WHO}$, reproductive health is total well being in the physical, social, emotional and behavioural aspects of reproduction.<br>II. According to the $\\mathrm{WHO}$, reproductive health is total well being in the physical, social and emotional aspects of reproduction.<br>III. A reproductively healthy society has people with physically and functionally normal reproductive organs.<br>IV. A reproductively healthy societies have abnormal sex-related emotional and behavioural interactions.','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'According to WHO, reproductive health is total well being in the physical, social, emotional and behavioral aspects of reproduction and reproductively healthy society has people with physically and functionally normal reproductive organs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48454,'biology',101,572,1151,'Medical assistance and care to people is required in reproduction related problems like<br>${\\rm{i}}{\\rm{. Pregnancy}}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ii}}{\\rm{. Delivery}}$<br>${\\rm{iii}}{\\rm{. STDs}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{iv}}{\\rm{. Abortions}}$<br>v. Contraception<br>vi. Menstrual problems<br>vii. Infertility','[{"text": "i, iii, v and vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv and vii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v and vii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v, vi and vii", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All options are related.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48455,'biology',101,574,1153,'Action of contraceptive is','[{"text": "Prevent the ovulation only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prevention of ovulation and fertilization only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prevention of ovulation, fertilization and implantation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prevent the rapid passing of eggs in oviduct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Action of contraceptive is Prevention of ovulation, fertilization and implantation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48456,'biology',101,574,1153,'Diaphragms are contraceptive devices used by the females. Choose the correct option from the statements given below:<br>i. They are introduced into the uterus<br>ii. They are placed to cover the cervical region<br>iii. They act as physical barriers for sperm entry.<br>iv. They act as spermicidal agents','[{"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct options are<br>ii. They are placed to cover the cervical region<br>iii. They act as physical barriers',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48457,'biology',101,574,1153,'Choose the right one among the statements given below','[{"text": "IUDs increase phagocytosis reactions in the uterus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IUDs are generally inserted by the user herself", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUDs suppress gametogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUDs once inserted need not to be replaced.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'IUDs increase phagocytosis reactions in the uterus is correct answer.<br>O In every second woman with the desire of pregnancy and with normal female genital tract and function positive spermatozoa recovery rates in the peritoneal fluid at mid cycle can be expected.<br>O Inspite of positive post coital cervical sperm migration tests, no spermatozoa seems to be detected in the peritoneal fluid in women with IUD.<br>O The endometrial leukocytosis with increased phagocytosis of spermatozoa seems to be an important factor in the IUDs multifactorial mode of action.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48458,'biology',101,574,1153,'Administration of which of the following within 72 hours of coitus have been found to be effective as emergency contraceptives?<br>i. Progestogen<br>ii. Progestogen-estrogen combinations<br>iii. Intrauterine devices<br>iv. Diaphragms or cervical caps','[{"text": "i and ii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, and iii", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Administration of progestogens or progestogen-estrogencombinations or IUDs within 72 hours of coitus have been found to bevery effective as emergency contraceptives as they could be used to avoid possible pregnancy due to rape or casual unprotected intercourse. Diaphragms and cervical caps are barriers which can only block the entry of sperms through the cervix during coitus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48459,'biology',101,574,1153,'Refer to the given figure of human female reproductive system where $\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{R}$ and $\\mathrm{S}$ are the locations that are affected by different birth control measures.<br>Which of the following is incorrect regarding this?','[{"text": "Birth control measures effective at $\\\\mathrm{S}$ prevents fertilisation by blocking the entry of sperms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Birth control measures effective at $\\\\mathrm{Q}$ could be a diaphragm or a vault cap.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Birth control measures effective at $\\\\mathrm{P}$ inhibits ovulation and implantation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Birth control measures effective at $\\\\mathrm{R}$ is surgical and reversibility is very poor.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Birth control measures effective at $\\mathrm{Q}$ could be a diaphragm or a vault cap.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/101_48459_question_1.png'),
(48460,'biology',101,574,1153,'Fill in the blanks<br>Oral contraceptive pills have to be taken daily for a period of____A____ starting preferably within the first ____B____of menstrual cycle. After a gap of____C____ days (during which menstruation occurs) it has to be repeated in the same pattern till the female desires to prevent contraception.','[{"text": "A - 21 days; B - 5 days; C - 7 days", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - 28 days; B - 7 days; C - 5 days", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - 28 days; B - 5 days; C - 7 days", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - 22 days; B - 7 days; C - 5 days", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - 21 days; $\\mathrm{B}$ - 5 days; $\\mathrm{C}-7$ days',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48461,'biology',101,576,1155,'Identify the true statements from the below statements-<br>I. There are many side effects of tubectomy and vasectomy.<br>II. Purpose of tubectomy is to prevent egg formation.<br>III. The most important component of the oral contraceptive pills is progesterone.<br>IV. Contraceptive oral pills help in birth control by preventing ovulation.<br>V. Genital warts is a sexually transmitted disease caused by herpes virus.<br>VI. In India, there is rapid decline in infant mortality rate and MMR.','[{"text": "I, II and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV and VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V and VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I. There are many side effects of tubectomy and vasectomy. This can be corrected as, there are less side effects of tubectomy and vasectomy.<br>II.Purpose of tubectomy is to prevent egg formation, this can be corrected as, purpose of tubectomy is to prevent egg fertilisation.<br>V. Genital warts is a sexually transmitted disease caused by herpes virus, this can be corrected as, genital warts is a sexually transmitted disease caused by HPV.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48462,'biology',101,575,1154,'Which of the following is true? Consider the statements given below regarding contraception','[{"text": "Medical termination of pregnancy (MTP) during first trimester is generally safe", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Generally chances of contraception are nil until mother breast feeds the infants upto two years.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intra uterine devices like copper-T are non effective contraceptives", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contraceptive pills may be taken upto one week after coitus to prevents contraception", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Medical termination of pregnancy (MTP) during first trimester is generally safe.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48463,'biology',101,575,1154,'Nearly ___ A__ million MTPs performed in a year all over the world which accounts to___ B___ of the total number of conceived pregnancies in a year.','[{"text": "A - 40 to 50 ,B - ${\\\\rm{1/}}{{\\\\rm{4}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - 45 to 50 ,B - ${\\\\rm{1/}}{{\\\\rm{4}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - 45 to 50 ,${\\\\rm{B}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - 1/}}{{\\\\rm{5}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - 40 to 50 ,${\\\\rm{B}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ - 1/}}{{\\\\rm{5}}^{{\\\\rm{th}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A - 45 to 50, B - ${\\rm{1/}}{{\\rm{5}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48481,'biology',101,575,1154,'Following statements are given regarding MTP. Choose the correct options given below:<br>I. MTPs are also essential in certain cases where continuation of the pregnancy could be harmful or even fatal either to the mother or to the foetus or both<br>II. MTPs are always safe<br>III. MTPs are always surgical<br>IV. Government of India legalised MTP in 1971','[{"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both these statements are correct.<br>I. MTPs are also essential in certain cases where continuation of the pregnancy could be harmful or even fatal either to the mother or to the foetus or both<br>IV. Government of India legalised MTP in 1971',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48464,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which of the following is incorrect regarding STDs?','[{"text": "STDs are reported to be very high among persons in the age group of 15-24 years.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Females infected with STDS may often be asymptomatic and hence remain undetected for long.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "STDs can lead to complications like pelvic inflammatory diseases and ectopic pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Patients with STDs should report to quacks for early detection of disease.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Patients with STD\'s should report to registered medical practitioners instead of quacks for early detection of disease. Early diagnosis of diseases can help in treatment of the disease and prevent complications like pelvic inflammatory disease, ectopic pregnancy, still birth, abortions and infertility.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48465,'biology',101,577,1156,'Match the ARTs with their description-<br>i. Collected gametes are made to form the zygote in the laboratory.<br>ii. Zygote or early embryo with upto 8 blastomeres is transferred into the oviduct.<br>iii. Zygote with more than 8 blastomeres is transferred into the uterus.<br>iv. Fusion of gametes within the female.<br>v. Transfer of ovum from a donor to the oviduct of the recipient.<br>vi. Sperm is injected into the ovum in-vitro<br>\\[{\\rm{A}}{\\rm{.}}\\;{\\rm{GIFT}}\\;\\;{\\rm{B}}{\\rm{.}}\\;{\\rm{ZIFT}}\\;\\;{\\rm{C}}{\\rm{.}}\\;{\\rm{AI}}\\]<br>\\[{\\rm{D}}{\\rm{.}}\\;{\\rm{ICSI}}\\;\\;\\;{\\rm{E}}{\\rm{.}}\\;{\\rm{IUT}}\\;\\;\\;\\;{\\rm{F}}{\\rm{.}}\\;{\\rm{IVF}}\\]<br>\\[{\\rm{G}}{\\rm{.}}\\;{\\rm{IUI}}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;{\\rm{H}}{\\rm{.}}\\;{\\rm{In - vivo}}\\;{\\rm{fertilisation}}\\]<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "i-F, ii- B, iii-A, iv- H, v-A, vi - G", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i-G, ii - B, iii - F, iv- H, v-A, vi - D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i-G, ii - B, iii- F, iv- H, v - C, vi - E", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i - F, ii - B, iii- E, iv- H, v-A, vi - D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'i - F, ii - B, iii - E, iv - H, v - A, vi - D',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48466,'biology',101,577,1156,'The main difference between GIFT and ZIFT is that','[{"text": "In ZIFT, fertilization takes place in vivo", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GIFT involves in vitro fertilization followed by embryo transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ZIFT involves intrauterine insemination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In GIFT, fertilization takes place in vivo", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In GIFT ovum is introduced into Fallopian tube where fertilization takes (in vivo). In ZIFT fertilization is done in vitro and the zygotes/ early embryos are introducedinto Fallopian tube or uterus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48467,'biology',101,574,1153,'How many of the following are emergency contraceptives, if used with in 72 hours of coitus.<br>Condoms, Implants, IUDS, Progestogen - estrogen combination, Lactational amenorrhoea','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Emergency contraceptive pill ( contains progesterone - oestrogen combination) that can be used up to 3 days (72 hours) after unprotected sex. IUD\'s can also be used as emergency contraceptives. ',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48468,'biology',101,577,1156,'In vitro fertilization is a technique that involves transfer of which one of the following into the fallopion tube','[{"text": "Embryo only, upto 8 celled stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo which is 32 celled stage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Either zygote or early embryo upto 8 celled stage", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Either zygote or early embryo upto 8 celled stage.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48469,'biology',101,574,1153,'Choose the correct option with respect to contraceptives<br>i. Breast cancer is a possible ill effect of using contraceptives<br>ii. Some give an additional benefit of protecting the user from contracting STDs<br>iii. Diaphragms are reusable<br>iv. Multiload 375 suppresses sperm motility and fertilizing capacity of sperms<br>v. Progestasert increases cervical mucus secretion','[{"text": "i, ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'i. Breast cancer is a possible ill effect of using contraceptives<br>ii. Some give an additional benefit of protecting the user from contracting STDs<br>iii. Diaphragms are reusable<br>iv. Multiload 375 suppresses sperm motility and fertilizing capacity of sperms<br>v. Progestasert increases cervical mucus secretion',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48470,'biology',101,572,1151,'Which of the following step is necessary for building up a healthy reproductive society?','[{"text": "Introduction of sex education in schools", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proper information about reproductive organs, adolescent and safe sexual practices.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To create awareness among people about reproduction related aspects", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Introduction of sex education in schools, proper information about reproductive or ans, adolescent and safe sexual practices, creating awareness among the people about reproduction related aspects etc are necessary for building up a healthy reproductive society.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48471,'biology',101,573,1152,'Which one of the following is indicative of improved reproductive health of the society?<br>i. Better awareness about sex related matters<br>ii. Increased number of medically assisted deliveries<br>iii. Better post-natal care<br>iv. Increased maternal and infant mortality rates<br>v. Decreased number of couples with small families<br>vi. Better detection and cure of STDs<br>vii. Overall increased medical facilities for all sex related problems','[{"text": "i, iii, iv and vii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, v and vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iv, v and vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, vi and vii", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All options are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48472,'biology',101,572,1151,'Reproductive health in society can be improved by <br>i. Introduction of sex education in schools<br>ii. Increased medical assistance<br>iii. Awareness about contraception and STDs<br>iv. Equal opportunities to male and female child<br>v. Ban on amniocentesis<br>vi. Encouraging myths and misconception','[{"text": "i, ii, iv and vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv and v", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Reproductive health in a society can be improved by introduction of sex education in schools, increased medical assistance, creating awareness about contraceptive and STD\'s, equal opportunities to male and female child and ban on aminocentesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48811,'biology',80,477,964,'Which factor affects the temperature optimum for photosynthesis in plants?','[{"text": "The water availability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The habitat they are adapted to", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Light intensity and duration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The temperature optimum for photosynthesis of different plants also depends on the habitat that they are adapted to.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
