(48474,'biology',101,574,1153,'What is true for "Lactational amenorrhoea"?<br>i. It means absence of menstruation<br>ii. Ovulation does not occur during the lactational period<br>iii. Chances of failure of contraception are almost nil upto six months following parturition<br>iv. Side effects are almost nil<br>v. Contraceptive efficiency reduces after the period of intense lactation<br>vi. It is a natural method of contraception<br>vii. It increases phagocytosis of sperms','[{"text": "All except vii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'True for lactation<br>i. It means absence of menstruation<br> ii. Ovulation does not occur during the lactational period<br>iii. Chances of failure of contraception are almost nil upto six months following parturition<br>iv. Side effects are almost nil<br>v. Contraceptive efficiency reduces after the period of intense lactation<br>vi. It is a natural method contraception',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48475,'biology',101,574,1153,'What is the reason for popularity of barrier method of family planning?','[{"text": "The absence of side effect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Comparatively more reliable", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protection from sexually transmitted diseases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both 1 and 3. The absence of side effect. Protection from sexually transmitted diseases.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48476,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following is an incorrect match w.r.t. the category of a contraceptive method, its type and the mode of its action?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Category }}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{: Sterilization}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Type}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Vasectomy}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Mode}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{action}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Prevents}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{gamete}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{transport}}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Category}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Intrauterine}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{device}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Type}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Lippes}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{loop}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Mode}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{action}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Inhibits}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ovulation}}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Category }}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{: Barrier}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{method}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Type}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Condoms}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Mode}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{action}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Prevent}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{meeting}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ovum}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{sperms}}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Category}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Pills}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Type}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Mala - D}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{Mode}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{action}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{:Inhibits}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ovulation}}\\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'IUD sincrease phagocytosis of sperms within the uterus and the $\\mathrm{Cu}$ ions released suppress sperm motility and the fertilising capacity of sperms. The hormone releasing IUDs, in addition, make the uterus unsuitable for implantation and the cervix hostile to the sperms.IUDs do not inhibit ovulation. Therefore (2) is incorrect match. (1), (3) and (4) are all correct',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48477,'biology',101,574,1153,'Read the following statements and find out the incorrect statement<br>I. Barrier methods are available for both males and females<br>II. In barrier methods, ovum and sperms are prevented from physically meeting with the help of barriers.<br>III. Condoms are made of thin rubber/ latex sheath that are used to cover the penis in male or vagina and cervix in the female, just before coitus so that the ejaculated semen would not enter into the female reproductive tract.<br>IV. Diaphragm, cervical caps and vaults are barriers made of rubber that are inserted into the female reproductive tract to cover cervix during coitus. These barriers are disposable.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'iv. Diaphragm, cervical caps and vaults are barriers made of rubber that are inserted into the female reproductive tract to cover cervix during coitus. These barriers are disposable.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48478,'biology',101,574,1153,'Lippe\'s loop prevents pregnancy because','[{"text": "It increases the phagocytosis of the sperm within the uterus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It increases thickness of cervical mucus and retards the entry of sperm into the uterus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It prevents ovulation by inhibiting the secretion of $\\\\mathrm{LH}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It suppresses the motility and fertilizing capacity of the sperm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lippes loop is a non-medicated IUD. IUDs increase phagocytosis of spermswithin the uterus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48479,'biology',101,574,1153,'What is true about "Saheli"?<br>i. Developed at the CDRI, Lucknow<br>ii. Contains a steroidal preparation<br>iii. "Once-a-week" pill<br>iv. Many sides effects<br>v. High contraceptrive value<br>vi. Very few side effects<br>vii. Low contraceptive value','[{"text": "i, iii, v, vi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, v, vi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i, iii, v, vi<br>i. Developed at the CDRI, Lucknow<br>iii. "Once-a-week" pill<br>v. High Contraceptrive value<br>vi. Very few side effects',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48480,'biology',101,574,1153,'What is true for surgical methods?<br>i. Also called sterilisation<br>ii. Terminal method of contraception<br>iii. Block gamete transport<br>iv. Called vasectomy in females and tubectomy in males<br>v. High reversibility and contraceptive efficiency<br>vi. High contraceptive efficiency','[{"text": "i, ii, iii, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, vi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii, iv, vi", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'i. Also called sterilisation<br>ii. Terminal method of contraception<br>iii. Block gamete transport<br>vi. High contraceptive efficiency',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
