(48493,'biology',101,574,1153,'Condoms are one of the most popular contraceptives because of the following reasons:','[{"text": "These are effective barriers for insemination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They do not interfere with coital act", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "These help in reducing the risk of STDs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of them. Condoms are one of the most popular contraceptives because of the following reasons:<br>i. These are effective barriers for insemination<br>ii.They do not interfere with coital act<br>iii. These help in reducing the risk of STDs',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48494,'biology',101,574,1153,'Choose the right one among the statements given below:','[{"text": "IUDs are generally inserted by the user herself", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUDs increase phagocytosis reaction in the uterus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IUDs suppress gametogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUDs once inserted need not be replaced", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A qualified medical professional is needed to insert IUD. IUD has no effect on gametogenesis because ovulation takes place in the ovary while IUD is placed at the junction of fallopian tubes and uterus. IUDs can be easily taken out. So, option \' 2 \' is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48495,'biology',101,574,1153,'The correct surgical procedure as a contraceptive method is:','[{"text": "Ovariectomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hysterectomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasectomy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Castration", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Vasectomy is tying of the vasa deferens so that sperms are prevented from entering into the urethra. Ovariectomy is removal of ovary which is carried out in case of ovarian cyst or cancer. Hysterectomy is removal or uterus which is carried out in case of uterine cancer or risk of uterine cancer. Castration is done in males (usually in animals).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48496,'biology',101,575,1154,'Following statements are given regarding MTP. Choose the correct options given below:<br>I. MTPs are generally advised during first trimester<br>II. MTPs are used as a contraceptive method<br>III. MTPs are always surgical<br>IV. MTPs require the assistance of qualified medical personnel','[{"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'MTP is carried out after conception and hence it cannot be a contraceptive method. MTP involves curettage of foetus by inserting a suitable tool in the uterus and this does not involve surgery. Hence, option (I) and (IV) are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48497,'biology',101,577,1156,'The method of directly injecting a sperm into ovum in Assisted Reproductive Technology is called:','[{"text": "GIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ZIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ICSI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ET", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ICSI stands for Intra Cytoplasmic sperm, Injection. Low or no sperm count is the reason behind ICSI technique.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48498,'biology',101,573,1152,'Increased IMR and decreased MMR in a population will:','[{"text": "Cause rapid increase in growth rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Result in decline in growth rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Not cause significant change in growth rate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Result in an explosive population", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Not cause significant change in growth rate',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48499,'biology',101,574,1153,'Intensely lactating mothers do not generally conceive due to the:','[{"text": "Suppression of gonadotropins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hyper secretion of gonadotropins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Suppression of gametic transport", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Suppression of fertilisation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Intensely lactating mothers do not generally conceive due to the: (1) Suppression of gonadotropins',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48500,'biology',101,574,1153,'Diaphragms are contraceptive devices used by the females. Choose the correct option from the statements given below:<br>i. They are introduced into the uterus<br>ii. They are placed to cover the cervical region<br>iii. They act as physical barriers for sperm entry<br>iv. They act as spermicidal agents','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{i}$ and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Diaphragms are made of rubber and rubber has no spermicidal property.<br>Diaphragm is placed over cervix and not into the uterus. Hence, (ii) and (iii) are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48501,'biology',101,574,1153,'Emergency contraceptives are effective if used within:','[{"text": "$72 \\\\mathrm{hrs}$ of coitus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$72 \\\\mathrm{hrs}$ of ovulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$72 \\\\mathrm{hrs}$ of menstruation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$72 \\\\mathrm{hrs}$ of implantation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Emergency contraceptions are called morning after pills. That can be used within 72 hours of coitus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48502,'biology',101,574,1153,'Sterilisation techniques are generally full proof methods of contraception with least side effects. Yet, this is the last option for the couples because:<br>i. It is almost irreversible<br>ii. Of the misconception that it will increase sexual urge<br>iii. It is a surgical procedure<br>iv. It block semen and ova passage in male and female.<br>Choose the correct option:','[{"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, iii and iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sterilisation techniques are generally full proof methods of contraception with least side effects. Yet, this is the last option for the couples because:<br>i. It is almost irreversible<br>iii. It is a surgical procedure<br>iv. It block semen & ova passage in male and female.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48503,'biology',101,576,1155,'From the sexually transmitted diseases mentioned below, identify the one which does not specifically affect the sex organs:','[{"text": "Syphilis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gonorrhea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genital warts", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'AIDS can be transmitted through sexual contact but is does not affect the reproductive system. It affects the immune system.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48605,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following is not a natural/ traditional contraceptive method?','[{"text": "Coitus interruptus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Periodic abstinence", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactational amenorrhea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vaults", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Vault is a barrier method of contraception which is made of rubber that is inserted into the female reproductive tract to cover the cervix during the coitus.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48504,'biology',101,577,1156,'Choose the correct statement regarding the ZIFT procedure:','[{"text": "Ova collected from a female donor are transferred to the fallopian tube to facilitate zygote formation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote is collected from a female donor and transferred to the fallopian tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ova from donor and sperms are collected fertilized invitro and are transferred to fallopian tube.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ova collected from a female donor and transferrerd to the uterus", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ZIFT stand for Zygote Intra Fallopian Transfer. The name shows that zygote is transferred to the fallopian tube. Transfer to the uterus will be useless because zygote needs to develop into blastocyst for implantation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48505,'biology',101,573,1152,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In India, there is rapid decline in infant mortality rate and MMR.<br></div><div class="column-right">Creating awareness among people about various reproduction related aspects and providing facilities and support for building up a reproductively healthy society are the major tasks under these programmes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement-A : In India, there is rapid decline in infant mortality rate and MMR.<br>Statement-B : Creating awareness among people about various reproduction related aspects and providing facilities and support for building up a reproductively healthy society are the major tasks under these programmes. Both are correct statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48506,'biology',101,574,1153,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Copper-T is an effective contraceptive device in human females.<br></div><div class="column-right">Copper-T prevents passage of sperms from vagina upwards into the fallopian tubes.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement-A : Copper-T is an effective contraceptive device in human females.<br>Statement-B : Copper-T prevents passage of sperms from vagina upwards into the fallopian tubes.Both statements are correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48507,'biology',101,574,1153,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Intra uterine devices (IUD) are very effective contraceptive method. <br></div><div class="column-right">IUD allow sperms to enter the uterus.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A : Intra uterine devices (IUD) are very effective contraceptive method, is correct statement',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48508,'biology',101,577,1156,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Inability to conceive or produce children even after 2 years of unprotected sexual cohabitation is infertility.<br></div><div class="column-right">Invitro fertilization followed by transfer of embryo into the female genital tract is Petridish baby\' programme.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A : Inability to conceive or produce children even after 2 years of unprotected sexual cohabitation is infertility. Is correct statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48509,'biology',101,577,1156,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The zygote or early embryos (with upto 8 blastomeres) could then be transferred into the fallopian tube (ZIFTzygote intra fallopian transfer)<br></div><div class="column-right">Transfer of an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube (GIFT - gamete intra fallopian transfer) of another female who cannot produce one, but can provide suitable environment for fertilisation and further development is another method attempted</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement-A : The zygote or early embryos (with upto 8 blastomeres) could then be transferred into the fallopian tube(ZIFT zygote intra fallopian transfer)<br>Statement-B : Transfer of an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube (GIFT - gamete intra fallopian transfer) of another female who cannot produce one, but can provide suitable environment for fertilisation and further development is another method attempted Both are correct statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48510,'biology',101,573,1152,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">According to the 2011 census report, the population growth rate was less than 2 %, i.e., 20/1000/year, a rate at which our population could increase rapidly.</div><div class="column-right">The world population which was around 2 billion (200 million) in 1900 rocketed to about 6 billions by 2000 .</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A : According to the 2001 census report, the population growth rate was still around 1.7 per cent, i.e., 17/1000/year, a rate at which our population could double in 33 years. Is correct statement.<br>Statement B can be corrected as the world population which was around 2 billion (2000 million) in 1900 rocketed to about 6 billion by 2000 and 7.2 billion in 2011.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48511,'biology',101,572,1151,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Reproductive and child healthcare programme is for reproduction related areas.<br></div><div class="column-right">It deals with creating awareness among varous financial related aspects.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A : Reproductive and child healthcare programme is for reproduction related areas is correct statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48512,'biology',101,573,1152,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Overpopulation has become a serious problem in the developing contries. <br></div><div class="column-right">Statutory raising of marriageable age of the female to 18 years and that of males to 21 years</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement-A : Overpopulation has become a serious problem in the developing countries.<br>Statement-B : Statutory raising of marriageable age of the female to 18 years and that of males to 21 years. Both are correct statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48513,'biology',101,574,1153,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Condoms are barriers made of thick rubber/latex sheath<br></div><div class="column-right">Diaphragms, cervical caps and vaults are barrier methods which prevent conceptions by blocking entry of sperms through cervix. They are reusable.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statement-B : Diaphragms, cervical caps and vaults are barrier methods which prevent conceptions by blocking entry of sperms through cervix. They are reusable.is correct statement.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48514,'biology',101,574,1153,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">There is chance of fertilisation during ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}{\\rm{ - 1}}{{\\rm{7}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ days of menstrual cycle.<br></div><div class="column-right">Menstrual phase can be expected during these days.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A: There is chance of fertilisation during ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}{\\rm{ - 1}}{{\\rm{7}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ days of menstrual cycle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48515,'biology',101,574,1153,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Barrier methods prevent conception.</div><div class="column-right">IUDs decrease phagocytosis of sperms within the uterus and the $\\mathrm{Cu}$ ions released suppress sperm motility and the fertilising capacity of sperms.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement-A : Barrier methods prevent conception.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48516,'biology',101,573,1152,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In India, there is rapid decline in infant mortality rate and MMR.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In India, more and more attention is being given to $\\mathrm{RCH}$ programs.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both assertion and reason are correct but reason is not the correct explanation of assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48517,'biology',101,574,1153,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Copper-T is an effective contraceptive device in human females.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Copper-T prevents passage of sperms from vagina upwards into the fallopian tubes.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Copper-T is surely one of the most effective methods of birth control. It releases $\\mathrm{Cu}$ ions, which makes it difficult for the sperms to reach the uterus (and the egg). Hence it prevents fertilization. Copper- T can prevent pregnancies up to 10 years. So the correct answer is \'Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation for Assertion\'.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48518,'biology',101,574,1153,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Intra uterine devices (IUD) are very effective Contraceptive method.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> IUD don\'t allow sperms to enter the uterus.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'IUDs are a highly effective contraceptive method with a failure rate of less than $1 \\%$. There are currently 5 IUDs available and marketed in the United States: the nonhormonal copper-containing IUD (Paragard Copper T380A; Ortho-McNeil) and 4 hormonal levonor-gestrelreleasing intrauterine systems (LNG-IUDs).<br>The hormones in the IUD prevent pregnancy in two ways: 1) Hormonal IUDs make the mucus on your cervix thicker. This mucus blocks sperm so it can\'t get to an egg. 2) The hormones in the IUD can also stop eggs from leaving your ovaries (called ovulation), which means there\'s no egg for a sperm to fertilize.<br>So the correct answer is \'Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation for Assertion\'.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48531,'biology',101,577,1156,'Artificial insemination means','[{"text": "Artificial introduction of sperms of a healthy donor into the vagina", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Introduction of sperms of healthy donor directly into the ovary", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transfer of sperms of a healthy donor to a test tube containing ova", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transfer of sperms of a husband to a test tube containing ova", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Artificial insemination means Artificial introduction of sperms of a healthy donor into the vagina.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48519,'biology',101,577,1156,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In ability to conceive or produce children even after 2 years of unprotected sexual cohabitation is infertility.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Invitro fertilization followed by transfer of embryo into the female genital tract is \'Test tube baby\' programme.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Infertility is the failure to conceive a child even after unprotected coitus due to sterility, unhealthy reproductive system or some other reasons.<br>When couples are unable to conceive a child due to incurable disorder, then they are assisted through some special technologies to have children. These are commonly known as Assisted Reproductive Technologies(ART). Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation for Assertion',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48520,'biology',101,577,1156,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Test tube baby has raised several legal problems.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> It involves in-vitro fertilization followed by embryo transfer.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation for Assertion. Test tube baby has raised several legal problems as to the right of motherhood between the surrogate mother and the biological mother.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48521,'biology',101,574,1153,'$\\mathrm{Cu}$ ions released from copper-releasing Intra Uterine Devices (IUDs)','[{"text": "Make uterus unsuitable for implantation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases phagocytosis of sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Suppress sperm motility", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prevent ovulation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{Cu}$ ions released from copper-releasing Intra Uterine Devices (IUDs) suppress sperm motility, and their ability to fertilze the ovum.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48522,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which one of the following is the most widely accepted method of contraception in India, at present?','[{"text": "Tubectomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diaphragm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUDs (intra uterine devices)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cervical caps", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Intrauterine contraceptive devices are widely accepeted now a days in India.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48523,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which ones are sexually transmitted diseases','[{"text": "AIDS, Syphilis, Cholera", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trichomoniasis, Malaria, HIV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gonorrhea, Hepatitis B, Chlamydia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hepatitis B, AIDS, Haemophilia", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cholera is a contogious disease, Malaria is a protozoan disease and Haemophilia is a sex linked disease.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48524,'biology',101,576,1155,'Urinogenital tract infection in males accompained by yellow discharge, burning feeling on passing urine, fever and headache is','[{"text": "AIDS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gonorrhea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hepatitis B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Syphilis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Gonorrhea, also spelled gonorrhoea, is a sexually transmitted infection (STI) caused by the bacteriumNeisseria gonorrhoeae. Many people have no symptoms. Men may have burning with urination, discharge from the penis, or testicular pain.Women may have burning with urination, vaginal discharge, vaginal bleeding between periods, or pelvic pain. Complications in women include pelvic inflammatory disease and in men include inflammation of the epididymis. If untreated, gonorrhea can spread to joints or heart valves',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48525,'biology',101,574,1153,'What is the function of copper-T?','[{"text": "Checks mutation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stops fertilization", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stops zygote formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stops oblituation of blastocoel", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'CuT have ionised $\\mathrm{Cu}$ which slowly diffuses at the rate of $50 \\mathrm{mg} /$ day. It has a local antifertility effect by bringing about release of toxic cytokines. They suppress the sperm motility and their ability to fertilize the ovum.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48527,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which contraceptive device makes uterus unsuitable for implantation?','[{"text": "Progestasert", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "CuT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lippes loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiload", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Progestasert is hormonal IUD which suppress endometrial changes and changes in cervical mucus, cause anovulation & insufficient luteal activity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48528,'biology',101,574,1153,'Progestasert and LNG-20 are','[{"text": "Implants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Copper releasing IUD\'s", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-medicated IUDs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hormone releasing IUDs", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Progestasert and LNG-20 are Hormone releasing IUDs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48529,'biology',101,574,1153,'One of the legal method of birth control is<br>','[{"text": "By abstaining from coitus from day 10 - 17 of the menstrual cycle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "By having coitus at the time of day break", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "By a premature ejaculation during coitus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abortion by taking an appropriate medicine", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'By abstaining from coitus from day 10-17 of the menstrual cycle',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48530,'biology',101,574,1153,'$\\mathrm{CuT}, \\mathrm{LNG}-20$ and $\\mathrm{Cu} 7$ are examples of','[{"text": "Contraceptive pills", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monoclonal antibodies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Surgical methods of sterilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intrauterine devices<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cu T, LNG-20 and Cu 7 are examples of Intrauterine devices',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48532,'biology',101,577,1156,'Assisted reproductive technology, IVF involves transfer of<br>','[{"text": "Ovum into the fallopian tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote into the fallopian tube", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zygote into the uterus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo with 16 blastomeres into the fallopian tube.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Assisted reproductive technology, IVF involves transfer of Zygote into the fallopian tube.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48533,'biology',101,574,1153,'Tubectomy is a method of sterilization in which<br>','[{"text": "Small part of the fallopian tube is removed or tied up", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ovaries are removed surgically", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Small part of vas deferens is removed or tied up", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Uterus is removed surgically", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tubectomy is the surgical sterilisation technique for the females. The two oviducts are interrupted by either ligation or cuts. Transport of ova is blocked.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48534,'biology',101,574,1153,'IUDs are used by females','[{"text": "Act as spermicidal gel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Block the entry of sperms into vagina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are implanted under skin where they release progesterone and estrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release copper ions in the uterus that increase phagocytosis of sperms.<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IUDs are used by females Release copper ions in the uterus that increase phagocytosis of sperms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48535,'biology',101,574,1153,'The hormone releasing intrauterine devices such as progestasert specifically<br>','[{"text": "Suppress sperm motility", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase phagocytosis of sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Make uterus unsustainable for implantation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Suppress fertilizing capacity of sperms", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The hormone releasing intrauterine devices such as progestasert specifically. Make uterus unsustainable for implantation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48536,'biology',101,576,1155,'Ectopic pregnancies are referred to as<br>','[{"text": "Implantation of embryo at site other than uterus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Implantation of defective embryo in the uterus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pregnancies terminated due to hormonal imbalance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pregnancies with genetic abnormality", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ectopic pregnancies are referred to as Implantation of embryo at site other than uterus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48537,'biology',101,577,1156,'A childless couple can be assisted to have a child through a technique called GIFT. The full form of this technique is','[{"text": "Gamete Internal Fertilization and Transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Germ cell Internal Fallopian Transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gamete Inseminated Fallopian Transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gamete Intra Fallopian Transfer", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A childless couple can be assisted to have a child through a technique called GIFT. The full form of this technique is Gamete Intra Fallopian Transfer.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48538,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following does not give the defined action of contraceptive?<br>','[{"text": "Hormonal contraceptives-prevent/ retard entry of sperms, prevent ovulation and fertilization.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasectomy- prevents spermatognesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Barrier methods- prevents fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intra uterine devices-increase phagocytosis of sperms, suppress sperm motility and fertilizing capacity of sperms.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Vasectomy- prevents spermatogenesis',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48539,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which of the following virus is not transferred through semen of an infected male?','[{"text": "Chikungunya virus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ebola virus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hepatitis B virus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Human immune deficiency virus<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chikungunya virus is transmitted to people through mosquito bites. Mosquitoes become infected when they feed on a person already infected with the virus. Infected mosquitoes can then spread the virus to other people through bites.<br> Chikungunya virus is most often spread to people by&nbsp;<em>Aedes aegypti</em> and&nbsp;&nbsp;<em>Aedes albopictus</em> mosquitoes. These are the same mosquitoes that transmit dengue virus. They bite during the day and at night.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48540,'biology',101,577,1156,'A childless couple can be administered to have a child through a technique called GIFT, the full form of this technique is','[{"text": "Gamete inseminated fallopian transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gamete intra fallopian transfer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gamete internal fertilization transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Germ cell internal fallopian transfer", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The full form of GIFT is "Gamete intra fallopian transfer". This method is used in females who cannot produce ova but can provide suitable environment for fertilization and further development of embryo in the oviducts. In such cases, ovum from the donor female is surgically removed and is then introduced into the fallopian tubes of such females. Such women then accept sperms from her husband during copulation, called Invivo fertilization.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48541,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following is incorrect regarding vasectomy?<br>','[{"text": "No sperm occurs in seminal tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No sperm occurs in epididymis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vas deferentia is cut and tied", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Irreversible sterility", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Epididymis is an accessory duct present in the male reproductive system. Sperms produced by testes are sent here by vasa efferentia and are temporarily stored here. These sperms do not reach to seminal vesicles when vas deferens is cut and tied in vasectomy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48542,'biology',101,572,1151,'In context of amniocentesis, which of the following statement is incorrect?<br>','[{"text": "It is used for prenatal sex determination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It can be used for detection of down syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It can be used for detection of cleft palate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is usually done when a woman is between 14-16 weeks pregnancy.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Cleft palate is a developmental abnormality which may occur in the developing foetus and so it can be detected by sonography, not by amniocentesis.<br>Amniocentesis is being misused for foetal sex determination test so it is banned in India.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48543,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following is hormone releasing IUD?','[{"text": "LNG-20", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multiload-375", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lippes loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Cu}-7$<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Hormone releasing IUD is LNG-20. The IUDs are ideal contraceptive methods used by females to prevent pregnancy. The hormone releasing IUDs make the uterus unsuitable for implantation and the cervix hostile to the sperms.<br>Concept enhancer Lippes loop is a non medicated IUD whereas Cu-7 and multiload -375 are copper releasing IUDs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48544,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following approaches does not give the defined action of contraceptive?','[{"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Intra uterine}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Increase}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{phagocytosis}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{of sperms,}}\\\\\\\\\\n{\\\\rm{devices}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{suppress}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{spermmotility}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{fertilizing}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{capacity of sperms}}{\\\\rm{.}}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\begin{array}{l}\\n{\\\\rm{Hormonal }}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Prevent/retardentry of}}\\\\,\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{contraceptives}}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{sperms, prevent}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{ovulation }}\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{fertilization}}\\n\\\\end{array}$<br><br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Vasectomy}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Prevents}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{permatogenesis}}$<br>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{Barrier}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{methods}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{Prevent}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{fertilization}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In vasectomy a small part of vas deferens is removed or tied up through a small incision on the scrotum in males. Vasectomy blocks the gamete transport and does not affect the spermatogenesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48545,'biology',101,577,1156,'In case of a couple where the male is having a very low sperm count, which technique will be suitable for fertilization?<br>','[{"text": "Gamete intra cytoplasmic fallopian transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Artificial Insemination", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intra cytoplasmic sperm injection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intrauterine transfer", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Artificial Insemination',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48546,'biology',101,574,1153,'The function of copper ions in copper releasing IUD\'s is :<br>','[{"text": "They inhibit gametogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They make uterus unsuitable for implantation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They inhibit ovulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They suppress sperm motility and fertilizing capacity of sperms", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The function of copper ions in copper releasing IUD\'s is They suppress sperm motility and fertilizing capacity of sperms.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48547,'biology',101,574,1153,'The contraceptive \'SAHELI\'<br>','[{"text": "Is an IUD.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases the concentration of estrogen and prevents ovulation in females.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blocks estrogen receptors in the uterus, preventing eggs from getting implanted.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Is a post-coital contraceptive.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Saheli is the first non-steroidal pill which contains centchroman and its functioning is based upon selective Estrogen Receptor modulation. It prevents implantation but does not inhibit ovulation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48548,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which of the following sexually transmitted diseases is not completely curable?<br>','[{"text": "Gonorrhoea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genital warts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genital herpes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlamydiasis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Genital herpes is caused herpessimplex virus, especially HSV-2 (HSV-1 generally causes oral herpes). At present there is no cure forgenital herpes. Other non-curable STIs are hepatitis-B and HIV.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48549,'biology',101,574,1153,'Select the hormone-releasing Intra-Uterine Devices.','[{"text": "Vaults, LNG-20", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiload 375, Progestasert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progestasert, LNG-20", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lippes Loop, Multiload 375<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Progestasert and LNG-20 are hormone (progestogen) releasing IUDs. They make uterus unsuitablefor implantation and the cervix hostile to sperms.LNG-20 releases Levonorgestrel (synthetic progestogen) 20 mcg per day.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48550,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following contraceptive methods do involve a role of hormone?','[{"text": "Lactational amenorrhea, Pills Emergency contraceptives.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Barrier method, Lactational amenorrhea, Pills.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CuT, Pills, Emergency contraceptives.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pills, Emergency contraceptives, Barrier methods.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In lactational amenorrhoea, due to high prolactin level, gonadotropin level decreases.<br>Oral pills are either progestogens or progestogen-estrogen combinations used by the females.<br>Emergency contraceptives includes the administration of progestogens or progestogenestrogen combination or IUDs within 72 hour of coitus.<br>So, lactational amenorrhoea, oral pills and emergency contraceptives involve a role of hormone.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48551,'biology',101,576,1155,'Select the option including all sexually transmitted diseases.<br>','[{"text": "Gonorrhoea, Malaria, Genital herpes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AIDS, Malaria, Filaria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cancer, AIDS, Syphilis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gonorrhoea, Syphilis, Genital herpes", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Gonorrhoea, Syphilis, Genital herpes',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48552,'biology',101,577,1156,'In which of the following techniques, the embryos are transferred to assist those females who cannot conceive?','[{"text": "GIFT and ZIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ICSI and ZIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GIFT and ICSI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ZIFT and IUT", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'ZIFT and IUT',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48553,'biology',101,576,1155,'Veneral diseases can spread through:<br>(i) Using sterile needles<br>(ii) Transfusion of blood from infected person<br>(iii) Infected mother to foetus<br>(iv) Kissing<br>(v) Inheritance<br><br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.','[{"text": "(i), (ii) and (iii) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii), (iii) and (iv) only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii) and (iii) only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(i) and (iii) only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Venereal diseases can spread through only Transfusion of infected blood from infected person and infected mother to fetus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48554,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which one of the following is an example of hormone releasing IUD?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{CuT}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LNG 20", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{Cu} 7$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiload 375<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'LNG-20 is IUD that releases levonorgestrel (LNG), causes endometrial atrophy and alters the stroma to inhibit implantation. It also increases sperm phagocytosis in the uterus',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48555,'biology',101,574,1153,'Match List - I with List - II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">a. Vaults<br>b. IUDs<br>c. Vasectomy<br>d. Tubectomy</div><div class="column-right">1. Entry of sperm through cervix  is blocked<br>2. Removal of a part of the vasa deferens<br>3. Phagocytosis of sperms within the uterus<br>4. Removal of a part of the fallopian tube</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{a - 4}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{b - 2}},\\\\,{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{c - 1}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{d - 3}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{a - 1}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{b - 3}},{\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,{\\\\rm{c - 2}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{d - 4}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{a - 2}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{b - 4}},\\\\,{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{c - 3}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{d - 1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{a - 3}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{b - 1}},\\\\,{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\rm{c - 4}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{d - 2}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{a - 1}},\\,{\\rm{b - 3}},{\\mkern 1mu} \\,{\\rm{c - 2}},\\,{\\rm{d - 4}}$',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48556,'biology',101,574,1153,'Lippe\'s loop is a type of contraceptive used as:<br>','[{"text": "Vault barrier", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-Medicted IUD", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Copper releasing IUD", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cervical barrier", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lippe\'s loop is a non-medicated IUD, it increases phagocytosis of sperms within the uterus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48557,'biology',101,574,1153,'Match Column - I with Column - II with respect to methods of contraception and their respective actions.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">a. Diaphragm<br>b. Contraceptive<br>c. Intra uterine<br>d. Lactational</div><div class="column-right">1. Inhibit ovulation and implantation<br>2. Increase pills phagocytosis of sperm within uterus<br>3. Absence of devices menstrual cycle and ovulation following parturition<br>4. They cover the cervix Amenorrhea blocking the entry of sperms<br></div></div>','[{"text": "a-4, b-1, c-2, d-3", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a-2, b-4, c-1, d-3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-3, b-2, c-1, d-4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a-4, b-1, c-3, d-2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Diaphragms - They cover the cervix blocking the entry of sperms.<br>Contraceptive pills - Inhibit ovulation and implantation<br>Intra uterine devices - Increase phagocytosis of sperm within uterus<br>Lactational amenorrhea - Absence of Menstrual cycle and ovulation following parturitio',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48558,'biology',101,574,1153,'An example for hormone releasing IUD is','[{"text": "Multiload 375", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lippes loop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Implant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "LNG – 20", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'LNG – 20<br>Levenorgesterol – 20 (on) progestasert is hormone releasing IUD.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48559,'biology',101,575,1154,'MTPs are considered relatively safe during','[{"text": "24 weeks of pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "180 days of pregnancy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "First trimester", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Second trimester", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'First trimester<br>MTP’s are relatively safe during first trimester because placenta and organs of foetus are not fully formed & developed',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48560,'biology',101,577,1156,'Which of the following is abbreviated as ZIFT?','[{"text": "Zygote Inter Fallopian Transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote Intra Fallopian Tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote Inter Fallopian Tube", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote Intra Fallopian Transfer", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'ZIFT – Zygote Intra fallopian transfer In this zygote is transferred into fallopian tube',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48561,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which one of the following common sexually transmitted diseases is completely curable when detected early and treated properly?','[{"text": "Genital herpes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gonorrhoea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hepatitis-B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "HIV Infection", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Except for hepatitis-B, genital herpes and HIV infection other STIs are completely curable if detected early and treated properly. Gonorrhoea is a bacterial disease which can be treated and cured completely, other diseases\nmentioned are viral diseases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48562,'biology',101,574,1153,'Match Column I with Column II.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Vasectomy<br>B. Coitus interruptus<br>C. Cervical caps<br>D. Saheli</div><div class="column-right">P. Oral method<br>Q. Barrier method<br>R. Surgical method<br>S. Natural method</div></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-P, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'P. Vasectomy is a surgical method of contraception<br>Q. Coitus interruptus is a natural method of contraception<br>R. Cervical cap is a barrier method of contraception<br>S. Saheli is an oral method of contraception which is a non-steroidal pill',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48563,'biology',101,573,1152,'Read the Assertion and Reason carefully to mark the correct options given below:<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Amniocentesis for sex determination is one of the strategies of Reproductive and Child Health Care Programme<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Ban on amniocentesis checks increasing menace of female foeticide.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and R is NOT the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A is false but R is true. as ‘Reproductive and Child Health Care (RCH) programme’ deals with creating awareness among people about various reproduction related aspects and providing facilities and support for building up a reproductively healthy society.<br>Amniocentesis is not a sex determination technique in India and is not a strategy of RCH.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48572,'biology',101,574,1153,'Lactational amenorrhea:','[{"text": "Prevents secretion of milk from breast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prevents conception", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prevents secretion of prolactin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Prevents spermatogenesis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In lactational amenorrhea, immediately after parturition, during period of lactation, there is absence of menstruation. As long as breastfeeding is continued, chances of pregnancy are extremely low. The duration of becoming pregnant during this time is about six months after parturition.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48564,'biology',101,574,1153,'Match the contraceptive methods given under Column I  (Contraceptive Method) with their examples given under Column II (Examples). Select the correct choice from those given below:<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Chemical<br>B. IUDs<br>C. Barriers<br>D. Sterilization</div><div class="column-right">P. Tubectomy & Vasectomy<br>Q. Copper T & Loop<br>R. Condom & Cervical cap<br>S. Spermicidal Jelly & Foam<br>T. Coitus interruptus and calender method</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{T} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S} ; \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q} ; \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{T} ; \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Various foams, creams, jellies, suppositories and douches that contain sperm killing agents, or spermicides, make the vagina and cervix unfavourable for sperm survival.<br>Intra Uterine Devices (IUDs) is a small object made of plastic, copper, or stainless steel that is inserted by a health-care professional into the cavity of the uterus through vagina. The IUDs can be non-medicated such as Lippes loop, copper-releasing such as $\\mathrm{CuT}, \\mathrm{Cu} 7$, Multiload 375 and hormone releasing such as Progestasert, LNG-20, etc.<br>Barrier methods use a physical barrier and are designed to prevent sperm from gaining access to the uterine cavity and fallopian tubes for example, condom and cervical cap.<br>Surgical sterilization is a procedure that renders an individual incapable of further reproduction, hence is a permanent method of birth control. In males, it is known as vasectomy and in females, it is known as tubectomy or tubal ligation.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48565,'biology',101,574,1153,'The time for optimum chances of conception in a woman is ____  starting from the $1^{\\text {st }}$ day of menstruation.','[{"text": "$1^{\\\\text {st }}$ day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2^{\\\\text {nd }}$ day", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$14^{\\\\text {th }}$ day", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$26^{\\\\text {th }}$ day", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Ovulation, the rupture of the mature (Graafian) follicle and the release of the secondary oocyte into the pelvic cavity, usually occurs on day 14 to 16 in a 28 days cycle. In this time, the chances of conception are very high.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48566,'biology',101,576,1155,'The sexually transmitted disease, that can affect both the male and the female genitals and may damage the eyes of babies born of infected mothers is:','[{"text": "AIDS", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Syphilis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gonorrhoea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hepatitis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gonorrhoea (flow of seed) is caused by the bacterium Neiseria gonorrhoeae. In males, urethra is the site of infection while in females, it is the cervix, followed by urethra, anal canal and pharynx. If a pregnant woman has a gonorrheal infection, she may give the infection to her infant as the infant passes through the birth canal during delivery. This infection in an infant can cause eye infections, pneumonia, or infections of the joints or blood.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48567,'biology',101,574,1153,'Read the Statements A and B and Identify the correct choice from those given<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Women are at the peak of conception on the day of ovulation.<br></div><div class="column-right">Vasectomy is the method normally employed to avoid conception in females.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is wrong, Statement B is right.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is right, Statement B is wrong.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are right", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are wrong.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In males, a portion of vas deferens is removed by surgical method. Although sperm production continues in the testes, sperm can no longer reach the exterior, thus control the birth.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48568,'biology',101,573,1152,'One of the following causes population explosion:','[{"text": "Decrease in death rate, maternal mortality rate and infant mortality rate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decrease in death rate and increase in maternal mortality rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease in infant mortality rate and increase in death rate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease in infant mortality rate and decrease in the number of people in reproductive age", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The rapid growth of population is due to a difference in the rate of birth and death. A decrease in infant mortality rate (IMR) and maternal mortality rate (MMR) due to better medical facilities are also responsible for increase in population.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48569,'biology',101,574,1153,'IUDs which are used by females','[{"text": "Act as spermicidal jellies", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Block the entry of sperms into vagina", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Are implanted under the skin and they release progestogen and oestrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release copper ions in the uterus that increase phagocytosis of sperms.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The IUDs can be non-medicated such as Lippes loop, copper-releasing such as CuT, $\\mathrm{Cu}$, Multiload 375 and hormone releasing such as Progestasert, LNG-20, etc. IUDs prevent fertilization from taking place by blocking sperm from entering the fallopian tubes. They also enhance phagocytosis of the sperms. The copper ions reduce sperm motility and fertilizing capacity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48570,'biology',101,577,1156,'Assisted Reproductive Technology (ART) does not include:','[{"text": "In vitro fertilization and embryo transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gamete intra fallopian transfer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote extra fallopian transfer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Artificial insemination", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Assisted Reproductive Technologies (ART) includes:<br>(i) Zygote Intra Fallopian Transfer (ZIFT)<br>(ii) In vitro Fertilisation (IVF) and embryo transfer<br>(iii) Artificial insemination<br>(iv) Gamete Intra Fallopian Transfer (GIFT).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48571,'biology',101,574,1153,'Progestasert is an IUD which makes the uterus unsuitable and cervix hostile to the sperms as they are:','[{"text": "Copper releasing IUDs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non - medicated IUDs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hormone releasing IUDs", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ideal contraceptive", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Intrauterine Contraceptive Devices (IUDs) are effective and popular methods of contraception. These are inserted by doctors or expert nurses in the uterus through vagina. These devices are presently available as the non-medicated IUDs (e.g., Lippes loop), copper releasing IUDs (CuT, Cu7, Multiload 375) and the hormone releasing IUDs (Progestasert, LNG-20). IUDs increase phagocytosis of sperms within the uterus and the $\\mathrm{Cu}$ ions released suppress sperm motility and the fertilizing capacity of sperms. The hormone releasing IUDs make the uterus unsuitable for implantation and the cervix hostile to the sperms. IUDs are ideal contraceptives for the females.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48573,'biology',101,574,1153,'Match the following Column I with Column II.<br> Select the code for the correct answer from the\noptions given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Surgical\nmethods<br>B. Barrier\nmethods<br>C. Natural\nmethods<br>D. Chemical\nmethods</div><div class="column-right">P. Condom<br>Q. Pills<br>R. Tubectomy<br>S. Lactational\namenorrhea</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  P, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Surgical sterilization is a procedure that renders an individual incapable of further reproduction, hence is a permanent method of birth control. In males, it is known as vasectomy and in females, it is known as tubectomy or tubal ligation.<br>Barrier methods use a physical barrier and are designed to prevent sperm from gaining access to the uterine cavity and fallopian tubes. They are available for both males and females. Among the barrier methods are the male condom, vaginal pouch, diaphragm and cervical cap.<br>Immediately after parturition, during period of lactation, there is absence of menstruation. As long as breast freeding is continued, chances of pregnancy are extremely slim. This is called lactational amenorrhea.<br>Oral contraceptives (the pill) are tablets that contain hormones (either progestogens or progestogen-oestrogen combinations) designed to prevent pregnancy. These pills should be taken daily for 21 days starting within the first five days of menstruation.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48574,'biology',101,573,1152,'The following factors indicate improved reproductive health of the society. Choose the correct option.<br>A. Better detection and cure of disease<br>B. Better post-natal care<br>C. Medically assisted deliveries<br>D. Increased MMR<br>Select the code for the correct answer from the options given below.','[{"text": "B, C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and C only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A, C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and D only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Awareness about methods to have sound reproductive health is not only beneficial to both mother and child but to the society at large. The benefits of these programmes are listed as follows:<br>Prevention of unwanted pregnancy by having knowledge about methods of contraception.<br>Prevention of high-risk pregnancy.<br>Having medically-assisted deliveries.<br>Planning pregnancy at an appropriate age when the mother is neither too young nor too old so as to maintain good health of both mother and child.<br>Appropriate spacing between two child births.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48575,'biology',101,574,1153,'The method of natural contraception which requires correct knowledge of menstrual cycle is:','[{"text": "Periodic abstinence", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lactational amenorrhoea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUDs - Intrauterine devices", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coitus interrupts", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In periodic abstinence, a couple can use their knowledge of the physiological changes that occur during the female reproductive cycle to decide either to abstain from intercourse on those days when pregnancy is a likely result, or to plan intercourse on those days if they wish to conceive a child.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48576,'biology',101,577,1156,'Choose the correct statement regarding GIFT (Gamete Intrafallopian Tube Transfer) procedure.','[{"text": "Ova collected from a female donor are transferred to the fallopian tube to facilitate zygote formation in the recipient.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zygote is collected from female donor and transferred to the fallopian tube of recipient.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote is collected from female donor and transferred to the uterus of recipient.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ova are collected from a female donor and are transferred to the uterus of recipient.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Ovum is a gamete and is inserted into the fallopian tube.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48577,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following contraceptives could be effective in avoiding pregnancy if used in 72 hours after casual unprotected intercourse?','[{"text": "Androgen - FSH combination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Testrosterone - Relaxin combination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Relaxin - Oxytocin combination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Progestogen - Estrogen combination", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Progesterone and oestrogen combination are taken to avoid conception in case of unprotected intercourse.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48578,'biology',101,574,1153,'Select the incorrect statement about contraceptives','[{"text": "They are regular requirement for the maintenance of reproductive health", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They have a significant role in checking uncontrolled growth population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They are practiced against a natural reproductive events like conception or pegnancy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The possible ill-effects like nausea, abdominal pain, irregular menstrual bleeding or even breast cancer should not be totally ignored.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Contraception provides solutions so that conception of the zygote / blastocyst (pregnancy)can be prevented, as such they do not maintain reproductive health.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48579,'biology',101,577,1156,'The technique advised by a doctor to overcome the problem of infertility :','[{"text": "RCH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "MTP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RTI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ART", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The problem of infertility can be overcome by assisted reproductive technology (ART) like IVF-ET, GIFT, ZIFT etc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48580,'biology',101,577,1156,'In which technique of ART, fertilization takes place in fallopian tube?','[{"text": "GIFT and ZIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ZIFT and AI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ZIFT and IUT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GlFT and AI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In GIFT, ovum is introduced into the fallopian tube. In artificial insemination (AI), semen is introduced into the vagina or the uterus. So, in both of these methods, fertilization occurs in fallopian tube.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48581,'biology',101,577,1156,'The technique called gamete intra fallopian transfer (GIFT) is recommended for those females','[{"text": "Who cannot produce an ovum.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Who cannot retain the foetus inside uterus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Whose cervical canal is too narrow to allow passage for the sperms.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Who cannot provide suitable environment for fertilization.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gamete Intra Fallopian Transfer (GIFT) is recommended for those females who cannot produce an ovum but can provide suitable environment for fertilization. In this process, the eggs of the donor woman are transferred into fallopian tube the woman who cannot produce ovum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48582,'biology',101,574,1153,'An individual undergoes sterilization process in which a small incision was done on \' $\\mathrm{X}$ \' and a part of vas deferens is removed or tied up. Identify \' $\\mathrm{X}$ \' and the intervention of this surgical process.','[{"text": "\' $\\\\mathrm{X}$ \' - Fallopian tube; Prevent ovulation and implantation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{X}$\' - Testes; Prevent conception by blocking sperm entry.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "\' $\\\\mathrm{X}$ \' - Epididymis; Inhibit maturation of sperm and its transport.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{X}$ \' - Scrotum; Gamete transport is blocked and thereby prevents conception.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The described sterilization process is called vasectomy in which a small incision was done on the scrotum and a part of vas deferens is removed or tied up. Due to this gamete transport is blocked and thereby prevents conception.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48583,'biology',101,574,1153,'Tying up or removing a small part of fallopian duct is called','[{"text": "Vasectomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ductus arteriosus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archidectomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tubectomy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Female sterilization (called tubectomy) prevents fertilization by interrupting the passage through fallopian tube.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48584,'biology',101,574,1153,'The most important component of the oral contra-ceptive pills is','[{"text": "Progesterone", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Growth hormone", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thyroxine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Luteinizing hormone", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oral administration of small doses of either progestogens or progestogen-estrogen combinations (in the form of pills) is one of the contraceptive methods used by the females.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48585,'biology',101,575,1154,'Choose the correct statements given below regarding contraception.<br>I. Medical Termination of Pregnancy (MTP) during first trimester is generally safe.<br>II. Generally, chances of conception are nil until mother breast-feeds the infant up to two years.<br>III. Intrauterine devices like copper-T are effective contraceptives.<br>IV. Contraception pills may be taken up to one week after coitus to prevent conception.','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Contraceptive pills have to be taken daily for a period of 21 days starting preferably within the first five days of menstrual cycle. It helps in the prevention of conception. As long as the mother feeds breast the child fully, chances of conception are almost nil only up to a maximum period of six months following parturition.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48586,'biology',101,577,1156,'The test-tube baby programme employs which one of the following techniques','[{"text": "Intra cytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intra uterine insemination (IUI)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gamete intra fallopin transfer (GIFT)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zygote intra fallopian transfer (ZIFT)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Test tube baby programme involves formation of zygote in vitro method and than transfer of zygote into fallopian tube.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48587,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which one of the following is an incorrect match?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Lactational - Natural contraception amenorrhoea method", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saheli - Steroidal pills", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lippes loop - Non medicated IUCD", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Test tube baby - In vitro fertilization", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Saheli is a nonsteroidal preparation and contains the drug centchroman (ormeloxifene).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48588,'biology',101,574,1153,'The diaphragm, cervical cap and vaults are','[{"text": "Disposable chemical barriers", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reusable contraceptives", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Non-medicated IUDs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cu-releasing IUDs", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Diaphragms, cervical caps and vaults are reusable barrier contraceptives made of rubber that are inserted into the female reproductive tract to cover the cervix during coitus. They prevent conception by blocking the entry of sperms through the cervix. They are reusable.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48589,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following approaches does not give the defined action of contraceptive?','[{"text": "Intra uterine devices - increase phagocytosis of sperms, suppress sperm motility and fertilizing capacity of sperms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hormonal contraceptives - Prevent/ retard entry of sperms, prevent ovulation and fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasectomy - prevents spermatogenesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Barrier methods - prevent fertilization", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Vasectomy does not interfere with spermatogenesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48590,'biology',101,574,1153,'Identify the wrong statements<br>I. Pills and hormone releasing IUDs make cervix hostile to sperms<br>II. The mode of action of implants is similar to that of pills<br>III. Vasectomy prevents conception<br>IV. Tubectomy blocks ovulation','[{"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Tubectomy blocks sperm and ovum meeting each other.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48591,'biology',101,576,1155,'Which of the following infections can also be transmitted by sharing of injection needles, surgical instruments, etc., with infected persons, transfusion of blood, or from an infected mother to the foetus too?','[{"text": "Hepatitis B and HIV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genital herpes and HIV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Syphilis and Hepatitis B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlamydiasis and Trichomoniasis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both hepatitis B and HIV diseases can be transmitted by sharing of injection needles, surgical instruments, etc., with infected persons, transfusion of blood, or from an infected mother to the foetus too.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48604,'biology',101,574,1153,'Match Column I with Column II<br>Choose the correct answer from the option given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Non-medicated IUD<br>B. Copper releasing IUD<br>C. Hormone releasing IUD<br>D. Implants</div><div class="column-right">P. Multiload 375<br>Q. Progestogens<br>R. Lippes loop<br>S. LNG-20</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  Q, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  R, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  P, C  -  Q, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q}}$ is the correct option. Lippes loop is a non-medicated IUD. Multiload 375 is a copper releasing IUD. LNG - 20 is a hormone releasing IUD. Progestogens are used as implants',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48592,'biology',101,576,1155,'Given below are some examples of sexually transmitted diseases. Identify the one or more which specifically affect the sex organs.<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{{\\rm{I}}{\\rm{.}}\\,{\\rm{AIDS}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{{\\rm{II}}{\\rm{.}}\\,{\\rm{Syphilis}}}&{}\n\\end{array}\\\\\n\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{III}}{\\rm{.}}\\,{\\rm{Gonorrhea}}}\n\\end{array}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}&{\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n{{\\rm{IV}}{\\rm{.}}\\,{\\rm{Genital}}\\,{\\rm{warts}}}\n\\end{array}}&{}\n\\end{array}\n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Syphilis, gonorrhea and genital warts are sexually transmitted disease which specifically affects the sex organs. Syphilis is caused by the spirochete bacterium Treponema pallidum. Gonorrhea is caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae. Genital warts are caused by human papilloma virus. The AIDS is caused by the retrovirus HIV. The illness alters the immune system. It does not specifically affect the sex organs.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48593,'biology',101,574,1153,'The process done in the given figure.','[{"text": "Prevents gamete transport", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Avoid insemination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Inhibits ovulation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases contraceptive efficiency", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The figure shows the process of tubectomy. This is a surgical method to prevent pregnancy in women. In tubectomy small part of the fallopian tube is removed or tied through a small cut in the abdomen or through vagina. Tubectomy blocks gamete transport and thereby prevent conception.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/101_48593_question_1.png'),
(48594,'biology',101,574,1153,'Given is a diagram of a contraceptive device. Identify it.','[{"text": "Multiload 375", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Contraceptive implant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Copper-T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vault", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Contraceptive implant, implanted below the skin in the arm.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/101_48594_question_1.png'),
(48595,'biology',101,577,1156,'Which of the following is correct?','[{"text": "In India, often the male is blamed for the couple being childless", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sometimes, use condoms during coitus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Government of India legalised MTP in 1961 with some strict conditions to avoid its misuse.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ICSI is a procedure to form an embryo in the laboratory in which a sperm is directly injected into the ovum.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'ICSI is a procedure to form an embryo in the laboratory in which a sperm is directly injected into the ovum. This is the only correct statement.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48596,'biology',101,577,1156,'The transfer of zygote or early embryo (up to 8 blasto-meres) into fallopian tube is called ____.','[{"text": "ICSI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ZIFT", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "GIFT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IUT", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'ZIFT (Zygote intra fallopian transfer) is the process in which the zygote or early embryos (with upto 8 blastomeres) is transferred into the fallopian tube.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48597,'biology',101,574,1153,'Select the correct match from the given option.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Non-Medicated IUDs- Multiload 375", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Saheli - Contains a non-steroidal preparation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lactational - Presence of amenorrhea menstruation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diaphragms, $\\\\quad-$ Cover the cervix cervical caps, vaults after the coitus is done", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Saheli is a non-hormonal birth control pill. It is different from other birth control pills because it doesn\'t contain any hormones. Instead of using the hormone estrogen to prevent pregnancy, it contains a drug that blocks estrogen.<br>Non Medicated IUDs - Lippes loop<br>Lactational amenorrhea - Absence of menstruation Diaphragms, cervical caps, vaults - Cover the cervix during the coitus.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48598,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following methods prevents conception by just blocking gamete transport?','[{"text": "Surgical methods", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Oral contraceptives", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Implants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Natural methods", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Surgical intervention blocks gamete transport and thereby prevents conception.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48599,'biology',101,574,1153,'Which of the following contraceptive also provides protection from contacting STDs and AIDS ?','[{"text": "Diaphragms", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spermicidal foams", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Condoms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lactational amenorrhea", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The use of condoms during coitus is some of the simple precautions to avoid contacting STDs like AIDS and syphilis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48600,'biology',101,574,1153,'A contraceptive pill prevents ovulation by','[{"text": "Inhibiting the release of FSH and LH", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Stimulating the release of FSH and LH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blocking of the fallopian tubes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Causing immediate degeneration of released ovum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Inhibiting the release of FSH and LH helps in checking ovulation. This is the main work of contraceptive pills.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48601,'biology',101,576,1155,'The appearance of chancre, rashes all over the body are the symptoms of:','[{"text": "Gonorrhoea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Syphilis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fever", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The symptoms of syphilis occur in four stages.<br>They begin with appearance of painless nonitchy skin ulcer called chancre.<br>It is followed bu skin rash over hands and sole of the feet.<br>No sign or symptom in latent stage.<br>In tertiary stage shows formation of granulomatous inflammations called gummas.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48602,'biology',101,575,1154,'The Government of India legalised MTP with some strict regulations in the year','[{"text": "1951", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1961", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1971", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2001", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'MTP refers to Medical Termination of Pregnancy or Induced abortion. Government of India legalised MTP in 1971 with some strict conditions to avoid its misuse.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48603,'biology',101,574,1153,'The process in which a small part of the vas deferens is removed or tied up through a small incision, is called','[{"text": "MTP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vasectomy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tubectomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GIFT", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sterilisation procedure in the male is called \'vasectomy\' and in the female, it is called \'tubectomy\'. GIFT- Gamete Intra fallopian transfer is a method of assisted reproductive technologies (ART).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48606,'biology',80,475,959,'In Kranz anatomy bundle sheath cells have','[{"text": "Thick walls, many intercellular spaces and few chloroplasts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thin walls, many intercellular spaces and no chloroplasts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thick walls, no intercellular spaces and large number of chloroplasts", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thin walls, no intercellular spaces and several chloroplasts", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The bundle sheath cells may form several layers around the vascular bundles; they are characterised by having a large number of chloroplasts, thick walls impervious to gaseous exchange and no intercellular spaces.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48607,'biology',80,477,962,'Of the total incident solar radiation the proportion of PAR is','[{"text": "About $60\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Less than $50\\\\% $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "More than $80\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "About $70\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Photosynthetically active radiation varies from season to season and the spectral range of solar radiation varies from 400-700 nm, photosynthetic organisms are able to use in the process of photosynthesis the amount which accounts for less than $50\\% $.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48608,'biology',80,475,959,'${C_4}$ plants are more efficient in photosynthesis than in ${C_3}$ plants due to','[{"text": "Higher leaf area", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of larger number of chloroplast in the leaf cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Presence of thin cuticle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "lower rate of photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${C_4}$ plants are more efficient in photosynthesis than ${C_3}$ plants but use more energy. The leaves of ${C_4}$ plants have more number of chloroplast when compared to ${C_3}$ plants,vascular bundles are covered by bundle sheath cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48609,'biology',80,475,959,'Kranz anatomy is one of the characteristic of the leaves of','[{"text": "Wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sugarcane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mustard", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Potato", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sugarcane, being a ${C_4}$ plant shows Kranz anatomy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48610,'biology',80,474,957,'PGA as the first $C{O_2}$ fixation product was discovered in photosynthesis of','[{"text": "Bryophyte", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gymnosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Angiosperm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alga", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Melvin Calvin made a study using 14C in alga-Chlorella in the photosynthetic $C{O_2}$ fixation and they were able to identify it as 3-carbon compound PGA-phosphoglyceric acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48611,'biology',80,473,955,'Read the following statement i, ii, iii and iv and select the right option having both correct statements<br>i. Z scheme of light reaction takes place in presence of PSI only<br>ii. Only PS I is functional in cyclic photophosphorylation<br>iii. Cyclic photophosphorylation results into synthesis of ATP and $NADP{H_2}$<br>iv. Stroma lamellae lack PS II as well as NADP____reductase','[{"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Z-scheme or non-cyclic photophosphorylation includes PS-I as well as PS-II. Cyclic photophosphorylation results in the synthesis of ATP only, not NADPH.<br>Correct statements are &ndash; ii and iv',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48612,'biology',80,474,958,'Transport of food material in the higher plants take place through','[{"text": "Transport tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tracheids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sieve elements", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Companion cells", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sieve elements – Major transporting element of food.Transfusion tissue – In place of lateral viens in gymnosperm leaves.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48613,'biology',80,470,949,'Oxygenic photosynthesis occurs in','[{"text": "<em>Chromatium</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Oscillatoria</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Rhodospirillum</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Chlorobium</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<em>Oscillatoria </em>is a photosynthetic cyanobacteria in which water is an electron donor and oxygen is byproduct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48614,'biology',80,473,955,'Cyclic phosphorylation results in the formation of','[{"text": "NADPH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP and NADPH", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP, NADPH and ${O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'During cyclic photophosphorylation only one photosystem is involved, P700. When the photons activate, a pair of electrons are raised to a higher energy level and captured by the electron acceptors. At each electron transfer proton gradient is established which is responsible for formation of ATP.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48615,'biology',80,475,959,'In the leaves of  ${C_4}$ plants, malic acid formation during $C{O_2}$ fixation occurs in the cells of','[{"text": "Mesophyll", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bundle sheath", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phloem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epidermis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The oxalic acid is reduced to malic acid in mesophyll cells, from mesophyll it is transferred to bundle sheath where it is decarboxylated to form $C{O_2}$ and pyruvic acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48616,'biology',80,476,960,'During photorespiration, the oxygen consuming reactions occurs in','[{"text": "Stroma of chloroplast and peroxisomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Grana of chloroplast and peroxisomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stroma of chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stroma of chloroplasts and mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the first reaction photorespiration occurs in stroma of chloroplast. In this reaction RuBP consumes one oxygen molecule in presence of enzyme RuBisCo.In peroxisome, the glycolate transferred from chloroplast takes up ${O_2}$ and forms the glyoxylate whereas, the ${H_2}{O_2}$ is released as a byproduct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48617,'biology',80,475,959,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> ${C_4}$  plants photosynthesise more efficiently than ${C_3}$ plants<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> As ${C_4}$ plants has a shorter $C{O_2}$ cycle','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${C_4}$ plants are more efficient when compared to ${C_3}$ plants because they have a reduced  $C{O_2}$ fixing mechanism.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48618,'biology',80,474,958,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Six molecules of  $C{O_2}$ and 12 molecules of NADPH and 18 ATP are used to form one hexose molecule<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Light reaction results in the formation ATP and $NADP{H_2}$','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hexose molecule is formed during Calvin cycle and it utilises ATP and NADPH.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48619,'biology',80,474,958,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The carbohydrate manufactured in the leaves of higher plants are distributed to roots and storage organ through phloem.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The long distance movement of organic compounds is called translocation','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plants synthesise carbohydrate and are transported to roots and storage organs through phloem.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48620,'biology',80,477,965,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Under conditions of water stress, the rate of photosynthesis declines<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Stomatal closure and resultant decrease in $C{O_2}$ supply','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Water stress causes the stomata to close hence reducing the $C{O_2}$ availability. Besides, water stress also makes leaves wilt, thus, reducing the surface area of the leaves and their metabolic activity as well. This as a whole decreases the rate of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48621,'biology',80,475,959,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> To reduce the effect of photorespiration ${C_3}$ plants have been gifted with $C{O_2}$ concentrating mechanism<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The $C{O_2}$ concentrating mechanism is called ${C_3}$ pathway','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$C{O_2}$ concentrating mechanism is known as Hatch and Slack pathway/ ${C_4}$ pathway.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48622,'biology',80,472,951,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The action spectrum of photosynthesis does not parallel the absorption spectrum of chlorophyll exactly<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Accessory pigments of carotenoids transfer some of the energy of excitation produced by green light to chlorophyll molecules','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The action spectrum of of photosynthesis does not coincide with the absorption spectrum of chlorophyll-a exactly. This is because a lot of accessory pigments also participate in the absorption of light energy which make a small difference in the graphs. Accessory pigments like chlorophyll-b, carotenoids, xanthophylls play a role here.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48623,'biology',80,472,951,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Chlorophyll appears green<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Chlorophyll absorbs green light from sunlight and it is this absorbed energy that drives photosynthesis','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chlorophyll is green coloured pigment which absorbs radiant energy of sun and combines with $C{O_2}$, water and leads to the formation of carbohydrate',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48624,'biology',80,472,951,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The absorption spectrum of chlorophyll-a shows close correlation with its action spectrum<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Chlorophyll is present in both the photosystems I and II','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chlorophyll is present in both the photosystems and chlorophyll-a shows a close correlation to the action spectrum.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48625,'biology',80,471,950,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The energy capturing part of photosynthesis occurs in thylakoid membranes and cannot proceed without solar energy.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The synthesis part of photosynthesis occurs in the stroma and does not require direct light energy.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The light reaction occurs in the thylakoid which captures the solar energy and the dark reaction occurs in stroma where the products of light reaction are utilised during dark reaction.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48716,'biology',80,474,957,'What is correct about Dark Reaction?','[{"text": "It is called Hill reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is biochemical, enzymatic, depeding on light raection", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is independent of enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Dark reaction thought light independent, requires products formed from light reaction. It uses various enzymes to carry out a series of reactions. Hence, it is also known as the biochemical phase of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48626,'biology',80,473,955,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Cyclic pathway of photosynthesis first appeared in some eubacterial species<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> ${O_2}$ started accumulating in the atmosphere after the noncyclic pathway of photosynthesis evolved','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cyclic pathway of photosynthesis was first discovered in eubacteria. It is supposed to be first evidence of production of ATP in the presence of light. During non-cyclic photophosphorylation, photolysis of water\ntakes place. This releases oxygen that accumulates in the environment.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48627,'biology',80,477,965,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Water stress is caused by insufficient soil moisture and is among the chief causes of poor growth or poor health in plants<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> There exists for each plant a range of watering, neither too wet nor too dry, within which it is able to grow and maintain good health.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Water is an indirect limiting factor. It maintains the turgidity of the assimilatory cells and the hydration of the protoplasm. Dehydration of protoplasm affects the activity of enzymes that catalyse photosynthesis.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48628,'biology',80,476,960,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The process of photosynthesis is sensitive to higher temperatures.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Affinity of the enzyme RuBisCO for $C{O_2}$ is reduced at high temperature','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Under favourable conditions of light and carbon dioxide concentration photosynthesis increases with increase in temperature till it reaches maximum.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48629,'biology',80,476,960,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Photorespiration is considered a loss to ${C_3}$ plants<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> During this photosynthetically fixed carbon is lost.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Photorespiration is a process which reduces the efficiency of photosynthesis, potentially reducing photosynthetic output by $25\\% $ in ${C_3}$ plants.Photorespiration involves a complex network of enzyme reactions that exchange metabolites between chloroplast, peroxisomes and mitochondria.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48630,'biology',80,476,960,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Photorespiration decreases photosynthetic output<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In photorespiratory pathway, neither ATP nor NADPH is produced','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are false.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Photorespiration is a wasteful pathway which also utilises the energy-assimilatory powers of light reaction.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48631,'biology',80,477,965,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Water stress causes the stomata to close hence reducing the $C{O_2}$ availability</div><div class="column-right">Water stress also makes leaves wilt, thus, reducing the surface area of leaves and their metabolic activity</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Water stress causes the stomata to close hence reducing the $C{O_2}$ availability. Besides, water stress also makes leaves wilt, thus, reducing the surface area of the leaves and their metabolic activity as well.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48632,'biology',80,477,964,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The ${C_4}$ plants have a much lower temperature optimum while ${C_3}$ plants respond to higher temperatures</div><div class="column-right">Tropical plants have a higher temperature optimum than the plants adapted to temperate climates</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The ${C_4}$ plants respond to higher temperatures and show higher rate of photosynthesis while ${C_3}$ plants have a much lower temperature optimum. The temperature optimum for photosynthesis of different plants also depends on the habitat that they are adapted to. Tropical plants have a higher temperature optimum than the plants adapted to temperate climates.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48633,'biology',80,477,963,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">${C_3}$ plants respond to higher $C{O_2}$ concentration leading to higher productivity has been used for some greenhouse crops such as tomatoes and bell pepper</div><div class="column-right">The ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants respond equally to $C{O_2}$ concentrations</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_3}$ plants respond to higher $C{O_2}$ concentration by showing increased rates of photosynthesis leading to higher productivity has been used for some greenhouse crops such as tomatoes and bell pepper. They are allowed to grow in carbon dioxide enriched atmosphere that leads to higher yields.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48634,'biology',80,477,963,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Carbon dioxide is the major limiting factor for photosynthesis</div><div class="column-right">${C_4}$ plants show saturation at about 450 ulL-1 while ${C_3}$ plants show saturation beyond 360 ulL-1</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Carbon dioxide is the major limiting factor for photosynthesis. ${C_4}$ plants show saturation at about 360 µlL-1 while ${C_3}$ responds to increased $C{O_2}$ concentration and saturation is seen only beyond 450 µlL-1.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48635,'biology',80,477,962,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">There is a linear relationship between incident light and  $C{O_2}$ fixation rates at low light intensities</div><div class="column-right">Light saturation occurs at 1 percent of the full sunlight</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'There is a linear relationship between incident light and  $C{O_2}$ fixation rates at low light intensities. t light saturation occurs at 10 per cent of the full sunlight.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48636,'biology',80,477,961,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The plant or external factors are dependent on the genetic predisposition and the growth of the plant</div><div class="column-right">The internal factors would include the availability of sunlight, temperature, $C{O_2}$ concentration and water</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The plant or internal factors are dependent on the genetic predisposition and the growth of the plant. The external factors would include the availability of sunlight, temperature, $C{O_2}$ concentration and water.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48637,'biology',80,476,960,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Photorespiratory pathway results in the release of  $C{O_2}$ with the utilisation of ATP</div><div class="column-right">Photorespiration is a wasteful process</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the photorespiratory pathway, there is neither synthesis of sugars, nor of ATP. Rather it results in the release of  $C{O_2}$ with the utilisation of ATP. In the photorespiratory pathway there is no synthesis of ATP or NADPH. The biological function of photorespiration is not known yet. It is a wasteful process.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48638,'biology',80,476,960,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">RuBisCO has a much greater affinity for  ${O_2}$ than for $C{O_2}$</div><div class="column-right">In ${C_3}$ plants, some ${O_2}$ binds with RUBP to form one molecule of phosphoglycerate and phosphoglycolate in a pathway called photorespiration</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'RuBisCO has a much greater affinity for $C{O_2}$ when the $C{O_2}$ : ${O_2}$ is nearly equal. In ${C_3}$ plants some ${O_2}$ does bind to RuBisCO, and hence $C{O_2}$ fixation is decreased. Here the RuB instead of being converted to 2 molecules of PGA binds with ${O_2}$ to form one molecule of phosphoglycerate and phosphoglycolate (2 Carbon) in a pathway called photorespiration.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48639,'biology',80,475,959,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In ${C_4}$ plants, bundle sheath cells are rich in PEPcase but lack RuBisCO</div><div class="column-right">Calvin pathway occurs in all the mesophyll cells of the ${C_3}$ plants but in ${C_4}$ plants it takes place in the bundle sheath cells</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The bundle sheath cells are rich in an enzyme Ribulose bisphosphate carboxylaseoxygenase (RuBisCO), but lack PEPcase. The basic pathway that results in the formation of the sugars, the Calvin pathway, is common to the ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants. In the ${C_4}$ plants it does not take place in the mesophyll cells but does so only in the bundle sheath cells.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48640,'biology',80,475,959,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In ${C_4}$ cycle, enzyme responsible for the primary  $C{O_2}$ fixation is PEP carboxylase which is present in the bundle sheath cells</div><div class="column-right">In ${C_4}$ plants, mesophyll cells lack PEP carboxylase enzyme</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The enzyme responsible for fixation in ${C_4}$ plants is PEP carboxylase or PEPcase. It is present in the mesophyll cells. These cells lack RuBisCO enzyme.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48641,'biology',80,475,959,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">${C_4}$ plants have a special type of leaf anatomy, called Kranz anatomy</div><div class="column-right">Large cells around the vascular bundles of the ${C_4}$ pathway plants are called Mesophyll cells</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_4}$  plants are special: They have a special type of leaf anatomy, they tolerate higher temperatures, they show a response to high light intensities, they lack a process called photorespiration and have greater productivity of biomass. The particularly large cells around the vascular bundles of the C4 plants are called bundle sheath cells, and the leaves which have such anatomy are said to have ‘Kranz’ anatomy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48642,'biology',80,474,958,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">For every $C{O_2}$ molecule entering the Calvin Cycle 3 molecules of ATP and 2 of NADPH are required</div><div class="column-right">To make one molecule of glucose 6 turns of the Calvin cycle are required</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For every  $C{O_2}$ molecule entering the Calvin cycle, 3 molecules of ATP and 2 of NADPH are required. To make one molecule of glucose 6 turns of the cycle are required.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48643,'biology',80,474,958,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In ${C_3}$ cycle, first stage is carboxylation which is catalysed by the enzyme RuBP oxygenase which results in the formation of two molecules of 3-PGA</div><div class="column-right">Second stage is reduction, in which utilisation of 2 molecules of ATP for phosphorylation and 2 of NADPH per $C{O_2}$ molecule fixed</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Carboxylation is the fixation of $C{O_2}$ into a stable organic intermediate. Carboxylation is the first and most crucial step of the Calvin cycle where $C{O_2}$ is utilised for the carboxylation of RuBP. This reaction is catalysed by the enzyme RuBP carboxylase which results in the formation of two molecules of 3-PGA. Second step, reduction involves utilisation of 2 molecules of ATP for phosphorylation and two of NADPH for reduction per $C{O_2}$ molecule fixed.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48644,'biology',80,474,957,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The plants in which first product of $C{O_2}$  fixation is a ${C_3}$ acid (OAA) is called ${C_3}$ pathway and the plants in which first product was a ${C_4}$ acid (PGA) is called ${C_4}$ pathway</div><div class="column-right">Calvin pathway occurs in most of the photosynthetic plants</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Those plants in which the first product of $C{O_2}$ fixation is a ${C_3}$ acid (PGA), i.e., the ${C_3}$ pathway, and those in which the first product was a ${C_4}$ acid (OAA), i.e., the ${C_4}$ pathway. The Calvin pathway occurs in all photosynthetic plants; it does not matter whether they have ${C_3}$ or ${C_4}$ (or any other) pathways.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48645,'biology',80,474,957,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Biosynthetic phase of photosynthesis directly depend on the presence of light but is independent on the products of the light reaction</div><div class="column-right">The use of radioactive 14C by Calvin in algal photosynthesis studies led to the discovery that the first $C{O_2}$ fixation product was a 3-carbon organic acid</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Biosynthetic phase of photosynthesis does not directly depend on the presence of light but is dependent on the products of the light reaction, i.e., ATP and NADPH, besides $C{O_2}$ and ${H_2}O$. The use of radioactive 14C by him in algal photosynthesis studies led to the discovery that the first $C{O_2}$ fixation product was a 3-carbon organic acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48646,'biology',80,473,956,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The products of light reaction are ATP, NADPH and ${O_2}$</div><div class="column-right">ATP and NADPH diffuses out of chloroplast while ${O_2}$ is used for the synthesis of food, i.e, sugars</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The products of light reaction are ATP, NADPH and ${O_2}$. Of these ${O_2}$ diffuses out of the chloroplast while ATP and NADPH are used to drive the processes leading to the synthesis of food, more accurately, sugars.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48647,'biology',80,473,956,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chemiosmosis requires a membrane, a proton pump, a proton gradient and ATPase</div><div class="column-right">Energy is used to pump protons across the membrane, to create a gradient within the thylakoid lumen</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chemiosmosis requires a membrane, a proton pump, a proton gradient and ATP synthase. Energy is used to pump protons across a membrane, to create a gradient or a high concentration of protons within the\nthylakoid lumen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48648,'biology',80,473,956,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The ATPase enzyme consists of two parts, the ${F_0}$ portion is embedded in the membrane and forms a transmembrane channel that carries out simple diffusion of protons across the membrane</div><div class="column-right">The other portion of  ${F_1}$ and it protrudes on the outer surface of the thylakoid membrane on the side that faces the stroma</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The ATP synthase enzyme consists of two parts: one called the $C{F_0}$ is embedded in the thylakoid membrane and forms a transmembrane channel that carries out facilitated diffusion of protons across the\nmembrane. The other portion is called $C{F_1}$ and protrudes on the outer surface of the thylakoid membrane on the side that faces the stroma',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48812,'biology',80,477,964,'How does ${C_4}$ plants respond to higher temperatures?','[{"text": "Show higher rate of photosynthesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Show lower rate of photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Higher rate of photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lower rate of photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The ${C_4}$ plants respond to higher temperatures and show higher rate of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(48649,'biology',80,473,956,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Within the chloroplast, protons in the stroma decrease in number, while in the lumen there is accumulation of protons</div><div class="column-right">Accumulation of protons in the lumen creates a proton gradient across the thylakoid membrane as well as a measurable decrease in pH in the lumen</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Within the chloroplast, protons in the stroma decrease in number, while in the lumen there is accumulation of protons. This creates a proton gradient across the thylakoid membrane as well as a measurable decrease in pH in the lumen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48650,'biology',80,473,956,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The NADP reductase enzyme is located on the grana side of the membrane</div><div class="column-right">Along with electrons that come from the acceptor of electrons of PS I, protons are necessary for the reduction of NADP + ${H^ + }$ to $NAD{P^ + }$</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The NADP reductase enzyme is located on the stroma side of the membrane. Along with electrons that come from the acceptor of electrons of PS I, protons are necessary for the reduction of $NAD{P^ + }$ to$NADP{H^ + }$ ${H^ + }$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48651,'biology',80,473,956,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">As electrons move through the photosystems, protons are transported across the membrane</div><div class="column-right">The primary acceptor of electron which is located towards the inner side of the membrane transfers its electron to an H carrier</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'As electrons move through the photosystems, protons are transported across the membrane. This happens because the primary accepter of electron which is located towards the outer side of the membrane\ntransfers its electron not to an electron carrier but to an H carrier.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48652,'biology',80,473,954,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Splitting of water molecule takes place on the inner side of the membrane</div><div class="column-right">The electrons that are produced by splitting of water accumulate within the lumen of the thylakoids</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The water splitting complex is associated with the PS II, which itself is physically located on the inner side of the membrane of the thylakoid. The protons and ${O_2}$ formed are released in the lumen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48653,'biology',80,473,954,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The water splitting complex is associated with PS I</div><div class="column-right">Water is split into ${{\\rm{H}}^ + }$, [O] and electrons, which creates oxygen, one of the net products of photosynthesis</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The splitting of water is associated with the PS II; water is split into 2${H^ + }$, [O] and electrons. This creates oxygen, one of the net products of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48654,'biology',80,473,956,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">ATP synthesis is linked to development of a proton gradient across the membrane</div><div class="column-right">In photosynthesis, proton accumulation is towards the inside of the membrane, i.e, in the lumen</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Like in respiration, in photosynthesis too, ATP synthesis is linked to development of a proton gradient across a membrane. This time these are the membranes of thylakoid. There is one difference though, here the proton accumulation is towards the inside of the membrane, i.e., in the lumen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48655,'biology',80,473,955,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The cyclic flow of electrons, results only in the synthesis of NADP + ${H^ + }$</div><div class="column-right">Cyclic photophosphorylation occurs when only light of wavelengths beyond 680nm are available for excitation</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The cyclic flow results only in the synthesis of ATP, but not of NADPH + ${H^ + }$ . Cyclic photophosphorylation also occurs when only light of wavelengths beyond 680 nm are available for excitation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48656,'biology',80,473,955,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The membrane or lamellae of the grana have only PS II</div><div class="column-right">The stroma lamellae lack PS I as well as NADP reductase enzyme</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'While the membrane or lamellae of the grana have both PS I and PS II the stroma lamellae membranes lack PS II as well as NADP reductase enzyme.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48813,'biology',80,477,964,'Dark reactions being enzymatic are __ controlled.','[{"text": "Temperature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pressure", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The dark reactions being enzymatic are temperature controlled.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48657,'biology',80,473,955,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cyclic photophosphorylation occurs in the stroma lamellae</div><div class="column-right">In cyclic photophosphorylation only PS I is functional, the electron is circulated within the photosystem and the phosphorylation occurs due to cyclic flow of electrons</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When only PS I is functional, the electron is circulated within the photosystem and the phosphorylation occurs due to cyclic flow of electrons . A possible location where this could be happening is in the stroma lamellae',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48658,'biology',80,473,953,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">When the two photosystems work in a series, first PS I and then PS II, a process called noncyclic photophosphorylation occurs</div><div class="column-right">The two photosystems are connected through an electron transport chain</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When the two photosystems work in a series, first PS II and then the PS I, a process called non-cyclic photo-phosphorylation occurs. The two photosystems are connected through an electron transport chain.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48659,'biology',80,473,953,'Match the following:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Photophosphorylation is the synthesis of ATP from ADP and inorganic phosphate in the absence of light</div><div class="column-right">ATP is synthesised by cells (in mitochondria and chloroplasts) is named photophosphorylation</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Photophosphorylation is the synthesis of ATP from ADP and inorganic phosphate in the presence of light. ATP is synthesised by cells (in mitochondria and chloroplasts), this process is named as phosphorylation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48660,'biology',80,473,952,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The single chlorophyll a molecule forms the reaction centre</div><div class="column-right">In PS I the reaction centre has an absorption peak at 680 nm and in PS II has absorption maxima at 700 nm</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The single chlorophyll a molecule forms the reaction centre. The reaction centre is different in both the photosystems. In PS I the reaction centre chlorophyll a has an absorption peak at 700 nm, hence is called P700, while in PS II it has absorption maxima at 680 nm, and is called P680.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48661,'biology',80,473,952,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The LHC are made up of hundreds of pigment molecules bound to lipids</div><div class="column-right">Each photosystems has all the pigments (except chlorophyll-a) forming a light harvesting system also called antennae</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The LHC are made up of hundreds of pigment molecules bound to proteins. Each photosystem has all the pigments (except one molecule of chlorophyll a) forming a light harvesting system also called antennae.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48662,'biology',80,473,952,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The pigments are organised into two discrete photochemical light harvesting complexes (LHC) within the Photosystem I and Photosystem II</div><div class="column-right">PS I and PS II are named in the sequence in which they function during the light reaction</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The pigments are organised into two discrete photochemical light harvesting complexes (LHC) within the Photosystem I (PS I) and Photosystem II (PS II). These are named in the sequence of their discovery, and\nnot in the sequence in which they function during the light reaction.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48663,'biology',80,473,952,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Light reactions include light absorption, water splitting, oxygen release, and the formation of high energy chemical intermediates, ATP and NADPH</div><div class="column-right">Light reactions is also known as photochemical phase</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Light reactions or the ‘Photochemical’ phase include light absorption, water splitting, oxygen release, and the formation of highenergy chemical intermediates, ATP and NADPH.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48664,'biology',80,472,951,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Most of the photosynthesis takes place in the blue and red regions of the spectrum</div><div class="column-right">Accessory pigments protect chlorophyll a from photoreduction</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Most of the photosynthesis takes place in the blue and red regions of the spectrum; some photosynthesis does take place at the other wavelengths of the visible spectrum. Accessory pigments not only enable a wider range of wavelength of incoming light to be utilised for photosyntesis but also protect chlorophyll a from photo-oxidation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48665,'biology',80,472,951,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chlorophyll-a is the major pigment responsible for trapping light</div><div class="column-right">Thylakoid pigments like chlorophyll b, xanthophylls and carotenoids are called accessory pigments</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chlorophyll a is the major pigment responsible for trapping light, other thylakoid pigments like chlorophyll b, xanthophylls and carotenoids, which are called accessory pigments, also absorb light and transfer the\nenergy to chlorophyll a.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48666,'biology',80,472,951,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chlorophyll a is bright or blue green and Chlorophyll b is yellow green</div><div class="column-right">Xanthophyll is yellow-to yellow orange and carotenoids is yellow in colour</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chlorophyll a (bright or blue green in the chromatogram), chlorophyll b (yellow green), xanthophylls (yellow) and carotenoids (yellow to yellow-orange).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48667,'biology',80,472,951,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The leaf pigments of any green plant can be separated through column chromatography</div><div class="column-right">A chromatographic separation of the leaf pigments shows that the colour we see in the leaves is only due to a single pigment</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Leaf pigments of any green plant can be separated through paper chromatography. A chromatographic separation of the leaf pigments shows that the colour that we see in leaves is not due to a single pigment but due to four pigments: Chlorophyll a (bright or blue green in the chromatogram), chlorophyll b (yellow green), xanthophylls (yellow) and carotenoids (yellow to yellow-orange).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48668,'biology',80,471,950,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The membrane system is responsible for trapping the light energy and also for the synthesis of ATP and NADPH</div><div class="column-right">In stroma, enzymatic reactions incorporate $C{O_2}$ into the plant leading to the synthesis of sugar, which in turn forms starch</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The membrane system is responsible for trapping the light energy and also for the synthesis of ATP and NADPH. In stroma, enzymatic reactions synthesise sugar, which in turn forms starch.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48669,'biology',80,471,950,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The chloroplasts align themselves along the walls of the mesophyll cells, such that they get the optimum quantity of incident light</div><div class="column-right">Within the chloroplast there is the membranous system consisting of stroma, the fret channel, and the fluid grana</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Usually the chloroplasts align themselves along the walls of the mesophyll cells, such that they get the optimum quantity of the incident light. Within the chloroplast there is membranous system consisting of grana, the stroma lamellae, and the matrix stroma.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48670,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">${C_6}{H_{12}}{O_6}$ represents glucose</div><div class="column-right">The ${O_2}$ released is from carbon dioxide, this was proved using radio isotope techniques</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_6}{H_{12}}{O_6}$ represents glucose. The ${O_2}$ released is from water; this was proved using radio isotope techniques.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48671,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In green plants ${H_2}O$ is the hydrogen donor and is oxidised to ${O_2}$</div><div class="column-right">When ${H_2}S$ instead is the hydrogen donor for purple and green sulphur bacteria, the oxidation product is sulphur or sulphate depending on the organism and not ${O_2}$</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In green plants ${H_2}O$ is the hydrogen donor and is oxidised to ${O_2}$. Some organisms do not release ${O_2}$ during photosynthesis. When ${H_2}S$, instead is the hydrogen donor for purple and green sulphur bacteria, the ‘oxidation’ product is sulphur or sulphate depending on the organism and not ${O_2}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48672,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Cornelius van Niel demonstrated that photosynthesis is essentially a light-independent reaction</div><div class="column-right">According to Neil, hydrogen from a suitable oxidisable compound reduces carbon dioxide to carbohydrates</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cornelius van Niel, who, based on his studies of purple and green bacteria, demonstrated that photosynthesis is essentially a light-dependent reaction in which hydrogen from a suitable oxidisable compound reduces\ncarbon dioxide to carbohydrates.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48673,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Plants could use light energy to make carbohydrates from  $C{O_2}$ and ${H_2}O$</div><div class="column-right">$C{H_2}O$ represents a carbohydrate</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Plants could use light energy to make carbohydrates from $C{O_2}$ and water. $C{H_2}O$ is represented as a carbohydrate (e.g., glucose)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48674,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A first action spectrum of photosynthesis resembles roughly the absorption spectra of chlorophyll a and b</div><div class="column-right">Engelmann observed that the bacteria accumulated mainly in the region of violet and red light of the split spectrum</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The first action spectrum of photosynthesis resembles roughly the absorption spectra of chlorophyll a and b. Engelmann observed that the aerobic bacteria accumulated mainly in the region of blue and red light of the split spectrum.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48675,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Using a prism, T.W Engelmann split light into its spectral components and then illuminated a green alga, chlamydomonas, placed in a suspension of aerobic bacteria</div><div class="column-right">The aerobic bacteria were used to detect the site of  $C{O_2}$ evolution</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Using a prism, T.W.Engelmann split light into its spectral components and then illuminated a green alga, Cladophora, placed in a suspension of aerobic bacteria. These aerobic bacteria were used to detect the sites\nof  ${O_2}$ evolution.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48676,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Julius von Sachs provided evidence for production of sucrose when plants grow</div><div class="column-right">Glucose is usually stored as starch</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Julius von Sachs provided evidence for production of glucose when plants grow. Glucose is usually stored as starch.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48677,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Priestley discovered hydrogen in 1774</div><div class="column-right">J. Ingenhousz also showed that it is only the green part of the plants that could release carbon dioxide</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Priestley discovered oxygen in 1774. Jan Ingenhousz showed that it is only the green part of the plants that could release oxygen.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48678,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Jan Ingenhousz showed that sunlight is essential to the plant process that somehow purifies the air fouled by burning candles or breathing animals</div><div class="column-right">Ingenhousz in an elegant experiment with an aquatic plant showed that in bright sunlight, small bubbles were formed around the green parts while in the dark they did not</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Jan Ingenhousz showed that sunlight is essential to the plant process that somehow purifies the air fouled by burning candles or breathing animals. Ingenhousz in an elegant experiment with an aquatic plant showed that in bright sunlight, small bubbles were formed around the green parts while in the dark they did not.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48679,'biology',80,470,949,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">J. Priestley performed a series of experiments, that revealed the essential role of water in the growth of green plants</div><div class="column-right">Priestley hypothesised as follows: Plants restore the air whatever breathing animals and burning candles remove</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Joseph Priestley in 1770 performed a series of experiments that revealed the essential role of air in the growth of green plants. He concluded that a burning candle or an animal that breathe the air, both somehow, damage the air',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48680,'biology',80,469,948,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In the half leaf experiment, a part of leaf is enclosed in a test tube containing some KOH soaked cotton, while the other half is exposed to air</div><div class="column-right">On testing for starch, it is found that the exposed part of the leaf tested positive for starch while the portion that was in the tube, tested negative</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A part of a leaf is enclosed in a test tube containing some KOH soaked cotton (which absorbs  $C{O_2}$ ), while the other half is exposed to air. The setup is then placed in light for some time. On testing for the presence of starch later in the two parts of the leaf, the exposed part of the leaf tested positive for starch while the portion that was in the tube, tested negative. This showed that $C{O_2}$ was required for photosynthesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48681,'biology',80,469,948,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Chlorophyll, light and $C{O_2}$ are required for photosynthesis to occur</div><div class="column-right">Within the chloroplasts, the membranes are sites for the dark reaction, while the chemosynthetic pathway occurs in the stroma</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement-A is correct but Statement-B is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement-A is incorrect but Statement-B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chlorophyll (green pigment of the leaf), light and $C{O_2}$ are required for photosynthesis to occur. Within the chloroplast, light reaction occurs inside membranes while dark reaction takes place within the stroma.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
