(48694,'biology',80,474,957,'Dark reaction in photosynthesis is called so because','[{"text": "It can occur in dark also", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It does not depend on light energy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It cannot occur during day light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It occurs more rapidly at night", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Splitting of water molecule and formation ATP are directly driven by light and hence are called light reactions. Rest of the steps are not directly light driven and hence are called dark reactions (as per convention). This does not mean that they happen in dark and not during the day.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48695,'biology',80,472,951,'Which light range is least effective in photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Blue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Red", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Violet", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Because chlorophyll, the pigment involved in photosynthesis is green (for the most part, there are other forms that are not green) and because it is green it reflects green wavelengths of light and does not absorb them.Plants need to absorb light to perform photosynthesis.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
