(48697,'biology',80,472,951,'Which pigment acts directly to convert light energy to chemical energy?','[{"text": "Chlorophyll a", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyll b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xanthophyll", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carotenoid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Maximum absorption of light takes place by chlorophyll a.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,'NCERT Exemplar','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48698,'biology',80,470,949,'Which of the following is incorrect about the experiment performed by Engelmann?','[{"text": "<em>Cladophora</em>, blue green algae is used.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prism was used to split light into its spectral component.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria accumulated mainly in the region of blue and red light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The aerobic bacteria were used to detect the sites of ${O_2}$ evolution.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<em>Cladophora</em>, a green alga was used in Engelmann&rsquo;s experiment.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48699,'biology',80,475,959,'Given below are some characterstics of photosynthetic plants.Which of these are true for ${C_4}$ plants<br>i) RuBisCo is the primary and first acceptor of $C{O_2}$<br>ii) The first stable compound formed is 4-carbon compound<br>iii) Thefirst stable compound formed is PGA<br>iv) Possess PEP carboxylase<br>v) The first carboxylation reaction occurs in bundle sheath cells<br>vi) The HSK cycle takes place in mesophyll cells\n<br>vii) 3-carbon in the primary $C{O_2}$ acceptor','[{"text": "(i),(iv),(v),(vii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i),(ii),(iii),(iv),(vii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii),(iii),(iv),(vi),(vii)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii),(iv),(vi),(vii)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'PEP is the primary acceptor of $C{O_2}$. OAA is the first stable product formed. First carboxylation occurs in mesophyll cells. The correct statements are - ii,iv,vi,vii',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48700,'biology',80,475,959,'Why are ${C_4}$ plants more tolerant to hot climates?','[{"text": "They do not close their stomata in hot, dry weather", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unlike ${C_3}$, ${C_4}$ plants fix $C{O_2}$ even in low concentration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Unlike ${C_3}$, ${C_4}$ plants fix ${O_2}$ even in low concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthesis is differently performed in ${C_4}$ plants and is irrespective of the temperature", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${C_4}$ plants are tolerant to hot weather. They can fix $C{O_2}$ even if it is low in concentration whereas in ${C_3}$ plants, RuBisCO binds to ${O_2}$ and carries out ${C_2}$ cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48701,'biology',80,474,957,'Find out the incorrect statement from the following:','[{"text": "The ${O_2}$ released is from water; this was proved using radio isotope techniques.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In stroma, enzymatic reactions incorporates $C{O_2}$ into the plant leading to the synthesis of sugar.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dark reaction depends on the product formed by light reaction.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Always, the chloroplasts align themselves along the walls of the mesophyll cells", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chloroplasts align themselves along the walls of mesophyll cells only occasionally, when they do not get optimum amount of sunlight.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48702,'biology',80,475,959,'Which of the following characteristics are present in ${C_3}$ plants but not in ${C_4}$ plants?','[{"text": "Initial involvement of RUBP carboxylase in $C{O_2}$ assimilation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of well developed bundle sheath", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both (1) and (2)',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48703,'biology',80,475,959,'All ${C_4}$ plants show Kranz anatomy and it is -','[{"text": "Environmentally determined", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-gentically adapted", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetically adapted", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Kranz anatomy in ${C_4}$ plants is genetically adapted.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48704,'biology',80,475,959,'PEPcase + RuBisCo is present in the ${C_4}$ plants. The advantage is that -','[{"text": "PEPcase is an enzyme while RuBisCo is just a structural protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PEP case combines with $C{O_2}$ even if it is less in amount RuBisCO comes in further .", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "PEPcase combines with ${O_2}$ + carbon dioxide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PEPcase is present in both mesophyll and bundle sheath but RuBisCO is not", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'PEPcase shows carboxylase activity only, even in the presence of less $C{O_2}$ concentration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48717,'biology',80,474,957,'Ribulose biphosphate carboxylase (RuBisCO) enzyme catalyses the reaction','[{"text": "Calvin cycle, ${C_4}$ pathway", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calvin cycle, ${C_3}$ pathway, Photorespiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Calvin cycle, ${C_3}$ pathway, Respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calvin cycle, respiration", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'RuBisCO under carboxylase activity catalyses ${C_3}$ cycle/ Calvin cycle. When acting as an oxygenase, it carries out Photorespiration/  ${C_2}$ cycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48705,'biology',80,474,958,'Select an incorrect statement for Biosynthetic phase of photosynthesis','[{"text": "Use of radioactive ${N_{15}}$ in algal photosynthesis studies led to the discovery", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "This process is independent on the products of the light reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "OAA and PGA either is formed depending on the type of morphology of the plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Radioactive ${C_{14}}$ in algal photosynthesis led to the discovery of the ${C_3}$ cycle. The dark reaction thought light-independent, is dependent on the products of light reaction. If its a ${C_3}$ plant, PGA is the first stable product formed after carboxylation. If its a ${C_4}$ plant, OAA is formed as first stable product after carboxylation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48706,'biology',80,474,957,'In the given statements I- VI<br>I. The most abundant enzyme in the world.<br>II. Its active site can bind to both $C{O_2}$ and O2 hence the name.<br>III. Has a much greater affinity for $C{O_2}$ than ${O_2}$.<br>IV. The relative conc. of  ${O_2}$ and $C{O_2}$ determines which of the two will bind to the enzyme.<br>V. It is present in all photosynthetic plants.<br>VI. It is present in chloroplast. <br>The above facts are characteristic of which enzyme?','[{"text": "PEPcase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RuBisCo", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Hexokinase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nitrogenase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'All the guven characteristics point towards one enzyme, RuBisCO.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48707,'biology',80,474,957,'RuBisCO is the most _________','[{"text": "Least carbohydrate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Least protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Abundant protein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Abundant carbohydrate", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'RuBisCO is the most abundant enzyme (protein) in the universe.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48708,'biology',80,474,958,'Select an incorrect statement for  ${C_3}$ cycle','[{"text": "The regeneration of RuBP from glyceraldehyde- 3-phosphate requires 2 ATP molecule each", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "With the oxidation of PGA, glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate is formed.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_3}$ cycle occurs only in ${C_3}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The regeneration of RuBP from glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate requires 1 ATP molecule each. With the reduction of PGA, glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate is formed. ${C_3}$ cycle is a common pathway in all kinds of plants. Hence, all statements are incorrect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48709,'biology',80,474,957,'The scientists believed that since the first product was ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ acid, the primary ${\\rm{C}}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ acceptor would be ____','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$- compound", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{3}}}$ - compound", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{5}}}$ - compound", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\rm{C}}_{\\\\rm{6}}}$ - compound", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Scientists believed that since the first product was a ${{\\rm{C}}_{\\rm{3}}}$ acid, the primary acceptor would be a 2-carbon compound; they spent many years trying to identify a 2-carbon compound before they discovered the 5-carbon RuBP',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48710,'biology',80,474,957,'Carbon dioxide enter photosynthesis through','[{"text": "PS I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biosynthetic phase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Light reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PS II", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Carbon dioxide enters in the carboxylation step of  ${C_3}$ cycle during dark/ biosynthetic phase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48711,'biology',80,474,957,'The reactions of Calvin cycle not directly dependent on light, but they usually do not occur at night - Why?','[{"text": "Night is often too cold for these reactions to occur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ concentration in night is too high for these reactions to occur", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants usually open their stomata at night", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calvin cycle is dependent on the products of light reaction", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Calvin cycle continues till products of light reaction are not completely consumed. Until night, all the ATP and NADPH produced by light reaction is already used for carbon fixation. Hence, ${C_3}$ cycle is shut down\nthroughout the night.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48712,'biology',80,471,950,'In terms of the spatial organization of photosynthesis within the chloroplast, what is the advantage of light reactions producing ATP and  $NADP{H_2}$ on the stromal side of the thylakoid membrane?','[{"text": "ATP and  $NADP{H_2}$ is required for Calvin cycle occurs in stromal lamellae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Light reaction occurs in stroma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Calvin cycle occurs in grana and needs ATP + $NADP{H_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP and  $NADP{H_2}$ is required for Calvin cycle occurs in stroma", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Products of light reaction i.e. ATP and NADPH formed on the stromal side of thylakoid membrane is advantageous as these products are required for dark reaction that occurs in the stroma itself',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48713,'biology',80,474,958,'Identify the incorrect statement w.r.t Calvin cycle','[{"text": "The first stable intermediate compound formed is phosphoglycerate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "NADH + ${H^ + }$ produced in light reaction is used to reduce diphosphoglycerate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "18 Molecules of ATP are synthesised during carbon fixation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The first stable product in ${C_3}$ cycle is 3-PGA. NADPH produced in light reaction is used to reduce 3-phosphoglycerate. 18 ATP is utilised during carbon fixation. Hence, all statements are incorrect.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48714,'biology',80,474,958,'What is the number of ATP utilized during regeneration of 6 molecules of RUBP from 10 molecules of G-3P?','[{"text": "Six", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Twelve", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Each molecule of RuBP requires 1 ATP to regenerate. 6 molecules of RuBP would take 6 ATP',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
