(48722,'biology',80,475,959,'The basic feature of typical C4 plants showing ‘Kranz’ anatomy is','[{"text": "The presence of non granal chloroplasts in bundle sheath cells and granal chloroplasts in mesophyll cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The presence of granal chloroplasts in bundle sheath cells and non granal chloroplasts in mesophyll cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The presence of chloroplasts with well formed grana in bundle sheath cells and chloroplasts absent in the mesophyll cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The chloroplast in both is the same", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Kranz anatomy is characterised by presence of bundle sheath cells. In the chloroplasts of these cells, grana are absent. They are present in the chloroplasts of normal mesophyll cells.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48723,'biology',80,473,956,'During photosynthesis the protons are transported across the thylakoid membrane into the lumen because','[{"text": "Electrons are transfered to hydrogen carrier, which is present on the outer side of membrane", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Electrons are transferred to electron carrier", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electrons are transferred to intermembrane space", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Electrons are transferred to hydrogen carrier which is present on inner membrane", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'During ETS, electron and proton exchange across the membranes takes place simultaneously. The protons are transported across the thylakoid membrane into the lumen because electrons are transfered to hydrogen carrier, which is present on the outer side of membrane.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
