(48758,'biology',80,470,949,'Who demonstrated that ${O_2}$ comes from water instead of  $C{O_2}$ during photosynthesis in their experiment, Also identify the organism used','[{"text": "Cornelius van Niel, purple and green bacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Engelmann van Niel, purple and green bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Julius van Niel, green bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cornelius van Niel, green bacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cornelius van Neil based on his studies of purple and green bacteria, demonstrated that ${H_2}O$ is the hydrogen donor and is oxidised to ${O_2}$. Some organisms do not release  ${O_2}$ during photosynthesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48759,'biology',80,470,949,'Photosynthesis is the fastest in','[{"text": "Blue light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intermittent white light", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Red light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green light", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'As far as the rate of photosynthesis is concerned, it is fastest in white light making the rate of photosynthesis maximum. Photosynthesis occurs highest in the shortest wavelength hence has the max energy.\nPhotosynthetic pigments absorb visible part of the radiation (i.e., 380 um and 760 um). For example, chlorophyll absorbs blue and red light. Usually, plants show a high rate of photosynthesis in the blue and red light.\nMaximum photosynthesis has been observed in red light than in blue light. The green light has a minimum effect. The rate of photosynthesis is maximum in white light or sunlight( Polychromatic light). On the other hand, red algae show maximum photosynthesis in green light and brown algae in blue light.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48760,'biology',80,470,949,'Von Sach studies shows that','[{"text": "Glucose is usually stored as starch.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Experiment were carried out in 1854", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green substance in plants is located in special bodies within the plant cell.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Julius von Sachs in 1854 provided evidence for production of glucose when plants grow. Glucose is usually stored as starch. His later studies showed that the green substance in plants (chlorophyll as we know it\nnow) is located in special bodies (later called chloroplasts) within plant cells. He found that the green parts in plants is where glucose is made, and that the glucose is usually stored as starch.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
