(48786,'biology',80,477,963,'It is expected that  $C{O_2}$ concentration could reach to a level of about 600 ml.L¬-1 by 2020. In such case, the ___ are likely to be benefitted more than the__.','[{"text": "${C_3}$ plants, ${C_4}$ plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${C_3}$ plants, ${C_2}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CAM plants, ${C_4}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_4}$ plants, CAM plants", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_4}$ plants show saturation at about 360 µlL-1 while  ${C_3}$ responds to increased  $C{O_2}$ concentration and saturation is seen only beyond 450 µlL-1. An increase in  $C{O_2}$ concentration would benefit ${C_3}$ plants more than ${C_4}$ plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48787,'biology',80,477,963,'Identify the family of the green house crops which show greater productivity in higher $C{O_2}$ concentration _','[{"text": "Liliaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fabaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brassicaceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Solanaceae", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The fact that ${C_3}$ plants respond to higher  $C{O_2}$ concentration by showing increased rates of photosynthesis leading to higher productivity has been used for some greenhouse crops such as tomatoes and bell pepper',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48788,'biology',80,476,960,'During photorespiration, there is a loss of __ of fixed carbon and no energy rich compound is produced.','[{"text": "$10\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$33\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$25\\\\% $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$75\\\\% $", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During photorespiration, RuBisCO acts as oxygenase and binds to ${O_2}$ hence, $C{O_2}$ fixation is decreased. RuBP forms one molecule of PGA and one molecule of phosphoglycolate. There is no synthesis of sugar, nor of ATP. Rather, 1 $C{O_2}$ molecule is released. Hence, there is net loss of  $25\\% $ of fixed oxygen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48789,'biology',80,476,960,'During photorespiration RuBisCO uses __ as substrate.','[{"text": "$C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${O_2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${N_2}O$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${N_2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During photorespiraton, RuBisCO binds to ${O_2}$ by showing its oxygenase property.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48790,'biology',80,477,962,'What causes the decrease in rate of photosynthesis after exposing plant to higher light intensities?','[{"text": "Carotenoids block photosynthesis pathway", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Destruction of chlorophyll molecule due to photo-oxidation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Change in leaf angle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Given question is wrong.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'On exposure to comparatively higher light intensities, chlorophyll present in mesophyll cells undergoes photooxidation and gets destroyed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48791,'biology',80,476,960,'The location of photorespiration is _','[{"text": "Ribosomes, chloroplast, mitochondria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria, chloroplast, peroxisomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ribosomes, chloroplast, peroxisomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ribosomes, mitochondria, nucleosome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Photorespiration takes place at three sitesmitochondria, chloroplast and peroxisome.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48792,'biology',80,476,960,'Why photorespiration is absent in ${C_4}$ plants?','[{"text": "Stomata closes when ${O_2}$ concentration is high", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stomata opens only when $C{O_2}$ concentration is high", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Intracellular $C{O_2}$ concentration is high in bundle sheath and it ensures RuBisCO function as carboxylase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Intracellular $C{O_2}$ concentration is high in bundle sheath and it ensures RuBisCO function as oxygenase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In ${C_4}$ plants photorespiration does not occur. This is because they have a mechanism that increases the concentration of  $C{O_2}$ at the enzyme site. This takes place when the  ${C_4}$ acid from the mesophyll is broken down in the bundle sheath cells to release  $C{O_2}$ – this results in increasing the intracellular concentration of  $C{O_2}$. In turn, this ensures that the RuBisCO functions as a carboxylase minimising the oxygenase activity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48793,'biology',80,476,960,'Read the following events and guess the process.<br>a. RuBisCO binds with ${O_2}$<br>b. Phosphoglycerate and phosphoglycolate is formed<br>c. Release of $C{O_2}$ <br>d. No sugar formation','[{"text": "Photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Digestion of lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photorespiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All these events occur in ${C_2}$ pathway, also known as photorespiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48794,'biology',80,476,960,'Which of the following is considered as photorespiration?','[{"text": "$C{O_2}$ fixation with the help of RuBisCO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ fixation with the help of PEPcase enzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binding of  ${O_2}$ with RuBisCO and subsequent reactions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Photorespiration is that pathway where RuBisCO shows its oxygenase property and binds to ${O_2}$ leading to different results.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48795,'biology',80,476,960,'Select the correct option for photorespiration_','[{"text": "ATP is used", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Release of $C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wastefull in terms of energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Photorespiration is a wasteful process as there is no synthesis of ATP, NADPH or sugars. Instead, 25% of fixed  $C{O_2}$  is released and energy is consumed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48796,'biology',80,477,963,'Which factor is not limited to normal conditions for photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Chlorophyll", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Air availability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ concentration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Chlorophyll is not counted as a limiting factor. It is present inside plants and hence, is not an external factor. Light, temperature, $C{O_2}$ (air availability) are major external limiting factors.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48798,'biology',80,477,962,'How do intermittent light impacts on the rate of photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Causes decrease in rate of photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Causes increase in rate of photosynthesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Rate remains unaffected", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "We can’t predict", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Intermittent light is the type of light which is not steady or continuous. Two types of reactions occur in plants that are: light reaction and dark reaction. Light reactions are faster than dark reactions. Due to this ATP and NADPH accumulate in the plants. Reduction of photosynthesis can occur due to this. In case there is an interruption of light ATP andNADPH are fully consumed. Reduction of  $C{O_2}$ leads to the formation of glucose. Thus, rate of photosynthesis increases.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48799,'biology',80,477,964,'Which of the following plant cannot work efficiently under comparatively higher temperature?','[{"text": "Sugarcane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Maize", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tomatoes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${C_4}$ plants respond to higher temperatures and show higher rate of photosynthesis while ${C_3}$ plants have a much lower temperature optimum. Sugarcane and Maize are ${C_4}$ plants, while tomatoes belong to the ${C_3}$ group.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48800,'biology',80,476,960,'Peroxisome in photorespiration','[{"text": "Helps in oxidation of glyoxylate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helps in breakdown of RuBisCO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helps in the oxidation of glycolate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Photorespiration takes place at three sitesmitochondria, chloroplast and peroxisome. In peroxisome, glycolate is oxidized to glyoxylate and peroxide.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48801,'biology',80,477,965,'i. Water<br>ii. Leaf orientation<br>iii. Temperature<br>iv. Genetic predisposition<br>v. Age of leaves<br>Among the given factors, which factors affect photosynthesis?','[{"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iv, v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii, iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Photosynthesis is under the influence of several factors, both internal (plant) and external. The plant factors include the number, size, age and orientation of leaves, mesophyll cells and chloroplasts, internal  $C{O_2}$ concentration and the amount of chlorophyll. The plant or internal factors are dependent on the genetic predisposition and the growth of the plant.The external factors would include the availability of sunlight, temperature,$C{O_2}$ concentration and water. As a plant photosynthesises, all these factors will simultaneously affect its rate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48802,'biology',80,477,962,'In which of the following plant light is limiting factor?','[{"text": "Wheat farm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plants in dense forest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Plants in a dense forest barely get any exposure to sunlight. Hence, light here is a limiting factor.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48803,'biology',80,477,965,'Identify the wrong statements among given statements.','[{"text": "Water is one of the reactants in the light reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water stress causes the stomata to close hence increasing the $C{O_2}$ availability", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Water stress also makes leaves wilt", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The effect of water as a factor is more through its effect on the plant, rather than directly on photosynthesis.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Water stress causes the stomata to close hence reducing the $C{O_2}$ availability.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48804,'biology',80,477,965,'Which of the following is impact of water stress on plant?','[{"text": "Wilting of leaves", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reducing of surface area of leaf", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reducing the metabolic activity of plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Water stress makes leaves wilt, thus, reducing the surface area of the leaves and their metabolic activity as well.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48805,'biology',80,477,965,'Closure of stomata causes due to_','[{"text": "Water stress", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Extra available water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ ¬attack", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Water stress causes the stomata to close.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48806,'biology',80,477,965,'What is the impact of closure of stomata on photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Increases the $C{O_2}$ availability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Reduces the $C{O_2}$ availability", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Increases  ${O_2}$ availability", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases temperature directly", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Closure of stomata causes decrease in $C{O_2}$ availability.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48807,'biology',80,477,965,'Rather than directly on photosynthesis, where is the effect of water as a factor?','[{"text": "Through effect on the photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Through effect on the plant indirectly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Through effect on the photorespiration indirectly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Through its effect on the plant directly", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Even though water is one of the reactants in the light reaction, the effect of water as a factor is more through its effect on the plant, rather than directly on photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48808,'biology',80,477,964,'As compared to plants in tropical regions, plants in ___ have a lesser temperature optimum for photosynthesis.','[{"text": "Desert", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thermal vents", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Temperate regions", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Tropical plants have a higher temperature optimum than the plants adapted to temperate climates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48809,'biology',80,477,964,'In which of the following climate plants usually show higher temperature optimum w.r.t. each other?','[{"text": "Tropical", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Temperate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tundra", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The temperature optimum for photosynthesis of different plants also depends on the habitat that they are adapted to. Tropical plants have a higher temperature optimum than the plants adapted to temperate climates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48810,'biology',80,477,964,'${C_3}$ plants have a ___ temperature optimum.','[{"text": "Much lower", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Much higher", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Average", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Can’t predict", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_3}$ plants have a much lower temperature optimum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48815,'biology',80,477,963,'What causes higher yield in ${C_3}$ plants?','[{"text": "Carbon dioxide enriched atmosphere", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carbon dioxide defficient atmosphere", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unaffected by  $C{O_2}$ concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sulphur dioxide enriched atmosphere", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Carbon dioxide enriched atmosphere provided by greenhouses leads to higher yields.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48816,'biology',80,477,963,'${C_3}$ plants respond to higher $C{O_2}$ concentration by showing','[{"text": "Increased rates of photosynthesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decreased rate of photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Stagnant rate of photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_3}$  plants respond to higher  $C{O_2}$ concentration by showing increased rates of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48817,'biology',80,477,963,'For which plant group does the current availability of  $C{O_2}$ levels are limiting?','[{"text": "${C_3}$  plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${C_4}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_3}$ and  ${C_4}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Current availability of  $C{O_2}$ levels is limiting to the ${C_3}$ plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48818,'biology',80,477,963,'What leads to higher productivity in some greenhouse crops such as tomatoes and bell pepper?','[{"text": "Decrease in rate of photosynthesis due to higher $C{O_2}$ concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in rate of photosynthesis due to higher  $C{O_2}$ concentration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decrease in rate of photosynthesis due to higher  ${O_2}$ concentration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase in rate of photosynthesis due to higher  ${O_2}$ concentration", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The fact that  ${C_3}$ plants respond to higher $C{O_2}$ concentration by showing increased rates of photosynthesis leading to higher productivity has been used for some greenhouse crops such as tomatoes and bell pepper. They are allowed to grow in carbon dioxide enriched atmosphere that leads to higher yields.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48819,'biology',80,477,963,'${C_3}$ plants respond to increased  $C{O_2}$ concentration and saturation is seen only __','[{"text": "Below 450 $\\\\mu l{L^{ - 1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beyond 450 $\\\\mu l{L^{ - 1}}$.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Beyond 550 $\\\\mu l{L^{ - 1}}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beyond 250 $\\\\mu l{L^{ - 1}}$.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${C_3}$  plants respond to increased  $C{O_2}$ concentration and saturation is seen only beyond 450 µlL-1.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48820,'biology',80,477,963,'At what $C{O_2}$ concentration the ${C_4}$ plants show saturation in rate of photosynthesis?','[{"text": "360 µlL-1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "340 µlL-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "460 µlL-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "440 µlL-1", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_4}$ plants show saturation in rate of $C{O_2}$ fixation at about 360 µlL-1',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48821,'biology',80,477,963,'At low light conditions which plant group responds to high $C{O_2}$ conditions?','[{"text": "${C_3}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_4}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'At low light conditions neither ${C_3}$ nor ${C_4}$ group of plants responds to high $C{O_2}$ conditions.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48822,'biology',80,477,963,'At high light intensities, ____in the rates of photosynthesis, until saturation.','[{"text": "Both ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$plants show decrease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ${C_3}$ plants show increase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants show increase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only ${C_4}$ plants show increase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'At high light intensities, both ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants show increase in the rates of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48823,'biology',80,477,963,'For photosynthesis, beyond 0.05% of $C{O_2}$ concentration in environment $C{O_2}$','[{"text": "Can be damaging over longer periods", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Can be beneficial over longer period", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Can be damaging instantly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Can be beneficial instantly", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Beyond 0.05% of $C{O_2}$ concentration, $C{O_2}$ can become damaging over longer periods.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48824,'biology',80,477,963,'The ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants respond ___ to $C{O_2}$ concentrations.','[{"text": "Exactly similar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Differently", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Alternatively in similar way", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Can’t say", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants respond differently to $C{O_2}$concentrations.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48825,'biology',80,477,963,'Increase in concentration of $C{O_2}$ up to how much per cent can cause an increase in $C{O_2}$ fixation rates?','[{"text": "$0.05$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$0.5$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.02$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Increase in concentration upto 0.05 per cent can cause an increase in $C{O_2}$ fixation rates.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48826,'biology',80,477,963,'Which of the following is the major limiting factor for photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Carbon dioxide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Water", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Temperature", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Carbon dioxide is the major limiting factor for photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48827,'biology',80,477,963,'What is the concentration of $C{O_2}$ in the atmosphere?','[{"text": "Between $0.03$ and $0.04$ per cent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Between $0.01$ and $0.05$ per cent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Between 2 to 5 per cent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.2$ to $0.5$ per cent", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The concentration of  $C{O_2}$ is very low in the atmosphere (between 0.03 and 0.04 per cent).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48828,'biology',80,477,962,'What will happen if we increase the incident light beyond a point','[{"text": "The rejuvenation of chlorophyll and an increase in photosynthesis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The breakdown of chlorophyll and an increase in photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The breakdown of chlorophyll and a decrease in photosynthesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The rejuvenation of chlorophyll and a decrease in photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Increase in incident light beyond a point causes the breakdown of chlorophyll and a decrease in photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48830,'biology',80,477,962,'Light is rarely a limiting factor in nature, except_','[{"text": "For plants in farm exposed to full sunlight", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "For plants in open deserts", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "For plants in shade or in dense forests", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Except for plants in shade or in dense forests, light is rarely a limiting factor in nature.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48831,'biology',80,477,962,'At higher light intensities, the rate of photosynthesis__','[{"text": "Does show sharp fall and becomes limiting factor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Does not show further increase as other factors become limiting.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gradually increases and other factoe becomes imiting", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "We cannot predict.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'At higher light intensities, gradually the rate of photosynthesis does not show further increase as other factors become limiting',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48832,'biology',80,477,962,'Which factor affects the photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Light quality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Light intensity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The duration of exposure to light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Light quality, light intensity and the duration of exposure to light, are all factors that affect photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48833,'biology',80,477,962,'What kind of relationship is shown in the graph by incident light and $C{O_2}$ fixation rates at low light intensities?','[{"text": "Hyperbolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Parabolic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linear", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sigmoid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'There is a linear relationship between incident light and $C{O_2}$ fixation rates at low light intensities.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48834,'biology',80,477,962,'In a green leaf, despite the presence of optimal light, optimal $C{O_2}$ conditions, and suboptimal level of temperature the plant is not photosynthesizing. The leaf will start photosynthesizing __.','[{"text": "If given the sub-optimal $C{O_2}$ conditions", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "If exposed to the sub-optimal level of light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "If given the optimal temperature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Despite the presence of a green leaf and optimal light and $C{O_2}$ conditions, the plant may not photosynthesise if the temperature is very low. This leaf, if given the optimal temperature, will start photosynthesising.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48835,'biology',80,477,961,'Which factor is the factor which directly affects the process if its quantity is changed according to Blackman&rsquo;s law?','[{"text": "The factor with average value", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The factor with its minimal value", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The factor with its maximum value", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The factor other than minimal factor", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The factor which is nearest to its minimal value is the factor which directly affects the process if its quantity is changed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48836,'biology',80,477,961,'Law of limiting factor is applied to_','[{"text": "${N_2}$ absorption by bacteroids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ fixation in plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${O_2}$ toxicity in plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Blackman gave the Law of Limiting Factors in relation to photosynthesis or $C{O_2}$ fixation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48837,'biology',80,477,961,'According to Blackman’s law of limiting factors, if a chemical process is affected by more than one factor, then its rate will be determined by the factor which is nearest to its ___value','[{"text": "Minimal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Maximum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Average", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Blackman’s law states that If a chemical process is affected by more than one factor, then its rate will be determined by the factor which is nearest to its minimal value.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48838,'biology',80,477,961,'Which law comes in effect, when several factors affect any [bio] chemical process?','[{"text": "Law of mass action (1905)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hill’s law of multiple factors (1855)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blackman’s (1905) Law of Limiting Factors", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When several factors affect any [bio] chemical process, Blackman’s (1905) Law of Limiting Factors comes into effect.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48839,'biology',80,477,961,'The scientist who gave law of limiting factor in relation to photosynthesis is _','[{"text": "Blackman", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Otto meyerhop", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "J. Parnas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gustav Embden", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Blackman gave the Law of Limiting Factors in relation to photosynthesis in 1905.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48840,'biology',80,477,961,'Read the following statements carefully and select the option showing correct statements<br>(a) Several factors interact and simultaneously affect photosynthesis or $C{O_2}$ fixation<br>(b) At any point the rate will be determined by the factor available at optimal levels<br>(c) One factor is the major cause or is the one that limits the rate of photosynthesis','[{"text": "b, c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, c", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'At any point the rate will be determined by the factor available at sub-optimal levels.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48841,'biology',80,477,961,'At any point the rate of $C{O_2}$ fixation will be determined by the factor available at __.','[{"text": "Optimal levels", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sub-optimal levels", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "High level", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'At any point the rate of photosynthesis will be determined by the factor available at suboptimal levels.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48842,'biology',80,477,961,'All external and internal factors affect photosynthesis rate__.','[{"text": "Occasionally", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Simultaneously", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Individually", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Periodically", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'As a plant photosynthesises, all these factors both internal and external will simultaneously affect its rate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48843,'biology',80,477,961,'Usually ___ is/are the major cause that limits/limit the $C{O_2}$ fixation rate.','[{"text": "One factor", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It’s unaffected by external/internal factors", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Usually one factor is the major cause or is the one that limits the rate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48844,'biology',80,477,961,'Which of the following factors are included under external factors _<br>(a) number, size, age and orientation of leaves,<br>(b) sunlight,<br>(c) mesophyll cells,<br>(d) chloroplasts,<br>(e) water,<br>(f) the amount of chlorophyll,<br>(g) temperature,<br>(h) internal $C{O_2}$ concentration,<br>(i) external $C{O_2}$ concentration.','[{"text": "b, e, g, i", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a, d, f, h", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a, b, e, d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "f, g, h, i", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The external factors would include the availability of sunlight, temperature, $C{O_2}$ concentration and water. This options are included in b,e,g,i.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48845,'biology',80,477,961,'The plant or internal factors are dependent on the _A_ and _B_.','[{"text": "A - genetic predisposition, B - the growth of the plant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - the growth of the plant, B - insects visiting plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - insects visiting plants, B - the area where plants are grown", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The plant or internal factors are dependent on the genetic predisposition and the growth of the plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48846,'biology',80,477,961,'Read the following factors affecting the photosynthesis carefully and select the number of factors which does not include under external factors_<br>(a) Number, size, age and orientation of leaves,<br>(b) Sunlight,\n(c) Mesophyll cells,<br>(d) Chloroplasts,<br>(e) Water,<br>(f) The amount of chlorophyll,<br>(g) Temperature,<br>(h) Internal $C{O_2}$ concentration','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "7", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The plant factors (internal factors) include the number, size, age and orientation of leaves, mesophyll cells and chloroplasts, internal $C{O_2}$ concentration and the amount of chlorophyll.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48847,'biology',80,477,961,'Which of the following factors influences photosynthesis,','[{"text": "Internal factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "External factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both internal (plant) and external factors", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neither internal (plant) nor external factors", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Photosynthesis is under the influence of several factors, both internal (plant) and external. The plant factors include the number, size, age and orientation of leaves, mesophyll cells and chloroplasts, internal $C{O_2}$ concentration and the amount of chlorophyll. The plant or internal factors are dependent on the genetic predisposition and the growth of the plant.The external factors would include the availability of sunlight, temperature, $C{O_2}$ concentration and water. As a plant photosynthesizes, all these factors will simultaneously affect its rate.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48848,'biology',80,476,960,'To which of the following ${C_4}$ plants show tolerance_','[{"text": "To lower temperatures", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To higher temperatures", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "To high salinity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To low salinity", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${C_4}$ plants show tolerance to higher temperatures.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48849,'biology',80,477,961,'Where does the studying of rate of photosynthesis is very important?','[{"text": "In determining the rate of photorespiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To understand the effect of transpiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To understand the mechanism of virus infection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In determining the yield of plants including crop plants", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The rate of photosynthesis is very important in determining the yield of plants including crop plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48850,'biology',80,476,960,'What is ensured by ${C_4}$ pathway?','[{"text": "The PEPcase functions as a carboxylase minimising the oxygenase activity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The RuBisCO functions as oxygenase minimising the carboxylase activity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The RuBisCO functions as a carboxylase minimising the oxygenase activity", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The PEPcase functions as a carboxylase maximising the oxygenase activity", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${C_4}$ pathway ensures that the RuBisCO functions as a carboxylase minimising the oxygenase activity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48851,'biology',80,476,960,'Why productivity and yields are better in ${C_4}$ plants?','[{"text": "It lacks photorespiration and don’t tolerate high temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It shows photorespiration and can’t tolerate high temperature", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It lacks photorespiration and shows tolerance to high temerature", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It shows photorespiration and tolerates high temperature.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ${C_4}$ plants lack photorespiration, this is why productivity and yields are better in these plants. In addition these plants show tolerance to higher temperatures.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48852,'biology',80,476,960,'What is the purpose, when the ${C_4}$ acid from the mesophyll is broken down in the bundle sheath cells?','[{"text": "In increasing the intercellular concentration of $C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In increasing the intracellularconcentration of $C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "In increasing the intracellular concentration of ${O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In increasing the intercellular concentration of ${O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'When the ${C_4}$ acid from the mesophyll is broken down in the bundle sheath cells to release $C{O_2}$ – this results in increasing the intracellular concentration of $C{O_2}$. In turn, this ensures that the RuBisCO functions as a carboxylase minimizing the oxygenase activity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48853,'biology',80,476,960,'Which of the following is wrong w.r.t photorespiration?','[{"text": "It releases $C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It uses ${O_2}$ molecule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It can be seen in ${C_4}$ plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It can be seen in ${C_3}$ plants", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In ${C_4}$ plants photorespiration does not occur. This is because they have a mechanism that increases the concentration of $C{O_2}$ at the enzyme site.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
