(48854,'biology',80,476,960,'Photorespiration is also known as','[{"text": "${C_3}$ cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_4}$ cycle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${C_2}$ cycle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phosphoglycolate (2C) is formed as one of the products in photorespiration. This is why it is also known as the ${C_2}$ cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48855,'biology',80,476,960,'Photorespiration occurs in _','[{"text": "${C_3}$ plants only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${C_4}$ plants only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both ${C_3}$ and C4 plants.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_4}$  plants lack photorespiration. It occurs in ${C_3}$ plants only.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48856,'biology',80,476,960,'In ${C_4}$ plants photorespiration does not occur because_','[{"text": "They have a mechanism that increases the concentration of ${O_2}$ at the enzyme site.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have a mechanism that increases the concentration of $C{O_2}$ at the enzyme site.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They have a mechanism that decreases the concentration of $C{O_2}$ at the enzyme site.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have a mechanism that increases the concentration of CO at the enzyme site.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In ${C_4}$ plants photorespiration does not occur. This is because they have a mechanism that increases the concentration of $C{O_2}$ at the enzyme site.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48857,'biology',80,476,960,'Read the following statements regarding photorespiration and select the total number of correct statements.<br>(a) In ${C_3}$ plants some ${O_2}$ does bind to RuBisCO, and hence $C{O_2}$ fixation is increased.<br>(b) In the photorespiratory pathway, there is neither synthesis of sugars, nor of ATP.<br>(c) Photorespiration results in the release of  ${O_2}$ with the utilisation of ATP.<br>(d) In the photorespiratory pathway there is no synthesis of ATP or NADPH.<br>(e) The biological function of photorespiration is not known yet.','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "5", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Three statements correct. In ${C_3}$ plants some ${O_2}$ does bind to RuBisCO, and hence  $C{O_2}$ fixation is decreased. Photorespiration results in the release of $C{O_2}$ with the utilisation of ATP',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48858,'biology',80,476,960,'Select the correct option regarding photorespiratory pathway.','[{"text": "Utilisation of  $C{O_2}$ synthesis of ATP, NADPH and release of ${O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Utilisation of ${O_2}$, ATP, synthesis of ATP or NADPH and release of  $C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Utilisation of  $C{O_2}$, ATP, no synthesis of ATP or NADPH and release of  ${O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Utilisation of ${O_2}$, ATP, no synthesis of ATP or NADPH and release of $C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Following the photorespiratory pathway leads to release of $C{O_2}$, utilisation of  ${O_2}$, no synthesis of sugars, ATP or NADPH.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48859,'biology',80,476,960,'Photorespiration results in the release of __A__ with the utilization of __B__.','[{"text": "A - $C{O_2}$, B - NADP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - ${O_2}$, B - ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - $C{O_2}$, B - ATP", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - ${O_2}$, B - NADP", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Photorespiration results in the release of  $C{O_2}$ with the utilisation of ATP.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48860,'biology',80,476,960,'In the photorespiratory pathway, ____.','[{"text": "There is synthesis of sugars but not ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is neither synthesis of sugars, nor of ATP", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "There is synthesis of sugars as well as ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "There is synthesis of ATP but not sugars", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the photorespiratory pathway, there is neither synthesis of sugars, nor of ATP.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48861,'biology',80,476,960,'With which of the following RuBP combines to form one molecule of phosphoglycerate and phosphoglycolate?','[{"text": "${H_2}O$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$CO$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${O_2}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RuBP binds with  ${O_2}$ to form one molecule of phosphoglycerate and phosphoglycolate in a pathway called photorespiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48862,'biology',80,476,960,'During photorespiration instead of being converted to 2 molecules of PGA RuBP forms_','[{"text": "One molecule of phosphoglycerate and phosphoglycolate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One molecule of phosphoenol and phosphoglycerate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One molecule of ethanol and pyruvic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One molecule of succinate and ethanol", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'RuBP instead of being converted to 2 molecules of PGA binds with ${O_2}$ to form one molecule of phosphoglycerate and phosphoglycolate in a pathway called photorespiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48863,'biology',80,476,960,'The root cause for photorespiration is_','[{"text": "Simultaneous binding of $C{O_2}$ and ${O_2}$ with ¬RuBisCO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binding of $C{O_2}$ with RuBisCO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${O_2}$ does bind to RuBisCO", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In ${C_3}$ plants some ${O_2}$ does bind to RuBisCO, and hence $C{O_2}$ fixation is decreased. Here the RuBP instead of being converted to 2 molecules of PGA binds with ${O_2}$ to form one molecule of phosphoglycerate and phosphoglycolate in a pathway called photorespiration.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48864,'biology',80,476,960,'In ${C_3}$ plants some ${O_2}$ does bind to RuBisCO, as result of this__','[{"text": "${O_2}$ fixation is decreased", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ fixation is decreased", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ fixation is increased", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (3)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In ${C_3}$ plants some ${O_2}$ does bind to RuBisCO, and hence $C{O_2}$ fixation is decreased.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48865,'biology',80,476,960,'The binding $C{O_2}$ and  ${O_2}$ with RuBisCO is ___.','[{"text": "Symbiotic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Competitive", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Co-operative", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The binding of  $C{O_2}$ and  ${O_2}$ with RuBisCO is competitive and depends on the relative concentration of the two.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48866,'biology',80,476,960,'What determines between ${O_2}$ and $C{O_2}$ which will bind to&nbsp; RuBisCO?','[{"text": "The relative concentration of ${O_2}$ and $C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The relative concentration of ${O_2}$ and RuBisCO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The relative concentration of $C{O_2}$ and RuBisCO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The relative concentration of ${O_2}$ and CO", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'It is the relative concentration of ${O_2}$ and $C{O_2}$ that determines which of the two will bind to the RuBisCO. RuBisCO has a much greater affinity for $C{O_2}$ when the CO2 : ${O_2}$ is nearly equal.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48881,'biology',80,475,959,'Total number of carboxylation in  ${C_4}$ pathway is?','[{"text": "One", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carboxylation occurs twice in ${C_4}$ cycle. First carboxylation occurs in mesophyll cell where PEP gets fixed to a ${C_4}$ acid (Malic/ Aspartic acid). Second carboxylation occurs in bundle sheath cells where the CO2 released is fixed by Calvin cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48867,'biology',80,476,960,'Read the following statements carefully and select the number of correct statements.<br>(a) RuBisCO is the most abundant enzyme in the world.<br>(b) RuBisCO has a much greater affinity for ${O_2}$ when the $C{O_2}$: ${O_2}$ is nearly equal.<br>(c) The binding  $C{O_2}$ and  ${O_2}$ with RuBisCO is symbiotic.<br>(d) It is the relative concentration of ${O_2}$ and $C{O_2}$ that determines which of the two will bind to the RuBisCO.','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'RuBisCO has a much greater affinity for $C{O_2}$ when the $C{O_2}$: ${O_2}$ is nearly equal. The binding of $C{O_2}$ and ${O_2}$ with RuBisCO is competitive.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48868,'biology',80,476,960,'RuBisCO has a much greater affinity for ___ when the $C{O_2}$: ${O_2}$ is nearly equal.','[{"text": "$C{O_2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${O_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Equal affinity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Data insufficient", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When the amount of  $C{O_2}$ and  ${O_2}$ present in the cell is nearly equal, RuBisCO enzyme shows greater affinity to $C{O_2}$ and acts as carboxylase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48869,'biology',80,476,960,'Which of the following enzyme is most abundant enzyme in the world?','[{"text": "RuBisCO", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "PEPcase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ptyalin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trypsin", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'RuBisCO is the most abundant enzyme in the world.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48870,'biology',80,476,960,'RuBisCO is characterised by the fact that its active site can bind ___.','[{"text": "$C{O_2}$ and  ${O_2}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$C{O_2}$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${O_2}$ only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CO", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'RuBisCO possesses active sites for both ${O_2}$ and $C{O_2}$. It acts as both carboxylase and oxygenase.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48871,'biology',80,476,960,'Which process creates an important difference between ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants?','[{"text": "Respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photorespiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Oneprocess that creates an important difference between ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants is Photorespiration. ${C_4}$ plants lack photorespiration, that is why productivity and yields are better in ${C_4}$ plants compared to ${C_3}$ plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48872,'biology',80,475,959,'The given diagram represents the Hatch and Slack pathway. Name the  $C{O_2}$ acceptor (A) and first stable product (B) of ${C_4}$ cycle respectively.','[{"text": "A - Phosphoglyceric acid, B - Phosphoenol pyruvate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - RuBisCO, B - Phosphoglyceric acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - RuBisCO, B - Oxaloacetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Phosphoenol pyruvate, B - Oxaloacetic acid", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The primary  $C{O_2}$ acceptor of  ${C_4}$ cycle is PEP (phosphoenol pyruvate) which undergoes carboxylation to foem the first stable product OAA (oxaloacetic acid).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/80_48872_question_1.png'),
(48873,'biology',80,475,959,'Which of the following cells of ${C_4}$ plants are prominently loaded with starch?','[{"text": "Mesophyll cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bundle sheath cells", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Epidermal cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Bundle sheath cells contain large parenchymatous cells which can act as storage cells for starch.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48874,'biology',80,475,959,'The given diagram represents Hatch and Slack cycle. Identify the different cells and name the structure which connects these cells (A-C) in ${C_4}$ cycle.','[{"text": "A - Mesophyll cell, B - Plasmodesmata, C - Bundle sheath cell", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Bundle sheath cell, B - Plasmodesmata, C - Mesophyll cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Mesophyll cell , B - Bundle sheath cell , C - Plasmodesmata", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Plasmodesmata, B - Bundle sheath cell, C - Mesophyll cell", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Mesophyll cell<br>B. Plasmodesmata<br>C. Bundle Sheath cell',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/80_48874_question_1.png'),
(48875,'biology',80,475,959,'PEPcase has an advantage over RuBisCO. The advantage is','[{"text": "RuBisCO combines with $C{O_2}$, but PEPcase does not", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RuBisCO combines with ${O_2}$, but PEPcase does not", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "PEPcase is present in both mesophyll cells and bundle sheath cells, but RuBisCO does not", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'PEPcase (PEP carboxylase) is strictly a carboxylase whereas RuBisCO (RuBP carboxylase oxygenase) has active sites for both ${O_2}$ and  $C{O_2}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48876,'biology',80,475,959,'In ${C_4}$ plants, the mesophyll cells and bundle sheath cells are connected with the help of?','[{"text": "Cytoplasmic connection", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Special connecting tissues", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plasmodesmata", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "No connection is present", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Bundle sheath cells and mesophyll cells in ${C_4}$ plants are connected to each other via plasmodesmatic connections.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48877,'biology',80,475,959,'Photosynthetic rate is high in ${C_4}$ plants because','[{"text": "No photorespiration", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Kranz anatomy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photosynthesize in low light intensity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${C_4}$ plants lack photorespiration, that is why productivity and yields are better in these plants. In addition these plants show tolerance to higher temperatures.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48878,'biology',80,475,959,'Which of the following acids are found in mesophyll cells?','[{"text": "Malic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Oxaloacetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aspartic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'PEP undergoes carboxylation to form the ${C_4}$acid OAA (oxaloacetic acid) in the mesophyll cells. It then forms other 4-carbon compounds like malic acid or aspartic acid in the mesophyll cells itself, which are transported to the bundle sheath cells. Hence, all three ${C_4}$ acids are found in mesophyll cells.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48879,'biology',80,475,959,'Which of the following is the secondary acceptor of  $C{O_2}$ in  ${C_4}$ plants?','[{"text": "PEP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RUBP", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "PEPA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "PGA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The primary acceptor of  $C{O_2}$ in ${C_4}$ plants is a 3 carbon molecule, phosphoenol pyruvate (PEP). The secondary acceptor of  $C{O_2}$ in  ${C_4}$ plants is RuBP, which undergoes carboxylation in Calvin pathway.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48882,'biology',80,475,959,'How many of the following statements is/are correct?<br>1. RuBisCO is the most abundant enzyme in plants only<br>2. In ${C_4}$ plants, Photorespiration occurs<br>3. RuBisCO has active sites for $C{O_2}$ only<br>4. The pathway common to ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants is called amphibolic pathway','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RuBisCO is the most abundant enzyme in the world. In ${C_4}$ plants, photorespiration is absent. RuBisCO has active sites for both oxygen and carbon dioxide. The pathway common to ${C_3}$ and ${C_4}$ plants is the Calvin Cycle.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48883,'biology',80,475,959,'The additional number of ATP molecules required by  ${C_4}$ plants for one glucose molecule produced in comparison to ${C_3}$ plants is?','[{"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "24", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "18", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'For the formation of one glucose molecule, ${C_3}$ plants require 18 ATP (3*6 turns of cycle) whereas ${C_4}$ plants require a total of 30 ATP (5* 6 turns of cycle). A difference of 12 ATP molecules exists.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
