(48944,'biology',80,473,956,'Match the following Columns I & II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Photosystem I<br>B. Light reaction<br>C. Photosystem II<br>D. Dark reaction</div><div class="column-right">P. Wavelength 680nm<br>Q. Light independent reaction<br>R. Photo-chemical phase<br>S. Wavelength 700nm</div></div>','[{"text": "A-P , B-R , C-S , D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P , B-Q , C-R , D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S , B-R , C-P , D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S , B-Q , C-P , D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A. Photosystem I - S. Wavelength 700nm<br>B. Light reaction - R. Photochemical phase<br>C. Photosystem II - P. Wavelength 680nm<br>D. Dark reaction - Q. Light independent reaction',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48945,'biology',80,473,956,'In chemiosmotic hypothesis for energy generation in chloroplast -','[{"text": "Electron transport carriers set up a proton gradient", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Electron transport carriers set up a electron gradient", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Proton transport carriers set up a proton gradient", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The electron transport carriers use energy of moving electron in uphill direction to form ATP", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to chemiosmotic hypothesis, electron carriers set up a proton gradient across the membrane of thylakoid. After this gradient is broken, enough energy is released to synthesise a molecule of ATP.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48946,'biology',80,473,956,'In photosynthesis, energy for attaching phosphate to ADP in photosystem II comes from','[{"text": "Oxidation of glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sunlight directly", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A proton gradient", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Substrate-level phosphorylation", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A proton gradient is created between the stroma of chloroplast and lumen of thylakoid. ATP synthase has a channel that allows diffusion of protons back across the membrane; this releases enough energy to activate ATP synthase enzyme that catalyses the formation of ATP',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48947,'biology',80,473,956,'The break down of the gradient provides enough energy to cause a conformational change in the _________of the ATP synthase, which makes the enzyme synthesise several molecules of energypacked ATP','[{"text": "PQ", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{F_0}$ particle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{F_1}$ particle", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The break down of the gradient provides enough energy to cause a conformational change in the $C{F_1}$ particle of the ATP synthase, which makes the enzyme synthesise several molecules of energypacked ATP.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
