(48952,'biology',80,473,956,'The ATP synthase of chloroplast consists of','[{"text": "$C{F_0}$ and $C{F_1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$C{F_1}$ and $C{F_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$C{F_0}$ and $C{F_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The ATP synthase enzyme consists of two parts: one called the $C{F_0}$ is embedded in the thylakoid membrane and forms a transmembrane channel that carries out facilitated diffusion of protons across the\nmembrane. The other portion is called $C{F_1}$ and protrudes on the outer surface of the thylakoid membrane on the side that faces the stroma.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
