(48970,'biology',80,473,955,'&nbsp;How many ${{\\rm{H}}^ + }$ ions are formed from 6 water molecules during non-cyclic photophsophorylation?','[{"text": "12", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "24", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "36", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "48", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Splitting of water takes place by the following reaction -<br>${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{O}} \\to {\\rm{4}}{{\\rm{H}}^ + }{\\rm{ + }}{{\\rm{O}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ + 4e}}$&minus;2 water molecules form 4${H^ + }$ ions. Therefore, 6 water molecules will result in the formation of 12${H^ + }$ ions during non-cyclic phosphorylation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
