(48989,'biology',80,473,952,'Photosystem I (PS I) and Photosystem II (PS II) are named in the___','[{"text": "Sequence of their discovery", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sequence in which they function during the light reaction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 ans 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'&nbsp;Photosystem I (PS I) and Photosystem II (PS II) are named in the sequence of their discovery.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48990,'biology',80,473,952,'Photosystems (PS) are made up of which of the following?','[{"text": "Reaction centre", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antennae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pigments", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'PS are made up of one reaction centre surrounded by number of light harvesting pigments/ antennae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48991,'biology',80,473,952,'Identify the two photosystems<br>i. Chl -a 700 &emsp; ii. Chl -a 680<br>iii. Chl -b 700 &emsp; iv. Chl -b 680<br>v. Chl -a 650','[{"text": "i, iii, iv,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii, iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i, ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "iii, iv", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The photosynthetic units are called photosystem-I/Chl-a 700 and photosystem-II/ Chl-a 680.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48992,'biology',80,473,952,'Light reaction and photochemical phase includes','[{"text": "Light absorption", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP and NADPH formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Water splitting and release of oxygen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Light reactions or the ‘Photochemical’ phase include light absorption, water splitting, oxygen release, and the formation of highenergy chemical intermediates, ATP and NADPH.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48993,'biology',80,473,952,'Light Harvesting complexes (LHCs) are','[{"text": "Present within PS-I and PS-II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Huge no.of chlorphyll-a", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hundreds of pigment molecules bound to proteins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The pigments are organised into two discrete photochemical light harvesting complexes (LHC) within the Photosystem I (PS I) and Photosystem II (PS II). The LHC are made up of hundreds of pigment molecules\nbound to proteins. Each photosystem has all the pigments (except one molecule of chlorophyll a) forming a light harvesting system also called antennae.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48994,'biology',80,472,951,'Following graph shows action spectrum and absorption spectrum. Identify in which regions of the spectrum, most of the photosynthesis take place?','[{"text": "Blue light only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red light only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The peaks at red and blue light wavelengths depict that maximum photosynthesis takes place there.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/80_48994_question_1.png'),
(48995,'biology',80,472,951,'The following diagram shows different types of graph (A-C). Identify the graph showing action spectrum of photosynthesis?','[{"text": "B only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A. Absorption spectrum of chlorophyll a,b and carotenoids<br>B. Action spectrum of photosynthesis<br>C. Action spectrum of photosynthesis superimposed on absorption spectrum of chlorophyll a.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/80_48995_question_1.png'),
(48996,'biology',80,472,951,'Match the following Columns I & II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Xanthophylls, Carotenoids<br>B. Chlorophyll-a,b<br>C. Emerson effect<br>D. Chlorophyll-a</div><div class="column-right">P. Accessory pigments<br>Q. Essential pigments<br>R. Photosystems<br>S. Reaction centre</div></div>','[{"text": "A-Q , B-P , C-R , D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P , B-Q , C-R , D-S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-P , B-R , C-S , D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R , B-S , C-P , D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A. Xanthophylls, Carotenoids - P. Accessory pigments<br>B. Chlorophyll-a,b - Q. Essential pigments<br>C. Emerson effect - R. Photosystems<br>D. Chlorophyll-a - S. Reaction centre<br>Emerson effect is the increase in the rate of photosynthesis after chloroplasts are exposed to the light of wavelength 680nm and more. The effect was an early evidence that two photosystems, processing different wavelengths cooperate in photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48997,'biology',80,472,951,'Maximum amount of chlorophyll is found in _','[{"text": "Green stems", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Quantasomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lumen of thylakoid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green leaf", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Quantasomes are particles found in the thylakoid membrane of chloroplasts. They possess the highest amount of chlorophyll there is.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48998,'biology',80,472,951,'Match the following Columns I & II and choose the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Chlorophyll-a<br>B. Xanthophylls<br>C. Chlorophyll-b<br>D. Carotenoids</div><div class="column-right">P. Yellow-green<br>Q. Yellow<br>R. Yellow to Yellow orange<br>S. Blue-green</div></div>','[{"text": "A-S , B-Q , C-R , D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S , B-R , C-Q , D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P , B-Q , C-R , D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S , B-Q , C-P , D-R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A. Chlorophyll-a - S. Blue-green<br>B. Xanthophylls - Q. Yellow<br>C. Chlorophyll-b - P. Yellow-green<br>D. Carotenoids - R. Yellow to yellow orange.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(48999,'biology',80,472,951,'What is the wavelength of radiations in visible spectrum?','[{"text": "400-700 nm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "400-800 nm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "390-760 nm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "760-390 nm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Visible spectrum ranges from 400nm to 700nm. The VIBGYOR lies here.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49000,'biology',80,472,951,'Which of the following is the main function of Xanthophylls?','[{"text": "Helps the plant from photo-damage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Not an accessory pigment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helps in photosynthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Helps in photo-respiration", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Xanthophylls are accessory pigments. They not only enable a wider range of wavelength of incoming light to be utilized for photosynthesis but also protect chlorophyll-a from photooxidation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49001,'biology',80,472,951,'Which of the following is not an accessory pigment?','[{"text": "Carotenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phycobilin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll-b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll-a", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Phycobilins are light-capturing pigments found in cyanobacteria. Chlorophyll-a is the chief pigment in autotrophic organisms. Xanthophylls, chlorophyll-b and carotenoids are all accessory pigments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49002,'biology',80,472,951,'Which light is absorbed more by chlorophyll-b?','[{"text": "Blue green", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blue", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Orange", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chlorophyll b absorbs mostly blue and yellow light',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49003,'biology',80,472,951,'A chromatographic paper is shown to you and it is asked that which of the following pigments is represented by the yellow orange colour band on the paper?','[{"text": "Chlorophyll-b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Porphyrin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carotenes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anthocyanin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Carotenes appear yellow to yellow-orange in colour on chromatogram.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49004,'biology',80,472,951,'A graph that plots the effect of different wavelengths of light on the rate of photosynthesis is called?','[{"text": "Action spectrum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Split spectrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Continuous spectrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Line spectrum", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The graphical curve showing the relative rates of photosynthesis at different wavelengths of light is known as the action spectrum.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49005,'biology',80,472,951,'Xanthophylls protect chlorophyll-a from ___','[{"text": "Photo-reduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photo-respiration", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Photo-oxidation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Accessory pigments like xanthophylls protect chlorophyll-a from photooxidation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49006,'biology',80,472,951,'Absorption spectrum of chlorophyll-a and the action spectrum of photosynthesis is identical because chlorophyll-a','[{"text": "Absorbs the red and violet light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Absorbs the red and blue light", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Adsorbs the minimum light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than one option is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Action spectrum of photosynthesis corresponds closely to absorption spectra of chlorophyll a showing that chlorophyll a is the chief pigment. It absorbs red and blue light, wavelengths at which most photosynthesis\ntakes place.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49007,'biology',80,472,951,'Accessory pigments enable a _____ range of wavelength of incoming light to be utilized for photosynthesis','[{"text": "Wider", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Narrower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Accessory pigments not only enable a wider range of wavelength of incoming light to be utilised for photosynthesis but also protect chlorophyll-a from photo-oxidation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49008,'biology',80,472,951,'Select the incorrect statement from the following?','[{"text": "Most of the photosynthesis takes place in the blue and red regions of the spectrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some photosynthesis does takes place at the other wavelengths of the visible spectrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll is the accessory pigment responsible for trapping light", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Chlorophyll-a is the major pigment responsible for trapping light.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49009,'biology',80,472,951,'Which of the given pigment does not play role in photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Xanthophyll", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carotenes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phycocyanin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anthocyanin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Xanthophyll and Carotenoids are accessory photosynthetic pigments. Phycocyanin is a blue photosynthetic pigment in cyanobacteria. Anthocyanin is a type of flavonoid. It is responsible for the coloration of fruits,\nvegetables, flowers and grains. It plays no role in photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49010,'biology',80,472,951,'Accessory pigments also absorb light and transfer the energy to _','[{"text": "Chlorophyll-b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll-a", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chlorophyll-c", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "More than one option is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Other thylakoid pigments like chlorophyll b, xanthophylls and carotenoids, which are called accessory pigments, also absorb light and transfer the energy to chlorophyll a.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
