(49013,'biology',80,472,951,'Chlorophyll is soluble in _','[{"text": "Alcohol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ether", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chlorophyll is soluble in organic solvents like alcohol, ether and acetone. As chlorophyll contains a long hydrocarbon (phytol) tail, it is also soluble in lipids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49014,'biology',80,472,951,'Green plants reflect ____ light','[{"text": "Green", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Red", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red and Violet", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'An objects appears to be in the colour complementary to the one it most strongly absorbs. Green plants absorb red light most efficiently and reflect back green light.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49015,'biology',80,472,951,'Which is the chief pigment associated with photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Chlorophyll-a", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Carotene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chlorophyll-b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xanthophyll", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the absorption spectrum, the wavelengths at which there is maximum absorption by chlorophyll a, i.e., in the blue and the red regions, also shows higher rate of photosynthesis. Hence, we can conclude that\nchlorophyll a is the chief pigment associated with photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49016,'biology',80,472,951,'Higher rate of photosynthesis is shown by which light?','[{"text": "Blue light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red light", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Green light", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Blue and red wavelengths show maximum absorption and hence a higher rate of photosynthesis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
