(49373,'biology',97,1195,2857,'Why foreign DNA cannot pass through cell membrane?','[{"text": "DNA is hydrophobic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA is hydrophilic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA is made of nucleotides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA is negatively charged", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'DNA is a hydrophilic molecule, which is negatively charged. Cell membrane or plasma membrane is hydrophobic. It mainly comprises lipids which do not allow hydrophilic molecules such as DNA to cross the cell membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
