(49660,'biology',94,791,1700,'Match the columns I and II wrt tRNA.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Anticodon loop<br>B. Amino acid acceptor end<br>C. Secondary structure<br>D. Actual structure</div><div class="column-right">P. It binds to specific amino acids<br>Q. Clover-leaf<br>R. Complementary<br>S. Inverted L</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{S}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49661,'biology',94,792,1701,'Translocation involves','[{"text": "The movement of the mRNA strand one triplet length in the A-site", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The release of the unattached tRNA from the E-site", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The movement of the tRNA from the A-site to the P-site", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During the translocation process of the elongation phase of protein synthesis, the mRNA is ahead of one codon, and is paired for movement of tRNA from the ribosomal A-site (i.e., aminoacyl) to P-site (i.e., peptidyl) and from P to E (exit ) sites, in a sequence catalyzed by elongation factor EF-G.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49662,'biology',94,792,1701,'Translation is','[{"text": "Formation of enzymes only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Protein formation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Formation of DNA from DNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Formation of RNA from DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Translation is the process of synthesizing protein from the present codon in a messenger RNA (mRNA) molecule .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49663,'biology',94,792,1701,'Protein synthesis requires','[{"text": "Sugars", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aminoacids", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fatty acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleotides", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Protein synthesis requires amino acids, m RNA, t RNA, ribosomes, energy, enzymes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49664,'biology',94,792,1701,'Protein synthesis in an animal cell occurs','[{"text": "Only on the ribosomes present in cytosol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "On ribosomes present in cytoplasm as well as in mitochondria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only on ribosomes attached to the nuclear envelope and endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "On ribosomes present in the nucleolus as well as in cytoplasm", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Protein synthesis in an animal cell occurs in cytoplasmic ribosomes, endoplasmic reticulum, in mitochondria - where greater energy is liberated during respiration membrane.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
