(49665,'biology',94,792,1701,'Which one of the following pairs is correctly matched<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Codon-site of tRNA molecule that contains complementary bases to the triple code on the mRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Translation-process by which protein is synthesized", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Translation -process by which mRNA carries the information from nucleus to the ribosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Translation-process by which protein is synthesized',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49666,'biology',94,792,1701,'The cellular factory / Organelle responsible for the synthesis of proteins is','[{"text": "Ribosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Golgi body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Centriole", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cellular factory/Organelle responsible for the synthesis of proteins is Ribosome',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49667,'biology',94,792,1701,'During protein synthesis, the correct amino acid is brought to the ribosome and inserted in correct sequence in the growing polypeptide chain by','[{"text": "Base pairing between DNA and tRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Interaction between two anticodons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Base pairing between mRNA codons and anticodon in tRNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Interaction between two triplet codons", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Translation is carried out on ribosomes and it is the last step on the way from DNA to protein. Thefirst component a mRNA directs the synthesis of proteins and the information present in the nucleotide sequence of the mRNA is read as triplets, called codons. In this each word stands for one amino acid. tRNA, the second component ia a specialized RNA molecule which carries an amino acid in one end and has a triplet of nucleotides, an anticodon in the other end. The anticodon of a tRNA base pairs i.e., forms chemical bonds, with the mRNA\'s three letter codon. Therefore, the tRNA plays the role of translator between mRNA and protein by bringing the specific amino acid coded by the mRNA codon.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49668,'biology',94,792,1701,'In protein synthesis during translation, tRNA','[{"text": "Reads the genetic code", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brings specific amino acids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During translation, the tRNAs carry amino acids to the ribosomes and also join their complementary codon in protein synthesis. The role of tRNA is to specify which sequence from the genetic code corresponds to which amino acid.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49669,'biology',94,792,1701,'In bacteria, which of the following plays a structural and catalytic role in translation process?','[{"text": "$23 \\\\mathrm{~S}$ m-RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$23 \\\\mathrm{~S}$ r-RNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$23 \\\\mathrm{~S}$ t-RNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$23 \\\\mathrm{~S}$  DNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The ribosome acts as a catalyst (23S rRNA in bacteria is the enzyme- ribozyme) for the formation of peptide bond.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49670,'biology',94,792,1701,'Which among the following process occur(s) during charging or aminoacylation of RNA?','[{"text": "Activation of amino acids in the presence of ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Activation of m-RNA by ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linking of amino acids to their cognate tRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Amino acids are activated in the presence of ATP and linked to their cognate tRNA -a process commonly called as charging of tRNA or aminoacylation of tRNA',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49671,'biology',94,792,1701,'In bacteria, catalytic RNA is found in','[{"text": "70S subunit of ribosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "50S subunit of ribosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "60S subunit of ribosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "40S subunit of ribosome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In bacteria, catalytic RNA is found in 50S subunit of ribosome',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49672,'biology',94,792,1701,'In the protein synthesis, tRNA carrying the amino acid enters from which site of the ribosome?','[{"text": "P-site", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-site", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "There is no such specificity", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Exit site", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In the protein synthesis, tRNA carrying the amino acid enters from A-site of the ribosome.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49673,'biology',94,792,1701,'The order and sequence of amino acids are defined by the sequences of the bases in','[{"text": "ATP", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "mRNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "tRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "srRNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The order and sequence of amino acids are defined by the sequences of the bases in mRNA',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49674,'biology',94,792,1701,'Match the columns I and II WRT Translation.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Ribosome<br>B. Release factor<br>C. Start codon<br>D. UTRs</div><div class="column-right">P. Recognised only by the initiator tRNA<br>Q. Moves from codon to codon<br>R. Binds to the stop codon<br>S. Present at the both 5’ -end and 3’ -end</div></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{S}$',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49675,'biology',94,792,1701,'Formation of a Peptide bond requires energy. Therefore, amino acids are activated in the presence______ of and linked to their cognate tRNA - a process commonly called as charging of tRNA or____ to be more specific.','[{"text": "GTP, aminoacylation of tRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP, aminoacylation of mRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP, amination of tRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ATP, aminoacylation of tRNA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'ATP, aminoacylation of tRNA',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
