(49697,'biology',94,793,1702,'In <i>E.coli</i> , \'lac\' operon is induced by','[{"text": "$\\\\beta$-galactosidase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i\' gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Promoter gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactose", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In <i>Escherichia coli</i>, the transport and metabolism of lactose is done by operon. The lac operon of E. coli has genes associated in lactose metabolism. This happens only when glucose is absent and lactose is present.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49698,'biology',94,793,1702,'Lactose is the substrate for the lac enzyme $\\beta$-galactosidase, it regulates','[{"text": "Switching off of the operon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Switching on of the operon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synthesis of polypeptide chain", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Regulation of lac operon by repressor is referred to as negative regulation. Lac operon is under control of positive regulation as well, but it is beyond the scope of discussion at this level',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
