(49700,'biology',94,793,1702,'Lac Operon is an example of','[{"text": "Inducible operon", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Repressible operon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Overlapping genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Lac operon is a negatively controlled inducible operon where the inducer molecule is allolactose. It utilizes lactose as an energy source and is activated when glucose is low and lactose is present.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49701,'biology',94,793,1702,'Which of the following gene is not a structural gene in the lac operon?','[{"text": "Lac a", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lac i", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lac z", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lac y", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Lac operon is a operon required for the transport and metabolism of lactose in <i>E. coli</i> and many other bacteria. Lac operon consists of one regulatory gene, common promoter, three structural genes and a operator. Structural genes are lac a, lac y and lac Z.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49702,'biology',94,793,1702,'Select the correct option<br>i. z gene codes $\\rightarrow$ beta-galactosidase $(\\beta$-gal $)$<br>ii. y gene codes $\\rightarrow$ permease<br>iii. a gene $\\rightarrow$ transacetylase<br>iv. i gene $\\rightarrow$ repressor of the lac operon','[{"text": "Only i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only ii,iii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only i, ii, iii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
