(49704,'biology',94,793,1702,'Select the correct option from the following statements<br>A. Lactose is the inducer<br>B. A very high level of expression of lac operon has to be present in the cell all the time, otherwise lactose cannot enter the cells.<br>C. The repressor protein binds to the operator region of the operon and prevents RNA polymerase from transcribing the operon.<br>D. In the presence of an inducer, such as lactose or allolactose, the repressor is activated by interaction with the inducer','[{"text": "A, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, C", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'B. is wrong A very low level of expression of lac operon has to be present in the cell all the time, otherwise lactose cannot enter the cells. $\\mathrm{D}$ is wrong : In the presence of an inducer, such as lactose or allolactose, the repressor is inactivated by interaction with the inducer.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
