(49711,'biology',94,793,1702,'Inducible enzymes are','[{"text": "Usually involved in the anabolic pathways", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produced when an activator molecule enhances the attachment of RNA polymerase with the operator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Produced when a small molecule inactivates the repressor protein", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Regulated by inherently inactive repressor", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Inducible enzymes or an adaptive enzymes are the enzymes which are produced in response to a specific substrate, and produced only when required. It is also a part of the Operon model that demonstrates a technique for genes to go to turn "on" and "off" position. The gene is caused to turn on by the inducer and the repressor protein causes the gene to turn off. This repressor can be removed by the inducer, directing genes to back on.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
