(49791,'biology',94,782,1687,'$1.7 \\mathrm{~m}$ double helical DNA will have base pairs_____','[{"text": "$3.4 \\\\times 10^{9}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.7 \\\\times 10^{9}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.7 \\\\times 10^{5}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$5 \\\\times 10^{9}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The length between two base pair is $0.34 \\mathrm{~nm}$. Total length of double helix DNA = total number of base pairs * distance between two bpHere, total no. of base pair is unknown, let us assume it to be ${\\rm{y}}{\\rm{.}}\\,{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.7\\,m = Y \\times 0}}{\\rm{.34 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{6}}}$<br>${\\rm{Y = 0}}{\\rm{.34 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{/1}}{\\rm{.7 = 5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{9}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
