(49794,'biology',94,782,1687,'Read the following statements and find out the incorrect statement.<br>I. The length of DNA is usually defined as number of nucleotides or base pairs present in it.<br>II. In DNA, every nucleotide residue has an addition -OH group present at $2^{\\prime}$ position in the deoxyribose.<br>III. Nuclein was discovered and named by in Meischer 1969.<br>IV. Adenine pair with Thymine and Guanine with Cytosine through H-bonds. This makes one strand complementary to the other.<br>v. The position of double helical model of DNA was also based on the observation of Erwin Charagaff.','[{"text": "II, III and V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and V only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'DNA as an acidic substance present in nucleus was first identified by Friedrich Meischer in 1869. He named it as \'Nuclein\'. In RNA, every nucleotide residue has an additional-OH group present at 2\'-position in the ribose.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49795,'biology',94,782,1687,'Choose the correct statement','[{"text": "Haploid content of human DNA is $4.6 \\\\times 10^{6} \\\\mathrm{bp}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A nitrogenous base is linked to pentose sugar through phosphodiester linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X-ray difdfraction data of Maurice Wilkins and Rosalind Franklin was the basis of Watson and Cricks model.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA as an acidic substance was first identified by Watson and Crick", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In 1953 James Watson and Francis Crick, based on the X-ray difdfraction data produced by Maurice Wilkins and Rosalind Franklin gave the Double helical model of DNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
