(49801,'biology',94,792,1701,'An eukaryotic cell, post transcription prepares itself for synthesis of proteins, so as to meet its metabolic needs. The modified mRNA translates into proteins through a sequential stepwise process. Identify the correct sequence of steps in translation and select the correct option.<br>i. Amino acylation of tRNA<br>ii. Attachment of larger subunit of ribosome to mRNA-tRNA complex.<br>iii. Linking of adjacent amino acid to form a polypeptide<br>iv. Codon anticodon reaction between RNA and amino acyl tRNA complex<br>v. Attachment of mRNA with smaller subunit of ribosome','[{"text": "i $\\\\rightarrow$ ii $\\\\rightarrow$ v $\\\\rightarrow$ iv $\\\\rightarrow$ iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii $\\\\rightarrow$ iii $\\\\rightarrow$ i $\\\\rightarrow$ iv $\\\\rightarrow$ v", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i $\\\\rightarrow$ v $\\\\rightarrow$ iv $\\\\rightarrow$ ii $\\\\rightarrow$ iii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii $\\\\rightarrow$ iv $\\\\rightarrow v \\\\rightarrow$ i $\\\\rightarrow$ iii", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{i} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{v} \\rightarrow$ iv $\\rightarrow$ ii $\\rightarrow$ iii is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49804,'biology',94,788,1695,'Given below is the sequence of noncoding strand of DNA in a transcription unit<br>3\'-ATTACACTATTAGC-5\'<br>Write the sequence of<br>(a) the mRNA<br>(b) its complementary strand','[{"text": "(a) 5\'-TAATGTGATAATCG-3 \'<br>(b) 5\'-UAAUGUGAUAAUCG-3\'", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a) 3\'-ATTACACTATTAGC-5\'<br>(b) 5\'-UAAUGUGAUAAUCG-3\'", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a) 5\'-UAAUGUGAUAAUCG-3\'<br>(b) 5\'-TAATGTGATAATCG-3\'", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(a) 3\'-ATTACACTATTAGC-5\'<br>(b) 5\'-TAATGTGATAATCG-3\'", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'(a) 5\'-UAAUGUGAUAAUCG-3\'<br>(b) 5\'-TAATGTGATAATCG-3 \'',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49805,'biology',94,792,1701,'How many ATP & GTP molecules are respectively used for each amino acid incorporated in peptide chain?','[{"text": "2 & 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 & 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 & 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 & 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'One GTP is hydrolyzed to GDP as each successive amino acid-tRNA complex attaches to the A site of the ribosome. A second GTP is broken down to GDP as the ribosome moves to each new codon in the mRNA. One ATP is hydrolyzed to AMP during amino acid activation. Thus, the formation of each peptide bond uses 3 high-energy molecules, one ATP and two GTP',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
