(49809,'biology',94,782,1687,'Phosphodiester bond of a segment of ds DNA having 1000 b.p will have?','[{"text": "1000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2000", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1998", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3000", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phosphodiester bond is between PO4group and sugar. Since our DNA is ${\\rm{1000}}\\,{\\rm{bp}}$ long, it means it has 1000 bases each strand. And, each base is connected to sugar. Each sugar is bonded to other by phosphodiester bond except the first one ( $5^{\\prime}$ end) and last one ( no phosphate just OH $3^{\\prime}$ ). So, the number of phosphodiester bond is 999. We need to double this number because 1000 bp DNA means double stranded DNA. So, total Phosphodiester Bond  =999+999=1998',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
