(49817,'biology',94,782,1687,'In the carbon skeleton of the pentose sugar in DNA, what is the attachment point of a base to form a nucleoside?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{4}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{C}_{3}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Deoxyribose is the sugar found in the backbone of DNA. $\\mathrm{C}_{1}$ of this sugar is linked to the $\\mathrm{N}_{1}$ of a pyrimidine or the $\\mathrm{N}_{9}$ of a purine base by a $\\beta$ - N-glycosidic linkage.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49818,'biology',94,782,1687,'If the DNA of humans contains $3 \\times 10^{9} \\mathrm{bp}$, and if an Okazaki fragment, on average, is $2000 \\mathrm{bp}$ long, how many initiation points for RNA primase are present in the genome?','[{"text": "$3.5 \\\\times 10^{6}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.5 \\\\times 10^{6}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1.5 \\\\times 10^{9}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.0 \\\\times 10^{6}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Divide the total number of base pairs by the size of the Okazaki fragment or$\\left(3 \\times 10^{9}\\right) /\\left(2 \\times 10^{3}\\right)=1.5 \\times 10^{6} \\text { initiation sites. }$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49819,'biology',94,782,1687,'The single stranded DNA of phage $\\phi \\times 174$ has 5400 nucleotides. If average protein contains 200 amino acids, how many different proteins could this phage DNA code ?','[{"text": "100", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "90", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "9", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "27", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'5400 nucleotides in DNA will form $5400 / 3=1800$ codons. 200 aminoacids, i.e., 200 codons form one protein and therefore, $1800 / 200=9$ proteins can be formed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
