(49920,'biology',94,782,1687,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> DNA and RNA is long polymers of Nucleotides.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> A nucleoside has three components - a nitrogenous base, a pentose sugar and a phosphate group.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'DNA and RNA are made up of many monomers called nucleotides, which are linked each other by phosphodiester bonds.       Nucleoside has only two components nitrogen base and pentose sugar.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49921,'biology',94,782,1687,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In DNA two chains have antiparallel polarity.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> One chain has the polarity 5\' to 3\' and the other chain has 3 \' to 5 \'.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Doble helix DNA has at one end a free phosphate moiety at $5^{\\prime}$-end of sugar, which is referred to as 5\'-end of polynucleotide chain and other end of the polymer the sugar has a free $\\mathrm{OH}$ of 3 \' $\\mathrm{C}$ group which is referred to as 3 \' -end of the polynucleotide chain.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49955,'biology',94,789,1698,'Which one of the following pairs of codons is correctly matched with their function or the sign for the particular amino acid?<br><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "GUU, GCU - Alanine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AUG, ACG - Start / Methionine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "UUA, UCA - Leucine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "UAG, UGA - Stop", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'UAG and UGA are stop codons (or termination codon) in RNA. In the standard genetic code, there are three different stop codons within messenger RNA viz., UAG, UAA, UGA.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49922,'biology',94,782,1687,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Francis Crick proposed the Central dogma in molecular biology.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In some viruses the flow of information is in reverse direction','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Generally central dogma of molecular biology states that the genetic information flows from DNA to RNA to Protein. But in Viruses flow of information is in reverse direction, that is from RNA to DNA and it is called Reverse transcription.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49923,'biology',94,783,1688,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Euchromatin is said to be transcriptionally active.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Because it is more densely packed and stains dark.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Euchromatin is said to be transcriptionally active, because it is loosely condensed and accessible by RNA polymerase.  More densely packed and stains darkly is Heterochromatin.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49924,'biology',94,784,1689,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Oswald Avery, Colin MacLeod and Maclyn McCarty concluded that DNA is the hereditary material.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Proteases and RNAses did not affect transformation, but digestion with DNase did inhibit transformation.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Oswald Avery, Colin MacLeod and Maclyn McCarty discovered that proteindigesting enzymes (proteases) and RNAdigesting enzymes (RNases) did not affect transformation, so the transforming substance was not a protein or RNA. But Digestion with DNase did inhibit transformation, suggesting that the DNA caused the transformation. They concluded that DNA is the hereditary material.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49925,'biology',94,785,1690,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> DNA is a better genetic material.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> DNA chemically is less reactive and structurally more stable when compared to RNA.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'DNA is more stable than RNA, because in DNA the two strands being complementary if separated by heating come together, when appropriate conditions are provided. Further, 2\'-OH group present at every nucleotide in RNA is a reactive group and makes RNA labile and easily degradable. RNA is also now known to be catalytic, hence reactive.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49926,'biology',94,792,1701,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In prokaryotes during translation or Protein synthesis ribosomes form polysomes.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Different ribosomes of polysomes utilize a single strand of mRNA and produce many copies of same protein.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Many ribosomes attach to single mRNA and it is called Polysome and in polysomes many ribosomes attach and translate single mRNA and produce many copies of same protein.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49927,'biology',94,787,1693,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Watson and Crick suggested semiconservative DNA replication.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Matthew Meselson and Franklin Stahl performed experimental proof for semi conservative replication.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In semi conservative mode, after completion of replication, each DNA molecule would have one parental and one newly synthesized strand.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49928,'biology',94,788,1696,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In prokaryotes transcription and translation take place in the same compartment.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In bacteria the mRNA does not require any processing to become active.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In prokaryotes transcription and translation are coupled, because in prokaryotes mRNA does not require any modification and in bacteria there is no separation of cytosol and nucleus in bacteria (no need of mRNA transport).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49929,'biology',94,788,1697,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> hnRNA is smaller than mRNA.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> hnRNA is made up of only introns.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Heterogeneous nuclear RNA (hnRNA) is larger than mRNA, because hnRNA is made up of exons and introns and during post transcriptional modifications introns are specificaaly removed by splicing process, hence mRNA becomes smaller than hnRNA.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49930,'biology',94,789,1698,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Genetic code is degenerate.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> All amino acids are coded by more than one codon.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In genetic code there are 64 codons, in these 61 codes for amino acids called sense codons and 3 codons do not code for any amino acids, hence they function as stop codons or Non sense codons.     61 codons code for 20 amino acids, means some amino acids are coded by more than one codon, hence the genetic code is degenerate.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49931,'biology',94,788,1697,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Association of RNA polymerase with certain factors alters the specificity RNA polymerase.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> RNA polymerase associates transiently with initiation-factor $(\\sigma)$ and termination-factor $(\\rho)$ to initiate and terminate the transcription, respectively.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When RNA polymerase associates with $(\\sigma)$ factor it initiate transcription and when it associates with<br>( $\\rho)$ factor it terminates transcription.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49932,'biology',94,790,1699,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Sickle cell anemia is due to point mutation.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> In sickle cell anemia change of single base pair in the gene for beta globin chains that result in the change of amino acid residue glutamate to valine.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Point mutation is the change of single base pair in the gene.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49933,'biology',94,793,1702,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In prokaryotes structural gene in a transcription unit is polycistronic type. <br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> A single-strand of mRNA is capable of forming different polypeptide chains in prokaryotes.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Cistron as a segment of DNA coding for a polypeptide, the structural gene in a transcription unit could be said as monocistronic (mostly in eukaryotes) or polycistronic (mostly in bacteria or prokaryotes).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49934,'biology',94,793,1702,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Regulation of lac operon by repressor is referred to as negative regulation.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The repressor protein binds to the operator region of the operon.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'When there is no lactose in the medium, then repressor protein binds to the operator region of the operon and prevents RNA polymerase from transcribing the operon.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49935,'biology',94,782,1687,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The sugar phosphate backbone of two chains in DNA double helix show anti-parallel polarity.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The phosphodiester bonds in one strand go from a 3\' carbon of one nucleotide to a 5\' carbon of adjacent nucleotide, whereas those in complementary strands go vice versa.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49936,'biology',94,784,1689,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In Griffith\'s experiment, a mixture of heat killed virulent bacteria $\\mathrm{R}$ and live non-virulent bacteria $\\mathrm{S}$, lead to the death of mice.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> \'Transforming principle\' got transferred from heat-killed $\\mathrm{S}$ strain to $\\mathrm{R}$ strain and made it virulent.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both Assertion and Reason are false. When bacteria Streptococcus pneumoniae are grown on a culture plate, some produce smooth shiny colonies $(\\mathrm{S})$ while others produce rough colonies (R). This is because the $\\mathrm{S}$ strain bacteria have a mucous (polysaccharide) coat, while R strain does not. Mice infected with the $S$ strain (virulent) die from pneumonia infection but mice infected with the $\\mathrm{R}$ strain do not develop pneumonia. In Griffith\'s experiment, some \'transforming principle\', transferred from the heat-killed S strain, had enabled the $\\mathrm{R}$ strain to synthesise a smooth polysaccharide coat and become virulent which must be due to the transfer of the genetic material. This is known as transformation.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49965,'biology',94,794,1703,'The enzyme which can cut molecules of DNA into segments is known as<br>','[{"text": "DNA ligase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Restriction enzyme", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA polymerase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA gyrase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Restriction enzymes or \'molecular scissors are DNA-cutting enzymes found in bacteria . As they make a cut inside the molecule, so they, are often called restriction endonucleases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49937,'biology',94,789,1698,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> A change in nitrogen base at the third position of a codon causes change in the expression of the codon.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The pairing of the third position bases of the codon may be ambiguous and varies according to the nucleotide present in this position.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'According to the Wobble hypothesis, only the first two position of a triplet codon on mRNA have a precise pairing with the bases of the tRNA anticodon. The pairing of the third position bases of the codon may be ambiguous and varies according to the nucleotide present in this position. Thus, a single tRNA type is able to recognise two or more codons differing only in the third base. The same is called wobble position.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49938,'biology',94,793,1702,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The predominant site for control of gene expression in prokaryotes is transcription initiation.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The activity of RNA polymerase is regulated by accessory proteins, which affect recognition of start sites.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In prokaryotes, control of the rate of transcriptional initiation is the predominant site for control of gene expression. In a transcription unit, the activity of RNA polymerase at a given promoter is in turn regulated by interaction with accessory proteins, which affect its ability to recognise start sites. These regulatory proteins can act both positively (activators) and negatively (repressors).',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49939,'biology',94,788,1696,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Polycistronic mRNA, found in prokaryotes, specify a number of polypeptides.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Monocistronic mRNA, found in eukaryotes, specify only a single polypeptide.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49940,'biology',94,788,1697,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> mRNA attaches to ribosome through its 3 end.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The mRNA has F-capsular nucleotide and bases of lagging sequence.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'mRNA attaches itself to $30 \\mathrm{~S}$ unit of ribosome through its $5^{\\prime}$ end. This process is helped by G-cap nucleotide and basis of leader sequence present on mRNA where G-cap is present as in eukaryotes. So, the correct answer is \'If both the assertion and reason are false\'',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49941,'biology',94,788,1697,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Replication and transcription occur in the nucleus but translation in the cytoplasm.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> m-RNA is transferred from the nucleus into the cytoplasm where ribosomes and amino acids are available for protein synthesis.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49942,'biology',94,787,1692,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The mechanism of DNA replication is semi-conservative in nature.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Each of the complementary strands of the parental double helix is conserved during the process.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'DNA replication is semi-conservative, a type of replication in which one strand of the daughter duplex is derived from the parent while the other strand is formed new. This is carried out by the separation of two strands. The separated strands function as templates. The new strands built up over the templates of old strands will have complementary base pairs (A opposite $\\mathrm{T}$ and $\\mathrm{G}$ opposite $\\mathrm{C}$ ). The two daughter DNA molecules thus formed will be carbon copies of the parent molecule but shall have one new strand and one old strand.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49943,'biology',94,794,1703,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> In recombinant DNA technology human genes are often transferred into bacteria (prokaryotes) or yeast (eukaryote).<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Both bacteria and yeast multiply very fast to form a huge population which expresses the desired gene.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49975,'biology',94,788,1695,'DNA-dependent RNA polymerase catalyzes transcription on one strand of the DNA which is called the :_____<br>','[{"text": "Alpha strand", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antistrand", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Template strand", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coding strand", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Template strand',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49944,'biology',94,790,1699,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> An organism with lethal mutation may not even develop beyond the zygote<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> All types of gene mutations are lethal.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'&nbsp;Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49945,'biology',94,788,1695,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Transcription is the mode in which DNA passes its genetic information to RNA<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Transcription takes place in the cytoplasm of eukaryotic cells.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The Assertion is true but the Reason is false.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49946,'biology',94,786,1691,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> The RNA molecules are essential for cell function in both prokaryotes and eukaryotes<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They play an important role in protein synthesis.','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49947,'biology',94,788,1696,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> \'Split genes\' concept is applicable only to the prokaryotes.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Prokaryotic genome is divided into exons and introns','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'\'Split genes\' concept is applicable only to the eukaryotes. Eukaryotic genome is divided into exons and introns',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49948,'biology',94,787,1694,'<strong>Assertion:</strong> Enzymes required for DNA replication are efficient enzymes.<br><br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> They can polymerise large number of nucleotides in very short time','[{"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct and Reason is the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are correct but Reason is not the correct explanation of the Assertion.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is correct but Reason is incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49949,'biology',94,782,1687,'Length of one loop of B-DNA is :','[{"text": "$3.40 \\\\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$10 \\\\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$20 \\\\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0.34 \\\\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Length of one loop of B-DNA or a complete turn of the double helix B-DNA has a length $3.40 \\mathrm{~nm}$. In one turn there are 10 base pairs, which are spaced at intervals of $0.34 \\mathrm{~nm}$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2006,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49950,'biology',94,782,1687,'Antiparallel strands of a DNA molecule means that:<br>','[{"text": "The phosphate groups at the start of two, DNA strands are in opposite position (pole)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One strand turns clockwise", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One strand turns anticlockwise", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The phosphate groups of two DNA strands at their ends share the same position", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Anti-parallel DNA strands resting at each end of the DNA helix move in opposite directions, accordingly their name i.e., the 3 prime and 5 prime names come from the notation for the sugar carbon atoms which holds the phosphodiester bonds together. A DNA strand is anti-parallel as it runs parallel to another strand, but turns in the opposite direction. This implies that the head of one strand runs parallel to the tail of the other.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49951,'biology',94,782,1687,'The two polynucleotide chains in DNA are :<br>','[{"text": "Parellel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Discontinuous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antiparallel", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Semiconservative", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A DNA contains two polynucleotide chains wound around each other forming a double helix. complementary base pairing holds the two chains together, i.e., distinct bonding between $A$ and $T$ bases and between $\\mathrm{G}$ and $\\mathrm{C}$ bases on the two strands. The two antiparallel DNA polynucleotide chains are held together by complementary base pairing.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49952,'biology',94,787,1694,'The Okazaki fragments in DNA chain growth','[{"text": "Prove semiconservative nature of DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polymerize in the 3\' to 5\' direction and forms replication fork", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polymerize in the 5\' to 3\' direction and explain 3\' to 5\' DNA replication", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Result in transcription", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The Okazaki fragments, newly synthesized DNAfragments are short and are formed during DNA replication on the lagging template strand. DNA replication always occurs in $5^{\\prime} \\rightarrow 3^{\\prime}$ direction, therefore while copying the $3^{\\prime}$ to 5 \' strand, replication is continuous.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2007,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49953,'biology',94,792,1701,'Polysome is formed by','[{"text": "Several ribosomes attached to a single mRNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ribosomes attached to each other in a linear arrangement", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Many ribosomes attached to a strand of endoplasmic reticulum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A ribosome with several units", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A polysome or polyribosome is a compound of an mRNA molecule and several ribosomes that act to form polypeptide chains (attached to a single mRNA), during active translation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49956,'biology',94,788,1697,'Removal of introns and joining the exons in a defined order in a transcription unit is called<br>','[{"text": "Splicing", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tailing", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transformation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Capping", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'One of the complexities in eukaryotes is that the primary transcripts contain both the exons and introns and are non-functional. Therefore, it leads to a process called Splicing, where introns are removed and exons are joined in a defined order in a transcription unit.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49957,'biology',94,789,1698,'Whose experiments cracked that a genetic code is a triplet?','[{"text": "Nirenberg and Mathaei", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Morgan and Strulevant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hershey and Chase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beadle and Tatum<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Marshall Nirenberg and Heinrich J. Matthaei cracked the DNA and discovered unequivocally that a genetic code is a "triplet". They were the first to elucidate the nature of a codon in 1961, at the National Institutes of Health. They used a cell-free system to translate a poly-uracil RNA sequence and discovered that the polypeptide that they had synthesized consisted of only the amino acid phenylalanine.They thereby deduced that the codon UUU specified the amino acid phenylalanine.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49958,'biology',94,783,1688,'Which one of the following statements about the particular entity is true?','[{"text": "Centromere is found in animal cells, which produces aster during cell division.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleosome is formed of nucleotides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The gene for producing insulin is present in every body cell.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA consists of core of eight histones.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The insulin producing gene is found in occurs in every body cell but it is not indicated in all cells. A nucleosome consists of a segment of DNA containing eight histone protein cores. A centromere found in chromosomes is a region of DNA where two chromatids are attached. While aster is produced by centriole (found in animal cells) during cell division.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49959,'biology',94,782,1687,'The $3^{\\prime} \\rightarrow 5^{\\prime}$ phosphodiester linkage inside a polynucleotide chain serve to join:<br>','[{"text": "One nucleotide with another nucleotide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One nucleoside with another nucleoside", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One nitrogenous base with pentose sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One DNA strand with the other DNA strand", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The DNA backbone is a polymer having alternating sugar-phosphate sequence. Inside a polynucleotide chain, the deoxyribose sugars are attached at both the 3\'-hydroxyl and 5\'-hydroxyl groups to phosphate groups in ester links, termed as "phosphodiester" bonds or linkage. Thus , 32 -52 phosphodiester bond is formed between carbon 3 of one nucleotide and carbon 5 of the other nucleotide.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2010,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49960,'biology',94,784,1689,'The unequivocal proof of DNA as the genetic material came from the studies on a<br>','[{"text": "Bacterial virus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacterium", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Viroid", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Alfred Hershey and Martha Chase conducted a series of experiments in 1952 to confirm that DNA is a genetic material.     Through their experiments they postulated that when bacteriophages (composed of DNA and protein), infect bacteria and their DNA enters the host bacterial cell. While a bacteriophage is a virus which infects and replicates inside a bacterium.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49961,'biology',94,788,1695,'If one strand of DNA has the nitrogenous base sequence as ATCTG, what would be the complementary RNA strand sequence?<br>','[{"text": "TTAGU", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AACTG", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "UAGAC", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ATCGU", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The mRNA is formed by transcribing the DNA or RNA. The process follows the same base pairing rules as DNA duplication. But it has one big difference i.e., absence of $\\mathrm{T}$ in RNA, but $\\mathrm{U}$ is present there. Thus, instead of pairing the A in the DNA with T in RNA, it is paired with U. Accordingly, the complementary RNA strand sequence is UAGAC.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49962,'biology',94,789,1698,'The one aspect which is not a salient feature of genetic code, is its being','[{"text": "Ambiguous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Specific", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Degenerate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Universal<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The salient features of genetic code includes: triplet in nature, universal, non overlapping, degenerate, comma less, nonambiguous or specific, initiator codon, nonsense or terminator codons. It does not include the characteristic ambiguous as each codon codes for only one amino acid that is why, it is specific in character.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49963,'biology',94,793,1702,'Which enzyme will be produced in a cell in if there is a nonsense mutation in the lac Y gene?<br>','[{"text": "$\\\\beta$-galactosidase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transacetylase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactose permease and transacetylase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactose", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A nonsense mutation in the lac Y gene causes generation of a nonfunctional permease. It is the one that stops polypeptide synthesis because termination or non -sense codon is formed. In lac operon, the structural genes sequence is $\\mathrm{Z}, \\mathrm{Y}, \\mathrm{X}$ that codes for â-galactosidase, lactose permease and transacetylase respectively. If the gene ${\\rm{Y}}$ has nonsense mutation, gene expression stops at it, resulting in non-expression of both gene $\\mathrm{Y}$ and successive gene. Thus, only $\\beta$-galactosidase enzyme is formed. In the protein coding sequence a stop codon is introduced & lactose is no longer transported into the cell.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49964,'biology',94,793,1702,'Which one of the following is wrongly matched?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Translation - using information in mRNA to make protein", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Transcription - Writing information from DNA to tRNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Repressor protein - Binds to operator to stop enzyme synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Operon - Structural genes, operator and promoter", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Transcription is the process through whichDNA is transcribed to mRNA, that carries the information required for protein synthesis. Whereas, an operon is a functional unit of genomic DNA containing a cluster of genes under the control of a single promoter.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49966,'biology',94,781,1686,'Identify the correct order of organization of genetic material from largest to smallest.<br>','[{"text": "Chromosome, genome, nucleotide, gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome, gene, genome, nucleotide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genome, chromosome, gene, nucleotide", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genome, chromosome, nucleotide, gene", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'DNA is the hereditary material in all living cells. A genome is simply the sum total of an organism\'s DNA and all the genes are there in a single set of chromosomes. A gene is a segment or part of chromosome. Nucleotides are sub-units that make up DNA.sub',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49967,'biology',94,793,1702,'Gene regulation governing lactose operon of E.coli that involves the lac I gene product is<br>','[{"text": "Negative and repressible because repressor protein prevents transcription", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Feedback inhibition because excess of â-galactosidase can switch offtranscription", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Negative and inducible because repressor protein prevents transcription", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Positive and inducible because it can be induced by lactose", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In negative inducible operons, a regulatory repressor protein is normally bound to the operator, which prevents the transcription of the genes in the operon. If an inducer molecule is present, it binds to the repressor and changes its conformation so that it is unable to bind to the operator. This allows for expression of the operon. The lac operon is a negatively controlled inducible operon, where the inducer molecule is allolactose.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49968,'biology',94,795,1704,'Satellite DNA is important because it<br>','[{"text": "Does not code for proteins and is same in all members of the population", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Shows high degree of polymorphism in population and also the same degree of polymorphism in an individual, which is heritable from parents to children", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Codes for enzymes needed for DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Codes for proteins needed in cell cycle", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Satellite DNA are the repetitive DNA sequences which do not code for any protein and exhibit high degree of polymorphism and form a bulk of DNA in a genome. It also forms important basis in DNA fingerprinting. Although, DNA from every tissue from an individual show the same degree of polymorphism, still they are found to be very useful as identification tool in forensic applications.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49969,'biology',94,787,1692,'Balbiani rings are sites of','[{"text": "DNA replication", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Synthesis of lipids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "RNA synthesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Synthesis of polysaccharides", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Balbiani rings are generally, the sites of RNA synthesis. The RNA enters the cytoplasm and makes proteins there at the ribosomes. These rings have active DNA or RNA in them and proteins are also synthesized here.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49970,'biology',94,782,1687,'DNA are not present in:','[{"text": "Ribosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chloroplast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mitochondria<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'DNA is absent in ribosomes.DNA is present inside the nucleus, mitochondria and chloroplasts of a cell and not in any other portion of a cell. Though ribosomes contain RNA and proteins.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49971,'biology',94,795,1704,'Which of the following is not required for any of the techniques of DNA fingerprinting available at present<br>','[{"text": "Polymerase chain reactio", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Restriction enzymes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Zinc finger analysis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "DNA-DNA hybridization", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Zinc finger analysis is not needed for DNA fingerprinting technique available at present. A zinc finger is a small protein structural motif which is characterized by the coordination of one or more zinc ions to stabilize the fold. Zinc fingers are really useful in gene regulation and genome manipulation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49972,'biology',94,793,1702,'Which of the following is required as inducer(s) for the expression of Lac operon?<br>','[{"text": "Glucose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Galactose", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lactose", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Lactose and galactose", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'For the expression of Lac operon lactose is required as an inducer. The lac operon is an inducible operon which uses lactose as an energy source for the bacterium E. coli and is activated when lactose is present and glucose is low.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49973,'biology',94,782,1687,'In sea urchin DNA, which is double stranded, $17 \\%$ of the bases were shown to be cytosine. The percentages of the other three bases expected to be present in this DNA are :','[{"text": "G 8.5 %,  A 50 %, T 24.5 %", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G 34 %,  A 24.5 %,  T 24.5 %", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G 17 %,  A 16.5 %,  T 32.5 %", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "G 17 %,  A 33 %,  T 33 %<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Rule by Chargaff:<br>The rule states that there is a percentage basepair equality for a double-stranded DNA molecule worldwide: percent A  is equal to percent T and percent G is equal to percent C. In the DNA double helix model, the robust validation of the law constitutes the basis of Watson-Crick pairs.<br>For each of the two DNA strands, the second rule holds that both percent A is equal to percent T and percent G is equal to percent C. In a single DNA strand, this describes only a global function of the base composition.<br>Both cellular DNAs, irrespective of the organisms, have a number of adenosine residues equal to the number of thymidine residues according to Chargaff\'s law, which means that A is equal to T; and the number of guanosine residues is equal to the number of cytidine residues; G is equal to C. There is 17 percent cytosine in the given question, meaning the percentage of guanine is also 17 percent.<br>Therefore,<br>$(\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{T})=(\\mathrm{G}+\\mathrm{C}),(\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{T})(\\mathrm{G}+\\mathrm{C})=1$<br>We know that,<br>$(\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{T}+\\mathrm{G}+\\mathrm{C})=100$ percent<br>${\\rm{A + T + 17 + 17 = 100, A + T = 100 - 34A + T = 66}}$ As ${\\rm{A = T, 2A = 66,}}\\,{\\rm{A = 33}}$,  ${\\rm{A = 33}}$ And $\\mathrm{T}=33$<br>Thus, if cytosine is $17 \\%, \\mathrm{G}$ is $17 \\%, \\mathrm{~A}$ is $33 \\%$, and $\\mathrm{T}$ is $33 \\%$<br>So, the correct answer is, \'G-17 %, A-33 %, T-33 %\'.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49974,'biology',94,785,1690,'A molecule that can act as a genetic material must fulfill the traits given below, except :-<br>','[{"text": "It should be unstable structurally and chemically", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It should provide the scope for slow changes that are required for evolution", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It should be able to express itself in the form of \'Mendelian characters\'", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It should be able to generate its replica", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The genetic material should be stable and sructurally and chemically.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49977,'biology',94,783,1688,'The association of histone $\\mathrm{H}_{1}$ with a nucleosome indicates:____<br>','[{"text": "Transcription is occurring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA replication is occurring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The DNA is condensed into a Chromatin Fibre", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The DNA double helix is exposed", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The association of  ${{\\rm{H}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ protein indicates the complete formation of nucleosome.Therefore the DNA is in condensed form.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49978,'biology',94,787,1694,'During DNA replication, Okazaki fragments are used to elongate .<br>','[{"text": "The leading strand towards replication fork", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The lagging strand towards replication fork", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The leading strand away from replication fork", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The lagging strand away from the replication fork", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Two DNA polymerase molecules work simultaneous at the DNA fork, one on the leading strand and the other on the lagging strand. Each Okazaki fragment is synthesized by DNA polymerase at lagging strand in ${\\rm{5\'}}$ $\\rightarrow 3$ \' direction. New Okazaki fragments appear as the replication fork opens further. As the first Okazaki fragment appears away from the replication fork, the direction of elongation would be away from replication fork.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49979,'biology',94,789,1698,'If there are 999 bases in an RNA that codes for a protein with 333 amino acids, and the base at position 901 is deleted such that the length of the RNA becomes 998 bases, how many codons will be altered?<br>','[{"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "11", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "33", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "333", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'If deletion occurs at 901 st position the remaining 98 bases specifying for 33 codons of amino acids will be altered.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49980,'biology',94,788,1697,'Spliceosomes are not found in cells of_____<br>','[{"text": "Plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Spliceosomes are used in removal of introns during post-transcriptional processing of hnRNA in eukaryotes only as split genes are absent as prokaryotes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
