(49982,'biology',94,787,1693,'The experimental proof for semiconservative replication of DNA was first shown in a<br>','[{"text": "Plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacterium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Fungus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Virus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Matthew Meselson and Franklin Stahl first time provided experimental proof for semiconservative replication of DNA in a bacterium Escherichia coli.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49983,'biology',94,788,1695,'AGGTATCGCAT is a sequence from the coding strand of a gene. What will be the corresponding sequence of the transcribed mRNA?<br>','[{"text": "ACCUAUGCGAU", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "UGGTUTCGCAT", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AGGUAUCGCAU", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "UCCAUAGCGUA", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Nucleotides of coding strand and mRNA will be similar But Thymine (T) will be replaced by Uracil (U). So the mRNA sequence will be AGGUAUCGCAU .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49984,'biology',94,795,1704,'Select the correct match<br><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Matthew Meselson and F. Stahl- <i>Pisum sativum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alfred Hershey and Martha Chase - TMV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alec Jeffreys - Streptococcus pneumoniae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Francois Jacob and Jacques Monod- Lac operon", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Francois Jacob and Jacque Monod proposed a model of gene regulation known as Lac operon model. Matthew Meselson and Franklin Stahl first time provided experimental proof for semiconservative replication of DNA in a bacterium Escherichia coli. Alfred Hershey and Martha Chase proved that DNA is the genetic material in Bacteriophage. Alec Jeffreys developed DNA finger printing technique.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49985,'biology',94,793,1702,'Match the following genes of the Lac operon with their respective products :<br>1. i gene &emsp;&emsp; (i) \\(\\beta\\)-galactosidase<br>2. z gene&emsp;&emsp;(ii) Permease<br>3. a gene&emsp;&emsp;(iii) Repressor<br>y gene&emsp;&emsp;(iv) Transacetylase<br>Select the correct option.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{1 - (i),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2 - (iii),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3 - (ii),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{4 - (iv)}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1 - (iii),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2 - (i),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3 - (ii),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{4 - (iv)}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1 - (i),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2 - (iii),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3 - (iv),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{4 - (ii)}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1 - (iii),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{2 - (iv),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{3 - (i),}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{4 - (ii)}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In lac operon<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{i}}\\,{\\rm{gene }}}& \\to &{{\\rm{Repressor}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\\\\{{\\rm{z}}\\,{\\rm{gene}}}& \\to &{\\beta {\\rm-{ galactosidase}}\\,\\,\\,}\\\\{{\\rm{y}}\\,{\\rm{gene}}}& \\to &{{\\rm{Permease}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,}\\end{array}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}{{\\rm{a}}\\,{\\rm{gane}}}& \\to &{{\\rm{Transacetylase}}}\\end{array}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49986,'biology',94,789,1698,'Which of the following features of genetic code does allow bacteria to produce human insulin by recombinant DNA technology?<br>','[{"text": "Genetic code is not ambiguous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic code is redundant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic code is nearly universal", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genetic code is specific", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In recombinant DNA technology bacteria is able to produce human insulin because genetic code is nearly universal.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(49987,'biology',94,794,1703,'Expressed Sequence Tags (ESTs) refers to :','[{"text": "Genes expressed as RNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Polypeptide expression", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "DNA polymorphism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Novel DNA sequences<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Expressed Sequence Tags (ESTs) are DNAsequences (genes) that are expressed as mRNA for protein synthesis. These are used in human Genome Project.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
