(50132,'biology',93,272,530,'In genetics the term test cross means','[{"text": "Crossing an  ${F_1}$ individual with either of the two parents.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The crossing of ${F_1}$ individual with homozygous recessive.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Crossing ${F_1}$ individual with that of ${F_2}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crossing ${F_1}$ individual with another ${F_1}$ individual.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Tt x tt (test cross) crossing of heterozygous with recessive parent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50133,'biology',93,272,530,'Ratio of progeny when a red coloured heterozygote is crossed with a white coloured plant in which red colour is dominant over white colour','[{"text": "$1:2:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$9:3:3:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1:1$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Test cross is the cross between heterozygous dominant with its recessive parents. The ratio of progeny in this case reflects 1:1 in monohybrid condition, while in dihybrid condition it shows 1:1:1:1.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50134,'biology',93,272,530,'Test cross involves a cross between','[{"text": "Recessive ${F_1}$-plant and dominant pure -plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Recessive ${F_1}$-plant and recessive parentplant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant ${F_2}$-plant and recessive parent plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dominant ${F_2}$-plant and dominant parent plants", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Test cross involves a cross between Dominant ${F_2}$-plant and recessive parent plants',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50135,'biology',93,272,530,'How would you test a pea plant whether it is a pure or hybrid for tallness?','[{"text": "Cross the pea plant with a pure tall pea plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross the pea plant with another tall pea plant unknown genotype", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross the pea plant with any pea plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cross the pea plant with a homozygous dwarf pea", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cross the pea plant with a homozygous dwarf Pea - test cross',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50136,'biology',93,272,530,'Test cross is when','[{"text": "${F_1}$ crossed with homozygous recessive parent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${F_1}$ crossed with heterozygous parent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${F_1}$ crossed with homozygous dominant parent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${F_1}$ crossed with homozygous parent", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A cross between ${F_1}$ hybrid (Aa) and the homozygous recessive parent (aa) is termed as Test Cross. This is called as test cross because it helps to find out whether the given dominant phenotype is homozygous or heterozygous',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50137,'biology',93,272,530,'Mendel performed test cross to know the','[{"text": "Genotype of ${F_1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phenotype of ${F_1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genotype of ${F_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotype of ${F_2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Therefore, to determine the genotype of a tall plant at ${F_2}$, Mendel crossed the tall plant from ${F_2}$  with a dwarf plant. This he called a test cross..',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50138,'biology',93,272,530,'A cross between ${F_1}$ hybrid and a recessive parent gives a ratio of :','[{"text": "$1:1$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$3:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4:1$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'If heterozygous dominant ${F_1}$ hybrid (Tt) is test crossed with the recessive parent, then 50% will be tall and the remaining 50% will be dwarf. Thus, they give a ratio of 1:1.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50139,'biology',93,272,530,'A test cross is carried out to','[{"text": "Determine the genotype of a plant at ${F_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Determine the genotype of a plant at ${F_1}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Determine the genotype of the parent plant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "To know if plant will grow / viable phenotype", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Therefore, to determine the genotype of a tall plant at ${F_2}$, Mendel crossed the tall plant from ${F_2}$ with a dwarf plant. This he called a test cross.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50140,'biology',93,272,530,'The crossing of ${F_1}$ hybrid to ______ is done in a test cross is called','[{"text": "${F_2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Recessive parent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${F_1}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant parent", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The crossing of ${F_1}$ hybrid to a recessive parent is called a test cross.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/93_50140_question_1.png'),
(50141,'biology',93,272,530,'Heterozygous purple flower is crossed with recessive white flower. The progeny has the ratio :','[{"text": "All white", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All purple", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "75% purple and 25% white", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "50% purple and 50% white", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'If heterozygous dominant purple flower is test crossed with the recessive white flower, then 50% will be purple and the remaining 50% will be white',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50142,'biology',93,272,530,'A cross involving ${F_1}$ hybrid and a double recessive parent is called:','[{"text": "Dihybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Trihybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Test cross", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Crossing of ${F_1}$ individual having dominant phenotype with its homozygous recessive parent is called test cross. The test cross is used to determine whether the individuals exhibiting dominant characters are homozygous or heterozygous.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50143,'biology',93,272,530,'Pure tall pea plant can be differentiated from hybrid tall pea plant by','[{"text": "Test cross with dwarf plant and finding the progeny of tall plants.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Selfing and finding the progeny of tall plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Selfing and test crossing to find the progeny of both tall and dwarf plants.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pure tall Pea plant can be differentiated from hybrid tall Pea plant by Test cross with dwarf plant and finiding the progeny of tall plants and Selfing and finding the progeny of tall plants.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50144,'biology',93,272,530,'Which of the following ratio refers to back cross?','[{"text": "Aa × aa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aa × AA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aa × Aa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Aa×aa & Aa×AA. Test cross is a type of back cross hence Aaaa, AaAA both represents Back cross.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50145,'biology',93,272,530,'Mendel gave us ___','[{"text": "Five principles of inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four principles of inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two principles of inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three principles of inheritance", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Law of dominance, law of segregation and law of independent assortment are the three major principles of inheritance enunciated by Mendel .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50146,'biology',93,272,530,'Mendel’s laws are valid for','[{"text": "Sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Asexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vegetative reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mendel’s laws are valid for every sexually reproducing organisms, along with garden peas and human beings. Thus, his laws are valid for sexual reproduction.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50147,'biology',93,272,530,'Mendel’s laws of inheritance can be explained with the help of :','[{"text": "Meiosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both of these", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to Mendel’s second law, the law of segregation, the two alleles gets separated from each other during meiosis.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50148,'biology',93,273,531,'When Mendel crossed plants with a pair of contrasting characters, he derived the','[{"text": "Law of co-dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Whenever any organism consisting of two contrasting alleles of a gene or trait, the one which expresses itself phenotypically is known as dominant, while the other allele which fails to express itself is recessive. Mendel formulated this law of dominance, when a pair of contrasting characters were crossed; this he did on the basis of his experiments.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50149,'biology',93,273,531,'When alleles of two contrasting characters are present together and one of the character expresses itself during the cross in a monohybrid cross while the other remains hidden gives the','[{"text": "Law of purity of gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When alleles of two contrasting characters are present together and one of the character expresses itself during the cross in a monohybrid cross while the other remains hidden gives the Law of dominance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50150,'biology',93,273,531,'The allele which express itself in both homozygous and heterozygous condition is called','[{"text": "Dominant allele", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Recessive allele", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lethal allele", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Codominant allele", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The allele which express itself in both homozygous and heterozygous condition is called Dominant allele.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50151,'biology',93,273,531,'Apperance of only one character in ${F_1}$ generation though it is a cross fertilisation is explained by','[{"text": "Law of codominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "law of incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "law of independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Apperance of recessive character in ${F_2} - $ generation is explained by Law of dominance',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50152,'biology',93,273,531,'Based on observations on monohybrid crosses Mendel proposed two general rules . They are','[{"text": "Law of Dominance and Law of Segregation.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of In Dominance and Law of Segregation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of CoDominance and Law of Segregation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of Independent assortment and Law of Segregation.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Based on observations on monohybrid crosses Mendel proposed two general rules. They are Law of Dominance and Law of Segregation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50153,'biology',93,273,531,'Select the correct statement with respect to law of Dominance<br>i. Characters are controlled by discrete units called factors.<br>ii. Factors occur in triplets.<br>iii. In a dissimilar pair of factors one member\nof the pair dominates (dominant) the other (recessive).','[{"text": "i is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i & iii are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "ii & iii are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statement i and iii correct, factors occur in pairs.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50154,'biology',93,273,531,'The law of dominance is applicable in inheritance of','[{"text": "Seed colour in pea", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Flower colour in Mirabilis jalapa", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Starch grain size in pea", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Roan coat colour in cattles", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The law of dominance is applicable in inheritance of Seed colour in pea. Flower colour in Mirabilis jalapa and Starch grain size in pea is incomplete dominance. Roan coat colour in cattles is codominance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50155,'biology',93,273,531,'Diploid cells have','[{"text": "Two chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two sets of chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One set of chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two pairs of homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Diploid cells are the cells which have two complete sets (2n) of chromosomes. In diploid organisms, one set of chromosomes is donated by each parent that makes up the two sets in the offspring.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50156,'biology',93,273,531,'If a plant is heterozygous for tallness is selfed, the ${F_2}$ generation has both tall and dwarf plants. This proves the principle of :','[{"text": "Dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Segregation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'According to the condition, a pair of contrasting genes stay together and segregate when there is gamete formation. This proves the principle of segregation, also known as Mendel’s first law of heredity.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50157,'biology',93,273,531,'The law of segregation of characters postulated by Mendel can be related to','[{"text": "A gamete receiving only one of the\\ntwo homologous chromosomes during\\nmeiosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The presence of two genes for each\\ncharacter in a somatic cell", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of both genes on the same\\nchromosome.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'It is also known as law of purity of gametes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50158,'biology',93,273,531,'Mendel’s principle of segregation is based on separation of alleles during','[{"text": "Seed formation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gamete formation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Embryonic development", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the ${F_1}$ hybrid , when a pair of allelomorphs are brought together they co-exist or remain together in the hybrid without blending or in any way contaminating each other and they separate completely and remain pure during the formation of gametes. This is stated in the law of segregation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50159,'biology',93,273,531,'Mendel’s principle of segregation means that the germ cells always receive:','[{"text": "One of the paired alleles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One pair of alleles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One quarter of the genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Any pair of alleles", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'According to Mendel’s principle of segregation, the germ cells always receive one of the paired alleles..',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50172,'biology',93,274,532,'The&nbsp;<em>Mirabilis jalapa</em>&nbsp;when two ${F_1}$ pink flowered plants were crossed with each other, the ${F_2}$ generation produced 40 red, 80 pink and 40 white flowering plants. This is a case of','[{"text": "Lethal genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Duplicate genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epistasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Incomplete dominance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50160,'biology',93,273,531,'In order to explain the mode of inheritance of character through successive generations, Mendel proposed that the two alternative factors for each character become separated during the formation of gametes and each factor has an equal chance of being transferred the offsprings. This phenomenon is known as :','[{"text": "Principle of segregation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Principle of independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Principle of incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mendel through his experiments determined that every parent provides one factor for a character to the ${F_1}$  hybrid. In this manner, the ${F_1}$  hybrid possess two factors for every character. As the ${F_1}$  hybrid forms gametes, the two factors gets separated from each other. This phenomenon of separation is called the Law of Segregation. As there is no mixing up of factors, therefore the purity of gametes is maintained.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50161,'biology',93,273,531,'Which statement is true for Law of Segregation','[{"text": "Characters are controlled by discrete units\\ncalled factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Factors or alleles of a pair segregate from each other such that a gamete receives only one of the two factors", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mendel crossed the tall plant from  ${F_2}$ with a dwarf plant. This he called a test cross.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hybrids contain alleles with contrasting traits, they are called homozygous.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'only option 2 is related to law of segregation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50162,'biology',93,273,531,'The law based on fact that the characters do not show any blending and both the characters are recovered as such in ${F_2}$-generation although one character was absent in ${F_1}$-progeny, is','[{"text": "Law of purity of gametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Law of Segregation-This law is based on the fact that the alleles do not show any blendingand that both the characters are recovered as such in the ${F_2}$ generationthough one of these is not seen at the ${F_1}$ stage. Though the parents containtwo alleles during gamete formation, the factors or alleles of a pair segregate from each other such that a gamete receives only one of the two factors.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50163,'biology',93,274,532,'The inheritance of flower colour in the __________ is a good example to understand incomplete dominance','[{"text": "Dog flower", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Snapdragon", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Antirrhinum sp", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All the names mean the same plant.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
