(50167,'biology',93,274,532,'Select the statement which is not false. A. The normal allele produces the normal enzyme that is needed for the transformation of a substrate S<br>B. The modified allele produces no enzyme at all, at all times','[{"text": "Only A", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both A & B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are false", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The modified allele produces no enzyme at all, but not at all times. This statement is false.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50168,'biology',93,274,532,'Theoretically the modified allele could be responsible for production of','[{"text": "The normal/less efficient enzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A non-functional enzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No enzyme at all", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Theoretically, the modified allele could be responsible for production of –<br> (i) the normal/less efficient enzyme, or<br> (ii) a non-functional enzyme, or<br> (iii) no enzyme at all',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50169,'biology',93,274,532,'The phenotype of an individual may be affected if the modified allele produces<br> a. No enzyme at all<br> b. The normal/less efficient enzyme<br> c. A non-functional enzyme','[{"text": "Only (a) is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a) and (c) are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(b) and (c) are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only (c) is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'If the allele produces a non-functional enzyme or no enzyme, the phenotype may be effected.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50170,'biology',93,274,532,'The unmodified allele, represents the original phenotype is the ____allele and the modified allele is generally the _______allele','[{"text": "Recessive, recessive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Recessive, dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant, recessive", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dominant, dominant", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The unmodified (functioning) allele, which represents the original phenotype is the dominant allele and the modified allele is generally the recessive allele.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50171,'biology',93,274,532,'In Incomplete dominance the recessive trait is seen due to','[{"text": "Non-functional enzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No enzyme is produced", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 & 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of them", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The recessive trait is seen due to non-functional enzyme or because no enzyme is produced.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50173,'biology',93,274,532,'${F_1}$ hybrid is intermediate between the two parents. The phenomenon is','[{"text": "Dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Codominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blending inheritance", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Incomplete dominance is a type of intermediate inheritance in which one allele for a particular trait is not completely expressed over its paired allele. Because of this a third phenotype is formed in which the expressed physical character is a blend of the phenotypes of both alleles. In this the phenotypic and genotypic monohybrid ratio in ${F_2}$ generation is 1(RR- red) :2 (Rr- pink ) : 1 (rr- white).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
