(50175,'biology',93,274,532,'The ${F_2}$ generation offspring in a plant showing incomplete dominance, exhibit :','[{"text": "Similar phenotypic and genotypic ratios\\nof 1:2:1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A genotypic ratio of 1:1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A phenotypic ratio of 3:1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Variable genotypic and phenotypic ratios", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The ${F_2}$ generation offspring in a plant showing incomplete dominance, shows similar phenotypic and genotypic 1:2:1 ratios. This ratio confirms the law of segregation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50176,'biology',93,274,532,'In incomplete dominance what is the colour of ${F_1}$ generation flowers?','[{"text": "Red (Rr)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "White (Rr)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pink (Rr)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Red (RR)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pink -Rr',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/93_50176_question_1.png'),
(50177,'biology',93,275,533,'When dominant and recessive alleles express themselves together, it is called','[{"text": "Pseudodominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co-dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Amphidominance", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In Co-dominance, both the alleles dominant or recessive of a gene express themselves in theheterozygotes. Phenotypes of both the parents appear in  ${F_1}$ hybrid rather than the intermediate phenotype.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50178,'biology',93,275,533,'The ABO blood groups are controlled by','[{"text": "I-gene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "c-gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B-gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "n-gene", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'ABO blood groups are controlled by the gene I.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50179,'biology',93,275,533,'Out of the three alleles of gene $I$, the sugar polymers on the plasma membrane of RBCc is controlled by how many alleles?','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The alleles ${I^A}$ and ${I^B}$ produce a slightly different form of the sugar while allele i does not produce any sugar.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50180,'biology',93,275,533,'With respect to human blood group inheritance which of the following sentences are correct?','[{"text": "${I^A}$ and ${I^B}$ are codominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${I^A}$ and ${I^B}$ are dominant over i", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is an example of multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All of the statements are correct.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50181,'biology',93,275,533,'Incomplete dominance and co dominance is similar in having identical','[{"text": "Phenotypic ratio", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genotypic ratio", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both (1) and (2)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Incomplete dominance and codominance exhibit 1:2:1 phenotypic and genotypic ratio.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50182,'biology',93,275,533,'How many phenotypes and genotypes are possible in case of ABO blood group system ?','[{"text": "3, 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6, 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4, 6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ABO blood group is determined by three different alleles. This gives rise to six possible genotypes and four possible blood types(phenotypes).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50183,'biology',93,275,533,'Phenotypic and genotypic ratio is similar in case of','[{"text": "Co- dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 & 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Incomplete dominance and codominance exhibit 1:2:1 phenotypic and genotypic ratio.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50184,'biology',93,275,533,'When there are more than two alleles controlling the same character. They are called','[{"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polyalleles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple alleles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When there are more than two, i.e., three alleles, governing the same character. Since in an individual only two alleles can be present, multiple alleles can be found only when population studies are made.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50185,'biology',93,275,533,'In ABO system a person has','[{"text": "2 alleles", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "3 alleles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "No alleles", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple alleles", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The gene ($I$) has three alleles $I$A, $I$B and i. But a person will have only 2 alleles.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50186,'biology',93,275,533,'A mother with blood group B type has a child with blood type O. What is the possibility of the genotypes of that mother and father?','[{"text": "${I^A}{I^B}$ (father) and ${I^B}{I^B}$ (mother)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${I^A}{I^A}$ (father) and ${I^B}{I^O}$ (mother)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${I^B}{I^o}$ (father) and  ${I^A}{I^O}$ (mother)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${I^A}{I^O}$(father) and ${I^B}{I^O}$ (mother)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the parents are heterozygous to the trait, and the child has received recessive traits from either parent.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50199,'biology',93,276,534,'Law of independent assortment is always true or applicable if two genes are located on','[{"text": "Same chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Different chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Same locus of different chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Different locus of same chromosome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Genes located on same chromosome show linkage, so law of independent assortment is true for genes located on different chromosome.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50187,'biology',93,275,533,'Inheritance of ABO blood group system is an example of','[{"text": "Partial dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Epistasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple allelism", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The human blood group system is a good example of multiple allelism. Humans have rbcs which are of type A, type B or type O. Following Mendel’s laws of inheritance, the three different alleles can be combined in\nvarious ways. As a result , genotypes make either type A, type B, type AB or type O blood.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50188,'biology',93,275,533,'ABO blood group is determined by three different alleles. How many genotypes and phenotypes are possible?','[{"text": "Genotype-6 &emsp; Phenotype-4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Genotype-3 &emsp; Phenotype-1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genotype-4 &emsp; Phenotype-6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genotype-9 &emsp; Phenotype-7", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'ABO blood group is determined by three different alleles. This gives rise to six possible genotypes and four possible blood types(phenotypes).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50189,'biology',93,275,533,'ABO blood grouping in human being cites the example of','[{"text": "Polygenic inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Co-dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 2 and 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The human blood group system is a good example of multiple allelism and codominance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50190,'biology',93,275,533,'The probability of having a child with blood group O to parents with blood groups A and B is','[{"text": "1 out of 4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "2 out of 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 out of 4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 out of 4", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'After all the blood group of parents are A and B, accordingly the their genotypes would be AO and BO. Thus, the desirable genotypes of their children will be AO, BO, AB and OO i.e., the probable blood groups are A, B,AB and O (that means any one out of these four) .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50191,'biology',93,275,533,'Match the columns I and II.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Incomplete dominance<br>B. Co-dominance<br>C. Pleiotropy</div><div class="column-right">P.  ABO blood group<br>Q.  Snapdragon<br>R.  Sickle cell anaemia</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R , B – P , C – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q , B – R , C – P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P , B – R , C – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q , B – P , C – R", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-R.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50192,'biology',93,275,533,'What will be possible blood group in children from the parents with O and AB blood groups?','[{"text": "A, O", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A, B, AB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, O", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A, B only as one parent is homozygous recessive and the other is dominant .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50193,'biology',93,275,533,'Consider the following statements regarding ABO blood group in human.<br>I. It is controlled by multiple alleles.<br>II. It shows codominance<br>III. Presence of fats on the surface of the RBC<br>Which of the following statement(s) given above are false ?','[{"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The plasma membrane of the red blood cells has sugar polymers that protrude from its surface and the kind of sugar is controlled by the gene.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50194,'biology',93,275,533,'In garden pea, starch is synthesised effectively in','[{"text": "Hybrid round seeded plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterozygous round seeded plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wrinkled seeded plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homozygous round seeded plants", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'After maturation of the seeds, BB seeds are round and the bb seeds are wrinkled.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50195,'biology',93,275,533,'Which of the following option (s) is/are correct for starch synthesis in pea seeds controlled by single gene which has two allelic forms B and b?','[{"text": "BB is round seed with large starch synthesis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "bb is wrinkled seed with large starch synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bb is round seed with less startch synthesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Starch is synthesised effectively by BB homozygotes and therefore, large starch grains are produced. In contrast, bb homozygotes have lesser efficiency in starch synthesis and produce smaller starch grains. After maturation of the seeds, BB seeds are round and the bb seeds are wrinkled. Heterozygotes produce round seeds, and so B seems to be the dominant allele. But, the starch grains produced are of intermediate size in Bb seeds',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50196,'biology',93,275,533,'Starch synthesis gene in pea plant in heterozygous condition produces starch grain of intermediate size. This shows','[{"text": "Complete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Codominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Starch grain size is considered as the phenotype, then from this angle, the alleles show incomplete dominance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50197,'biology',93,275,533,'Shape of a seed in Pisum sativum depends on starch granules size; so inheritance of seed shape shows _______________ relationship, while inheritance of starch grains show _____________.','[{"text": "Dominant recessive; incomplete\\ndominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multiple allelism; codominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy; codominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Codominance; incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Starch grain size is considered as the phenotype, the alleles show incomplete  dominance.Whereas seed shape shows dominant-round and recessive wrinkled relationship.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50198,'biology',93,275,533,'Find the incorrect statement<br>i. The starch grains produced are of intermediate size in bb seeds.<br>ii. Dominance is an autonomous feature of a gene or the product that it has information for<br>iii. Starch grain size is considered as the phenotype, then from this angle, the alleles show incomplete dominance','[{"text": "i and ii", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "i only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The starch grains produced are of intermediate size in Bb seeds & dominance is not an autonomous feature of a gene or the product that it has information for.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50200,'biology',93,276,534,'Out of the four phenotypes obtained in ${F_2}$ generation of dihybrid cross between yellow round and green wrinkled seeds of pea plant,','[{"text": "All were parental combination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All were with recessive trait", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All were new combination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two were parental and two were new\\ncombination", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The two parental combinations obtained were yellow round and green wrinkled. And the two new combinations formed were yellow wrinkled and green round.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50201,'biology',93,276,534,'Law of independent assortment can be proved by','[{"text": "Back cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Test cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dihybrid cross", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monohybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Dihybrid cross proves law of independent assortment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50202,'biology',93,276,534,'The independent assortment of two pairs of genes located on non-homologous chromosomes, occur as a result of the random orientation of chromosome during:','[{"text": "Telophase of the first meiotic division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase of the first meiotic division", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prophase of the second meiotic division", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The brief interphase between the two\\nmeiotic divisions", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Metaphase of meiosis - $I$ , the homologus chromosome align at the equator and separate during anaphase- $I$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50203,'biology',93,276,534,'Phenotypic ratio observed in dihybrid cross is','[{"text": "$3:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1:2:1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$9:7$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$9:3:3:1$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'9:3:3:1 is the phenotypic ratio of dihybrid cross.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50204,'biology',93,276,534,'The cytological event that corresponds to Mendel’s law of independent assortment is seen in:','[{"text": "Metaphase I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Anaphase II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Anaphase $I$ is the cytological event which corresponds to Mendel’s law of independent assortment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50205,'biology',93,276,534,'Mendel formulated the laws of heredity considering seven pairs of characters in the pea plant. If he had studied an eighth pair, the law which would have been altered is:','[{"text": "Law of independent assortment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of unit character", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mendel conducted dihybrid cross, and postulated the Law of Independent assortment, third law of principles of inheritance. Later it is not applicable to majority of organisms, because in the chromosomes, genes or characters are many and linked with one another. Due to this linkage, chances of separation of genes is less, results the less appearance of new characters in the progeny. It might be the exception, to the law of independent assortment. So, the correct option is ‘Law of independent assortment’.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50206,'biology',93,276,534,'Which of the following points further strengthened Mendelism?','[{"text": "Law of independent assortment which\\nwas based on monohybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Incomplete dominance gave a new way to\\nMendelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of independent assortment which\\ncould be stated on the basis of segregation\\nof gametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A character controlled by a pair of unit\\nfactors", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Law of independent assortment that could be stated on the basis of segregation of gametes. This point further strengthened Mendelism.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50207,'biology',93,276,534,'Heterozygous tall and red flowered pea plants are selfed and total 2000 seeds are collected. What is the total number of seeds for both Heterozygous traits?','[{"text": "500", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "250", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "750", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1250", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The cross is between TtRr x TtRr (where T is dominant on t and gives tallness over dwarfness while the R is dominant over r and gives red colour). So, on the crossing, we found that out of 16,4 progenies are having both the traits as heterozygous which are highlighted in the cross. So, out of 2000 progeny seeds formed the number of progenies with heterozygous traits are- 4/16 × 2000 = 500 seeds. So, the correct answer is ‘500’.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50208,'biology',93,276,534,'Some characters did not assort independently. Later researchers found it to be due to','[{"text": "Linkage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dominance of one trait over the other", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crossing over", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Amitosis", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mendel always observed independent assortment of genes, but his law was not accepted universally and later on Bateson and Punnett, Hutchinson and Morgan observed that genes have inclination towards inheriting in groups rather than individually. Such tendency of two or more genes to remain together during inheritance in the same chromosome is called linkage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50209,'biology',93,276,534,'Mendelian recombinations are due to :','[{"text": "Independent assortment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mutation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotrophy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crossing over", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Genetic linkage or recombinations is the exceptions to the Law of Independent Assortment. When DNA segments are situated near each other on the same chromosome, most probably they will inherit together. Though through recombination, where really DNA is separated and rejoined, these linkages are intermixed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50210,'biology',93,276,534,'In the cross Aa Bb X Aa Bb, what proportion of gametes are homozygous for both the traits','[{"text": "$2{\\\\rm{/}}16$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{1/4}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0/}}16$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{4/}}16$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Gametes can have only one allele and can never be homozygous. This term is associated with the genotypes of an organism no and not with the gametes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50211,'biology',93,276,534,'If a character is controlled by six alleles of a gene, then the possible genotypes would be','[{"text": "729", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "21", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "42", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "64", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The number of genotype possible is the sum of integers between 1 and  $n$.<br> $n$ = no of given alleles no. of possible genotype = 1+2+3+4+5+6=21.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50212,'biology',93,276,534,'In order to find out the different types of gametes produced by a pea plant having the genotype AaBb, it should be crossed to a plant with the genotype','[{"text": "AABB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "aaBB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "aabb", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "AaBb", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In the given question AaBb should be crossed with aabb. Scientists perform test cross to find out the different types of gametes or the genotypes of an unknown individual. Test cross is performed always between the  ${F_1}$ heterozygous plants and pure recessive (homozygous) parent plant. So, in the given case AaBb should be crossed with aabb.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50213,'biology',93,276,534,'Total 512 seeds are collected from the cross  ${W_W}{Y_Y} \\times {W_W}{Y_Y}$. Find the number of plants produced with first dominant and second recessive trait.','[{"text": "96", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "288", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "320", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "32", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'First dominant & second Recessive are<br> (RRyy, Rryy, Rryy)<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{3}}}{{16}} \\times 512 = 96$',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50214,'biology',93,276,534,'A human male produces sperms with the genotypes AB, Ab, aB and ab pertaining to two diallelic characters in equal proportions. What is the corresponding genotype of the person ?','[{"text": "AaBb", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "AaBB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AABB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AABb", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'As the sperms produced by the human male are with genotypes AB, Ab, aB and ab(with two diallelic characters), therefore the person must be heterozygous for both genes. Therefore, his genotype will be AaBb. According to the rule of 2$n$ where $n$ = number of heterozygous pairs of genes. Thus, ${2^2} = 4$ types of combinations are formed AB, Ab, aB and ab.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50215,'biology',93,276,534,'Types of gametes formed by the plant with genotype AABbccDD will be','[{"text": "16", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only one gene is heterozygous, Thus, ${2^1} = 2$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50216,'biology',93,276,534,'How many genetically different gametes will be produced by a heterozygous plant having the genotype Aa Bb Cc?','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Genetically eight different gametes will be produced viz., ABC, ABc, AbC, $Abc$, aBC, aBc, abC, abc. ${2^3} = 8$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50217,'biology',93,276,534,'Consider the following four statements (A,B,C, and D) and select the right option for incorrect statements.<br>i. Mendelian experiments had large sampling size, which gave greater credibility to the data that he collected.<br>ii. Recessive allele influences the appearance of pheno-type even in the presence of an alternative allele.<br>iii. Multiple alleles can be found only when population studies are made.<br>iv. In ${F_2}$ generation of Mendelian monohybrid cross, the tall and dwarf traits were identical to their parental types and showed blending.<br>The incorrect statements are','[{"text": "iii and iv", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "i and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iii", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ii and iv", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement ii and iv are wrong.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50218,'biology',93,276,534,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Monohybrid phenotype<br>B. Monohybrid genotype<br>C. Dihybrid genotype<br>D. Dihybrid phenotype</div><div class="column-right">P. 3:1<br>Q. 1:2:1:2:4:2:1: 2:1<br>R. 1:2:1<br>S. 9:3:3:1</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R , B – P , C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q , B – R , C – P, D – S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P , B – R , C – Q, D – S", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – Q , B – P , C – R , D – S", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-P, B-R, C-Q, D-S.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50219,'biology',93,276,534,'Which of the following laws is universally accepted?','[{"text": "Law of dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of segregation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of co- dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Law of segregation is universally accepted',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50220,'biology',93,276,534,'Why is law of independent assortment not universally accepted?','[{"text": "Due to Law of dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Due to Law of segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Due to Linkage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Due to Law of Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mendel always observed independent assortment of genes, but his law was not accepted universally and later on Bateson and Punnett, Hutchinson and Morgan observed that genes have inclination towards inheriting in groups rather than individually. Such tendency of two or more genes to remain together during inheritance in the same chromosome is called linkage.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50221,'biology',93,276,534,'Why is law of dominance not universally accepted?','[{"text": "Due to co-dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Due to Law of Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Due to Linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both 1 & 2", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Law of dominance is not universally accepted due incomplete dominance and codominance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50222,'biology',93,279,537,'Traits controlled by three or more genes are called as_____','[{"text": "Co-dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polygenic traits", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Traits are generally controlled by three or more genes and are called as polygenic traits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50223,'biology',93,279,537,'Skin colour inheritance in man is:','[{"text": "Epistasis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex-linked", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monogenic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polygenic", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Human Skin colour is a very good example of polygenic (i.e. multiple gene) inheritance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50224,'biology',93,279,537,'What concept do the following sentences explain?<br>i. Human height is an example of this trait<br>ii. Human skin colour is another classic example for this<br>iii. It takes into account the influence of environment<br>iv. In this trait, the effect of each allele is additive','[{"text": "Multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polygenic inheritance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Codominance", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The statements mentioned explain polygenic inheritance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50225,'biology',93,279,537,'In case of polygenic inheritance of skin colour, the genotype with all the __________alleles (AABBCC) will have the __________skin colour and that with all the __________alleles (aabbcc) will have the ________skin colour.','[{"text": "Recessive, darkest, dominant, lightest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant, darkest, recessive, lightest", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dominant, darkest, dominant, lightest", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Recessive, darkest, recessive, lightest", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The genotype with all the dominant alleles (AABBCC) will have the darkest skin colour and that with all the recessive alleles (aabbcc) will have the lightest skin colour.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50226,'biology',93,277,535,'Mendel published his work on inheritance of characters in','[{"text": "1856", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1865", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1866", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1863", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Mendel published his work on inheritance of characters in 1865 but for several reasons, it remained unrecognised till 1900.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50227,'biology',93,277,535,'Mendel’s work remained unrecognised till 1900 because','[{"text": "Mendel was unable to explain the concept\\nof variation with regards to factor and\\nunable to provide physical proof for\\nexistence of factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "communication was not easy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Application of maths to biology was not\\naccepted", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of them", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Firstly,communication was not easy (as it is now) in those days and his work could not be widely publicised. Secondly, his concept of genes (or factors, in Mendel’s words) as stable and discrete units that controlled the expression of traits and, of the pair of alleles which did not ‘blend’with each other, was not accepted by his contemporaries as an explanation for the apparently continuous variation seen in nature.Thirdly, Mendel’s approach of using mathematics to explain biological phenomena was totally new and unacceptable to many of the biologists of his time. Finally, though Mendel’s work suggested that factors (genes)were discrete units, he could not provide any physical proof for the existence of factors or say what they were made of.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50228,'biology',93,277,535,'Mendel’s work remained unrecognised till 1900 because<br>(a) Mendel’s approach of using mathematics to explain biological phenomena was totally new and unacceptable to many of the biologists of his time<br>(b) Concept of genes (or factors, in Mendel’s words) as stable and discrete units that controlled the expression of traits and, of the pair of alleles which did not ‘blend’ with each other, was not accepted by his contemporaries','[{"text": "(a) is correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(a), (b) correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(b) is correct only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are wrong", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Both the statements are correct .',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50229,'biology',93,277,535,'Mendel’s result on inheritance of characters were rediscovered by','[{"text": "de Vries", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Correns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Von Tshermak", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mendel and his laws were rediscovered by Hugo Marie de Vries, Karl Franz Joseph Correns and Erich Tschermak von Seyesenegg',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50230,'biology',93,277,535,'In 1900 A.D. three biologists independently discovered Mendel’s principles. They are','[{"text": "De Vries, Correns and Tschermak", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Correns, Punnet and Watson", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sutton, Morgan and Correns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Avery, McLeod and McCarty", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mendel’s work was essentially ignored. However, at the beginning of the twentieth century, Mendel and his laws were rediscovered by Hugo Marie de Vries, Karl Franz Joseph Correns and Erich Tschermak von Seyesenegg.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50231,'biology',93,277,535,'The literal meaning of chromosome is','[{"text": "Genetic body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coloured body", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Replicating body", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thread-like body", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Chromosomes (colored bodies, as they were visualised by staining).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50232,'biology',93,277,535,'Chromosomes were first seen by','[{"text": "Flemming", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Waldeyer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Strasburger", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hofmeister", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Chromosomes are thread-like DNA protein complex which carry genetic material in a linear series of genes. In 1848, W. Hofmeister first discovered chromosomes in the dividing pollen mother cells of Tradescantia. And in 1875, Strasburger first observed chromosome during cell division.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50233,'biology',93,277,535,'Select the correct option<br>A. Chromosomes -Divide and double, colored bodies, as they were visualised by staining.<br> B. By 1902, the chromosome movement during mitosis had been worked out','[{"text": "A and B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only A is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only A is correct.In 1902, the chromosome movement during meiosis had been worked out.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50234,'biology',93,277,535,'Who observed that the behaviour of chromosomes at meiosis can serve as the cellular basis of both segregation and independent assortment?','[{"text": "Morgan and Boveri", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sutton and Boveri", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Boveri and Brauer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "W. Flemming", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Walter Sutton and Theodore Boveri noted that the behaviour of chromosomes was parallel to the behaviour of genes and used chromosome movement (Figure 5.8) to explain Mendel’s laws.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50235,'biology',93,277,535,'One pair segregates independently of other pair is always applicable for','[{"text": "Chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Gene", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Neither chromosome nor gene", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both chromosome and gene", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'One pair segregates independently of other pair is always applicable for Gene',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50236,'biology',93,277,535,'Match the columns I and II.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Independent pairs segregate independently of each other<br>B. One pair segregated independently of another pair<br>C. Anaphase-I</div><div class="column-right">P. Gene<br>Q. Separation of homologous chromosome<br>R. Chromosome</div></div>','[{"text": "A – R, B – P , C – Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A – Q, B – R, C – P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – P , B – R, C – Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A – Q, B – P , C – R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A-R, B-P, C-Q',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50237,'biology',93,277,535,'Which of the following statement for chromosomal theory of inheritance is incorrect?','[{"text": "Pairing and separation of a pair of\\nchromosomes would not lead to the\\nsegregation of a factor they carried", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Behaviour of chromosomes is parallel to\\nthe behaviour of genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The two alleles of a gene pair are located\\non homologous sites on homologous\\nchromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomes as well as genes occur in\\npairs", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sutton and Boveri argued that the pairing and separation of a pair of chromosomes would lead to the segregation of a pair of factors they carried.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50238,'biology',93,277,535,'Two alternative forms of a gene do not blend with each other and maintain its discrete nature it is explained by','[{"text": "Law of dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Law of segregation", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Law of independent assortment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Unit of hypothesis", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Two alternative forms of a gene do not blend with each other and maintain its discrete nature it is explained by Law of segregation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50239,'biology',93,277,535,'The phenomenon of exchange of segments between paternal and maternal chromosomes is called','[{"text": "Recombination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crossing over", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The phenomenon of exchange of segments between paternal and maternal chromosomes is called Crossing over',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50240,'biology',93,277,535,'Name the scientist who argued that the pairing and separation of a pair of chromosomes would lead to the segregation of a pair of factors they carried?','[{"text": "Boveri only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sutton and Boveri", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Boveri and Mendel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sutton only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Sutton and Boveri argued that the pairing and separation of a pair of chromosomes would lead to the segregation of a pair of factors they carried.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50241,'biology',93,277,535,'Sutton united the knowledge of chromosomal segregation with Mendelian principles and called it the________________','[{"text": "Nuclear theory of inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Nucleolar theory of inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosomal theory of inheritance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sex chromosomal theory of inheritance", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Sutton united the knowledge of chromosomal segregation with Mendelian principles and called it the chromosomal theory of inheritance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50242,'biology',93,277,535,'Which alphabet is represented correctly with its phase?','[{"text": "D - Diploid cells", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C - Meiosis - II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D - ${G_2}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'C- Meiosis-II.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/93_50242_question_1.png'),
(50243,'biology',93,278,536,'Experimental verification of the chromosomal theory of inheritance was given by','[{"text": "Sutton and Boveri", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Correns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "T.H.Morgan", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mendel", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Experimental verification of the chromosomal theory of inheritance by Thomas Hunt Morgan.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50244,'biology',93,278,536,'Fruit flies are one of the best materials for genetic studies because of all, except','[{"text": "Ability to grow on simple synthetic\\nmedium in the laboratory", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Short life span", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Production of a large number of progeny\\nin each mating", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of few externally visible and\\n\\t identifiable contrasting traits", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Drosophila melanogaster which were found very suitable for such studies. They could be grown on simple synthetic medium in the laboratory. They complete their life cycle in about two weeks, and a single mating\ncould produce a large number of progeny flies. Also, there was a clear differentiation of the sexes – the male and female flies are easily distinguishable. It has many types of hereditary variations that can be seen with low power microscopes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50245,'biology',93,277,535,'The following figure represents<br>','[{"text": "Only spermatogenesis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Independent assortment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex determination", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The diagram represents independent assortment.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/93_50245_question_1.png'),
