(50250,'biology',93,278,536,'Select the appropriate option<br> a. Morgan knew that the genes were located on the Y chromosome<br>b. Morgan hybridised yellow-bodied, white-eyed females to brown-bodied, red-eyed males and intercrossed their ${F_1}$ progeny.','[{"text": "Only a is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only b is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "a and b is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of them is correct", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Morgan and his group knew that the genes were located on the X chromosome, So statement b is correct only.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50251,'biology',93,284,547,'Which of the following statement is correct?','[{"text": "Change in whole set of chromosomes is called aneuploidy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sickle cell anaemia is a quantitative problem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female carrier for haemophilia may transmit the disease to sons", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Thalassemia is a qualitative problem", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Female carrier for haemophilia may transmit disease to sons <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50251_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50252,'biology',93,278,536,'‘Gene – mapping’ technology was developed\nby','[{"text": "Correns", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sturtvent", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mendel", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tschermak", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Gene mapping technology developed by\nSturtvent by recombination frequency',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50253,'biology',93,280,538,'Find the correct statement<br>I. Generally a gene regulates a trait, but sometimes one has effect on multiple traits<br>II. The trait AB – blood group of man is regulated by one dominant allele and another recessive allele. Hence it is co – dominant.','[{"text": "Statement II is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements I and II are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are wrong", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I is correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Generally a gene regulates a trait, but some\ntimes one gene has effect on multiple traits is\ncalled pleiotropy.<br>The trait AB blood group of Man is regulated\nby both dominant alleles called codominance.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50254,'biology',93,281,539,'In male heterogametic type of sex\ndetermination','[{"text": "Female parent produces dissimilar\\ngametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male parent produces dissimilar gametes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Males do not produce gametes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male parent produces similar gametes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Male parent produces dissimilar gametes.\nHeterogametes means production of dissimilar\ngametes<br>Eg: Human males are heterogametic i.e. XY',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50255,'biology',93,273,531,'In one of the hybridization experiments, a\nhomozygous dominant parent and a\nhomozygous recessive parent are crossed for\na trait. (Plant shows Mendelian inheritance\npattern)','[{"text": "Dominant parent trait appears in both ${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}{\\\\rm{\\\\& }}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ generations, recessive parent trait appears in only ${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ generation.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Dominant parent trait appears in ${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}$ generation and recessive parent trait appears in ${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}{\\\\rm{\\\\& }}{{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ generations.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant parent trait appears in ${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ generation and recessive parent trait appears only in ${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}$ generation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominant parent trait appears in ${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{1}}}$ generation and recessive parent trait appears in ${{\\\\rm{F}}_{\\\\rm{2}}}$ generation", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dominant parent trait appears in both ${{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{\\& }}{{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ generation and recessive parent trait appears in only ${{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ generation',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50256,'biology',93,280,538,'The phenomenon of pleiotropism refers to','[{"text": "Presence of several alleles of a single gene controlling a single crossover", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Presence of two alleles, each of the two genes controlling a single trait", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A single gene affecting multiple\\nphenotypic expression", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "More than two genes affecting a single\\ncharacter", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'When a single gene affects multiple\nphenotypic expression, the gene is called\npleiotropic gene and the phenomenon is called\npleiotropism.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50257,'biology',93,278,536,'Frequency of recombination between gene pairs on same chromosome as a measure of the distance between genes to map their position on chromosome, was used for the first time by','[{"text": "Thomas Hunt Morgan", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sutton and Boveri", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alfred Sturtevant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Henking", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Alfred Sturtevant used the frequency of\nrecombination between gene pairs on the same\nchromosome as a measure of the distance\nbetween genes and ‘mapped’ their position on\nthe chromosome.<br>Thomas Hunt Morgan proved chromosomal theory of inheritance and proposed the concept of linkage.\n<br>Sutton and Boveri proposed chromosomal\ntheory of inheritance.\nHenking discovered X-chromosome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50258,'biology',93,285,549,'Which of the following statements are correct about Klinefelter’s Syndrome?\nA. This disorder was first described by\nLangdon Down (1866).\nB. Such an individual has overall masculine\ndevelopment. However, the feminine\ndevelopement is also expressed.\nC. The affected individual is short statured.\nD. Physical, psychomotor and mental\ndevelopment is retarded.\nE. Such individuals are sterile.\nChoose the correct answer from the options\ngiven below:','[{"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B and E only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and E only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Klinefelter’s syndrome is caused due to the\npresence of an additional copy of\nX-chromosome resulting into a karyotype of\n47, XXY. Such an individual has overall\nmasculine development, however, the feminine\ndevelopment is also expressed. Such\nindividuals are sterile. Thus, statement B and E\nare correct regarding Klinefelter’s syndrome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50259,'biology',93,285,548,'Broad palm with single palm crease is visible\nin a person suffering from-','[{"text": "Down’s syndrome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Turner’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Klinefelter’s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thalassemia", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Down’s syndrome is caused by an\nadditional copy of chromosome number 21.\nIts symptoms include–<br>1. Broad palm with characteristic palm crease\n<br>2. Short statured with small round head\n<br>3. Furrowed tongue and partially open mouth,\netc.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50260,'biology',93,283,541,'Which one of the following symbols represents mating between relatives in human pedigree analysis?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The symbol representing mating between relatives (consanguineous mating) in human pedigree analysis is . <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50260_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50261,'biology',93,272,530,'A condition where a certain gene is present in only a single copy in a diploid cell is called:','[{"text": "Homozygous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemizygous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Heterozygous", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Monogamous .", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Hemizygous is a condition in which only one copy of a gene or DNA sequence is present in diploid cells. Males are hemizygous for most genes on sex chromosomes, having only one $\\mathrm{X}$ and one $\\mathrm{Y}$ chromosome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50262,'biology',93,276,534,'A dihybrid test cross-yielding a result of $1: 1$ : $1: 1$ ratio is indicative of:','[{"text": "4 different types of generation dihybrids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 different types of gametes produced by the parent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 different types of gametes produced by the dihybrid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Homozygous condition of the dihybrid", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A dihybrid cross describes a mating experiment between two organisms that are identically hybrid for two traits. Test crossing a dihybrid, resulted in $1: 1: 1: 1$ ratios, confirming that genes are assorting independently. Thus, dihybrid forms four types of gametes in equal numbers.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2008,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50263,'biology',93,272,530,'A true breeding plant producing red flowers is crossed with a pure plant producing white flowers. Allele for red colour of flower is dominant. After selfing , the plants of first filial generation, the proportion of plants producing white flowers in the progeny would be:','[{"text": "$\\\\dfrac{1}{4}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{1}{3}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{1}{2}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\dfrac{3}{4}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50263_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50264,'biology',93,275,533,'The offspring produced from a marriage have only $\\mathrm{O}$ or  $\\mathrm{A}$ blood groups. Of the genotypes given below, the possible genotypes of the parents would be:','[{"text": "$I^{A} I^{o}$ and $I^{o} I^{o}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$I^{A} I^{A}$ and $I^{O} I^{O}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$I^{A} I^{O}$ and $I^{O} I^{O}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$I^{A} I^{A}$ and $I^{A} I^{O}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50264_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50265,'biology',93,275,533,'Four children belonging to the same parents have the following blood groups:<br>$\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B},   \\mathrm{AB}$ and $\\mathrm{O}$. Hence, the genotypes of the two parents are:','[{"text": "Both parents are homozygous for \' $\\\\mathrm{A}$ \' group", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One parent is homozygous for \' $\\\\mathrm{A}$ \' and another parent is homozygous for \' $\\\\mathrm{B}$ \'", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One parent is heterozygous for \' $\\\\mathrm{A}$ \' and another parent is heterozygous for \' $\\\\mathrm{B}$ \'", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both parents are homozygous for \' $\\\\mathrm{B}$ \' group", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In men, ABO blood group is best example\nof multiple allelism. The four children of\nblood group. A, B, AB and O can be born only\nif both the parents are heterozygous for A and\nB, which means the genotype of one parent is\n${l^A}l$ and of other is${l^B}l$, <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50265_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2011,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50266,'biology',93,276,534,'In a typical Mendelian cross which is a dihybrid cross, one parent is homozygous for both dominant traits and another parent is homozygous for both recessive traits. In the generation, both parental combinations and recombination appear. The phenotypic ratio of parental combinations to recombination is:','[{"text": "$10: 6$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$12: 4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$9: 7$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$15: 1$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A cross of homozygous round yellow seeds (RRYY) and homozygous green wrinkled seed (rryy) plants produced 9:3:3:1 ratio of plants. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50266_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50266_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50267,'biology',93,275,533,'With regard to the ${\\rm{A B O}}$ blood typing system, if a man who has type $\\mathrm{B}$ blood and a woman who has type $\\mathrm{O}$ blood were to have children, what blood types could the children have?','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}$ or $\\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{B}$ or $\\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{AB}$ or $\\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}, \\\\mathrm{B}, \\\\mathrm{AB}$ or $\\\\mathrm{O}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The man has type B blood group; his genotype $l^{B} l^{B}$ can be or $l^{B} \\mathrm{i}$.<br>The woman has type $\\mathrm{O}$ blood group; her genotype can be ii only.<br>The blood type of child will be either B or O This is illustrated below;<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{l^B}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{l^B}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{l^B}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{i}}\\\\\n{\\rm{i}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{l^B}{\\rm{i}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{l^B}{\\rm{i}}\\,\\,{\\rm{or}}\\,\\,{\\rm{i}}\\\\\n{l^B}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ii}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{l^B}{\\rm{i}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{i}}{l^B}{\\rm{ii}}\\,\\\\\n{\\rm{ii}}\\,\n\\end{array}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50268,'biology',93,284,544,'If father shows normal genotype and mother shows a carrier trait for haemophilia:','[{"text": "All the female offspring will be normal.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the female offspring will be carriers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A male offspring has $50 \\\\%$ chances of active disease.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Female offspring has probability of $50 \\\\%$ to have active disease.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'If father shows normal genotype (XY) and mother shows a carrier trait for haemophilia $\\left(\\mathrm{XX}^{\\mathrm{h}}\\right)$ <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50268_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Thus, a male offspring has $50 \\%$ chances of getting active disease, while a female offspring has $50 \\%$  chance of being a carrier.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2012,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50276,'biology',93,285,549,'Which of the following conditions correctly describes the manner of determining the sex in the given example?','[{"text": "XO type of sex determines male sex in grasshopper.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "XO condition in humans as found in Klinefelter\'s syndrome determines female sex.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homozygous sex chromosome XX produce male in <i>Drosophila</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homozygous sex chromosome ZZ determine female sex in birds.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Homozygous sex chromosome XX produces female in Drosophila. Homozygous sex chromosome ZZ determines male sex in birds and some reptiles. In Klinefelter\'s syndrome there is trisomy of sex chromosome, $44+$ XXY.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50269,'biology',93,284,543,'A colour-blind man marries the daughter of another colour-blind man whose wife had a normal genotype for colour vision. IN their progeny:','[{"text": "All the children would colour-blind", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All their sons are colour-blind", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the daughters would be colour-blind", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Half of their sons and half of their daughters would be colour- blind", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The daughter of a colour-blind man$\\left(\\mathrm{X}^{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{Y}\\right)$ whose wife had a normal genotype ${\\rm{(X Y)}}$ for colour vision would have $\\left(\\mathrm{X}^{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{Y}\\right)$ genotype.<br>On marrying a colour-blind man $\\left(\\mathrm{X}^{\\mathrm{C}} \\mathrm{Y}\\right)$. They children are expected to have: <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50269_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Thus, half of their sons and half of their daughters will be colour-blind.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50270,'biology',93,277,535,'Read the statements and choose the correct option.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">For a particular character in an individual, each gamete gets only one allele.<br></div><div class="column-right">Chromatids of a chromosome split (separate) and move towards opposite poles during anaphase of mitosis.</div></div>','[{"text": "Both the statements are correct, and Statement B is the reason for Statement A.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both the statements are correct, and Statement B is not the reason for Statement A.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is correct and Statement B is wrong.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement B is correct, and Statement A is wrong.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The two contrasting traits or alternate forms of a gene which appears on the same locus are called allele. Gametes contain either of the two alleles in equal proportion. Mendel established two principles of genetic transmission:<br>The alleles of a gene segregate from each other, and the alleles of different genes assort independently.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(50271,'biology',93,272,530,'In garden pea, round shape of seeds is dominant over wrinkled shape. A pea plant heterozygous for round shape of seed is selfed and 1600 seeds produced during the cross are subsequently germinated. How many seedlings would have the parental phenotype?','[{"text": "1600", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "800", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "400", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1200", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'As pea plant is heterozygous for round shape, its genotype would be Rr.<br>Parents:<br>Progeny: <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50271_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Phenotypically, the ratio will be $3: 1$ i.e., only rr seeding will show wrinkled phenotype. rest will show round shape When the total number of seeds is 1600 so 1200 - Round shape (RR,Rr) 400-Wrinkled (rr)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50272,'biology',93,285,548,'Down\'s syndrome is an example for:','[{"text": "Aneuploidy of sex chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aneuploidy of autosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Syndrome caused due to gene mutation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Loss of one sex chromosome from the diploid set", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An aneuploidy organism or cell is the one having a chromosome number that is not an exact multiple of the monoploid (n) with one genome. A trisomy is a condition in which an individual has inherited an extra chromosome, resulting in three copies of a particular chromosome instead of the usual two copies. Therefore, the individual would have 47 instead of 46 chromosomes. The presence of an extra copy of chromosome 21 leads to Down syndrome.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50273,'biology',93,275,533,'Identify the wrong statement.','[{"text": "Alleles $\\\\mathrm{I}^{\\\\mathrm{A}}$ and $\\\\mathrm{I}^{\\\\mathrm{B}}$ produce sugars.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both $\\\\mathrm{I}^{\\\\mathrm{A}}$ and $\\\\mathrm{I}^{\\\\mathrm{B}}$ are present together and they express because of co-dominance.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Alleles b and c also produce sugar.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "When $\\\\mathrm{I}^{\\\\mathrm{B}}$ and $\\\\mathrm{b}$ or $\\\\mathrm{i}$ are present only $\\\\mathrm{I}^{\\\\mathrm{B}}$ is expressed.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'ABO blood group in humans is controlled by three multiple alleles, and i. There are two types of antigens present in the surface coating of red blood cells-A and B. The and alleles produce enzyme glycosyltransferase for synthesis of sugars. The sugars are attached to lipids and produce glycolipids. These glycolipids then associate with membrane of RBC to form blood group antigens. Allele i does not produce any enzyme/ antigen. Both and are codominant (i.e., able to express themselves in presence of each other) but are dominant over i.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50274,'biology',93,284,546,'With respect to phenylketonuria identify which statement is not correct.','[{"text": "It is an example of pleiotropy.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is an error in metabolism.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is a case of aneuploidy.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Caused due to autosomal recessive trait.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Phenylketonuria is an inborn error of metabolism. It is an autosomal recessive disorder in which the homozygous recessive individual lacks the enzyme phenylalanine hydroxylase needed to change phenylalanine (amino acid) to tyrosine (amino acid) in the liver. Lack of the enzyme is due to abnormal autosomal recessive gene on chromosome 12 . The defective gene influences many characters, so it is an example of pleiotropic gene.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50275,'biology',93,285,548,'Three copies of chromosome 21 in a child with Down\'s syndrome have been analysed using molecular biology technology to detect any possible DNA polymorphism with reference to different alleles located on chromosome 21. Results showed that out of 3 copies 2 of the chromosomes of the child contain the same alleles as one of the mother\'s alleles. Based on this when did the non-disjunction event most likely occur?','[{"text": "Maternal meiosis I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Maternal meiosis II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Paternal meiosis I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Paternal meiosis II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Down\'s syndrome is an autosomal aneuploidy, caused by the presence of an extra chromosome number 21. Both the chromosomes of the pair 21 pass into a single egg due to non-disjunction during oogenesis. The non-disjunction is more common in females. The frequency of non-disjunction of chromosome pair 21 increases with mothers age. Usually non-disjunction of chromosomes takes place in meiosis 1 .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50277,'biology',93,284,546,'The gene disorder phenylketonuria is an example for:','[{"text": "Polygenic inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Multiple allelism", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Multiple factor", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In human beings, pleiotropy is exhibited by sickle cell anaemia and phenylketonuria. In phenylketonuria, due to mutation of a gene that codes for the enzyme phenyl alanine hydroxylase, causes mental retardation and a reduction in hair and skin pigmentation.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50278,'biology',93,284,544,'The gene for haemophilia is located on \' $\\mathrm{X}$ \' chromosome. Hence it is normally impossible for a:','[{"text": "Haemophilic father to pass the gene to his daughter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carrier mother to pass the gene to her daughter", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Carrier mother to pass the gene to her son", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemophilic father to pass the gene to his son", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In males, a single gene for defect is able to express itself as the $\\mathrm{Y}$ chromosome has no allele for this gene. If a male is then he is haemophilic. The males inherit the mutation from their heterozygous mothers. These males reproduce and pass the mutation to their daughters, who are not affected as they inherit a wild-type allele from their mothers. Also, affected males never transmit the mutant allele to their sons.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50279,'biology',93,284,544,'A human male is heterozygous for autosomal genes \' A\' and \' B \'. He is also hemizygous for haemophilic gene \' h \'. What percentage of sperms will carry \'abh\' genotype?','[{"text": "$25 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$50 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$75 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$0 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The genotype of human male should be . Thus, types of gametes would be formed that includes . Clearly, only proportion that is $25 \\%$ of his sperms would be abh.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50280,'biology',93,283,541,'From the following pedigree chart of a family, one can make an analysis that:','[{"text": "It is an autosomal dominant trait", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is an autosomal recessive trait", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It is an allosomal dominant trait", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It is an allosomal recessive trait", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Since both female and male progeny is affected, it is an autosomal disease, and the trait is recessive as for a recessive trait to be inherited. The parents not showing traits are giving birth to affected progeny.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/93_50280_question_1.png'),
(50281,'biology',93,285,548,'Example for autosomal hyper aneuploidy is:','[{"text": "Down\'s syndrome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Klinefelter\'s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Turner\'s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemophilia", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A hyper aneuploidy organism is the one having chromosome number higher<br>(i.e., $2 \\mathrm{n}+1$ ), than a normal individual with one genome. For example, Down\'s syndrome $(47,21)$ in which chromosome number 21 (autosome) is in triplicate in human beings. Another example is Klinefelter\'s syndrome (47, XXY) in which when an extra $\\mathrm{X}$ chromosome (sex chromosome) is present in males',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50282,'biology',93,276,534,'In dihybrid cross. When plants (RrYy) are self-hybridised, the ratio of segregation of yellow and green in is:','[{"text": "$1: 2: 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3: 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$9: 3: 3: 1$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1: 1: 1: 1$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'On self-breeding, the resultant F2 generation shows four types of plants-yellow and round (YYRR, YYRr, YyRR, YyRr); yellow and wrinkled (YYrr, Yyrr); green and round (yyRR, yyRr); green and wrinkled (yyrr) with phenotype ratio $9: 3: 3: 1$. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50282_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50282_explanation_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50283,'biology',93,284,545,'Replacement of which one of the following nucleotides in the gene causes sickle cell anaemia?','[{"text": "A to T", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "T to A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "U to A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C to G<", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The sixth amino acid from the amino terminus of the beta-chain of is glutamic acid (a negatively charged amino acid). A mutation in one of the bases from an $\\mathrm{A}$ to a $\\mathrm{T}$ of the gene coding for glutamic acid in the DNA, changes the amino acid from glutamic acid to valine (no charge at neutral $\\mathrm{pH}$ ) at the same position .',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50284,'biology',93,284,545,'Sickle-cell anaemia is due to the following mutant gene:','[{"text": "CTC - CAC", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "CTC - GAG", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "CAC- GUG", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "GAG - GUG", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'In the case of sickle cell anaemia, the substitution of valine (CTC) for glutamic acid (CAC) at the sixth position in the chain allows a new bond to form, which changes the conformation of the haemoglobin and leads to aggregation of haemoglobin molecules. This is an example of silent point mutation. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50284_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50285,'biology',93,279,537,'Choose the possible genotypes responsible for lightest skin colour in human beings.','[{"text": "AABBCC", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "AaBbCc", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "aabbcc", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "AABbCc", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Three genes (six alleles) contribute to skin colour. The three genes are A, B and C and their alleles are $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{B}$ and $\\mathrm{b}$, and $\\mathrm{C}$ and $\\mathrm{c}$, where $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}$, and $\\mathrm{C}$ contribute to dark skin colour and a, b, and c contribute to light skin colour. For human skin colour, the alleles code for the production of the skin pigment melanin, and their effect is cumulative. This implies that a person with genotype AABBCC has six alleles that code for high production. of melanin, thus indicating that their skin would be very dark. On the other hand, a person with genotype aabbcc has six alleles that code for low production of melanin, and thus their skin would be very light',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50286,'biology',93,284,543,'Both male and female have normal vision though their fathers were colour blind, and mothers did not have any gene for colour blindness. The probability of their daughter becoming colour blind is:','[{"text": "$0 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$15 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$25 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$50 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The male\'s father was colour blind with genotype and mother had no gene for colour blindness with genotype XX, thus genotype of male would be<br>$X^{c} Y \\times X X$<br>$\\mathrm{XY}$<br>The female\'s father was also colour blind with genotype $X^{c} Y$ and mother had no gene for colour blindness, thus with genotype XX, thus genotype of female would be<br>$X^{c} Y \\times X X$<br>$X X^{c}$<br>On crossing this male and female:<br>$X Y \\times X^{c} X$<br>Their daughter can have genotype XX or ${\\rm{X}}{{\\rm{X}}^{\\rm{c}}}$, thus she could be normal or carrier, but the probability of she being colour blind is $0 \\%$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50287,'biology',93,284,547,'Identify the odd one among the following disorders.','[{"text": "Haemophilia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sickle-cell anaemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenylketonuria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thalassemia", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Haemophilia is an inherited sex-linked recessive disease-causing deficiency of clotting. Sickle cell anaemia. phenylketonuria and thalassemia are autosomal recessive disorders',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50288,'biology',93,281,539,'From the chromosomal complements given below, identify the one which shows female heterogamety.','[{"text": "XX - XO", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X X - XY", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "XX - XXY", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "ZZ - ZW", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In birds, reptiles, some fishes, butterflies etc., females are heterogametic with autosomes and ZW allosomes; while males are homogametic with autosomes and $\\mathrm{ZZ}$ allosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50289,'biology',93,283,541,'In the following symbols, used in human pedigree analysis, identify the symbol that denotes consanguineous mating.<br>','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Consanguineous mating (Usually between cousins) <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50289_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50290,'biology',93,271,529,'Which of the following characters not studied by Mendel in his Pea plant experiment','[{"text": "Stem height", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed shape", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pod shape", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Leaf shape", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Mendel never considered the shape of leaf as a character.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50291,'biology',93,276,534,'A pure breeding pea plant with round yellow seeds was crossed with pea plant having wrinkled green seeds. On selfing of hybrid of his cross, 64 progeneis were obtained in generation. Find out the number of progenies showing non-parental characters<br>','[{"text": "36", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "24", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The F2 phenotypic ratio in a dihybrid cross is 9:3:3:1. The first and last term in ratio i.e, 9 and 1 represent the parental genotypes while the second and third term i.e, 3 and 3 represent the recombinant genotypes. Therefore, the number of F2 progenies out of 64 progenies showing non-parental characters will be $=(6 / 16) \\times 64=24$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50292,'biology',93,275,533,'A man with blood group A marries a woman having blood group B. The maximum possible blood groups among their progenies are','[{"text": "AB only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, AB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, AB, O", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Both the man and woman can be heterozygous to the trait so all the possible combinations may be available.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50293,'biology',93,285,548,'Match Column I with Column II and find the correct answer<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Aneuploidy<br>B. Monoploidy<br>C. Polyploidy<br>D. Diploidy</div><div class="column-right">P. Increase in whole set of chromosomes<br>Q. Loss or gain of a chromosome<br>R. Two sets of chromosomes<br>S. A single set of chromosomes</div></div>','[{"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R, B - P, C - Q, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q, B - S, C - P, D - R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I- Q , II- S, III- P , IV- R',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50294,'biology',93,275,533,'The genotype of a husband and wife are ${{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}\\,\\,{\\rm{\\& }}\\,\\,{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{i}}$. Among the blood types of their children, how many different genotypes and phenotypes are possible?<br>','[{"text": "3 genotypes; 3 phenotypes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 genotypes; 3 phenotypes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4 phenotypes; 3 genotypes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4 phenotypes; 4 genotypes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The 4 genotypes are IAIA, IA i, IBi, IAIB and 3 phenotypes are A, B and O',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50295,'biology',93,275,533,'What is the possible blood group of children whose parents are heterozygous for A and B blood groups?<br>','[{"text": "A, B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, AB and O", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "AB only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B and AB only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Genotype of the parent having blood group A may be Ai<br>Genotype of the parent having B blood group may be Bi.<br>Thus, possible blood groups of children can be i, A, B or AB.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50296,'biology',93,285,550,'Match the column-I and column-II<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Autosomal\ntrisomy<br>B.Allosomal\ntrisomy<br>C. Allosomal\nMonosomy<br>D. Cystic\nfibrosis</div><div class="column-right">P. Turner’s\nsyndrome<br>Q. Mendelian\ndisorder<br>R. Klinefelter’s\nSyndrome<br>S. Down’s\nSyndrome</div></div>','[{"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - P, B - Q, C - S, D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - Q, D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S, B - R, C - P, D - Q", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I- S , II- R, III- P, IV- Q',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50297,'biology',93,271,529,'Which among the following characters selected by Mendel in a pea plant is a recessive character?<br>','[{"text": "Inflated (full) pod", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Green pod colour", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "White flower", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Axillary flower", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'White coloured flower is recessive over purple/ violet coloured flower.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50298,'biology',93,281,539,'XO type of sex determination and X Y type of sex determination are the examples of','[{"text": "Male Homogamety", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male Heterogamety", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Female Homogamety", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Female Heterogamety", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'XO XY type of sex determination are examples of male heterogamety. XO type is found examples of male heterogamety. XO type is found in male grass hoppers and XY type in human beings.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50299,'biology',93,284,547,'Example for Non-Mendelian disorder :','[{"text": "Thalaseemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemphilia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cystic fibrosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Down\'s syndrome", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Down\'s syndrome is considered as chromosomal aberration. Thalessemia, haemophilia and cystic fibrosis are genetic or Mendelian Disorders.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50301,'biology',93,275,533,'In the human $\\mathrm{ABO}$ blood system, the alleles $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$ are dominant to $\\mathrm{O}$. What will be number of different possible genotype?','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Formula to calculate number of genotype for multiple allelism $\\dfrac{n(n+1)}{2}$ if where $\\mathrm{n}=$ no. of alleles controlling the trait. Thus, the number of different possible genotype would be 6 viz., $\\mathrm{AA}, \\mathrm{AB}, \\mathrm{AO}, \\mathrm{BB}, \\mathrm{BO}$ and $\\mathrm{OO}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50302,'biology',93,277,535,'The genes contributed by mother to each of her progeny','[{"text": "$1 / 2$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$1 / 4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1 / 8$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1 / 16$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mother contributes half of the set (haploid).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50303,'biology',93,276,534,'In a Mendelian dihybrid cross kinds of recombinants formed in F2 generation','[{"text": "2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Two types/kinds of recombinants are formed, one character from each parental type.<br>A dihybrid cross is a cross between two different traits. The first filial generation produces four identical offsprings, the second filial generation, which occurs by crossing the members of the first filial generation, shows a phenotypic ratio of 9:3:3:1, where the 9 represents the proportion of individuals displaying both dominant traits, the first 3 represents the individuals displaying the first dominant trait and the second recessive trait, the second 3 represents those displaying the first recessive trait and second dominant trait and the 1 represents the homozygote, displaying both recessive traits.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50304,'biology',93,276,534,'Three yellow and round pea seeds labelled A,B,C were taken and grown into plants. The plants were crossed to a plant grown from green wrinkled pea. 100 seeds obtained from each cross were sorted into phenotypic classes as follows: A: 100 yellow round, B: 51 yellow round 49 green round, $\\mathrm{C}: 24$ yellow round, 26 yellow wrinkled, 25 green round, 25 green wrinkled. The genotype of plant $C$ would be','[{"text": "YyRr", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "YYRR", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "YYRr", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "YyRR", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'This is an e.g. of Dihybrid test cross ratio is $1: 1: 1: 1$. A Dihybrid cross is a cross between two different genes having different characters. Dihybrid test crossing is the cross in which one parent from $\\mathrm{F} 1$ generation having heterozygous condition gets crossed with a parent which is double homozygous and recessive in nature.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50305,'biology',93,272,530,'The postulate of Mendel that cannot be explained with monohybrid cross','[{"text": "unit factors in pairs", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Segregation of factor", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dominance / recessive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Independent assortment of factor", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The postulate of Mendel that cannot be explained with monohybrid cross is Independent assortment of factor',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50306,'biology',93,276,534,'In a dihybrid cross the ratio of pure double dominants and pure double recessive individuals in $\\mathrm{F} 2$ generation','[{"text": "$9: 7$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1: 9$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$4: 16$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1: 1$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In a Dihybrid test cross-ratio is $1: 1: 1: 1$. A Dihybrid cross is a cross between two different genes having different characters. Dihybrid test crossing is the cross in which one parent from F1 generation having heterozygous condition gets crossed with a parent which is double homozygous and recessive in nature.<br>In a dihybrid cross the ratio of pure double dominants and pure double recessive individuals in F2 generation is $1: 1$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50307,'biology',93,277,535,'The phenomenon of exchange of segments between paternal and maternal chromosomes is called','[{"text": "Recombination", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Linkage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Crossing over", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The phenomenon of exchange of segments between paternal and maternal chromosomes is called crossing over',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50308,'biology',93,278,536,'Father of experimental genetics','[{"text": "T. H Morgan", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Mendal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Boveri", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Correns", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Father of experimental genetics is T. H Morgan',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50309,'biology',93,283,541,'Which one of the following symbols and its representation used in human pedigree analysis is correct?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'is correct because it is symbolizing consanguineous mating',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50310,'biology',93,277,535,'If a diploid cell contains six chromosomes, how many possible random arrangements of homologous could occur during Metaphase-I ?','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "64", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In metaphase I, each pair of bivalents (i.e, two chromosomes, four chromatids) line up on the metaphase plate, the position of each chromosome in the bivalents is random; that means either parental homolog can occur on each side. Thus, in a diploid cell with six chromosomes (means 3 pairs of chromosomes), there are $8\\left(2^{3}=8\\right)$ possible ways to arrange the chromosomes, during Metaphase I.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50311,'biology',93,276,534,'A dihybrid helps to understand','[{"text": "One gene inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two gene inheritance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Three gene inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four gene inheritance", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A dihybrid condition includes concurring inheritance of two pairs of Mendelian factors. Hence 2 gene inheritance.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50312,'biology',93,272,530,'The alleles are','[{"text": "Multiple forms of genes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genes present in allosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genes governing eye characters", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A pair of genes governing a specific character such as tallness or dwarfness or alternate form of gene.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'alleles are the alternative forms of the same character, which produce different effects. They also occupy same position on the homologous chromosomes. For example; tall and dwarf plants are contrasting alleles representing the same character i.e., height of pea plant',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50313,'biology',93,273,531,'The allele which does not express in the $F_{1}$ generation in presence of another allele is','[{"text": "dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "co-dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "incompletely dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "recessive", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Only dominant characters are expressed by dominant genes, in F1 generation, while recessive genes and their expressions are suppressed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50314,'biology',93,279,537,'How many genetically different gametes will be produced by a heterozygous plant having the genotype ${\\rm{Aa}}\\,{\\rm{Bb}}\\,{\\rm{Cc}}$ ?','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Genetically eight different gametes will be produced viz., $\\mathrm{ABC}, \\mathrm{ABc}, \\mathrm{AbC}, \\mathrm{Abc}$, $\\mathrm{aBC}, \\mathrm{aBc}, \\mathrm{abC}, \\mathrm{abc}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50315,'biology',93,272,530,'A cross is made between the two organisms both of which have a genetic make up of $\\mathrm{Bb}$ for a particular trait, and two offsprings are produced. the first offspring exhibit the dominant trait. What is the probability that the second offsprings will exhibit the recessive trait?','[{"text": "100", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1 / 4$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Zero", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3 / 4$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The probability that the second offsprings will exhibit the recessive trait is $1 / 4$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50316,'biology',93,275,533,'In the human $\\mathrm{ABO}$ blood system, the alleles $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$ are dominant to $\\mathrm{O}$. What will be number of different possible phenotype?','[{"text": "4", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'There will be 4 phenotypes, blood group $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{AB}$ and $\\mathrm{O}$.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50317,'biology',93,276,534,'If a person has one copy of each of two different alleles for a given gene, the person is for that trait.','[{"text": "true-breeding", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "heterozygous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "recessive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "homozygous", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'If a person has one copy of each of two different alleles for a given gene, the person is heterozygous for that trait.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50318,'biology',93,278,536,'The linked characters would always inherits together until they are','[{"text": "Delinked due to segregation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Masked by dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mutated", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Separated due to crossing over", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The linked characters would always inherits together until they are separated due to crossing over.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50319,'biology',93,284,542,'If a character is always transmitted directly from a father to all his sons and from their sons to all their sons, then which chromosome carries the gene for ____ the character?','[{"text": "X-Chromosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Y-Chromosome", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Autosome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Y chromosome is responsible for inheritance of characters from father to son.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50320,'biology',93,275,533,'Which one of the following statements is wrong?','[{"text": "There are six different genotypes of the human $\\\\mathrm{ABO}$ blood types.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{ABO}$ blood grouping provides a good example of multiple alleles.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mendelian disorders cannot be traced in a family by the pedigree analysis.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The genetic make-up of the sperm determines the sex of the child.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Mendelian disorders are the disorders that are caused by mutation or alteration in single genes. These disorders can be traced in a family with the help of pedigree analysis but cannot be confirmed by using karyotyping.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50321,'biology',93,275,533,'Which of the following is a mismatch?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Phenotypic $\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ ratio of 3:1 - Monohybrid cross", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotypic $\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ ratio of 3:1 - partial dominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phenotypic $\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ ratio of 1:2:1 - Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotypic $\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ ratio of 1:2:1 - codominance", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Phenotypic F2 ratio of 15:1 is seen in Phenotypic F2 ratio of 9:3:4 is seen in recessive epistasis. Phenotypic F2 ratio of 1:2:1 is seen in co-dominance. And Phenotypic F2 ratio of $3: 1$ is seen in monohybrid inheritance and not in partial dominance.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50322,'biology',93,277,535,'In the given diagram \' X \' and \' Y \' represent which stage of cell division?','[{"text": "Telophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anaphase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Prophase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Metaphase", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'X-represents Anaphase I without centromeres split( the actual reductional division) and Y represents Anaphase II with centromeres splitting.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/93_50322_question_1.png'),
(50323,'biology',93,283,541,'A pedigree chart shows','[{"text": "Which genes are co-dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The genotypic ratios of the offspring", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The types of gametes produced by the parents", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The pattern of inheritance of a specific gene", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A pedigree is a diagrammatic representation of the ancestral relationships and transmission of genetic traits over several generations in a family. Square symbol represents males, while the circles are used to represent females.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/93_50323_question_1.png'),
(50324,'biology',93,284,542,'The figure represented below is the inheritance pattern of a particular type of trait in humans. Which one of the following conditions could be an example of this pattern','[{"text": "Haemophilia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phenylketonuria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Thalassemia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sickle Cell anaemia", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Haemophilia could be the example of this pattern.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-3',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/93_50324_question_1.png'),
(50344,'biology',96,1160,2773,'Which one of the following equipments is essentially required for growing microbes on a large scale, for industrial production of enzymes?<br>','[{"text": "BOD incubator", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sludge digester", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Industrial oven", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bioreactor", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'To produce enzyme in large quantity equipment required are bioreactors. Large scale production involves use of bioreactors.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50325,'biology',93,272,530,'Test cross in pea plant is','[{"text": "A cross between $\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ tall plant and recessive parent.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A cross between $\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ dwarf plant and recessive parent", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A cross between $\\\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ tall plant with dominant parent.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A cross between two $F_{1}$ plants.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Test cross is a cross which is performed to identify the genotype of an unknown individual. In a test cross, dominant phenotype plant (whose genotype is not known) is crossed with recessive parent to know the genotype.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50326,'biology',93,285,550,'Find the incorrect statement among the following:','[{"text": "In sex linked recessive traits the gene is transmitted from unaffected carrier female to some of male progeny.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Accumulation of phenylpyruvic acid in brain results in mental retardation", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Individuals affected by Down\'s Syndrome will have congenital heart defect and are more intelligent.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Turner\'s Syndrome is caused due to the absence of one X-chromosome.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Down\'s syndrome is a genetic disorder caused, due to the presence of an additional copy of the chromosome number 21(trisomy 21).<br>Symptoms:<br>The affected individual is short statured with small round head, furrowed tongue and partially open mouth. Palm is broad with characteristic palm crease. Physical, psychomotor and mortaldevelopment is retarded.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50327,'biology',93,276,534,'In a dihybrid cross between a true breeding round yellow seeded and true breeding wrinkled green seeded pea plant, the ratio of segregation of round and wrinkled seed traits in $F_{2}$ is','[{"text": "$9: 1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3: 1$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$9: 3$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3: 3$<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In a dihybrid cross, Mendel self hybridised the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ plants (hybrids) RrYy. He found that $3 / 4^{\\text {th }}$ of $\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ plants had yellow seeds and $1 / 4^{\\text {th }}$ had green. The yellow and green colour segregated in a $3: 1$ ratio. Round and wrinkled seed shape also segregated in a $3: 1$ ratio, just like in a monohybrid cross.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50328,'biology',93,272,530,'Match Column I with Column II<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Two or more alternative forms of a gene<br>B. Cross of ${{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{1}}}$\nprogeny\nwith homozygous\nrecessive parent<br>C. Cross of ${{\\rm{F}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ progeny with any of the parents<br>D. Number of chromosome sets in plant</div><div class="column-right">P. Back cross<br>Q. Ploidy<br>R. Allele<br>S. Test cross</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  P, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  R, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S}}$ is the correct option.<br>(1) Two or more alternative forms of gene are called alleles.<br>(2) Cross of $F_{1}$ progeny with homozygous recessive parent is a test cross.<br>(3) Cross of $F_{1}$ progeny with any of the parents is a back cross.<br>(4) Number of chromosome sets in plant is called ploidy.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50329,'biology',93,272,530,'In a plant, black seed color $(\\mathrm{BB} / \\mathrm{Bb})$ is dominant over white seed color (bb). In order to find out the genotype of the black seed plant, with which of the following genotype will you cross it?','[{"text": "BB", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "bb", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bb", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "BB / Bb", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'To determine the genotype of a black seed colour at $F_{2}$, the black seed from $F_{2}$ is crossed with the white seed colour. This is called a test cross.<br>Therefore to determine the genotype of black seed we need to cross them with white seed i.e. bb.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50330,'biology',93,273,531,'Which one of the following can be explained on the basis of Mendel\'s Law of Dominance?<br>A. Out of one pair of factors one is dominant and the other is recessive.<br>B. Alleles do not show any expression and both the characters appear as such in $\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ generation.<br>C. Factors occur in pairs in normal diploid plants.<br>D. The discrete unit controlling a particular character is called factor.<br>E. The expression of only one of the parental characters is found in a monohybrid cross.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "A, B and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, C, D and E only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B, C and D only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C, D and E", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'According to Law of Dominance<br>(1) Characters are controlled by discrete units called factors<br>(2) Factors occur in pairs<br>(3) In a dissimilar pair of factors one member of the pair dominates (dominant) the other recessive<br>The law of dominance is used to explain the expression of only one of the parental characters in a monohybrid cross.<br>Law of segregation is based on the fact that the alleles do not show any expression and both the characters are recovered as such in $\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ generation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50331,'biology',93,274,532,'A pink flowered Snapdragon plant was crossed with a red flowered Snapdragon plant. What type of phenotype/s is/are expected in the progeny?','[{"text": "Only red flowered plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red flowered as well as pink flowered plants", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only pink flowered plants", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Red, Pink as well as white flowered plants", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pink colour flower in snapdragon have genotype Rr<br>Red flowered snapdragon have genotype RR when they both are crossed.<br> <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_50331_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> So the progeny that we get are red and pink flowered plants only',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50343,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Select the correct group of biocontrol agents.<br>','[{"text": "<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>, Tobacco mosaic virus, Aphids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trichoderma</i>, Baculovirus, <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Oscillatoria, Rhizobium, Trichoderma</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nostoc, Azospirillium, Nucleopolyhedrovirus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Fungs Trichoderma, Baculoviruses (NPV) and Bacillus thuringiensis are used as biocontrol agents. Rhizobium, Nostoc, Azospirillumand Oscillatoria are used as biofertilisers, whereas TMV is a pathogen and aphids are pests that harm crop plants.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50332,'biology',93,285,549,'Match Column I with Column II:<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Down\'s syndrome<br>B. α-Thalassemia<br>C. β-Thalassemia<br>D. Klinefelter\'s syndrome</div><div class="column-right">P. ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{1}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ chromosome<br>Q. \'X\' chromosome<br>R. ${\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{1}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ chromosome<br>S. ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{6}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ chromosome</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  Q, B  -  R, C  -  S, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A  -  S, B  -  P, C  -  Q, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{R,}}\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{S,}}\\,{\\rm{C}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{P,}}\\,{\\rm{D}}\\,{\\rm{ - }}\\,{\\rm{Q}}$ is the correct option. Down\'s syndrome is due to presence of an additional copy of chromosome number<br>21. Klinefelter\'s syndrome is caused due to presence of an additional copy of X-chromosome. $\\alpha$-Thalassemia is controlled by two closely linked genes on chromosome 16 of each parent. ${\\rm{\\beta }}$-Thalassemia is controlled by a single gene HBB on chromosome 11 of each parent.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50333,'biology',93,275,533,'As per ABO blood grouping system, the blood group of father is $\\mathrm{B}^{+}$, mother is $\\mathrm{A}^{+}$and child is $\\mathrm{O}^{+}$. Their respective genotype can be<br>A.${{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}^{\\rm{i}}{\\rm{/}}{{\\rm{I}}^{{{\\rm{A}}^{\\rm{i}}}}}{\\rm{/ii}}$<br>B. ${{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}{\\rm{/}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{/ii}}$<br>C. ${{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}{\\rm{/i}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{/}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}$<br>D. ${{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{i}}\\,{\\rm{/}}\\,{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}{\\rm{i}}\\,{\\rm{/}}\\,{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{i}}$<br>E. ${\\rm{i}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}{\\rm{/i}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{/}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{A}}}{{\\rm{I}}^{\\rm{B}}}$<br>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :','[{"text": "A only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C & B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D & E only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Genotype of father with blood group $\\mathrm{B}^{+}=\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}} \\mathrm{i}$Genotype of mother with blood group$\\mathrm{A}^{+}=\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{A}} \\mathrm{i}$Genotype of child with blood group $\\mathrm{O}^{+}=$ii',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50334,'biology',96,1164,2779,'The first stable product of fixation of atmospheric nitrogen in leguminous plants is<br>','[{"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ammonia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$$\\\\mathrm{NO}_{3}$$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Glutamate", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$$\\mathrm{N}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{N}_{2} \\mathrm{H}_{4} \\rightarrow \\quad 2 \\mathrm{NH}_{3}$$ (Nitrogen) (Dimide) (Hydrazine) (Ammonia)',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50335,'biology',96,1160,2775,'A good producer of citric acid is____','[{"text": "<em>Aspergillus</em>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Mucor</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Rhizopus</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Penicillium</em>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<em>Aspergillus niger</em> is very good producer of Citric acid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2013,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50336,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Cyclosporin $$\\mathrm{A}$$, an immunosuppressive agent commercially obtained from','[{"text": "<i>Trichoderma viridea</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trichoderma harzianum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Trichoderma reesei</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'CyclosporinA.an immunosuppressive agent is commercially obtained from <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'AIPMT','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50337,'biology',96,1162,2777,'The primitive prokaryotes responsible for the production of biogas from the dung of ruminant animals includes','[{"text": "Methanogens", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Pseudomonos</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Eubacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Methanogens are microorganisms that produce methane as a metabolic by product in anoxic conditions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50338,'biology',96,1162,2777,'Methanogens belong to<br>','[{"text": "Archeabacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Eubacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mycoplasma", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Biogas producing obligate anaerobe, methanogens belong to domain Archaebacteria.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50339,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Microbe used for bio control of pest butterfly caterpillars is','[{"text": "<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Bacillus thermolactis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Bacillus tequilensis</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Bacillus thioparans</i><br>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> is used to control pest butterfly caterpillars in cotton fields.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50340,'biology',96,1163,2778,'<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> forms protein crystals which contain insecticidal proteins. This protein<br>','[{"text": "Is coded by several genes including the gene cry.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Binds with epithelial cells of midgut of the insect pest ultimately killing it.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Is activated by acidic $$\\\\mathrm{pH}$$ of the foregut of the insect pest.<br>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Does not kill the carrier bacterium which is itself resistant to this toxin.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cryoproteins bind with epithelial cells of midgut of the insects and ultimately leads to dead by mottling.<br>',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50341,'biology',96,1161,2776,'Which of the following in sewage treatment removes suspended solids?<br>','[{"text": "Secondary treatment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Primary treatment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sludge treatment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Tertiary treatment", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Primary treatment involves basic processes to remove suspended solid waste and reduce its biochemical oxygen demand (BOD). This in turn increases dissolved oxygen, which is good for aquatic organisms and food webs.<br>Primary treatment can reduce BOD by 20 $$30 \\%$$ and suspended solids by up to $$60 \\%$$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50342,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Which of the following is correctly matched for the product produced by them?<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "<em>Methanobacterium</em> : Lactic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Penicillium notatum</em>: Acetic acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae </em>: Ethanol", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<em>Acetobacter</em> <em>aceti </em>: Antibiotics", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Yeast or <em>Sacchromyces cerevisiae</em> produces Ethanol from carbohydrates by the process of Fermentation',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50345,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Which of the following can be used as a biocontrol agent in the treatment of plant disease?','[{"text": "<i>Trichoderma</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Chlorella</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Anabaena</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Lactobacillus</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Fungus <i>Trichoderma</i> is a biological control agent being developed for use in the treatment of plant diseases.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50346,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Which of the following is a commercial blood cholesterol lowering agent?','[{"text": "Cyclosporin A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Streptokinase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipases<br>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Statin is obtained from a yeast (Fungi) called Monascus purpureus<br>• It acts by competitively inhibiting the enzyme responsible for synthesis of cholesterol.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50347,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Match the following organisms with the products they produce<br>Select the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Lactobacillus</em><br>B. <em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</em><br>C. <em>Aspergillus niger</em><br>D. <em>Acetobacter aceti</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Cheese<br>Q. Curd&nbsp;<br>R. Citric acid<br>S. Bread<br>T. Acetic acid</div></div>','[{"text": "A - Q; B - S; C - T; D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q; B - S; C - R; D - T", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - R; B - S; C - T; D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q; B - P; C - R; D - T", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Microbes are used in production of several household and industrial products_<br><em>Lactobacillus</em> - Production of curd<br><em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</em> - Bread making<br><em>Aspergillus niger</em> - Citric acid production<br><em>Acetobacter aceti</em>-Acetic acid',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2019,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50348,'biology',96,1161,2776,'Which of the following is put into anaerobic sludge digester for further sewage treatment?<br>','[{"text": "Floating debris", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Effluents of primary treatment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Activated sludge", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Primary sludge", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Activated sludge',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50349,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Match the following columns and select the correct option.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Clostridium butylicum</em><br>B. <em>Trichoderma polysporum</em><br>C. <em>Monascus</em><br>D. <em>Aspergillus niger</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Cyclosporin-A<br>Q. Butyric acid<br>R. Citric acid<br>S. Blood cholesterol lowering agent</div></div>','[{"text": "A - Q; B - P; C - S; D - R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - P; B - Q; C - S; D - R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S; B - R; C - Q; D - P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - R; B - S; C - Q; D - P", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - Q; B - P; C - S; D - R',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50350,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Bt cotton variety that was developed by the introduction of toxin gene of <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> (Bt) is resistant to:','[{"text": "Fungal diseases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Plant nematodes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insect predators", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Insect pests", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Insect pests',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50351,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Match List - I with List - II.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. <em>Aspergillus niger</em><br>B. <em>Acetobacter aceti</em><br>C. <em>Clostridium</em> <em>butylicum</em><br>D. <em>Lactobacillus</em></div><div class="column-right">P. Acetic acid<br>Q. Lactic acid<br>R. Citric acid<br>S. Butyric acid</div></div>','[{"text": "A - R; B - P; C - S; D - Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - P; B - Q; C - R; D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Q; B - R; C - P; D - S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - S; B - Q; C - P; D - R", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'option 1 - is paring with correct sequence given in the match.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50352,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Identify the microorganism which is responsible for the production of an immunosuppressive molecule cyclosporin A :','[{"text": "<em>Clostridium</em> <em>butylicum</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Aspergillus niger</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Streptococcus cerevisiae</em>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<em>Trichoderma polysporum</em>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cyclosporin A that is used as an immunosuppressive agent in organ-transplant patients is produced by the fungus&nbsp;<em>Trichoderma polysporum</em>.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50353,'biology',96,1159,2772,'Roquefort cheese is ripened by','[{"text": "Fungi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Virus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Yeast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacterium", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Roquefort cheese is ripened by Fungi Pencillium roquefort',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50354,'biology',96,1161,2776,'Four students were assigned a science project\nto find out the pollution levels of lakes in their\nsurrounding. After analyzing the quality of\nwater samples, the BOD values were found as\nfollows:\nWhich among the following water samples is\nhighly polluted?','[{"text": "0.06 mg/L", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6 mg/L", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0.16 mg/L", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0.6 mg/L", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'More the BOD , means more pollution',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2023,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50355,'biology',96,1162,2777,'Match the microbial products listed under Column I with the related microbes given under Column II; choose the appropriate option from the given choices.<br><div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Citric acid<br>B. Cyclosporin A<br>C. Statin<br>D. Gobar gas</div><div class="column-right">P. <i>Methanobacterium</i><br>Q.  <i>Monascus\npurpureus</i><br>R. <i>Aspergillus niger</i><br>S. <i>Trichoderma\npolysporum</i><br>T. Clostridium\nbutylicum</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  Q, D  -  P}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  T, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  Q, B  -  S, C  -  T, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  Q, D  -  T}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The mould Aspergillus niger makes acid when molasses is used as the fermentation substrate.<br>Cyclosporin $\\mathrm{A}$ is produced by the fungus Trichoderma polysporum. It is used as an immuno suppressive agent.<br>Statins are produced by the yeast Monascus purpureus. They are used as agents that lower the blood-cholesterol.<br>Gobar gas is a biogas which results after long period of decay of animal and vegetable matter brought about my strictly anaerobic methanogens in the presence of high pressure and optimum temperature. Some examples of methanogens are Methanobacterium, Methanococcus, etc.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50356,'biology',96,1161,2776,'\'Flocs\' is:<br>','[{"text": "The primary sludge produced in sewage treatment", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A type of biofortified food", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A mesh-like structure formed by the association of bacterial and fungal filaments in sewage treatment", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The effluent in primary treatment tank obtained during sewage treatment", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An activated sludge is generated by aeration of sewage which consists of organic material containing large number of microorganisms consisting of bacteria (coliforms Clostridium, Pseudomonas, etc.) and fungi that form a filamentous mesh-like filter and are called floc. This floc is then added to waste water coming in after primary treatment.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2014,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50357,'biology',96,1160,2774,'Ernest chain and Howard Florey\'s contribution was:<br>','[{"text": "Discovery of Streptokinase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Discovery of DNA sequence", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Establishing the potential of penicillin as an effective antibiotic", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Production of genetically engineered insulin", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Penicillin was the first antibiotic to be discovered by Alexander Fleming (1928). He found that fungus Penicillium notatum or its extract could inhibit the growth of bacterium Staphylococcus aureus. However, its full potential as an effective antibiotic was established much later by Ernst Chain and Howard Florey. This antibiotic was extensively used to treat American soldiers wounded in the World War II. Fleming, Chain and Florey were awarded the Nobel prize in 1945, for this discovery.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2015,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50358,'biology',96,1160,2775,'A person admitted to hospital as he had myocardial infarction A cardiologist injecting him \'streptokinase\', why?<br>','[{"text": "It reduces hypertension", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It reduces the level of blood cholesterol", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It stimulates heartbeat.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It acts as clot buster.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<i>Streptokinase</i> works as a tissue plasminogen activator. It helps in dissolving blood clots inside the blood vessels, has fibrinolytic effect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2016,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50359,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Which one of the following has been commercialised as blood-cholesterol lowering agent?<br>','[{"text": "Streptokinase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyclosporin A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statins", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Trypsin -A", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statins are produced by the yeast Monascus purpureus. They are used as agents that lower the blood-cholesterol. The enzyme 3-hydroxy-3-methyl-glutaryl-CoA reductase (HMG CoA reductase) is involved in synthesis of cholesterol in the liver.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50360,'biology',96,1161,2776,'As the organic matter increases in a water body, the BOD:<br>','[{"text": "Increases", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decreases", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Remains unchanged", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Not a parameter", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'BOD is the amount of oxygen that is required for biochemical decomposition of organic matter in one litre of water by bacteria. It is the amount of oxygen that is required for biochemical decomposition processes. High BOD is an indicator of heavy load of organic matter.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50361,'biology',96,1161,2776,'The microorganisms involved in floc formation during sewage treatment are:<br>','[{"text": "Anaerobic bacteria and fungus", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Aerobic bacteria and fungus", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Autotrophic bacteria and yeast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungus and algae", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'An activated sludge is generated by aeration of sewage which consists of organic material containing large number of microorganisms consisting of bacteria (coliforms Clostridium, Psedomonas, etc.) and fungi that form a filamentous mesh-like filter and are called floc. This floc is then added to waster water coming in after primary treatment. The mixture is aerated and agitated. The microorganisms feed on the organic matter in the waste water and degrade it. After a sufficient period of time, the water is taken to a settling tank and allowed to settle.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50362,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Identify the incorrect statement with reference of biocontrol agents.<br>','[{"text": "They do not show any negative impact on crop plants.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They help to increase the use of synthetic pesticides", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They are significant in treating ecologically sensitive area.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They do not affect non-target pests.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The natural enemies like parasitism, predation and other mechanisms for controlling the plant pests are referred as a biocontrol agent. They play an important role in controlling the plant pests like nematodes weeds, insects, and mites. They are environmentally friendly and cause no side effects. They eliminate the need for synthetic pesticide.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2019,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50363,'biology',96,1162,2777,'Ruminant animals can digest cellulose in their food, where as human beings are unable to do so. This is because<br>','[{"text": "Methanogens are present in human gut.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose is a complex sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulose is a complex sugar", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Methanogens are absent in human gut", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Methanogens are bacteria that produce methane during the breaking down of substrates like cellulose. Plants are the major food consumed by ruminant animals. Cellulose is a polymer of glucose found in the cell wall of plants. The gut of the ruminant animals have methanogens that help in the digestion of cellulose and produce methane. Methanogens are absent in the case of human beings. Because of this reason, humans are unable to digest cellulose.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50364,'biology',96,1161,2776,'In sewage treatment, secondary treatment is considered highly significant, because<br>','[{"text": "It helps to remove debris from the sewage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It reduces the BOD level of sewage", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "It helps in the production of biogas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "It increases the organic content of sewage", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Secondary treatment involves aerobic digestion which leads to reduction in BOD.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50365,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Which among the following products of microbes is not obtained from fungi?','[{"text": "Penicillin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statins", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Swiss cheese", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Cyclosporin-A", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Swiss cheese is obtained from a bacterium Propionibacterium.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50366,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Match the following<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Cyclosporin- A<br>B. Steptokinase<br>C. Statins<br>D. Penicillin</div><div class="column-right">P. Clot busters<br>Q. Antibiotic<br>R.Immuno\nsuppressive\nagent<br>S. Blood\ncholesterol\nlowering\nagent</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R, B  -  P, C  -  S, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  R, B  -  S, C  -  P, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  P, B  -  Q, C  -  S, D  -  R}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'i -c ii - a, iii - d iv- b cyclosporin $\\mathrm{A}$ is an immunosuppressant, streptokinase is a clot buster, statin is a blood cholesterol lowering agent, iv- penicillin is an antibiotic.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2021,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50367,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Enzyme which is useful to remove the oily stains in laundry?','[{"text": "Amylase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Renin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lipase", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Protease", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Lipase is useful to remove the oily stains in laundry.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50368,'biology',96,1160,2773,'Find the odd one w.r.to distilled alcoholic beverages','[{"text": "Rum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beer", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dough", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Whisky", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Dough is used to make cakes, idli and dosa, it is not an alcoholic product.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50369,'biology',96,1160,2773,'Wine and beer are produced directly by fermentation whereas brandy and whisky require both fermentation and distillation. This is because','[{"text": "Fermentation is inhibited at an alcohol level of $10-18 \\\\%$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distillation prolongs storage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distillation improves quality", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distillation purifies the beverage", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Beverages like Beer, Wine are fermented but not distilled, they have relatively low alcohol content typically less than $100 \\%$. Hard liquor like Brandy and Whisky are produced by both fermentation and distillation. Distillation process purifies them and removes diluting components like water and increases the alcohol content.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50370,'biology',96,1162,2777,'Dung can be used as for generation of biogas, commonly called as','[{"text": "Gobar gas", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "LPG", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Natural gas", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mustard gas", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Dung can be used for generation of biogas, commonly called as gobar gas.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50371,'biology',96,1163,2778,'The majority of Baculo viruses are used as biological control agents because','[{"text": "These are excellent candidates for species specific applications", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "They have no negative impact on non target plants and animals", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beneficial insects are being conserved", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All the above", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct. Baculoviruses are pathogens that attack insects and other arthropods.<br>The majority of baculoviruses used as biological control agents are in the genus<br>Nucleopolyhedrovirus. These viruses are excellent candidates for species-specific, narrow spectrum insecticidal applications. They have been shown to have no negative impacts on plants, mammals, birds, fish or even on non-target insects.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50372,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Match the items in Column I and Column II then choose correct order.<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A. Blue green algae\nas biofertilizer<br>B.\nFungi as\nbiofertilizer<br>C.\nBacteria as\nbiofertilizer<br>D.\nFungi as\nBiocontrol</div><div class="column-right">P. Ecto mycorrhiza<br>Q.<i>Trichoderma</i><br>R.<i>Rhizobium</i><br>S.<i>Anabaena</i></div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - S, B - P, C - R, D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P, B - Q, C - S, D - R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P, B - Q, C - R, D - S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P, B - R, C - P, D - Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Anabaena</i> is biofertilizer, Fungi glomus is ecto <i>mycorrhiza</i>, <i>Rhizobium</i> is bacterial origin biofertilizer, and Fungi Trichoderma is plant biocontrol agent.',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50373,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Biofertilizers include','[{"text": "Blue green algae, <i>Rhizobia</i> and other $\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ fixing bacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blue green algae, <i>Rhizobia</i> and lichens", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Rhizobia</i>, other $\\\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ fixing bacteria and Non mycorrhizal fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blue green algae, <i>Rhizobia</i> and mycorrhizal fungi", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Blue green algae, rhizobia and other $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ fixing bacteria are used as biofertilizers.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50374,'biology',96,1160,2774,'Which is the correct statement on a good antibiotic?','[{"text": "A good antibiotic is the one which is harmless to host its microflora but is effective against all strains of pathogens.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A good antibiotic is the one which is harmful to host and its microflora", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A good antibiotic should not be effective against all strains of pathogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of these", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A good antibiotic is the one which is harmless to host and its microflora but is effective against all strains of pathogens.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50375,'biology',96,1160,2774,'Which one of the following is not true about antibiotics?','[{"text": "First antibiotic was discovered by Alexander Fleming", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The term \'antibiotic\' was coined by S. Waksman in 1942", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Some person can be allergic to a particular antibiotic", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Each antibiotic is effective only against one particular kind of germ", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The corrected statement will be - Each antibiotic is effective against variety of germ',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
