(50415,'chemistry',44,401,798,'Consider the ground state of Cr atom ${\\rm{(Z = 24)}}$. The numbers of electrons with the Azimuthal quantum numbers ${\\rm{l = 1}}$ and 2 are, respectively','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{16}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{5}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{12}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{5}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{16}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,4$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{12}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{and}}\\\\,\\\\,4$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${\\rm{Cr(Zn = 24)}}$<br>Electronic configuration is : ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{4}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{d}}^{\\rm{5}}}$<br>so, number of electron in  ${\\rm{l = 1}}$, i.e., p subshell is 12 and number of electron in ${\\rm{l = 2}}$., p subshell is 5.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50416,'chemistry',44,397,792,'Consider the following sets of quantum numbers<br>${\\rm{(i)}}\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{n = 3,}}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{l = 0,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{m = 0,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{s =  + 1/2}}$<br>${\\rm{(ii)}}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{n = 2,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{l = 2,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{m = 1,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{s =  + 1/2}}$<br>${\\rm{(iii)}}\\,\\,{\\rm{n = 4,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{l = 3,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{m =  - 2,}}\\,{\\rm{s =  + 1/2}}$<br>${\\rm{(iv)}}\\,\\,{\\rm{n = 1,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{l = 0,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{m =  - 1,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{s =  - 1/2}}$<br>${\\rm{(v)}}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{n = 3,}}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{l = 2,}}\\,\\,{\\rm{m = 3,}}\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{s =  + 1/2}}$<br>Which of the following sets of quantum number is not possible?','[{"text": "(ii), (iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(i), (ii), (iii) and (iv)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(ii), (iv),and (v)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(i) and (iii)", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The value of 1 varies from 0 to  ${\\rm{(n - 1)}}$ and the value of m varies from ${\\rm{ - 1}}$ to +1 through zero.<br>The value of ‘s’  ${\\rm{ \\pm 1/2}}$ which signifies the spin of electron.<br>The correct sets of quantum number are:<br>&emsp; &emsp; ${\\rm{ n}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{l}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,{\\rm{m}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{s}}$<br>${\\rm{(ii)}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{2}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{1}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{1}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ + 1/2}}$<br>${\\rm{(iv)}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{1}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{0}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{0}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ - 1/2}}$<br>${\\rm{(v)}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{3}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{2}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{2}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\rm{ + 1/2}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
