(50454,'chemistry',44,401,798,'The correct set of four quantum numbers for outermost electron of potassium ${\\rm{(Z = 19)}}$ is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{3,1,0,}}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{4,0,0,}}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{3,0,0,}}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{4,1,0,}}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The electronic configuration of ${\\rm{K(Z = 19)}}$ is ${\\rm{1}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{2}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{3}}{{\\rm{p}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{4}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{.}}$<br>Thus, the outermost configuration is ${\\rm{4}}{{\\rm{s}}^{\\rm{1}}}$, the four quantum numbers for this  ${{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ - }}}$ are :<br>${\\rm{n = 4,l = 0,m = 0}}$ and ${\\rm{s = 1/2}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2009,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
