(50502,'chemistry',44,393,782,'<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The radius of the first orbit of hydrogen atom is ${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.529}}\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}} $</div><div class="column-right">Radius of each circular orbit ${\\rm{(}}{{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{n}}}{\\rm{)0}}{\\rm{.529}}\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}} {\\rm{(}}{{\\rm{n}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{/Z),}}$ where ${\\rm{n = 1,2,3}}$ and ${\\rm{Z = }}$atomic number</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is correct but statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but statement B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statements are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Radius, ${{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{n}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}^{\\rm{2}}}{{\\rm{h}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{{{\\rm{4\\pi }}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{mZ}}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{n}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{{\\rm{Z}}}{\\rm{ \\times 0}}{\\rm{.529}}\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}} $<br>For first orbit of H-atom ${\\rm{n = 1}}$<br>${{\\rm{r}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{{\\left( {\\rm{1}} \\right)}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ \\times 0}}{\\rm{.529}}\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}} {\\rm{ =  \\times 0}}{\\rm{.529}}\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}} $',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50503,'chemistry',44,397,792,'Consider the following statements:<br>I. The shape of the orbitals is given by magnetic quantum number.<br>II. In an atom, all electrons travel with the same velocity.<br>III. If the value of  ${\\rm{l = 0}}$, the electron distribution is spherical <br>IV. Angular momentum of 1s, 2s, 3s electrons 	are equal.<br>Choose the correct statements and select the correct option.','[{"text": "II and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III and IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statements III and IV are correct, while the other statements are incorrect.<br>Corrected form are as follows:<br>I. The shape of the orbitals is given by azimuthal quantum number.<br>II. In an atom, all electrons travel with the different velocity.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
