(50505,'chemistry',44,391,775,'Consider the following statements:<br>I. The energy of electrons in atoms is quantised.<br>II. The existence of quantised electronic energy 	levels is a direct result of the wave like properties of electrons.<br>III. The path of an electron in an atom can never be determined accurately.<br>The correct statements are','[{"text": "I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50506,'chemistry',44,388,761,'Consider the following statements about cathode rays.<br>I. These moves from cathode to anode.<br>II. These are visible rays.<br>III. Television picture tubes are cathode rays tubes.<br>IV. In the absence of electrical or magnetic field, these rays travel in a straight  line.','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Statements I, III and IV are correct, while statement II is incorrect. Its correct form is as follows:<br>These rays themselves are not visible but their behaviour can be observed with the help of certain kind of materials (fluorescent or phosphorescent) which glow when hit by them.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50507,'chemistry',44,388,763,'Consider the following statements:<br>I. Canal rays are simply the charged gaseous ions.<br>II. Charge to mass ratio of these particles is found to depend on the gas from which these originate.<br>III. Some of the positively charged particles carry a multiple of the fundamental unit of electrical charge.<br>IV. Behaviour of canal rays in the electrical or magnetic field is opposite to that observed for cathode rays or electron.<br>Which of the above mentioned statements are correct?','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All of these", "isCorrect": true}]',3,NULL,NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50508,'chemistry',44,391,775,'The energy of one mole of photons of radiation of wavelength 300nm is <br>(Given: ${\\rm{h = 6}}{\\rm{.63 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 34}}}}{\\rm{Js}}$, ${{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{ = 6}}{\\rm{.02 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}{\\rm{mo}}{{\\rm{l}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$, ${\\rm{c = 3 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{8}}}{\\rm{m}}{{\\rm{s}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$)','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{235kJmo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{325kJmo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{399kJmo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{435kJmo}}{{\\\\rm{l}}^{{\\\\rm{ - 1}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Energy of one mole of photons ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{hc}}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ \\times }}{{\\rm{N}}_{\\rm{A}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{6}}{\\rm{.63 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 34}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 3 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{8}}}}}{{{\\rm{300 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 9}}}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 6}}{\\rm{.02 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 399}}{\\rm{.13 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{3}}}{\\rm{Joule/mole}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 399}}\\,{\\rm{kJ/Joule}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50509,'chemistry',44,400,795,'Consider the following pairs of electrons  <br>${\\rm{(A)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{(a)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{n = 3,l = 2,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{l}}}{\\rm{ = 1,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{s}}}{\\rm{ =  + }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{(b)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{n = 3,l = 2,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{l}}}{\\rm{ = 1,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{s}}}{\\rm{ =  + }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{(B)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{(a)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{n = 3,l = 2,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{l}}}{\\rm{ =  - 2,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{s}}}{\\rm{ =  - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{(b)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{n = 3,l = 2,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{l}}}{\\rm{ =  - 1,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{s}}}{\\rm{ =  - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{(C)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{(a)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{n = 4,l = 2,}}\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{l}}}{\\rm{ = 2,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{s}}}{\\rm{ =  + }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{(b)}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{n = 3,l = 2,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{l}}}{\\rm{ = 2,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{s}}}{\\rm{ =  + }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>The pairs of electron present in degenerate orbitals is / are :','[{"text": "Only A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(B) and (C)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Based on "n+l" rule, only (B) has pair of electrons in degenerate orbitals i.e., same energy level.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2022,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50510,'chemistry',44,397,792,'The number of orbitals associated with quantum numbers ${\\rm{n = 5}},\\,\\,{{\\rm{m}}_{\\rm{s}}}{\\rm{ =  + }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$ is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{15}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{50}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{11}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{25}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'No. of orbitals ${\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{n}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{5}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 25}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2020,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50511,'chemistry',44,392,780,'Determine ratio of wavelength of first line & third line of Balmer series in H-Spectrum','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1.512$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}{\\\\rm{.512}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Transition for  ${{\\rm{1}}^{{\\rm{st}}}}$ line of Balmer series, ${\\rm{3}} \\to {\\rm{2}}$<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = R}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{3}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ = R}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{9}}}} \\right){\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{5R}}}}{{{\\rm{36}}}}$<br>${\\rm{\\lambda  = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{36}}}}{{{\\rm{5R}}}}$<br>Transition for  line of Balmer series, ${\\rm{5}} \\to {\\rm{2}}$<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = R}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{5}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ = R}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{25}}}}} \\right){\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{21R}}}}{{{\\rm{100}}}}$<br>${\\rm{\\lambda  = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{100}}}}{{{\\rm{21R}}}}$<br>Ratio of wavelength is $ = \\frac{{\\frac{{36}}{{5R}}}}{{\\frac{{100}}{{21R}}}} = 1.512$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2021,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50512,'chemistry',44,392,780,'For emission line of atomic hydrogen from ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{i}}}{\\rm{ = 8}}$ to ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{f}}}{\\rm{ = n}}$, the plot of wave number ${\\rm{(\\bar \\upsilon )}}$ against $\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}} \\right)$ will be (The Rydberg constant  ${R_H}$ is in wave number unit)','[{"text": "linear with intercept ${\\\\rm{ - }}{{\\\\rm{R}}_{\\\\rm{H}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "non-linear", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "linear with slope ${{\\\\rm{R}}_{\\\\rm{H}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "linear with slope ${\\\\rm{ - }}{{\\\\rm{R}}_{\\\\rm{H}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\overline {\\rm{v}} {\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{8}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}} \\right){\\rm{c}}{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}$<br>$\\frac{{{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}}}{{{\\rm{64}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ =  - }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ + }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}}}{{{\\rm{64}}}}$<br>Comparing it with general straight line equation, ${\\rm{y = mx + c}}$, we get<br>slope (m) ${\\rm{ =  - }}{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}$, Intercept ${\\rm{(c) = }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}}}{{{\\rm{64}}}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2019,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50513,'chemistry',44,391,776,'Ejection of the photoelectron from metal in the photoelectric effect experiment can by stopped by applying 0.5 V when the radiation of 250 nm is used. The work function of the metal is:','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{4}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{eV}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{5}}{\\\\rm{.5}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{eV}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{4}}{\\\\rm{.5}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{eV}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{5}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{eV}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'${\\rm{\\lambda  = 250nm = 2500}}\\mathop {\\rm{A}}\\limits^{\\rm{o}} $<br>${\\rm{E = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{hc}}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{12400}}}}{{{\\rm{2500}}}}{\\rm{ = 4}}{\\rm{.96}}\\,{\\rm{eV}}$<br>${\\rm{KE = stopping}}\\,\\,{\\rm{potential}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\rm{ = 0}}{\\rm{.5eV}}$<br>${\\rm{E = }}{{\\rm{W}}_{\\rm{0}}}{\\rm{ + K}}{\\rm{.E}}$<br>${\\rm{4}}{\\rm{.96 = W + 0}}{\\rm{.5}}$<br>${{\\rm{W}}_{\\rm{0}}}{\\rm{ = 4}}{\\rm{.46}} \\approx {\\rm{4}}{\\rm{.5eV}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2018,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50514,'chemistry',44,392,780,'If the shortest wavelength in Lyman series of hydrogen atom is A, then the longest wavelength in Paschen series of ${\\rm{H}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ is:','[{"text": "$\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{5A}}}}{{\\\\rm{9}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{9A}}}}{{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{36A}}}}{{\\\\rm{5}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\frac{{{\\\\rm{36A}}}}{{\\\\rm{7}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'For Lyman series (shortest wavelength), ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 1}},\\,\\,{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = }}\\infty $<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = R}}{{\\rm{Z}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right)$<br>$ \\Rightarrow \\,\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{R}}\\left( {\\frac{1}{1} - \\frac{1}{\\infty }} \\right) \\Rightarrow \\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{ = R}}$<br>Longest wavelength is  ${{\\rm{1}}^{{\\rm{st}}}}$ line of Paschen series,<br>${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 3,}}{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 4}}$<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = R}}{{\\rm{Z}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\left( {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{3}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{4}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}} \\right) \\Rightarrow \\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{R7}}}}{{{\\rm{36}}}}$<br>${\\rm{R = }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{A}}}$<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{A}}}{\\rm{ \\times 7}}}}{{{\\rm{36}}}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{\\rm{7}}}{{{\\rm{36A}}}} \\Rightarrow {\\rm{\\lambda  = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{36A}}}}{{\\rm{7}}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2017,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
