(50578,'chemistry',44,394,787,'The accelerating potential that must be applied to a proton beam to give it an effective wavelength of 0.005 nm is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{32}}{\\\\rm{.85}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{V}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{3}}{\\\\rm{.285}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{V}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{0}}{\\\\rm{.3285}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{V}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{328}}{\\\\rm{.5}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{V}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'${\\rm{\\lambda  = }}\\frac{{\\rm{h}}}{{\\sqrt {{\\rm{2meV}}} }}$<br>For an electron, ${\\rm{\\lambda  = }}\\sqrt {\\frac{{{\\rm{150}}}}{{\\rm{V}}}} {\\rm{ \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 8}}}}{\\rm{cm}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.005nm = }}\\sqrt {\\frac{{{\\rm{150}}}}{{\\rm{V}}}} {\\rm{ \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 8}}}}{\\rm{cm}}$<br>${\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.05 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 7}}}}{\\rm{cm = }}\\sqrt {\\frac{{{\\rm{150}}}}{{\\rm{V}}}} {\\rm{ \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 8}}}}{\\rm{cm}}$<br>${\\rm{V = 32}}{\\rm{.85}}\\,{\\rm{V}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50579,'chemistry',44,392,780,'The ionization enthalpy of hydrogen atom is ${\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.312 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{J/mol}}$. The energy required to excite the elctron in the atom  from to  ${\\rm{n = 1}}\\,\\,{\\rm{to}}\\,\\,{\\rm{n = 2}}$ is','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{8}}{\\\\rm{.51 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{5}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J/mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{6}}{\\\\rm{.56 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{5}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J/mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{7}}{\\\\rm{.56 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{5}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J/mol}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{9}}{\\\\rm{.84 \\\\times 1}}{{\\\\rm{0}}^{\\\\rm{5}}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J/mol}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\rm{\\Delta }}\\,{\\rm{E = }}{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ =  - }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{{{{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ + }}\\frac{{{{\\rm{E}}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{{{{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{1}}{\\rm{.312 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{6}}}}}{{{{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ + 1}}{\\rm{.312 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{6}}}{\\rm{ = 9}}{\\rm{.84 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{5}}}{\\rm{J/mol}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50580,'chemistry',44,392,780,'The energy emitted when electron of 1.0 g atom of hydrogen undergo transition giving  the spectral line of lowest energy in the visible region  of its atomic spectrum is ${\\rm{(}}{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.1 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{7}}}{{\\rm{m}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{,}}\\,{\\rm{c = 3 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{8}}}{\\rm{m}}{{\\rm{s}}^{{\\rm{ - 1}}}}{\\rm{,}}$ ${\\rm{h = 6}}{\\rm{.62 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 34}}}}{\\rm{Js)}}$','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{182}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{kJ}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{182}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{J}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{182}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{cal}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{182}}\\\\,{\\\\rm{erg}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The spectral line lies in the visible region i.e., it corresponds to the Balmer series i.e., ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}$ and hence ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 3,4,5}}$ etc.<br>For lowest energy, ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 3}}$<br>Substituting values in the following relation.<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}^{\\rm{2}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>${\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.1 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{7}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{9}}}} \\right]$<br>${\\rm{ = 1}}{\\rm{.1 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{7}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{5}}}{{{\\rm{36}}}}$<br>Now we know that<br>${\\rm{E = hv = h \\times }}\\frac{{\\rm{c}}}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}}$<br>${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{6}}{\\rm{.62 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 34}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 3 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{8}}}}}{{{\\rm{6}}{\\rm{.55 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 7}}}}}}{\\rm{ = 3}}{\\rm{.03 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 19}}}}{\\rm{J}}$<br>Energy corresponding to 1g atom of hydrogen<br>${\\rm{ = 3}}{\\rm{.03 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 19}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 6}}{\\rm{.02 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{23}}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 18}}{\\rm{.25 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{J = 182}}{\\rm{.5kJ}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50581,'chemistry',44,392,780,'The wave number of light emitted for the transition  ${\\rm{n = 4}}$ to  ${\\rm{n = 2}}$ of  ${\\rm{H}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ is equal to the transition in H atom corresponding to which of the following?','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{n = 3}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{to}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{n = 1}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{n = 2}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{to}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{n = 1}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{n = 3}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{to}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{n = 2}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{n = 4}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{to}}\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\rm{n = 3}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'${{{\\rm{\\bar v}}}_{{\\rm{H}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ + }}}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ \\times 4 \\times }}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{4}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}} \\right]$<br>${{{\\rm{\\bar v}}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ \\times 1 \\times }}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>Given, ${{{\\rm{\\bar v}}}_{{\\rm{H}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ + }}}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{{\\rm{\\bar v}}}_{\\rm{H}}}$<br>${\\rm{4}}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{16}}}}} \\right]{\\rm{ = }}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>$\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{\\rm{4}}}} \\right]{\\rm{ = }}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>$\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}} \\right]{\\rm{ = }}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>$\\therefore {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} {{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 1,}}\\,\\,{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}$',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50582,'chemistry',44,392,779,'Electronic transition in  ${\\rm{L}}{{\\rm{i}}^{{\\rm{2 + }}}}$ ion takes from ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}$  to ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}$ shell when electrons transition to ${{\\rm{1}}^{{\\rm{st}}}}$ shell from ${{\\rm{3}}^{{\\rm{rd}}}}$ shell, the number of spectral line formed are','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{10}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{8}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{5}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{3}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Number of lines ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{n}}\\left( {{\\rm{n + 1}}} \\right)}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>where, ${\\rm{n = }}{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ - }}{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 3 - 1 = 2}}$<br>Number of lines ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{2 \\times 3}}}}{{\\rm{2}}}$<br>${\\rm{ = 3}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50583,'chemistry',44,392,780,'Find the quantum no. ‘n’ corresponding to the 	excited state of  ${\\rm{H}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ ion if on transition to the ground state that ion emits two photons in succession with wavelengths 108.5 nm and 30.4 nm.','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{5}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{7}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{2}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{4}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Given, ${{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 108}}{\\rm{.5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 7}}}}{\\rm{cm;}}$<br>${{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 30}}{\\rm{.4 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 7}}}}{\\rm{cm}}$<br>Let excited state of ${\\rm{H}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ be ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{.}}$ It comes from ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}$ to  ${{\\rm{n}}_1}$ and then  ${{\\rm{n}}_1}$ to 1 to emit two successive photons.<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}{{\\rm{Z}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{30}}{\\rm{.4 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 7}}}}}}{\\rm{ = 109678 \\times 4 \\times }}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>$\\therefore \\quad {{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}$<br>For ${{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{;}}{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{1}}}{\\rm{ = 2}}$ and ${{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = ?}}$<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{\\rm{1}}}}}{\\rm{ = }}{{\\rm{R}}_{\\rm{H}}}{\\rm{ \\times }}{{\\rm{Z}}^{\\rm{2}}}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>$\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{108}}{\\rm{.5 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{ - 7}}}}}}{\\rm{ = 109678 \\times 4 \\times }}\\left[ {\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}}{\\rm{ - }}\\frac{{\\rm{1}}}{{{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}^{\\rm{2}}}}} \\right]$<br>$\\therefore \\quad {{\\rm{n}}_{\\rm{2}}}{\\rm{ = 5}}$<br>Thus, excited state for  ${\\rm{H}}{{\\rm{e}}^{\\rm{ + }}}$ is  ${{\\rm{5}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ orbit.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(50584,'chemistry',44,392,779,'Which are in the ascending order of wavelength?','[{"text": "${{\\\\rm{H}}_{(3 \\\\to 2)}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{(4 \\\\to 2)}}{\\\\rm{,}}{{\\\\rm{H}}_{(5 \\\\to 2)}}{\\\\rm{,}}.....$ lines in Balmer series of hydrogen atom", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lyman limit, Balmer limit, Paschen limit in the hydrogen spectrum", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Blue, violet, yellow, red colours in solar spectrum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "X-rays, Cosmic rays, ${\\\\rm{\\\\gamma  - }}$ rays", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(1) In Balmer series,<br>$\\mathop {{{\\rm{H}}_{(3 \\to 2)}}}\\limits_{{\\rm{\\lambda  = 656}}{\\rm{.3nm}}} {\\rm{ > }}\\mathop {{{\\rm{H}}_{(4 \\to 2)}}}\\limits_{{\\rm{486}}{\\rm{.1nm}}} {\\rm{ > }}\\mathop {{{\\rm{H}}_{(5 \\to 2)}}}\\limits_{{\\rm{434}}{\\rm{.1nm}}} $<br>(2) In ascending order of wavelength :<br>Lyman series in UV region < Balmer series in visible region < Paschen series in IR region<br>(3) ${{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{{\\rm{Red}}}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{{\\rm{Yellow}}}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{{\\rm{Blue}}}}{\\rm{ > }}{{\\rm{\\lambda }}_{{\\rm{Violet}}}}$<br>(4) wavelengths increase in the order :<br>Cosmic rays ${\\rm{ < \\gamma  - rays < X - rays}}{\\rm{.}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
