(50633,'chemistry',44,388,764,'Let mass of electron is half, mass of proton is two times and mass of neutron is three fourth of original. The  new atomic wt. of  ${{\\rm{O}}^{{\\rm{16}}}}$ atom','[{"text": "Increases by 37.5%", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Remains constant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increases by 12.5%", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decreases by 25%", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'We can neglect the mass of electron.<br>In ${{\\rm{O}}^{{\\rm{16}}}}$ atom, total 8 protons and 8 neutrons are present.<br>The mass of proton has proton increased two times, so it’s contribution becomes 16 and neutronmass has changed to ${\\rm{3/}}{{\\rm{4}}^{{\\rm{th}}}}$ of initial mass, so it’s contribution becomes 6.<br>Total mass becomes ${\\rm{ = }}\\frac{{{\\rm{22 - 16}}}}{{{\\rm{16}}}}{\\rm{ \\times 100 = 37}}{\\rm{.5\\% }}$<br>i.e., mass will increase by 37.5%',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
