(50684,'chemistry',44,391,775,'Among the following, the one that is not a characteristic of Planck’s quantum theory of radiation is','[{"text": "Radiations are associated with energy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Magnitude of energy associated with a quantum is equal to ${{\\\\rm{h}}^{{\\\\rm{1/2}}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Radiation energy is neither emitted nor absorbed continuously", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A body can emit less or more than a quantum of energy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'According to Planck\'s quantum theory, a body must emits radiation with the same energy as that of absorbed.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
