(50714,'chemistry',44,400,796,'The below configuration is not correct as it violates','[{"text": "Only Hund’s rule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only Pauli’s exclusion principle", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{(n + l)}}$ rule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(Hund + Pauli) rule", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'According to Pauli\'s exclusion rule, no 	two electrons can have same four quantum numbers. In s-orbital, 2 electrons have same spin 	quantum number.<br>According Hund\'s rule, electrons are first singly filled in each orbital with parallel spin then pairing starts which violates in p - orbital.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','chemistry/44_50714_question_1.png'),
