(51048,'chemistry',44,392,778,'Match Column I (Alkali Metal) with Column II (Emission Wavelength in nm).<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A.Li<br>B.Na<br>C.Rb<br>D.Cs</div><div class="column-right">P.589.2<br>Q.455.5<br>R.670.8<br>S.780.0</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{S,B}} - {\\\\rm{Q,C}} - {\\\\rm{P,D}} - {\\\\rm{R}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{Q,B}} - {\\\\rm{S,C}} - {\\\\rm{R,D}} - {\\\\rm{P}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{R,B}} - {\\\\rm{P,C}} - {\\\\rm{S,D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{P,B}} - {\\\\rm{S,C}} - {\\\\rm{R,D}} - {\\\\rm{Q}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The emission wavelengths (in nm ) are given below<br>(A) Li - ${\\mathrm{670.8(\\mathrm{R})}}$<br>(B) ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Na}-589.2}}$ (P)<br>(C) ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Rb}-780.0(\\mathrm{~S})}}$<br>(D) ${\\mathrm{\\mathrm{Cs}-455.5(\\mathrm{Q})}}$<br>So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(51049,'chemistry',44,390,772,'The candela is the luminous intensity, in a given direction, of a source that emits monochromatic radiation of frequency \' A \' ${\\mathrm{\\times 10^{12}}}$ Hertz and that has a radiant intensity in that direction of ${\\mathrm{\\dfrac{1}{\\mathrm{~B}}}}$, watt per steradian. \' A \' and \' B \' are respectively','[{"text": "450 and 683", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "450 and ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\dfrac{1}{683}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "540 and ${\\\\mathrm{\\\\dfrac{1}{683}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "540 and 683", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The candela is the luminous intensity, in a given direction, of a source that emits monochromatic radiation of frequency<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{\\rm{540 \\times 1}}{{\\rm{0}}^{{\\rm{12}}}}{\\rm{\\,Hz}}\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,{\\rm{that}}\\,{\\rm{has}}\\,{\\rm{a}}\\,{\\rm{radiant}}\\,{\\rm{intensity}}\\,{\\rm{in}}\\,\\\\\n{\\rm{that}}\\,{\\rm{direction}}\\,{\\rm{of}}\\,{\\rm{1/683}}\\,{\\rm{watt}}\\,{\\rm{per}}\\,{\\rm{steradian}}{\\rm{.}}\\\\\n{\\rm{Hence}}\\,{\\rm{A}}\\,{\\rm{is}}\\,{\\rm{540}}\\,{\\rm{and}}\\,\\,{\\rm{B}}\\,{\\rm{is}}\\,{\\rm{683}}{\\rm{.}}\n\\end{array}$<br>So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(51050,'chemistry',44,394,787,'According to the wave-particle duality of matter by de-Broglie, which of the following graph presents most appropriate relationship between wavelength of electron ${\\mathrm{(\\lambda)}}$ and momentum of electron ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{p})}}$ ?','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'De-Broglie\'s equation, ${\\mathrm{\\lambda=\\dfrac{h}{p}}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\lambda \\propto \\dfrac{1}{\\mathrm{p}}}}$  <br>So, correct graph is rectangular hyperbola.(rectangular hyperbola)    <img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/44_51050_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(51051,'chemistry',44,392,779,'Match Column I (Spectral Series for Hydrogen) with Column II (Spectral Region/Higher Energy State).<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">A.Lyman<br>B.Balmer<br>C.Paschen<br>D.Pfund</div><div class="column-right">P.Infrared  region<br>Q.UV region<br>R.Infrared  region<br>S.Visible region</div></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{Q,B}} - {\\\\rm{R,C}} - {\\\\rm{P,D}} - {\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{P,B}} - {\\\\rm{Q,C}} - {\\\\rm{R,D}} - {\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{P,B}} - {\\\\rm{R,C}} - {\\\\rm{Q,D}} - {\\\\rm{S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{A}} - {\\\\rm{Q,B}} - {\\\\rm{S,C}} - {\\\\rm{R,D}} - {\\\\rm{P}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/44_51051_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(51061,'chemistry',44,399,794,'Compare the energies of following sets of quantum numbers for multielectron system.<br>$\\begin{array}{l}\n{\\rm{(I)n}} = 4,l = 1\\\\\n{\\rm{(II)n}} = 4,l = 2\\\\\n{\\rm{(III)n}} = 3,l = 1\\\\\n{\\rm{(IV)n}} = 3,l = 2\\\\\n{\\rm{(V)n}} = 4,l = 0\n\\end{array}$<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below','[{"text": "(V) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (I) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (II)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(III) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (V) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (I) ${\\\\mathrm{ < }}$ (II)", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "(II) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (I) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (V) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (IV)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(V) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (III) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (IV) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (I) ${\\\\mathrm{>}}$ (II)", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'According to ${\\mathrm{(n+1)}}$ rule,<br>(i) higher ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{n}+1)}}$ value - higher is the energy of orbital.<br>(ii) If ${\\mathrm{(\\mathrm{n}+1)}}$ value is same, orbital with higher \' ${\\mathrm{n}}$ \' value will have higher energy.<br>$({\\rm{I}})\\,{\\rm{4 + 1 = 5}}{\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\mkern 1mu} ({\\rm{II}})\\,{\\rm{4 + 2 = 6}}$<br>$({\\rm{III}})\\,{\\rm{3 + 1 = 4}}{\\mkern 1mu} {\\mkern 1mu} \\,\\,({\\rm{IV}})\\,{\\rm{3 + 2 = 5}}$<br>$({\\rm{V}})\\,{\\rm{4 + 0 = 4}}$<br>So, correct order is<br>(II) ${\\mathrm{>}}$ (I) ${\\mathrm{>}}$ (IV) ${\\mathrm{>}}$ (V) ${\\mathrm{>}}$ (III)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(51062,'chemistry',44,398,793,'The number of radial node/s for ${\\mathrm{3 p}}$ orbital is / are','[{"text": "3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'No. of radial nodes $ = {\\rm{n}} - l - 1$<br>For \' 3 p \' orbital, ${\\rm{n = 3}},l{\\rm{ = 1}}$<br>${\\mathrm{\\therefore}}$ No. of radial nodes ${\\mathrm{=3-1-1=1}}$<br>So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(51063,'chemistry',44,399,794,'Read the Statement - A and Statement - B carefully to mark the correct options given below<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The orbitals having same energy are called as degenerate orbitals.</div><div class="column-right">In hydrogen atom, 3 p and 3 d orbitals are not degenerate orbitals.</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statements are correct.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statements are incorrect.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In hydrogen atom, orbitals having same principal quantum number ( n ) are degenerate orbitals, i.e., energy of ${\\mathrm{3 s=3 p=3 d}}$. So, the correct option is (3).',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(51064,'chemistry',44,397,792,'The four quantum numbers for the electron in the outermost orbital of potassium (atomic no. 19) are','[{"text": "${\\\\rm{n = 4}},l{\\\\rm{ = 2}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{m =  - 1}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{s =  + }}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{n = 3}},l{\\\\rm{ = 0}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{m = 1}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{s =  + }}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{n = 2}},l{\\\\rm{ = 0}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{m = 0}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{s =  + }}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\rm{n = 4}},l{\\\\rm{ = 0}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{m = 0}},\\\\,{\\\\rm{s =  + }}\\\\frac{{\\\\rm{1}}}{{\\\\rm{2}}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Electronic configuration of potassium atom is ${\\mathrm{[\\mathrm{Ar}] 4 \\mathrm{~s}^{1}}}$. So, the last electron is in 4 s orbital Hence, ${\\rm{n = 4}},l{\\rm{ = 0}},\\,{\\rm{m = 0}},\\,{\\rm{s =  + 1/2}}$. So, the correct option is (4).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2024,'JEE Main','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(51266,'biology',74,247,489,'Why are archaebacteria able to survive in extreme environments unlike other bacteria:','[{"text": "They are heterotrophic and depend on decaying organic matter.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": " They produce large amounts of biogas which helps them survive.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Their cell wall structure is fundamentally different, enabling adaptation to harsh conditions.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "They undergo photosynthesis at very high temperatures", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Their cell wall structure is fundamentally different, enabling adaptation to harsh conditions.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102220,'biology',9,25,48,'How many plants in the list given below are the members of non vascular embryophytes / Bryophyta.<br><i>Funaria, Spirogyra, Volvox, Marchantia, Fucus, Polysiphonia, Polytrichum, Selaginella, Sphagnum, Equisetum</i>.','[{"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<i>Marchantia, Funaria, Polytrichum, Sphagnum</i>, belong to bryophyta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(91289,'physics',3,310,572,'A meter scale is given along a path, as shown in the diagram. <img src=\'/img/data/physics/3_91289_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />  A point object starts from $O,$ moves to $B,$ then\nturns back and reaches at point $C.$ Choose the\ncorrect option.','[{"text": "Displacement of object is ${-10 \\\\hat{i} m}$.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Displacement of object is ${-50 \\\\hat{i} m}$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Distance covered by object is $80\\\\,m$.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Position vector of ${C}$ with respect to ${A}$ is ${-10 \\\\hat{i} m}$.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Displacement is ${\\overrightarrow{O C}=-10 \\hat{i}}$<br>Distance is ${=O B+B O+O C=90 {~m}}$<br>Position vector of ${C}$ with respect to ${A}$ is<br>${\\overrightarrow{A C}=10 \\hat{i}}$',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(92682,'chemistry',54,1213,2907,'Increasing order of stability of the resonance structures is given. Choose the correct answer from the options given below.<br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_92682_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_92682_qtext_2.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_92682_qtext_3.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> <br><img src=\'/img/data/chemistry/54_92682_qtext_4.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />','[{"text": "C, D, B, A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D, C, B, A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D, C, A, B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C, A, B, D", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Structure \' C \' is least stable as highly electronegative oxygen carries a positive charge. \' D \' is the most stable due to octet completion. Between \'${\\text{A}}$\' and \' ${\\text{B}}$ \', \'${\\text{A}}$\'  is less stable due to repulsion between the lone pair on nitrogen and the negative charge on carbon. Hence, the order is $\\mathrm{C} < \\mathrm{A} < \\mathrm{B} < \\mathrm{D}$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2023,'JEE','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102197,'biology',9,25,48,'Read the given statements and choose the correct option:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Gemmae are green, unicellular, sexual buds which develop in receptacles called gemma cups.</div><div class="column-right">Protonema develops directly from a spore.</div></div>','[{"text": "Both statement A and statement B are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statement A and statement B are true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is true and statement B is false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is false but statement B is true", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Statement A is false but Statement B is true Statement A is false: Gemmae are indeed green and asexual. They are multicellular structures involved in asexual reproduction in bryophytes like <i>Marchantia</i>, and are produced in gemma cups. Statement B is true: Protonema is the first stage in the moss gametophyte and develops directly from a spore.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102198,'biology',9,25,46,'In bryophytes, the gemmae help in which one of the following?','[{"text": "Gaseous exchange", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sexual reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Asexual reproduction", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nutrient absorption", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>Gemmae are green, multicellular, and lens shaped structures that function as asexual buds. They develop in small, cup-like structures known as gemma cups (commonly seen in liverworts like Marchantia). When detached from the parent plant, they grow into new individuals, thus enabling asexual reproduction. Hence, gemmae help in asexual reproduction in bryophytes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102199,'biology',9,28,51,'Match Column-I with Column-II <img src=\'/img/data/biology/9_102199_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Choose the option with all correct matches.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-S, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is (3).<br>Pteridophyte - <i>Salvinia</i><br>Bryophyte - <i>Polytrichum</i><br><i>Angiosperm - Salvia</i><br><i>Gymnosperm - Ginkgo</i>',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102200,'biology',9,27,50,'Which one of the following is the characteristic feature of gymnosperms?','[{"text": "Gymnosperms have flowers for reproduction", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seeds are enclosed in fruits", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seeds are naked", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Seeds are absent", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>The term "gymnosperm" literally means "naked seeds" (Gymnos = naked, sperma = seed). In these plants, ovules are not enclosed by an ovary wall—they remain exposed both before and after fertilization. As a result, the seeds that form after fertilization are not enclosed within fruits, hence called naked seeds',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102201,'biology',9,26,49,'Given below are the stages in the life cycle of pteridophytes. Arrange the following stages in the correct sequence.<br>A. Prothallus stage<br>B. Meiosis in spore mother cells<br>C. Fertilisation<br>D. Formation of archegonia and antheridia in gametophyte.<br>E. Transfer of antherozoids to the archegonia in presence of water.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "E, D, C, B, A", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, A, D, E, C", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B, A, E, C, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D, E, C, A, B", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>B. Meiosis in spore mother cells – occurs in the sporangia of the sporophyte to produce haploid spores<br>A. Prothallus stage – spores germinate to form a multicellular, photosynthetic gametophyte called the prothallus.<br>D. Formation of archegonia and antheridia – the prothallus develops sex organs: archegonia (female) and antheridia (male).<br>E. Transfer of antherozoids – flagellated antherozoids swim through water to reach the archegonia.<br>C. Fertilisation – fusion of male and female gametes produces the zygote, leading to formation of a new sporophyte. Hence, the correct sequence is<br>B $ \\to $ A $ \\to $ D $ \\to $ E $ \\to $ C.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102202,'biology',9,25,46,'The correct sequence of events in the life cycle of bryophytes is<br>A. Fusion of antherozoid with egg.<br>B. Attachment of gametophyte to substratum.<br>C. Reduction division to produce haploid spores.<br>D. Formation of sporophyte.<br>E. Release of antherozoids into water.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :','[{"text": "D, E, A, B, C", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D, E, A, C, B", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, E, A, C, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, E, A, D, C", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>The correct sequence of events in the life cycle of bryophytes is:<br>B. Attachment of gametophyte to substratum – the gametophyte develops from a germinating\nspore and anchors to the surface.<br>E. Release of antherozoids into water – the male gametes (antherozoids) are released from the antheridia and require water for movement.<br>A. Fusion of antherozoid with egg – fertilization occurs in the archegonium, leading to zygote formation.<br>D. Formation of sporophyte – the zygote develops into a multicellular diploid sporophyte.<br>C. Reduction division to produce haploid spores – meiosis occurs in the capsule of the sporophyte to produce spores.<br>Thus, the correct chronological order is<br>B $ \\to $ E $ \\to $ A $ \\to $ D $ \\to $ C',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102203,'biology',9,23,40,'Which statement(s) is/are correct in relation to numerical classification?<br>(I) In this classification, we can use computers for analysis.<br>(II) All characters considered for analysis are given equal importance and weightage.<br>(III) This system of classification is considered better because it uses a large number of comparable characters to assign a place to the species.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III are correct. Numerical Taxonomy which is now easily carried out using computers is based on all observable characteristics. Number and codes are assigned to all the characters and the data are then processed. In this way each character is given equal importance and at the same time hundreds of characters can be considered.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102205,'biology',9,23,40,'Which of the following statements about the artificial system of classification are correct?<br>(I) It does not indicate the evolutionary relationship of organisms.<br>(II) It is not based on morphological characteristics.<br>(III) It does not consider androecium structure.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I is correct. The artificial systems gave equal weightage to vegetative and sexual characteristics. It does not indicates the relationship of organism.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102206,'biology',9,26,49,'Which of the following statement is correct for Pteridophyta?<br>(I) The main plant body is the gametophyte.<br>(II) The gametophyte is differentiated into true roots, stems, and leaves.<br>(III) Their sporophyte lacks vascular bundles.<br>(IV) The gametophyte requires cool, damp, and shady places to grow.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IV is the only correct statement. In pteridophyta the main plant body is sporophyta, which is differentiated into true roots, stems and leaves and it has vascular bundle tissue in it.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102207,'biology',9,26,49,'Which of the following structures can be observed in the life cycle of vascular cryptogams/Pteridophyta from the given assemblage of terms?<br>(I) Vascular tissue, Prothallus, Ovule formation, Fruit formation.<br>(II) Gemmae, Prothallus, Archegonium, Pollen grains.<br>(III) Double fertilization, Haploid endosperm, Vascular tissue, Protonema.<br>(IV) Prothallus, Archegonium, Vascular tissue.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(IV) Prothallus, Archegonium, Vascular tissue is the correct assemblage of terms for pteridophyta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102208,'biology',9,27,50,'Consider the following statements and select the correct ones for gymnosperms:<br>(I) <i>Salvinia, Ginkgo</i>, and <i>Pinus</i> are all gymnosperms.<br>(II) Ovules are not enclosed by any ovary wall and remain exposed, both before and after fertilization.<br>(III) Gymnosperms are both homosporous and heterosporous.<br>(IV) <i>Sequoia</i> is one of the tallest gymnosperm.<br>(V) The leaves of gymnosperms are not well adapted to extremes of climate.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, IV are correct, Gymnosperms are heterosporous. <i>Salvinia</i> is a pteridophyta. The leaves of gymnosperms are well adapted to extremes of climate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102209,'biology',9,26,49,'Which of the following statements correctly describe the prothallus in pteridophytes?<br>(I) It is a thalloid structure formed from the fusion of gametes.<br>(II) It represents the diploid ( 2n ), free-living gametophyte generation.<br>(III) It is a vascular, diploid, multicellular sporophyte.<br>(IV) It develops from spores through mitotic division.<br>(V) It is a haploid, multicellular, small, and mostly photosynthetic thalloid body.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IV, V is correct. Prothallus in pteridophyte is - formed by mitosis in spores. It is haploid, multicellular, small mostly photosynthetic thalloid body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102210,'biology',9,26,49,'Choose the correct sequence of the following events in the life cycle of pteridophytes starting from dispersal of a haploid structure produced by meiosis:<br>(I) Sex organ formation<br>(II) Gamete formation<br>(III) Zygote formation<br>(IV) Embryo formation<br>(V) Fertilization<br>(VI) Spore formation<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "V, II, III, IV, I, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "VI, I, II, V, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'VI, I, II, V, III, IV is the right sequence regarding the life cycle of pteridophyta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102211,'biology',9,26,49,'Which statement is correct for homosporous pteridophytes?<br>(I) Gametophyte and sporophyte are usually parasitic.<br>(II) Gametophyte is autotrophic, while the sporophyte is parasitic.<br>(III) Gametophyte is a parasite, and the sporophyte is autotrophic.<br>(IV) Sporophyte is autotrophic.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sporophyte is autotrophic in case of homosporus pteridophyta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102212,'biology',9,26,49,'Which of the following plants belong to Pteridophyta?<br> <i>Salvinia, Azolla, Lycopodium, Funaria, Spirogyra, Volvox, Dryopteris, Marchantia, Fucus, Polysiphonia, Polytrichum, Selaginella, Sphagnum, Equisetum</i>.','[{"text": "<i>Salvinia, Azolla, Lycopodium Funaria, Spirogyra, Volvox</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Polysiphonia, Polytrichum, Selaginella, Sphagnum</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Selaginella, Salvinia, Azolla, Lycopodium, Dryopteris, Equisetum</i>.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Marchantia, Fucus, Polysiphonia, Polytrichum, Selaginella, Sphagnum</i>.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'<i>Salvinia, Azolla, Lycopodium, Selaginella, Dryopteris, Equisetum</i> belong to pteridophyta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102213,'biology',9,26,49,'Some characters/structures are given below. Which of them are found in both Bryophyta and Pteridophyta?<br>(I) Archegonium<br>(II) Protonema<br>(III) Embryo<br>(IV) Prothallus<br>(V) Vascular tissue<br>(VI) Antheridium','[{"text": "Antheridium, Vascular tissue, Protonema", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archegonium, Embryo, Antheridium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Embryo, Prothallus, Vascular tissue", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Archegonium, Protonema, Embryo", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Antheridium, archegonium,embryoare found in both bryophyta and pteridophyta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102214,'biology',9,27,50,'Choose the incorrect statement(s) from the following:<br>(I) Gymnosperms include horsetails and ferns.<br>(II) In heterosporous pteridophytes, the female gametophyte depends on the sporophyte for some period.<br>(III) In mosses, roots are adventitious and branched.<br>(IV) In bryophytes, germination of spores results in prothallus.<br>(V) In gymnosperms, the female gametophyte is free-living.<br>(VI) The origin of the seed habit is seen in pteridophytes.<br>Options:','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV, V are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the Pteridophytes include horsetails and ferns. In mosses there are no roots present, instead rhizoids are present. In bryophytes germination of spore results in protonema. In gymnosperms female gametophyte is dependent on the sporophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102215,'biology',9,27,50,'Choose the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) In <i>Ginkgo</i>, the male gametophyte is not independent.<br>(II) Sexual reproduction in <i>Volvox</i> is isogamous.<br>(III) The pteridophyte gametophyte has a protonemal and leafy stage.<br>(IV) The pigments present in red algae are chlorophyll-a, chlorophyll-d, and r-phycoerythrin.<br>(V) In <i>Equisetum</i>, the female gametophyte is retained on the parent sporophyte.<br>Options:','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III, V are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Sexual reproduction in <i>Volvox</i> is oogamous. Bryophyte gametophyte has a protonemal and leafy stage. <i>Equisetum</i>, is homosporic, the gametophyte is independent and hence gametophytes are not retained on the parent sporophytes. The spores germinate shortly after shedding and gives rise to prothallus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102216,'biology',9,26,49,'Choose the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) Algin and Agar-Agar can be obtained from Rhodophyceae and Phaeophyceae, respectively.<br>(II) In Pteridophytes, sporophylls may form distinct compact structures called cones or strobili.<br>(III) Mycorrhiza is an association of only gymnospermic plant roots and fungi.<br>(IV) <i>Sphagnum</i> is a moss and is used as packing material.<br>(V) Gemma are asexual spores of liverworts.<br>(VI) Antheridiophores and archegoniophores are present in Pteridophytes.<br>Options:','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Algin and Agar-Agar can be obtained from phaeophyceae and rhodophyceae respectively. In pteridophytes Antheridia and Archegonia are present directly without being present on antheridiophores and archegoniophores respectively. Mycorhiza is association of higher plant roots (angiosperms and gymnosperms) and fungi.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102217,'biology',9,25,48,'Choose the incorrect option about Bryophytes:<br>(I) In mosses, asexual reproduction takes place by green, multicellular buds called gemmae.<br>(II) Protonema is a green, creeping, branched, and filamentous stage in mosses, which develops directly from a spore.<br>(III) The sporophyte of bryophytes is differentiated into foot, seta, and capsule, and it is a free-living generation.<br>(IV) Liverworts have an elaborate mechanism of seed dispersal.<br>(V) In liverworts, the zygote undergoes meiosis and then produces a sporophyte.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV, V are incorrect statement. The incorrect statements can be corrected as In liverworts asexual reproduction takes place by green, multicellular buds called gemmae, The sporophyte of bryophytes is a dependent generation. The mosses have an elaborate mechanism of spore dispersal. Liverworts-zygote undergoes mitosis and then produces sporophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102218,'biology',9,27,50,'Choose the incorrect statements for Gymnosperms:<br>(I) Pollination in gymnosperms is mainly carried by air currents.<br>(II) The multicellular female gametophyte of gymnosperms is retained within the megasporangium.<br>(III) They are heterosporous.<br>(IV) Ovules are enclosed by an ovary wall.<br>(V) All gymnosperms are dioecious without any exception.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV, V are incorrect, In gymnosperms, ovules are not enclosed by any ovary wall. Gymnosperm, some are dioecious and some monoecious',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102219,'biology',9,25,48,'Which one of the following is not an ecological importance of moss plants?<br>(I) Mosses form a major portion of food for astronauts.<br>(II) Mosses form dense mats on the soil and reduce the impact of falling rain.<br>(III) Mosses, along with lichens, are the pioneering organisms to colonize rocks.<br>(IV) The very high water-holding capacity of mosses is useful for the trans-shipment of living materials.<br>(V) Some mosses provide food for herbaceous mammals, birds, and other animals.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, IV  these statements are not ecological importance of moss plants. Algae serve as food for astronauts, Very high water holding capacity of mosses is useful for trans-shipment of living materials could be of economic importance.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102221,'biology',9,25,46,'Which of the following statements is/are not true for Bryophytes?<br>(I) They are called amphibians of the plant kingdom.<br>(II) They are photosynthetic in nature.<br>(III) Their spore germinates and produces a gametophyte.<br>(IV) <i>Sphagnum</i> is used as packing material for the trans-shipment of living organisms.<br>(V) <i>Sphagnum</i> is a liverwort that has been used as fuel.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'V is not true, <i>Sphagnum</i> is a moss.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102222,'biology',9,27,50,'Choose the incorrect statement(s) for Gymnosperms:<br>(I) The ovule is a specialized megasporangium, which is integumented.<br>(II) One of the cells of the nucellus differentiates into a megaspore mother cell.<br>(III) The male and female cones (strobili) may be borne on the same tree.<br>(IV) The sporophyte and the gametophyte do not have an independent free-living existence.<br>(V) The leaves are well-adapted to withstand extremes of temperature, humidity, and wind. Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV is incorrect, In gymnosperms the sporophyte is independent and the gametophyte is dependent on the sporophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102224,'biology',9,24,44,'The following statements describe certain characteristics of a plant group. Choose the correct answer regarding the classification of these organisms:<br>(I) The plant body is usually attached to the substratum by a holdfast, and has a stipe and a leaf-like photosynthetic organ (frond).<br>(II) Vegetative reproduction occurs by fragmentation.<br>(III) Asexual reproduction takes place by biflagellate zoospores that are pear-shaped (pyriform) and have two laterally attached unequal flagella.<br>(IV) Sexual reproduction can be isogamous, anisogamous, or oogamous.<br>(V) The union of gametes may occur in water or inside the oogonium in oogamous species.<br>(VI) The common genera include <i>Ectocarpus, Dictyota, Laminaria, Sargassum</i>, and <i>Fucus</i>.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV, V - Correct for Rhodophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, VI - Correct for Bryophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V, VI - Correct for Chlorophyceae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V, VI - Correct for Phaeophyceae", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV, V, VI - Correct for Phaeophyceae (Brown Algae).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102225,'biology',9,24,42,'In oogamy, fertilization involves:<br>(I) A large motile female gamete and a small non-motile male gamete.<br>(II) A small non-motile female gamete and a large motile male gamete.<br>(III) A large non-motile female gamete and a small motile male gamete.<br>(IV) A large non-motile female gamete and a small non-motile male gamete.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In oogamy, fertilization involves a large non - motile female gamete and a small motile male gamete',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102226,'biology',9,27,50,'Choose the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) Psilopsida - <i>Psilotum</i><br>(II) Living fossil - <i>Gingko</i><br>(III) <i>Fucus</i> - Isogamy<br>(IV) <i>Pinus</i> - Dioecious<br>(V) Phaeophyceae - <i>Ectocarpus</i><br>Options:','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Fucus</i> - oogamy <i>Pinus</i> - monoecious',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102227,'biology',9,26,49,'Choose the incorrect options from the following:<br>(I) Lycopsida - <i>Lycopodium, Selaginella</i><br>(II) Sphenopsida - <i>Equisetum</i><br>(III) <i>Salvinia</i> - Homosporous<br>(IV) <i>Equisetum</i> - Heterosporous<br>(V) Chlorophyceae - <i>Ulothrix</i><br>Options:','[{"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III,IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III,IV are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Salvinia</i> -Heterosporous <i>Equisetum</i> - Homosporous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102228,'biology',9,27,50,'Choose the correct options from the following:<br>(I) <i>Cycas</i> - Dioecious<br>(II) Pteropsida - <i>Dryopteris, Pteris, Adiantum</i><br>(III) <i>Chlamydomonas</i> - Anisogamous<br>(IV) <i>Volvox</i> - Oogamous<br>(V) <i>Spirogyra</i> - Anisogamous','[{"text": "V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III,V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II,III, IV are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Spirogyra</i> - Isogamous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102229,'biology',9,27,50,'Consider the following statements and select the correct ones for Gymnosperms:<br>(I) In <i>Cycas</i>, coralloid roots are associated with mycorrhiza.<br>(II) Gymnosperms do not show xerophytic characters.<br>(III) The ovules are not enclosed by any ovary wall and remain exposed, both before and after fertilisation.<br>(IV) They show double fertilization.<br>(V) Seeds are developed pre-fertilization.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'III is correct, In <i>Cycas</i> coralloid roots are associated with nitrogen fixing cyanobacteria, Gymnosperms do show xerophytic character. They do not show double fertilization, Seeds are developed post - fertilization',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102230,'biology',9,27,50,'Consider the following statements and select the correct ones for <i>Cycas</i>:<br>(I) Unbranched stem<br>(II) Monoecious plant<br>(III) Nucellus protected by an envelope<br>(IV) It belongs to angisopserms.<br>(V) Male gametes are carried by water currents<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III are correct, <i>Cycas</i>, male cones and megasporophylls are borne on different trees, has unbranched stem, <i>Cycas</i> leaves are not simple or needle-like, but rather large and pinnately compound, Nucellus protected by envelope.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102505,'biology',74,247,489,'Match Column-I with Column-II and choose the correct option given below:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-P, C-Q, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A-R, B-P, C-S, D-Q<br>Coccus → Spherical (R)<br>Bacillus → Rod-shaped (P)<br>Vibrio  → Comma-shaped (S)<br>Spirillum → Spiral (Q)',NULL,'Easy','Match the following',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/74_102505_question_1.png'),
(102231,'biology',9,26,49,'Choose the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) In pteridophytes, the gametophytic generation is highly reduced and is confined to only a single cell.<br>(II) <i>Chlorella</i> and <i>Spirulina</i> are protein-rich unicellular algae.<br>(III) Pteridophytes are used as soil binders and for medicinal purposes.<br>(IV) Large and small types of leaves are present in pteridophytes.<br>(V) Pteridophytes are the first terrestrial plants to possess xylem and phloem.<br>(VI) Most pteridophytes produce two kinds of spores (macro and microspores) by meiotic division.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV ,V, VI are correct, In pteridophytes, gametophytic generation is multicellular, small, inconspicuous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102232,'biology',9,24,45,'Choose the incorrect statement regarding Rhodophyceae (Red Algae):<br>(I) They show red color due to the predominance of r-phycocyanin.<br>(II) They store food as floridean starch.<br>(III) They reproduce asexually by non-motile spores and sexually by non-motile gametes.<br>(IV) Common members are <i>Polysiphonia, Porphyra, Gelidium, Gracilaria</i>.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, They show red colour due to predominance of r-phycoerythrin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102234,'biology',9,28,51,'Some examples of plants are given here, which of the following have predominantly sporophytic plant bodies?<br>Eucalyptus, Rose, Wheat, <i>Euglena, Ulothrix, Cycas, Spirogyra, Polytrichum, Lycopodium, Pinus, Volvox, Funaria</i>.','[{"text": "<i>Polytrichum, Lycopodium, Pinus, Volvox, Funaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Eucalyptus</i>, Rose, Wheat, <i>Lycopodium, Pinus, Cycas</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wheat, <i>Euglena, Ulothrix, Cycas, Spirogyra</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Euglena, Ulothrix, Cycas, Spirogyra, Polytrichum</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Lycopodium, Pinus</i>, Wheat, rose, <i>Cycas, Eucalyptus</i> have predominant sporophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102235,'biology',9,25,46,'In which of the following ways do liverworts resemble green algae?<br>(I) They have a differentiated plant body with roots and stems.<br>(II) They possess a thallus-like plant body, lack vascular tissue, do not have true roots, and follow an autotrophic mode of nutrition.<br>(III) They have a thallus-like plant body, but possess roots and follow a heterotrophic mode of nutrition.<br>(IV) They have a filamentous body and follow an autotrophic mode of nutrition.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II Liverworts resemble green algae on the following basis thallus like plant body, lack of vascular tissue, absence of roots and autotrophic mode of nutrition',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102236,'biology',9,24,45,'Which of the following is correctly matched?<br>(I) Chlorophyceae: Chlorophyll \\(\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{b}+\\) pecto - cellulosic cell wall.<br>(II) Phaeophyceae: Chlorophyll \\(\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{c}+\\) carrageen in the cell wall.<br>(III) Diatoms: Chlorophyll \\(\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{c}+\\mathrm{CaCO}_{3}\\) cell wall.<br>(Iv) Rhodophyceae: Chlorophyll \\(a+b\\), phycoerythrin.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I is correct.<br>(2) Pheophyceae: chlorophyll-a +<br>chlorophyll-c + algin cell wall<br>(3) Diatoms : chlorophyll-a, $\\mathrm{CaCO}_{3}$ cell wall<br>(4) Rhodophyceae - chlorophyll-a, chlorophyll-d, phycoerythrin',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102237,'biology',9,24,44,'Which option is not related to brown algae (Phaeophyceae)?<br>(I) Gelatinous coating of algin.<br>(II) Gametes are pear-shaped and bear two laterally attached flagella.<br>(III) The food is stored as starch.<br>(IV) They possess chlorophyll-a, chlorophyll-c, carotenoids, and xanthophylls.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III is not related with brown algae. The food is stored as mannitol, laminarin',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102238,'biology',9,24,45,'Which of the following is not matched correctly<br>(I) Chlorophyceae - Chlorophyll a & b<br>(II) Phaeophyceae - Chlorophyll a & b<br>(III) Rhodophyceae - Chlorophyll a & d<br>(IV) Phaeophyceae - Food stored as laminarin & mannitol<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II is the mismatch. Phaeophyceae Chlorophyll a & c.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102239,'biology',9,25,46,'Identify the correct sequence of various developmental stages in the life cycle of bryophytes:<br>Options:','[{"text": "Gametophyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametes $\\\\rightarrow$ Foot, Seta, Capsule $\\\\rightarrow$ Spores $\\\\rightarrow$ Sporophyte.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Gametophyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Foot, Seta, Capsule $\\\\rightarrow$ Sporophyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametes $\\\\rightarrow$ Spores.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Spores $\\\\rightarrow$ Sporophyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Foot, Seta, Capsule $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametophyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Foot, Seta, Capsule $\\\\rightarrow$ Sporophyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametophyte $\\\\rightarrow$ Spores $\\\\rightarrow$ Gametes.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Gametophyte $\\rightarrow$ Gametes $\\rightarrow$ foot, seta, capsule $\\rightarrow$ spores $\\rightarrow$ sporophyte is the correct sequence for bryophytes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102242,'biology',9,23,40,'Which of the following statements are correct regarding the Natural System of Classification?<br>(I) It considers fewer characteristics for classification.<br>(II) It takes into account both external and internal characteristics of organisms.<br>(III) It is based only on sexual characteristics.<br>(IV) It classifies organisms only on the basis of phylogenetic relationships.<br>(V) It was proposed by George Bentham and Joseph Dalton Hooker.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, V are correct. In natural classification, the external features, internal features, like ultrastructure, anatomy, embryology and phytochemistry. This classification for flowering plants was given by George Bentham and Joseph Dalton Hooker.<br>',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102506,'biology',74,247,489,'The cell wall less prokaryote among the following is','[{"text": "Mycoplasma", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Bacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Blue-Green Algae", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Mycoplasma are the smallest known living cells and are unique among prokaryotes because they lack a cell wall.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102507,'biology',74,246,488,'Each of the following characteristics represent a Kingdom proposed by Whittaker. Arrange the following in increasing order of complexity of body organization.<br>A. Multicellular heterotrophs with cell wall made\nof chitin.<br>B. Heterotrophs with tissue/organ/organ system level of body organization.<br>C. Prokaryotes with cell wall made of polysaccharides and amino acids.<br>D. Eukaryotic autotrophs with tissue/organ level of body organization.<br>E. Eukaryotes with cellular body organization.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :','[{"text": "C, E, A, B, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, C, E, B, D", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C, E, A, D, B", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A, C, E, D, B", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>According to increasing complexity of body organization as per Whittaker’s Five Kingdom classification, the correct sequence is:<br>C. Monera – Prokaryotes with a cell wall made of polysaccharides and amino acids (least complex)<br>$ \\downarrow $<br>E. Protista – Unicellular eukaryotes with cellular level of organization<br>$ \\downarrow $<br>A. Fungi – Multicellular heterotrophs with a chitin cell wall<br>$ \\downarrow $<br>D. Plantae – Eukaryotic autotrophs with tissue/organ level of organization<br>$ \\downarrow $<br>B. Animalia – Eukaryotic heterotrophs with tissue/organ/organ system level (most complex) Thus, the increasing order of complexity is C, E, A, D, B.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102508,'biology',74,247,489,'Choose the correct statements from the following about Kingdom Monera:<br>(I) <i>Rhizobium</i> is a soil bacterium that can fix atmospheric nitrogen in a free-living condition.<br>(II) <i>Lactobacillus</i> bacteria is a saprotroph.<br>(III) Based on the hydrogen donor, autotrophic bacteria are of two types: chemosynthetic and photosynthetic.<br>(IV) Both anoxygenic and oxygenic types of photosynthesis occur in members of the Kingdom Monera.<br>(V) Some members of the Kingdom Monera can fix both nitrogen and carbon dioxide.<br>(VI) Cyanobacterial photosynthesis is oxygenic.','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, IV, V, VI are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as on the basis of source of energy, autotrophic bacteria are of two type i.e. chemosynthetic and photosynthetic. <i>Rhizobium</i> is a soil bacteria which can fix atmospheric nitrogen in symbiotic conditions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102509,'biology',74,249,499,'Choose the correct statements regarding Basidiomycetes:<br>(I) Commonly known forms include <i>Agaricus</i>.<br>(II) Karyogamy and meiosis take place in the basidium.<br>(III) Rust, smut, and mushroom belong to this group.<br>(IV) Sexual reproduction occurs through fragmentation.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Commonly known forms are club fungi. They reproduce vegetatively by fragmentation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102510,'biology',74,249,496,'Study the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) The sexual life cycle of fungi involves three sequential steps: Plasmogamy, followed by Karyogamy, and then Meiosis in the zygote.<br>(II) In bacteria, the mesosome helps in photosynthesis.<br>(III) Bacteria are the sole members of the Kingdom Monera<br>(IV) A handful of soil contains hundreds of bacteria.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as In bacteria, mesosome help in respiration.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102512,'biology',74,249,500,'Find the correct matching options from the following:<br>(I) <i>Vibrio cholerae</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) Cholera<br>(II) <i>Salmonella typhi</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) typhoid<br>(III) Yeast \\(\\rightarrow\\) Phycomycetes<br>(IV) <i>Alternaria</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) Perfect fungi<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Yeast-ascomycetes, <i>Alternaria</i> - imperfect fungi',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102513,'biology',74,249,499,'Choose the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) The second component of a biological name represents the subspecific epithet.<br>(II) In Basidiomycetes, karyogamy and meiosis take place in the mycelium.<br>(III) Fungi prefer to grow in cold and humid places.<br>(IV) Biological names are printed in italics to indicate their Latin origin.<br>(V) <i>Nostoc</i> can fix both nitrogen and carbon dioxide.<br>(VI) Yeast is used to make bread and beer.','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as in basidiomycetes, karyogamy and meiosis takes place inbasidium. Second component of biological name represent specific epithet. Fungi prefer to grow in warm and humid places.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102514,'biology',74,255,506,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Fungal bodies consist of long, slender, threadlike structures called mycelium.<br>(II) Viroids are infectious proteinaceous agents that lack nucleic acid.<br>(III) Lichens do not grow in polluted areas.<br>(IV) <i>Rhizobium, Anabaena</i>, and <i>Nostoc</i> can fix nitrogen.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III, IV are the correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as prions are infectious proteinaceous agent that lacked the nucleic acid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102515,'biology',74,248,490,'Study the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Protists are always unicellular eukaryotes.<br>(II) Protists reproduce both sexually and asexually.<br>(III) All bacteria are saprotrophs.<br>(IV) All bacteria are autotrophs.<br>(V) Prokaryotes and protists are the same.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as prokaryotes belong to monera and protista has eukaryotic cell. Bacteria can be autotrophic, heterotrophic, parasitic and saprotrophic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102516,'biology',74,253,504,'Choose the incorrect statements from the following about fungi:<br>(I) Karyogamy in fungi occurs after plasmogamy.<br>(II) Prion is a fungal component involved in asexual reproduction.<br>(III) Sexual reproduction in fungi takes place by conidia and zoospores.<br>(IV) Mycelium of <i>Albugo</i> is aseptate and coenocytic.<br>(V) Viroids were discovered by T.O. Diener.<br>(VI) An intervening dikaryotic phase occurs in all fungi.','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III,V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, V, VI are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Viroids were discovered by T.O. Diener (Question talks of fungi not viroids), An intervening dikaryotic phase occurs in some fungi, like basidiomycetes, ascomycetes.<br>Sexual reproduction in fungi takes place by basidiospores, ascospores, oospores. Prions are infectious proteinaceous agent that lacked the nucleic acid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102517,'biology',74,248,493,'Choose the correct statemens from the following:<br>(I) Plasmids are circular DNA.<br>(II) <i>Chlorella</i> is a green alga placed under Protista.<br>(III) Proteinaceous pellicle makes the body of <i>Euglena</i> flexible.<br>(IV) Diatoms are the chief producers in the oceans.<br>(V) Bacterial structure is very complex, yet they are very simple in their behavior. <br>(VI) Cellular organization of the body is the defining feature of life forms.','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, IV, VI are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the bacterial structure is very simple, they are very complex in behaviour.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102518,'biology',74,250,501,'Protista is similar to Plantae and different from Monera in having:<br>(I) Protista and Plantae have a nuclear membrane.<br>(II) Protista and Plantae are eukaryotes, whereas Monera are prokaryotes.<br>(III) All Protista and Plantae are chlorophyll bearing and perform photosynthesis.<br>(IV) Protista and Plantae have a cellulosic cell wall.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II are correct statements. Plantae have cellulosic cell wall and not the cellwall in protista may have silica or cellulose, some protist are heterotrophic as well.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102519,'biology',74,247,489,'Which of the following is true regarding Mycoplasma?<br>(I) They do not have a cell wall.<br>(II) They produce a cell wall made up peptidoglycan.<br>(III) They can survive without oxygen.<br>(IV) They can cause diseases in animals and plants.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, IV are true. Mycoplasma do not have a cell wall.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102520,'biology',74,253,504,'Consider the following four statements and select the option which includes only the correct ones:<br>(I) Chemosynthetic bacteria are nitrogen fixers.<br>(II) Potato spindle tuber disease is caused by prions.<br>(III) Bacteriophages generally contain doublestranded DNA.<br>(IV) Slime moulds have fungal saprotrophic character','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'III, IV are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Chemosynthetic bacteria are involved in nitrification. Potato spindle tuber disease is caused by viroids.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102521,'biology',74,249,500,'Read the following features and identify the group of organisms they belong to:<br>(I) Body is septate and branched.<br>(II) They act as decomposers of litter.<br>(III) They reproduce only by asexual spores known as conidia.<br>(IV) When their sexual forms were discovered, they were moved into the classes they rightly belong to.','[{"text": "Phycomycetes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Euglenoids", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Deuteromycetes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Basidiomycetes", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The following features belong to Deuteromycetes. Deuteromycetes (Imperfect Fungi) are fungi that reproduce only by asexual spores (conidia).<br>Their sexual reproduction is unknown, which is why they are called "imperfect fungi." When their sexual stage is discovered, they are reclassified into either Ascomycetes or Basidiomycetes.<br>They include saprophytic and parasitic fungi, often found decomposing litter. Example: <i>Alternaria, Colletotrichum</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102522,'biology',74,247,489,'What is true regarding plasmids?<br>(I) Plasmids are used to monitor genetic transformation.<br>(II) Plasmids are present in bacterial cells.<br>(III) Plasmids are organisms with antibiotic resistance.<br>(IV) Plasmids are DNA molecules with Ori (origin of replication).','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, IV are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Plasmids are not organisms but are DNA molecules present in bacterial cell.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102523,'biology',74,252,503,'Choose the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) Deuteromycetes are called \'Fungi Imperfecti\' because only their asexual or vegetative phases are known.<br>(II) Slime moulds lack a cell wall in their vegetative phase.<br>(III) Bacteriophages and plant viruses usually have ssRNA and dsDNA, respectively.<br>(IV) Mycoplasma is the smallest acellular living organism.<br>(V) Mycoplasma is a pleomorphic organism that lacks a cell wall.<br>(VI) Prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells have the same type of nuclear membrane.','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as bacteriophages and plant viruses are usually having dsDNA and ssRNA respectively, Mycoplasma is the smallest living cellular organism. Prokaryotes do not have nucleus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102524,'biology',74,246,488,'According to Whittaker\'s classification, how many of the following characteristics are present in both Kingdom Plantae and Fungi?<br>(I) Eukaryotic, generally multicellular.<br>(II) Heterotrophic mode of nutrition.<br>(III) Polysaccharide cell wall.<br>(IV) True tissue present, and both asexual and sexual reproduction occur.<br>(V) Well-developed nucleus and other organelles.<br>(VI) Presence of chloroplast.','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Fungi do not possess chloroplast and plant are autotrophs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102525,'biology',74,249,498,'Find the correct matching options from the following:<br>(I) Ascospore - Asexual spore<br>(II) <i>Nitrosomonas</i> - Nitrogen fixation<br>(III) <i>Aspergillus niger</i> - Produces acetic acid.<br>(IV) <i> Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> -Ascomycetes.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV is correct statement. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Ascospore - sexual spore, <i>Nitrosomonas</i> - Nitrification, <i>Aspergillus niger</i> - produces citric acid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102526,'biology',74,249,498,'Find the correct matching options from the following:<br>(I) Bread mould - Ascomycetes<br>(II) Oospore - Sexual spore<br>(III) Chief oceanic producers - Diatoms<br>(IV) Red tide- Dinoflagellates<br>(V) Mixotrophic nutrition - Euglenoids<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III, IV, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Bread mould - phycomycetes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102527,'biology',74,254,505,'Find the correct matching options from the following:<br>(I) <i>Plasmodium</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) Slime moulds \\(\\rightarrow\\)Saprotrophic protists<br>(II) Experimental genetic \\(\\rightarrow\\) <i>Neurospora</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) Ascomycetes<br>(III) Prions \\(\\rightarrow\\) PSTD \\(\\rightarrow\\) Protein<br>(IV) Edible fungi \\(\\rightarrow\\) Truffles and Morels \\(\\rightarrow\\) Ascomycetes<br>(V) Animal virus \\(\\rightarrow\\) ssRNA \\(\\rightarrow\\) HIV<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, IV, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Prions - Madcow disease/ CJD - protein.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102528,'biology',74,249,500,'Which of the following features belong to deuteromycetes /\'fungi imperfecti\'?<br>(I) Only asexual or vegetative phases of these fungi are known.<br>(II) They help in mineral cycling.<br>(III) Their mycelium is septate and branched.<br>(IV) The deuteromycetes members may be saprophytes or parasites.<br>(V) Some examples are <i>Alternaria, Colletotrichum</i> and <i>Plasmodium</i>.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, IV are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as some examples are <i>Alternaria, Colletotrichum</i> and <i>Trichoderma</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102529,'biology',74,246,488,'Study the given properties. Which one option has all the properties found in all organisms of the five-kingdom classification?<br>(I) Presence of a cell membrane<br>(II) Cell wall present<br>(III) Autotrophic nutrition<br>(IV) Chemosynthetic nutrition<br>(V) Cellular respiration','[{"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as cell wall is absent in animalia, animal, fungi, some monerans and protists are heterotrophs, Chemosynthetic nutrition is seen in some members of monera.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102530,'biology',74,249,496,'Which of the following statements are correct for the members of Kingdom Fungi?<br>(I) Fungi are heterotrophic organisms and show great diversity in morphology and habitat.<br>(II) All members are coenocytic.<br>(III) They can form associations with algae and plants.<br>(IV) A dikaryotic phase is seen in the life cycle of all fungi.<br>(V) Some unicellular fungi also exist, e.g., yeast.','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as, Some members are septate, ascomycetes and basidiomycetes an intervening dikaryotic stage is seen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102531,'biology',74,252,503,'Find the correct matching options from the following:<br>(I) Plant virus - ssRNA - Mosaic disease<br>(II) Zoospore - Asexual spore - Phycomycetes<br>(III) <i>Plasmodium</i> - Sporozoan - Malaria<br>(IV) Rust fungi - <i>Puccinia</i> - Basidiomycetes<br>(V) Conidia - Sexual spore - Ascospore<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, IV are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Conidia-Asexual spore - Ascospore sexual spore.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102532,'biology',74,253,504,'Find the correct matching options from the following:<br>(I) Antibiotic source - <i>Penicillium</i> -Ascomycetes<br>(II) <i>Paramecium</i> - Ciliated protozoan - Two nuclei<br>(III) <i>Trypanosoma</i> - Flagellated protist Sleeping sickness<br>(IV) Viroids - PSTD - DNA<br>(V) Yeast - Unicellular - Ascospore<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III,V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Viroids - PSTD - RNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102533,'biology',74,247,489,'The main difference between photosynthetic and chemosynthetic bacteria is that:<br>(I) Water is used by photosynthetic bacteria, whereas it is rejected by chemosynthetic bacteria.<br>(II) Photosynthetic bacteria are seen as parasites within green plant cells, whereas chemosynthetic bacteria are seen as saprophytes on decaying food substances.<br>(III) Photosynthetic bacteria include <i>Nostoc, Anabaena</i>, whereas chemosynthetic bacteria include <i>Nitrosomonas</i>.<br>(IV) Energy from sunlight is used in photosynthetic bacteria, while in chemosynthetic bacteria, energy is used by the oxidation of inorganic substances.<br>(V) Some photosynthetic bacteria are involved in nitrogen fixation, whereas chemosynthetic bacteria are involved in nitrification','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'III, IV, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Water is used by both photosynthetic bacteria, and chemosynthetic bacteria. Photosynthetic bacteria are either free living or symbiotic with green plant cells, whereas chemosynthetic bacteria are seen as saprophytes on other decaying food substances.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102534,'biology',74,249,498,'Which of the given statements are correct for Ascomycetes?<br>(I) The mycelium is septate and branched.<br>(II) Conidia are formed exogenously.<br>(III) Sexual spores are called ascospores, which are produced endogenously in sac-like asci.<br>(IV) Hyphae are aseptate.<br>(V) Includes <i>Mucor , Penicillium</i>','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Mucor</i> is a phycomycetes. The mycelium is septate and branced.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102535,'biology',74,249,498,'Which of the following statements is false about Ascomycetes?<br>(I) <i>Aspergillus, Claviceps</i>, and <i>Neurospora</i> are important members of Ascomycetes.<br>(II) Includes unicellular (e.g., yeast) and multicellular forms.<br>(III) Mode of nutrition is saprophytic, decomposer, coprophilous (growing on dung), and parasitic.<br>(IV) The sexual spores are conidia produced exogenously on the special mycelium called conidiophores','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV is false. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the asexual spores are conidia produced exogenously on the special mycelium called conidiophores.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102536,'biology',74,249,499,'What is common in <i>Ustilago, Neurospora</i>, and <i>Agaricus</i>?<br>(I) All have a dikaryotic phase in their life cycle.<br>(II) All produce motile sexual spores.<br>(III) All are edible.<br>(IV) The mycelium is branched and septate.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, IV are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Agaricus</i> is edible. Ascospores are non - motile, sexual spores produced inside sac like structure as in case of <i>Neurospora</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102537,'biology',74,247,489,'What is the role of heterocysts in a cyanobacterial filament?<br>(I) They carry out photosynthesis and nitrogen fixation.<br>(II) They carry out only photosynthesis.<br>(III) They oxidize inorganic substances to obtain energy.<br>(IV) It is an enzyme.<br>(V) It is a cyst.<br>(VI) They carry out only nitrogen fixation.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'VI only is correct. Heterocysts are specialized nitrogen-fixing cells, produced by some filamentous cyanobacteria, which form during nitrogen starvation conditions. These specialized cells do not possess functioning photosynthetic apparatus because their primary function is the anaerobic fixation of atmospheric nitrogen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102538,'biology',74,252,503,'Read the following statements about viruses and identify the incorrect ones:<br>(I) Virus means poisonous fluid or venom.<br>(II) Viruses are inert outside the host cell.<br>(III) W.M. Stanley (1953) showed that viruses could be crystallized, and crystals consist largely of proteins.<br>(IV) Viruses can pass through bacteria-proof filters.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only III is incorrect statement. The incorrect statement can be corrected as W.M. Stanley (1935) showed that viruses could be crystallised and crystals consist largely of proteins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102539,'biology',74,247,489,'How many organisms in the list given below are autotrophs?<br> <i>Mucor, Albugo, Penicillium, Lactobacillus, Nostoc, Nitrosomonas, Nitrobacter, Streptomyces, Saccharomyces, Trypanosoma, Porphyra</i>','[{"text": "Five", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Six", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Three", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<i>Nostoc, Nitrosomonas, Nitrobacter, Porphyra</i> are autotrophic. <i>Mucor, Albugo, Penicillium, Saccharomyces</i> is fungi. <i>Lactobacillus</i> is a bacteria.<i>Trypanosoma</i> is a heterotrophic protists.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102540,'biology',74,249,497,'Read the names of different fungi given below<br> <i>Alternaria, Mucor, Albugo, Penicillium, Ustilago, Colletotrichum, Agaricus, Aspergillus ,Rhizopus</i>.<br>How many of the following belong to the class Phycomycetes?','[{"text": "Three", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Four", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seven", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Mucor, Albugo, Rhizopus</i> belong to the class Phycomycetes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102541,'biology',74,248,491,'The following features represent which group of organisms?<br>(I) Microscopic<br>(II) Chief producers in oceans<br>(III) Found in fresh water as well as in marine environments, planktons.<br>(IV) Indestructible cell wall<br>(V) The walls are embedded with silica, making them indestructible.','[{"text": "Dinoflagellates", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Slime moulds", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Diatoms", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Algae", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Diatoms are microscopic, chief producers in oceans, found in fresh water as well as in marine environments, planktons have indestructible cell wall, the walls are embedded with silica and thus the walls are indestructible.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102542,'biology',74,247,489,'Choose the correct statements regarding decomposers:<br>(I) They play a great role in ecology.<br>(II) All protists decompose dead and decaying organic matter.<br>(III) Fungi, bacteria, and a few protists are decomposers.<br>(IV) They may be unicellular or multicellular.<br>(V) They may be prokaryotes or eukaryotes.','[{"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III, IV, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as few protists are decomposers, some autotrophic, some holozoic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102543,'biology',74,247,489,'Choose the correct statements regarding Methanogens:<br>(I) They can be found in marshy areas.<br>(II) They have a different cell wall structure, and this feature is responsible for their survival in extreme conditions.<br>(III) They are also known as halophiles.<br>(IV) They are responsible for the production of biogas from the dung of ruminants.<br>(V) They are present in the gut of several ruminants like cows and buffaloes.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, IV, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as halophiles are present in extremely salty areas.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102544,'biology',74,246,488,'Which of the following are not considered in the five kingdom system of classification?<br>${\\text{(I)}}\\,{\\text{Lichen}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(II)}}\\,{\\text{Virus}}$<br>${\\text{(III)}}\\,{\\text{Viroid}}\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(IV)}}\\,{\\text{Slime}}\\,{\\text{moulds}}$','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III are not considered in the five kingdom system of classification. Slime moulds are placed under protista.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102545,'biology',74,247,489,'Study the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Bacteria are responsible for the recycling of nutrients.<br>(II) The cell wall of Archaebacteria is made up of peptidoglycan.<br>(III) Bacteria are the most abundant microorganisms.<br>(IV) All bacteria are parasites.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Archaebacteria differ from other bacteria in having a different cell wall structure and this feature is responsible for their survival in extreme conditions, not all bacteria are parasites, some are free - living saprotrophs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102546,'biology',74,248,494,'Study the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Mycoplasma is a wall-less prokaryote.<br>(II) Pigments of euglenoids are identical to those present in brown algae.<br>(III) <i>Gonyaulax</i> undergoes rapid multiplication that makes the sea appear red.<br>(IV) Spores of slime molds are extremely resistant and survive for many years.<br>(V) Slime molds are saprophytic protists.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, IV, V are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as pigments of euglenoids are identical to those present in higher plants.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102547,'biology',74,247,489,'The following characteristics are seen in which group of organisms?<br>(I) They are able to perform photosynthesis.<br>(II) Unicellular, colonial, filamentous, marine, or terrestrial forms.<br>(III) They often form blooms in water bodies.<br>(IV) The colonies are surrounded by a gelatinous sheath.<br>(V) Some can fix atmospheric nitrogen in specialized cells called heterocysts.','[{"text": "Chrysophytes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyanobacteria", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Archaebacteria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Euglenoids", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Cyanobacteria/Blue green algae have chlorophyll a similar to green plants and are photosynthetic autotrophs. The cyanobacteria are unicellular, colonial or filamentous, freshwater/marine or terrestrial algae. The colonies are generally surrounded by gelatinous sheath. They often form blooms in polluted water bodies. Some of these organisms can fix atmospheric nitrogen in specialised cells called heterocysts.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102548,'biology',74,248,490,'Study the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) All bacteria can fix $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ into carbohydrates.<br>(II) In Carl Woese\'s classification system, the domain that includes dinoflagellates, slime molds, algae, and bryophyta is Eukarya.<br>(III) Cyanobacteria/blue-green algae are photoautotrophs.<br>(IV) Protists are always non-flagellated.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as some protists are flagellated like euglenoids, dinoflagellates. Only few bacteria like cyanobacteria, chemosynthetic bacteria can fix carbon dioxide.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102549,'biology',74,255,506,'Find the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) Bacteria reproduce mainly by budding.<br>(II) Archaebacteria differ from other bacteria in having a different cell wall structure.<br>(III) Mycobiont is the major part of lichen thallus.<br>(IV) Lichen plays a major role in ecological succession.<br>(V) Mycorrhizal association helps in $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ fixation.<br>(VI) Lichen acts as an indicator of $\\mathrm{SO}_{2}$ pollution.','[{"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, V are incorrect statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Bacteria reproduce mainly by Fission. ycorrhizal association help in nutrient bsorption.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102550,'biology',74,247,489,'Which of the following organisms in the list given below are autotrophs and perform oxygenic photosynthesis?','[{"text": "Purple sulphur bacteria, <i>Oscillatoria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Nostoc, Anabaena, Oscillatoria</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Anabaena, Sacharomyces</i>, Green sulphur bacteria, <i>Frankia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Rhizobium, Nostoc, Anabaena</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Nostoc, Anabaena</i>, are photoautotrophs while Purple and green sulphur bacteria perform anoxygenic photosynthesis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102551,'biology',74,249,500,'Find the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) <i>Puccinia</i> - exogenous basidiospores Deuteromycetes<br>(II) <i>Mucor</i> - Septate and coenocytic mycelium- Ascomycetes<br>(III) <i>Morchella</i> - edible - Ascomycetes<br>(IV) <i>Trichoderma</i> - sexual stage is absent Deuteromycetes<br>(V) <i>Aspergillus</i> - Endogenous ascospore Ascomycetes<br>(VI) Dinoflagellates - cell wall stiff cellulose plates on the outer surface - red tides.','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II are incorrect statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Puccinia</i> - exogenous basidiospores-Basidiomycetes, <i>Mucor</i> - Septate and coenocytic mycelium - Phycomycetes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102552,'biology',74,248,491,'In _____ \'A\' _____ the cell walls form two thin overlapping shells which fit together as in soap box. The walls are embedded with _____ \'B\' _____ and thus the walls are _____ \' C \' _____ .','[{"text": "A - Euglenoids, B - Pellicle, C - Flexible", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Dinoflagellates, B - Silica, C - indestructible", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Slimemoulds, B - Cellulose, C - destructible", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Diatoms, B - Silica, C - indestructible", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In diatoms, the cell walls form two thin overlapping shells which fit together as in a soap box. The walls are embedded with silica and thus the walls are indestructible.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102553,'biology',74,247,489,'<br>${\\text{(I)}}\\,{\\text{Cholera}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(}}\\,{\\text{II)}}\\,{\\text{Tetanus}}$<br>${\\text{(III)}}\\,{\\text{Plague}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(IV)}}\\,{\\text{Turnip}}\\,{\\text{mosaic}}$<br>${\\text{(V)}}\\,{\\text{Citrus}}\\,{\\text{canker}}\\,\\,\\,{\\text{(VI)}}\\,{\\text{Polio}}$<br>Which of the following diseases mentioned above are caused by bacteria?','[{"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, V are bacterial diseases. Turnip mosaic and polio are viral diseases.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102555,'biology',74,248,492,'Study the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Diatoms float passively in water currents.<br>(II) Red tides are formed due to bioluminescence.<br>(III) Dinoflagellates are mostly fresh water organisms and photosynthetic.<br>(IV) Chrysophytes are found in freshwater as well as in marine environments.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, IV are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Red tides are formed due to rapid multiplication of the dinoflagellate - <i>Gonyaulax</i>. Dinoflagellates are mostly marine water organism & photosynthetic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102556,'biology',74,249,499,'Find the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) Truffles - Club fungi<br>(II) Methanogens - Human intestine<br>(III) Thermoacidophiles - Hot sulphur springs<br>(IV) Slime moulds - True wall found in the vegetative stage.<br>(V) Whittaker\'s system of Classification - brought together <i>Chlamydomonas, Chlorella</i> with <i>Paramoecium, Amoeba</i> in protista.<br>(VI) Roquefort cheese - Ascomycetes','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, IV are incorrect statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Truffles - sac fungi, Methanogens - ruminants intestine, Slime moulds - True wall found in spore stage.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102557,'biology',74,255,506,'Find the correct statement from the following<br>(I) Linnaeus\'s Kingdom system of classification includes Plantae and Animalia.<br>(II) Dinoflagellates - Water bloom.<br>(III) Golden algae - Chief producer in the ocean.<br>(IV) Mycoplasma - Smallest cell.<br>(V) "<i>Drosophila</i> of the plant kingdom " - <i>Claviceps</i>.<br>(VI) In lichen, the algal component is known as mycobiont and the fungal component as phycobiont.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III, IV are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as "<i>Drosophila</i> of plant kingdom" <i>Neurospora</i>, In lichen algal component is knows as phycobiont and fungal component as mycobiont.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102558,'biology',74,250,501,'<i>Euglena, Nostoc, Chlorella, Mangifera</i> Select the correct statement with respect to all these organisms:<br>(I) All are unicellular.<br>(II) All are photosynthetic and act as producers in nature.<br>(III) All belong to Kingdom Plantae.<br>(IV) Presence of chloroplast and cell wall.','[{"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II All are photosynthetic and act as producer in nature is multicellular, <i>Nostoc</i> is a monera so it does not have chloroplast and <i>Euglena</i> does not have cell wall.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102559,'biology',74,249,499,'The characteristics mentioned below belong to:<br>(I) No asexual spores are generally formed.<br>(II) Mycelium is branched and septate.<br>(III) Vegetative reproduction by fragmentation is common.<br>(IV) Sex organs are absent, but sexual reproduction takes place by somatogamy.<br>(V) Basidia are arranged in basidiocarp.','[{"text": "Sac fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Club fungi", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Algal fungi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fungi imperfecti", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Club fungi/basidiomycetes show the following features. The mycelium is branched and septate. The asexual spores are generally not found, but vegetative reproduction by fragmentation is common. The sex organs are absent, but plasmogamy is brought about by fusion of two vegetative or somatic cells of different strains or genotypes. The resultant structure is dikaryotic which ultimately gives rise to basidium. Karyogamy and meiosis take place in the basidium producing four basidiospores. The basidiospores are exogenously produced on the basidium.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102560,'biology',74,249,498,'Find the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) According to the five-kingdom classification of R.H. Whittaker, producers are placed in Monera, Protista, and Plantae.<br>(II) In Whittaker\'s five-kingdom classification, eukaryotes are assigned to all five kingdoms.<br>(III) <i>Saccharomyces</i> is unicellular and useful in fermentation.<br>(IV) According to the three-domain theory, two domains include prokaryotic organisms.<br>(V) Euglenoids have two flagella, one lies longitudinally and the other transversely.<br>(VI) Slime mould spores are dispersed by air currents.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV, VI are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as In Whittaker\'s five-kingdom classification eukaryotes are assigned to only four kingdoms. Dinoflagellates have two flagella one lies longitudinally and the other transversely.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102561,'biology',74,248,492,'Select the incorrect statement with respect to dinoflagellates:<br>(I) These are golden-brown photosynthetic protists.<br>(II) They are mostly marine, and some are found in fresh water.<br>(III) They appear yellow, green, brown, blue, or red depending on the main pigments present in their cells.<br>(IV) Most of them are filamentous and lack flagella except in the reproductive stage.','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IV is incorrect. Most of dinoflagellates have two flagella; one lies longitudinally and the other transversely in a furrow between the wall plates.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102562,'biology',74,249,499,'<i>Sacharomyces, Albugo, Rhizopus, Ustilago, Puccinia, Agaricus, Trichoderma, Alternaria</i>. Which of the following examples are belongs to class basidiomycetes.','[{"text": "<i>Ustilago, Puccinia, Agaricus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Agaricus, Trichoderma, Alternaria</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Sacharomyces, Albugo, Rhizopus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Puccinia, Agaricus, Trichoderma</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Puccinia, Agaricus, Ustilago</i> belong to basidiomycetes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102563,'biology',74,253,504,'Difference between virus and viroid is<br>(I) Absence of protein coat in viroid but present in virus.<br>(II) Presence of low molecular weight RNA in virus but absent in viroid.<br>(III) Some viruses have RNA as genetic material and <i>viroids</i> also have RNA as their genetic material.','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III are correct statements. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Presence of low molecular weight RNA in viroids whereas virus have DNA or RNA .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102565,'biology',75,719,1518,'Which of the following is an example of a zygomorphic flower?','[{"text": "Chilli", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Petunia</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Datura</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pea", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>Zygomorphic flowers exhibit bilateral symmetry, meaning they can be divided into two equal halves only through one vertical plane. Among the given options: Pea has zygomorphic\nflowers. Chilli, <i>Petunia</i>, and <i>Datura</i> have actinomorphic (radially symmetrical) flowers. Hence, Pea is the correct example of a zygomorphic flower.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102566,'biology',75,722,1526,'Given below are two statements:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In a floral formula $ \\oplus $ stands for zygomorphic nature of the flower, and ${\\underset{\\raise0.3em\\hbox{$\\smash{\\scriptscriptstyle-}$}}{G} }$ stands for inferior ovary</div><div class="column-right">In a floral formula $ \\oplus $ stands for actinomorphic nature of the flower and ${\\underset{\\raise0.3em\\hbox{$\\smash{\\scriptscriptstyle-}$}}{G} }$ stands for superior ovary.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct answer is option 1.<br>In floral formulae, the symbol $ \\oplus $ represents actinomorphic (radially symmetrical) flowers, while % represents zygomorphic (bilaterally symmetrical) flowers. G represents the gynoecium. When the line is below the $G\\left( {\\underset{\\raise0.3em\\hbox{$\\smash{\\scriptscriptstyle-}$}}{G} } \\right)$ it denotes a superior ovary; when the line is above the $G(\\bar G)$, it denotes an inferior ovary.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102567,'biology',75,724,1528,'Identify the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) Pentamerous, actinomorphic flowers, monocarpellary ovary with an oblique ovary, and fruit as a capsule or berry are characteristic features of Solanaceae.<br>(II) Keel is the characteristic feature of the flower of Brassicaceae.<br>(III) Fumigatory (tobacco) and ashwagandha belong to Solanaceae.<br>(IV) The reduced cotyledon in grasses is called epicotyl.<br>(V) Valvate aestivation of corolla is found in cotton (Malvaceae).<br>(VI) The floral formula given <img src=\'/img/data/biology/75_102567_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> belongs to <i>Nicotiana</i>.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, V are correct, Pentamerous, actinomorphic flowers, bicarpellary ovary with oblique ovary and fruit as a capsule or berry are characteristic feature of Solanaceae. Keel is the characteristic feature of the flower of <i>Trifolium</i>. The reduced cotyledon in grasses called Epiblast.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102568,'biology',75,719,1521,'Identify the correct match from the following:<br>(I) Epitepalous - Lily<br>(II) Diadelphous - <i>Sesbania</i><br>(III) Polyadelphous - <i>Citrus</i><br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, and III ARE CORRECT.  Lily is epitepatous, Sesbania is diadelphous, Citrus is polyadelphous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102569,'biology',75,719,1522,'Identify the correct match from the following:<br>(I) Polyadelphous - Pea<br>(II) Epiphyllous - Lily<br>(III) Monoadelphous - Hibiscus<br>(IV) Monoadelphous - <i>Pisum sativum</i><br>(V) Twisted aestivation - Chinarose<br>(VI) Apocarpous - Lotus<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, IV, V are correct, In Pisum, (Pea), the stamens are diadelphous $(9+1$ arrangement), not monoadelphous or polyadelphous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102570,'biology',75,724,1528,'Identify the correct match from the following:<br>(I) Epipetalous - Ashwagandha<br>(II) Roots - Absorption of water and nutrients<br>(III) The petiole - Help hold the blade to light<br>(IV) Region of meristematic activity - The cells of this region gradually differentiate.<br>(V) Region of maturation - The cells of this region are very small, thin-walled, and with dense protoplasm; they divide repeatedly.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III are correct, Region of meristematic activity - The cells of this region are very small, Thin walled and with dense protoplasm, they divide repeatedly. Region of maturation -The cell of this region gradually differentiates and cells become permanent.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102571,'biology',75,719,1523,'Which of the given plants have marginal placentation?<br>(I) Pea, Tomato, Marigold.<br>(II) Pea, Muliathi, <i>Sesbania</i>, Indigofera, <i>Lupin</i>.<br>(III) Muliathi, <i>Petunia</i>, <i>Citrus</i>.<br>(IV) Pea, <i>Pistia</i>','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Pea, Muliathi, <i>Sesbania, Indigofera</i>, Lupin, belong to fabaceae and have marginal placentation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102574,'biology',75,719,1523,'Identify the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) The leaf is attached to the stem by the leaf base.<br>(II) The arrangement of veins and veinlets in the lamina of a leaf is termed aestivation.<br>(III) Root hairs can be unicellular or multicellular.<br>(IV) In racemose type of inflorescence, the flowers are borne laterally in an acropetal succession.<br>(V) The ovary is one-chambered but becomes multi-chambered due to the formation of a false septum in Mustard and <i>Acacia</i>.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, V are incorrect, The arrangement of veins and the veinlets in the lamina of leaf is termed as venation, Root hair are unicellular, Ovary is one chambered but it becomes two - chambered due to the formation of false septum in Mustard and <i>Argemone</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102575,'biology',75,722,1526,'Identify the incorrect match from the following:<br>(I) Septa absent - <i>Dianthus</i>.<br>(II) Parthenocarpic fruit - Product of fertilization.<br>(III) Staminode flower - Male flower.<br>(IV) Brassicaceae - Grass.<br>(V) Sepals free - Polysepalous.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV are incorrect The incorrect statement can be corrected as Parthenocarpic fruit - fruit is formed without fertilisation,Staminate flower - Male flower, Poaceae Grass.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102576,'biology',75,716,1511,'Identify the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) The aestivation in petals of lady finger is twisted, and in <i>Calotropis</i>, it is valvate.<br>(II) Drupe fruit in mango is developed from a superior ovary.<br>(III) Out of the four whorls of a flower, androecium and gynoecium are sterile.<br>(IV) In mint and jasmine, a slender lateral branch arises from the base of the main axis and, after growing aerially for some time, arches downward to touch the ground.<br>(V) Stems are characterized by the presence of nodes and internodes.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as out of the 4 whorls of flower,calyx ,corolla are sterile.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102577,'biology',75,720,1524,'Which of the following statements are correct regarding the structure of fruit?<br>(I) A fruit consists of a wall (pericarp) and seeds.<br>(II) The pericarp can be either dry or fleshy.<br>(III) When the pericarp is thick and fleshy, it is differentiated into epicarp, mesocarp, and endocarp.<br>(IV) The epicarp is the innermost layer of the pericarp.<br>(V) The endocarp is the outermost layer of the pericarp.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the epicarp is the outermost, not the innermost layer. The endocarp is the innermost, not the outermost layer.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102579,'biology',75,717,1516,'Identify the correct options from the following:<br>(I) True septum - Mustard.<br>(II) Monocarpellary unilocular ovary-Fabaceae.<br>(III) Tendril of Beans - Modified leaf.<br>(IV) Petals united - Gamopetalous.<br>(V) Sepals persistent - Tomato, Brinjal.<br>(VI) Imbricate aestivation - <i>Cassia</i>.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III,VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV,VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, V, VI are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as False septum Mustard.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102580,'biology',75,715,1509,'Identify the correct options from the following:<br>(I) In cymose type of inflorescence, the main axis terminates in a flower, hence it is limited in growth.<br>(II) Drupe fruit in mango and coconut are developed from superior and inferior ovary respectively.<br>(III) Hanging roots mainly found in Banyan tree are tap roots.<br>(IV) Pinnately compound leaves have a rachis as in Neem.<br>V. The aestivation in petals of Cotton is twisted, and in the Potato family, it is valvate.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Drupe fruit in mango and coconut are developed from superior ovary. Hanging roots mainly found in Banyan tree are adventitious roots.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102581,'biology',75,716,1511,'Identify the incorrect match from the following:<br>(I) Inferior ovary - Sunflower, Cucumber, Potato.<br>(II) Single ovule - Sunflower - Poaceae.<br>(III) Stem tendril - Gourds.<br>(IV) Imbricate aestivation - Gulmohar.<br>(V) Petals free - Polypetalous.<br>(VI) Bicarpellary bilocular ovary - Solanaceae.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II are incorrect, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Inferior ovary - sun flower, cucumber, potato has superior ovary, Single ovule - Sunflower - Compositae',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102585,'biology',75,719,1520,'If the margins of sepals or petals overlap one another but not in any particular direction, the aestivation is called _____and is present in which plant?<br>(I) Vexillary - Pea, Bean.<br>(II) Imbricate - Chinarose, <i>Calotropis </i>.<br>(III) Twisted - China rose, Gulmohar.<br>(IV) Imbricate -  <i>Cassia</i>, Gulmohar.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'If the margins of sepals or petals overlap one another but not in any particular direction, the aestivation is called Imbricate, seen in <i>Cassia</i> and Gulmohar.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102586,'biology',75,722,1526,'Which of the following characters cannot be identified on the basis of a floral formula?<br>(I) Cohesion of stamens<br>(II) Position of ovary<br>(III) Number of whorls present<br>(IV) Aestivation<br>(V) Placentation<br>(VI) Sexuality of the flower<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IV, V is the correct option. The placentation and aestivation are not included in floral formula.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102587,'biology',75,719,1520,'The following petal arrangement is characteristic of which type of aestivation, and which of the given examples correctly represents it?<br>(I) Standard petals<br>(II) Wings laterally<br>(III) Keel petal','[{"text": "Valvate aestivation, <i>Calotropis</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Twisted aestvation, <i>Abelmoschus</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Imbricate aestivation, Gulmohar.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vexillary aestivation, <i>Lathyrus</i>.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Vexillary aestivation, <i>Lathyrus</i> is the correct answer. In pea and bean flowers, there are five petals, the largest (standard) overlaps the two lateral petals (wings) which in turn overlap the two smallest anterior petals (keel); this type of aestivation is known as vexillary or papilionaceous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102589,'biology',75,717,1514,'When multiple leaflets are present on a common axis, it is known as (A).This common axis is referred to as (B),which represents the (C) of the leaf. This type of leaf is found in (D).<br>Options:','[{"text": "A: Pinnately compound, B: Rachis,<br>C: Midrib, D: Alstonia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: Palmately compound, B: Petiole,<br>C: Midrib, D: Neem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A: Pinnately compound, B: Rachis,<br>C: Midrib, D: Neem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A: Pinnately compound, B: Petiole,<br>C: Midrib, D: Silk cotton", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In a pinnately compound leaf a number of leaflets are present on a common axis, the rachis, which represents the midrib of the leaf as in neem.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102590,'biology',75,717,1516,'Identify the correct match from the following.<br>(I) Multilocular ovary - Tomato.<br>(II) Pitcher of <i>Nepenthes</i> - Modified leaf.<br>(III) Staminode - Sterile stamen.<br>(IV) Sepals free - Polysepalous.<br>(V) Racemose inflorescence - Basipetal succession.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Racemose inflorescence - Acropetal succession.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102592,'biology',75,722,1526,'The floral formula is represented by some symbols. Find out the correct match.<br>(I) K - Corolla<br>(II) C - Calyx.<br>(III) \\(\\%\\) - Zygomorphic.<br>(IV) \\(\\oplus\\) - Actinomorphic.<br>(V) \\(\\cap\\) - Fusion.<br>(VI) ( )- Adhesion.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'III, IV are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as C - Corolla, K - Calyx, () Fusion, $\\cap$ - Adhesion.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102593,'biology',75,720,1524,'Select the incorrect statement with respect to drupe fruits:<br>(I) They are developed from a monocarpellary ovary.<br>(II) Mango and coconut are examples of this type of fruit.<br>(III) The endosperm of mango and the mesocarp of coconut is edible.<br>(IV) These fruits have a stony endocarp.<br>(V) In these fruits, the mesocarp is always fleshy and edible.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'III, V are incorrect. The endosperm of coconut and mesocarp of mango is edible.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102594,'biology',75,719,1519,'Which of the plants from the given list have both actinomorphic symmetry and hypogynous flowers?<br>(I) Rose, Mustard, Apple, <i>Datura</i>.<br>(II) Plum, Cucumber, Chilli.<br>(III) Chinarose, Guava.<br>(IV) Chilli, Chinarose, Mustard, <i>Datura</i>','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IV, Chilli, Chinarose, Mustard, <i>Datura</i> have both actinomorphic symmetry and hypogynous flowers.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102595,'biology',75,724,1528,'Mark the correct one about Solanaceae family:<br>(I) $\\mathrm{K}_{(5)}$<br>(II) Stamens attached to petals.<br>(III) Bicarpellary gynoecium<br>(IV) Valvate aestivation of petals.<br>(V) Solitary, axillary or cymose as in <i>Solanum</i>.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct. Valvate aestivation of petals, Solitary, axillary or cymose as in Solanum, Calyx: sepals five, united, persistent, Gynoecium: bicarpellary obligately placed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102596,'biology',75,719,1518,'Which of the following statements are correct regarding floral structure?<br>(I) A flower is termed trimerous, tetramerous, or pentamerous when its floral appendages are in multiples of 3,4 , or 5 , respectively.<br>(II) Flowers with reduced leaves at the base of the pedicel are called ebracteate.<br>(III) Flowers that lack bracts are referred to as ebracteate.<br>(IV) Bracteate flowers possess bracts, whichare reduced leaf-like structures at the base of the pedicel.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV are correct. Flowers with reduced leaves at the base of the pedicel are called bracteate, not ebracteate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102598,'biology',75,719,1523,'Choose the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) Parietal placentation - Pea.<br>(II) Palmately compound leaves - Silk cotton.<br>(III) Zygomorphic symmetry - Gulmohar.<br>(IV) Sepals free - Polysepalous.<br>(V) Sepals united - Gamosepalous.<br>(VI) Free central placentation - Primrose.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, V, VI are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Parietal placentation - <i>Argemone</i> and mustard',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(102599,'biology',75,719,1522,'Identify the correct term, its definition, and its correct example:<br>Given Statements:<br>(I) Carpels are free - Syncarpous - Lotus, Tomato.<br>(II) Carpels are fused - Apocarpous - Rose, Tomato.<br>(III) Carpels are free - Apocarpous - Rose, Lotus.<br>(IV) Carpels are fused - Syncarpous - Mustard, Tomato.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV are correct, Carpels free (as in lotus and rose) and are called apocarpous. They are termed syncarpous when carpels are fused, as in mustard and tomato.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102600,'biology',75,724,1528,'Choose the statements that are not true from the following:<br>(I) The aestivation in petals of Solanaceae is imbricate, and the aestivation in sepals of Solanaceae is valvate.<br>(II) Axillary buds are capable of forming a branch or a flower.<br>(III) Apical meristem gives rise to axillary buds.<br>(IV) In dicotyledonous plants, the direct elongation of the radicle leads to the formation of the primary root.<br>(V) Leaves originate from shoot apical meristems and are arranged in a basipetal order.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, IV,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, V are not true. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the aestivation in petals of solanaceae is valvate and the aestivation in sepals of solanaceae is valvate. Leaves originate from shoot apical meristems and are arranged in an acropetal order.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102602,'biology',75,719,1523,'Choose the statements that are not true from the following:<br>Given Statements:<br>(I) Pea, <i>Calotropis</i>, Groundnut, Cucumber, and Lupin have a hypogynous condition and vexillary aestivation in the corolla of their flowers.<br>(II) Whorled phyllotaxy is found in <i>Alstonia</i>.<br>(III) The leaf is attached to the stem by the leaf base and may bear two lateral small leaf - like structures called petioles.<br>(IV) A bud is present in the axil of leaflets of the compound leaf.<br>(V) Axile placentation is found in Lemon, Mustard, China rose, and Marigold.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV, V are not true. The incorrect statement can be corrected as a bud is present in the axil of petiole in both simple and compound leaves, but not in the axil of leaflets of the compound leaf. The leaf is attached to the stem by the leaf base and may bear two lateral small leaf like structures called stipules. Pea, Groundnut, Lupin - the following plantshave hypogynous condition and vexillary aestivation in corolla in their flowers, Marigold shows basal placentation, Axile placentation:- Lemon, Mustard, China - rose.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102603,'biology',75,722,1526,'Identify the correct characteristics of the Brassicaceae (Mustard family):<br>(I) Flower: Bisexual and zygomorphic.<br>(II) Calyx: Sepals four, polysepalous, aestivation imbricate, generally arranged in two whorls.<br>(III) Androecium: Stamens 6, tetradynamous.<br>(IV) Gynoecium: Bicarpellary, superior ovary with parietal placentation, apocarpous.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III are correct. Flower: Bisexual and actinomorphic. Gynoecium: Bicarpellary, superior ovary with parietal placentation. syncarpous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102604,'biology',75,721,1525,'Choose the statements that are true from the following:<br>(I) The arrangement of flowers on the floral axis is termed as venation.<br>(II) In some leguminous plants, the leaf base may become swollen, which is called the pulvinus.<br>(III) If a fruit is formed without fertilization of the ovary, it is called a parthenocarpic fruit.<br>(IV) Each ovary bears one or more ovules attached to a flattened, cushion-like placenta.<br>(V) The seed coat has two layers, the outer tegmen and the inner testa.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III, IV are true. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the arrangement of flowers on the floral axis is termed as inflorescence. The seed coat has two layers, the outer testa and the inner tegmen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102605,'biology',75,721,1525,'Choose the options that are true from the following.<br>(I) Two small and shield shaped cotyledon - scutellum.<br>(II) Thalamus - receptacle.<br>(III) Gram and pea - nonendospermic seed.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III are true. The incorrect statement can be corrected as one large and shield shaped cotyledon known as scutellum.<br>',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102606,'biology',76,852,1896,'A student observed the T.S. of a plant organ slide under microscope. He observed the vascular bundles in the stelar region as conjoint collateral and open. Based on these features of vascular bundle, identify the correct option from below.','[{"text": "Monocot Stem", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot Root", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dicot Stem", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Monocot Root", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'These features are characteristic of the dicot stem:<br>Conjoint: Xylem and phloem are located on the same radius.<br>Collateral: Xylem is towards the center (inner side), phloem towards the periphery.<br>Open: Presence of cambium between xylem and phloem — indicates secondary growth capability.<br>Monocot stems have closed vascular bundles (no cambium).<br>Roots have a different arrangement — radial\nvascular bundles, not conjoint.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102607,'biology',76,853,1897,'Match the Column-I with Column-II and choose the correct option:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-S, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P<br>(A) Radial, tetrarch, cambial ring between xylem and phloem at later stages $ \\to $ T.S. of dicot root<br>(Q) $ \\to $ Radial arrangement, tetrarch xylem, and secondary growth due to a cambial ring is characteristic of dicot roots.<br>(B) Conjoint, open and endarch $ \\to $T.S. of dicot stem (S)$ \\to $ Vascular bundles are conjoint (xylem and phloem together), open (with cambium), and endarch xylem in dicot stems.<br>(C) Radial, polyarch, large pith without cambial ring $ \\to $ T.S. of monocot root (R) $ \\to $ Monocot roots have polyarch xylem (many xylem patches), large pith, and no cambial ring.<br>(D) Conjoint, closed with sclerenchymatous bundle sheath $ \\to $ T.S. of monocot stem (P) $ \\to $ Monocot stems show conjoint, closed vascular bundles with a sclerenchymatous sheath.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508','biology/76_102607_question_1.png'),
(102608,'biology',76,853,1897,'Find the statement that is not correct with regard to the structure of monocot stem.','[{"text": "Phloem parenchyma is absent.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hypodermis is parenchymatous", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vascular bundles are scattered", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Vascular bundles are conjoint and closed", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>In a monocot stem, the key structural features are:<br>Phloem parenchyma is absent – Correct<br>Vascular bundles are scattered throughout the ground tissue – Correct.\nVascular bundles are conjoint and closed (i.e., xylem and phloem lie together; no cambium) – Correct.<br>Hypodermis is sclerenchymatous, not parenchymatous – Incorrect.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102609,'biology',76,850,1894,'Read the following statements and select the option that includes all the correct ones only:<br>(I) Palisade tissue and protophloem in leaves are present towards the abaxial and adaxial surfaces, respectively.<br>(II) Parenchyma, collenchyma, and sclerenchyma-all three-are present in the ground tissue system of the sunflower stem.<br>(III) Parenchyma, collenchyma, and sclerenchyma-all three-are present in the ground tissue system of the maize stem.<br>(IV) In terrestrial plants, the cuticle is absent on the surface of the epiblema of the root.<br>(V) The protoxylem lies towards the periphery, and the metaxylem lies towards the center. Such an arrangement of primary xylem is called endarch and is found in the root.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV , V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Parenchyma, collencyma and sclerenchyma all three are present in ground tissue system in dicot stem and maize is monocot. Palisade tissue and protophloem in leaves are present towards adaxial and abaxial surface respectively. The protoxylem lies towards periphery and metaxylem lies towards the centre. Such arrangement of primary xylem is called exarch and found in root.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102611,'biology',76,850,1893,'Which of the following is not a part of the ground tissue system?<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {\\left( {\\text{I}} \\right)\\,{\\text{General}}\\,{\\text{cortex}}} \n\\end{array}\\,\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {\\left( {{\\text{II}}} \\right)\\,{\\text{Endodermis}}} \n\\end{array}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {\\left( {{\\text{III}}} \\right)\\,{\\text{Xylem}}} \n\\end{array}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {\\left( {{\\text{IV}}} \\right)\\,{\\text{Pericycle}}} \n\\end{array}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {\\left( {\\text{V}} \\right)\\,{\\text{Phloem}}} \n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV , V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'III, V is the correct option. All tissues except epidermis and vascular bundles constitute the ground tissue. It consists of simple tissues such as parenchyma, collenchyma and sclerenchyma.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102612,'biology',76,850,1894,'Consider the following statements and select the option which includes all the correct ones only:<br>(I) Radial vascular bundles are found in roots.<br>(II) In a closed type of vascular bundle, cambium is absent.<br>(III) In an open type of vascular bundle, cambium is absent.<br>(IV) In leaves, a conjoint type of vascular bundle is found.<br>(V) Vascular bundles are conjoint and closed in the monocot stem.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, IV, V are correct . The incorrect statements can be corrected as in open type of vascular bundle, cambium is present.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102613,'biology',76,850,1894,'Find the correct match from the following:<br>(I) Root - Exarch xylem - Radial vascular bundle.<br>(II) Stem - Exarch xylem - Conjoint vascular bundle.<br>(III) Leaf - Endarch xylem - Concentric vascular bundle.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I is correct . The incorrect statements can be corrected as Stem - endarch xylem - Conjoint vascular bundle. Vascular bundles of dicot leaf are conjoint, collateral and closed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102614,'biology',76,850,1892,'Identify the incorrect statements about stomata:<br>(I) Present in the epidermis of leaves.<br>(II) Bean-shaped in dicots.<br>(III) Dumbbell-shaped in monocots.<br>(IV) They help in the exchange of gases.<br>(V) Surrounded by subsidiary cells.<br>(VI) They are cells meant for transpiration.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III, V, VI are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as stomata are opening, surrounded by guard cells. The guard cells are dumb - bell shaped in monocots, bean shaped in dicots.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102616,'biology',76,852,1896,'Identify the correct statements:<br>(I) The arrangement of layers from outside to inside in a dicot stem:<br>Hypodermis $\\rightarrow$ Endodermis $\\rightarrow$ Pericycle $\\rightarrow$ Phloem $\\rightarrow$ Xylem.<br>(II) The stomatal aperture, mesophyll cells, and the surrounding subsidiary cells are together called the stomatal apparatus.<br>(III) Trichomes are always secretory.<br>(IV) The vascular system consists of simple tissues, the phloem and the xylem.<br>(V) The epidermal layer of the root is called epiblema.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as the vascular system consists of complex tissues, the phloem and the xylem. The stomatal aperture, guard cells and the surrounding subsidiary cells are together called stomatal apparatus. Trichomes may be secretory.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102617,'biology',76,852,1896,'Which of the following characters are not found in a dicot stem?<br>(I) Scattered vascular bundles.<br>(II) Shoot hair.<br>(III) Bundle sheath sclerenchymatous.<br>(IV) Root cap.<br>(V) Conjoint, open vascular bundles.<br>(VI) Sclerenchymatous hypodermis.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV, VI are not found in dicot stem. The dicot stem has shoot hair, vascular bundle is conjoint and open.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102618,'biology',76,852,1896,'Identify the correct match in a dicot stem:<br>(I) Hypodermis - Sclerenchyma.<br>(II) Pericycle - Collenchyma.<br>(III) Endodermis - Starch sheath.<br>(IV) Pith - Parenchyma.<br>(V) Protoxylem - Endarch.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV , V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Hypodermis - collenchyma, Pericycle - sclerenchyma & parenchyma.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102619,'biology',76,853,1897,'Identify the correct match:<br>(I) Epidermis - Trichomes - Prevents transpiration.<br>(II) Hypodermis - Sclerenchymatous - Monocot stem.<br>(III) Endodermis - Casparian strips - Suberin.<br>(IV) Pith - Inconspicuous - Dicot root.<br>(V) Cambium - Secondary growth - Monocot root.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as monocots do not show secondary growth.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102620,'biology',76,850,1892,'Which of the following is true for guard cells?<br>(I) The outer walls of guard cells are thin.<br>(II) Dumbbell-shaped in dicots.<br>(III) Bean-shaped in monocots.<br>(IV) The inner walls (away from the stomatal pore) are highly thickened.<br>(V) They possess chloroplasts and regulate the opening and closing of stomata.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as the guard cells are dumb-bell shaped in monocots, bean shaped in dicots, the inner walls (towards the stomatal pore) are highly thickened.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102621,'biology',76,850,1894,'Which of the following statements is/are true?<br>(I) In the stem of the <i>Yucca</i> plant, the condition of xylem is endarch.<br>(II) The outside of the epidermis is often covered with a waxy thick layer called the cuticle.<br>(III) The cuticle prevents the loss of water.<br>(IV) The epidermis is usually single-layered.<br>(V) Cambium is always responsible for primary growth.','[{"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as cambium is responsible for secondary growth.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102622,'biology',76,853,1897,'Which of the following is true for the maize plant?<br>(I) More than six xylem bundles are present in the root.<br>(II) Collenchyma is present in the hypodermis.<br>(III) Vascular cambium in the root is completely secondary in origin.<br>(IV) Sclerenchymatous hypodermis.<br>(V) Absence of phloem parenchyma.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II,.III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as collenchyma is present in hypodermis in dicot stem, vascular cambium is absent.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102623,'biology',76,852,1896,'Which of the following is true for the vascular bundle in the stem of Bengal gram?<br>(I) 2-6 vascular bundles are present.<br>(II) Vascular bundles are almost similar in size.<br>(III) Conjoint, endarch vascular bundles are present.<br>(IV) Presence of cambium.<br>(V) Presence of a ring arrangement.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV , V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as 2-6 vascular bundle are present in monocot root.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102625,'biology',76,850,1892,'Which of the following is true for epidermal appendages?<br>(I) Trichomes, stomatal apparatus, and root hair are the main epidermal appendages.<br>(II) The trichomes are usually multicellular.<br>(III) On the stem, the epidermal hairs are called trichomes.<br>(IV) The root hair may be branched or unbranched and soft or stiff.<br>(V) The root hair is unicellular.<br>(VI) The stomata help in protection.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, III, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as the trichome may be branched or unbranched and soft or stiff. The stomata helps in transpiration is correct but it is not an epidermal appendage.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102629,'biology',76,854,1898,'Find out the correct matching pairs from the given options:<br>(I) Monocot stems - Closed vascular bundle Cambium absent.<br>(II) Dicot roots - Casparian strips - Suberized.<br>(III) Monocot stems - Hypodermis - Collenchyma.<br>(IV) Dicot stems - Pericycle - Only sclerenchyma.<br>(V) Mesophyll - Chloroplast - Leaves.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV ,V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, V are correct . The incorrect statements can be corrected as Monocot stems - Hypodermis - sclerenchyma, Dicot stems - Pericycle - parenchyma and sclerenchyma.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102630,'biology',76,850,1892,'Read the following statements and choose the correct option:<br>(I) Within angiosperms, the monocots and dicots are also seen to be anatomically different.<br>(II) On the basis of their structure and location, there are two types of tissue systems.<br>(III) The epidermal tissue system forms theoutermost covering of the whole plant body.<br>(IV) Epidermal cells are parenchymatous with a small amount of cytoplasm lining the cell wall and a small vacuole.<br>(V) The cuticle is absent in roots.','[{"text": "I , IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as on the basis of their structure and location, there are three types of tissue systems. Epidermal cells are parenchymatous with a small amount of cytoplasm lining the cell wall and a large vacuole.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102631,'biology',76,851,1895,'Monocot root differs from dicot root in -<br>(I) Presence of epidermis.<br>(II) Lacking secondary growth.<br>(III) Presence of root hair.<br>(IV) Having Casparian strips in the endodermis.','[{"text": "I , IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Only II is correct. Monocot root differs from dicot root in lacking secondary growth.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102632,'biology',76,854,1898,'Which of the following cells are parenchymatous?<br>(I) Trichoblast cells<br>(II) Medullary ray cells<br>(III) Epidermal cells<br>(IV) Dicot hypodermis<br>(V) Stomata','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as dicot hypodermis is collenchymatous, stomata is not cell.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102633,'biology',76,852,1896,'Which of the following statements are correct about the cortex of a dicot stem?<br>(I) It consists of several layers of parenchyma cells.<br>(II) These parenchyma cells are thick-walled.<br>(III) It has no intercellular spaces.<br>(IV) The innermost layer is called the endodermis.<br>(V) The cortex is inner to the epidermis.','[{"text": "I , IV,V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, IV, V are correct about cortex of dicot stem. The incorrect ones can be corrected as these parenchyma cells thin - walled. It possess intercellular spaces.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102634,'biology',76,852,1896,'Which of the following statements are correct about the endodermis?<br>(I) The root endodermis consists of a single layer of barrel-shaped cells.<br>(II) The root endodermis has no intercellular spaces.<br>(III) The tangential as well as radial walls of the root endodermal cells have a deposition of suberin in the form of Casparian strips.<br>(IV) The cells of the stem endodermis are rich in starch grains.<br>(V) Next to the root endodermis lies a single layer of cells called the pericycle.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV ,V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, IV are correct . The incorrect statements can be corrected as next to root endodermis lies a few layers of cells called as pericycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102635,'biology',76,851,1895,'Which of the following statements are correct about dicot root?<br>(I) Initiation of lateral roots and vascular cambium during secondary growth takes place in the pith.<br>(II) The pith is small or inconspicuous.<br>(III) The parenchymatous cells that lie between the xylem and the phloem are called conjunctive tissue.<br>(IV) There are usually two to four xylem and phloem patches.<br>(V) Epiblema is the outermost layer.<br>(VI) Pericycle, vascular bundles, and pith constitute the stele.<br>','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV ,V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, V, VI are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Initiation of lateral roots and vascular cambium during the secondary growth takes place in pericycle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102636,'biology',76,853,1897,'Which of the following statements are correct about the monocot stem?<br>(I) It has a parenchymatous hypodermis.<br>(II) Presence of a large number of scattered vascular bundles.<br>(III) Each vascular bundle is surrounded by a parenchymatous bundle sheath.<br>(IV) Presence of a large, conspicuous parenchymatous ground tissue.<br>(V) Vascular bundles are conjoint and closed.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV ,V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV ,V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as it has a sclerenchymatous hypodermis. Each vascular bundles surrounded by a sclerenchymatous bundle sheath.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102637,'biology',76,854,1898,'Identify the incorrect match:<br>(I) Root endodermis - Starch sheath.<br>(II) Stem endodermis - Impermeable wax.<br>(III) Pericycle in dicot root- Thick-walled parenchyma.<br>(IV) Water-containing cavities - Monocot stem.<br>(V) Mesophyll differentiated - Monocot stem.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV ,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV ,V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, V are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Root endodermis - Impermeable wax. Stem endodermis - starch sheath. Mesophyll undifferentiated - Monocot leaf',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102638,'biology',76,854,1898,'Which of the following statements are correct about vascular bundles in a dicot leaf?<br>(I) Peripheral vascular bundles are generally smaller than the centrally located ones.<br>(II) Vascular system includes vascular bundles, which can be seen in the veins and the midrib.<br>(III) The size of the vascular bundles depends on the size of the veins.<br>(IV) Reticulate venation is seen.<br>(V) The veins vary in thickness.<br>(VI) The vascular bundles are surrounded by a layer of thick-walled bundle sheath cells.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, V, VI are correct . The incorrect statements can be corrected as peripheral vascular bundles are generally smaller than the centrally located ones in monocot stem.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102639,'biology',76,854,1898,'Which of the following statements are correct about a dicot leaf?<br>(I) The mesophyll is differentiated into palisade parenchyma and spongy parenchyma.<br>(II) The adaxially placed palisade parenchyma.<br>(III) The palisade is made up of elongated cells, which are arranged vertically and parallel to each other.<br>(IV) The spongy parenchyma is oval or round and tightly arranged.<br>(V) There are numerous large spaces and air cavities between spongy parenchyma cells.','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV ,V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as the spongy parenchyma is oval or round and loosely arranged.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102640,'biology',76,854,1898,'Which of the following statements is incorrect?<br>(I) Peripheral vascular bundles are generally smaller than the centrally located ones.<br>(II) Water-containing cavities are present within the vascular bundles.<br>(III) In grasses, certain abaxial epidermal cells along the veins modify themselves into large, empty, colourless cells.<br>(IV) The parallel venation in monocot leaves is reflected in the nearly similar sizes of vascular bundles.','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III is incorrect. In grasses, certain adaxial epidermal cells along the veins modify themselves into large, empty, colourless cells.<br>',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102641,'biology',73,149,338,'Identify the incorrect statements with respect to the rules of Binominal Nomenclature.','[{"text": "Biological names are printed in Italics to indicate their non-Latin origin", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The first word represents the genus while second component denotes the specific epithet", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biological names are generally in Latin or Latinised irrespective of their origin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Biological names are underlined separately when handwritten", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statement (1) is incorrect because biological names are printed in italics not to show non-Latin origin, but to distinguish them as scientific names, which are in Latin.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102642,'biology',73,150,339,'Choose the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) All living organisms are not linked to one another because they have common genetic material of the same type.<br>(II) <i>Mangifera</i> is the name of a species.<br>(III) Polymoniales is the name of a family.<br>(IV) Dicotyledonae is the name of a division.<br>(V) <i>Triticum</i> is the name of a genus.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV are incorrect, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Polymoniales is a name of order. Dicotyledonae is name of class. <i>Mangifera</i> is a name of genus. All living organisms are linked to one another because they share common genetic material but to varying degrees.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102643,'biology',73,150,339,'Match the taxonomic categories of Mango and identify the correct option:<br>(I) Genus - <i>Mangifera</i><br>(II) Class - Dicotyledonae<br>(III) Order - Sapindales<br>(IV) Family - Anacardiaceae<br>(V) Species - <i>Indica</i><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Species -<i>indica</i>.<br>(I) Genus - <i>Mangifera</i>.<br>(II) Mango belongs to the class Dicotyledonae.<br>(III) Mango belongs to the order Sapindales<br>(IV) Mango belongs to the family Anacardiaceae.<br>(V) The species of Mango is indica (<i>Mangifera indica</i>).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102644,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following is not the correct hierarchical arrangement?<br>(I) Class $\\rightarrow$ Family $\\rightarrow$ Genus<br>(II) Phylum $\\rightarrow$ Order $\\rightarrow$ Family<br>(III) Class $\\rightarrow$ Order $\\rightarrow$ Family<br>(IV) Family $\\rightarrow$ Class $\\rightarrow$ Order<br>(V) Kingdom $\\rightarrow$ Division $\\rightarrow$ Class','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The incorrect hierarchical arrangements are I, II, IV. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the correct hierarchical arrangement in taxonomy is: Kingdom $\\rightarrow$ Phylum/Division $\\rightarrow$ Class $\\rightarrow$ Order $\\rightarrow$ Family $\\rightarrow$ Genus $\\rightarrow$ Species.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102645,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following is not true for wheat?<br>(I) Order: Poales, Class: Monocotyledonae<br>(II) Order: Poales, Kingdom: Poaceae<br>(III) Class: Monocotyledonae,<br>Kingdom: Angiospermae<br>(IV) Order: Sapindales,<br>Class: Monocotyledonae<br>(V) Family: Poaceae, Kingdom: Plantae','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV are not true for wheat, The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Triticum</i> - genus, Poaceae - family, Poales order, Monocotyledonae - class, Angiospermae-division.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102646,'biology',73,148,337,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Cellular organization of the body is the defining feature of life forms.<br>(II) Reproduction is the defining characteristic of living organisms.<br>(III) Metabolism is absent in some living organisms.<br>(IV) Metabolism is the defining characteristic of living organisms.<br>(V) Unicellular organisms also perform several metabolic reactions.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as metabolism is present in all living organisms, reproduction is not the defining characteristic of living organisms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102647,'biology',73,148,337,'Which of the following is/are not incorrect?<br>(I) Mules, female honey bees are sterile.<br>(II) The most obvious and technically complicated feature of all living organisms is to sense their surrounding environment and respond to these environmental stimuli.<br>(III) Non-living things may show consciousness.<br>(IV) Cellular organization is absent in viruses.<br>(V) Most of the living organisms lack metabolism.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, IV are (not incorrect) correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Non-living things do not have consciousness. Consciousness is a trait of living organisms only. Metabolism is a key feature of all living organisms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102648,'biology',73,149,338,'With respect to binomial nomenclature, identify the incorrect statements:<br>(I) The specific epithet is written in a capital letter.<br>(II) Biological names are always in bold and written in Latin.<br>(III) The generic name starts with a capital letter.<br>(IV) Both names are separately underlined to indicate their Latin origin.<br>(V) The author\'s name is given after the species name in abbreviated form in italics<br>(VI) The first word denoting the genus is written in a small letter.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, V, VI are incorrect, The incorrect statement can be corrected as the first word denoting the genus starts with a capital letter. The specific epithet starts with a small letter The author\'s name is not italicized but written normally after the species name.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102649,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following are correct statements?<br>(I) Genus is a group of related species.<br>(II) Family is a group of related genera.<br>(III) Class is a group of related orders.<br>(IV) Order is a higher category than family.<br>(V) Domain is a group of classes.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as domain is a higher category to kingdom and is a group of kingdoms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102650,'biology',73,150,339,'According to the hierarchical system of classification, which of the following statements is/ are correct?<br>(I) Species is the most basic level of the taxonomic category followed immediately by family.<br>(II) Similarities decrease from species to kingdom.<br>(III) Similarities increase from kingdom to species.<br>(IV) Dissimilarities decrease from division to species.<br>(V) Similarities decrease from species to class.','[{"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Species is the most basic level of taxonomic category followed by genus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102651,'biology',73,149,338,'Which of the following is/are true with reference to taxonomy?<br>(I) A taxon always belongs to a category.<br>(II) A category always indicates a taxonomic rank.<br>(III) In the taxonomic hierarchy, various taxa are arranged in descending or ascending order.<br>(IV) Each rank or taxon represents a unit of classification.<br>(V) Insecta is represented by organisms having a pair of jointed legs.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as insecta is represented by organisms having three pair of jointed legs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102652,'biology',73,149,338,'Identify the correct statement(s):<br>(I) Scientific names are given in Latin as it is a popular language throughout the world.<br>(II) Animals, mammals, and dogs represent taxa at the same level.<br>(III) In <i>Chlamydomonas</i> and <i>Amoeba</i>, reproduction is synonymous with growth, i.e., increase in the number of cells.<br>(IV) The prime source of taxonomic studies of various species of plants, animals, and other organisms is the collection of actual specimens.<br>(V) The description of any organism should enable people in any part of the world to arrive at the same name.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'III, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Scientific names are given in Latin languages, as it is dead language, so chances of changes are minimum. Animals, mammals and dogs represent taxa at different levels.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102653,'biology',73,150,339,'Match the following and choose the correct option:<br>(I) Family - Dicot<br>(II) Kingdom - Plantae<br>(III) Order - Polymoniales<br>(IV) Species - <i>tuberosum</i><br>(V) Genus - <i>Solanum</i><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Family - Malvaceae/ solanaceae, dicotyledonae - is a class.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102654,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following scientific name is most correct according to ICBN (International Code of Botanical Nomenclature)?<br>(I) Mangifera Indica Linn<br>(II) Solanum <i>tuberosum</i> Linn<br>(III) <i>Solanum tuberosum</i> Linn<br>(IV) <i>Solanum</i> tuberosum Linn<br>(V) <i>Solanum tuberosum Linn</i><br>(VI) <i>Mangifera indica</i> Linn<br>(VII)<i>Mangifera indica Linn</i>','[{"text": "IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'III,VI are correct, <i>Mangifera indica</i> Linn and <i>Solanum tuberosum</i> Linn are the correct representation according to ICBN.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102655,'biology',73,150,339,'Match the following and choose the correct option for the housefly:<br>(I) Family - Muscidae<br>(II) Kingdom - Animalia<br>(III) Order - Diptera<br>(IV) Phylum - Arthropoda<br>(V) Class - Mammalia<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Class - Insecta.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102656,'biology',73,150,339,'Consider the following statements and select the correct option:<br>(I) Mango, dicots, and plants present taxa at the same level.<br>(II) Wheat family and mango family belong to different orders but the same division.<br>(III) Potato and sweet potato families are included in order Polymoniales.<br>(IV) Species is the least basic taxonomic category.<br>(V) Dicots, monocots, and mammals represent taxa at the same level.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Mango, dicots and plants present taxa at different level. Species is the most basic taxonomic category.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102657,'biology',73,150,339,'Identify the correct statements and choose the correct option:<br>(I) Taxonomic categories are distinct biological entities and not merely morphological aggregates.<br>(II) Lion and Tiger represent different species of different genera.<br>(III) In the binomial nomenclature system, the binomial epithet includes the common name and generic name only.<br>(IV) Chordata represents a division.<br>(V) Class Mammalia has Order Primata and Order Carnivora.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Lion & Tiger represents different species of same genus. In binomial nomenclature system, binomial epithet includes generic name, species epithet and author citation. Chordata represents a phylum.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102660,'biology',73,150,339,'Select the correct match with respect to brinjal:<br>(I) Family - Solanaceae.<br>(II) Class - Dicotyledonae.<br>(III)Genus - <i>Solanum</i>.<br>(IV)Order - Sapindales.<br>(V) Species - <i>melongena</i>.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, V are correct match with respect to brinjal. The incorrect statement can be corrected as order - solanales.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102661,'biology',73,150,339,'Match the following and choose the correct option:<br>(I) Genus - Group of related species.<br>(II) Family - Group of related genera.<br>(III) Order - Group of related families.<br>(IV) Class - Group of related orders.<br>(V) Species - Group of potentially breeding individuals.<br>(VI) Kingdom - Group of related orders.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Kingdom-Group of related division.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102662,'biology',73,150,339,'Which of the following is correct for wheat?<br>(I) Its genus is <i>Triticum</i>.<br>(II) Its family is Poaceae.<br>(III) It belongs to the order Poales.<br>(IV) It belongs to the class Monocotyledonae.<br>(V) It belongs to the order Sapindales.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as wheat belongs to the order poales.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102663,'biology',73,149,338,'Study the following statements and identify the correct statements:<br>(I) Systematics is the study of different kinds of organisms, their diversities, and relationships among them.<br>(II) Lower the taxa, more are the characteristics that the members within the taxon share.<br>(III) Higher the taxonomic category, greater is the difficulty of determining the relationships to other taxa at the same level.<br>(IV) In lower taxa, the problems of classification become more complex.<br>(V) As we go higher from species to kingdom, the number of common characters increases.','[{"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Lower the taxa, more are the characteristics that the members within the taxon share. Higher the category, greater is the difficulty of determining the relationship to other taxa at the same level.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102664,'biology',73,149,338,'Consider the following statements. Which of the following statements are related to the universal rules of nomenclature?<br>(I) This naming system was given by Carolus Linnaeus.<br>(II) Scientific names are generally in Latin.<br>(III) The first word in a scientific name represents the generic name, while the second word denotes the specific epithet.<br>(IV) Both the words in a scientific name, when handwritten, are underlined together, or printed in italics to indicate their Latin origin.<br>(V) The generic name starts with a capital letter, while the specific epithet starts with a small letter.','[{"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as both the words in a scientific name, when handwritten, are separately underlined, or printed in italics to indicate their latin origin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102665,'biology',73,149,338,'Read the following statements and identify the incorrect ones:<br>(I) Classification is a single step process.<br>(II) Classification involves heirarchy of steps in which each step represent a rank or category.<br>(III) Taxon is a unit of ecological hierarchy.<br>(IV) Insects represents a species.<br>(V) Systematics takes into account evolutionary relationships between organisms.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, IV are incorrect, The incorrect statement can be corrected as insecta is a class, classification is a multistep process, An organism (or an individual) is a living unit of nature and is the most basic unit of ecological hierarchy.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102666,'biology',73,150,339,'Select the correct option with respect to classification of potato?<br>(I) Family - Solanaceae.<br>(II) Order - Poales.<br>(III) Genus - <i>Solanum</i>.<br>(IV) Class - Dicotyledonae.<br>(V) Division - Angiospermae.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as order-solanales.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102667,'biology',73,150,339,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Characterization, identification, classification, and nomenclature are the processes that are basic to taxonomy.<br>(II) The scientific term for the categories is taxa.<br>(III) Plant families like Convolvulaceae and Solanaceae are included in the order Polymoniales, and it\'s mainly based on vegetative characters.<br>(IV) <i>Solanum tuberosum</i> and <i>Mangifera indica</i> have the same genus but different species.<br>(V) The biodiversity is around 1.7-1.8 million species.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Plant families like convolvulaceae and solanaceae are included in the order of Polymoniales, and it\'s mainly based on floral characters. <i>Solanum tuberosum</i> and <i>Mangifera indica</i> have same the division but different species.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102668,'biology',73,148,337,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Growth is a fundamental characteristic of all living organisms and it is regarded as an intrinsic property in them.<br>(II) Ernst Mayr pioneered the currently accepted definition of a biological species.<br>(III) Mayr was awarded the three prizes widely regarded as the triple crown of biology.<br>(IV) The fungi, all algae, the protonema of mosses, all easily multiply by fragmentation.<br>(V) Reproduction is a defining characteristic of living organisms.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as the fungi, the filamentous algae, the protonema of mosses, all easily multiply by fragmentation. Reproduction, is not a defining characteristic of living organisms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102669,'biology',73,148,337,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) The sum total of all the chemical reactions occurring in our body is catabolism.<br>(II) In <i>Planaria</i>, true regeneration is seen.<br>(III) Cellular organisation of the body is the defining feature of life forms.<br>(IV) Fungi multiply by asexual spore.<br>(V) In <i>Amoeba</i>, reproduction is synonymous with growth.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, III, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as the sum total of all the chemical reactions occurring in our body is metabolism.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102670,'biology',89,1287,3108,'In the mechanism of muscle contraction or shortening of muscle, the ____ get reduced whereas the ____ retain the length.','[{"text": "A bands, Z line", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A bands, I bands", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I bands, A bands", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "lines, I bands", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'During muscle contraction (sliding filament theory), the following changes occur: I bands (light bands) shorten as actin filaments slide inward over the myosin. A bands (dark bands) retain their length because the length of myosin filaments remains unchanged.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102949,'biology',93,281,539,'From the different types of sex determination systems, identify the correctly represented cases:<br>(I) <i>Columba</i> (pigeon) - WW<br>(II) Grasshopper - XO<br>(III) Man - XY<br>(IV) <i>Apis</i> (honey bee) - Haplo-diploid','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, III, IV are correct. The incorrect one can be corrected as <i>Columba</i> - ZZ/ ZW',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102678,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Read the statements regarding muscle proteins about Actin. Identify the correct statements:<br>(I) Actin is a thin filament and is made up of two F-actins.<br>(II) The two F (filamentous) actins are helically wound around each other.<br>(III) The complex protein tropomyosin is distributed at regular intervals on the troponin.<br>(IV) Myosin is a thick filament, which is also a polymerized protein.<br>(V) The globular head of meromyosin consists of light meromyosin (LMM).','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II are correct. The incorrect options can be corrected as a complex protein Troponin is distributed at regular intervals on the tropomyosin. IV and V are about myosin and the question asked is about actin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102679,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Read the following statements about muscle contraction and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) The length of the I-band decreases.<br>(II) The A-band remains constant.<br>(III) The Z-line attached to the actins is pulled outwards.<br>(IV) Myosin heads attach to open active sites on actin filaments to form cross-bridges.<br>(V) The length of the sarcomere decreases.','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect options can be corrected as the \' Z \' line attached to these actins are also pulled inwards.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102680,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Arrange the following events of muscle contraction in sequence:<br>(I) Generation of action potential in the sarcolemma.<br>(II) Formation of a cross-bridge.<br>(III) Release of a neurotransmitter (Acetylcholine).<br>(IV) Release of calcium ions.<br>(V) Pulling of the attached actin filaments towards the center of the A-band.<br>(VI) Removal of masking of active sites for myosin.<br>(VII) Signal sent by the central nervous system (CNS) via a motor neuron.','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{I} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{II} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{III} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{IV} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{VII} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{V} \\\\rightarrow \\\\mathrm{VI}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $\\\\rightarrow$ IV $\\\\rightarrow$ I $\\\\rightarrow$ II $\\\\rightarrow$ VI $\\\\rightarrow$ VII $\\\\rightarrow$ V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III $\\\\rightarrow$ I $\\\\rightarrow$ IV $\\\\rightarrow$ II $\\\\rightarrow$ V $\\\\rightarrow$ VII $\\\\rightarrow$ VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "VII $\\\\rightarrow$ III $\\\\rightarrow$ I $\\\\rightarrow$ IV $\\\\rightarrow$ VI $\\\\rightarrow$ II $\\\\rightarrow$ V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is (4) VII $\\rightarrow$ III $\\rightarrow$ I $\\rightarrow$ IV $\\rightarrow$ VI $\\rightarrow$ II $\\rightarrow$ V because the correct sequence of events in muscle contraction is as follows:<br>VII: Signal is sent by the central nervous system (CNS) via a motor neuron.<br>III: Release of a neurotransmitter (Acetylcholine).<br>I: Generation of action potential in the sarcolemma.<br>IV: Release of calcium ions.<br>VI: Removal of masking of active sites for myosin.<br>II: Formation of a cross-bridge.<br>V: Pulling of the attached actin filaments towards the center of the A-band.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102682,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Which one of the following options gives the correct characters of different muscle type?<br>(I) Striated - Cylindrical, fibres branched, voluntary controlled by CNS, Multi nucleated.<br>(II) Cardiac - Cylindrical, fibres branched, Uninucleated.<br>(III) Non-striated - Fibres branched, Uni nucleated, involuntary under the control of ANS.<br>(IV) Striated - Cylindrical, fibres unbranched, Multi nucleated.<br>(V) Cardiac - Voluntary in nature as the nervous system does not control their activities directly.<br>(VI) Non-striated - Spindle shaped, fibres unbranched, Uninucleated.','[{"text": "I, II, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, IV, VI are correct. Non- striated Spindle shaped, fibres unbranched, uninucleate, involuntary under the control of ANS.<br>Striated - Cylindrical, fibres unbranched, voluntary controlled by CNS, Multi nucleated Cardiac - Cylindrical, fibres branched, Uninucleated, involuntary in nature as the nervous system does not control their activities directly.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102685,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Identify the correct statements regarding the sliding filament theory:<br>(I) Contraction of a muscle fibre takes place by the sliding of thin filaments over thick filaments.<br>(II) A motor neuron, along with the muscle fibres connected to it, constitutes a motor unit.<br>(III) Action potential spreads through the muscle fiber and causes the release of $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ ions into the sarcoplasm.<br>(IV) During shortening of the muscle (i.e., contraction), the \'I\' band is reduced, whereas the \'A\' band retains its length.<br>(V) The cross-bridge cycle continues until $\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$ ions are pumped back into the sarcoplasmic cisternae, resulting in the masking of myosin filaments.','[{"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV are correct. The incorrect options can be corrected as the cross bridge cycle continues till the $\\mathrm{Ca}^{++}$ions are pumped back to the sarcoplasmic cisternae resulting in the masking of actin filaments.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102687,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Which of the following are features of red muscle?<br>(I) Myoglobin content is high<br>(II) Plenty of mitochondria<br>(III) Sarcoplasmic reticulum is high<br>(IV) Aerobic muscle','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I,II, IV are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Sarcoplasmic reticulum is low.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102688,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Which one of the following pairs is incorrect regarding cardiac muscles?<br>(I) Location - Myometrium<br>(II) Branching - Present<br>(III) Gap junction - Absent<br>(IV) Striated - Yes<br>(V) Communication junctions - Intercalated discs','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III are wrong. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Gap junction - present intercalated disc. The location is myocardium.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102691,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Muscles involved in a marathon race are characterized by all of the following except:<br>(I) Contains plenty of sarcoplasmic reticulum.<br>(II) Contains more quantity of myoglobin and high $\\mathrm{O}_{2}$ storing capacity.<br>(III) Specialized for slow and less powerful contractions but for longer duration.<br>(IV) Depends on aerobic processes for energy.<br>(V) Myoglobin content is high in some.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV,V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I is the correct answer, Marathon muscles are typically red muscles and have less sarcoplasmic reticulum compared to white muscles.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102692,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Identify the incorrect statements:<br>(I) All voluntary muscles are non-striated in nature.<br>(II) All involuntary muscles are striated in nature.<br>(III) All striated muscles are voluntary in nature.<br>(IV) All non-striated muscles are involuntary in nature.<br>(V) Cardiac muscles are involuntary but striated.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as voluntary muscles are striated and involuntary are smooth, some striated muscles may not be voluntary.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102701,'biology',89,1287,3108,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) In the relaxed state, both the thin and thick filaments remain overlapped except in the center part of the thick filament.<br>(II) The central part of the A band, which is not overlapped by thin filaments, is called the H-zone.<br>(III) The joint between adjacent vertebrae in the vertebral column is an example of a fibrous joint.<br>(IV) During contraction, troponin unmasks the active sites on actin by binding with \\(\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}\\) ions.<br>(V) The globular head of actin is an active ATPase enzyme with sites for ATP binding and a binding site for myosin.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, IV are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as The joint between the adjacent vertebrae in the vertebral column is an example of cartilaginous joint. Globular head of myosin is an active ATPase enzyme which has site for ATP binding and binding site of actin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102707,'biology',89,1285,3106,'Which of the following is a characteristic of muscles?<br>(I) Excitability - Ability of muscle to respond to stimuli.<br>(II) Contractility -Ability of muscle to contract or shorten its size.<br>(III) Elasticity - Ability of muscles to return to original length after stretching.<br>(IV) Secretability - Ability to be unnoticed.<br>(V) Extensibility - Ability of muscle to stretch.','[{"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as muscles do not show secretability.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102711,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Which of the following statements is not correct regarding muscles found in the internal organs?<br>(I) These muscles are found in visceral organs, so they are called visceral muscles.<br>(II) I and A bands are absent.<br>(III) Sarcomere is the functional unit of contraction.<br>(IV) They are controlled by the autonomic nervous system.<br>(V) They are smooth/non-striated.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as sarcomere is functional unit of contraction in skeletal muscle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102727,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Which of the following functions are not related to the medulla oblongata?<br>(I) Hunger, Thirst<br>(II) Human behavior, Hearing<br>(III) Speech, Memory, Rage, Intelligence<br>(IV) Respiration, Gastric secretion','[{"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III are not related to medulla oblongata. Respiration, gastric secretion are functions of medulla oblongata.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102717,'biology',89,1286,3107,'Read the following statements and find the correct option:<br>(I) A bands are dark and contain myosin and actin.<br>(II) I bands are light and contain actin.<br>(III) During action, the A band relaxes.<br>(IV) The part between two Z-lines is a sarcomere.<br>(V) The central part of the thin filament, not overlapped by thick filament, is the H zone.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, IV are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as during action, A band contracts. This central part of thick filament, not overlapped by thin filaments is called the \' H \' zone.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102721,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Identify the correct sequence of action potential as it arrives at the axon terminal from the choices given below:','[{"text": "Axon terminal → Synaptic vesicles → Post-synaptic membrane → Synaptic cleft→ Post-synaptic neuron", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axon terminal → Synaptic vesicles → Synaptic cleft → Post-synaptic membrane → Post-synaptic neuron", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Axon terminal → Synaptic cleft → Synaptic vesicles → Post-synaptic neuron → Post-synaptic membrane", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Axon terminal → Post-synaptic membrane → Synaptic cleft → Synaptic vesicles → Post-synaptic neuron", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Axon terminal → Synaptic vesicles → Synaptic cleft → Post-synaptic membrane → Post-synaptic neuron.<br>The correct sequence of nerve impulse transmission across a synapse is:<br>Action potential reaches the axon terminal of the presynaptic neuron. This stimulates synaptic vesicles to release neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft. Neurotransmitters diffuse across the synaptic cleft and bind to receptors on the\npost-synaptic membrane. This leads to the initiation of a new action potential in the postsynaptic neuron.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102722,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Read the following statements and choose the correct option:<br>(I) The cerebellum is a part of the hindbrain.<br>(II) The midbrain is located between the thalamus of the forebrain and the pons of the hindbrain.<br>(III) A canal called the cerebral aqueduct passes through the midbrain.<br>(IV) The ventral portion of the midbrain consists mainly of four round swellings called corpora quadrigemina.<br>(V) The association areas is responsible for complex functions like memory, communication, and intersensory association.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III,V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as corpora quadrigemina is present on the dorsal side of midbrain.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102723,'biology',90,1332,3215,'In the following list, identify the structures included in the grey matter:<br>(I) Cell body, Tract<br>(II) Myelinated axon, Dendron<br>(III) Corpus callosum, Myelinated axon<br>(IV) Cerebral cortex, Cerebellar cortex<br>(V) Cell body, Dendron','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV, V are correct. Grey matter is made up of cell body, dendron and is present in Cerebral cortex, cerebellar cortex.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102724,'biology',90,1331,3214,'Which of the following statements are true?<br>(I) The neural system provides an organized network of point-to-point connections for quick coordination.<br>(II) The endocrine system provides chemical integration through enzymes.<br>(III) Coordination is the process through which two or more organs interact and complement the functions of one another.<br>(IV) The neural organization is very complex in lower invertebrates.<br>(V) The human neural system includes the CNS and PNS.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III,V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the endocrine system provides chemical integration through hormones. The neural organisation is very simple in lower invertebrates',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102725,'biology',90,1333,3216,'In case of depolarization, which of the following does not occur?<br>(I) Efflux of proteins.<br>(II) Efflux of potassium ions.<br>(III) Influx of sodium ions.<br>(IV) Voltage-gated potassium channels remain open during this phase.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'During depolarization, voltage-gated sodium channels open, allowing influx of sodium ions, which reduces the negativity of the membrane potential. Potassium efflux and the opening of voltage-gated potassium channels occur during repolarization, not depolarization.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102728,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Which of the following functions are related to the cerebellum?<br>(I) Posture, equilibrium, tone<br>(II) Regulation of breathing<br>(III) Fine and skillful voluntary movements<br>(IV) Formation of the brain stem<br>(V) Regulation of the body temperature<br>(VI) Maintenance of body balance','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, VI are correct. Cerebellum is involved in posture, equilibrium, tone, fine and skillfull voluntary movements and maintenance of body balance.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102729,'biology',90,1337,3220,'Read the following statements carefully and identify the correct statements:<br>(I) The midbrain is located between the thalamus/hypothalamus of the forebrain and the pons of the hindbrain.<br>(II) A canal called the cerebellar aqueduct passes through the midbrain.<br>(III) The midbrain and parts of the hindbrain form the brainstem.<br>(IV) The midbrain consists of four round swelling lobes called the corpora quadrigemina.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as a canal called the cerebral aqueduct passes through the midbrain. Brain stem forms the connections between the brain and spinal cord.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102731,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Impulse transmission across an electrical synapse is always faster than that across a chemical synapse.<br>(II) The medulla contains centres which control respiration, cardiovascular reflexes, and gastric secretions.<br>(III) The cerebral cortex is made up of grey matter because myelinated axons are concentrated here.<br>(IV) Association areas are responsible for memory, intersensory association, and communication.<br>(V) The limbic system is composed of the pons, medulla, and midbrain.','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as cerebral cortex is made up of grey matter because myelinated axons are concentrated here. The inner parts of cerebral hemispheres and a group of associated deep structures like amygdala, hippocampus, etc., form a complex structure called the limbic lobe or limbic system.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102732,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Which of the following statements are true about the electrical synapse?<br>(I) At electrical synapses, the membranes of pre- and post-synaptic neurons are in very close proximity.<br>(II) Electrical current can flow directly from one neuron into the other across the synapse.<br>(III) Transmission of an impulse across electrical synapses is very similar to impulse conduction along a single axon.<br>(IV) Electrical synapses pass electrical signals between cells with the use of acetylcholine.<br>(V) Electrical synapses are fast.<br>(VI) Electrical synapses are rare in our system.','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III,V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, V, VI are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as at electrical synapse, the transfer of impulse occurs by purely electrical means without involving any neurotransmitter.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102733,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Read the following options and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Synaptic cleft - Structural bridge<br>(II) Multipolar neurons - Cerebral cortex<br>(III) Synapse - No membranes<br>(IV) Bipolar neuron - Retina of ear<br>(V) Synaptic knob - Neurotransmitter<br>(VI) Dendrite - Nissl\'s granules','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, II", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, V, VI are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Synaptic cleft - gap, Synapse - junction. Bipolar neuron Retina of eye.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102734,'biology',90,1331,3214,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Peripheral nervous system is divided into the somatic nervous system and autonomic nervous system.<br>(II) Central nervous system includes the brain and vertebral column.<br>(III) Afferent nerve fibres transmit impulses from the CNS to organs.<br>(IV) Efferent fibres transmit regulatory impulses from the CNS to the concerned peripheral tissues/organs.<br>(V) CNS is the site of information processing and control.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Central nervous system includes brain & spinal cord. Afferent nerve fibre transmit impulse from organ to CNS.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102735,'biology',90,1333,3216,'During the resting stage of the neuron, identify the correct options related to it:<br>(I) Axoplasm - High $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$and low $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$<br>(II) Axolemma - More permeable to sodium ions.<br>(III) Axolemma - Impermeable to negatively charged proteins.<br>(IV) Fluid outside the axon - Low $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$and high $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$<br>(V) $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}-\\mathrm{K}^{+}$pump - Passive transport','[{"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Axolemma more permeable to potassium ions. $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}-\\mathrm{K}^{+}$ pump - Active transport.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102736,'biology',90,1333,3216,'Read the following statements and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) In polarization $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ions move from ECF to ICF and inner charge is positive.<br>(II) The electrical potential difference across the resting plasma membrane is called the resting potential.<br>(III) In depolarization, $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ions move from ECF to ICF through ion channels.<br>(IV) In repolarization, $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$ions move from ICF to ECF through ion channels, and the inner charge becomes negative.<br>(V) During an action potential, the outer surface of the membrane becomes negatively charged, and the inner side becomes positively charged.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as in polarisation axonal membrane is impermeable to sodium ions. In polarization $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ions move from ICF to ECF and inner charge is negative.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102738,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Find the correct match:<br>(I) Limbic system - Regulation of sexual behaviour with hypothalamus.<br>(II) Thalamus - Coordinates sensory and motor signals.<br>(III) Nephrons - Impulses from tissues to CNS and vice versa.<br>(IV) Association areas- Intersensory association, memory, and communication.<br>(V) Pons - Consists of fibre tracts that interconnect different brain regions.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Neurons Impulses from tissues to CNS and vice-versa.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102739,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Identify the correct match from the following:<br>(I) Medulla oblongata - Association centres.<br>(II) Cerebral aqueduct - Midbrain.<br>(III) Corpus callosum - Cerebral hemispheres.<br>(IV) Hippocampus - Limbic system.<br>(V) Pons - Hindbrain.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'II, III IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Medulla oblongata - control respiration, cardiovascular reflexes and gastric secretions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102740,'biology',90,1338,3221,'Which of the following statements are false?<br>(I) Action potential is in fact termed as nerve impulse.<br>(II) Brain stem forms the connections between the brain and spinal cord.<br>(III) The electrical potential difference across the resting plasma membrane is called as action potential.<br>(IV) The rise in the stimulus induced permeability to $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$last for a long time.<br>(V) When $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$diffuses outside the axon, it restores the resting potential of membrane at the site of excitation.','[{"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III,V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, V are false. The incorrect statements can be corrected as the electrical potential difference across the resting plasma membrane is called as resting potential. The rise in the stimulus induced permeability to $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$last for a long time.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102741,'biology',90,1332,3215,'"The neural system of all the animals is composed of highly specialised cells called neurons which can detect, receive and transmit different kinds of stimuli". The above highlighted words represents which property of neurons respectively?<br>(I) Excitability, Conductivity, Sensitivity<br>(II) Conductivity, Sensitivity, Excitability<br>(III) Excitability, Sensitivity, Conductivity<br>(IV) Sensitivity, Excitability, Conductivity','[{"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV is correct. "The neural system of all the animals is composed of highly specialised cells called neurons which can detect, receive and transmit different kinds of stimuli, represents sensitivity,excitability, and conductivity.Detect: This refers to the ability of neurons to respond to a stimulus, which is called excitability.Receive: This refers to the neuron\'s ability to perceive and process sensory information, which is sensitivity.Transmit: This refers to the ability to carry the signal or impulse to another neuron or effector, which is conductivity.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102744,'biology',90,1331,3214,'Read the following statements and choose the option which is true about the visceral nervous system:<br>(I) It is part of the peripheral nervous system.<br>(II) It comprises the whole complex of nerves, fibres, ganglia, and plexuses.<br>(III) It is part of the central nervous system.<br>(IV) Impulses travel from the central nervous system to the viscera and from the viscera to the central nervous system.<br>(V) It comprises the whole complex of nerves, fibres, nuclei, and axons.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Visceral nervous system is the part of the peripheral nervous system. It comprises the whole complex of nerves, fibres, ganglia, and plexuses.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102745,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Identify the correct statements from the following about neurotransmitters:<br>(I) Neurotransmitters are involved in the transmission of impulses.<br>(II) Neurotransmitters are stored in vesicles.<br>(III) Acetylcholine is an e.g. of neurotransmitter.<br>(IV) Neurotransmitters bind to receptors in the pre-synaptic membrane.<br>(V) Binding of neurotransmitters opens ion channels allowing the entry of ions which can generate a new potential in the post-synaptic neuron.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Neurotransmitters bind to receptors in post synaptic membrane.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102746,'biology',90,1334,3217,'Identify the correct statements from the following about chemical synapse:<br>(I) The membranes of the pre-and postsynaptic neurons are separated by a fluid filled space called the synaptic cleft.<br>(II) The two neurons involved are known as pre-synaptic and post-synaptic neurons.<br>(III) They are rare in our system.<br>(IV) They are fast in transmission.<br>(V) Synaptic vesicles move towards the membrane where they fuse with the plasma membrane in chemical synapse.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as chemical synapse are slow in transmission. Electrical synapses are rare in our system.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102747,'biology',90,1335,3218,'Identify the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) The brain is divided into three major parts: forebrain, midbrain, and hindbrain.<br>(II) The human brain is well protected by the skull.<br>(III) The brain is covered by cranial meninges.<br>(IV) The outer layer of the meninx is called arachnoid.<br>(V) The very thin middle layer of the meninx is called pia mater.<br>(VI) The inner layer of the meninx in contact with the brain tissue is called dura mater.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as the outer layer is called dura mater. The very thin middle layer called arachnoid The inner layer in contact with the brain tissue is called pia mater.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102748,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Identify the correct statements from the following about the neuron:<br>(I) It is a macroscopic structure composed of three major parts.<br>(II) The parts are the cell body, dendrites, and exon.<br>(III) The cell body contains cytoplasm with typical cell organelles and certain granular bodies called Nissl\'s granules.<br>(IV) Short fibres that branch repeatedly and project out of the cell body are called dendrites.<br>(V) The axon is a long fibre, the distal end of which is branched.<br>(VI) The branch of the axon terminates as a bulb-like structure called the synaptic knob.','[{"text": "III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'III, IV, V, VI are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as It is a microscopic structure composed of three major parts. They are cell body, dendrites and axon.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102749,'biology',90,1331,3214,'Identify the false statements from the following:<br>(I) The somatic neural system relays impulses from the CNS to skeletal muscles.<br>(II) The autonomic neural system transmits impulses from the CNS to the involuntary organs and smooth muscles of the body.<br>(III) The autonomic neural system is further classified into the central neural system (CNS) and the peripheral neural system (PNS).<br>(IV) The nerve fibres of the PNS are of two types: they are afferent (motor) fibres and efferent (sensory) fibres.<br>(V) The human neural system is divided into two parts: the sympathetic neural system and the parasympathetic neural system.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV, V are false. The incorrect statements can be corrected as the nerve fibres of the PNS are of two types, they are afferent (sensory) fibres and the efferent (motor) fibres. The human neural system is divided into two parts : the central neural system (CNS) and the peripheral neural system (PNS). The autonomic neural system is further classified into sympathetic neural system and parasympathetic neural system.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102750,'biology',90,1332,3215,'Identify the correct option from the following:<br>(I) Dendrites - These fibres transmit impulses towards the cell body.<br>(II) Synaptic vesicles - Contain chemicals called neurotransmitters.<br>(III) Axons - Transmit nerve impulses away from the cell body to a synapse or to a neuromuscular junction.<br>(IV) Multipolar neurons - One axon and two or more dendrites.<br>(V) Non-myelinated neurons - Nodes of Ranvier.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as myelinated neurons - Nodes of Ranvier.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102751,'biology',83,499,1015,'During a field trip, a student observed a marine organism with worm-like body. The cylindrical body was divisible into proboscis, collar and a long trunk. The organism may be','[{"text": "<i>Trygon</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Balanoglossus</i>", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "<i>Ophiura</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Pterophyllum</i>", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'<i>Balanoglossus</i> is a marine, bilaterally symmetrical, and triploblastic organism. It shows a body plan with three distinct regions: proboscis, collar, and trunk.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102752,'biology',83,500,1018,'Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion and the other is labelled as Reason.<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> All vertebrates are chordates but all chordates are not vertebrate<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The members of subphylum vertebrata possess notochord during the embryonic period, the notochord is replaced by cartilaginous or bony vertebral column in adults.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>Assertion is true: All vertebrates are part of the phylum Chordata, but not all chordates are vertebrates. Some chordates (like urochordates and cephalochordates) lack a vertebral column and are therefore non-vertebrate chordates.<br>Reason is also true: In vertebrates (subphylum Vertebrata), a notochord is present during embryonic development, which is later replaced by a bony or cartilaginous vertebral column in the adult form. Since the Reason correctly explains the Assertion, the correct answer is: (2) Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102753,'biology',83,501,1019,'All living members of the class Cyclostomata are:','[{"text": "Ectoparasite", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Free living", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endoparasite", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Symbiotic", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct answer is option 1. Members of class Cyclostomata, such as lampreys and hagfishes, are jawless, marine vertebrates. All living cyclostomes are ectoparasites on some fishes. They attach to the host’s body surface using a suctorial mouth and feed on blood and body fluids.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102754,'biology',83,498,1014,'Role of the water vascular system in Echinoderms is<br>A. Respiration and Locomotion<br>B. Excretion and Locomotion<br>C. Capture and transport of food<br>D. Digestion and Respiration<br>E. Digestion and Excretion<br>Choose the correct answer from the options<br>given below :','[{"text": "B, D and E Only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and B Only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and C Only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B and C Only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>The water vascular system is a unique feature of echinoderms (e.g., starfish, sea urchins) and performs the following functions:<br>Locomotion – Movement of tube feet using\nhydraulic pressure<br>Capture and transport of food – Tube feet assist in holding prey and moving food Respiration – Gas exchange also occurs through tube feet and dermal branchiae<br>Excretion – Echinoderms lack a specialized excretory system; waste is eliminated via diffusion across the body surface.<br>Digestion – Performed by the digestive system, not the water vascular system.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103290,'biology',103,965,2247,'Malignant malaria is caused by','[{"text": "<i>Plasmodium rubrum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Plasmodium malariae</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Plasmodium vivax</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Plasmodium falciparum</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'<i>Plasmodium falciparum</i> causes malignant (most severe and fatal) malaria. It can lead to serious complications like cerebral malaria and death if untreated.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102755,'biology',83,489,1004,'While trying to find out the characteristic of a newly found animal, a researcher did the histology of adult animal and observed a cavity with presence of mesodermal tissue towards the body wall but no mesodermal tissue was observed towards the alimentary canal. What could be the possible coelome of that animal?','[{"text": "Spongocoelomate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Acoelomate", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pseudocoelomate", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Schizocoelomate", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3. In pseudocoelomates, the body cavity (pseudocoel) is not completely lined by mesoderm — it is present only on the outer side, not around the gut. This is characteristic of animals like\nAschelminthes (e.g., roundworms).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102756,'biology',83,489,1003,'Consider the following statements and select the option which includes all the correct ones:<br>(I) The majority of members of Animalia are multicellular, but a few are unicellular.<br>(II) In sponges, the cells are arranged as loose cell aggregates.<br>(III) Platyhelminthes exhibit a cellular level of organization.<br>(IV) All multicellular animals do not exhibit the same pattern of organization of cells.<br>(V) In coelenterates, the organ level of organization is seen.<br>(VI) Organ systems in different groups of animals exhibit various patterns of complexities.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II,IV, VI are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as in coelenterates, tissue level of organisation is seen. All members of Animalia are multicellular, unicellular animal like organisms are placed under Protista. Platyhelminthes exhibit organ - organ system level of organisation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102757,'biology',83,500,1017,'Which of the following statements are incorrect?<br>(I) <i>Aplysia</i> and <i>Chaetopleura</i> both are included in mollusca.<br>(II) <i>Salpa</i> is a euchordata.<br>(III) In echinodermata, exoskeleton of calcareous ossicles are present.<br>(IV) Circulatory system is open in Hemichordata.<br>(V) Radial symmetry is observed in Annelids & Echinoderms.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as The radial symmetry is observed in coelenterates & echinoderms. <i>Salpa</i> has notochord in the larval tail only. In echinodermata endoskeleton of calcareous ossicles are present.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102760,'biology',83,495,1011,'Which of the following is a correct match of the animal with its respective feature?<br>(I) Earthworm - Monoecious<br>(II) <i>Ascaris</i> - Malpighian tubules<br>(III) <i>Nereis</i> - Trachea<br>(IV) Flatworms - Pseudocoelom<br>(V) <i>Ascaris</i> - Dioecious<br>(VI) <i>Fasciola</i> - Monoecious<br>(VII) <i>Taenia</i> - Monoecious<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, VI, VII", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V, VI, VII", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, V, VI, VII are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as In <i>Ascaris</i>, the excretory system consists of one or two large renette gland cells. Parapodia in <i>Neresis</i> are paired, unjointed lateral appendages found in polychaete worms, which are often fleshy (especially in marine polychaetes) and used for locomotion, respiration, and other functions. Flatworms have a flat body because they do not have a coelom or even a pseudocoelom.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102761,'biology',83,503,1021,'Identify the correct option about the organism and its correct feature from the following:<br>(I) <i>Catla</i>: Freshwater habitat with a streamlined body, two-chambered heart, air bladder present to regulate buoyancy.<br>(II) <i>Exocoetus</i>: Bony fish, body is covered with cycloid scales, mouth is ventral, freshwater fish.<br>Four pairs of gills with operculum.<br>(III) <i>Trygon</i>: Stingray, internal fertilization, viviparous.<br>(IV) <i>Myxine</i>: Hagfish, cranium and vertebral column are cartilaginous. Circulation is of the closed type.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV are correct. <i>Exocoetus</i> - It is a bony fish. The body is covered with cycloid scales. The mouth is terminal, and the jaws bear teeth. It is a marine fish. Four pair of gills with operculum.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102762,'biology',83,501,1019,'Identify the correct option about the organism and its correct feature from the following:<br>(I) <i>Petromyzon</i>: Flying fish, after spawning, within a few days, they die. Their larvae, after metamorphosis, return to the ocean.<br>(II) <i>Limulus</i>: A primitive aquatic arthropod, and is considered a "living fossil."<br>(III) <i>Saccoglossus</i>: Worm-like marine animals, presence of posterior proboscis.<br>(IV) Roundworm: Pseudocoelomate, alimentary canal is complete with a well developed muscular pharynx.<br>(V) <i>Pinctada</i>: Mollusca, oviparous with indirect development.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Saccoglossus</i> - worm - like marine animals, presence of anteriorproboscis, <i>Petromyzon</i> - Lamprey.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102763,'biology',83,503,1021,'Identify the incorrect statement/match:<br>(I) Cyclostomata is a class<br>(II) <i>Labeo</i> - Three-chambered heart<br>(III) Subphylum - Urochordata, Cephalochordata, Vertebrata<br>(IV) <i>Petromyzon</i> - Body covered with placoid scales and mouth is ventral<br>(V) Superclass - Pisces, Tetrapoda<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, IV are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Labeo - Two chambered heart. Petromyzon have a sucking and circular mouth without jaws Their body is devoid of scales and paired fins.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102764,'biology',83,502,1020,'Which of the statements are correct for cartilaginous fish?<br>(I) In males, pelvic fins bear claspers.<br>(II) Four pairs of gills are covered by an operculum.<br>(III) Cartilaginous endoskeleton.<br>(IV) Poikilotherms.<br>(V) Mostly oviparous, fertilization is usually external.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III, IV are correct for cartilagenous fish. The incorrect statement can be corrected as gills are not covered by operculum, They have internal fertilisation and many of them are viviparous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102765,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Vertebrate which doesn\'t possess a jaw is <i>Petromyzon</i>.<br>(II) <i>Pristis</i> is an example of a bony fish.<br>(III) <i>Carcharodon</i> is the great white shark.<br>(IV) <i>Pterophyllum</i> is an example of a bony fish.<br>(V) <i>Trygon</i> is a sting ray.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV, V are correct .The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Pristis</i> is an example of cartilaginous fish.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102766,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which of the following is incorrect for amphibians?<br>(I) Development is indirect.<br>(II) They can respire through the skin only.<br>(III) Some amphibians are found in the sea.<br>(IV) Body is divisible into head and trunk.<br>(V) The heart is three-chambered (one auricle and two ventricles).<br>(VI) The eyes have eyelids.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II,III, V are incorrect for amphibians. The incorrect statement can be corrected as the heart is three chambered (two auricles and one ventricle). Respiration is by gills, lungs and through skin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102768,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which of the following statements are incorrect?<br>(I) All the members of the phylum Ctenophora are marine.<br>(II) Sponges have a protoplasmic level of body organization.<br>(III) Parasitic flatworms have a well developed digestive tract.<br>(IV) Male <i>Ascaris</i> is long, and the female is short.<br>(V) <i>Bufo, Corvus</i>, and <i>Delphinus</i> are homeothermal animals.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, III, IV, V are incorrect .The incorrect statement can be corrected as Sponges have cellular level of body organisation. Parasitic flatworms do not have well developed digestive tract. <i>Bufo</i> is poikilotherm. Male <i>Ascaris</i> has curved posterior end ; female <i>Ascaris</i> has straight posterior end.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102770,'biology',83,502,1020,'Identify the correct match from the following:<br>(I) <i>Adamsia</i> - Sea anemone - Polyp only<br>(II) <i>Aurelia</i> - Jellyfish - Polyp and medusa both<br>(III) <i>Pristis</i> - Dogfish - Chondrichthyes<br>(IV) <i>Obelia</i> - Sea fur - Polyp and medusa both<br>(V) <i>Pleurobrachia</i> - Sea walnut - No polyp and medusa<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, IV, V are correct .The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Aurelia</i> - Jelly fish - Medusa only, Pristis - saw fish Chondrichthyes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102772,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which of the following is incorrectly matched?<br>(I) <i>Sycon</i> - Asymmetrical, Tissue level organisation, Diploblastic.<br>(II) Platyhelminthes - Bilateral symmetry, Organ system level organisation, Triploblastic.<br>(III) Coelenterata - Asymmetrical, Tissue level organisation, Diploblastic.<br>(IV) <i>Physalia</i> - Marine habitat, Member of Ctenophora, Body asymmetric.<br>(V) Mollusca - Bilateral symmetry, Organ system level organisation, Triploblastic.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, IV are incorrect, the incorrect statement can be corrected as.<br>(II) Platyhelminthes - Bilateral symmetry, Organ level organisation, Triploblastic.<br>(IV) <i>Physalia</i> - Marine habitat, Member of ctenophora, Radially symmetrical.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102775,'biology',83,494,1010,'Identify the correct statements for <i>Ascaris</i>:<br>(I) Muscular pharynx.<br>(II) Pseudocoelomate.<br>(III) Often females are longer than males.<br>(IV) Nephridia for osmoregulation and excretion.<br>(V) Presence of organ system level of organisation.<br>(VI) Causative agent of the disease Elephantiasis.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, V are correct, the incorrect statement can be corrected as Renette glands for osmoregulation and excretion. Causative agent of the disease ascariasis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102776,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which is the incorrect match for the animal and its common name?<br>(I) <i>Obelia</i> - Jellyfish<br>(II) <i>Gorgonia</i> - Sea fan<br>(III) <i>Pennatula</i> - Brain coral<br>(IV) <i>Nereis</i> - Earthworm<br>(V) <i>Pila</i> - Pearl oyster<br>(VI) <i>Taenia</i> - Tapeworm<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, IV,V are incorrect, the incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Aurelia</i> - Jelly fish, <i>Pennatula</i> - sea pen, <i>Pheretima</i> Earthworm, <i>Pila</i> - apple snail.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102777,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which animal is correctly matched with its taxon group and character?<br>(I) <i>Balanoglossus</i> - Circulatory system is absent - Hemichordata.<br>(II)  <i>Hippocampus</i> - Air bladder is present Chondrichthyes.<br>(III)  <i>Sycon</i> - Pore bearing, canal system Porifera.<br>(IV) <i>Periplaneta</i> - Jointed appendages, chitinous exoskeleton - Arthropoda.<br>(V) <i>Asterias</i> - Spiny skinned, water vascular system - Echinodermata.<br>(VI) <i>Pila</i> - Body segmented, mouth with radula - Mollusca.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV, V are correct, the incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Hippocampus</i> - Air bladder is present - osteichthyes, <i>Pila</i> Body unsegmented, mouth with Radula Mollusca.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102788,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) <i>Echinus</i> - Echinodermata<br>(II) <i>Locusta</i> - Gregarious pest<br>(III) <i>Limulus</i> - King Crab<br>(IV) <i>Taenia solium</i> - Muscular pharynx<br>(V) Human - Indirect development Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Aschelminthes - Muscular pharynx, Human - direct development.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102778,'biology',83,500,1018,'Which of the following statements are incorrect?<br>(I) Tetrapoda has cranium, vertebral column, ventral heart, pulmonary respiration, and two pairs of limbs.<br>(II) Female <i>Ascaris</i> have cloaca.<br>(III) First phylum to have a complete digestive tract can be represented by <i>Pheretima</i>.<br>(IV) In the evolutionary history of the animal kingdom, organ level of organisation and metameric segmentation evolved for the first time in phylum Platyhelminthes.<br>(V) Devil fish is a true fish.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, III, IV, V are incorrect, the incorrect statement can be corrected as Male <i>Ascaris</i> has curved posterior end ; female <i>Ascaris</i> has straight posterior end. First phylum to have complete digestive tract can be represented by <i>Ancylostoma</i>. In the evolutionary history of the animal kingdom, organ level of organisation, Bilateral symmetry have evolved for the first time in phylum platyhelminthes. Devil fish is a mollusca.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102779,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) <i>Laccifer</i> belongs to Arthropoda.<br>(II) Sponges are generally marine except <i>Spongilla</i>.<br>(III) The body of <i>Chaetopleura</i> is divided into proboscis, collar, and trunk.<br>(IV) The importance of the presence of air bladder in Pisces is that it regulates buoyancy.<br>(V) Coelenteron cavity is found in Cnidaria.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III , IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, IV, V are correct, the incorrect statement can be corrected as the body of is hemichordates is divided into proboscis, collar and trunk. Chaetopleura is a mollusca.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102780,'biology',83,502,1020,'Which of the following is a characteristic of cartilaginous fishes?<br>(I) 2-chambered heart, teeth are modified placoid scales that are backwardly directed.<br>(II) Paired fins, gills without operculum, powerful jaw.<br>(III) Presence of a swim bladder; does not need to swim constantly.<br>(IV) Gills without operculum, streamlined body.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, IV are correct, the incorrect statement can be corrected as in cartilaginous fishes there is absence of swim bladder, they have to swim constantly to avoid sinking.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102781,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which group of animals belongs to same phylum?<br>(I) <i>Catla, Pavo, Trygon</i><br>(II) <i>Sycon, Euspongia, Physalia</i><br>(III) <i>Ascaris, Neries, Fasciola</i><br>(IV) <i>Pila, Sepia, Octopus</i><br>(V) <i>Euspongia, Spongilla, Scoliodon</i><br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, IV are correct, the incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Euspongia, Sycon, Spongilla</i>-Porifera, Scoliodon Chondrichthyes, Physalia- coelentarata, <i>Ascaris</i>-aschelminthes, <i>Neries</i>- annelida, <i>Fasciola</i> -platyhelminthes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102782,'biology',83,504,1022,'Identify the incorrectly matched option:<br>(I) <i>Torpedo</i> - Electric ray<br>(II) <i>Trygon</i> -Angel ray<br>(III) Toad - Two chambered heart<br>(IV) Fish - Warm blooded animals<br>(V) Frog - Three chambered heart<br>(VI) <i>Hyla</i> - Limbless amphibian<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II , V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, VI are incorrect, The incorrect statement can be corrected as Toad - 3 - chambered heart , Fish - Cold blooded animals, <i>Hyla</i> - is tree frog and has limbs. Trygon - Sting ray.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102783,'biology',83,505,1023,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Special mode of feeding by radula is found in sea hare.<br>(II) Dogfish is a true fish.<br>(III) The body of <i>Balanoglossus</i> is divided into proboscis, collar, and trunk.<br>(IV) All animals of Cnidaria and Echinodermata are exclusively marine.<br>(V) Well-developed respiratory system is found in Aves.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as all animals of Ctenophora & Echinodermata are exclusively marine.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102785,'biology',83,500,1016,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Osteichthyes - <i>Scoliodon</i><br>(II) <i>Chelone</i> - Aquatic reptile<br>(III) <i>Bufo</i> - Amphibian<br>(IV) <i>Nereis</i> - An aquatic form, dioecious<br>(V) Tapeworm - Dorsoventrally flat.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Scoliodon chondrichthyes</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102786,'biology',83,502,1020,'Which of the following statements/options are correct?<br>(I) <i>Planaria</i> - Low regeneration capacity<br>(II) <i>Ascaris</i> - Triploblastic, acoelomate<br>(III) <i>Pristis</i> - Cartilaginous fish<br>(IV) <i>Spongilla</i> - Fresh water sponge<br>(V) Mosquito - Indirect development<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as <i>Planaria</i> - high regeneration capacity, <i>Ascaris</i> - Triploblastic, pseudocoelomate.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102787,'biology',83,494,1010,'Which of the following features are not exhibited by members of Aschelminthes?<br>(I) Commonly known as "flatworms"<br>(II) Animals are bilaterally symmetrical and triploblastic.<br>(III) Exclusively parasites on animals.<br>(IV) Pseudocoelomate animals having organ system level of body organization.<br>(V) Body shows segmentation.<br>(VI) Alimentary canal is complete with a well developed muscular pharynx.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, V are not exhibited by members of Aschelminthes, they are roundworms, they can be free living and body does not show segmentation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102789,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) In vertebrates, the notochord is completely replaced by the vertebral column.<br>(II) Operculum and air bladder are absent in Clarias (catfish).<br>(III) Butterfly and silverfish have an open circulatory system.<br>(IV) Amphibia - A tympanum represents the ear.<br>(V) Aves - Digestive tract has additional chambers, the crop and gizzard.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'III, IV, V are correct, The incorrect statement can be corrected as in vertebrates the notochord is partially or fully replaced by vertebral column. Operculum and Air bladder present in <i>Clarias</i> (cat fish).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102790,'biology',83,491,1007,'Fill in the blanks with appropriate options:<br>I. ____ A ____ - cells are also called as nematocytes.<br>II. ____ B ____ is seen in Cnidaria.<br>III. <i>Physalia</i> is also known as ____ C ____<br>IV. ____ D ____ is found in <i>Aurelia</i>.<br>Options:','[{"text": "A - Cnidoblasts, B - Cellular level of organisation, C - Sea fan, D - Bilateral symmetry.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Nematocytes, B - Tissue level, C - Brain-coral, D - Radial symmetry.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Stinging, B - Cellular level of organisation, C-Sea cucumber, D-Bilateral symmetry.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Cnidocytes, B - Tissue level of organisation, C - Portuguese man of war, D - Radial symmetry.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct options are<br>(I) Cnidocytes - cells are also called as nematocytes.<br>(II) Tissue level of organisation is seen in Cnidaria.<br>(III) <i>Physalia</i> is also known as<br>Portuguese man of war.<br>(IV) Radial symmetry is found in <i>Aurelia</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102795,'biology',83,505,1023,'Which of the following is a correct match of the animal with it\'s common name?<br>(I) <i>Exocoetus</i> - Flying frog<br>(II) <i>Hemidactylus</i> - Wall lizard<br>(III) <i>Clarias</i> - Rohu<br>(IV) <i>Betta</i> - Fighting fish<br>(V) Angel ray - <i>Pterophyllum</i><br>(VI) Krait - Bangarus<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV ,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V ,VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, IV, VI, are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as <i>Exocoetus</i> - Flying fish, Angel fish - <i>Pterophyllum, Labeo</i> - Rohu.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102797,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which of the following statements/options are correct?<br>(I) Metagenesis - <i>Obelia</i><br>(II) Radula - <i>Pila</i><br>(III) Open circulatory system - <i>Aedes, Aplysia</i><br>(IV) Notochord - <i>Balanoglossus, Saccoglossus</i>.<br>(V) True coelom - <i>Ornithorhynchus, Neophron</i>.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as Stomochord <i>Balanoglossus, Saccoglossus</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102798,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following group of animals is correctly matched with their characteristic<br>feature ?<br>(I) <i>Amphioxus, Pristis, Bufo, Corvus</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) Chordates.<br>(II) <i>Labeo, Rana, Testudo, Pavo</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) Poikilotherms.<br>(III) <i>Nereis, Apis, Laccifer, Pila</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) Coelomate.<br>(IV) <i>Naja, Vipera, Alligator</i> \\(\\rightarrow\\) Poisonous<br>(V) <i>Hydra, Echinus</i> (adult) \\(\\rightarrow\\) Radially symmetrical.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as <i>Pavo</i> $\\rightarrow$ Homeotherms, <i>Alligator</i> $\\rightarrow$ non poisonous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102799,'biology',83,497,1013,'Which of the following statements/options are incorrect?<br>(I) Muscular pharynx - <i>Ascaris</i><br>(II) Prawn - Economical insect<br>(III) Shell - <i>Octopus</i><br>(IV) <i>Laccifer</i> - <i>Locust</i><br>(V) <i>Bombyx</i> - <i>Limulus</i>','[{"text": "I, II, III,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV, V are incorrect. The incorrect ones can be corrected as Prawn-Economical crustacea, Shell absent-<i>Octopus, Laccifer-lac insect, Bombyx-silkworm</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102800,'biology',83,499,1015,'Which of the following options are correct?<br>(I) Hemichordates - <i>Saccoglossus</i><br>(II) Echinoderms - <i>Ophiura</i><br>(III) Ctenophora - <i>Ascidia</i><br>(IV) Mollusca - <i>Chaetopleura</i><br>(V) Aschelminthes - <i>Ancylostoma</i>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as Urochordata - <i>Ascidia</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102801,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Amphibian body is divided into head and trunk. The skin is moist without scales. The heart is three-chambered.<br>(II) <i>Aptenodytes</i> and <i>Struthio</i> are flightless birds.<br>(III) Pelvic claspers are found in female members of Chondrichthyes.<br>(IV) Animals in which the body cavity is not lined by mesoderm, but instead, the mesoderm is present as scattered pouches between the ectoderm and endoderm. Such a body cavity is called an enterocoel.<br>(V) <i>Echinus</i> - Excretory system is absent.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, III, IV ,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as pelvic claspers are found in male members of Chondrichthyes .Animals in which body cavity is not lined by mesoderm, instead, the mesoderm is present as scattered pouches in between the ectoderm and endoderm. Such type of body cavity is called as pseudocoel.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102802,'biology',83,498,1014,'Which of the following matchings are correct?<br>(I) <i>Limulus</i> - King Crab<br>(II) <i>Locusta</i> - Gregarious pest<br>(III) <i>Taenia solium</i> - Muscular pharynx<br>(IV) Frog - Indirect development<br>(V) <i>Echinus</i> - Echinodermata<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as Frog - indirect development, aschelminthes - Muscular pharynx, <i>Taenia solium</i> is aplatyhelminthes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102803,'biology',83,491,1007,'Consider the following statements for coelenterates and identify the correct option.<br>(I) Medusa is present in <i>Hydra</i>.<br>(II) Polyp produces medusa asexually.<br>(III) Medusa produces polyp sexually.<br>(IV) Polyps are free-swimming and cylindrical in shape.<br>(V) Medusa are umbrella-shaped and sessile.<br>(VI) Medusa are free-swimming.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, VI are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as <i>Hydra</i> is free swimming. Medusa are umbrella shaped and free swimming. Polyp are sessile.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102804,'biology',83,500,1016,'Which of the following characteristics are related to chordates?<br>(I) Ventral nerve cord<br>(II) Ventral heart<br>(III) Dorsal notochord<br>(IV) Post-anal tail<br>(V) Pharynx perforated by gill slits.<br>Options:','[{"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as dorsal nerve cord.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102805,'biology',83,496,1012,'Which of the following statements are correct for the Arthropoda phylum?<br>(I) Sensory organs like antennae, eyes (compound and simple), statocysts, or balancing organs are present.<br>(II) Chitinous exoskeleton.<br>(III) Solid double ventral nerve cord.<br>(IV) Radial symmetry.<br>(V) Closed circulatory system.<br>(VI) Second largest phylum.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as arthropods are bilaterally symmetrical, open circulation, largest phylum.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102806,'biology',83,497,1013,'Select the correct statements for Mollusca:<br>(I) Apple snail, pearl oyster, cuttlefish, squid are related to Mollusca.<br>(II) The space between the shell and mantle is called the mantle cavity.<br>(III) They are segmented because they are bilaterally symmetrical.<br>(IV) Feather-like gills have only a respiratory function.<br>(V) The anterior head region has sensory tentacles.<br>(VI) Devil fish, sea hare, tusk shell, and chiton are related to Mollusca.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V, VI<br>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, V, VI are correct, In mollusca, the space between the hump and the mantle is called the mantle cavity They are unsegmented and the feather like gills have respiratory and excretory functions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102807,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Platyhelminthes - Dorso-laterally flattened body - Flatworms.<br>(II) <i>Pinctada, Planaria</i>, Pila has a closed circulatory system.<br>(III) Aquatic arthropods, Mollusca, Fishes, Tadpoles respire through gills.<br>(IV) <i>Pheretima, Rana</i> has a closed circulatory system.<br>(V) Aschelminthes - Circular in transverse cross-section - Roundworms<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV,V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as <i>Planaria</i> are not able to circulate since they lack a circulatory system. Class sepia includes squid, octopus, and cuttlefish. These creatures are molluscs, but they have a closed circulatory system. <i>Pila, Pinctada</i> have open circulatory system.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102811,'biology',83,497,1013,'What is not common among annelids, arthropods, and molluscs?<br>(I) They all are diploblastic.<br>(II) They all have an open circulatory system.<br>(III) All of them have an organ system grade of body organization.<br>(IV) They all are radially symmetrical.<br>(V) They all are triploblastic.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, IV are not common among annelids, arthropods and molluscs. They have bilateral symmetry, annelids have closed circulation, they all are triploblastic.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102812,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Ctenophora - Comb jellies.<br>(II) <i>Salamandra</i> - A tympanum represents the ear; fertilization is external.<br>(III) Porifera - Has minute pores in the body wall.<br>(IV) <i>Pteropus</i> - Skin possesses hair; oviparous; Mammalia.<br>(V) <i>Ascaris</i> - Body segmented; males and females distinct.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are correct, The incorrect ones can be corrected as <i>Pteropus</i> - Skin prossesses hair, viviparous Mammalia.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102813,'biology',83,505,1023,'In the given list, which of the following animals have vertebral column, cranium, jaw<br>(I) Sea horse, <i>Herdmania</i>, Snake, <i>Torpedo</i><br>(II) Earthworm, Frog, Snake, <i>Torpedo</i> Hag fish.<br>(III) <i>Amphioxus, Petromyzon</i>, Snake, <i>Torpedo</i><br>(IV) Sea horse, Frog, Snake, <i>Torpedo</i><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IV is correct. Animals have vertebral column, cranium, jaw - Sea horse, Frog, Snake, <i>Torpedo</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102815,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Metamerism - True segmentation<br>(II) <i>Aurelia</i> - Cnidoblasts, Organ level of organization.<br>(III) <i>Osteichthyes</i> -Terminal mouth.<br>(IV) <i>Neophron</i> -Vulture<br>(V) <i>Apis</i> - Honey bee<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II,V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as <i>Aurelia</i> - Cnidoblasts, tissue level of organization.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102816,'biology',83,500,1017,'Which of the following statements is/are totally wrong about the occurrence of notochord while the other are correct?<br>(I) It is present throughout life in <i>Amphioxus</i>.<br>(II) It is present only in larval tail in <i>Ascidians</i><br>(III) It is replaced by a vertebral column in adult frog.<br>(IV) It is absent throughout life in humans from the very beginning.<br>(V) It is mesodermal in origin.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IV is wrong. Notochord is present in embryonic stage in humans and replaced by a vertebral column in adult.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102817,'biology',83,507,1025,'Which one of the following groups of animals is correctly matched with its characteristic feature without even a single exception?<br>(I) Porifera - Presence of osculum and ostia. Skeleton is made up of spicules or spongin fibres.<br>(II) Reptilia - Possess a 3-chambered heart with one incompletely divided ventricle.<br>(III) Chordata - Possess a mouth provided with an upper and a lower jaw.<br>(IV) Chondrichthyes - Possess cartilaginous endoskeleton.<br>(V) Mammalia - Give birth to young ones.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, IV are correct. Crocodile, a reptile has 4 chambered heart. Cyclostomata -a chordate has no jaw, Platypus - a mammal lays eggs.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102818,'biology',83,503,1021,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Notochord - Chordates, Mesodermal in origin.<br>(II) <i>Laccifer</i> - Lac insect.<br>(III) Osteichthyes -Marine, Fresh water.<br>(IV) Ctenophora - Eight internal row of ciliated comb plates on body.<br>(V) Triploblastic - Three germ layers<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Ctenophora Eight external row of ciliated comb plates on body.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102819,'biology',83,506,1024,'Which of the following are correct?<br>(I) <i>Hippocampus</i> - Sea horse<br>(II) <i>Struthio</i> - Penguin<br>(III) <i>Corvus</i> - Crow<br>(IV) <i>Psittacula</i> - Parrot<br>(V) <i>Columba</i> - Pigeon<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as <i>Struthio</i> Ostrich.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102820,'biology',83,497,1013,'Find out the correct match from the following:<br>(I) <i>Ancylostoma</i> - Hookworm Aschelminthes.<br>(II) <i>Sepia</i> - Cuttlefish - Mollusca.<br>(III) <i>Chaetopleura</i> - Chiton - Mollusca.<br>(IV) <i>Antedon</i> - Sea lily - Echinodermata.<br>(V) <i>Wuchereria</i> - Filarial worm - Annelida.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as <i>Wuchereria</i> Filarial worm - Aschelminthes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102821,'biology',83,504,1022,'Which of the following options gives the correct categorisation of the animals according to the type of respiratory organs?<br>(I) Adult frog - Tracheal system<br>(II) <i>Apis</i> - gills<br>(III) <i>Pila</i> - Gills<br>(IV) Cutaneous - <i>Hirudinaria</i><br>(V) Tracheal system - <i>Aedes</i><br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Adult frog cutaneous, brachial and pulmonary respiration. <i>Apis</i> - tracheal system.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102823,'biology',83,498,1014,'Find out the correct match from the following:<br>(I) Radula - Rasping organ - <i>Pila</i>.<br>(II) Hooks and suckers - <i>Taenia</i> - Annelida.<br>(III) Tube feet - <i>Asterias</i>, <i>Dentalium</i>- Echinodermata.<br>(IV) Comb plates - <i>Pleurobrachia, Aurelia</i>- Ctenophora.<br>Options:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I is correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as Hooks and suckers - <i>Taenia</i> - platyhelminthes, Tube feet - <i>Asterias</i>, Echinodermata, <i>Dentalium</i> is mollusca, Comb plates - <i>Pleurobrachia</i>, - Ctenophora, <i>Aurelia</i> is cnidaria.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102824,'biology',83,500,1018,'Select the correct option to identify A, B, C in the given chart: <img src=\'/img/data/biology/83_102824_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />','[{"text": "A - Pisces, B -Tetrapoda, C - Ostracodermi", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Cyclostomata, B - Pisces, C -Tetrapoda", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Tetrapoda, B -Pisces, C - Cyclostomata.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Cyclostomata, B - Ostracodermi C -Tetrapoda.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Cyclostomata, B - Pisces, C -Tetrapoda is the correct option.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102825,'biology',83,507,1025,'Find out the correct option from the following:<br>(I) Chordata is a phylum.<br>(II) Agnatha is a division.<br>(III) <i>Betta</i> - Fighting fish<br>(IV) <i>Marcopus</i> - Mammary glands Mammalia.<br>(IV) <i>Anopheles</i> - Malpighian tubules Arthropoda.<br>(V) Prawn - Crustacean -Arthropoda<br>(VI) <i>Adamsia</i> - Polyp and medusa stage in its lifecycle - Coelenterata<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as <i>Adamsia</i> Polyp only.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102826,'biology',8,154,328,'When pollen grains of a flower of a plant pollinate the stigma of flower of another plant, it is called','[{"text": "Geitonogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xenogamy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Autogamy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Dichogamy", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Xenogamy: Pollination between flowers of two different plants of the same species. This leads to true genetic variation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102827,'biology',8,156,332,'Fusion of a male gamete with the central cell in the embryo sac of an angiosperm is called','[{"text": "Apomixis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Double fertilization", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Triple fusion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Syngamy", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Triple fusion: Fusion of the second male gamete with the diploid central cell (which contains two polar nuclei) $ \\to $ forms triploid primary endosperm nucleus (PEN).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102837,'biology',8,153,324,'What is correct about the generative cell?<br>(I) It floats in the cytoplasm of the vegetative cell.<br>(II) It is spindle-shaped.<br>(III) It has an abundant food reserve.<br>(IV) It has dense cytoplasm and a nucleus.','[{"text": "I, II and III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II and IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II and IV are correct. The generative cell is small and floats in the cytoplasm of the vegetative cell. It is spindle shaped with dense cytoplasm and a nucleus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102829,'biology',8,153,326,'How many meiotic and mitotic divisions need to occur for the development of a mature female gametophyte from the megaspore mother cell in an angiosperm plant?','[{"text": "No Meiosis and 2 Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2 Meiosis and 3 Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 Meiosis and 2 Mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 Meiosis and 3 Mitosis", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>In angiosperms, the megaspore mother cell undergoes 1 meiotic division to form 4 haploid megaspores, of which 1 survives. This functional megaspore then undergoes 3\nmitotic divisions to form the<br>8-nucleate embryo sac (female gametophyte).Total divisions: 1 meiosis + 3 mitosis',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102830,'biology',8,153,323,'Given below are two statements : One is labelled as Assertion (A) and other is labelled as Reason (R).<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Cells of the tapetum possess dense cytoplasm and generally have more than one nucleus<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> Presence of more than one nucleus in the tapetum increases the efficiency of nourishing the developing microspore mother cells.<br>In light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>Tapetal cells are nutritive cells of the anther and possess dense cytoplasm.They are often binucleate or multinucleate, which enhances their metabolic activity and supports the development of pollen grains.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102831,'biology',8,157,335,'Match Column I with Column II <img src=\'/img/data/biology/8_102831_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Choose the option with all correct matches<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-Q, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>A. Scutellum Q – Cotyledon of monocot seed Scutellum is the single cotyledon in monocots (e.g., maize).<br>B. Non-albuminous seed R – Groundnut<br>Groundnut stores food in cotyledons, hence non albuminous.<br>C. Epiblast S – Rudimentary cotyledon Epiblast is a small rudimentary structure in monocots.<br>D. Perisperm P – Persistent nucellus Perisperm is the remnant of nucellus, seen in black pepper. Correct matches: A–Q, B–R, C–S, D–P.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102832,'biology',8,153,326,'Given below are two statements : One is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> A typical unfertilised, angiosperm embryo sac at maturity is 8 nucleate and 7-celled.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The egg apparatus has 2 polar nuclei.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :','[{"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>Assertion (A): True – A mature angiosperm embryo sac is 8-nucleate and 7-celled (3 cells in egg apparatus, 2 synergids, 1 egg cell, 2 polar nuclei in central cell, 3 antipodals).<br>Reason (R): False – The egg apparatus has 1 egg cell and 2 synergids, not polar nuclei. The 2 polar nuclei lie in the central cell, not in the egg apparatus.',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102833,'biology',8,154,328,'Given below are two statements: One is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).<br><br><strong>Assertion:</strong> Both wind and water pollinated flowers are not very colourful and do not produce nectar.<br><br><strong>Reason:</strong> The flowers produce enormous amount of pollen grains in wind and water pollinated flowers.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "Assertion is false but Reason is true", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true and Reason is the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Assertion and Reason are true but Reason is not the correct explanation of Assertion", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Assertion is true but Reason is false", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>Assertion (A): True – Wind and water pollinated flowers are not colourful and do not produce nectar, as they do not rely on insects or animals for pollination. <br>Reason (R): True – Such flowers produce large quantities of pollen grains to compensate for the loss during passive transfer via wind or water. Reason is not the direct explanation for lack of colour/nectar - it\'s a separate adaptation. Both statements are true, but Reason is not the correct explanation',NULL,'Medium','Assertion and Reason',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102834,'biology',8,157,334,'In the seeds of cereals, the outer covering of endosperm separates the embryo by a proteinrich layer called:','[{"text": "Aleurone layer", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Coleoptile", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Coleorhiza", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Integument", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct answer is option 1.<br>In monocot cereal seeds (e.g., maize), the endosperm is separated from the embryo by a protein-rich layer known as the aleurone layer. It plays a role in enzyme secretion during\ngermination.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102835,'biology',8,153,324,'Pick the correct option regarding the substance that degrades sporopollenin:','[{"text": "Environmental factors", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cellulase enzyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Strong acid", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sporopollenin cannot be degraded", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Sporopollenin can not be degraded.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102836,'biology',8,153,324,'Identify the correct statements about asymmetric mitosis in plants:<br>(I) It occurs in one-celled pollen grains.<br>(II) It occurs in two-celled pollen grains.<br>(III) It results in the formation of two-celled pollen grains.<br>(IV) It results in the formation of three-celled pollen grains.<br>(V) It results in the formation of vegetative and generative cells.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, V are correct. Asymmetric mitosis in plants occurs in 1 - celled pollen grain, results in formation of 2 - celled pollen grain vegetative and generative cell.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102838,'biology',8,153,324,'How many male gametes are produced in a pea flower which have 50 microspore mother cell in one microsporangia?','[{"text": "1600", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "16000", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "8000", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pea is diadelphous and has 10 anthers.<br>1 anther has 4 microsporangia. therefore $10 \\times 4=40$ microsporangia.<br>1 PMC produces 4 microspores/pollen grain $50 \\mathrm{~PMC}=200$ pollen grain;<br>One pollen grain has 2 male gametes. $40 \\times 200 \\times 2=16,000$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102839,'biology',8,153,326,'What would be the number of chromosomes in the cells of the aleurone layer in a plant species with 9 chromosomes in its antipodals?','[{"text": "9", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "18", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "27", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "0", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Aleurone layer is the covering of the endosperm and its ploidy is 3 n , therefore the answer will be $3 \\times 9=27$.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102840,'biology',8,153,324,'Select the incorrect pair:','[{"text": "Pollen allergy - <i>Parthenium</i> or carrot grass", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen banks - preservation of pollen at $-196^{\\\\circ} \\\\mathrm{C}$ in liquid nitrogen", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen germination - antipodals", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pollen grain (2-celled) - vegetative cell and generative cell", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Pollen germination - Antipodals is incorrect. Pollen germination - synergids is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102841,'biology',8,153,323,'How many pollen mother cells are required for the following?<br>(I) Formation of 8 gametes<br>(II) Formation of 8 pollen grains<br>(III) Formation of 8 microspores','[{"text": "$1,1,1$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$1,2,2$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2,1,2$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2,2,2$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'1 Pollen mother cells produce 4 microspores, which eventually becomes pollen grains each and each pollen grain will have 2 male gametes. Therefore 2 Pollen mother cells produce 8 microspores, which eventually becomes 8 pollen grains.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102842,'biology',8,153,324,'How many cells and male gametes are present in the mature male gametophyte of angiosperms, respectively?','[{"text": "2 & 2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 & 2", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "7 & 8", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3 & 3", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'3 cell- 2 male gametes and vegetative cell are present in the mature male gametophye.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102843,'biology',8,153,324,'Which of the following statements is true for pollen grains?<br>(I) Pollen can be preserved at $-196^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ in liquid nitrogen.<br>(II) In some cereals, such as rice and wheat, pollen grains lose viability within 30 seconds.<br>(III) Pollen from some plants may cause asthma and bronchitis.<br>(IV) In some members of Rosaceae, Leguminosae, and Solanaceae, pollen grains can maintain viability for months.','[{"text": "I, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III and IV only. In some cereals such as rice and wheat, pollen grains lose viability within 30 minutes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102844,'biology',8,153,323,'Tapetum is:','[{"text": "The outer nutritive layer that persists at maturity of the anther.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The inner nutritive layer that persists at maturity of the anther.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The inner nutritive layer that degenerates at maturity of the anther.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The outer nutritive layer that degenerates at maturity of the anther", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Tapetum is inner nutritive layer that degenerates at maturity of anther',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102845,'biology',8,153,323,'Select the correct statement with respect to the anther:<br>(I) Anther lobes are attached to each other by a band of vascularized sterile tissue.<br>(II) The innermost wall layer is the middle layer.<br>(III) Microsporangia, upon maturity, get filled with pollen grains.<br>(IV) A homogeneous mass of meristematic cells in the microsporangium forms microspore mother cells.<br>(V) Cells of the tapetum nourish the developing pollen grains.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, V are correct. II statement can be corrected as the innermost wall layer is the tapetum.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102846,'biology',8,153,323,'Which of the following statements are correct regarding stamen?<br>(I) Stamen is a unit of Androecium.<br>(II) Stamen is also known as microsporophyll.<br>(III) Stamen is differentiated into filament and anther.<br>(IV) Stamen are the male sex organ of the flower.','[{"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III and IV are correct stamen is a unit of Androecium. Stamen is also known as microsporophyll. Stamen is differentiated into filament and anther. Stamen are the male sex organ of the flower.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102847,'biology',8,153,324,'Which of the following options is correct?<br>(I) <i>Parthenium</i>, or carrot grass, which came into India as a contaminant with imported wheat, causes pollen allergy.<br>(II) In about $40 \\%$ of angiosperms, pollination occurs at the 2-celled stage.<br>(III) Generative cells divide meiotically to form two male gametes.<br>(IV) In about $60 \\%$ of angiosperms, pollination occurs when a pollen grain forms at least a vegetative and generative cell.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I and IV are correct <i>Parthenium</i> or carrot grass that came into India as a contaminant with imported wheat, causes pollen allergy In about 60% of angiosperm, pollination occur when a pollen grain at least form a vegetation and generative cell.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102848,'biology',8,153,323,'Which of the following statements is/are correct for the middle layer of the anther wall?<br>(I) It degenerates at maturity.<br>(II) It is polyploid.<br>(III) It nourishes developing pollen grains.<br>(IV) It helps in the dehiscence of pollen grains due to its hygroscopic nature.','[{"text": "I, IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All except II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, IV only are correct. The outer three wall layers perform the function of protection and help in dehiscence of anther to release the pollen. Tapetum nourishes the developing pollen grains and is polyploid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102849,'biology',8,153,324,'Cryopreservation is:<br>(I) The storage of pollen grains of only exotic species.<br>(II) The fossilization of pollen grains.<br>(III) The storage of pollen grains in liquid nitrogen ( $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ ) for various artificial plant breeding programs.','[{"text": "II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Only (III) is correct. Cryopreservation is storage of pollen grains in liquid $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ for various artificial plant breeding.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102850,'biology',8,153,326,'Select the correct statement(s) regarding the structure of a mature embryo sac:<br>(I) The egg apparatus is situated towards the chalazal end.<br>(II) Antipodal cells are situated towards the micropylar end.<br>(III) A typical angiospermous embryo sac is an 8-celled, 7-nucleate structure.<br>(IV) A typical angiospermous embryo sac is a 7-celled, 8-nucleate structure.','[{"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A typical angiospermous embryo sac is 7 - celled, 8 - nucleate structure is the correct statement. The egg apparatus is located towards the micropylar end.<br>Antipodal cells are situated at the chalazal end.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102851,'biology',8,153,326,'Select the correct statement(s) regarding the structure of an embryo sac:<br>(I) The egg apparatus consists of two synergids and two egg cell.<br>(II) The large central cell has three polar nuclei.<br>(III) The synergids have special cellular thickenings at the chalazal tip called the filiform apparatus.<br>(IV) Polar nuclei are situated below the egg apparatus in the large central cell.','[{"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The egg apparatus, consists of two synergids and one egg cell. The synergids have special cellular thickenings at the micropylar tip called filiform apparatus, which play an important role in guiding the pollen tubes into the synergid. The large central cell, has two polar nuclei.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102852,'biology',8,153,324,'Which of the following statements about sporopollenin is incorrect?<br>(I) Exine is made up mainly of sporopollenin.<br>(II) Sporopollenin is one of the most resistant organic materials.<br>(III) Sporopollenin can withstand high temperatures and strong acids.<br>(IV) Exine has an aperture called the micropyle where sporopollenin is absent.','[{"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only IV is incorrect. Exine has aperture called germpore where sporopollenin is absent',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102853,'biology',8,153,324,'Select the correct statement with respect to pollen grains:','[{"text": "Exine is rich in pectocellulose.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The viability of pollen grains of wheat and rice is for many years.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The generative cell floats in the cytoplasm of the vegetative cell.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The tapetum is present in the pollen grains of entomophilous plants.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Generative cell floats in the cytoplasm of vegetative cell. This is the correct statement.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102854,'biology',8,155,330,'In an angiospermic ovule, the central cell of the embryo sac, prior to the entry of the pollen tube, contains:','[{"text": "A single haploid nucleus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two haploid polar nuclei.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "One diploid and one haploid nucleus.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "One diploid secondary nucleus.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'In an angiospermic ovule, central cell of the embryo sac, prior to the entry of pollen tube, contains two haploid polar nuclei.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102855,'biology',8,153,325,'An ovary may have a single ovule, as in A, or many ovules, as in B Identify A and B.','[{"text": "A - Rice, B - Wheat", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Rice, B - Mango", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Wheat, B - Orchid", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Orchid, B - Papaya", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'An ovary may have a single ovule as in wheat or many ovules as in Orchid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102857,'biology',8,153,325,'Which of the following plants have many ovules in their ovaries?','[{"text": "Mango, watermelons", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Papaya, watermelons", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Wheat, papaya", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Wheat, papaya, watermelons", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The number of ovules in an ovary may be one (wheat, paddy, mango) to many (papaya, water melon, orchids).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102858,'biology',8,153,325,'Which of the following statements is/are correct about ovules in an ovary?<br>(I) The number of ovules in an ovary may be one to many.<br>(II) The number of ovules in an ovary may be one (e.g. orchids, paddy, mango).<br>(III) The number of ovules in an ovary may be many (e.g. papaya, watermelon, wheat).','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only I is correct. The number of ovules in an ovary may be one (wheat, paddy, mango) to many (papaya, water melon, orchids).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102859,'biology',8,153,326,'The ploidy level of the nucellus, integument, and antipodal cells of a plant, respectively, is:','[{"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ploidy level of nucellus -2n, integument -2n and antipodal cell -n of plant.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102861,'biology',8,153,325,'Which of the following statements is true for the nucellus?<br>(I) It provides nutrition to the developing embryo sac.<br>(II) It is present inside the embryo sac.<br>(III) It is diploid tissue.<br>(IV) It is enclosed within the integuments.<br>(V) Ovules generally differentiate a single megaspore mother cell (MMC) in the micropylar region of the nucellus.<br>(VI) The embryo sac is present inside it.','[{"text": "I, II are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V, VI are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV, V, VI are correct. Enclosed within the integuments is a mass of cells called the nucellus. Cells of the nucellus have abundant reserve food materials. Located in the nucellus is the embryo sac or female gametophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102862,'biology',8,153,326,'Which of the following statements is true regarding polar nuclei?<br>(I) Polar nuclei are haploid.<br>(II) They fuse to form the secondary nucleus just after fertilization.<br>(III) Polar nuclei are situated below the egg apparatus.<br>(IV) They are present in the large central cell.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, IV are correct The polar nuclei on fertilisation becomes the primary endosperm nucleus.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102863,'biology',8,153,326,'What will happen in the functional megaspore of an angiosperm?','[{"text": "The embryo sac is formed by mitosis, then meiosis.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The embryo sac is formed by three mitotic nuclear divisions, with cell walls laid down later.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "The embryo sac is formed by three mitotic nuclear divisions, with nuclear divisions followed immediately by cell wall formation.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "The embryo sac is formed by two mitotic nuclear divisions, with cell walls laid down later.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The mitotic divisions in angiosperms are strictly free nuclear, that is, nuclear divisions are not followed immediately by cell wall formation. After the 8 - nucleate stage, cell walls are laid down leading to the organisation of the typical female gametophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102864,'biology',8,154,328,'Read the following four statements (I - IV) and identify the incorrect ones.<br>(I) The tallest flower is <i>Amorphophallus</i>, reaching about 6 feet in height.<br>(II) A relationship exists between a species of moth and the plant <i>Yucca</i>, where both species the moth and the plant cannot complete their life cycles without each other.<br>(III) Wind-pollinated flowers have feathery stigmas.<br>(IV) Wind-pollinated flowers generally have sticky pollen grains.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'IV is incorrect, Sticky pollen grains are seen in animal pollinated flowers',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102865,'biology',8,154,328,'Which of the following statements is not true for insect pollination?<br>(I) Insect pollination occurs mainly through honey bees.<br>(II) Flowers are attractive and colorful.<br>(III) There is a large quantity of nectar production.<br>(IV) Pollen grains are sticky due to sporopollenin.<br>(V) Cleistogamous flowers.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'IV and V are not true for insect pollination. Pollens are sticky due to pollen kit. Cleistogamous flowers produce assured seed set even in the absence of pollinators.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102866,'biology',8,154,328,'Select the mismatched pair:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Monosporic embryo sac - <i>Polygonum</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pollen allergy - Carrot grass.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chasmogamous flowers - Exposed anthers and stigma.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Xenogamy - Self pollination.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Xenogamy - Self pollination is incorrect, it is cross pollination.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102867,'biology',8,154,328,'Choose the incorrectly matched pair:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Syncarpous pistil - <i>Papaver</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apocarpous pistil - <i>Michelia</i>.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Anemophily - Corn.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cleistogamous flower - <i>Mirabilis jalapa</i>.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cleistogamous flowers are seen in plants such as <i>Viola</i> (common pansy), <i>Oxalis</i>, and <i>Commelina</i>.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102868,'biology',8,154,327,'Read the following statements and identify the correct option:<br>(I) Two individuals are never required for sexual reproduction.<br>(II) Cleistogamous flowers are invariably autogamous, as there is no chance of crosspollen landing on the stigma.','[{"text": "Statement I and II both are false", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I is true and Statement II is false.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement I and II both are true.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement I is false and Statement II is true.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I & II both are true',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
INSERT INTO `qb_questions` (`id`, `subject_id`, `chapter_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_html`, `options`, `correct_index`, `explanation`, `explanation_image_url`, `difficulty`, `qtype`, `year`, `tag`, `created_at`, `question_image_url`) VALUES
(102869,'biology',8,154,328,'Which of the following is not a characteristic feature of water-pollinated flowers?<br>(I) Mucilaginous covering on pollen grains.<br>(II) Long, sticky, unwettable stigma.<br>(III) Large, often feathery stigma to easily trap airborne pollen grains.<br>(IV) Light and unwettable pollen grains.<br>(V) Presence of nectaries and fragrance.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III and V are not a characteristic feature of water-pollinated flowers, presence of nectaries and fragrance is seen in insect pollinated flowers and large often - feathery stigma to easily trap air-borne pollen grains is seen in wind pollinated flowers.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102870,'biology',8,154,328,'Identify the correct features of anemophilous flowers:<br>(I) Large, colored flowers.<br>(II) Formation of nectar.<br>(III) Light and non-sticky pollen grains.<br>(IV) Single ovule in each ovary.<br>(V) Well-exposed stamens.<br>(VI) Numerous flowers packed into an inflorescence.<br>(VII) Large, often feathery stigma.','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V, VI, VII", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V, VII", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV, V, VI and VII, pollen grains are light and non - sticky so that they can be transported in wind currents. They often possess well - exposed stamens and large often - feathery stigma to easily trap air - borne pollen grains. Wind pollinated flowers often have a single ovule in each ovary and numerous flowers packed into an inflorescence.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102871,'biology',8,154,329,'A plant with bisexual flowers can exhibit:','[{"text": "Autogamy only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autogamy and geitonogamy only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Geitonogamy and xenogamy only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autogamy, geitonogamy, and xenogamy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Plant with bisexual flower can show : Autogamy, geitonogamy and xenogamy.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102885,'biology',8,157,334,'Which of the following plant structures in the list below are haploid in nature?','[{"text": "Antipodals, pollen grain, microspore, megaspore.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucellus, tapetum.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ovule, synergids, endosperm.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo, embryo sac.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Antipodals, pollen grain, synergids, microspore, megaspore, embryo sac are haploid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102872,'biology',8,154,327,'Which of the following statements is true?<br>(I) Pollen grains are rich in nutrients.<br>(II) Tapetum cells become polyploid due to free nuclear division.<br>(III) Pollen of some plants may cause asthma and bronchitis.<br>(IV) Cleistogamous flowers invariably show self-pollination.<br>(V) The hard inner layer called the exine is made up of sporopollenin.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III and IV are correct. The hard outer layer called the exine is made up of sporopollenin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102873,'biology',8,154,328,'Animal visitors are required for pollination in:<br>(I) <i>Oxalis</i><br>(II) Fig<br>(III) Cucumber<br>(IV) <i>Commelina</i><br>(V) Grass<br>(VI) Water lily<br>(VII) <i>Amorphophallus</i>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, VI, VII", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V, VII", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, VI, VII", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, VI, VII is correct. <i>Oxalis</i> and <i>Commelina</i> has cleistogamous flowers, therefore pollinator is not required, Grass is wind pollinated.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102874,'biology',8,154,328,'Read the following five statements $(\\mathrm{I}-\\mathrm{V})$ :<br>(I) Wind pollination is rare in grasses.<br>(II) Cleistogamous flowers produce assured seed set even in the absence of pollinators.<br>(III) Water-pollinated plants <i>Vallisneria</i> and <i>Hydrilla</i> grow in fresh water.<br>(IV) The majority of flowering plants produce hermaphrodite flowers.<br>(V) In seagrasses, the female flower reaches the surface of the water by a long stalk, and the male flowers or pollen grains are released on the surface of the water.Which of the above statements are incorrect:','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I and V are wrong. In water pollinated plants such as seagrasses, female flowers remain submerged in water and the pollen grains are released inside the water. Wind pollination is quite common in grasses. Cleistogamous flowers produce assured seed - set even in the absence of pollinators.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102876,'biology',8,155,331,'Choose the correct option based on the following statements:<br>(I) Emasculation is done to make a plant into the male parent.<br>(II) Emasculation is done to prevent self pollination.<br>(III) Emasculation prevents undesirable cross pollination.<br>(IV) Emasculation is done to make a plant into the female parent.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(II) Emasculation is done to prevent self pollination, (IV) Emasculation is done to make a plant into female parent, both are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102877,'biology',8,153,326,'How many reduction divisions are required to produce 120 antipodal cells in a Polygonum-type embryo sac?','[{"text": "120", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "60", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "40", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Data is insufficient", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'40 Meiosis (reduction division) will result in 120 antipodal cells, as one embryo sac has 3 antipodals.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102878,'biology',8,154,329,'Select the mismatched pair:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Prevention of self-pollination - Unisexual flowers.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Papaya - Dioecy.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Genetic mechanism to prevent self-pollination-Self-incompatibility.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Continued cross-pollination - Inbreeding depression.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Continued cross pollination - Inbreeding depression is incorrect, it is corrected as continued self pollination - Inbreeding depression.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102879,'biology',8,156,332,'Which of the following events do not take place after the degeneration of the generative cell in the pollen grain?<br>(I) Entry of the pollen tube inside the embryo sac.<br>(II) Syngamy.<br>(III) Only triple fusion but not syngamy.<br>(IV) Neither entry of the pollen tube inside the embryo sac nor fertilization.<br>(V) Triple fusion.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, V only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'(II) Syngamy, (V) Triple fusion, both are a product of fertilisation, since generative cell is absent both these processes will not occur.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102880,'biology',8,156,332,'Identify how many nuclei participate in:<br>a. Syngamy<br>b. Triple fusion, respectively.','[{"text": "3,2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "3,3", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2,2", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "2, 3", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'One of the male gametes moves towards the egg cell and fuses with its nucleus.<br>Completing the syngamy, resulting in a diploid cell, the zygote. The other male gamete moves towards the two polar nuclei located in the central cell and fuses with them to produce a triploid primary endosperm nucleus (PEN) As this involves the fusion of three haploid nuclei it is termed triple fusion.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102882,'biology',8,157,333,'Which of the following is correctly matched :<br>\\[\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;{\\text{Cell/tissue}}\\;\\;\\] \\[{\\text{Ploidy}}\\;\\] \\[{\\text{Function}}\\;\\]<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Endosperm 3N Nutrition to developing embryo is the correct answer.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102883,'biology',8,157,333,'Which of the following in the list given below are haploid in nature in flowering plants?','[{"text": "Endosperm, Embryo.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Egg, Antipodals, Synergid, Pollen grain.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Nucellus, Integuments.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seed, Tapetum, Endothecium, Anther", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Egg, antipodals, synergids, pollen grains are haploid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102884,'biology',8,157,334,'Find out the ploidy level of the following structures, respectively:<br>Aleurone layer, Microspores, Placenta, Embryo sac, Embryo.','[{"text": "$2 \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}, 3 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$3 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}, \\\\mathrm{n}, 2 \\\\mathrm{n}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'3n, n, 2n, n, 2n, this is the correct ploidy for Aleurone layer, Microspores, Placenta, Embryo sac, Embryo respectively',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102887,'biology',8,153,324,'Read the following statements carefully and identify the correct statements:<br>(I) Annual plants are always monocarpic.<br>(II) All seeded plants are heterosporous.<br>(III) The sporophyte is completely independent in angiosperms.<br>(IV) The male gametophyte of angiosperms is the most reduced and has three cells at maturity.','[{"text": "I, II, and IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II and IV only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'All are correct. Annual plants are always monocarpic. All seeded plants are heterosporous. Sporophyte is completely independent in angiosperm. Male gametophyte of angiosperm is most reduced and have three cells at maturity.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102888,'biology',8,154,328,'Which of the following is true regarding a monoecious plant having unisexual flowers?','[{"text": "Autogamy and geitonogamy cannot occur, but xenogamy can occur.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autogamy and geitonogamy can occur, but xenogamy does not occur.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autogamy cannot occur, but geitonogamy and xenogamy can occur.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "None of the options are correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Autogamy can not occur but geitonogamy and xenogamy can occur in monoecious plant having unisexual flower',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102889,'biology',8,153,324,'How many meiotic and mitotic divisions are required to form a one mature male gametophyte from microspore?','[{"text": "0 meiosis, 1 mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "1 meiosis, 1 mitosis", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "0 meiosis, 2 mitosis", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1 meiosis, 2 mitosis", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'0 meiosis, 2 mitosis is the correct option, microspore is formed by meiosis and is haploid. It undergoes 2 mitosis to form 3 celled mature male gametophyte.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102890,'biology',8,153,326,'Which of the following is commonly observed in the female flower of <i>Cucurbita</i>?','[{"text": "Anther", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Embryo sac", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Pollen grain", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "None of the above", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Anther and pollen grain are not found in female flower of cucurbita.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102891,'biology',8,153,326,'Select the correct option given below:<br>(I) Megasporophyll - Carpel<br>(II) Microsporophyll - Embryo sac<br>(III) Female gametophyte - Embryo sac<br>(IV) Megasporangia - Ovule','[{"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II is incorrect, it can be corrected as Microsporophyll.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102892,'biology',8,157,334,'Select the odd one with respect to ploidy level in angiosperms:','[{"text": "Antipodal", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Male gamete", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Endosperm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Vegetative cell of pollen", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Endosperm is triploid whereas others are haploid.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102893,'biology',8,157,335,'How many chromosomes are present in the endosperm and perisperm if 26 chromosomes are present in the meiocyte of an angiosperm?','[{"text": "39 and 26, respectively", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "26 and 26, respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "39 and 13, respectively", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "26 and 39, respectively", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'39 & 26 respectively, endosperm is triploid and perisperm is diploid.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102894,'biology',8,157,333,'In which one of the following plants does the endosperm not get completely consumed by the developing embryo, and it may persist in the mature seed?<br>(I) Bean<br>(II) Castor<br>(III) Groundnut<br>(IV) Pea','[{"text": "I, II, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Castor is endospermic seed.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102895,'biology',8,158,336,'What is common between vegetative reproduction and apomixis?','[{"text": "Both do not show the flowering phase.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both are applicable only to dicot plants.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both produce progeny genetically identical to the parent.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both produce progeny genetically nonidentical but phenotypically identical to the parent.", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Both produces progeny genetically identical to the parent.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102896,'biology',8,157,335,'In which of the following situations would parthenocarpy not be advantageous for plants?','[{"text": "Epicarp is edible", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Seeds are edible", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Endocarp is edible", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Fruit is edible, but seeds are not edible", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Parthenocarpic fruits have no seeds, therefore they will not be advantageous in case, seeds are edible.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102897,'biology',8,157,335,'Choose the incorrect match:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "Mango - One ovule", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cashewnut - False fruit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Banana - Parthenocarpic fruit", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apple - True fruit", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Apple - True fruit is incorrect, apple is false fruit.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102898,'biology',8,157,335,'Identify the correct match:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "The wall of the ovary forms the seed coat True.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Apple fruits develop without the process of fertilization-True.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "False fruits do not have seeds - True.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A recent record of a 2,000-year-old viable seed is of the date palm, <i>Phoenix dactylifera</i> - True.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A recent record of 2000 years old viable seed is of the date palm, <i>Phoenix dactylifera</i> - true',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102899,'biology',8,157,335,'Which of the following options is correct?<br>(I) Achene is seen in strawberry.<br>(II) Reproductive processes such as pollination and fertilisation are independent of water; seed formation is more dependable.<br>(III) In the seeds of some grasses, there are remains of a second cotyledon. It is called the epiblast.','[{"text": "I and II are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I and III are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II and III are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All are correct", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'All are correct. Achene is seen in strawberry.<br>Reproductive processes such as pollination and fertilisation are independent of water, seed formation is more dependable. In the seeds of some grasses, there are remains of second cotyledon. It is called epiblast.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102900,'biology',8,158,336,'Which one of the following statements is not true?','[{"text": "<i>Orobanche</i> and <i>Striga</i> are parasitic plants producing tiny seeds.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Orchid</i> produces tiny seeds.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Ficus</i> produces multiple tiny seeds, and its inflorescence is pollinated by insects.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In some seeds, such as black pepper and pea, remnants of the nucellus are called perisperm.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In some seeds such as black pepper and beet, remnants of nucellus are also persistent. This residual, persistent nucellus is the perisperm.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102901,'biology',8,158,336,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Some species of Asteraceae and grasses have evolved a special mechanism to produce seeds without fertilisation.<br>(II) In <i>Citrus</i> plants, the ovule contains many embryos which develop from nucellar cells.<br>(III) In mango, the ovule contains one embryo which develops from nucellar cells.<br>(IV) The occurrence of more than one embryo in a seed is referred to as apomixis.','[{"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Two are correct (I and II )As in many Citrus and Mango varieties some of the nucellar cells surrounding the embryo sac start dividing, protrude into the embryo sac and develop into the embryos. In such species each ovule contains many embryos. Occurrence of more than one embryo in a seed is referred to as polyembryony.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102902,'biology',93,283,541,'In a practical examination, the following pedigree chart was given as a spotter for identification. The students identify the given pedigree chart as <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_102902_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />','[{"text": "Sex-linked recessive", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autosomal dominant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Autosomal recessive", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Sex-linked dominant", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'In this pedigree:<br>a. Unaffected parents (first generation) have an affected son, indicating a recessive trait.<br>b.Both males and females appear unaffected or affected with equal probability — so it is not\nsex-linked.<br>c.This rules out dominant and sex-linked inheritance.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102903,'biology',93,276,534,'How many types of gametes will be formed by a parent with genotype ‘AaBbCc’?','[{"text": "12", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "6", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "4", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "8", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The number of gametes formed = ${{\\text{2}}^{\\text{n}}}$, where<br>n = number of heterozygous gene pairs.<br>In AaBbCc, all 3 genes are heterozygous $ \\to $<br>so, 2³ = 8 gametes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102904,'biology',93,280,538,'When a single gene exhibits multiple phenotypic expression, the phenomenon is called','[{"text": "Co-dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Polygenic inheritance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Pleiotropy", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Pleiotropy refers to a condition where a single gene affects multiple traits or phenotypes. The gene for PKU (Phenylketonuria) affects skin pigmentation, hair, and mental development',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102905,'biology',93,284,543,'A colourblind man marries a carrier woman. The percentage of their colourblind progeny in the next generation will be','[{"text": "${\\\\text{100}}\\\\,{\\\\text{% }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{25}}\\\\,{\\\\text{% }}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{50}}\\\\,{\\\\text{% }}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{75}}\\\\,{\\\\text{% }}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Colorblindness is an X-linked recessive disorder. Cross: ${{\\text{X}}^{\\text{c}}}{\\text{Y}}$ (man) $ \\times \\,{{\\text{X}}^{\\text{c}}}{\\text{X}}$ (carrier woman) Possible progeny:<br>Sons: 50% colorblind $\\left( {{{\\text{X}}^{\\text{c}}}{\\text{Y}}} \\right)$, 50% normal (XY)<br>Daughters: 50% carrier $\\left( {{{\\text{X}}^{\\text{c}}}{\\text{X}}} \\right)$, 50% colorblind\n$\\left( {{{\\text{X}}^{\\text{c}}}{{\\text{X}}^c}} \\right)$ So, 50% of the total progeny will be colorblind',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102906,'biology',93,285,550,'Identify which one of the given pair of options is correct with respect to Down’s syndrome and Turner’s syndrome https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764951111/preptracker/questions/q_102906_question_1764951111381.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "c", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Down’s Syndrome: Caused by trisomy of chromosome 21. Symptoms include broad palms, mental retardation, and developmental delay. Turner’s Syndrome: Caused by absence of one X chromosome (XO). Affects females, who are sterile and have rudimentary ovaries.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102907,'biology',93,276,534,'Genes R and Y follow independent assortment. If RRYY produce round yellow seeds and rryy produce wrinkled green seeds, what will be the phenotypic ratio of the ${{\\text{F}}_{\\text{2}}}$ generation?','[{"text": "Phenotypic ratio- 9 : 7", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotypic ratio -1 : 2 : 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotypic ratio -3 : 1", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenotypic ratio - 9:3:3:1", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>A classical dihybrid cross performed by Mendel involves:<br>A cross which was made between a pure round yellow seeded pea plant (RRYY) with wrinkled green seeded plant (rryy). Yellow colour is dominant over green and round seed shape over wrinkled seed shape.<br>Phenotypic ratio in ${{\\text{F}}_{\\text{2}}}$ generation<br> <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_102907_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102909,'biology',93,279,537,'What is the pattern of inheritance for polygenic trait?','[{"text": "X-linked recessive inheritance pattern", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Mendelian inheritance pattern", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Non-mendelian inheritance pattern", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Autosomal dominant pattern", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>Polygenic traits are controlled by multiple genes, each contributing to the phenotype. Such traits (e.g., skin colour, height) do not follow Mendel\'s laws strictly and exhibit continuous variation.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102950,'biology',93,281,539,'Identify the sex determination type, in which both male and female individuals have same number of chromosomes. Identify the correct one:<br>I. XY type<br>II. XO type<br>III. ZW type<br>IV. Haplo-diplontic type','[{"text": "Only I and II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I and III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only I and IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "All, except IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Same number of chromosomes in male and female occur in XX - XY type of sex determination and ZZ - ZW type of sex determination.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102910,'biology',93,276,534,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) ABO blood groups are controlled by the gene $I$.<br>(II) $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{A}}$ and $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}}$ produce the same type of sugar in ABO blood grouping.<br>(III) The ABO system is an example of dominance.<br>(IV) In a dihybrid cross, if we get a 9:3:3:1 ratio, it means that the alleles of two genes segregate independently.<br>(V) If the D allele is completely dominant over the d allele, the percentage of offspring exhibiting the dominant phenotype is $75 \\%$.<br>(VI) A 1:1:1:1 ratio of progenies can be obtained if the plants for crossing are $\\mathrm{TtRr} \\times$ ttrr.','[{"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only I, IV, V and VI are correct. The corrected statements are: $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{A}}$ and $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}}$ produce different type of sugar in ABO blood grouping. ABO system is an example of codominance.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102911,'biology',93,276,534,'Identify the&nbsp; correct match from the following:<br>(I) Test cross - \\(\\mathrm{Tt} \\times \\mathrm{tt}\\)<br>(II) Monohybrid cross - 2:1<br>(III) Dihybrid cross - 9:3:3:1<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III are the correct answer. The corrected option is Monohybrid cross - $3: 1$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102912,'biology',93,272,530,'Which characters can express in both homozygous and heterozygous conditions in the garden pea plant (<i>Pisum sativum</i>)?<br>(I) Full pod<br>(II) Yellow seed color<br>(III) Dwarf plant<br>(IV) Green pod color','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, IV are correct. Full pod,yellow seed colour, green pod colour are expressed in homozygous and heterozygous conditions.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102913,'biology',93,276,534,'Match the following and choose the correct combination from the option given: https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764957708/preptracker/questions/q_102913_question_1764957707531.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{S}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{R}$ is the correct answer.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102914,'biology',93,281,539,'Observe the sex determination in the following and identify the correct ones:<br>(I) Human males = Male heterogamety<br>(II) Female hen $=$ Female heterogamety<br>(III) Male <i>Drosophila</i> = Male heterogamety<br>(IV) Male grasshopper = Male homogamety<br>(V) Male birds = Male homogamety','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III and V are correct. Male grasshopper $=$ heterogamety',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102915,'biology',93,275,533,'Identify the correct matching:<br>(I) Removal of anther - Masculation<br>(II) Laws of inheritance - Morgan<br>(III) Multiple allelism - <i>Antirrhinum</i><br>(IV) Universal donor - O blood group<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only IV is correct. Universal donor - O blood group is correct. Removal of anther emasculation, Multiple allelism -ABO blood group, Laws of inheritance - Mendel',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102916,'biology',93,276,534,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) Punnett square is a graphical representation to calculate the probability of all possible genotypes of offspring in a genetic cross.<br>(II) A plant shows a dominant phenotype; the genotype will be determined by codominance.<br>(III) Mendel\'s law of heredity can be explained with the help of mitosis.<br>(IV) A gamete produced by a diploid organism contains one allele of a gene.<br>(V) The genotype AaBbCc will never produce the gamete - cBb .<br>(VI) Law of dominance is based on the fact that the alleles do not show any blending and that both parental traits are recovered in the $\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ generation, though one of them is not seen at the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ stage.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements will be corrected as a plant shows dominant phenotype, the genotype will be determined by dominance. Mendel\'s law of heredity can be explained with the help of meiosis. Law of segregation is based on the fact that the alleles do not show any blending and that both the characters are recovered as such in the $\\mathrm{F}_{2}$ generation though one of these is not seen at the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ stage',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102917,'biology',93,276,534,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) A true-breeding line shows stable trait inheritance and expression for several generations.<br>(II) Characters are controlled by discrete units called factors.<br>(III) A pink-flowered plant exhibiting incomplete dominance will produce offspring with three kinds of flowers if self-pollinated.<br>(IV) When the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ progeny resembles both parents, the type of gene interaction is codominance.<br>(V) $\\mathrm{An} \\mathrm{F}_{2}$ dihybrid Mendelian cross produces $62.5 \\%$ parental phenotype.<br>(VI) Genes that code for a pair of contrasting traits are known as characters.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV, V are correct. Genes which code for a pair of contrasting traits are known as allele.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103020,'biology',96,1160,2775,'The drug prescribed to the patients who have undergone organ transplant is ____ and is produced by ____','[{"text": "Statin, <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyclosporin-A,  <i>Monascus purpureus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statin,  <i>Monascus purpureus</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cyclosporin-A,  <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Cyclosporin-A is an immunosuppressive drug given to patients after organ transplantation to prevent rejection. It is produced by the fungus <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102918,'biology',93,275,533,'Which of the following statements are incorrect?<br>(I) Genes that code for a pair of contrasting traits are known as dominant genes.<br>(II) A child with the blood-group genotype $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{A}} \\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}}$ is born to a woman with the genotype $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}} \\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}}$. The father can never be a man of genotype $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}} \\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}}$.<br>(III) In pea plants, the genotype (Bb) shows round seeds with intermediate-sized starch grains.<br>(IV) In the case of inheritance of one gene, the 3:1 phenotypic ratio can be explained on the basis of Segregation and Codominance.<br>(V) Dominance is an autonomous feature of a gene or its product when more than one phenotype is influenced by the same gene.','[{"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only I, IV, V are incorrect. The correct statements are -(II) A child with blood-group genotype $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{A}} \\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}}$ is born to a woman with genotype $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}} \\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}}$. The father can never be a man of genotype $\\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}} \\mathrm{I}^{\\mathrm{B}}$. (III) In pea plant, genotype (Bb) shows round seed with intermediate sized starch grain.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102919,'biology',93,275,533,'\\(F_{1}\\) generation resembles:<br>(A) Either of the two parents<br>(B) An intermediate between the two parents<br>(C) Both of the parents<br>Choose the correct match:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A - Dominance, B - Incomplete dominance, C - Codominance", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - Dominance, B - Codominance, C -Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Incomplete dominance, B -Codominance, C - Dominance", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Codominance, B - Dominance, C -Incomplete dominance", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - either of the two parents -Dominance B - in between of the two parents -Incomplete dominance. C - with both of the parents -Co-dominance.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102920,'biology',93,276,534,'Read the following statements and choose the correct option:<br>(I) In the genotype Tt , the alleles share a common locus, represent the same character, and form an allelic gene pair.<br>(II) Mendel selected two seed-related characters for dihybrid cross study.<br>(III) On the basis of monohybrid crosses, Mendel proposed only one conclusion.<br>(IV) By simply looking at the phenotype of a dominant trait, it is impossible to determine the exact genotypic composition.<br>(V) In the genotype Tt, the alleles can be present on non-homologous chromosomes.<br>Choose the correct option:','[{"text": "I, II, & IV are correct & III & V are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV & V are correct & III is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I & IV are correct & II, III & V are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III are correct & IV & V are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II & IV are correct  III & V are incorrect. About genotype Tt, can be present on homologous chromosome. On the basis of monohybrid crosses, Mendel proposed two conclusion.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102921,'biology',93,272,530,'Identify the correct statements about a test cross:<br>(I) It produces the same genotypic and phenotypic ratio.<br>(II) It is used to determine the purity and impurity of a recessive trait.<br>(III) In a test cross, the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ hybrid is crossed with the dominant parent.<br>(IV) It is a type of back cross.<br>(V) The hybrid is crossed with a double recessive genotype in a dihybrid cross.<br>(VI) It is used to determine whether a plant is homozygous or heterozygous dominant.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, IV, V, VI are correct. In test cross ${{\\text{F}}_{\\text{1}}}$ hybrid is crossed with recessive parent to test the progeny if it is homozygous or heterozygous.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102922,'biology',93,279,537,'Select the correct statements with respect to polygenic inheritance:<br>(I) It is also called quantitative inheritance.<br>(II) Intermediate phenotypes are more frequent.<br>(III) Dominant alleles show a cumulative effect.<br>(IV) The parental population remains constant irrespective of the number of polygenes.<br>(V) A single dominant allele expresses only a unit of the trait.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV, V are correct. The inheritance of polygenic traits (trait controlled by two or more genes) is called polygenic or quantitative inheritance. Intermediate phenotypes are more frequent. Dominant alleles show cumulative effect. Parental population remains constant irrespective of polygenes number. A single dominant allele express only a unit of the trait.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102923,'biology',93,284,545,'Identify the correct statement(s):<br>(I) The possibility of a female becoming haemophilic is extremely rare because the mother of such a female must be at least a carrier, and the father should be haemophilic.<br>(II) The possibility of a female becoming sickle cell anaemic is extremely rare.<br>(III) Sickle cell anaemia is an autosome linked dominant trait.','[{"text": "III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II. The possibility of a female becoming a sickle cell anaemic is extremely rare is wrong, as it is an autosomal disorder.<br>III. Sickle cell anaemia is an autosome linked recessive trait.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102924,'biology',93,272,530,'Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) The phenotype of an organism is the result of genotype and environmental interactions.<br>(II) In his classic experiments on pea plants, Mendel did not use pod length.<br>(III) Alleles show blending, and both characters recover as such in the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ generation.<br>(IV) Out of one pair of factors, one is dominant and the other is recessive.<br>(V) The discrete unit controlling a particular character is called a factor.','[{"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only I, II, IV and V are correct. Alleles do not show blending and both the characters recover as such in $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ generation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103076,'biology',98,1189,2848,'Which of the following genetically engineered organisms was used by Eli Lilly to prepare human insulin?','[{"text": "Phage", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Bacterium", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Yeast", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Virus", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>Eli Lilly used genetically engineered bacteria (<i>E.coli</i>) to produce human insulin. Separate genes for insulin A and B chains were inserted into plasmids of <i>E.coli</i>, which expressed them and were later combined to form functional insulin',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102925,'biology',93,279,537,'Identify the incorrect statement from the following:<br>(I) A pea plant with intermediate-sized starch grains in seeds is crossed with another plant having small-sized starch grains in seeds. The total number of seeds obtained in the progeny is 630 . The number of plants obtained are 315 (intermediate size) and 315 (small size).<br>(II) Multiple alleles can be found only when population studies are made.<br>(III) In Snapdragon, pure red-flowered plants are crossed with pure white-flowered plants, and $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ individuals have pink flowers. The alleles of the hybrid pink-flowered plant will segregate if self-pollinated.<br>(IV) In <i>Antirrhinum majus</i>, when a pink flowered plant is crossed with a white flowered plant, the total number of plants obtained is 120 . The percentage of white flowered phenotype in the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ offspring is $50 \\%$.<br>(V) If a polygenic trait is controlled by two gene pairs, then the probability of individuals in a generation showing exact resemblance to the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ generation phenotype of parents is 2/16.','[{"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "V only", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'V is incorrect. If a polygenic trait is controlled by two gene pairs than the probability of individuals in generation showing exact resemblance to the $\\mathrm{F}_{1}$ generation phenotype of parents is $4 / 16$.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102926,'biology',93,280,538,'Identify the correct option.<br>(I) Pleiotropic genes have multiple phenotypic effect.<br>(II) ABO system of blood grouping exhibits multiple allelism<br>(III) Polygenes exhibit continuous variation.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are correct. Pleiotropic genes have multiple phenotypic effect. ABO system of blood grouping exhibits multiple allelism. Polygenes exhibit continuous variation. All are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102927,'biology',93,284,547,'Which of the following option is incorrect?','[{"text": "Sex chromosome - Phenylketonuria.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Chromosome no. 11 - Sickle cell anaemia.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome no. 11 or 16 - Thalassemia.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sex chromosome - Hemophilia.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Sex chromosome - Phenylketonuria is wrong, it is an autosomal recessive disorder.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102928,'biology',93,280,538,'Match the terms given in Column I with their description in Column II and select the correct option: https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764951063/preptracker/questions/q_102928_question_1764951063437.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{S}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{P}$ is correct.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102929,'biology',93,275,533,'Which of the following are mismatched?<br>(I) Incomplete dominance - Exception of the postulate of Independent Assortment.<br>(II) Co-dominance - Exception of the Law of Purity of Gametes.<br>(III) Multiple allelism - Rh system.<br>(IV) RBC is sickle shaped - Sickle cell anaemia.<br>(V) Multiple alleles are present on the same locus on homologous chromosomes.<br>(VI) Inheritance of seed shape - Dominant recessive relationship.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only I, II and III are incorrect/mismatched. Incomplete dominance - Exception of postulate of dominance Co - dominance Exception of law of dominance. III. Multiple allelism-ABO system',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102930,'biology',93,280,538,'Match the terms in Column - I with Column -II and choose the correct option. https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764956821/preptracker/questions/q_102930_question_1764956820483.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{Q}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{S}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{P}$ is the correct answer.',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102931,'biology',93,284,545,'Mark the correct statement with respect to sickle cell anaemia:','[{"text": "Homozygous individuals for $\\\\mathrm{Hb}^{\\\\mathrm{A}}$ show the diseased phenotype.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Heterozygous individuals exhibit sickle cell trait.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Heterozygous individuals are affected and diseased.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Homozygous individuals for $\\\\mathrm{Hb}^{\\\\mathrm{s}}$ are apparently unaffected.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Heterozygous individuals exhibit sickle cell trait is correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102932,'biology',93,277,535,'Identify the correct statement:<br>(I) Boveri and Sutton combined cytological observations on meiotic cell division and Mendel\'s concept of inheritance to propose the Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance.<br>(II) Boveri combined cytological observations on meiotic cell division and Mendel\'s concept of inheritance to propose the Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance.<br>(III) Sutton combined cytological observations on meiotic cell division and Mendel\'s concept of inheritance to propose the Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance.<br>(IV) Experimental verification of the Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance was done by Thomas Hunt Morgan.','[{"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'III and IV are correct. Sutton combined Cytological observation on meiotic cell division and Mendel\'s concept on inheritance to propose Chromosomal theory of inheritance.<br>Experimental verification of the chromosomal theory of inheritance was done by Thomas Hunt Morgan.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102933,'biology',93,285,550,'Match the following columns https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764957709/preptracker/questions/q_102933_question_1764957708963.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  P, B  -  Q}}\\\\,{\\\\text{& }}\\\\,{\\\\text{R,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  T, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  P, B  -  Q}}\\\\,{\\\\text{& }}\\\\,{\\\\text{R,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  S, D  -  R}}\\\\,{\\\\text{& }}\\\\,{\\\\text{T}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  P, B  -  Q}}\\\\,{\\\\text{& }}\\\\,{\\\\text{T,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  R, D  -  S}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  T& P, B  -  S,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{C  -  R, D  -  Q}}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'${\\text{A  -  T & P, B  -  S,}}\\,{\\text{C  -  R, D  -  Q}}$ is correct.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102934,'biology',93,278,536,'Select the correct statement from the following with respect to a dihybrid cross.<br>(I) Genes loosely linked on the same chromosome show similar recombination as the tightly linked genes.<br>(II) Tightly linked genes on the same chromosome show very few recombinations.<br>(III) The term linkage was coined by Sturtevant.<br>(IV) Genes used by Mendel for the dihybrid cross in <i>Drosophila</i> were located on the X chromosome.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only II is correct. The corrected statements are<br>(I) Genes loosely linked on the same chromosome do not show similar recombination as the tightly linked ones<br>(III) The term linkage was coined by Morgan.<br>(IV) Genes used by Morgan for dihybrid cross in <i>Drosophila</i> were located on the X chromosome.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102935,'biology',93,277,535,'Select the incorrect statement with respect to the Chromosomal Theory of Inheritance:<br>(I) It was proposed by Sutton and Boveri.<br>(II) The behavior of chromosomes is parallel to the behavior of genes.<br>(III) Chromosomes and genes occur in pairs in diploid and haploid cells, respectively.<br>(IV) The paired condition of both chromosomes as well as Mendelian factors is restored during fertilization.','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II , III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III is incorrect.Chromosomes and genes occur in pairs in diploid cells only.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102936,'biology',93,285,548,'Pick out the correct statements.<br>(I) Thalassemia is a sex - linked recessive disease.<br>(II) Down\'s syndrome is due to aneuploidy.<br>(III) Phenylketonuria is an autosomal recessive gene disorder.<br>(IV) Sickle cell anaemia is a sex - linked dominant gene disorder.','[{"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(II) and (III) are correct. Down\'s syndrome is due to aneuploidy.Phenylketonuria is an autosomal recessive gene disorder. Thalassemia is an autosomal - linked recessive disease. Sickle cell anaemia is a autosomal linked recessive gene disorder.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102937,'biology',93,278,536,'The A and B genes are linked. What will be the genotypes of the progeny resulting from a cross between $\\mathrm{AB} / \\mathrm{ab}$ and $\\mathrm{ab} / \\mathrm{ab}$ ?Choose the correct option:<br>(I) AABB<br>(II) AaBb<br>(III) AAbb<br>(IV) aabb','[{"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Since A and B genes are linked, the parental genotypes " $\\mathrm{AB} / \\mathrm{ab}$ " and " $\\mathrm{ab} / \\mathrm{ab}$ " will produce only non-cross over gametes. So, AaBb and aabb will be the genotype of progeny in a cross between $\\mathrm{AB} / \\mathrm{ab}$ and $\\mathrm{ab} / \\mathrm{ab}$. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_102937_explanation_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102938,'biology',93,278,536,'Morgan carried out several dihybrid crosses in <i>Drosophila</i>. Choose the option that contains the correct statements regarding his experiment:<br>(I) The genes for body color, eye color, and wing shape are present on the allosome (sex chromosome).<br>(II) The strength of linkage between the genes for body colour and eye color is higher than that between the genes for eye color and size of the wing.<br>(III) The genes for white eye color and miniature wing are more tightly linked than the genes for yellow body and white eye color.<br>(IV) The genes for wild body color and wild eye color are present on the Y chromosome.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II are correct. The corrected answers are<br>(III) Gene of white eye and miniature wing are loosely linked than the gene of yellow body and white eye colour.<br>(IV) Gene of wild body colour and wild eye colour are present on X chromosome.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102939,'biology',93,278,536,'Linkage is unexceptionally absent between:','[{"text": "Two genes present on the same arm of a homologous pair of chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two genes present on different arms of a homologous pair of chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Two genes present on non-homologous chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Two genes present on the same sister chromatids", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Linkage is unexceptionally absent between Two genes present on non homologous chromosomes.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102940,'biology',93,275,533,'Which of the following conditions represents a case of co-dominant genes?<br>(I) A gene expresses itself, suppressing the phenotypic effect of its alleles.<br>(II) Genes that are similar in phenotypic effect when present separately, but when together, interact to produce a different trait<br>(III) Alleles, both of which interact to produce a trait, which may resemble either of the parental types.<br>(IV) Alleles, each of which produces an independent effect in the heterozygous condition.<br>(V) The genes of an allelic pair express equally.','[{"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(IV) Alleles, each of which produces an independent effect in heterozygous condition (V) The genes of an allelic pair express equally, both are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102951,'biology',93,285,548,'Consider the following statements about polyploidy:<br>(I) It is a failure of cytokinesis.<br>(II) It occurs after metaphase.<br>(III) This condition is often seen in plants.<br>(IV) This condition is often seen in animals.','[{"text": "IV is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II and IV are incorrect. Failure of cytokinesis after telophase stage of cell division results in an increase in a whole set of chromosomes in an organism and, this phenomenon is known as polyploidy. This condition is often seen in plants.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102941,'biology',93,285,550,'Match the Column - I and Column - II https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764957716/preptracker/questions/q_102941_question_1764957716087.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{S}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Q, B-P, C-S, D-R is the correct option. sickle cell anaemia - Substitution from GAG to GUG, klinefelter\'s- extra sex chromosome, turners - absence of sex chromosome, downs syndrome - Palm is broad',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102942,'biology',93,278,536,'In <i>Drosophila melanogaster</i>.<br>(I) Recombinant<br>a. The genes white and yellow shows ____a____<br>b. Genes white and miniature wing shows ____ b ____.<br>(II) Linkage<br>a. The genes white and yellow shows ____a _____<br>b. Genes white and miniature wing shows ____ b ____ .','[{"text": "I ( $\\\\mathrm{a} \\\\rightarrow 1.3 \\\\%, \\\\mathrm{~b} \\\\rightarrow 62.8 \\\\%$ ),\\\\begin{equation*}\\\\text { II }(\\\\mathrm{a} \\\\rightarrow 98.7 \\\\%, \\\\mathrm{~b} \\\\rightarrow 62.8 \\\\%)\\\\end{equation*}", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I (a $\\\\rightarrow 98.7 \\\\%,, \\\\mathrm{~b} \\\\rightarrow 37.2 \\\\%$ ),\\\\begin{equation*}\\\\text { II }(\\\\mathrm{a} \\\\rightarrow 98.7 \\\\%, \\\\mathrm{~b} \\\\rightarrow 62.8 \\\\%)\\\\end{equation*}", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{I}(\\\\mathrm{a} \\\\rightarrow 1.3 \\\\%, \\\\mathrm{~b} \\\\rightarrow 37.2 \\\\%)$,\\\\begin{equation*}\\\\text { II }(\\\\mathrm{a} \\\\rightarrow 98.7 \\\\%, \\\\mathrm{~b} \\\\rightarrow 37.2 \\\\%)\\\\end{equation*}", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{I}(\\\\mathrm{a} \\\\rightarrow 1.3 \\\\%, \\\\mathrm{~b} \\\\rightarrow 37.2 \\\\%)$,\\\\begin{equation*}\\\\text { II }(\\\\mathrm{a} \\\\rightarrow 98.7 \\\\%, \\\\mathrm{~b} \\\\rightarrow 62.8 \\\\%)\\\\end{equation*}", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I (a $\\rightarrow 1.3 \\%, \\mathrm{~b} \\rightarrow 37.2 \\%$ ),\\begin{equation*}\\text { II }(\\mathrm{a} \\rightarrow 98.7 \\%, \\mathrm{~b} \\rightarrow 62.8 \\%) \\text { is correct. }\\end{equation*}',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102943,'biology',93,278,536,'A. In a cross between individuals homozygous for (a and b) and wild type $(++), 600$ out of 1000 individuals were of the parental type. What is the genetic distance between genes a and b ?<br>B. _____ used the frequency of recombination between gene pairs on the same chromosome as a measure of the distance between genes and \'mapped\' their position on the chromosome.','[{"text": "A. 20 map units, B. Sturtevant", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A. 100 map units, B. Morgan", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A. 40 map units, B. Sturtevant", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A. 60 map units, B. Morgan", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'40 map unit, According to the problem the number of recombinant offsprings are (1000 $-600)=400$, which helps us find the recombinant frequency by the formula (No of recombinant progeny/ Total number of offsprings) $=400 / 1000=0.4$. Thus the distance between the genes is $0.4\\,{\\text{X}}\\,100 = 40$ map units. Sturtevant used the frequency of recombination between gene pairs on the same chromosome as a measure of the distance between genes and \'mapped\' their position on the chromosome.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102944,'biology',93,278,536,'Given below are statements regarding linkage of genes. Which of the following statements are correct?<br>(I) The strength of linkage is determined by the distance between the two genes.<br>(II) Morgan coined the term recombination to describe the physical association of genes on a chromosome, and the term linkage to describe the generation of non-parental gene combinations.<br>(III) Two genes are said to be linked when they fail to show independent assortment.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The corrected statement is Morgan coined the term linkage to describe this physical association of genes on a chromosome and the term recombination to describe the generation of non-parental gene combinations.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102945,'biology',93,281,539,'In a certain taxon of insects, some individuals have 32 chromosomes, while others have 31 chromosomes. Which of the following correctly describes these organisms?','[{"text": "Grasshopper - Males and Drones, respectively.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Grasshopper - Females and Males, respectively.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Honey bees - Drones and Females, respectively.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "<i>Drosophila</i> - Males and Females, respectively.", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Grasshopper - Females and males, respectively is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102946,'biology',93,281,539,'In honey bees, match the correct ploidy with its chromosome number and the sex of the insect:-<br>(I) Diploid - 46 - Female<br>(II) Haploid - 23 - Male<br>(III) Diploid- 32 - Female<br>(IV) Haploid - 16 - Male<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV are correct. Haploid - 16 -Male, Diploid (32) - Female honey bees formed by fertilisation of male and female gamete.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102947,'biology',93,281,539,'Choose the wrong statement:','[{"text": "Henking (1891) could trace a specific nuclear structure throughout spermatogenesis in a few insects.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In <i>Drosophila</i>, males have one X and one Y chromosome, whereas females have a pair of X chromosomes along with autosomes.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In birds, females have one Z and one W chromosome.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "In insects with the XO type of sex determination, all sperms contain an X chromosome along with autosomes.", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'In insects with XO type of sex determination, all sperms have X - chromosome besides autosomes is wrong, it can be corrected as in insects with XO type of sex determination, some sperms have X chromosome besides autosomes whereas some do not.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102948,'biology',93,281,539,'Identify A and B:<br>A. <i>Drosophila melanogaster</i> (female ) &<br>B. <i>Drosophila melanogaster</i> (male) has','[{"text": "A. 2 pairs of autosomes and (XX) sex chromosomes<br>B. 3 pairs of autosomes and (XY) sex chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A. 3 pairs of autosomes and (XX) sex chromosomes<br>B. 3 pairs of autosomes and (XY) sex chromosomes", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A. 1 pairs of autosomes and (XY)sex chromosomes<br>B. 3 pairs of autosomes and (XX) sex chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A. 3 pairs of autosomes and (XY)sex chromosomes<br>B. 3 pairs of autosomes and (XX) sex chromosomes", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'3 pairs of autosomes and (XX) sex chromosomes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102952,'biology',93,278,536,'Which of the following statements is incorrect with reference to sex linkage in <i>Drosophila</i>?<br>(I) The genes for eye colour and body colour are tightly linked and show $1.3 \\%$ recombinants.<br>(II) The genes for body colour and eye colour are loosely linked and show 37.2% recombinants.<br>(III) The genes for eye colour and wing shape are tightly linked and show $98.7 \\%$ parental types.<br>(IV) The genes for wing shape and body color are loosely linked and show 37.2% recombinants.','[{"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'II, III, IV are incorrect. Gene of eye colour and body colour are tightly linked and show $1.3 \\%$ recombinants is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102953,'biology',93,281,539,'Find out the correct match:<br>I. Henking - X body<br>II. Chromosomal map - Sturtevant<br>III. Hugo de Vries - Mutation<br>IV. Morgan - <i>Pisum sativum</i><div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III are correct. The correct answer is Mendel - <i>Pisum sativum</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102954,'biology',93,281,539,'Identify the correct option:<br>(I) Male <i>Apis</i> (drone) is produced by fertilization.<br>(II) Henking named a specific nuclear structure as the Y body, but he could not explain its significance.<br>(III) In <i>Homo sapiens</i>, only females are a product of fertilization.<br>(IV) Cytological observations in birds led to the development of the concept of genetic/ chromosomal basis of sex determination.<br>(V) In Aves (birds), both sexes are a product of parthenogenesis.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, and V are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, and V are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, and V are incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, and V are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III, IV and V are incorrect Corrected statements<br>(I) Male Apis (drone) by means of parthenogenesis<br>(II) Henking gave a name to this structure as the X body but he could not explain its significance.<br>(III) In Homo sapiens both the sexes are a product of fertilisation<br>(IV) the cytological observations made in a number of insects led to the development of the concept of genetic/chromosomal basis of sex - determination.<br>(V) In aves, both the sexes are a product of fertilisation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102955,'biology',93,281,539,'Identify the correct match from the following:<br>(I) Mendel - Law of inheritance<br>(II) Sutton & Boveri - Chromosomal theory of Inheritance<br>(III) Henking - 1891<br>(IV) Meiosis - 1902<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV are correct. (I) Mendel- Law of inheritance, (II) Sutton & Boveri Chromosomal theory of Inheritance (III) Henking - 1891, (IV) Meiosis - 1902',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102956,'biology',93,281,539,'Identify the correct statement(s) regarding sex determination in arthropods:<br>(I) <i>Drosophila</i> (arthropoda) follows the XX-XY type of sex determination.<br>(II) Grasshopper (arthropoda) follows the XX-XO type of sex determination.<br>(III) Honey bee (arthropoda) follows the haplo-diploid type of sex determination.','[{"text": "Only I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, III are correct. <i>Drosophila</i> (arthropoda) shows XX-XY type of sex determination. Grasshopper (arthropoda) shows XX - XO type of sex determination. Honey bee (arthropoda) shows haplodiplontic type of sex determination. All are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102957,'biology',93,284,547,'Which of the following statements are applicable to Thalassemia?<br>(I) Queen Victoria was a carrier of the disease.<br>(II) RBCs change their structure from a biconcave disc to an elongated sickle-like structure.<br>(III) It is an autosome-linked recessive blood disease.<br>(IV) Chromosome number 11 or 16 and/or both may be affected.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV are correct. Queen Victoria shows a number of haemophilic descendents as she was a carrier of the disease, RBC change their structure from biconcave disc to elongated sickle like structure in sickle cell anaemia.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102958,'biology',93,278,536,'The recombination frequency is:<br>(I) A measure of the distance between genes.<br>(II) Directly proportional to the distance between linked genes.<br>(III) Used to map the position of genes on a chromosome.<br>(IV) Equal to map units (centimorgans, cM).<br>Choose the correct option:','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III, IV are correct. Sturtevant used the frequency of recombination between gene pairs on the same chromosome as a measure of the distance between genes and \'mapped\' their position on the chromosome. Recombination frequency is inversely proportional to the distance between linked genes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102959,'biology',93,277,535,'Identify the incorrect statement(s) from the following:<br>(I) Sutton and Boveri stated that the pairing and separation of a pair of chromosomes would lead to the segregation of a pair of factors they carried.<br>(II) Genes are the units of inheritance.<br>(III) There are 5 different alleles that determine ABO blood types.<br>(IV) The phenotypic ratio of a Mendelian monohybrid cross is $3: 1$.','[{"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III is incorrect. There are 3 different alleles which determine ABO blood types',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102960,'biology',93,278,536,'Identify the correct statement with respect to:Morgan worked with <i>Drosophila</i> because:(I) <i>Drosophila</i> is called a genetic engineer of the plant kingdom.<br>(II) <i>Drosophila</i> completes its life cycle in 14 weeks.<br>(III) It belongs to the phylum Arthropoda.<br>(IV) There is a clear differentiation of sexes, with males being larger and females being smaller.<br>(V) <i>Drosophila</i> has many types of hereditary variations that can be observed under a low power microscope.','[{"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, V are correct. They complete their life cycle in about two weeks, females are larger than the males. <i>Agrobacterium</i> is called genetic engineer.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102961,'biology',93,278,536,'Which of the following statements are correct based on Morgan\'s experiment and the concept of linkage?<br>(I) Morgan and his group discovered that genes located on the X chromosome showed an equal proportion of parental and non parental gene combinations in dihybrid crosses.<br>(II) Morgan observed that when two genes in a dihybrid cross were situated on the same chromosome, the proportion of parental gene combinations was much higher than nonparental types.<br>(III) The term "linkage" was coined b Morgan to describe the physical association of genes on a chromosome.<br>(IV) The term "recombination" was used by Morgan to describe the generation of new gene combinations (non-parental types) due to crossing over.<br>(V) Linkage always prevents recombination, and genes that are linked never show nonparental combinations.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, III, IV are correct. If the genes were independently assorted, the proportion would be equal (Mendelian ratio 9:3:3:1). However, linked genes showed more parental combinations than recombinants. Recombination can still occur between linked genes, depending on their distance from each other.Genes far apart on the same chromosome can still assort independently due to crossing over.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102962,'biology',93,285,549,'Consider the following statements:<br>(I) Failure of segregation of chromatids during the cell division cycle results in the gain or loss of chromosomes, a condition called aneuploidy.<br>(II) Sickle-cell anemia is an autosomal recessive trait.<br>(III) Klinefelter\'s syndrome was first described by Henking.<br>(IV) Myotonic dystrophy is an autosomal dominant trait.','[{"text": "Only III is incorrect", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III and IV are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Only III is incorrect. Klinefelter\'s syndrome is named for Harry Klinefelter\'s an American physician who in 1942 described a set of symptoms that characterized the condition.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102963,'biology',93,283,541,'Given below is a pedigree chart showing the inheritance of a certain trait in humans. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/93_102963_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> The trait traced in the above pedigree chart is','[{"text": "Muscular dystrophy", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phenylketonuria", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Hemophilia", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sickle cell anaemia", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Muscular dystrophy is autosomal dominant disorder and the picture depicts autosomal dominant disorder.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102964,'biology',93,284,547,'Which of the following are Mendelian disorder?<br>Klinefelter\'s, Haemophilia, Cystic fibrosis, Muscular dystrophy, Sickle cell anaemia, Colour blindness, Phenylketonuria, Myotonic dystrophy, Polydactyly, Thalassemia, Down syndrome','[{"text": "Haemophilia, Cystic fibrosis, Muscular dystrophy, Klinefelter\'s", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Haemophilia, Cystic fibrosis, Muscular dystrophy, Sickle cell anaemia, Colour blindness, Phenylketonuria, Myotonic dystrophy, Thalassemia", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Phenylketonuria, Myotonic dystrophy, Thalassemia, Down\'s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Sickle cell anaemia, Colour blindness, Phenylketonuria, Turner\'s syndrome", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Haemophilia, Cystic fibrosis, Muscular dystrophy, Sickle cell anaemia, Colour blindness, Phenylketonuria, Myotonic dystrophy, Polydactyly, Thalassemia,are mendelian disorders.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102965,'biology',93,284,545,'In sickle-cell anemia, substitution occurs between:<br>(I) An amino acid and a polypeptide in a protein.<br>(II) An amino acid and a protein in a polypeptide.<br>(III) An acidic amino acid and an aromatic amino acid in a polypeptide.<br>(IV) An acidic amino acid and a neutral amino acid in a polypeptide.<br>(V) A purine and a pyrimidine in mRNA.<br>(VI) A purine and a purine in mRNA.','[{"text": "I, IV and V are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV and VI are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV and V are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III and IV are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV and V are correct Sickle cell anaemia is caused by the substitution of Glutamic acid (Glu) by Valine (Val) at the sixth position of the beta globin chain of the haemoglobin molecule and also GAG to GUG in mRNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102966,'biology',93,284,544,'Consider the following statements and select the option that includes only the correct ones:<br>(I) Haemophilia is a sex-linked recessive disease.<br>(II) The possibility of a male becoming haemophilic is extremely rare.<br>(III) Haemophilia can be transmitted from an affected haemophilic male to his male progeny.<br>(IV) In haemophilia, a single protein that is part of the cascade of proteins involved in blood clotting is affected.<br>(V) Haemophilia is also called "bleeder\'s disease."','[{"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, IV and V. The possibility of a female becoming a haemophilic is extremely rare.It can be transmitted from an affected haemophilic male to his female progeny.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102968,'biology',93,284,547,'Identify the statement about Thalassemia and sickle cell anemia.<br>(I) Both are due to a quantitative defect in globin chain synthesis<br>(II) Thalassemia may involve both $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ chains and sickle cell involves $\\beta$ chain<br>(III) Sickle cell anemia is due to a quantitative problem of globin molecules<br>(IV) Both are due to a qualitative defect in globin chain synthesis','[{"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Thalassemia may involve both $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ chains and sickle cell involves $\\beta$ chains is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102988,'biology',94,795,1704,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect matching:<br>(I) Exons - Translated part of DNA.<br>(II) Alec Jeffreys - DNA Fingerprinting.<br>(III) George Gamow - Codon is triplet.<br>(IV) Structural and catalytic role during translation - rRNA.<br>(V) Not a part of the translation unit - UTR.<br>(VI) VNTR - 11-60 bp.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only VI is incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as VNTR varies in size from 0.1 to 20 kb .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102969,'biology',93,274,532,'Which of the following statements are correct regarding alleles, enzyme production, and dominance?<br>(I) A dominant allele always produces a less efficient enzyme than a recessive allele.<br>(II) If the modified allele produces a nonfunctional enzyme or no enzyme at all, the phenotype is determined solely by the unmodified allele.<br>(III) If a modified allele produces an enzyme that is as efficient as the normal enzyme, it results in the same phenotype as the normal allele.<br>(IV) The recessive allele generally produces a non-functional enzyme or fails to produce an enzyme, which is why its phenotype is not expressed when paired with a dominant allele.<br>(V) The transformation of substrate S is always dependent on the presence of a functional enzyme, and any mutation leading to enzyme inefficiency will alter the phenotype.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, III, IV, V are correct regarding alleles, enzyme production, and dominance. A dominant allele is simply the one whose trait is expressed in heterozygous condition. The normal allele produces the normal enzyme that is needed for the transformation of a substrate S .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102970,'biology',93,284,543,'Mr. Amarjeet, who is colour blind, marries a phenotypically normal woman. They have two sons and three daughters, and all the children appear normal.<br>Considering the inheritance pattern of colour blindness, which of the following conclusions are correct?<br>(I) Colour blindness is caused by an X-linked recessive allele.<br>(II) Mr. Amarjeet\'s sons could have been colour blind if their mother were a carrier.<br>(III) Mr. Amarjeet\'s daughters are obligate carriers of the colour blindness allele.<br>(IV) If the couple had a colour-blind daughter, it would confirm that the mother was a carrier of the trait.<br>(V) If Mr. Amarjeet had married a colourblind woman, all of their sons and daughters would have been affected.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III, IV, V are correct. Colour blindness is caused by X linked recessive allele, so the daughters will be carriers and son will not be affected, therefore all children will be normal.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102971,'biology',93,285,550,'Consider the following statements and identify which belongs to Turner\'s syndrome (T), Down\'s (D) syndrome and Klinefelter\'s (K) respectively:<br>(I) Gynaecomastia<br>(II) Furrowed tongue and partially open mouth<br>(III) Bleeding disorder<br>(IV) 45 with X0, females are sterile as ovaries are rudimentary<br>(V) Cannot differentiate colours','[{"text": "T- I, D-II, K-IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "T- I, D-III, K-IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "T- IV, D- II, K-I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "T- (IV, V), D-(II, III), K- I", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV, II & I. (I) Gynaecomastia - Klinefelter\'s syndrome.<br>(II) Furrowed tongue and partially open mouth- Downs syndrome.<br>(III) 45 with X0, females are sterile as ovaries are rudimentary - Turners syndrome',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102974,'biology',94,788,1697,'RNA polymerase II is responsible for the transcription of','[{"text": "snRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "tRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "rRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "hnRNA", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'RNA Polymerase II transcribes hnRNA (heterogeneous nuclear RNA), which is the precursor of mRNA in eukaryotes.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102975,'biology',94,793,1702,'Which of the following enzymes increases the permeability of the bacterial cell to lactose?','[{"text": "Amylase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\beta $ -galactosidase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Permease", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Transacetylase", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Permease is an enzyme that increases the permeability of the bacterial cell membrane to lactose, allowing it to enter the cell. It is one of the structural genes of the lac operon.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102976,'biology',94,788,1696,'Which of the following statements are correct with reference to prokaryotic genome?<br>(a) Monocistronic structural genes<br>(b) Introns absent in structural genes<br>(c) Transcription and translation are coupled\nprocesses<br>(d) Primary transcript undergoes splicing<br>(e) Only one RNA polymerase is present','[{"text": "Only a, b and c are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only a, b and d are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only b, c and e are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only a, d and e are correct", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only b, c and e are correct<br>Prokaryotes typically have polycistronic mRNA (multiple genes under one promoter). No splicing in prokaryotes due to absence of introns.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102977,'biology',94,789,1698,'Who proposed that the genetic code for amino acids should be made up of three nucleotides?','[{"text": "Franklin Stahl", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "George Gamow", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Francis Crick", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Jacque Monod", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>George Gamow, a physicist, proposed that the genetic code is a triplet code, i.e., three nucleotides code for one amino acid.<br>This was based on mathematical reasoning to\nexplain how 4 nucleotides could code for 20 amino acids',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102978,'biology',94,783,1688,'Histones are enriched with -','[{"text": "Phenylalanine & Arginine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysine & Arginine", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Leucine & Lysine", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Phenylalanine & Leucine", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>Histones are positively charged basic proteins that help in DNA packaging in eukaryotes. They are rich in lysine and arginine, which facilitate tight binding to the negatively charged\nDNA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102979,'biology',94,788,1695,'Which factor is important for termination of transcription?','[{"text": "$\\\\gamma $ (gamma)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\alpha $ (alpha)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\sigma $ (sigma)", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\rho $(rho)", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>In prokaryotes, transcription termination requires the help of $\\rho $(rho) factor, a protein that facilitates dissociation of RNA polymerase from the DNA template $\\sigma $ (sigma) factor helps only in initiation, not termination',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103222,'biology',106,1356,3259,'The ‘Sixth Extinction’ of species, presently in progress, is ____ times faster than the previous five episodes of mass extinctions.','[{"text": "1 to 10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "10 to 100", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "100 to 1000", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "1000 to 10000", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The ‘Sixth Extinction’ refers to the ongoing mass extinction driven by human activities. The current rate of species extinction is 100 to 1000 times faster than the natural or background extinction rate observed in the past.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102980,'biology',94,785,1690,'Given below are two statements :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">In the RNA world, RNA is considered the first genetic material evolved to carry out essential life processes. RNA acts as a genetic material and also as a catalyst for some important biochemical reactions in living\nsystems. Being reactive, RNA is unstable</div><div class="column-right">DNA evolved from RNA and is a more stable genetic material. Its double helical strands being complementary, resist changes by evolving repairing mechanism.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the\nmost appropriate answer from the options given below :</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is incorrect but statement B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statement A and statement B are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statement A and statement B are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>Statement A: Correct – In the RNA world hypothesis, RNA was the first genetic material, capable of information storage and catalytic activity (e.g., ribozymes). RNA is unstable and\nhighly reactive.<br>Statement B: Correct – DNA evolved later, offering greater stability due to its doublestranded structure and repair mechanisms, making it a better long-term genetic material. Both statements are correct.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102981,'biology',94,793,1702,'Which of the following are the post transcriptional events in an eukaryotic cell?<br>A. Transport of pre-mRNA to cytoplasm prior to splicing.<br>B. Removal of introns and joining of exons.<br>C. Addition of methyl group at ${\\text{5\'}}$ end of hnRNA.<br>D. Addition of adenine residues at ${\\text{3\'}}$end of hnRNA.<br>E. Base pairing of two complementary RNAs.<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :','[{"text": "C, D, E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A, B, C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B, C, D only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B, C, E only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>B. Splicing – Removal of introns and joining of exons<br>C. 5\' capping – Addition of a methylated cap at the 5\' end of hnRNA<br>D. 3\' polyadenylation – Addition of adenine\nresidues at the 3\' end (poly-A tail), these are correct statements. Splicing occurs before export to cytoplasm. Base pairing of complementary RNAs – Not part of post-transcriptional modification.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102982,'biology',94,783,1688,'Match Column-I with Column- II. <img src=\'/img/data/biology/94_102982_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' /> Choose the correct answer from the options given below:<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A-R, B-Q, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>A. Alfred Hershey & Martha Chase S. DNA as genetic material confirmation<br>B. Euchromatin R. Loosely packed and light stained<br>C. Frederick Griffith P. <i>Streptococcus\npneumoniae</i><br>D. Heterochromatin Q. Densely packed and<br>dark-stained<br>Correct matching: A–S, B–R, C–P, D–Q.',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102983,'biology',94,794,1703,'Which chromosome in the human genome has the highest number of genes?','[{"text": "Chromosome 10", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome X", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome Y", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chromosome 1", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>The human chromosome with the highest number of genes is Chromosome 1, which contains approximately 2968 genes',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102984,'biology',94,787,1694,'Read the following statements and select the correct statements:<br>(I) If the sequence of bases in one strand of DNA is ATGCATGCA, the sequence of bases on the complementary DNA strand is TACGTACGT.<br>(II) If the sequence of bases in one strand of DNA is ATGCATGCA, the sequence of bases on the complementary DNA strand is UACGUACGU.<br>(III) Other than DNA polymerase, some other enzymes are also involved in DNA synthesis.<br>(IV) The discontinuous DNA strand is synthesized on the DNA template strand with a polarity of 3\'-5\'.<br>(V) Euchromatin is loosely packed and stains dark.<br>(VI) The process of transformation is not affected by RNase, protease, and lipase enzymes but is affected by the DNase enzyme.','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, VI are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Pentose sugar is found in nucleic acid, Euchromatin is loosely packed and stains light. Discontinuous DNA strand is synthesized on DNA template strand with polarity 5\'- 3\', If the sequence of bases in one strand of DNA is ATGCATGCA, the sequence of bases on complementary RNA strand is UACGUACGU.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102985,'biology',94,788,1697,'Identify the correct match from the following options:<br>(I) Exon - Coding sequence<br>(II) Promoter - Site for binding of RNA polymerase<br>(III) Capping - Methyl guanosine triphosphate<br>(IV) Tailing - Adenylate residues<br>(V) RNA replication - S-phase<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, IV are correct. The incorrect one is corrected as RNA replication - S - phase.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102986,'biology',94,794,1703,'Read the following statements and select the correct statements:<br>(I) DNA from every tissue of an individual shows the same degree of polymorphism.<br>(II) In a gene encoding a polypeptide of 50 amino acids, if the ${\\text{2}}{{\\text{5}}^{{\\text{th}}}}$ codon (UAU) is mutated to UAA, a polypeptide of 25 amino acids will be formed.<br>(III) Polycistronic messenger RNA (mRNA) usually occurs in bacteria and prokaryotes.<br>(IV) Exons express to form enzymes as well.<br>(V) The methodologies of the Human Genome Project (HGP) involve only one major approach: sequencing the entire genome\'s DNA.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, III, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as, In a gene encoding a polypeptide of 50 amino acids, $25{ }^{\\text {th }}$ codon (UAU) is mutated to UAA, a polypeptide of 24 amino acids will be formed. The methodologies of HGP involves only two major approach of sequencing entire DNA of genome.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103251,'biology',105,1280,3097,'Who is known as the father of Ecology in India?','[{"text": "Birbal Sahni", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "S.R. Kashyap", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ramdeo Misra", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Ram Udar", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>Ramdeo Misra is regarded as the Father of Ecology in India for his pioneering work in ecological research and education',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102989,'biology',94,795,1704,'Read the following statements and select the correct statements:<br>(I) If the sequence of bases in the coding strand of DNA is ATTCGATG, then the sequence of bases in mRNA will be AUUCGAUG.<br>(II) <i>Escherichia coli</i> fully labeled with ${ }^{15} \\mathrm{~N}$ is allowed to grow in a ${ }^{14} \\mathrm{~N}$ medium. The two strands of the DNA molecule in the first generation bacteria have different densities and do not fully resemble the parent DNA.<br>(III) The protein-synthesizing machinery has evolved around DNA.<br>(IV) If 100 heavy DNA molecules are replicated twice in a medium containing $^{{\\text{14}}}{\\text{N}}$, we will have 200 hybrid and 200 light DNA molecules.<br>(V) The last step of DNA fingerprinting is auto radiography.','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I,II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Protein synthesizing machinery has evolved around RNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102990,'biology',94,789,1698,'Identify the incorrect match:<br>(I) Griffith - Transformation.<br>(II) Hershey and Chase - DNA is the genetic material.<br>(III) Meselson and Stahl - DNA replication.<br>(IV) George Gamow - Transcription.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV is incorrect. The incorrect one is corrected as George Gamow - triplet.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102991,'biology',94,792,1701,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect statements:<br>(I) Elongation in translation is controlled by the sigma factor.<br>(II) UTRs are found just before the stop codon as well as just after the initiation codon.<br>(III) There is a single DNA-dependent RNA polymerase that catalyzes the transcription of all types of RNA in plant cells.<br>(IV) In eukaryotic cells, charging of tRNA occurs in the cytoplasm.','[{"text": "Only I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, III are incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as.<br>(I) Elongation in transcription is by the enzyme RNA polymerase.<br>(II) The UTRs are present at both 5\'- end (before start codon) and at 3 \'- end (after stopcodon). They are required for efficient translation process.<br>(III) There is a single DNA dependent RNA polymerase that catalyses transcription of all type of RNA in bacterial cell.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102992,'biology',94,795,1704,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect statements:<br>(I) Codons are not found in bacteria.<br>(II) All amino acids have more than one codon.<br>(III) In the lac operon, the y-gene codes for permease, which increases the permeability of the cell to $\\beta$-galactosides.<br>(IV) Amino acids may have more than one codon.<br>(V) During DNA fingerprinting, the next step after blotting is gel electrophoresis.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II, V are incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as during DNA fingerprinting the next step after blotting is hybridisation, Codons are common for higher and lower organisms.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102993,'biology',94,789,1698,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect matching:<br>(I) tRNA - Adapter<br>(II) Cistron - Triplet coding sequence<br>(III) Codon - Gene<br>(IV) Genetic code - Nearly universal<br>(V) Genetic code - Unambiguous<br>(VI) Gene pool - Genome<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III, VI are incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as Cistron gene, Codon - triplet, Gene pool - entire collection of genes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102994,'biology',94,793,1702,'Read the following statements about the Lac operon and select the incorrect option:<br>(I) The z-gene codes for $\\beta$-galactosidase.<br>(II) The y-gene of the lac operon codes for permease.<br>(III) In the lac operon, one regulatory gene<br>(i-gene) is present; here, the term "i" refers to the inducer.<br>(IV) Lactose is the substrate for the enzyme<br>$\\beta$-galactosidase, and it regulates switching on and off the operon.<br>(V) In the lac operon, structural genes are regulated by a common promoter and regulatory gene.<br>(VI) Lactose is the inducer.','[{"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only III is incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as in lac-operon one regulatory gene (the i gene) is present, here the term i refers to the inhibitor.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102995,'biology',94,788,1697,'Which of the following is/are incorrect with respect to the transcription unit, transcription, or post-transcription?<br>(I) hnRNA is the precursor of mRNA.<br>(II) In bacteria, transcription and translation take place in the same compartment.<br>(III) The terminator is located towards the 3\'- end (downstream) of the coding strand.<br>(IV) The promoter is located towards the 5\'end (upstream) of the coding strand.<br>(V) Apart from the promoter and terminator, additional regulatory sequences are absent upstream or downstream of the promoter.<br>(VI) RNA polymerase I is responsible for the transcription of tRNA.','[{"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only V, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'V, VI are incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as apart from promoter and terminator, additional regulatory sequences are present upstream or downstream to the promoter. RNA polymerase III is responsible for transcription of tRNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103004,'biology',94,792,1701,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect statements:<br>(I) mRNA carries genetic information.<br>(II) The untranslated regions (UTR) are required for the efficient translation process.<br>(III) tRNA was known as an adapter molecule before the genetic code was postulated.<br>(IV) In tailing, adenylate residues (200-300) are added at the 3\' end in a template independent manner.<br>(V) mRNA has a catalytic role during translation.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, V are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as follows ,the tRNA, then called sRNA (soluble RNA), was known before the genetic code was postulated. rRNA has catalytic role during translation.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102996,'biology',94,793,1702,'Select the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) In transcription, both strands of DNA are copied into RNA.<br>(II) Sometimes, the regulatory sequences are loosely defined as regulatory genes, as these sequences always code for regulatory proteins.<br>(III) DNA-dependent RNA polymerase establishes phosphodiester bonds during translation.<br>(IV) In tailing, 200-300 adenylate residues are added in a template-dependent manner.<br>(V) RNA polymerase I is responsible for the synthesis of RNA involved in splicing in bacteria.<br>(VI) The number of $\\mathrm{N}_{2}$ bases in a diploid human cell is $13.2 \\times 10^{9}$.','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only VI is correct.The incorrect statements can be corrected as.<br>(I) In transcription, only one strand of DNA is copied into RNA.<br>(II) There are additional regulatory sequences that may be present further upstream or downstream to the promoter and are not coded into proteins.<br>(III) DNA dependent RNA polymerase establishes phospho-diester bonds during transcription.<br>(IV) In tailing, 200-300 adenylate residues are added in template independent manner.<br>(V) RNA polymerase I is responsible for synthesis of rRNA (28S, 18S, and 5.8S).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102997,'biology',94,794,1703,'Identify the incorrect match from the following:<br>(I) Largest gene - Dystropin<br>(II) DNA - dependent RNA -Transcription polymerase<br>(III) SNP - 1.4 million<br>(IV) Maximum gene - Chromosome 1<br>(V) Maximum gene - Chromosome X<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Only V is incorrect match. Maximum gene - Chromosome 1 is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(102998,'biology',94,794,1703,'Select the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) SNPs help in tracing human history.<br>(II) Repetitive sequences are stretches of RNA.<br>(III) Less than $2 \\%$ of the genome codes for protein.<br>(IV) Chromosome Y has the fewest number of genes.<br>(V) A bacteriophage with radioactive DNA and protein, when infecting a bacterium, will show radioactivity inside the bacterium located in the protein.<br>(VI) AUG has dual functions.','[{"text": "I, II, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only II , V are incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as a bacteriophage with radioactive DNA and protein when infects a bacterium the radioactivity inside the bacterium will be located in DNA, Repetitive sequences are stretches of DNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103000,'biology',94,789,1698,'Read the following statements and select the false statements:<br>(I) Non-availability of tRNA for stop codon.<br>(II) The role of eukaryotic RNA polymerase I is the transcription of major rRNA transcripts.<br>(III) Nucleosome = Binding DNA + Histone Octamer + Linker DNA $+\\mathrm{H}_{1}$ histone.<br>(IV) A new DNA strand, during replication, elongates only in the 5\' to 3\' direction because Okazaki fragments prevent elongation in the 3\' to 5\' direction.<br>(V) Life began around RNA, as indicated by the fact that the process of translation has evolved around RNA.','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only IV is false. The false statements can be corrected as follows, a new DNA strand, during replication, elongates only in $5^{\\prime}$ to $3^{\\prime}$ direction because DNA polymerase can add nucleotides only at the free 3\' end.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103001,'biology',94,788,1697,'Match the Column I and Column II. https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764951747/preptracker/questions/q_103001_question_1764951746625.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,Q,T,V;}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - S,W;}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R,U}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,Q,V;}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - S,U,W;}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R,T}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - P,Q,T;}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\, {\\\\text{B - S,W;}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R,U,V}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - T,V,Q;}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\text{B - P,S,W;}}{\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} {\\\\mkern 1mu} \\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{C - R,S}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'A - P,Q,T B - S,W C - R,U,V<br>The RNA polymerase I transcribes rRNAs ( 28 S , 18S , and 5.8S), whereas the RNA polymerase III is responsible for transcription of tRNA, 5srRNA, and snRNAs (small nuclear RNAs). The RNA polymerase II transcribes precursor of mRNA, the heterogeneous nuclear RNA (hnRNA).',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103002,'biology',94,793,1702,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect statements:<br>(I) A continuous DNA strand is synthesized on the DNA template strand with polarity $5^{\\prime} \\rightarrow 3^{\\prime}$.<br>(II) In capping, an unusual nucleotide is added at the 3 \' end of hnRNA.<br>(III) A protein acquires charge depending on the abundance of amino acid residues with charged side chains.<br>(IV) <i>E. coli</i> cells with a mutated z-gene of the lac operon cannot grow in a medium containing only lactose as the source of energy because they cannot synthesize functional $\\beta$-galactosidase.','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as.<br>(I) Continous DNA strand is synthesized on DNA template strand with polarity $3^{\\prime}-5^{\\prime}$.<br>(II) In capping, an unusual nucleotide is added at 5\' end of hnRNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103003,'biology',94,795,1704,'Read the following statements and select the incorrect matching:<br>(I) Start codon \\(\\rightarrow\\) UAG<br>(II) Alec Jeffreys \\(\\rightarrow\\) PCR<br>(III) Khorana \\(\\rightarrow\\) VNTR<br>(IV) Jacob and Monod \\(\\rightarrow\\) Operon concept<br>(V) Initiation codon \\(\\rightarrow\\) AUG<br>(VI) Stop codons \\(\\rightarrow\\) UAA, UAG, UGA<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as.<br>(I) Start codon $\\rightarrow$ AUG<br>(II) Alec Jeffrey $\\rightarrow$ DNA fingerprinting<br>(III) Khorana $\\rightarrow$ homopolymer, copolymers',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103005,'biology',94,795,1704,'Read the following statements and select the false statements:<br>(I) Point mutation -A single base pair change in DNA.<br>(II) DNA fingerprinting relies on identifying minisatellites, which are repetitive coding short DNA sequences.<br>(III) The Southern blotting technique used in DNA fingerprinting involves the transfer of DNA from gel to a nylon membrane.<br>(IV) A typical nucleosome contains 200 base pairs of DNA.<br>(V) The histone octamer contains<br>2( $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{A}$, $\\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{H}_{3}, \\mathrm{H}_{4}$ ).','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'Only II is false. The false statements can be corrected as follows, DNA finger printing relies on identifying minisatellites, which are repetitive non-coding short DNA sequences.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103006,'biology',94,793,1702,'Read the following statements and select the correct statements:<br>(I) In RNA, every nucleotide residue has an additional - OH group present at the 2\' position in the ribose.<br>(II) In RNA, uracil occurs in place of 5-methyl uracil.<br>(III) The repressor of the lac operon is synthesized constitutively from the regulator gene.<br>(IV) The correct order of molecular weight is tRNA $ < $ mRNA $ < $ DNA.<br>(V) The average rate of polymerization of DNA polymerase is 2000 bp per second.<br>(VI) If two different sets of $\\mathrm{T}_{2}$ bacteriophages, after being labeled respectively with radioactive sulfur $\\left({ }^{35} \\mathrm{~S}\\right)$ and phosphorus $\\left({ }^{32} \\mathrm{P}\\right)$, are kept with $E$. coli for a few minutes and the mixture is then shaken in a blender and centrifuged, the radioactivity of ${ }^{35} \\mathrm{~S}$ will be in the supernatant, and the radioactivity of ${ }^{32} \\mathrm{P}$ will be in the <i>E. coli</i>.','[{"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV, V, VI are correct.<br>Statement (I): Correct. In RNA, each nucleotide has an additional-OH group at the 2\' position in ribose, which distinguishes it from DNA.<br>Statement (II): Correct. In RNA, uracil replaces thymine (5-methyl uracil) found in DNA.<br>Statement (III): Correct. The repressor protein in the lac operon is constitutively synthesized from the regulator gene (i-gene).<br>Statement (IV): Correct. The molecular weight order is tRNA $ < $ mRNA $ < $ DNA.<br>Statement (V):Correct. DNA polymerase has an average rate of polymerization of about 2000 base pairs per second in prokaryotes.<br>Statement (VI): Correct.<br>In the Hershey-Chase experiment, 35S labeled proteins, which remain in the supernatant, while 32P labeled DNA entered the <i>E. coli</i> cells.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103007,'biology',94,784,1689,'Which of the following is incorrect according to Griffith\'s experiments?<br>(I) S-Strain $\\rightarrow$ Injected into mice $\\rightarrow$ mice live<br>(II) R-Strain $\\rightarrow$ Injected into mice $\\rightarrow$ mice live<br>(III) S-Strain $\\rightarrow$ Injected into mice $\\rightarrow$ mice live (heat-killed)<br>(IV) Heat killed S-Strain + R-Strain $\\rightarrow$ Injected into mice $\\rightarrow$ mice die.','[{"text": "I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'S-Strain $\\rightarrow$ Injected into mice $\\rightarrow$ mice live is incorrect.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103008,'biology',94,789,1698,'TMV infects a variety of plants, including <i>Zinnia</i> and tobacco. When TMV-RNA is used for infection, the amino acid sequence of the coat protein of the progeny is the same whether the host is <i>Zinnia</i> or tobacco. This proves that the genetic code is:<br>(I) Degenerate<br>(II) Universal<br>(III) Ambiguous<br>(IV) Non-overlapping','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The genetic code is universal.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103009,'biology',94,794,1703,'Select the incorrect statements about HGP (Human Genome Project):<br>(I) Less than $2 \\%$ of the genome codes for protein.<br>(II) The functions are unknown for over $50 \\%$ of the discovered genes.<br>(III) Repetitive sequences make up a very large portion of the human genome.<br>(IV) Chromosome 1 has the fewest genes (231).','[{"text": "Only I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Only II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'IV is incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as follows Chromosome Y has fewest genes (231).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103010,'biology',94,794,1703,'Select the incorrect option about HGP (Human Genome Project):<br>(I) One approach focused on identifying all the genes that are expressed as RNA, referred to as Expressed Sequence Tags (ESTs).<br>(II) Another approach was sequencing the whole genome, which contained all coding and non-coding sequences, and later assigning different regions in the sequence with functions.<br>(III) For sequencing, the total DNA from each and every cell is isolated and converted into random fragments of relatively smaller sizes.<br>(IV) The commonly used hosts were bacteria and yeast.<br>(V) The vectors used were BAC (Bacillus Artificial Chromosomes) and YAC (Yeast Artificial Chromosomes).','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, V are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as for sequencing, the total DNA from a cell is isolated and converted into random fragments of relatively smaller sizes. The vectors were called as BAC (bacterial artificial chromosomes), and YAC (yeast artificial chromosomes).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103011,'biology',94,784,1689,'Read the following statements and select the correct statements from the following.<br>(I) In Griffith\'s experiment, when S strain of bacteria is injected into mice $\\rightarrow$ Mice died, and when R strain is injected into mice $\\rightarrow$ Mice live.<br>(II) Two nucleotides are linked through a 5\' -3\' phosphodiester bond.<br>(III) The pitch of the DNA helix is 3.4 $ \\mathop {\\rm{A}}^{\\circ}  $.<br>(IV) The total number of nitrogenous bases with glycosidic linkages in bacteriophage $\\varphi \\times 174$ is 5386.<br>(V) The average rate of polymerization of DNA polymerase is 2000 bp per second.<br>(VI) The stability of the DNA helical structure is conferred by hydrogen bonds, and the plane of one base pair stacks over the other.','[{"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, IV, V, VI are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Two nucleotides are linked through 3\'- 5\' phosphodiester linkage to form a dinucleotide. The pitch of the helix is 3.4 nm .',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103012,'biology',94,795,1704,'Read the following and select the incorrect match:<br>(I) SSR / Microsatellite - 15-20 bp<br>(II) Methionine - AUG<br>(III) Southern Blotting - Nitrocellulose membrane<br>(IV) Meselson and Stahl - Regulation of gene expression<br>(V) Chromosome number 1-2968 genes in humans<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, IV are incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as SSR / microsatellite - refers to a short segment of DNA, usually one to six or more base pairs in length, Meselson and Stahl - semi conservative replication of DNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103013,'biology',94,789,1698,'Read the following statements and select the false statements:<br>(I) In prokaryotic cells, charging of tRNA occurs in the cytoplasm.<br>(II) Each intron is a set of three terminator codons.<br>(III) Exons are present in eukaryotes, but introns are present in prokaryotes.<br>(IV) Introns are present in mRNA, while exons are present in tRNA.<br>(V) Out of 64 codons, 61 code for 20 types of amino acids. This is due to the degeneracy of the genetic code.','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, III, IV are false. The false statements can be corrected as follows, UAA, UGA, UAG are three terminator codons, Exons and introns are present in eukaryotes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103014,'biology',94,788,1697,'Read the following statements and select the correct option:<br>(I) The complementary sequence of a genetic codon is present on tRNA.<br>(II) RNA polymerase II catalyzes the formation of the most abundant RNA in the cell.<br>(III) The primary transcript undergoes splicing for the removal of exons.<br>(IV) Mature mRNA contains multiple adenylate residues at its 3\' end.<br>(V) Synthesis of RNA occurs in the nucleus of an animal cell.','[{"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, IV, V are correct.The incorrect statements can be corrected as primary transcript undergoes splicing for the removal of introns, The RNA polymerase II transcribes precursor of mRNA, the heterogeneous nuclear RNA (hnRNA).',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103015,'biology',94,789,1698,'Read the following and select the correct matching:<br>(I) Predominance of the RNA world hypothesis - Splicing.<br>(II) Point mutation - Change in a single pentose sugar of DNA.<br>(III) Severo Ochoa - DNA polymerase.<br>(IV) DNA template with 3\'-5\' polarity Continuous replication of DNA.<br>(V) Anticodons - mRNA.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, IV are correct.The incorrect statements can be corrected as Point mutation - change in a single base pair of DNA, Severo Ochoa enzyme (polynucleotide phosphorylase), Anticodons -<br>t-RNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103016,'biology',94,788,1695,'Read the following statements and select the statements that are true:<br>(I) Both strands of DNA are not copied during transcription because, if both strands acted as templates, they would code for RNA molecules with different sequences. The two RNA molecules, if produced simultaneously, would be complementary to each other and form a double-stranded RNA.<br>(II) The most abundant RNA in the cell is rRNA.<br>(III) DNA is chemically and structurally more stable compared to RNA due to the presence of thymine instead of uracil.<br>(IV) The heavy/radioactive isotope ${ }^{35} \\mathrm{~S}$ is not suitable for DNA labeling in studies.','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV are correct. All are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103017,'biology',94,793,1702,'Read the following statements and select the correct statements:<br>(I) Permease increases the permeability of the cell for $\\beta$-galactosidase.<br>(II) Regulation of transcription is the only step for the regulation of gene expression in eukaryotes.<br>(III) The UTRs (untranslated regions) are present at both the 5 \' end (before the start codon) and the 3 \' end (after the stop codon).<br>(IV) If a hybrid DNA molecule is allowed to replicate three times in a medium containing<br>${ }^{14} \\mathrm{~N}$, the percentage of hybrid DNA after the third replication will be $12.5 \\%$.','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as follows<br>(I) Permease increase the permeability of cell for b-galactoside.<br>(II) In eukaryotes, the regulation could be exerted at transcriptional level, processing level, transport of mRNA from nucleus to the cytoplasm, translational level.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103018,'biology',94,793,1702,'Read the following statements and select the correct statements:<br>(I) The z gene codes for $\\beta$-galactosidase.<br>(II) Codons are present on tRNA and recognize the anticodon of mRNA.<br>(III) The triplet code was proposed by Khorana.<br>(IV) Operons are found in bacteria.','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as follows<br>(II) Anticodon are present on tRNA and recognises codon of mRNA<br>(III) Triplet code was proposed by George Gamow.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103019,'biology',94,788,1697,'Find the correct statement with respect to transcription:<br>(I) Elongation is controlled by the sigma factor.<br>(II) Alteration of the specificity of RNA polymerase is due to the association of factors during transcription.<br>(III) There is a single DNA-dependent RNA polymerase that catalyzes the transcription of all types of RNA in viruses.<br>(IV) The rho factor terminates transcription when it associates with the DNA polymerase enzyme.','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II is correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as follows.<br>(I) Initiation is controlled by sigma factor.<br>(III) There is single DNA dependent RNA polymerase that catalyses transcription of all type of RNA in bacterial cell.<br>(IV) Rho factor terminates the transcription, when it associates with RNA polymerase enzyme<br>',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103021,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Read the following statements and select the correct option<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Biocontrol refers to the use of biological methods for controlling plant diseases and pests</div><div class="column-right"><i>Trichoderma</i> species are effective bio control agents for several plant pathogens</div></div>','[{"text": "Statements A and B are correct.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statements A and B are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Statements A and B are correct. Statement A is correct: Biocontrol means using living organisms like microbes, insects, etc., to control pests and plant diseases.<br>Statement B is correct: <i>Trichoderma</i> species\nare well-known biocontrol agents against several plant pathogens, especially in soil.',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103022,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Match the Column-I with Column-II. Choose the correct option given below https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764951748/preptracker/questions/q_103022_question_1764951748136.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A-S, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-R, C-S, D-P", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-S, B-R, C-P, D-Q", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q,B-R, C-S, D-P<br>(A) <i>Streptococcus</i> → (Q) Clot buster<br>(B) <i>Penicillium</i> → (R) Source of antibiotic<br>(C) Methanogens → (S) Biogas production<br>(D) <i>Anabaena</i> → (P) Free living nitrogen fixing bacteria',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103023,'biology',96,1159,2772,'Which of the following microbes is not involved in the preparation of household products?<br>A. <i>Aspergillus niger</i><br>B. <i>Lactobacillus</i><br>C. <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i><br>D. <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i><br>E. <i>Propionibacterium sharmanii</i><br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "C and E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A and C only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br><i>Lactobacillus</i> is used for production of curd. <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i> is used for the fermentation in bakery and brewery. <i>Propionibacterium sharmanii</i> is used for production of swiss cheese. <i>Aspergillus niger</i> is used for the commercial production of citric acid. <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i> is used for the production of cyclosporin A and also act as a\nbiocontrol agent. A,C are used in industrial production of citric acid and cyclosporin-A',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103024,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Streptokinase produced by bacterium <i>Streptococcus</i> is used for','[{"text": "Removing clots from blood vessels", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Curd production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ethanol production", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Liver disease treatment", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Streptokinase, produced by <i>Streptococcus</i> and modified genetically, is used as a clot buster. It helps dissolve blood clots in patients with myocardial infarction (heart attack). Curd production is done by <i>Lactobacillus</i> and ethanol production is done by <i>Saccharomyces</i>',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103025,'biology',96,1160,2773,'Which of the following is an example of non-distilled alcoholic beverage produced by yeast?','[{"text": "Rum", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Whisky", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Brandy", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Beer", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The correct answer is option 4.<br>Beer is a non-distilled alcoholic beverage produced by the fermentation of cereals using yeast (e.g., <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i>). In contrast, whisky, rum, and brandy are distilled products.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103026,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Which of following organisms cannot fix nitrogen?<br>A. <i>Azotobacter</i> B. <i>Oscillatoria</i><br>C. <i>Anabaena</i> D. <i>Volvox</i><br>E. <i>Nostoc</i><br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "E only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "B only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br><i>Azotobacter, Oscillatoria, Anabaena</i>, and <i>Nostoc</i> are all nitrogen-fixing organisms. <i>Volvox</i>, a colonial green alga, does not fix nitrogen.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103027,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Identify the incorrect statement(s) from the following:<br>(I) An immunosuppressive agent used in organ transplant patients is Cyclosporine A, and it is produced by <i>Monascus purpureus</i>.<br>(II) ‘Toddy’, a traditional drink in some parts of southern India, is made by fermenting sap from palm trees.<br>(III) Once the BOD of sewage or waste water increases significantly, the effluent is then passed into a settling tank, where bacterial \'flocs\' are allowed to sediment.<br>(IV) Microbial biocontrol agents that can be introduced to control butterfly caterpillars include the bacterium <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> (often written as Bt ).<br>(V) <i>Methanobacterium</i> is commonly found in aerobic sludge during sewage treatment.<br>(VI) The Ministry of Environment and Forests has initiated the Ganga Action Plan and Yamuna Action Plan to save these major rivers of our country from pollution.','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, III, V are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as An immunosuppressive agent used in organ transplant patient is Cyclosporin A and is produced by <i>Trichoderma</i>. Once the BOD of sewage or waste water is reduced significantly, the effluent is then passed into a settling tank where the bacterial \'flocs\' are allowed to sediment. <i>Methanobacterium</i> are commonly found in the anaerobic sludge during sewage treatment.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103028,'biology',96,1160,2774,'Alexander Fleming, while working on a (A) once observed a mould growing in one of his unwashed culture plates around which (B) could not grow. He found that it was due to a chemical produced by the mould and he named it (C) after the (D). The blanks can be filled by:','[{"text": "(A) fungus<br>(B) <i>Trichoderma</i><br>(C) Cyclosporin A<br>(D) bacteria <i>Penicillium notatum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(A) bacterium<br>(B) <i>Trichoderma</i><br>(C) Penicillin<br>(D) mould <i>Penicillium notatum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(A) bacterium<br>(B) <i>Streptococcus</i><br>(C) Streptomycin<br>(D) bacteria <i>Penicillium notatum</i>", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "(A) bacterium<br>(B) <i>Staphylococcus</i><br>(C) Penicillin<br>(D) mould <i>Penicillium notatum</i>", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Alexander fleming while working on a bacterium once observed a mould growing in one of his unwashed culture plates around which <i>Staphylococcus</i> could not grow. He found that it was due to a chemical produced by the mould and he named it penicillin after the <i>Penicillium notatum</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103029,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Match the column I and Column II: https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764958010/preptracker/questions/q_103029_question_1764958010162.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{T}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{Q}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{R}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$\\\\mathrm{A}-\\\\mathrm{R}, \\\\mathrm{B}-\\\\mathrm{S}, \\\\mathrm{C}-\\\\mathrm{T}, \\\\mathrm{D}-\\\\mathrm{P}, \\\\mathrm{E}-\\\\mathrm{Q}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'$\\mathrm{A}-\\mathrm{R}, \\mathrm{B}-\\mathrm{S}, \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{P}, \\mathrm{D}-\\mathrm{T}, \\mathrm{E}-\\mathrm{Q}$ is correct',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103030,'biology',96,1160,2773,'Match the column I and Column II: https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764958012/preptracker/questions/q_103030_question_1764958012140.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "${\\\\text{A  -  P,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{Q }}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B  -  R, S, T}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - R,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{S}}\\\\quad \\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{T}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - S,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{R}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{Q,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{T}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${\\\\text{A - S,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{R}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{B - P,}}\\\\,{\\\\text{Q,T}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A- P, Q, B- R, S, T is correct',NULL,'Medium','Match the following',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103031,'biology',96,1162,2777,'Identify the correct statement(s) from the following:<br>(I) Lactic acid bacteria (LAB) convert curd into milk.<br>(II) The full potential of Penicillin as an antibiotic was established by Chain and Florey.<br>(III) An immunosuppressive agent used in organ transplant patients is Cyclosporin A, and it is produced by the bacterium <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>.<br>(IV) Roquefort cheese is ripened by growing a specific bacteria on it.<br>(V) Primary treatment involves the physical removal of particles - large and small - from sewage through filtration and sedimentation.<br>(VI) The primary effluent is passed into large aeration tanks, where it is constantly agitated mechanically.','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, V, VI are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Lactic acid bacteria (LAB) produce acids that coagulate and partially digest milk proteins, An immunosuppressive agent used in organ transplant patient is Cyclosporin A and is produced by fungi <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>. The \'Roquefort cheese\' are ripened by growing a specific fungi on them.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103032,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Identify the blank spaces A, B, C and D and select the correct answer: <img src=\'/img/data/biology/96_103032_qtext_1.png\' alt=\'Question Image\' style=\'max-width:100%;\' />','[{"text": "A - <i>Lactobacillus</i>, B - <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>,<br>C - Bacterium, D - Penicillin.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A - <i>Staphylococcus</i>, B - <i>Clostridium</i>, C - yeast,<br>D - Penicillin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - <i>Lactobacillus</i>, B - <i>Microsporum</i>, C - Yeast,<br>D - Penicilin.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - <i>Staphylococcus</i>, B - <i>Microsporum</i>,<br>C - Bacterium, D - Penicillin.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'A - <i>Lactobacillus</i>, B - <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>, C - Bacterium, D - Penicillin',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103033,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Identify the correct option from the following:<br>(I) <i>Anabaena, Nostoc, Oscillatoria</i> are nitrogen fixers.<br>(II) The technology of biogas production was developed in India mainly due to the efforts of Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI) and Khadi and Village Industries Commission (KVIC).<br>(III) The biogas plant consists of a concrete tank (10-15 feet deep) in which biowastes are collected, and a slurry of dung is fed.<br>(IV) Cyanobacteria are autotrophic eukaryotes.<br>(V) <i>Azospirillum</i> and <i>Azotobacter</i> are free-living nitrogen fixers.','[{"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, V are correct. The incorrect ones can be corrected as cyanobacteria are autotrophic eukaryotes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103034,'biology',96,1160,2775,'Identify the correct option from the following:<br>(I) Plague - Viral disease<br>(II) Whooping cough - Kali khansi<br>(III) <i>Aspergillus butylicum</i> - A bacterium<br>(IV) Leprosy - Kusht rog<br>(V) <i>Acetobacter aceti</i> - A bacterium<br>(VI) Diphtheria - Gal ghotu','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'II, IV, V, VI are correct. The incorrect options can be corrected as plague- bacterial disease, <i>Aspergillus</i> niger - a fungus <i>Clostridium butylicum</i> - a bacterium',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103035,'biology',96,1163,2778,'Identify the correct option with respect to biological control of insects/pests:<br>(I) Organic farmers work to create a system where pests are not eradicated but kept at manageable levels.<br>(II) Ladybird and Dragonflies are useful to get rid of mosquitoes and aphids, respectively.<br>(III) Baculovirus can have a negative impact on plants, mammals, and birds.<br>(IV) Baculovirus kills both useful and harmful organisms indiscriminately.<br>(V) The method is more harmful as compared with the use of chemical pesticides.<br>(VI) Baculoviruses are excellent candidates for species-specific, broad spectrum insecticidal applications. <br>(VII) <i>Trichoderma</i> species are symbiotic fungi that are very common in root ecosystem','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, VII", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only I", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only I is correct.The incorrect statements can be corrected as Ladybird, and Dragonflies are useful to get rid of aphids and mosquitoes. Baculoviruses are excellent candidates for species-specific, narrow spectrum insecticidal applications. <i>Trichoderma</i> species are free living fungi that are very common in the root ecosystems.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103107,'biology',100,558,1116,'Find the incorrect statement from the following about colostrum:<br>(I) It is not healthy for the baby.<br>(II) It is thick in nature.<br>(III) It is the first milk produced after childbirth.<br>(IV) It contains IgA.<br>(V) It is white in color and is produced during the first pregnancy only.<br>Options:','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, V are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as colostrum is very healthy for the baby and is yellowish in colour and produced in the start of all lactation post all pregnancies.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103036,'biology',96,1160,2775,'(i) Bacterium ____ (A) ____ produce commercial product called lactic acid.<br>(ii) A fungus ____ (B) ____ produce cyclosporin A.<br>(iii) _____ (C) _____ <i>(Monascus purpureus)<i/> produce statins.<br>(iv) A fungus <i>(Penicillium notatum)<i/> produce _____ (D) _____.','[{"text": "A - <i>Lactobacillus</i>,<br>B - <i>Trichoderma</i>,<br>C - <i>Agaricus</i>(Fungus),<br>D-Penicillin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - <i>Lactobacillus</i>,<br>B - <i>Trichoderma</i>,<br>C - Yeast (Algae),<br>D - Penicillin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - <i>Lactobacillus</i>,<br>B - <i>Trichoderma</i>,<br>C - Yeast (Prokaryote),<br>D-Penicillin", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - <i>Lactobacillus</i>,<br>B - <i>Trichoderma</i>,<br>C - Yeast (Fungus),<br>D-Penicillin", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'(i) Bacterium <i>Lactobacillus</i> produce commercial product called lactic acid.(ii) A fungus <i>Trichoderma</i> produce (cyclosporin A).(iii) Yeast (Fungus) (<i>Monascus purpureus</i>) produce statins.(iv) A fungus (<i>Penicilium notatum</i>) produce Penicillin.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103037,'biology',96,1161,2776,'Identify the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) Microbes are used to ferment fish, soyabean, and bamboo shoots to make foods.<br>(II) The large holes in \'Swiss cheese\' are due to the production of a large amount of $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ by a bacterium named <i>Propionibacterium sharmanii</i>.<br>(III) Different varieties of cheese are known by their characteristic texture, flavour, and taste, the specificity coming from the microbes used.<br>(IV) Antibiotics are used to treat viral, fungal, and bacterial diseases.<br>(V) The municipal waste water is called sewage.','[{"text": "I,II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as antibiotics are used to treat bacterial diseases.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103038,'biology',96,1161,2776,'Identify the correct statements about STP (Sewage Treatment Plant):<br>(I) Treatment of waste water - heterotrophic bacteria<br>(II) Primary treatment - no bacteria<br>(III) Tertiary treatment - anaerobic bacteria<br>(IV) Secondary treatment - autotrophs<br>(V) Secondary treatment - fungi as a part of flocs','[{"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as flocs (masses of bacteria associated with fungal filaments to form mesh like structures) are used in secondary treatment.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103039,'biology',96,1162,2777,'Identify the incorrect statements about biogas:<br>(I) Certain bacteria, which grow aerobically on cellulosic material, produce large amounts of methane along with $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{H}_{2}$.<br>(II) <i>Methanobacterium</i> is used in biogas production.<br>(III) These bacteria are archaebacteria.<br>(IV) These bacteria are commonly found in the anaerobic sludge during sewage treatment.<br>(V) In the omasum of ruminants, these bacteria help in the breakdown of cellulose.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, V are incorrect. The incorrect statement can be corrected as certain bacteria, which grow anaerobically on cellulosic material, produce large amount of methane along with $\\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{H}_{2}$. A lot of cellulosic material present in the food of cattle is also present in the rumen. In rumen, these bacteria help in the breakdown of cellulose and play an important role in the nutrition of cattle.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103040,'biology',96,1164,2779,'Identify the correct statements about mycorrhizae:<br>(I) Fungal association with roots of higher plants are known as mycorrhizae.<br>(II) It is a type of mutual association called commensalism.<br>(III) <i>Glomus</i> is one such fungus involved in this association.<br>(IV) Plants having such associations are resistant to root-borne pathogens, and tolerant to salinity and drought.<br>(V) Plants having such associations show an increase in plant growth and development.','[{"text": "I, II,III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, V only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as it is a mutual association called symbiosis.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103041,'biology',97,1199,2861,'Match the following contents of Column-I with Column-II https://res.cloudinary.com/doe6oiv2h/image/upload/v1764951750/preptracker/questions/q_103041_question_1764951749676.png<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "A-Q, B-P, C-R, D-S", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A-S, B-Q, C-R, D-P", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-P, B-Q, C-S, D-R", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'A-Q, B-S, C-P, D-R<br>(A) Bioreactors → (Q) Vessels which convert raw material into specific product<br>(B) Downstream processing → (S) Involves separation and purification<br>(C) Recombinant protein → (P) Insulin produced by rDNA technology<br>(D) PCR → (R) Detect mutated genes in suspected cancer patient',NULL,'Hard','Match the following',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103042,'biology',97,1194,2856,'The part of plasmid that codes for proteins involved in the replication of the pBR322 Plasmid is','[{"text": "cloning site", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Ori site", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Selectable marker", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "“rop”", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'The “rop” (repressor of primer) region in pBR322 plasmid is involved in regulation of plasmid replication. It codes for proteins that help in the initiation and control of plasmid copy number.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103043,'biology',97,1196,2858,'To isolate DNA form fungal cells, bacterial cells and plant cells, the enzymes required are respectively','[{"text": "Cellulase, Protease and Lysozyme", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysozyme, Cellulase and Chitinase", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Lysozyme, Proteases and Ribonuclease", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Chitinase, Lysozyme and Cellulase", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'To isolate DNA from different cells, specific enzymes are used to break their cell walls:<br>Fungal cells → Chitinase (breaks chitin)<br>Bacterial cells → Lysozyme (breaks peptidoglycan)<br>Plant cells → Cellulase (breaks cellulose)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103220,'biology',102,772,1677,'Which of the following statements/ options are correct:<br>(I) Haldane - England.<br>(II) Spontaneous generation theory - Life came from dead, decaying rotting matter.<br>(III) Oparin - France.<br>(IV) Theory of biogenesis - Life came from pre-existing life.<br>(V) Modern theory - Life came from nonliving organic molecule.','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statement can be corrected as Oparin - Russia.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103044,'biology',97,1193,2855,'Given below are two statements :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The DNA fragments extracted from gel electrophoresis can be used in construction of recombinant DNA</div><div class="column-right">Smaller size DNA fragments are observed near anode while larger fragments are found near the wells in an agarose gel.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is incorrect but statement B is correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statement A and statement B are correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statement A and statement B are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>Statement A: Correct – DNA fragments separated by gel electrophoresis can be extracted (eluted) and used in the construction of recombinant DNA.<br>Statement B: Correct – In agarose gel electrophoresis, smaller DNA fragments move faster and farther towards the anode, while larger fragments remain near the wells',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103045,'biology',97,1194,2856,'The blue and white selectable markers have been developed which differentiate recombinant colonies from non-recombinant colonies on the basis of their ability to produce colour in the presence of a chromogenic substrate.<br>Given below are two statements about this method:<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">The blue coloured colonies have DNA insert in the plasmid and they are identified as recombinant colonies.</div><div class="column-right">The colonies without blue colour have DNA insert in the plasmid and are identified as recombinant colonies.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given\nbelow:</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is incorrect but Statement B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both Statement A and Statement B are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but Statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct answer is option 1.<br>Statement A: Incorrect – Blue colonies indicate functional $\\beta $-galactosidase; no insert is present.<br>Statement B: Correct – White colonies result from insertional inactivation of the $\\beta $-galactosidase gene, indicating the presence of the DNA insert',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103046,'biology',97,1193,2854,'Which of the following enzyme(s) are not essential for gene cloning?<br>A. Restriction enzymes<br>B. DNA ligase<br>C. DNA mutase<br>D. DNA recombinase<br>E. DNA polymerase<br>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:','[{"text": "B and C only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "D and E only", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>Essential enzymes for gene cloning include:<br>Restriction enzymes (A) – cut DNA at specific sites<br>DNA ligase (B) – joins DNA fragments<br>DNA polymerase (E) – amplifies or synthesizes DNA<br>DNA mutase (C) and DNA recombinase (D) are not essential for standard gene cloning procedures.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103048,'biology',97,1197,2859,'Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) amplifies DNA following the equation','[{"text": "${{\\\\text{N}}^{\\\\text{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$2\\\\,{{\\\\text{N}}^{\\\\text{2}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "${{\\\\text{2}}^{\\\\text{n}}}$", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "${\\\\text{2n + 1}}$", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'The correct answer is option 3.<br>PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) amplifies DNA exponentially.<br>After n cycles, the number of DNA copies = ${{\\text{2}}^{\\text{n}}}$. For example, after 3 cycles $ \\to $ ${{\\text{2}}^3}$ = 8 copies $ \\to $ Option (3)',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103051,'biology',97,1194,2856,'Find the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) Electrophoresis is a technique used for the separation of substances based on their size and charge.<br>(II) In EcoRI, the Roman numeral I indicates that it was the first enzyme isolated from $E. coli$ Ry13.<br>(III) It is not advisable to use an exonuclease enzyme while producing a recombinant DNA molecule.<br>(IV) Plasmids are extra-chromosomal, self replicating, usually circular, double-stranded DNA molecules found naturally in many bacteria.<br>(V) Restriction endonucleases are the most widely used enzymes in recombinant DNA technology. They are obtained from bacteriophages and are prokaryotes.','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "V only", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'V only is incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Restriction endonucleases are most widely used in recombinant DNA technology. They are obtained from bacterial cells and are prokaryotes.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103053,'biology',97,1199,2861,'Find the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) The characteristic generally not preferred for a cloning vector is multiple restriction sites.<br>(II) The characteristic generally preferred for a cloning vector is an antibiotic resistance marker.<br>(III) The characteristic generally not preferred for a cloning vector is the origin of replication.<br>(IV) Any protein-encoding gene that is expressed in a heterologous host is called a recombinant protein.<br>(V) Bioreactors are useful in the processing of large volumes of culture.<br>(VI) Downstream processing and quality control testing are the same for all products.','[{"text": "I, II, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as the characteristics generally preferred for a cloning vector is an origin of replication. The downstream processing and quality control testing vary from product to product.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103054,'biology',97,1197,2859,'Which statements are true for the <i>Taq</i> polymerase enzyme?<br>(I) It is a type of RNA polymerase that is isolated from bacteria.<br>(II) DNA polymerase is used in gel electrophoresis.<br>(III) DNA polymerase remains active at high temperatures.<br>(IV) DNA polymerase is used in DNA isolation.<br>(V) DNA polymerase is isolated from an archaebacterium.','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'III, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as <i>Taq</i>-polymerase is a DNA polymerase, isolated from an archaebacteria, used in PCR.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(106539,'chemistry',58,169,371,'Solubility of a gas in a liquid increases with','[{"text": "Increase of P and decrease of T", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Decrease of P and decrease of T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Increase of P and increase of T", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Decrease of P and increase of T", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Solubility of gas in a liquid increases with increase of pressure $(\\mathrm{P})$ and decrease of temperature (T).',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2022,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103055,'biology',97,1194,2856,'Find the correct statements with respect to the following statements:<br>(I) The colonies of recombinant bacteria appear white, in contrast to the blue colonies of nonrecombinant bacteria, due to insertional inactivation of the $\\beta$-galactosidase gene in recombinant bacteria.<br>(II) The larger the DNA fragment size, the farther it moves in gel electrophoresis.<br>(III) Nowadays, the most commonly used matrix in gel electrophoresis is agarose, which is a synthetic polymer extracted from seaweeds.<br>(IV) DNA fragments separate (resolve) according to their size through the sieving effect provided by agarose gel.<br>(V) Pure DNA cannot be seen under UV light without staining.<br>(VI) EcoRI produces blunt ends.','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, IV, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as smaller the fragment size of DNA, the farther it moves. Now - a - days the most commonly used matrix is agarose which is a natural polymer extracted from sea weeds. EcoRI produce sticky end.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103056,'biology',97,1193,2854,'Find out correct recognition sequence of following restriction endonuclease enzyme:','[{"text": "$BamHI\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,EcoRI$<br>$\\\\begin{gathered}\\n  \\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{GGATCC}}} \\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{GAATTC}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\, \\\\hfill \\\\\\\\\\n  {\\\\text{CCTAGG}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{CTTAAG}} \\\\hfill \\\\\\\\ \\n\\\\end{gathered} $", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "$BamHI\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,EcoRI$<br>${{\\\\text{GAATCAA}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{TTGCAAC}}}$<br>${{\\\\text{CTTAGTT}}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,{\\\\text{AACGTTG}}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$BamHI\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,EcoRI$<br>${\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{GGATCC}}} \\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{AGCTCC}}} \\n\\\\end{array}}$<br>${\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{CCTAGG}}} \\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{TCGAGG}}} \\n\\\\end{array}}$", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "$BamHI\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,EcoRI$<br>$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{GACTAA}}} \\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{GCCTTA}}} \\n\\\\end{array}} \\n\\\\end{array}}&{} \\n\\\\end{array}$<br>$\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{CTGATT}}} \\n\\\\end{array}} \\n\\\\end{array}\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\,\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {\\\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\\n  {{\\\\text{CGGAAT}}} \\n\\\\end{array}} \\n\\\\end{array}}&{} \\n\\\\end{array}$", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Bam HI</i> - <i>EcoRI</i><br>GGATCC - GAATTC<br>CCTAGG - CTTAAG<br>Option (1) is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103057,'biology',97,1194,2856,'Find the incorrect statements from the following statements:<br>(I) The tumor-inducing (Ti) plasmid of <i>Agrobacterium tumefaciens</i> has now been modified into a cloning vector, which is more pathogenic to plants.<br>(II) The same kind of sticky ends are produced when a DNA molecule is cut by different restriction enzymes.<br>(III) Plasmid DNA acts as a vector to transfer the piece of DNA attached to it.<br>(IV) The construction of the first recombinant DNA emerged from the possibility of linking a gene encoding antibiotic resistance with a native plasmid of <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>.<br>(V) A bacteriophage has the ability to replicate within bacterial cells by integrating its DNA with bacterial DNA, even in the presence of restriction endonucleases.<br>(VI) Hind II was the first restriction endonuclease to be isolated.','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, II, V are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as The tumor inducing (Ti) plasmid of <i>Agrobacterium tumifaciens</i> has now been modified into a cloning vector which is no more pathogenic to the plants, Same kind of sticky ends are produced when a DNA has been cut by same restriction enzymes.A bacteriophage has the ability to replicate within bacterial cells by integrating its DNA with bacterial DNA, in the absence of restriction endonuclease. Endonucleases makes cuts at specific position within the DNA.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103058,'biology',97,1194,2856,'Find the incorrect statements from the following statements:<br>(I) The origin of replication (ori) is responsible for controlling the copy number of the linked DNA.<br>(II) In the year 1968, the two enzymes responsible for restricting the growth of bacteriophages in <i>Escherichia coli</i> were isolated.<br>(III) The separated bands of DNA, cut out from the agarose gel and extracted from the gel piece, is known as spooling.<br>(IV) Each restriction endonuclease recognizes a specific palindromic nucleotide sequence in DNA.<br>(V) Transformation is a procedure through which a piece of RNA is introduced into a host bacterium. The vector requires a selectable marker, which helps in identifying and eliminating non-transformants, selectively permitting the growth of transformants.<br>(VI) The stickiness of DNA ends facilitates the action of DNA ligase.','[{"text": "I, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, V", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'II, III, V are incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as in the year 1963, the two enzymes responsible for restricting the growth of bacteriophage in <i>Escherichia</i> coli were isolated.The separated bands of DNA cut out from the agarose gel and extracted from the gel piece is known as elution. Transformation is a procedure through which a piece of DNA is introduced in a host bacterium.the vector requires a selectable marker, which helps in identifying and eliminating nontransformants and selectively permitting the growth of the transformants.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103059,'biology',97,1193,2854,'Which is the palindromic nucleotide sequence?<br>$\\left( {\\text{I}} \\right){\\text{ GAATTC }}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\text{CTTAAG}}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {\\left( {{\\text{II}}} \\right){\\text{ AGGCCT}}}&{\\,\\,\\,{\\text{TCCGGA}}} \n\\end{array}$<br>$\\begin{array}{*{20}{l}}\n  {\\left( {{\\text{III}}} \\right){\\text{ CAGTCG}}}&{\\,\\,{\\text{GTCAGC}}} \n\\end{array}$','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I and II is correct. (I) GATTC CTTAAG<br>(II) AGGCCT TCCGGA, these are correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103108,'biology',100,558,1116,'Find the correct statement from the following:<br>(I) Identical twins are monozygotic.<br>(II) Identical twins are formed from two eggs and two sperms.<br>(III) The myometrium exhibits strong contractions during parturition.<br>(IV) Colostrum contains IgA, which provides passive immunity to the newborn.<br>(V) The opening of the cervix is often partially covered by a membrane called the hymen.<br>Options:','[{"text": "III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV are correct.The incorrect statements can be corrected as the opening of vagina is often covered partially by a membrane called hymen. Identical twins are formed from one egg and one sperm.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103060,'biology',97,1199,2861,'Find the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) If any protein-encoding gene is expressed in a homologous host, it is called a recombinant protein.<br>(II) In elution, the separated bands of DNA are cut out from agarose gel and extracted from the gel piece.<br>(III) Competent bacterial cells cannot take up the plasmid.<br>(IV) Downstream processing and quality control testing vary from product to product.<br>(V) Restriction endonucleases are used in genetic engineering for ligating two DNA molecules.<br>(VI) The <i>E. coli</i> cloning vector pBR322 has Ori, antibiotic resistance genes, rop, and several restriction sites.','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, III, V are incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as If any protein encoding gene is expressed in a heterologous host is called recombinant protein, Competent bacterial cells can take up the plasmid. Restriction endonucleases are used in genetic engineering for breaking phosphodiester bonds in DNA molecules.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103061,'biology',97,1197,2859,'Find the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) Primers are small chemically synthesized oligonucleotides.<br>(II) DNA polymerase is isolated from <i>Thermus aquaticus</i>.<br>(III) Sal I is a selectable marker on the plasmid of <i>Salmonella typhimurium</i>.<br>(IV) Hind III is a restriction site on pBR322.<br>(V) Rop codes for a protein involved in the replication of the plasmid.<br>(VI) Ori is responsible for controlling the copy number of linked DNA.','[{"text": "I, IV, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, IV, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'III is incorrect.The incorrect option can be corrected as Sal I - restriction sites on <i>E. coli</i> cloning vector pBR322.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103062,'biology',97,1194,2856,'Find the correct statements from the following statements:<br>(I) In the naming of restriction endonucleases, the Roman numeral indicates the order of discovery.<br>(II) In gel electrophoresis, the separated DNA fragments are visualized after staining with ethidium bromide, followed by exposure to UV radiation.<br>(III) A foreign DNA fragment is inserted at the Cla I site of pBR322. This recombinant vector is introduced into <i>Escherichia coli</i>. The transformed cells are grown on two different media, one containing ampicillin and the other containing tetracycline. The recombinant bacteria will not grow on either tetracycline or ampicillin-containing media.<br>(IV) A foreign DNA fragment is inserted at the Cla I site of pBR322. This recombinant vector is introduced into <i>Escherichia coli</i>. The transformed cells are grown on two different media, one containing ampicillin and the other containing tetracycline. The recombinant bacteria will grow on both tetracycline and ampicillin-containing media.','[{"text": "I, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'II, IV are correct. The incorrect statements can be corrected as Roman numbers following the names indicate the order in which the enzymes were isolated from that strain of bacteria. Some foreign DNA fragment is attached to Cla I site of pBR 322. This recombinant vector in used to transition <i>Escherichia coli</i>. Then on two different media, one containing ampicillin and the other containing tetracycline. The transformed cells containing the recombinant vector will grow on both, tetracycline and ampicillin containing media.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103063,'biology',97,1197,2859,'Find the incorrect statements from the following:<br>(I) The definition given by EFB (European Federation of Biotechnology) is as follows: "The integration of natural sciences and organisms, cells, parts thereof, and molecular analogues for products and services."<br>(II) Bacterial colonies that have a foreign DNA fragment inserted into the plasmid will appear colourless, because the $\\beta$-galactosidase gene shows insertional inactivation.<br>(III) Primers are chemically synthesized oligonucleotides that are complementary to specific DNA regions in PCR.<br>(IV) The source of the restriction enzyme Hind III is <i>E. coli</i>.<br>(V) The micro-injection method for injecting recombinant DNA is used for animal cells.','[{"text": "I, III, V", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, II, III, V", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only IV is incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as source of the restriction enzyme Hind III is <i>Haemophilus influenzae</i>.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103064,'biology',97,1198,2860,'Fill in the blanks with appropriate answer:<br>(A) The vector needs to have very few, preferably single, ____ for the commonly used restriction enzymes.<br>(B) Disruption of the cell wall can be achieved by treating the bacterial cells, plant or animal tissue with enzymes such as ____ (bacteria), ____ (plant cells) and ____ (fungus).<br>(C) If any protein encoding gene is expressed in a heterologous host, it is called as ____ <br>(D) In gel electrophoresis, the separated DNA fragments can be seen only after staining the DNA with a compound known as ____ followed by exposure to UV radiation.','[{"text": "A - sticky ends;<br>B - lysozyme, cellulase, chitinase;<br>C - recombinant protein;<br>D - ethidium bromide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - sticky ends;<br>B - exonuclease, cellulase, chitinase;<br>C - recombinant protein;<br>D - ethidium bromide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - cut ends;<br>B - hemicellulose, cellulase, chitinase;<br>C - native glycoprotein;<br>D - CsCl", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A - Recognition sites;<br>B - lysozyme, cellulase, chitinase;<br>C - recombinant protein;<br>D - ethidium bromide", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'A-Recognition sites; B-lysozyme, cellulase, chitinase; C-recombinant protein; D-ethidium bromide is correct.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103065,'biology',97,1194,2856,'Find the correct statements from the following:<br>(I) Stanley Cohen and Herbert Boyer contributed to recombinant DNA technology by using the native plasmid of <i>Salmonella</i> as a cloning vector.<br>(II) EcoRI was the first restriction enzyme to be discovered and is widely used in genetic engineering.<br>(III) Gel electrophoresis is a technique used for the separation of DNA fragments based on size, where smaller fragments migrate faster through the gel matrix.<br>(IV) The BamHI restriction site is located at the tetracycline resistance gene in the vector pBR322, which allows for the identification of recombinant bacteria through insertional inactivation.','[{"text": "I, II, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'I, III, IV are correct statements. Statement II is incorrect $\\rightarrow$ The first restriction enzyme discovered was Hind II, not EcoRI.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103066,'biology',97,1194,2856,'Find the correct option with respect to the following statements:<br>(I) 5\' - GAATTC - 3\'<br>3\' - CTTAAG - 5\'<br>This is the palindromic recognition site for EcoRI.<br>(II) Bacteriophages, due to their high number per cell, have very high copy numbers of their genome within bacterial cells.<br>(III) The origin of replication (ori) is a sequence from where replication starts, and any piece of DNA linked to this sequence can be made to replicate within the host cells.<br>(IV) <i>Agrobacterium tumefaciens</i>, a pathogen of several dicot plants, is able to deliver a piece of DNA known as \'T-DNA\'.','[{"text": "I, IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II,III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II, III, IV", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'I, II, III, IV are correct. 5\' ____ GAATTC ____ 3\'<br>3\' ____ CTTAAG ____ 5\'. This is the palindromic site for EcoRI. Bacteriophages because of their high number per cell, have very high copy numbers of their genome within the bacterial cells. Origin of replication (ori) is a sequence from where replication starts and any piece of DNA when linked to this sequence.can be made to replicate within the host cells.Agrobacterium tumifaciens, a pathogen of several dicot plants is able to deliver a piece of DNA known as \'T-DNA\'.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103067,'biology',97,1199,2861,'Find the correct statements based on the given column matching.<br>(I) Primers are short oligonucleotides used in PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) to initiate DNA synthesis.<br>(II) Separation and purification of biological products is a key step in downstream processing.<br>(III) Biolistics, also known as the gene gun method, is used to introduce DNA into plant cells.<div class="matching-question"></div>','[{"text": "I, II, III", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "I, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "II, III only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II only", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'I, II, III are correct. All are correct statements.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103069,'biology',97,1194,2856,'Identify the correct option.','[{"text": "Selectable marker - $\\\\mathrm{amp}^{\\\\mathrm{R}}$ gene Identification of transformant.", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Restriction Enzyme - Random cutting of DNA.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "pBR322 - Cloning - Linear DNA vector.", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "BAC - Host cell - Isolation of DNA.", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'Selectable - amp ${ }^{\\mathrm{R}}$ gene - Identification of marker transformant.is correct',NULL,'Medium','MCQ',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103070,'biology',97,1193,2855,'Consider the following statements with respect to gel electrophoresis and find the incorrect ones.<br>(I) DNA fragments are separated according to their charge only, their sizes do not affect the process.<br>(II) DNA fragments move towards cathode on the basis of their charges.<br>(III) Separation of DNA fragments is according to their sizes as they move through sieves in the agarose gel.<br>(IV) The gel used for isolation of DNA fragments is made of agarose.','[{"text": "I, III,", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "IV only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, II", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "II, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'I, II are incorrect. The incorrect statements can be corrected as DNA fragments are separated according to their charge and their sizes .DNA fragments move towards anode on the basis of their charges.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103071,'biology',98,1187,2846,'A scientist wants to produce virus-free plant in tissue culture. Which part of the plant will he used as an explant?<br>(a) mature stem<br>(b) axillary meristem<br>(c) apical meristem<br>(d) mesophyll cell<br>Choose the correct option from the following','[{"text": "c and d", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "a only", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "b and c", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "b only", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Apical meristem and axillary meristem are virus-free regions in infected plants. These tissues are used in meristem culture to produce virus-free plants',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103072,'biology',98,1189,2848,'In mature insulin, which of the peptide is not present ?','[{"text": "A and B peptides", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "A-peptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "B-peptide", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "C-peptide", "isCorrect": true}]',3,'Proinsulin (the inactive precursor of insulin) contains A, B, and C peptides. During maturation, the C-peptide is removed, and only A and B peptides remain connected by disulfide bonds to form mature insulin.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103073,'biology',98,1187,2846,'Some strains of <i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> produce proteins that kill insects. Which one of the following is not killed by proteins of <i>Bacillus thruingiensis</i>?','[{"text": "Tapeworm", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Tobacco budworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Armyworm", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Cotton bollworm", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i> (Bt) produces insecticidal proteins (Cry proteins) that are toxic to certain insect larvae, especially: Tobacco budworm, armyworm, cotton bollworm Tapeworm is a helminth (parasitic worm), not an insect, and is not affected by Bt toxins',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'KCET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103074,'biology',98,1188,2847,'Silencing of specific mRNA is possible via RNAi because of','[{"text": "Non-complementary ssRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Complementary dsRNA", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Inhibitory ssRNA", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Complementary tRNA", "isCorrect": false}]',1,'The correct answer is option 2.<br>RNA interference (RNAi) is a gene-silencing mechanism in eukaryotes where complementary double-stranded RNA (dsRNA) binds to a specific mRNA. This binding prevents\ntranslation and leads to degradation of the target mRNA.',NULL,'Easy','MCQ',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103075,'biology',98,1188,2847,'Given below are two statements :<div class="matching-question"><div class="column-left">Transfer RNAs and ribosomal RNA do not interact with mRNA</div><div class="column-right">RNA interference (RNAi) takes place in all eukaryotic organisms as a method of cellular defence.<br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</div></div>','[{"text": "Statement A is incorrect but statement B is correct", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "Both statement A and statement B are correct", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Both statement A and statement B are incorrect", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Statement A is correct but statement B is incorrect", "isCorrect": false}]',0,'The correct answer is option 1.<br>Statement A: Incorrect – Both tRNA and rRNA interact with mRNA during translation: tRNA brings amino acids by pairing with codons on mRNA. rRNA forms the ribosomal complex\nthat facilitates mRNA decoding.<br>Statement B: Correct – RNA interference (RNAi) is a conserved cellular defense mechanism in all eukaryotic organisms',NULL,'Medium','MCQ type-2',2025,'NEET','2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL),
(103077,'biology',98,1189,2848,'1. Find out the incorrect statement for Insulin:<br>(I) C-peptide is not present in mature insulin.<br>(II) Recombinant insulin does not induce unwanted immunological response.<br>(III) Insulin used for diabetes was earlier extracted from the pancreas of slaughtered cattle and pigs.<br>(IV) Insulin from an animal source caused some patients to develop allergies or other types of reactions to the foreign proteins.<br>(V) In mammals, including humans, insulin is synthesized as a prohormone, which needs to be processed before it becomes a fully mature and functional hormone.<br>(VI) Eli Lily, an American company, prepared one DNA sequence that produces two polypeptide chains (A and B), and both are attached by a disulfide bond.','[{"text": "I, III, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "I, III, IV", "isCorrect": false}, {"text": "Only VI", "isCorrect": true}, {"text": "IV, V, VI", "isCorrect": false}]',2,'Only VI is incorrect.The incorrect statements can be corrected as Eli Lilly an American company prepared two DNA sequences corresponding to A and B , chains of human insulin and introduced them in plasmids of <i>E.coli</i> to produce insulin chains.',NULL,'Hard','MCQ type-2',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-25 18:34:34.081508',NULL);
